-- QuestLocFlavor (generado 2026-10-17): objetivos completos, con dialogos, solo para narrar.
_G.QuestLocFlavor = _G.QuestLocFlavor or {}
QuestLocFlavor[6] = {
[3000]={"Itûr stands in the planning room to the right of the refuge's entrance.","Itûr wonders what has befallen the prisoners.","'None would mistake me for one of the Corsairs of legend; my prowess is not in combat or swordplay. I spent many weeks in the gaol when the nobleman I thought to rob of his purse proved more vigilant than I expected, so I would not recommend you assign me tasks of thievery!'\
\
Itûr laughs suddenly.\
\
'There is one thing I can help you steal, Dax. Together we will steal the hearts of the people, right from under the noses of the Kindred! Folk have already come here searching for someone to lead them, and more are sure to come. We are going to need a place where we can make our plans.\
\
'Maybe we should set up the room on the right so we can accommodate our growing numbers.'","'Hármelak and Khôltekh have imprisoned two of our most significant figures, Dax. The city will not forgive this outrage, and as word of it spreads, the dominion of the Kindred must begin to weaken. Did they underestimate how beloved ${PLAYER} has become to the people of Umbar Baharbêl? Did they underestimate the popularity of your brother Jajax?\
\
'I think these were mistakes, Dax. But now we must ask ourselves an important question. For how long will the Kindred keep Jajax and ${PLAYER} in captivity? Are they still alive, and if they are, for how long will they remain so?'","Nakûr, another recent arrival, sits in the entrance to the refuge.","'Messages arrive from all throughout the city, Daxamat.\
\
'The Song of Waves and Wind passing so near to the city has caused our numbers to grow. The people cannot disbelieve the evidence of their own eyes: that the Kindred allowed these ships to sink an Umbari galley. They have allied with Orcs, and by so doing are no better than those vile creatures!\
\
'The fleet has sailed into the Bay and left us behind, but the Kindred will still come to rue its passage.'","Talk to Nakûr in the entrance to the refuge","Set up chairs in the room to the right of the entrance","With the heroes imprisoned, it falls to Daxamat to take up the struggle!\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>","'This is a start, but there is more to be done. The Kindred of the Coins has two places where their leadership can feel safe: within the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, and within the strong walls of the Citadel of the Winds. As our numbers grow, we will need to find some way of threatening these bastions, making the Kindred question its safety and the sources of its power.\
\
'There is something else, too.'","Talk to Itûr in the planning room","Chapter 18.4: The Cage and the Captives","If you are to lead a rebellion against traitorous powers, you will need to prepare. The room to the right of the refuge's entrance should serve.","'Folk have already come here searching for someone to lead them, and more are sure to come. We are going to need a place where we can make our plans. Maybe we should set up the room on the right so we can accommodate our growing numbers.'"},
[3001]={"The last time Nakûr checked there were no messages, but perhaps now there will be. If so, the shopkeeper Sekét will have slipped them under the door at the top of the stairs on the left side of the entrance to the refuge.","Return to the entrance of the refuge and learn what has happened","Rothog the Storm stares at you carefully.","Talk to Nakûr in the entrance to the refuge","Something has happened by the entrance to the refuge. You hear the sound of voices raised in anger!","'I bring good news from Umbar-môkh, Daxamat.\
\
'My contact has spoken with . ${PLAYER:She[f]|He} and Jajax are being held within the Fleetfast gaol, and the Terâsi girl is willing to show us a secret way inside. She seemed very insistent that if she performs this task for us, we will see that the enemy fleet is destroyed. I know not if that is within our power... but I told her we would consider it.\
\
'We need  and Jajax freed. We can consider nothing until that happens, am I right?'","Chapter 18.5: Catching Sparks","You should spread out the papers on the table in the planning room to the right of the entrance to the refuge.","You heave a sigh of relief as they lower their weapons","Two leaders of the Kindred of the Coins stand ready to fight!","Shêsha and her cat Rûmina study the papers in the planning room.","Perhaps Birûk has returned from Umbar-môkh with tidings?","You collect the messages slipped under the door by an ally to Ilma-ghôli's cause","Kinsman Belondor appraises you.","With the heroes imprisoned, it falls to Daxamat to take up the struggle!\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>","Talk to Belondor in the entrance to the refuge","Check if there are any messages atop the stairs on the left side of the entrance to the refuge","'You are Daxamat, yes? The brother of Jajax? These men follow your command?'\
\
Belondor looks you up and down, and releases his hand from the hilt of his sword.\
\
'I should have known something was amiss, Daxamat. Hármelak's sudden interest in the Thardúth should have raised my suspicion, for always has she dismissed the servants of Morgoth we faced in Urash Dâr as less of a threat to Umbar than others. To ask Rothog and I to travel to Damarzâg, to learn if they have any presence there... it seems an obvious ruse, now, a means of keeping two members of the Kindred from interfering with her plans. When we departed I thought only that at last she was taking seriously the danger.\
\
'But now we have returned, and we must decide what can be done. Where is ? We should ask ${PLAYER:her[f]|him} for ${PLAYER:her[f]|his} thoughts.'","Nakûr will be pleased to see the arrival of these new messages.","Can bloodshed be avoided?","'For now I relent. If you give me a reason to fight, I will not again lower my khopeshes until the battle is done!\
\
'Belondor and I were away from the city, visiting the arid hills of Damarzâg and looking for evidence of the Thardúth. We found none, but when we returned to Umbar Baharbêl the shouting of its people could be mistaken by no one. Someone had allowed a fleet of Mordor and Ordâkh to pass by the city, and as it sailed into the Bay it turned its cannons upon Umbari ships! Even now the wreck of an Umbari galley smoulders with the blue flames of the Hungry Fire!\
\
'Some members of my Kindred seem to have allied with this fleet, but only one arranged for me and Belondor to be away from the city when it arrived. This was the work of Hármelak! She knew this fleet was on its way, and she wanted to ensure Rothog did not stop it!'","Spread out the papers on the table in the planning room","'Something has happened upstairs! Are we discovered?'","'Messages are coming from every Ward of the city; I have been running hither and yon all morning! Let me rest, I beg you, only for a moment! Once I have caught my breath I will return to the work!'\
\
You tell Nakûr he should rest, for he will be of little use to Ilma-ghôli, the rising tide of rebellion, if he falls down from exhaustion. He smiles gratefully.\
\
'I only need a moment, Daxamat, really! But if you climb the stairs and check to see if Sekét has slipped any more messages under his door, my rest should cost us very little. There were none when last I checked, but that was a few minutes ago.'","'I only need a moment, Daxamat, really! But if you climb the stairs and check to see if Sekét has slipped any more messages under his door, my rest should cost us very little. There were none when last I checked, but that was a few minutes ago.'","'Already there are more messages from elsewhere in the city? Events are moving quickly, Daxamat! You should spread out those papers on the planning table. More folk wait for their orders!'","Two leaders of the Kindred stand ready to fight!","Talk to Shêsha in the planning room","'Rûmina and I can move unnoticed through the Lower Ward with great speed... until the moment we want to be seen, and to be heard. I am confident we can spread the news of Hármelak's betrayal of the city, and that Khôltekh may be aiding her. It will not be difficult: few of the Umbari failed to see the enemy ships as they passed the city, and it was apparent to all that their Corsair crews had joined hands with soldiers of Ordâkh and Orcs of Mordor. It is an outrage and a mockery!\
\
'I understand there is a plan in motion to free your brother and ${PLAYER} from captivity? Has there yet been any word?'","Go down to the cellar and see if Birûk has returned","'One more thing! I understand there is a plan in motion to free your brother and ${PLAYER} from captivity? Has there yet been any word?'","Talk to Rothog in the entrance to the refuge","'You should spread out those papers on the planning table. More folk wait for their orders!'","Birûk was due to arrive sometime soon. You should go down to the cellar and see if the Temámir has returned.","You hear voices from above... voices raised in anger!"},
[3002]={"'But you are the leader of this band of fighters, Daxamat. Consider all that must be done, and give your people their commands. The uprising in Umbar begins now!'","'The Harlond burns. We have arrived too late.'","The assembled fighters of Ilma-ghôli listen to your directives","'I know of a place where many weapons are stored, Dax: beneath the Dahâl Huliz, in Kamrabezûr, are racks and racks of weapons for use in the arena. But that is not all we can take from there. The gladiators revere Rothog as both a great warrior and a leader of the city. If they are shown he sides with us to overthrow the villains who betray Umbar Baharbêl, we will have obtained not just weapons, but fighters to wield them as well.\
\
'We must not underestimate the reputation of Rothog the Storm! The prospect of facing him in single combat was enough to keep me safely and content in the gaol. I knew not that Kinsman Belondor would free me from captivity without fighting only days later, but I did know not to face Rothog on the blood-sands for my freedom!\
\
'But today I will fight for freedom from the traitors who pretend to speak for Umbar... but I fight beside the Storm, and not against him!'","<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>\
\
You have arrived at the Harlond in time of war, the port-city wreathed in flames.","With the heroes imprisoned, it falls to Daxamat to take up the struggle!\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>","Give your allies their orders in the planning room of the refuge","'You have given these folk their orders, Daxamat. What now is your role to play?'\
\
You tell Belondor that you are ready to free your brother Jajax and the hero ${PLAYER} from the Fleetfast gaol, but before you can say anything else, he shakes his head.\
\
'I think not, Daxamat. That is a dangerous undertaking. I cannot say how it has happened, but you have somehow become the leader of this rising tide, this Ilma-ghôli. Without you to focus these varied and disparate fighters, I think this uprising is snuffed out like a torch doused in sea-water. You must remain here at this refuge in order to coordinate the efforts of Ilma-ghôli.\
\
'The rescue of ${PLAYER} and your brother must be left to others.'","Your gathered allies await their orders in the planning room to the right of the entrance to the refuge.","'Rothog and I will lead this rescue mission. ${PLAYER} and Jajax are imprisoned by those we counted allies, even friends. The two of us must set this right.\
\
'I will speak with the Temámir about this secret entrance he has discovered. Were it not now of use, I would rue its very existence! But it seems such a way into the gaol will now help us bring our friends to freedom, and about that I will not complain.\
\
'Regret not that you do not accompany us! There will be danger enough for you here, Daxamat. All of the city will soon come alive with anger, and you must be ready to guide its furious voice!'","Use the table in the planning room to address the gathering","Talk to Belondor and stay behind while he goes to rescue the prisoners","Chapter 18.6: The Uprising Begins","Talk to Belondor and go with him to rescue the prisoners","The time has come for you to use the table and address the gathering in the planning room to the right of the entrance.","'Imprisoned? We will need to do something about that.\
\
'Something else troubles me. Some of the people with whom I spoke claim that Nakási commands the fleet, and she has joined hands with Balakhâd, the son of Balakhôr; their ships are crewed with Heirsworn Corsairs, Orcs of Mordor, and Ordâkhai soldiers alike. If this is true, fully half of the Kindred of the Coins have changed their loyalties: Nakási, Hármelak, and Khôltekh can no longer be trusted to lead.\
\
'Where is Tatháta in all this? She has always been more solitary than the rest, but if she sides with the betrayers it will be difficult for Rothog and I to convince the city that our position is just. That way is certain to lead to bloodshed. I do not fear it! I would prefer not to slay my fellows if it might be avoided, but we need to remove the blight from the Kindred of the Coins in order to cleanse it, one way or another. \
\
'But you are the leader of this band of fighters, Daxamat. Consider all that must be done, and give your people their commands. The uprising in Umbar begins now!'","'There is no need to draw stones, as is the custom among my people in Khabârkhad; I know what duty is set before me.\
\
'First I will go to Mekab-kuphâr with this unpleasant news: Khôltekh has jeopardized the lives, safety, and wealth of the Temámir people. I will bring those of my fellows who agree with this position to the Shoreward Stone, where we will seek an audience with Inîk Jewel-brow, the Hall-father. One way or another, Khôltekh will be removed from power for his part in this calamity.\
\
'While I do this, someone else must make use of the secret entrance into the Fleetfast gaol in order to free your brother and ${PLAYER}.'","Belondor awaits the word to begin the rescue mission.","Talk to Tatháta while the Harlond burns","'Rûmina and I have many contacts within the Sail-haven and the Lower Ward. We will spread the news of Hármelak's betrayal, and rally the Umbari to march upon Dâr Laja. Corsairs and mariners, vendors and caravan drivers, even the troublemakers and brigands of the Gut... all these folk have reason to overthrow the rulers who think to sell us to Mordor or to Ordâkh!\
\
'Even the Corsair Jeduth may join us in this. He has retired from the privateering trade, but he will see the rightness of Ilma-ghôli's cause!'"},
[3003]={"King Elessar stands atop the overlook, preparing for the counter-attack","'¡${PLAYER}!'","You have sailed in haste to Gondor, but the Song arrived before you, and the Harlond is in flames.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>","'Look for Borndir at the base of the slope to the north! He guards the path to the King's encampment!'","Find more defenders north-west of the Harlond, past the graveyard","A soldier of Gondor greets you by the southern side of the burning Harlond, desperate hope written on his face.","Make your way north-west in search of Gondorian defenders","'Do my eyes deceive me? No! You have returned to stand with us against the Corsairs of Umbar, ${PLAYER}? I only hope you have not arrived too late!\
\
'When we travelled with King Elessar to Outer Gondor that he might hear the concerns of his people and help them rebuild from the war, I did not think we would so soon be thrust once again into such horrors as have come to the Harlond this day!\
\
'It was my duty, and Lornion's, to safeguard the King. But how can we protect him against a fleet that wields such terrible weapons, and is crewed by every enemy that ever vowed to destroy Gondor: Corsairs, Haradrim, and Orcs, all united in hatred against us?\
\
'King Elessar has established a camp on the overlook atop this sloping path, ${PLAYER}. Go to him and learn what can be done against these invaders, if there be anything!'","Talk to King Elessar at the overlook north-west of the burning Harlond","A soldier of Gondor beckons you to him","King Elessar prepares for the counter-attack from the overlook north-west of the burning Harlond.","'Gondor cannot be without defenders! Where are its knights? Where are its fighters? The King of Gondor would not permit an incursion so near to the White City to remain unmet... unless he had no choice.\
\
'We must press forward to the north-west in search of any who might stand against Nakási.'","Borndir calls out in greeting as you approach the upward slope","'¡Aquí!'","Borndir told you that King Elessar has gathered a number of soldiers on the overlook at the top of the sloping path north-west of the burning Harlond, and prepares to make a counter-attack against the invaders.","You should make your way north-west past the reeds in search of Gondorian defenders.","Talk to the soldier of Gondor by the south-western edge of the Harlond","King Elessar stands here.","'Press forward and search for Gondor's defenders! Follow the sound of fighting to the north-west!\
\
'Gondor would not willingly abandon this port-city to the ravages of the Song.'","'Is that you, ${PLAYER}? We are hard-pressed here, and have lost many men in an attempt to learn what villain bedevils us! I thought the Corsairs tasted bitter defeat during the war, and their fleet destroyed!'\
\
You tell the soldier that the Song of Waves and Wind had been kept secret from most of Umbar, but a number of their captains schemed to use it against Gondor.\
\
'We sallied forth from Minas Tirith when we first received word of enemy ships sailing toward the Harlond. King Elessar led the charge, but we could not get near enough for fear of the terrible blue flames fired from their weapons! Is it true they have wrought new quantities of the Umbari Fire?\
\
'The King was pushed away from the river... find his men to the north-west, past the graveyard!'","Borndir stands on the slope north-west of the burning Harlond, past the graveyard.","Chapter 18.7: The Song In Gondor","'You will find King Elessar at the top of this path! Go to him with haste!'","King Elessar turns to face you, his expression brightening as he recognizes your return from distant lands.\
\
'You return to Gondor in its time of need, my friend; I deem that is no coincidence. Tell me everything you know of this fleet and the villains who captain it!'","Talk to Borndir on the slope north-west of the graveyard outside the Harlond","Find King Elessar at the overlook atop the sloping path north-west of the graveyard outside the burning Harlond","Defenders of Gondor fought bravely against the assault of the Song, but were pushed back to a slope north-west of the Harlond, beyond the graveyard."},
[3004]={"'We have to do something about the Narghâk weapons Nakási has mounted upon the Song, ${PLAYER}.'","Aphadaer urgently calls you to him","Chapter 18.8: Taking Back the Harlond","Leave the weapons you collected in the barrel by the graveyard","Defeated Orc invaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Orcs throughout the burning Harlond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Leave the swords you collected in a barrel by the graveyard for other soldiers to wield in defence of Gondor!'","Agladal has been sent to safety","'The ships sailed into the Harlond with no warning, ${PLAYER}. Their crews of Orcs and Haradrim set the port ablaze in the span of a single hour. They came ashore and we met them with sword and spear, but we were unprepared for such ferocity in time of peace. Our counter attack will come, and it must come soon!\
\
'Face any of those who now pillage the Harlond, and you will help us regain the advantage!'","With the tasks given to you by King Elessar's attendants now completed, you should return to the graveyard outside the burning Harlond and prepare to push back the invaders.","Talk to King Elessar at the graveyard","Retrieved Gondorian swords dropped during the retreat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'King Elessar rode bravely from the White City and led a sortie against the invaders, but we were pushed back to this hill. During the retreat, some of our soldiers dropped their weapons on the slope. Retrieve these weapons as you descend from the overlook, and leave them in the weapons barrel that has been placed by the graveyard. They will be used again!'","The weapons you collected can now be used again in defence of Gondor","'How have the Heirs of Castamir come to wield these blue flames? Is the son of Balakhôr an enchanter?'","King Elessar is at the graveyard outside the burning Harlond, preparing to strike back against the invaders.","Talk to Belondor at the graveyard","Gaeranor has been sent to safety","King Elessar has asked you to speak to his attendants on the overlook north-west of the burning Harlond to learn what must be done for the counter-attack to begin.","Talk to Aphadaer at the graveyard","Defeated Ordâkhai invaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Aphadaer stands here.","Talk to Lornion on the overlook","Return to the graveyard outside the burning Harlond","Aphadaer has called you to him at the graveyard outside the burning Harlond.","Find the horse Gaeranor along the main street and send him to safety","Gondor has suffered a defeat, but now it is time for the counter-attack to begin.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>","'Speak to my attendants and learn how we can fight back against Nakási and Balakhâd!'","Talk to Glindor on the overlook","'Did you see the son of Balakhôr? I heard shouting above the tumult, and voices cried that the Heirs of Castamir have designs upon the White City! Could it be true?'\
\
You assure Aphadaer that the Heirsworn will not have victory, despite their initial success, and that the counter attack will begin at Elessar's command.\
\
'Of course, of course. Heed not my jumbled thoughts!'","Elessar sighs when you finish your account, and you can tell the events of the day have taken their toll.\
\
'The death of Nakási's husband Tumúldo at the hands of the Heirsworn was an injustice, but it cannot warrant such an attack as this. Had she remained in Umbar, nursing her hatred of Gondor, that would be a sorrow, and I would share her grief. But for her to seize command of this fleet and these weapons and bring them to bear against my people... that cannot be forgiven.\
\
'Five ships have come to the Harlond wielding the Hungry Fire I thought was gone. Nakási captains the largest of these. Two others are crewed by Haradrim soldiers, and one has Orcs aboard. I could not see who commands the crew of the last ship, but from your account I deem it must be Balakhâd, son of Balakhôr the Scourge. The Heirs of Castamir remain to trouble us, it seems.\
\
'It has been a losing struggle to this point, ${PLAYER}, but perhaps your arrival will help to turn the tide. Speak to my attendants here on the overlook and we will begin to fight back against these invaders!'","Retrieve Gondorian swords dropped on the path to the overlook during the retreat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It has only been a matter of weeks since I travelled with you in Anfalas, ${PLAYER}, but so much has happened! Is it true that the son of Balakhôr the Scourge captains one of these ships against us? Are the Heirs of Castamir behind this attack?'\
\
You tell Aphadaer that Balakhâd supplied Corsair crews for some of Nakási's fleet, but most of those ships were damaged before they could sail to Gondor. You ask him what you can do to help fight against the five ships that made the journey.\
\
'There was much chaos as we retreated to this overlook, ${PLAYER}, and we were pursued by our enemies. As the King's groom, it is my job to see to the horses, and I did as best I could, but two of them slipped from my tending and fled toward the main street that runs through the centre of the Harlond. They were crazed by the flames, you see. Who among us was not? If you find Agladal and Gaeranor, send them back to me, if they still live!'","Find the horse Agladal along the main street and send him to safety","The King motions to the man standing nearby, a man once of Gondor but now of Umbar.\
\
'Belondor tells me Nakási has broken with the Kindred of the Coins, and I believe him.'","'The horses bolted from the unnatural blue flames. Search for them along the main street of the Harlond, to the east!'","The King's expression is already greatly-changed from when you first encountered him today. His weariness has been replaced with determination.\
\
'This is the hour in which we fight back against the invaders,' he says.\
\
'Belondor tells me that Nakási has broken with his Kindred, and is an enemy too of Umbar. I believe him. He counts himself no longer a man of Gondor, but today we will fight side by side to prevent Nakási and her allies from endangering our lands and our homes, though they be not shared.'","Defeat Ordâkhai soldiers throughout the burning Harlond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gondorian swords were dropped on the sloping path when the soldiers retreated to the overlook north-west of the burning Harlond.","'Can you pick up the weapons we dropped on the path as we climbed to this overlook? After you have them, leave them in a barrel by the graveyard for other soldiers to wield in defence of Gondor!'","'We must prove to the Orcs and Haradrim that Gondor is not without courage!'","You were told to leave the swords you retrieved in a barrel by the graveyard outside the burning Harlond, rescue frightened horses that fled in the direction of the main street, and defeat Orcs and Ordâkhai that threaten the port.","Belondor is at the graveyard outside the burning Harlond.","Talk to Aphadaer on the overlook"},
[3005]={"'I don't... I don't know what happened!'","Jajax stands here.","Jajax is on the eastern side of the port-city, preparing to storm the docks.","The King has been wounded! What happened while you were away?","Talk to Borndir at the graveyard","'Belondor and Rothog will disable the Narghâk weapons on another of the ships? Then let it be a competition, ${PLAYER}! With your good fortune and my incredible skill we will accomplish our own mission before they succeed!'","Jajax stands bravely among the flames not far from the docks","'Find Jajax and work with him to disable the Narghâk weapons on one of the ships! Rothog and I will do the same for another!\
\
'This is what Sirgon wanted: peace between Gondor and Umbar. I will not allow Nakási to shatter the chance for good relations between our peoples!'","'I don't... I don't know what happened! One moment the King was issuing commands to his knights, and the next he was upon the ground!\
\
'I think he has been stabbed by a secret knife, ${PLAYER}!'","Find Jajax on the eastern side of the burning Harlond, preparing to storm the docks","Talk to Borndir at the graveyard and learn what happened to the King.","Chapter 18.9: The Lesson of the Flames","As long as the Song possesses its Narghâk weapons, every shore in Middle-earth remains at risk.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>","'Nakási inflicted great damage upon the Harlond with her initial attack, but her forces are limited to those who made the crossing. The soldiers of Minas Tirith greatly outnumber the warriors at Nakási's disposal; when King Elessar mounts his counter attack, they should be able to overwhelm the crews of the Song. The Narghâk weapons remain the real danger, for they greatly make up for her disadvantage in numbers. We have to disable those weapons, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I will go with Rothog to destroy the Narghâk weapons aboard the Orc ship. You should find Jajax on the eastern side of the port-city, near the docks, and go with him to destroy the Narghâk weapons aboard one of the Ordâkhai vessels! Then we will have levelled the playing-field somewhat, and given King Elessar an opportunity to mount the counter attack. This is what Sirgon wanted, ${PLAYER}: peace between Gondor and Umbar. I will not allow Nakási to shatter the chance for good relations between our peoples!'","The day is not yet won. You must return to the graveyard outside the burning Harlond and learn what next can be done.","Return to the graveyard and talk to King Elessar","Talk to Jajax and go with him to sabotage the Narghâk weapons of the Song"},
[3006]={"Goldagnir está en Thangúlhad, el puesto avanzado de la Hueste Dorada más cercano a Dol Guldur.\
\
Ningloril te ha dicho que hables con Goldagnir, quien está organizando el último asalto a la torre.","'Hemos tenido la victoria, ${PLAYER}; al menos tanta victoria como teníamos derecho a esperar. No podemos mantener esta fortaleza, y puede que no pase mucho tiempo antes de que el Enemigo contraataque con tal fuerza que nos empuje de nuevo al otro lado del río.\
\
'Lothlórien será atacada, eso es seguro. Pero esto es una victoria si hemos retrasado ese ataque aunque sea un solo día. Mi corazón me dice que lo hemos hecho, y al mantener los ojos del Enemigo centrados en la puerta de la fortaleza del Nazgûl, hemos hecho lo que el señor Celeborn y la dama Galadriel querían que hiciéramos.\
\
'La batalla puede haber terminado, por ahora, pero algunas historias no han tenido su final. Así es la vida, ¿no? Ha sido un placer luchar a tu lado, ${PLAYER}, en esta campaña. Que tu historia continúe una y otra vez.'","Completa la Escaramuza: La Batalla en la Torre","La Hueste Dorada inicia su asalto final sobre Dol Guldur y se te ha pedido que luches junto a los Malledhrim durante la batalla.","'Serás ${PLAYERNAME:un aliado importante[m]|una aliada importante[f]} durante la escaramuza en la torre, . ¡Espero que estés ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para este asalto final sobre Dol Guldur!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que puede ser completada en solitario, en dúo, en pequeña comunidad, en comunidad o en grupo de incursión utilizando el panel de escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","Capítulo 18: La Batalla en la Torre","Habla con Goldagnir en Thangúlhad","Tienes tu propio papel que desempeñar en la escaramuza en la torre, el asalto final de la Hueste Dorada sobre Dol Guldur.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que puede ser completada en solitario, en dúo, en pequeña comunidad, en comunidad o en grupo de incursión utilizando el panel de escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","Goldagnir está en Thangúlhad, el puesto avanzado de la Hueste Dorada más cercano a Dol Guldur.\
\
Con una pequeña victoria en mano, deberías regresar a Goldagnir.","'Goldagnir puede compartir contigo los planes de batalla relacionados con el asalto final sobre la torre de los Nazgûl. Él está aquí, en Thangúlhad.'","'No habrá mejor momento que este para asaltar la torre de los Nazgûl, ${PLAYER}. El señor Celeborn ha determinado que no podremos resistir la contraofensiva si todas las fuerzas de Dol Guldur se lanzan sobre nosotros a la vez; este será nuestro último ataque.\
\
'Dividiremos nuestras fuerzas y lideraremos un ataque concentrado sobre la torre: la fuerza principal de la Hueste Dorada asaltará la entrada principal, despejando el camino para que un segundo grupo de aventureros, una comunidad de gran notoriedad, pueda asaltar la torre.\
\
'Mientras tanto, tú y tus aliados entraréis en la fortaleza por el camino secreto utilizado por Mithrandir y os enfrentaréis en una escaramuza dentro de la torre. El Enemigo estará en desorden, sin saber en qué frente luchar, y el día será nuestro.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que puede ser completada en solitario, en dúo, en pequeña comunidad, en comunidad o en grupo de incursión utilizando el panel de escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","'El asalto final sobre Dol Guldur está sobre nosotros, ${PLAYER}. Atacaremos el bastión de los Nazgûl en el Bosque Negro y que los cimientos de la torre se estremezcan con los tambores de batalla.\
\
'Goldagnir ha diseñado un plan para el asalto. Habla con él para saber cuál es tu papel en él y el de tus aliados.'"},
[3007]={"'Where did we hear this news? One of the great Eagles spied Thranduil and a small host of his kindred entering Caras Galadhon. It was a fleeting glimpse, even for a beast of such keen sight, and she could tell us little more.'","'I will tarry here briefly to speak with my father. You return to Mordor. As Lady Galadriel said, we will surely see each other soon.'","Talk to Lady Galadriel","'We are indeed fresh from battle, as Legolas observes. Against his father's domain and our own the Enemy's forces marched, even as war waged in the place from whence you have arrived. Is it any wonder that the foe should set all his plans into motion at once?'","Chapter 1: A Council Waiting","Legolas seems as if he also wishes to talk with you.","'We await the arrival of the Elf, Glorfindel, ${PLAYER}. Without him this council is not complete and I feel we cannot act. \
\
'I reached out to him as soon as I was able and he swore that he would come with all possible haste. I do not yet fear the worst, and yet still the fact that he has not arrived is troubling.\
\
'Your arrival, friend, is some consolation, and your service to our cause eases my fears even more. There is little else we can do now, but soon, I feel certain, we shall meet again. We must hope that by then, Glorfindel is with us.'","Talk to Thranduil and experience 'Session: the Battle Under the Trees'.","'Listen, and I will tell you of the Battle Under the Trees.'","'Have you come for the Council of War? If not, it is some strange chance that brings you here now. \
\
'Oh, I do not wish to sound unwelcoming! Go on and approach the council. Doubtless you have news and I am certain you will have their ears. They are waiting still and can do nothing yet!'","You should talk to Haldir at the entrance to the Court of Lothlórien.","'Greetings, ${CLASS}. My son travels in strange company, it seems, but then, these are strange times and it is through great pains that I have recently learned the difference between a stranger and a foe.\
\
'You have told your tale uncommonly well and it fills my heart with wonder. We, too, have weathered much, and in our tale is much, I believe, that you should know.'","Having spoken to Celeborn and Galadriel, you should talk to King Thranduil as well.","'In the end, our losses were great, but not nearly so great as those of our enemy's. They have retreated to their shadowed fastnesses, wounded but not so harmed that they may not cause us grief again. That is why we must choose our actions with care and gather all wisdom to us before we do.'","Habla con Galadriel","'The time of watching and waiting has gone completely, or nearly so. I would move to retaliate swiftly and absolutely. Although this Lord and Lady do not disagree, generally, they feel that we must yet wait for the arrival of another, before we do.'","Find Legolas in Dor Amarth","'Word has reached my ears from Lothlórien, friend, and I know not what to make of it. Thranduil, Lord of Mirkwood, is there, but on what errand? In these times, the reason cannot be a light or merry one.\
\
'Whatever the case, Legolas may wish to be by his father Thranduil's side. Will you find him in Dor Amarth and tell him all I have told to you?'","Hear what the Council of War has to say after Thranduil's recounting of the Battle Under the Trees.","Legolas can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth in Dor Amarth.\
\
You should bring word to Legolas in Dor Amarth of his father's visit to Lothlórien.","Talk to Thranduil","Talk to Lord Celeborn","What has brought King Thranduil of Mirkwood to the Court of Lothlórien?","'That is my father Thranduil, there,' Legolas whispers. 'Look, they are garbed as if fresh from combat!'","Having arrived at the Council of War, you should talk to the lord and lady of the court first.","Habla con Legolas.","Approach the Council of War in the Court of Lothlórien.","Habla con Haldir","Approach the War Council","'Find Legolas in Dor Amarth and bear him word that his father, King Thranduil, has come to the Court of Lothlórien.'","'My heart tells me you have as great a tale to tell as we do - no, I think greater. The fact that your face is not harrowed and drained of hope tells me much, but I would hear more!'\
\
Addressing the entire council, you briefly describe all the events of war between the Pelennor and the Black Gates.\
\
A silence falls over those around you once you are done.\
\
'This is joyous news, then!' Galadriel pronounces, at last. 'And such as shall be sung and told of for long to come. Though even the most joyous of changes come with a tinge of sorrow to we who have dwelled long here and have parted with so much.'","Hear Thranduil's tale of the events in Mirkwood and Lothlórien.","Legolas hears the news with a furrowed brow.\
\
'My father would not stir so far from his domain if the occasion were not great, and like Elladan, I fear dark reasons rather than happy ones. Yes, I think I must go and learn what has passed among my cousins and people. \
\
'Will you travel with me, ${PLAYER}? The miles will pass swiftly with company and I find myself loath to tear Gimli away for this, just now. I will be happier knowing that I will soon rejoin him here.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Advancing will teleport you directly to the Court of Lothlórien.</rgb>"},
[3009]={"'I understand you fought in the battles to the south? I hope you do not think we were idle, for indeed we had battles of our own to fight! A great army of Easterlings crossed the river and fell upon our allies at Dale, and we emerged from our mountain to lend the Men our strength. The fighting continued for several days, but the enemy force was too great and we were driven back to the very gate of Erebor. It was there that King Brand of Dale was overcome. King Dáin stood in defence of his friend, but no Man or dwarf could have survived long against that assault. The King under the Mountain, Dáin Ironfoot, was slain.\
\
'It was the command of his son, Thorin III, that we retreat into the Mountain and prepare for a siege. He is now king and we follow his commands, but there were whispers that we should not have bolted our gate, that we should have stayed and fought. I do not agree with these whispers, but I am one dwarf and there are many others who think this retreat was craven.\
\
'During the siege, the Hall under the Mountain became a place for the recovery of hurts, where good dwarves hope to heal from their injuries, lest they succumb. It will not remain so, but the toll from the Battle of Dale is high and it will take time to set it right again.'","This area of the hall has been set aside for treating the wounded and infirm","King Thorin is currently meeting with his advisors, and is not free for an audience. Foldgráf recommended that you make yourself familiar with the Hall under the Mountain while you wait.","During the siege, this area was used for storage of provisions and other perishables","Foldgráf stands ready to welcome you to the Hall under the Mountain.","'Welcome to Erebor, ${PLAYER}. I hope you will forgive the state in which you find these halls, but battle was lately joined and we feared a long siege. Many supplies were brought from elsewhere in the mountain to be near at hand in the event they were needed, and they have yet to be returned.\
\
'I have summoned adventurers of renown to Erebor in order to advance the cause of Durin's Folk in Middle-earth, but especially as it concerns the Land of Mordor. Those gates have long been shut to us, but I desire brave heroes to enter that forbidding land and retrieve for the dwarves any treasures that might be found.\
\
'If my father had lived to see Mordor opened, I know he would advance this purpose, and fear nothing. So too will I. I have charged these dwarves with the same goal. Speak to them and they will share what they have learned of the dangers that await, and what they have learned of the great wealth that may wait as well.'","King Thorin is meeting with adventurers about opportunities in Mordor","Chapter 1: Beneath the Lonely Mountain","'The Land of Mordor has been shrouded in mystery for as long as I have lived, ${PLAYER}, and it has an evil reputation. But that makes the prospect of adventuring within its bounds even more attractive to me, for Eirek Glory-seeker fears nothing! The greater the danger, the greater the honour of facing it, and that goes double for doing so in the name of one's king. I would have quested in Mordor for Dáin, and now that he has undertaken his final battle I will adventure on behalf of his son Thorin. Glory for Durin's Folk!\
\
'We share a common purpose, but I hope beyond the Mountains of Shadow you will hunt elsewhere. The treasure I bring back, and the glory, should belong to Eirek and to his king alone!'","Talk to Foldgráf at the entrance to the Hall under the Mountain","'You say you are an adventurer? Are you certain? I have never heard of you, and I wear the dust of many distant lands on my boots. Have you faced down the terrible fire-troll Ashthrok, or the unsightly Vélnas? What about the terrible Hrimdyr, vile snow-beast of the blinding snow? I have fought them all, and lived to tell the tale.\
\
'Now I will delve beyond the Mountains of Shadow and adventure in the Black Land of Mordor, and the tale of Mogi will grow! Stay out of my way, ${PLAYER}.'","Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.","'Adventure in Mordor for Durin's Folk, and return with treasure and glory!'","'Before you begin to adventure on behalf of Durin's Folk, you should return to Erebor and speak with the King under the Mountain! That title belongs now to Thorin III, for his father Dáin fell before the gates of Erebor during the Battle of Dale. He died well, but now the responsibility of leading the dwarves falls to his son. Go to the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor, and present yourself to him. He will be glad to have your service!'","'I am pleased that you have pledged to aid Durin's Folk as we adventure in Mordor, ${PLAYER}! Who knows what treasures were wrongfully stolen from us, and now wait to be reclaimed and restored to their rightful owners?\
\
'My adventuring days are not yet done. My captivity by the Dourhands in the North Downs has taught me the value of caution, and I will exercise it smartly. See that you do as well, my valiant friend, for the land of Mordor is a place of evil, Dark Lord or no!\
\
'But before you begin to adventure on behalf of Durin's Folk, you should return to Erebor and speak with the King under the Mountain! That title belongs now to Thorin III, for his father Dáin fell before the gates of Erebor during the Battle of Dale. He died well, but now the responsibility of leading the dwarves falls to his son. Go to the Hall under the Mountain, in Erebor, and present yourself to him. He will be glad to have your service!'","Foldgráf is at the entrance to the Hall under the Mountain.","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Durin's Folk and fight on their behalf in Mordor.","'You must be ${PLAYER} the ${CLASS}, who has sworn to adventure on behalf of Durin's Folk? King Thorin will see you now and charge you with tasks befitting your skill.'","Talk to Dómor by the throne","Talk to Margald in the Hall under the Mountain","'I look forward to hearing of your great deeds on behalf of Durin's Folk, ${PLAYER}. Adventure in Mordor with caution, and know that our thoughts are with you even as you walk in the distant, dangerous wilds!\
\
'Return in triumph, and with treasure and glory for the dwarves!'","Talk to Hrostyr, the personal guard of King Thorin III","'The king awaits, for he has a task with which to charge you.'","Three adventuring dwarves stand by the throne in the Hall under the Mountain. They have been charged by King Thorin III with the same task as you.","Talk to Laurík in the Hall under the Mountain","Talk to Mogi by the throne","Travel to the Hall under the Mountain, in Erebor","'King Thorin has no shortage of heroes and adventurers willing to brave the dangers of Mordor on his behalf, but the folk that remain behind whisper in their beards and compare him unfavorably to his father. I will return from Mordor with treasure enough to silence their whispers. They call him Stonehelm, and say he hides within the mountain? When I return they will call him Gilded-helm, and I will be richly-rewarded for my efforts!\
\
'There are adventures enough to be had in that land, but do not expect to share in my treasure or my glory, ${PLAYER}. There will be enough for all of us, no doubt.'","'King Thorin is currently speaking with his advisors and an audience will have to wait until he is free. Perhaps you can make yourself familiar with these halls while you wait?'","Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor. You should present yourself to Hrostyr, his personal guard.","Talk to Bróthi in the Hall under the Mountain","King Thorin should now be ready to meet with you.","Talk to Eirek by the throne","'If my father had lived to see Mordor opened, I know he would advance this purpose, and fear nothing. So too will I. I have charged these dwarves with the same goal. Speak to them and they will share what they have learned of the dangers that await, and what they have learned of the great wealth that may wait as well.'","'Erebor was recently besieged by a great army of Easterlings, and only when word of the Dark Lord's fall came to their ears did they falter in their attack. Then did Thorin III, the new King under the Mountain, emerge from Erebor and drive them back.\
\
'Not all are pleased with the new king, but I think he will prove a worthy successor to King Dáin, in time. He is heir to Dáin's bloodline; he will do what is best for Durin's Folk in these difficult times. I have heard that the Land of Mordor, far to the south, is now ripe for the taking. King Thorin has issued the call for great heroes to adventure in Mordor on behalf of the dwarves, and that is enough for me to put my trust in him! What treasures of the dwarves might we reclaim from that place?'","After a long journey, you have arrived at Erebor and gained entrance to its halls","Weapons and armour-pieces were brought to this area for accessibility during the siege","'Welcome to the Hall under the Mountain, ${PLAYER}, noble seat of Erebor and pride of Durin's Folk! I understand you have pledged to aid the dwarves as they adventure in Mordor and desire to speak with the king, and I will not stand in your way!\
\
'And yet, King Thorin is currently speaking with his advisors and an audience will have to wait until he is free. Perhaps you can make yourself familiar with these halls while you wait?'","Talk to Foldgráf","Find King Thorin III, in the Hall under the Mountain","'King Thorin should be ready to meet with you now.'","Thorin III is now King under the Mountain, and rules Durin's Folk from Erebor. Now that you have pledged to aid the dwarves as they adventure in Mordor, Dori believes you should meet with Thorin at the Lonely Mountain.","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain","'When Dale was beset by the Dark Lord's northern army, King Dáin emerged from Erebor with his finest warriors and sought to defend our allies, the Dale-men. He fought bravely and long, but it was not enough and he fell beneath the axes of his enemies. With his death, his son Thorin III ascended to the kingship of Durin's Folk, and all looked to him to defeat the Easterlings.'\
\
Margald snorts derisively.\
\
'His first command? He ordered that we retreat into the mountain and bar the gates! Our friends and allies were abandoned, and we relied upon the defences of Erebor to keep us safe! Some of my fellows have taken to calling him 'Stonehelm,' for he pulled the rock of Erebor snugly down upon his ears and thought to wait out our enemies from the safety of our halls. What would Dáin Ironfoot have to say of his son if he were alive to hear of this? Nothing good, I warrant!\
\
'Thorin is now King under the Mountain, and upon my honour as a dwarf I will not speak against him. But neither will I speak against my fellows when they name him Stonehelm, either!'"},
[3010]={"'Muchas disculpas, ${PLAYER}, pero no soy el Thorgnyr que buscas. Estás buscando a mi hermano, también llamado Thorgnyr, que actualmente está de guardia fuera de las Puertas de Durin en la Puerta de Acebeda de Khazad-dûm.'","'¿Así que los problemas dentro de Moria ya han comenzado? No me sorprende que hayan llegado, pero no esperaba que estuvieran sobre nosotros tan pronto. Habría instado a tener más precaución, pero me contuve. Bósi y Brogur son enanos capaces, y no quería escuchar las advertencias de mi corazón.\
\
'Aprobaré esta decisión de ordenar una mayor frecuencia de entregas a Moria. Desde hace mucho tiempo he dicho que la comida se ha enviado demasiado lentamente a las minas, porque cualquier número de obstáculos podría sitiar nuestros suministros, dentro o fuera de las minas.\
\
'Te daré la primera de estas entregas; llévala a Slóthi en la Cámara de la Encrucijada y dile que seguirán más.'","'Thórgnyr y Tulk se encuentran fuera de Moria, cerca de las Puertas de Durin. Habla con Thórgnyr sobre establecer entregas más frecuentes de comida y suministros, porque podríamos necesitarlos antes de lo que esperábamos.'","Thórgnyr se encuentra fuera de Moria, cerca de las Puertas de Durin, junto a la laguna tranquila.\
\
Slóthi quiere asegurarse de que la ruta de suministro fuera de Moria permanezca abierta y que haya suficiente comida dentro de las minas para que los enanos puedan sobrevivir a un largo asedio.","Capitulo 1: Manteniendo la cadena de suministro","Slóthi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Thórgnyr te ha dado la primera de varias entregas de comida para Slóthi, que se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada.","'¿Dónde está la primera entrega? No me has traído nada, pero se necesita rapidez.'","Slóthi está preocupado de que cuando los Orcos ataquen, los enanos puedan quedar aislados del mundo exterior y no puedan sobrevivir a un largo asedio.","Lleva suministros de comida a Slóthi","'Se suponía que debías llevar esos suministros a Slóthi en la Cámara de la Encrucijada y decirle que seguirán más. ¡No lo olvides!'","'Ah, la primera de varias entregas de Thórgnyr, ¿espero? ¡Bien, bien! Esta vez no estaremos aislados del mundo exterior y atrapados desprevenidos. ¡Estaremos preparados para cualquier cosa!'","'Bósi ha intentado mantenerlo en secreto, pero los rumores se propagan rápidamente en los pasajes de Moria. La mayoría de nosotros ya conocemos el destino de Balin. Estaban rodeados: Orcos por el este y por debajo, y la terrible criatura en la piscina junto a la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
'No podemos permitir que eso vuelva a suceder, ${PLAYER}, pero si sucede, es mi responsabilidad asegurarme de que tengamos suficientes suministros para resistir un largo asedio.\
\
'Quiero que salgas de Moria y hables con Thórgnyr justo afuera de las Puertas de Durin; dile que nos envíe toda la comida que pueda y que organice más entregas en un horario regular. No podemos permitirnos estar en la misma situación desesperada que la compañía de Balin. Quiero vernos vengarlos para que puedan descansar en paz bajo las piedras.'"},
[3011]={"Braiglinn está en Imlad Lalaith, en el lado de Lothlórien del río Anduin.\
\
Ha llegado el momento de encontrarse con los miembros de la compañía que llevan a Mazog a Dol Guldur. Debes hablar con Braiglinn cuando estes ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}.","'Ahora debes regresar a Imlad Lalaith y decirle a Braiglinn que hemos asegurado nuestro primer punto de apoyo al otro lado del río. Es hora de que el segundo grupo cruce, ya que son ellos quienes tienen la misión sigilosa de llevar a Mazog a Dol Guldur a cambio de los prisioneros enanos. El oficial de lanzamiento, Calengoth, cerca de los barcos, te llevará de regreso a Lothlórien.\
\
'Me encargaré del resto de los preparativos necesarios para que Echad Sirion sirva como campamento para nuestras primeras excursiones en el Bosque Negro.'","Alfirimbes está esperando para hablar contigo en Echad Sirion, el campamento en las orillas del Anduin, en la frontera del Bosque Negro.\
\
Has conocido a la compañía responsable de llevar a Mazog en secreto a Dol Guldur, y han cruzado al Bosque Negro. Ahora deberías hablar con Alfirimbes.","'Ahora ha comenzado, ${PLAYER}. Para bien o para mal, ahora no tenemos otra opción que embarcarnos en este viaje. Que ambos objetivos de los Malledhrim vean la victoria al final: el rescate de los prisioneros retenidos por el Enemigo en Dol Guldur y el retraso de un ataque desde el Bosque Negro sobre Lothlórien.\
\
'Haremos todo lo que podamos para ver que ambos se cumplan.'","Habla con Braiglinn en Imlad Lalaith","'¿La primera travesía fue un éxito, ${PLAYER}? Eso significa que es hora de que la segunda compañía, más pequeña, cruce el Anduin.\
\
'Te llevaré a conocerlos; después de todo, ayudarás a estos Elfos con el transporte de Mazog a Dol Guldur, y el camino estará lleno de peligros.\
\
'Dime cuando estés ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]}, y te los presentaré.'","Habla con Alfirimbes en Echad Sirion","'Regresa al oficial de lanzamiento, Calengoth, cerca de los barcos, y él te llevará de regreso a Lothlórien para que puedas hablar con Braiglinn. Dile que es hora de la segunda travesía.'","Braiglinn está en Imlad Lalaith, en el lado de Lothlórien del río Anduin.\
\
Alfirimbes está complacido de que la primera travesía haya sido exitosa y te ha enviado a Braiglinn para notificar al grupo responsable de llevar a Mazog a Dol Guldur que ha llegado el momento de su propio cruce.","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para conocer a la compañía responsable de la peligrosa tarea de llevar a Mazog a Dol Guldur a cambio de los prisioneros? Te llevaré a ellos y haré las presentaciones.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no se puede completar con una comunidad.</rgb>","La primera travesía del Anduin por los Malledhrim ha sido un éxito, y ahora es hora de que la compañía encargada de transportar a Mazog también cruce.","Habla con Braiglinn y viaja para encontrarte con los miembros de la compañía","Capítulo 1: Planes de la Hueste Dorada","'Alfirimbes ha comenzado los preparativos para llevar a Mazog fuera de los Lindes Oscuros y más cerca de la fortaleza de Dol Guldur. Habla con ella en el campamento de Echad Sirion, al otro lado del río.'"},
[3012]={"Sporr está esperando fuera de la Cámara de la Encrucijada.\
\
El primo de Sigdan, Sporr, va a hacer una exploración de las vías de acceso a la Cámara de la Encrucijada, buscando cualquier Orco que pueda estar preparándose para atacar.","'¡Bien hecho! ¡Estoy contento de que hayas estado con Sporr cuando tuvo problemas! Mi primo es valiente y valiente, pero algunos desafíos son simplemente demasiado para un solo enano.\
\
'Gracias, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Quizás estaremos listos a tiempo después de todo.'","Has acompañado a Sporr en su ronda","Habla con Sporr","Capítulo 1: Explorando las vías de acceso","'Mi primo Sporr se ha encargado de explorar las vías de acceso a esta cámara para detectar Orcos. Ayúdalo con su patrulla, ${PLAYER}, y te estaré agradecido.'","Sigdan te ha pedido que ayudes a su primo Sporr a hacer una exploración de las vías de acceso a la Cámara de la Encrucijada para detectar cualquier actividad relacionada con los Orcos.","Sigdan se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has acompañado a Sporr en su ronda para detectar Orcos en las vías de acceso a la Cámara de la Encrucijada, y ahora deberías informar a Sigdan.","'¿Crees que estaremos listos para cuando los Orcos nos ataquen? No sé si lo estaremos... si los Orcos supieran lo vulnerables que somos ahora, no se retrasarían. ¡Nos atacarían en la misma hora!\
\
'Mi primo Sporr se ha encargado de explorar las vías de acceso a la Cámara de la Encrucijada; si los Orcos tienen planes de atacarnos pronto, él verá las señales y podrá advertirnos a tiempo.\
\
'Por favor, ve a ayudarlo con su patrulla. Estoy ansioso por que Sporr tenga algo de ayuda, por si algún enemigo desagradable se cruza en su camino.'","'Si tienes buen ojo y brazos fuertes, te daré la bienvenida en mi patrulla, ${PLAYER}. Vamos a hacer una exploración para detectar cualquier Orco que piense que puede sacar ventaja al espiar las vías de acceso a la Cámara de la Encrucijada.'"},
[3013]={"'¿Dices que Melmar encontró el fondo del pozo, y que está seguro de que los Orcos no pueden trepar por él? ¡Eso es una buena noticia! Ahora me preocupa menos su presencia.\
\
¡Podemos salir adelante después de todo, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! Gracias por investigar esto por mí.'","'¡Aquí estamos! ¿Ves ese agujero en el techo de esta cueva, justo encima de nosotros? Es el fondo del pozo en la Cámara de la Encrucijada. Sin embargo, no creo que debamos preocuparnos por los Orcos trepando por él...\
\
'¡Oye! ¡Saca tu arma!'","'No me gusta ese pozo. Miré hacia abajo y no pude ver el fondo, pero estoy bastante seguro de que hay agua allí abajo. Me pone nervioso.\
\
¿Qué pasaría si los Orcos encuentran el fondo del pozo e intentan trepar por él? ¡Podrían usarlo para entrar en esta cámara sin que los centinelas se den cuenta! No necesito decirte lo desastroso que sería eso.\
\
Me sentiría mejor si pudieras encontrar el fondo del pozo y asegurarte de que no hay forma de que los Orcos puedan trepar por él para entrar en esta sala. Melmar fue a buscarlo, pero nunca supe nada de él. No sé cómo llegarás al fondo de forma segura, pero deberías encontrar una manera de bajar a las Obras Hidráulicas y luego buscar a Narag-kheleb, el fondo del pozo. Espero que lo encuentres al suroeste del imponente acueducto en las profundidades. Sin embargo, no te lances al pozo a menos que creas que podrías caer por incontables brazas y aterrizar vivo sobre tus pies.'","El fondo del pozo probablemente se encuentre en algún lugar de las Obras Hidráulicas, en las profundidades de Moria, al suroeste del imponente acueducto. El enano Melmar podría estar en algún lugar cerca del fondo.\
\
Thálfi está preocupado por la posibilidad de que los Orcos puedan trepar desde el fondo del pozo, y quiere que investigues para asegurarte de que eso no sea posible.","Encuentra el fondo del pozo","A Thálfi no le gusta el pozo que se encuentra en el centro de la Cámara de la Encrucijada, y le preocupa que los Orcos puedan trepar por él si las centinelas no están alerta.","'Cualquier cosa que pueda permitir a los Orcos colarse en esta cámara me pone nervioso. Encuentra el fondo de este pozo, en algún lugar de las Obras Hidráulicas al suroeste del gran acueducto, y asegúrate de que los Orcos no puedan trepar por él desde el fondo.\
\
'¡Melmar fue a buscar el fondo! Podrías encontrarlo por ahí abajo.'","Capítulo 1: El fondo del pozo","Thálfi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has encontrado el fondo del pozo pero descubriste que estaba bien protegido, y ahora deberías regresar con Thálfi.","Has defendido a Melmar de sus enemigos."},
[3015]={"'The further conquest of Mordor must wait. Aragorn has business to which he must attend at the White City, and he will want to have us there at his side, ${PLAYER}. Speak to me and we will go together, all of us.'","'I wish to thank you for the great help you have provided to me and to Middle-earth, ${PLAYER}, but it would be premature. I am certain you will continue to lend invaluable service to the Kingdom of Gondor, and I welcome it! Still, I thank you on this day, and will again!\
\
'I am now king, but my thoughts before were ever for the safety of my people and that has not changed. We must preserve the safety of Minas Tirith, and of all Gondor, and to that end I ask that you keep watch on the land of Mordor. By so doing, I hope we can ensure that none of the evils remaining in Sauron's wake can be made to threaten Gondor.\
\
'Venture forth for Gondor, my friend! I await your return with hopeful heart and glad confidence.'","'I did not mean just the two of us, ${PLAYER}. All the Host of the West will return with Aragorn. Do not worry! We shall come back to Mordor and continue our conquest, but this is something that must be done if that is to have the greatest chance of success.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Aragorn and the Kingdom of Gondor, and to fight on their behalf in Mordor.","King Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.","Talk to King Elessar in his throne room","'King Elessar waits for you in his throne room, ${PLAYER}, if you have matters that demand his attention. He will listen to you readily and gladly, I do not doubt!'","Chapter 1: The King and the Steward","Talk to Prince Imrahil and return with him to the White City","Prince Imrahil is outside the Black Gate, waiting to return with you to Minas Tirith."},
[3016]={"Talk to Prince Ingór","Explore the balcony","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.","The hall of Vérnozal was built over, and is powered by, this underground river","'Ah, my friend, ${PLAYER}. We have undertaken many missions together, have we not? Aye, that we have! If we are to reclaim Gundabad for the Zhélruka, I say we will adventure together a great deal more. There is much history to learn of the Mountain-home and old halls to explore beneath the Three Peaks. Speak with Ausma or myself if you wish to carry out a mission.'","Explore the living quarters","Talk to the Zhélruka Clan Quartermaster","Chapter 1: The Rightful Claim","Talk to Zóva","'Good work on dealing with those night-time visitors. There is more work to be done here in Gundabad, and it is a long road that lies ahead of us. At least the travel on this road involves making a home, rather than searching for one.'","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
Prince Ingór wishes for you to explore Vérnozal.","'Welcome, ${CLASS}. I am glad that you are assisting the Zhélruka in Gundabad. Come see me here in Vérnozal when Prince Ingór decides that you deserve to be rewarded for your efforts.'","Explore the waterway","'I am here to assist Hórin and Scout-master Ausma on important missions for the Zhélruka. If you assist us on these missions, I will certainly share the rewards with you, ${CLASS}.'","'You see the potential offered to us by the hall of Vérnozal? Yes, I have seen it too.\
\
'Potential is not enough for the Zhélruka, however! This hall must be a place of beauty, restored to the shining beacon it once was. Right now the hall is covered in dust and crawling with small night-time beasts! Perhaps tonight you could take care of these unwelcome visitors for me.'","Many coming to Gundabad could seek a comfortable shelter here in Vérnozal","Habla con Hórin","'Your first task for the Zhélruka? Familiarize yourself with the hall of Vérnozal. Explore the hall and talk with those you see, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to the Gundabad Missions Quartermaster","From this seat many proclamations were made by the lords of Gundabad","'I knew you would assist our cause!\
\
'Advising Prince Ingór can be difficult at times, but it is always worth the effort. He has a good heart, and wishes only the best for his people. I am certain we will work closely together, for you have his ear as much as I do!'","The view from the balcony over the court is truly impressive","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to the Zhélruka and to fight on their behalf in Gundabad.","'I am pleased that you have pledged to aid the Zhélruka as we work to reclaim Gundabad, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Under my command, the Zhélruka will no longer be a wandering people. As Durin II promised, so long ago, Gundabad shall be the welcoming home of all Zhélruka!\
\
'Now, there is much work to be done. After a brave expedition through Máttugard, we have secured this hall: Vérnozal. It is a place for the Zhélruka to gather as we work to reclaim the Three Peaks of Gundabad. This hall was once the nobles' court and a seat of power in Gundabad. Soon it will be a place of trade and commerce, as well as a refuge of safety, for many frightful beasts and foes still lurk beneath the Three Peaks.\
\
'Your first task for the Zhélruka? Familiarize yourself with the hall of Vérnozal. Explore the hall and speak with those you see, ${PLAYER}.'","Explore the throne"},
[3018]={"Chapter 2 - Lost Ledger","'Aphamâr is not at her post in Rakhatâb. I cannot say what occurred. Please inquire with the Núrut of Rakhatâb about Aphamâr's whereabouts. We must deliver this ledger.'","Zarai provided a general area east along the mountains where a courier lost their delivery. She requires that the satchel reaches Aphamâr, the ledger-keeper of Rakhatâb.","Zarai has a concern that she needs to address. Speak with her in Jax Phanâl.","Find Aphamâr in Râhal Ghol, the upper ward of Umbar Bahârbel.","Find the satchel along the foot of the mountains to the south-east","'Find the satchel somewhere to the south-east beside the mountains and deliver it to Aphamâr. She should be amongst the workers in Rakahtâb.'","'You are a friend, a warden of merit, and a courier too.\
\
'My time at Rakhatâb unceremoniously ended nearly a month ago. Ulanor's sway there will abate. Time and the pits judge all who transgress the Kindred in Umbar Baharbêl; her time will come.\
\
'I have expectantly waited for this delivery from our usual courier. Strangely, you are here, but your legend in Umbar Baharbêl grows as swiftly as the tides in storm.\
\
'For now, ${PLAYER}, this is all I require. When the time is right, we will call upon you again.'","The Ledger-keepers maintain the Books of Balance informing the Kindred of the Coins of the honour gained by the citizens of Umbar Baharbêl. Your name is now entered in the Books of Balance.","'Aphamâr hasn't graced the walkways of Rakhatâb for nearly a moon. Ulanor, the overseer, found her presence untenable.\
\
'Last I heard, Aphamâr returned to Umbar Baharbêl and took residence in the Upper Ward. You may find her there.'","Deliver the runed satchel to Aphamâr at Rahâl Ghol in Umbar Baharbêl","Speak with Núrut in Rakhatâb","Aphamâr is not here; speak with the foreman","'If Aphamâr returned to Umbar Baharbêl, she will be in Rahâl Ghol. That is the uppermost ward in the city. Hurry and deliver the ledger to her.'","Speak with Zarai at her post in Jax Phanâl","Deliver the runed leather satchel to Aphamâr in Rakhatâb","With the satchel recovered you should deliver it to the ledger-keeper Aphamâr in Rakhatâb. You were told she usually stands across the path from the stable-master.","'Our roles, while necessary, breed discontent with some areas of the populace. Some believe, incorrectly, that our records detail all actions undertaken within Umbar Baharbêl and that we expose or trade secrets to the guards or Kindred's enforcers. Some believe we still serve the Heirs of Castamir.\
\
'Neither is true.\
\
'We humbly do our work as a form of penance for the years of torment wrought upon the populace. Self-preservation is a powerful motivator.\
\
'Because of this, our couriers and aides sometimes find themselves the target of ire or worse.\
\
'A courier travelling south toward Rakhatâb was assaulted and lost one of our ledgers during the attack. The courier is well. You needn't concern yourself with their welfare. I require your attention on the ledger.\
\
'While escaping an assailant, the courier stumbled off his mount and ran east toward the mountains. Along the way, he dropped the pack containing my latest ledger. I no longer require the book; I need it delivered to my colleague Aphamâr at Rakhatâb. She usually stands across the path from the stable-master in Rakhatâb.\
\
'Can you do this?'","'It is fortuitous that you return to me. I sent you a letter. I was unsure if it reached you. That is of no matter now.'\
\
She pauses and shifts uncomfortably.\
\
'You prove yourself daily to Umbar Baharbêl. There is a matter that recently came to my attention. I would ask for your aid if you are willing to provide it.'","${PLAYER},\
\
We hope this message finds you well. Your efforts throughout Umbar Baharbêl fill our pages with credibility and nobility unseen in these lands for ages. We are pleased that an ally like you is in our midst.\
\
It is for this reason that I write to you. Your proven capacity for both compassion, discretion, and swift reciprocity are needed. At your earliest convenience, please return to me at Jax Phanâl. There is a matter of import I wish to discuss.\
\
Zarai\
Ledger-keeper of Jax Phanâl","Aphamâr is not where you expected to find her. Núrut of Rakhatâb likely knows her whereabouts. Find and speak with the dwarf near their office at the crest of Rakhatâb.","You collected the runed leather satchel"},
[3019]={"Caebar made a list of the most common complaints of Linhir's townsfolk: foes in Dor-en-Ernil, pests in the town, burned timbers in Linhir, and listening to the concerns of the people.","'I told Caebar to make a list of notable tasks. Meet up with him in Linhir and learn the content of his catalogue of things that need doing. Afterwards, he is to guide the company through Dor-en-Ernil and into the Ringló Vale. Arwen and I will meet up with you there, or in Lamedon if we meet with delays.'","Defeat enemies of Gondor in Dor-en-Ernil or the Ringló Vale, King's Gondor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Examine the sketch of Barad Rill given to you by Caebar","Hear the concerns of Nimdol","'I have sent the rest of the travelling party on to Linhir with instructions to aid the people there. Your report that supporters of the Heirs of Castamir maintained a presence in that city is worrisome to me; perhaps if we can give the townsfolk what help they need we will help reduce support for any of that sort who remain.\
\
'I told Caebar to make a list of notable tasks. Meet up with him in Linhir and learn the content of his catalogue of things that need doing. Afterwards, he is to guide the company through Dor-en-Ernil and into the Ringló Vale. Arwen and I will meet up with you there, or in Lamedon if we meet with delays.'","Caebar gave you a sketch of the lighthouse of Barad Rill, seen in happier days.","'I made that sketch of Barad Rill in much happier days.'","Talk to Uilin at the entrance of Ethring, in King's Gondor","Caebar hands you a time-weathered sketch of the lighthouse of Barad Rill","Caebar is by the eastern entrance of the town of Linhir, in King's Gondor.","Travel to the southern entrance of Ethring, in the Ringló Vale, King's Gondor","Return Caebar's sketch of Barad Rill to him","Uilin stands at the entrance of Ethring, glaring at you and Caebar.","Defeated enemies of Gondor in Dor-en-Ernil or the Ringló Vale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Caebar by the eastern entrance of Linhir, in King's Gondor","'Oh, ${PLAYER}, I am glad to see you, for I am at the end of my wits! The King instructed me to make a list of things we might do to aid the people of Linhir, but everyone I asked had a different idea of where to start! Some are concerned about the foes that still stalk Dor-en-Ernil, to the west of the river. Others claim the pests that inhabit the town have gotten out of control in recent weeks, others say the burned timbers that remain in Linhir pose a risk to the health of the citizenry, and some... well, I think some folk just want to talk.\
\
'I don't know with which of these things you want to start, but the King did say we were to be comprehensive on his behalf! I will see to the burned timbers, but perhaps you can tackle the other items on the list?'","'It is worse than I expected.'","'You took care of everything on the list? You are good at this, aren't you?\
\
'The King asked me to direct everyone through Dor-en-Ernil and into the Ringló Vale, where he and Queen Arwen will rejoin us. I don't know why he chose me for this task... do you think he knows that I was born in Ethring? I might have mentioned it to you once when he was nearby, but surely he would not remember a thing like that!\
\
'The grand lighthouse of Barad Rill is on our way, and I would not mind stopping to see it before we continue on to Ethring. I visited it when I was just a boy and found it most impressive. I heard a disturbing rumour that the lighthouse sustained some damage during the war, but perhaps that talk was exaggerated? I hope so, at any rate.'","Maeriel is worried that some of her neighbours have disappeared","'As we make our way north through Dor-en-Ernil to my hometown of Ethring, let us face whatever foes we encounter with courage and strength, for the King and for Gondor.'","A villager of Ethring glares at you and Caebar with distrust","Chapter 2.10: Caebar","Barad Rill is located to the south-west of Linhir, at the southern point of the peninsula of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.","'Everyone I asked had a different idea of where to start! Some are concerned about the foes that still stalk Dor-en-Ernil, to the west of the river. Others claim the pests that inhabit the town have gotten out of control in recent weeks, others say the burned timbers that remain in Linhir pose a risk to the health of the citizenry, and some... well, I think some folk just want to talk.'","Nimdol is concerned about the increase in pests around Linhir","Caebar's hometown of Ethring is located in the Ringló Vale, north of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.","'It is much worse than I expected, ${PLAYER}. What manner of devilry did the Corsairs of Umbar harness to knock down such a structure as the grand lighthouse? But more than that: how could they bring themselves to do it?\
\
'I did not bring much of my artwork with me when I left for Minas Tirith to join the service of the City as a scribe, but I did bring one piece: a sketch I made of this lighthouse when I was just a boy. Here, you can see it if you like.'","'The grand lighthouse of Barad Rill is on our way, and I would not mind stopping to see it before we continue on to Ethring. I visited it when I was just a boy and found it most impressive. I heard a disturbing rumour that the lighthouse sustained some damage during the war, but perhaps that talk was exaggerated? I hope so, at any rate.'","Travel to Barad Rill, the grand lighthouse in Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor","Caebar has a renewed interest in facing the foes of Gondor that prowl Dor-en-Ernil or the Ringló Vale, in King's Gondor.","Hear the concerns of Forcharn","Talk to Caebar in view of Barad Rill, in King's Gondor","Forcharn is not really worried about anything. He's just lonely","Hear the concerns of Maeriel","Caebar stares at the ruin of Barad Rill with great sadness","Defeat pests in Linhir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated pests in Linhir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'So you're back, are you?'","'So you're back now, Caebar, now that Ethring doesn't need you? Your mother will weep to hear it.\
\
'And who is this stranger? You have the look of an Elf-friend, and that is not a popular thing to resemble in these days.'","Caebar stares at the ruin of Barad Rill at the southern peninsula of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.","'Ah, thank you, ${PLAYER}. The sketch is painful now, but I will keep it close as a reminder of what the enemies of Gondor will not hesitate to take from us. It lifts my spirits to see the construction effort! But I wish it were not necessary.\
\
'As we make our way north through Dor-en-Ernil to my hometown of Ethring, let us face whatever foes we encounter with courage and strength, for the King and for Gondor.'","King Elessar and Queen Arwen's journey westward will next pass into Dor-en-Ernil and the Ringló Vale."},
[3020]={"'My uncle Carlong may be right about me, but he is wrong about the King. King Elessar is a good man, and he wants what is best for Gondor!\
\
'I don't have time to be upset about this, ${PLAYER}. I was given a task by my King, and I am going to see it done. Let us do what we can for the folk of Ethring, and perhaps my mother and my uncle will see that King Elessar is not a pawn of the Elves or of anyone else!'","'You should just return to your King, and take Caebar with you. This is no longer his home.'","A man stands in front of the door to Sirdis's home","'The King and Queen have come to Calembel! It is true, they are here with their entire retinue! I saw them going to speak with Galengam!\
\
'Look for his shop to the north-west, inside the city, and you might catch a glimpse of them. Imagine that: the King and Queen, here in Lamedon! I never would have expected them to travel so far from Minas Tirith, and yet I saw them with my own eyes!'","Find the home of Caebar's mother, Sirdis","Talk to Galengam inside his shop in Calembel, King's Gondor","Garthaben calls excitedly to you south-east of the entrance to Calembel.","'If there was ever any doubt that I sell only the finest of goods, let that doubt now be dispelled! I am to be the personal merchant of the King and Queen of Gondor themselves, as always I dreamed!'","Caebar has returned home to Ethring, but it is not a pleasant homecoming.","She glares at you suspiciously, and says nothing","'It is for the best that Caebar move on. His mother already has... she was forced to do so when he departed.'","'Where was Caebar when the skies turned dark and the sun never rose? He was away in the White City, feasting and drinking fine wine while the rest of us suffered! He spared not a thought for Ethring, and now when things are good he wants to return? Let him try, that's what I say. We have not forgotten.'","Travel to the entrance of Calembel in Lamedon, King's Gondor","Talk to Caebar outside his mother's house in Ethring, in King's Gondor","Chapter 2.11 Welcome and Unwelcome","Caebar has returned to his hometown of Ethring at the King's direction, but the homecoming is not a pleasant one.","She stares at you with cold eyes, and refuses to say anything","Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts is in the south-west corner of Calembel, in King's Gondor.","'I should have come back before now. My family and my friends had to endure the darkness Sauron sent before his armies, just as I did, but they had to do it without the armies of Minas Tirith near at hand. I understand why Uilin is upset. I should go to see my mother, ${PLAYER}. Our house... her house... is to the north, across the bridge and to the right.'","'I don't have time to be upset about this, ${PLAYER}. I was given a task by my King, and I am going to see it done. Let us do what we can for the folk of Ethring, and perhaps my mother and my uncle will see that King Elessar is not a pawn of the Elves or of anyone else!'","Garthaben excitedly calls you over to him","Talk to Caebar at the entrance of Ethring","'It is true that I left home before war seemed certain, but how could I have known how bad things would get? I worried about home every day...'\
\
Caebar casts his eyes to the ground.\
\
'I should have come back before now. My family and my friends had to endure the darkness Sauron sent before his armies, just as I did, but they had to do it without the armies of Minas Tirith near at hand. I understand why Uilin is upset. I should go to see my mother, ${PLAYER}. Our house... her house... is to the north, across the bridge and to the right.'","'She doesn't want to see him.'","Talk to Garthaben south of Calembel, in King's Gondor","Talk to Carlong in front of Sirdis's house","Enter Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts in the south-west corner of Calembel, in King's Gondor","Caebar's mother's house is to the north across the bridge and to the right, in the village of Ethring, in King's Gondor.","'She doesn't want to see you, Caebar. You had better find somewhere else to go.'\
\
Carlong looks at you appraisingly.\
\
'You're with the new King, just as Caebar seems to be? You can keep moving, same as my nephew. We here in Ethring know the Elves are behind putting this Elessar on the throne, and we're not going to let them interfere with life in the Ringló Vale. When Caebar left, it broke his mother's heart... but it broke again when he became a puppet of the Elves. She doesn't want to see him.'","'There is nothing left for me here, and the King and Queen have not arrived. We should move on to Calembel. The King said he might rejoin us in Lamedon.'","The town of Calembel is north-west of the Ringló Vale, in Lamedon, King's Gondor.","'You are not wanted here, and neither is my nephew.'","Galengam is inside his crowded shop in the south-west corner of Calembel, in King's Gondor.","He murmurs that the best way to help Ethring is for you to leave","Caebar wants you to listen to the concerns of Ethring's villagers.","'Caebar left us to make his own way in the world. He could have returned when war seemed unavoidable, but instead he left his mother to fend for herself. Poor Sirdis is fortunate that her brother was here to take care of her, and the rest of the town did what we could.\
\
'Where was Caebar when the skies turned dark and the sun never rose? He was away in the White City, feasting and drinking fine wine while the rest of us suffered! He spared not a thought for Ethring, and now when things are good he wants to return? Let him try, that's what I say. We have not forgotten.'","Hear the concerns of Ethring's villagers (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The man spoke true: the shop is very crowded with King Elessar's retinue","Carlong blocks the way into the home of Caebar's mother, Sirdis.","'Did anyone... did anyone want our help, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
Caebar appears more defeated than you have ever seen him, and you ask what has happened.\
\
'I told my uncle I would leave, if that is what my mother truly wants, but that I would like to retrieve some of the sketches I had left inside when I departed for Minas Tirith. He said... he said when I was gone, my mother burned them all.'\
\
Caebar sighs heavily, and raises his head.\
\
'There is nothing left for me here, and the King and Queen have not arrived. We should move on to Calembel. The King said he might rejoin us in Lamedon.'","Caebar stands outside his mother's house in Ethring, in King's Gondor."},
[3021]={"Chapter 2.12: In the Palace of the Swan","'Galengam has been promised nothing of the kind by either my husband or myself, but he seems so happy that neither of us have the heart to correct him. He is an excitable man, is he not?'","Queen Arwen is inside Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, in Calembel, King's Gondor.","'I can hardly believe my good fortune!'","Talk to King Elessar in Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts","Talk to Queen Arwen in Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts","'How were your travels with Caebar, ${PLAYER}? Were you able to help the folk of Dor-en-Ernil and the Ringló Vale?'\
\
You tell Elessar about Caebar's unfortunate homecoming, and he frowns.\
\
'I am sorry to hear that. The war was not easy for anyone, and I sympathize with the plight of Caebar's family even as I believe they treat him unfairly. I can only hope that in time they will open their hearts to him again.\
\
'Our course now is to speak with Prince Imrahil of Dol Amroth. I have sent Rossaran ahead to prepare our way.'","The Swan-knight Rossaran stands at the western entrance south of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor, waiting to bring you to Prince Imrahil.","The Swan-knight Rossaran waves you to him","'Our course now is to speak with Prince Imrahil of Dol Amroth. I will send Rossaran ahead to prepare our way.'","'I have seen many surprising things in my life, ${PLAYER}, but never did I expect such figures as these to step from the mists of legend into my hall. These are truly days of wonder.\
\
'I have some matters to discuss with King Elessar, but I am pleased you accompanied him to Dol Amroth. I have heard your name recently, and I need you to deal with something personally.'","Talk to Prince Imrahil in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor","King Elessar and Queen Arwen have crossed into Lamedon, and now their sights are set upon Dol Amroth and the Palace of the Swan.","Travel to the western entrance south of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor","'Let us go to speak with Prince Imrahil, my friend. I will bring us by the quickest way. After all, I spent many years in service to this city!'","Prince Imrahil is inside the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor.","Rossaran will meet you and the rest of the company at the western entrance south of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor.","'When I awoke this morning, I did not think I should be made the King's Own Merchant by the afternoon, and yet so it is! Let the passing of the war lead to great wealth and riches for Galengam, personal merchant of the King and Queen of Gondor!'","Talk to Rossaran at the western entrance south of Dol Amroth and travel with him to see Prince Imrahil","King Elessar is inside Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, in Calembel, King's Gondor."},
[3022]={"'Gondor is wide, and the King and Queen will not travel swiftly. They will have reached Imloth Melui by now. Let me speed you upon your way, so you can aid them with utmost haste.'","Talk to Lady Vanyalos in her hall, in King's Gondor","'Not all dreams have the meaning you give to them, Vanyalos, but my people know well that some there are to whom the Valar grant the gift of foresight. \\qGift,\\q I say, but if so it must be an unwelcome one.'\
\
Vanyalos nods unhappily, and Arwen briefly takes her hand.\
\
'None disbelieve you, sweet woman. Your dreams came to pass in the way you foresaw, and great is the pain to grieve, especially when the grieving must begin before the loss is suffered. But to think you might have prevented what the Valar showed to you... can you really believe it might be so? Does the Lady of Imloth Melui stand among the ranks of such as they?'\
\
The expression of guilt on Vanyalos's face disappears, replaced with shock. Arwen continues.\
\
'Of course not, my dear. Let me help you ease this burden. ${PLAYER}, take this bowl and fill it with water from one of the fountains outside the hall. Then add to it some of the water that falls from the heights in the north-western reaches of Imloth Melui. This will help to soothe the mind of Lady Vanyalos.'","Lady Vanyalos is in her hall in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.","King Elessar is in the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor.","Queen Arwen hands you a small ceramic bowl","Fill the bowl with water from a fountain outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos","'Is this Elf-magic, my Queen? The water is cool and refreshing, and even as it passed my lips I confess I felt my burdens lift!\
\
'I cannot thank you enough for your kind words, and for this remedy. I will grieve for my family, and keenly, but you are right: if the dreams of Vanyalos were sent by the Powers, none would think her able to turn aside from them, or prevent the horrors so revealed. That would be arrogance unbefitting the Lady of Lossarnach, or indeed any woman of Gondor.\
\
'Thank you for aiding Queen Arwen with this ritual of Elf-magic, ${PLAYER}. I appreciate what you have done, and will not forget it.'","'My friend Ioreth would tell you no remedy acts as quickly as we might wish, but I hope you will find the comfort you deserve, Vanyalos. Grieve for your husband Forlong, and for your brother Denethor, but think not to carry the blame of what befell them! In that you are blameless, and the fault lies with Sauron who wove it, or with the Valar who thought such dreams might be of use to you.'","Talk to King Elessar in the Imloth Melui guard-house","Talk to Ioreth in the Hall of Lady Vanyalos","'Arwen has taken one of the healers who accompanies us, and the two of them have gone to speak with the Lady Vanyalos. Will you attend them and learn if my Queen's administrations have eased her sorrow? The Hall of Lady Vanyalos is to the east.'","'Even in time of peace, Gondor is wide and travel will take some time! After all, the King desires to speak with as many of his folk as he can, doing whatever might be done to ease their burdens after the war. Speak with him inside and learn what he wishes to accomplish in Imloth Melui before continuing his journey.'","The Hall of Lady Vanyalos is to the east of the tower guard-house in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.","'I am pleased we were able to help.'","King Elessar and Queen Arwen have begun to tour their kingdom so the wounds inflicted during the War of the Ring might be healed.","King Elessar is inside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor.","'How delightful to have been of service! When my Queen asked me to attend her on this tour of the kingdom, I never suspected we would be able to do such good, and so early on the journey! Of course, I never doubted her intent or her ability, but it does remind me of a saying from my youth, when I was just a young girl growing up among the flowers of Imloth Melui. It feels so long ago now, but of course that is natural, is it not? Anyway, this is the saying...'\
\
You should likely return to the King, for once Ioreth begins a story it can often take her a long time to finish it.","'Would that I had no part in this! Then might I grieve as does the rest of Gondor! But I have done as they did not, for I dreamed of what would transpire, and I did nothing to prevent it! It is as if I put the axe in the hand of he who slew my Forlong, or cast the torch that set aflame the city walls behind which my brother Denethor perished! It is as if I, Vanyalos, did these things, by failing to prevent them!'","Chapter 2.1: Elf-queen of Gondor","Enter the Hall of Lady Vanyalos in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor","'Arwen was able to provide some comfort to the Lady Vanyalos? I am pleased to hear it, but it is no surprise to me. She has always had a rare talent for putting folk at ease, which is only one of the reasons for which I am glad she accompanies me on this tour of our kingdom.\
\
'She left me little choice, of course. But it will do Gondor much good to see its Queen.'","Talk to Lady Vanyalos in her hall","Return the ceramic bowl filled with water to Queen Arwen in the Hall of Lady Vanyalos, in King's Gondor","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Arwen accepts the ceramic bowl from you, taking care not to spill any of the liquid within. She passes her hand over the water and speaks quietly.\
\
'Idhido i nin hin, a caetho hend,' she says, and hands the bowl to Lady Vanyalos. She indicates the Lady of Lossarnach should take a sip of the cool waters. When Vanyalos has done so, Arwen smiles.\
\
'My friend Ioreth would tell you no remedy acts as quickly as we might wish, but I hope you will find the comfort you deserve. Grieve for your husband Forlong, and for your brother Denethor, but think not to carry the blame of what befell them! In that you are blameless, and the fault lies with Sauron who wove it, or with the Valar who thought such dreams might be of use to you.'","Talk to Queen Arwen in the Hall of Lady Vanyalos","'I am sure the Queen will do whatever she can to comfort Lady Vanyalos. I will do my best, as well! Perhaps a story of some sort to take her mind from her troubles? I know many such tales! But which one will suffice? Oh, that is a difficult decision to make...'","Ioreth must have seen something in Arwen's expression, for she falls silent","Queen Arwen is in the Hall of Lady Vanyalos, in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.","Fill the bowl with water from the falls in the north-western reaches of Imloth Melui","'The Queen and her healer Ioreth mean well, ${PLAYER}, but they can provide no healing for me. Mine is no ordinary grief! This is not the sorrow of a woman whose husband marched to war and perished there, or that of a woman whose brother ruled a city and fell when it burned.'\
\
The eyes of the Lady Vanyalos shine with tears, but sadness alone does not line her face. Her expression is haunted too by guilt.\
\
'Would that I had no part in this! Then might I grieve as does the rest of Gondor! But I have done as they did not, for I dreamed of what would transpire, and I did nothing to prevent it! It is as if I put the axe in the hand of he who slew my Forlong, or cast the torch that set aflame the city walls behind which my brother Denethor perished! It is as if I, Vanyalos, did these things, by failing to prevent them!'","Arwen asked you to fill the ceramic bowl she gave you with water from one of the fountains outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos and with water from one of the falls in the north-western reaches of Imloth Melui.","The healer Ioreth is deep in discussion with Lady Vanyalos and Queen Arwen","'Oh! ${PLAYER}! I was just telling the Lady Vanyalos that all clouds will surely pass, and even in time of grief there will be a new dawning and the sun will shine out in the morn such as you could never expect in the night-time, when all seemed darkest! It is true that these have been sorrowful days, and many tears have been shed, but it is like I always say: there's a remedy for it, you just have to find the right one! And I learned a great deal about healing remedies when I was just a child in Imloth Melui.\
\
'Yes, I grew up here, among all these flowers. Did I ever tell you that? It is true! Why, when I was just a girl, I never expected to see much further than just down the hill or past that curve in the road, and wouldn't you know that I went on to dwell in Minas Tirith, and in the Houses of Healing there would be a great many ailments that would take more than medicine, but also a soothing word or three! It is like I always say...'","Talk to King Elessar in the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor","'Fill the bowl I gave you with water from one of the fountains outside the hall. Then add to it some of the water that falls from the heights in the north-western reaches of Imloth Melui. This will help to soothe the mind of Lady Vanyalos.'","'I too am concerned about the Kindred of the Coins, ${PLAYER}, but whatever power now controls Umbar is beyond the bay; we must first see to the well-being of our people, while we have the time to do so.\
\
'Already we have come to some of the deepest wounds inflicted by the War of the Ring. The Lady Vanyalos dwells here in sorrow; she is the widow of my fighting companion Forlong, who perished on the Pelennor. Her grief is two-fold, for she also survives another: her brother Denethor, victim of Sauron's manipulations.\
\
'Arwen has taken one of the healers who accompanies us, and the two of them have gone to speak with the Lady Vanyalos. Will you attend them and learn if my Queen's administrations have eased her sorrow? The Hall of Lady Vanyalos is to the east.'","'I appreciate what you have done, and will not forget it.'"},
[3023]={"'This sceptre is indeed an artifact of Cardolan, ${PLAYER}! I recognize this name here and this one. I do not know what they portend, but I do know a reference to Nogbenn when I see it! There is a barrow among the downs with the same name. I believe that if you bring this sceptre to that barrow, evils will be drawn to the corruption that surrounds it. Perhaps destroying those evils will cleanse the sceptre of its darkness! Me? Oh, I will not go. I do not have the fortitude to brave the barrows in such circumstances! That is a younger man's game!'","'I cannot explain why this sceptre fills me with such a feeling of unease, but I tell you that it does! What evils have this rod borne witness to? I do not wish to handle it overlong... aye, take it back, and I thank you.\
\
'You say that it was a sceptre of Cardolan? I would have said it belonged to one of the three ancient kingdoms, it is true, but I do not know how you can be certain it was that one. Some of my people have found artifacts with similar markings as this on Weathertop, the great hill to the west. Indeed, some of the Eglain are there now, if you wish to show it to them and see if they know more. Cythred often spends time on that hill, seeking to solve the mysteries of the past.'","'This is a sceptre from the Kingdom of Cardolan, of that I have little doubt. The Dúnedain of that land did not care for ornamentation, and this rod lacks the decorations I would expect from most other kingdoms. They fought long against the Witch-king, but he proved victorious, in the end. Perhaps that is when the sceptre was taken to Mordor, and it remained there during the long years since?\
\
'The Eglain of the Lone-lands have often found similar artifacts from the three kingdoms. Go to Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands, and ask Frideric the Elder what he can tell you about this heirloom.'","Defeat evil-fascinated wights outside Haudh Nogbenn (2/3)","'That is a most interesting find you've got there! It is rare for such an artifact to lie undisturbed for so long. You say it came from this hill? It must be an heirloom of the kingdom of Arthedain.'\
\
You tell Cythred that you are not sure of its origin, but that the sceptre spent a good deal of time hidden in darkness, and corruption now envelops it.\
\
'Yes, I can feel the sickness of it now. Many artifacts from divided Arnor have fallen into shadow, and the three kingdoms each contested this hill for its strategic usefulness. It is a pity, but we of the Eglain have done what we can to uncover relics of that time and are familiar with their assorted dangers. Wait... do you feel that? Something stirs!'","'Thank you for putting an end to that creature and saving my friend! I will set aside for the moment that the presence of the cursed sceptre also drew that danger upon him in the first place.\
\
'Cythred is older and wiser than I am, but once he gets an idea in his head he does not easily abandon it, despite new discoveries. That is not an artifact of Arthedain. Indeed, I think that the spirit it drew to us confirms my own suspicion. That sceptre has some tie to the Kingdom of Cardolan, which fell beneath the heel of Angmar long ago. You can still see their barrows if you travel south of Bree-town, but I do not recommend it.\
\
'Most of the Eglain do not mingle with the settled folk to the west, but we scholars are a different sort and seek our kind among all peoples. That is why I advise that you travel not to the barrows, but to Bree-town itself. Seek out a man named Newbold Leafcutter at the Scholar's Stair Archives, and he may be able to tell you more about the sceptre than Cythred could.'","Bring the Sceptre of Cardolan to Elrond in Rivendell","Talk to Newbold Leafcutter in the Scholar's Stair Archive","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang, and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Defeat evil-fascinated wights outside Haudh Nogbenn (${NUMBER}/3)","A fallen wooden shield catches your eye outside the entrance to the barrow of Haudh Nogbenn.","'Most of the Eglain do not mingle with the settled folk to the west, but we scholars are a different sort and seek our kind among all peoples. That is why I advise that you travel not to the barrows, but to Bree-town itself. Seek out a man named Newbold Leafcutter at the Scholar's Stair Archives, and he may be able to tell you more about the sceptre than Cythred could.'","Séca is on Weathertop.\
\
You have defended Cythred from an attack, and now his assistant Séca wishes to thank you.","Examine the wooden shield and search Haudh Nogbenn for its owner","Newbold Leafcutter is in the Scholar's Stair Archive in the Town of Bree.","'I have studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang. It bears a powerful corruption, but it was not made in the land of Mordor. It came from elsewhere, and the corruption that envelops it stems from its long stay in the Black Land. If this evil could be cleansed, I believe that Elrond could imbue it with a powerful and vital force for Good.\
\
'Before that can happen, however, we must do something about the corruption that Mordor has worked upon it. There are different methods to accomplish this, though the Wise disagree upon the effectiveness of each. My preferred means for such a cure is to bring the corrupted item to the place where it was made, or to places of some significance upon its path, and to thereby diffuse the foul touch of Mordor that has, in the interim, claimed it. We must learn the story of this heirloom before it came to Mordor.'\
\
The Wizard turns the artifact over in his hands, studying it for some clue to its origin. It is a sceptre, about the length of the Wizard's forearm, and while there are some markings near the clawed orb at its head, the overall impression is of simplicity.\
\
'This is a sceptre from the Kingdom of Cardolan, of that I have little doubt. The Dúnedain of that land did not care for ornamentation, and this rod lacks the decorations I would expect from most other kingdoms. They fought long against the Witch-king, but he proved victorious, in the end. Perhaps that is when the sceptre was taken to Mordor, and it remained there during the long years since?\
\
'The Eglain of the Lone-lands have often found similar artifacts from the three kingdoms. Go to Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands, and ask Frideric the Elder what he can tell you about this heirloom.'","Talk to Séca on Weathertop","The low hum of conversation stops as the sceptre's presence is felt","This small wooden shield is scored with many dents and cracks, and tracks lead toward the entrance to the barrow. Whoever dropped the shield here may be in trouble!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","You catch sight of a battered shield, just outside the entrance to the barrow","Defeated evil-fascinated wights at Haudh Nogbenn (${NUMBER}/3)","Séca of the Eglain told you to consult with Newbold Leafcutter in the Scholar's Stair Archives in the Town of Bree.","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of Cardolan","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Sceptre of Cardolan, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Cythred is on the hill of Weathertop, in the Lone-lands.","Talk to Frideric the Elder in Ost Guruth","'Welcome, ${PLAYER}. It has been many a day since you last came to the Ruin-hold! You must have learned much in your travels, and faced many dangers! What has turned your steps back to the humble home of the Eglain?'\
\
You show the corrupted heirloom to Frideric, and he grimaces.\
\
'I cannot explain why this sceptre fills me with such a feeling of unease, but I tell you that it does! What evils have this rod borne witness to? I do not wish to handle it overlong... aye, take it back, and I thank you.\
\
'You say that it was a sceptre of Cardolan? I would have said it belonged to one of the three ancient kingdoms, it is true, but I do not know how you can be certain it was that one. Some of my people have found artifacts with similar markings as this on Weathertop, the great hill to the west. Indeed, some of the Eglain are there now, if you wish to show it to them and see if they know more. Cythred often spends time on that hill, seeking to solve the mysteries of the past.'","'I will meet you at the Haven of Orladion, ${PLAYER}.'","'I know why you have come, ${PLAYER}. If you are to journey beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, you will need the aid of a light that can pierce the darkness.'\
\
Elrond takes the Sceptre of Cardolan from you and dips it into the font beside him. When the artifact emerges from the glowing circle, light drips soundlessly from it and pools like water in the basin. Not since that forgotten prince stood in the space between his subjects and the Men of Carn Dûm with the moon high has the sceptre shined with such luster. Elrond smiles at the sight, and his voice contains both determination and joy when he speaks again.\
\
'With the Light of Eärendil, you will be able to walk where the shadows lie, and overcome them.'","'Oh dear, ${PLAYER}, what is that? I can see that it is a ruling rod of some sort, a sceptre of Cardolan to my eye, but it is possessed of a sickness that fills me with uneasiness! For that reason I do not want to see it any nearer, but I am also tempted by the promise of historical knowledge. What to do? Ah, give it here, and may the learning be worth the risk!'\
\
Newbold studies the markings near the clawed orb at the top of the sceptre, and his decision is rewarded.\
\
'Ah, this sceptre is indeed an artifact of Cardolan, ${PLAYER}! I recognize this name here and this one. I do not know what they portend, but I do know a reference to Nogbenn when I see it! There is a barrow among the downs with the same name. I believe that if you bring this sceptre to that barrow, evils will be drawn to the corruption that surrounds it. Perhaps destroying those evils will cleanse the sceptre of its darkness! Me? Oh, I will not go. I do not have the fortitude to brave the barrows in such circumstances! That is a younger man's game!'","Talk to Cythred on Weathertop","Frideric the Elder is in Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands.\
\
Mithrandir believes the Eglain of the Lone-lands may know something about the corrupted heirloom of Cardolan you discovered.","Find the Scholar's Stair Archives in Bree-town","Haudh Nogbenn is at the southern tip of the Northern Barrow-downs.\
\
Newbold Leafcutter thinks that evils will be drawn to the sceptre when you bring it to Haudh Nogbenn."},
[3024]={"Greith told you of a number of doors south-west of the Twenty-first Hall that the corrupted key might unlock.","The key does not fit in the lock","'I know why you have come, ${PLAYER}. If you are to journey beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, you will need the aid of a light that can pierce the darkness.'\
\
Elrond takes the Key of the Forgotten from you and dips it into the font beside him. When the artifact emerges from the glowing circle, light drips soundlessly from it and pools like water in the basin. An image rises unbidden in your mind, of the rune-keepers standing in a circle and holding hands in the darkness of Machurful, believing themselves forgotten and preparing for the end. As the key shines brightly in Elrond's hands, the names of those lost dwarves come to mind; they are not forgotten, though their time was long ago. Elrond smiles at the sight of the soft glow, and his voice contains both determination and joy when he speaks again.\
\
'With the Light of Eärendil, you will be able to walk where the shadows lie, and overcome them.'","The key fits cleanly in the lock, and turns! The door is unlocked","Bring the Key of the Forgotten to Elrond in Rivendell","Talk to Greith in the Twenty-first Hall, in Khazad-dûm","'I have studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang. It bears a powerful corruption, but it was not made in the land of Mordor. It came from elsewhere, and the corruption that envelops it stems from its long stay in the Black Land. If this evil could be cleansed, I believe that Elrond could imbue it with a powerful and vital force for Good.\
\
'Before that can happen, however, we must do something about the corruption that Mordor has worked upon it. There are different methods to accomplish this, though the Wise disagree upon the effectiveness of each. My preferred means for such a cure is to bring the corrupted item to the place where it was made, or to places of some significance upon its path, and to thereby diffuse the foul touch of Mordor that has, in the interim, claimed it. We must learn the story of this heirloom before it came to Mordor.'\
\
The Wizard turns the artifact over in his hands, studying it for some clue to its origin. To your eye the heirloom is a stone key, with many angular corners and smooth sides.\
\
'The origin of this artifact is no mystery, ${PLAYER}, for its shape and the runes upon it state as clearly as possible from where it came. This key opens a door in Moria, in Khazad-dûm.\
\
'But which door and where? That will be the real mystery. Perhaps the best place to start is with the Iron Garrison. Look for dwarves in the Twenty-first Hall that proclaim themselves lock-masters, and they will no doubt have a catalogue of locks to which this key may fit. Unlocking the door may cleanse the key of its corruption.'","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Key of the Forgotten, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Unlock the door south-west of the Twenty-first Hall with the Corrupted Key","'For now, let us try the key in doors to the south-west of here. A series of staircases descend, and there are locked doors on many of the levels. This strange key may unlock one of them.'","'The origin of this artifact is no mystery, ${PLAYER}, for its shape and the runes upon it state as clearly as possible from where it came. This key opens a door in Moria, in Khazad-dûm.\
\
'But which door and where? That will be the real mystery. Perhaps the best place to start is with the Iron Garrison. Look for dwarves in the Twenty-first Hall that proclaim themselves lock-masters, and they will no doubt have a catalogue of locks to which this key may fit. Unlocking the door may cleanse the key of its corruption.'","'Perhaps this one? It is worth trying, anyway.'","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of Khazad-dûm","Talk to Greith outside the unlocked door and explore beyond","Greith is outside the unlocked door in Khazad-dûm, south-west of the Twenty-first Hall and down many levels.","'By my beard, it worked! The door is unlocked. Are you ready to see what lies within? Speak to me when you are ready, and we can open the door together! I do not know what to expect. Treasure perhaps? Let us hope so, if Durin smiles!'","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","'I will meet you at the Haven of Orladion, ${PLAYER}.'","'Let us open the door and see what lies beyond it!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'If you are seeking the master of locks himself, you have found him! I am Greith, and I have taken it upon myself to open every last one of the hidden chambers of Khazad-dûm! Progress is slow, for now, but it would be slower for any other! Have you discovered a door that needs opening?'\
\
You tell Greith that you have the opposite problem: a key but no door.\
\
'Ah, then you truly have come to the right dwarf, for I know of several such doors that might be opened by this key you carry. But what is wrong with it? It causes a sickness to rise in me, and I feel a terrible dread in its presence! This is very unusual for a dwarf, and upsetting. If the key is possessed of such corruption, what evils might lie behind the door it opens?\
\
'We will worry about that when we stand in the threshold... if even then! For now, let us try the key in doors to the south-west of here. A series of staircases descend, and there are locked doors on many of the levels. This strange key may unlock one of them.'","Talk to Greith outside the unlocked door south-west of the Twenty-first Hall and down many levels","The key almost fits in the lock... but not quite","Greith is outside the unlocked door south-west of the Twenty-first Hall and down many levels, in Khazad-dûm.","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Greith in the Twenty-first Hall considers himself a master of locks and keys and is always telling people so.\
\
Mithrandir thinks that finding the door unlocked by the corrupted key might cleanse the heirloom of its evil."},
[3025]={"'I know why you have come, ${PLAYER}. If you are to journey beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, you will need the aid of a light that can pierce the darkness. Now that this rigging-hook has been cleansed of the corruption that settled upon it, perhaps it can serve that purpose for you.'\
\
Elrond takes the Anchor of the Past from you and dips it into the font beside him. When the artifact emerges from the glowing circle, light drips soundlessly from it and pools like water in the basin. Elrond smiles at the sight, and his voice contains both determination and joy when he speaks again.\
\
'With the Light of Eärendil, you will be able to walk where the shadows lie, and overcome them.'","'You are the Mariner here, my friend, and if you say this artifact is a rigging-hook of the sort used by sailors I will not say otherwise! But this symbol here tells me where you should begin your investigation, for these markings seem to indicate a number of buildings built upon a bridge over a rapidly-flowing river. Whoever once owned this rigging-hook may have operated out of Osgiliath. Now that the Host of the West has passed through the city, it should be safe to ask sailors in that city if they know about this artifact.'","'I will meet you at the Haven of Orladion, ${PLAYER}.'","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of Osgiliath","Find a sailor in Osgiliath who knows about the corrupted rigging-hook","'What's that? You think I might know something about a rigging-hook? Most captains and every mate need one, which you'd know if you were truly a Mariner. I cannot give you mine, if you've broken yours. I still make my living on the river, or would do if there weren't Orcs still hiding in the city and along the river-banks.'\
\
Nathlad turns the rigging-hook over in his hands, and a dark cloud passes across his features.\
\
'Wait... I do know this particular hook. How did you come by it, and why does it fill me with such a feeling of dread?'\
\
You stare Nathlad in the eye and say that you can tell him some of the story, but you want to know what he knows about it first. He sighs.\
\
'Well, I am not going to tell you here. There's work that needs doing. I'll tell you what you want to know, but you are going to need to help me first. Otherwise we will go around in circles, and no one will learn anything. Do we have an agreement?'","'I have studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang. It bears a powerful corruption, but it was not made in the land of Mordor. It came from elsewhere, and the corruption that envelops it stems from its stay in the Black Land. If this evil could be cleansed, I believe that Elrond could imbue it with a powerful and vital force for Good.\
\
'Before that can happen, however, we must do something about the corruption that Mordor has worked upon it. There are different methods to accomplish this, though the Wise disagree upon the effectiveness of each. My preferred means for such a cure is to bring the corrupted item to the place where it was made, or to places of some significance upon its path, and to thereby diffuse the foul touch of Mordor that has, in the interim, claimed it. We must learn the story of this heirloom before it came to Mordor.'\
\
The Wizard turns the artifact over in his hands, studying it for some clue to its origin.\
\
'The metal with which it is made is bronze, and fashioned into a hook of some kind. I cannot identify the purpose of this artifact. Perhaps there is none, and it was merely a decorative element of a larger piece?'\
\
You cannot help but smile, for while the Wizard may not have seen this type of artifact before, to your eye it is most familiar. You tell Gandalf that the artifact is a rigging-hook, used by Mariners to rapidly descend along the ropes of their vessels without burning the palms of their hands, made of bronze so it will not rust in the damp.\
\
'You are the Mariner here, my friend, and only a fool would not defer to your wisdom on such matters! But this symbol here tells me where you should begin your investigation, for these markings seem to indicate a number of buildings built upon a bridge over a rapidly-flowing river. Whoever once owned this rigging-hook may have operated out of Osgiliath. Now that the Host of the West has passed through the city, it should be safe to ask sailors in that city if they know about this artifact.'","Talk to Nathlad in Osgiliath and learn what he knows of the corrupted rigging-hook","Nathlad in Osgiliath is waiting for to agree to help him with his work before he tells you what he knows of the rigging-hook you recovered from Mordor.","'Very well, are you ready to help me with my work? I will tell you what I know, and you will tell me what you know, and we must each be satisfied.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Anchor of the Past, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption, it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Mithrandir believes you should ask sailors in Osgiliath if they know the story of the rigging-hook you found in Mordor.\
\
Now that soldiers of the Host of the West have passed through Osgiliath, the city should be reasonably safe for you to search for such a sailor.","Bring the Anchor of the Past to Elrond in Rivendell"},
[3026]={"'The cold water of the Misty Mountains had no lasting effect upon the corruption that grips the cup of Rhudaur? That was always a possibility. There is one other road available to us, but it travels to a dangerous place where much evil was done both long ago, and more recently. I speak of the Rhudauran Lost Temple.\
\
'The cup must be brought to the innermost chamber of the temple and set upon the dais. If the evil is then cleansed, you may return with it here and I will imbue it was a force for Good. Otherwise, young Burglar, you must leave it behind.\
\
'Speak to me when you are ready to depart for the temple, and I will have further advice for you.'","'I sense that you have brought an artifact of great evil to my house, ${PLAYER}. It is not the first time that an object of great power and evil has been brought here over my complaints, nor is it the most evil, but still I am not pleased at this transgression. Who gave you the idea this was acceptable? No, do not answer me. I know the advice of Wizards when it comes unhappily near. You may as well show me this thing, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
You hand the small cup to Elrond and he studies it with distaste.\
\
'Yes, this cup remained in Mordor for many years, but the corruption that encircles it has roots long before it came to the Black Land. Cups of this type were used in sacrifices committed by priests of Rhudaur in their evil ceremonies. Do not drink from it!\
\
'It may be that the pure cold water of the Misty Mountains can cleanse the evil from it. Near the source of the Bruinen in the mountains north of Rivendell you will find a series of waterfalls. Fill the cup at each of these, and defeat any creatures that draw near. By that process, it could be that the cup will be cleansed of its evil.'","Elrond is in his library in Rivendell, waiting to advise you about your journey to the Lost Temple to cleanse the cup of Rhudaur.","Elrond can be found in the library of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.","'This cup is quite plain, but the clay from which it was fashioned is of a type that was oft-used among the hill-men that populated Rhudaur during the days of that kingdom's ascension. Elrond may know more, for the Last Homely House is hidden not far from the reaches of old Rhudaur. Yes, speak to Elrond, and learn what he may know of this heirloom of Rhudaur.'","Talk to Elrond in his library in Rivendell","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of Rhudaur","Elrond is in the library of Rivendell.","The course of the Bruinen in the Misty Mountains falls in three levels before it comes out of the mountains.\
\
Elrond asked you to fill the cup of Rhudaur with cold, clear water from waterfalls in the Misty Mountains, and to defeat any creatures drawn by its corruption.","Talk to Elrond and travel to the Lost Temple to cleanse the Cup of Rhudaur","Fill the Cup of Rhudaur at waterfalls near the Bruinen source and defeat the creatures drawn by its evil (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Cup of Sacrifice and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","'The Lost Temple should be empty, and you should have no difficulty reaching its innermost chamber. But listen to these words of caution! I have known burglars to occasionally have difficulty leaving well enough alone. If you can resist touching anything while you make your way to the inner chamber, the venture should pass without incident. But if you cannot...'\
\
Elrond looks at you sternly and lets the rest of the sentiment hang in the air, unspoken.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","The beast falls, free of the evil that compelled it to attack","'I have studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang. It bears a powerful corruption, but it was not made in the land of Mordor. It came from elsewhere, and the corruption that envelops it stems from its long stay in the Black Land. If this evil could be cleansed, I believe that Elrond could imbue it with a powerful and vital force for Good.\
\
'Before that can happen, however, we must do something about the corruption that Mordor has worked upon it. There are different methods to accomplish this, though the Wise disagree upon the effectiveness of each. My preferred means for such a cure is to bring the corrupted item to the place where it was made, or to places of some significance upon its path, and to thereby diffuse the foul touch of Mordor that has, in the interim, claimed it. We must learn the story of this heirloom before it came to Mordor.'\
\
The Wizard turns the artifact over in his hands, studying it for some clue to its origin. To your eye the heirloom is a small and mostly featureless cup. Then you see that a single blood-red ruby is mounted on one face of the cup, and you marvel that no enterprising Orc in Mordor ever sought to remove the valuable gem. Mithrandir seems to know your thought.\
\
'Yes, the stone is precious, but that is not what has caught my eye. This cup is very plain, otherwise, but the clay from which it was fashioned is of a type that was oft-used among the hill-men that populated Rhudaur during the days of that kingdom's ascension. Elrond may know more, for the Last Homely House is hidden not far from the reaches of old Rhudaur. Yes, speak to Elrond, and learn what he may know of this heirloom of Rhudaur.'","You fill the cup with cold water, but the corrupting evil remains","'It is good that you have cleansed the corruption from the Cup of Sacrifice, ${PLAYER}, for if you are to journey beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, you will need the aid of a light that can pierce the darkness. Did you follow my advice within the Lost Temple and touch nothing?'\
\
Before you can answer, Elrond takes the Cup of Sacrifice from you and dips it into the font beside him. When the artifact emerges from the glowing circle, light drips soundlessly from it and pools like water in the basin. Never in all its long years has the cup been filled with such joyful purpose, and the radiance contained within blinds the eye and lifts the heart to song. Elrond smiles at the sight, and his voice is filled with determination when he speaks again.\
\
'With the Light of Eärendil, you will be able to walk where the shadows lie, and overcome them.'","Bring the Cup of Sacrifice to Elrond in Rivendell","'I will meet you at the Haven of Orladion, ${PLAYER}.'","'It may be that the pure cold water of the Misty Mountains can cleanse the evil from the cup of Rhudaur. Near the source of the Bruinen in the mountains north of Rivendell you will find a series of waterfalls. Fill the cup at each of these, and defeat any creatures that draw near. By that process, it could be that the cup will be cleansed of its evil.'","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Talk to Elrond in the library of Rivendell"},
[3027]={"Bring the Seeds of Defiance to Elrond in Rivendell","Talk to Rhothlas and hear his tale","'You come to help Jorthkyn? Always welcome! But what is that you have?'\
\
You show Aarnikka the sealed leather bag, and he recoils.\
\
'Not seen one of those since long ago! Used to be many Jorthkyn had pouches like that. Do not remember why, but someone gave them to us. But this one... something wrong. Feels bad to be near. Where did little Lore-master find?'\
\
You tell Aarnikka that the bag must have spent a long time in Mordor, and the evil of that place has corrupted it, but you hope to cleanse it of its corruption.\
\
'Would be nice if could, little Lore-master. I do not remember why Jorthkyn had pouches like that. It makes me sad to forget. Makes me sad to see this one twisted for evil. Do not know why.'","'Maybe show to Aarnikka. Hope for shiny things inside may help him try to open. Also ask Santtu about pouch. He carry skulls on path through canyon, see much. May know.'","A pack of hunting Wargs has been drawn to you by the evil emanating from the corrupted pouch.","Defeated evil-fascinated Wargs (${NUMBER}/3)","You hear a curious creaking sound coming from the south-west side of the pond","There is a pond in the North Downs, in the south-east corner of Nan Amlug East, where the Rauta-lehmä gather. Santtu told you Trotsiv was going to go there, but he is worried that something happened to him because the pond is very near to Kar Lak, war-camp of the Rauta-lehmä.","'Kar Lak is far to the south. Pond there is sacred for Jorthkyn, but Rauta-lehmä make it dangerous to go.'","Find the pond revered by the Rauta-lehmä near Kar Lak, in Nan Amlug East","Defeat evil-fascinated Wargs at the pond near Kar Lak (2/3)","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Earth-kin","Talk to Chief Tuokki at Lehmä-koti","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Seeds of Defiance, and should bring them now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Chief Tuokki is at the Earth-kin village of Lehmä-koti, in the Ram Dúath, south of Angmar.","'You come to Suuri-lehmä village to lend your strength? If strength measured in wit or in learning, maybe so! Jorthkyn have strength to spare.'\
\
You show Chief Tuokki the sealed leather bag and ask if he can use his great strength to untie the knot that binds it shut. His smile turns to a frown as he tries and fails to untie it.\
\
'This is trick? Some magic keeps pouch closed. Not nice of little Lore-master to play tricks. I forgive your joke. Strange to have pouch of Jorthkyn make, but not be Jorthkyn. Very old. Not seen one in long time, since before we came to Lehmä-koti.\
\
'Maybe show to Aarnikka. Hope for shiny things inside may help him try to open. Also ask Santtu about pouch. He carry skulls on path through canyon, see much. May know.'","'Hoom... you are not like the others that came to this place. What brings you to the still water? I do not count time the way you do, hoom, hum. I have been standing here, drinking water and feeling the sun. Many creatures came to this place, and many creatures left. One remained. The skin you carry was his. What is the word? Bag? Pouch? A container for carrying. When he stayed behind, he became part of the earth. Hoom.\
\
'My name is not one you could speak. You could call me Rhothlas, or Rattleleaf if you prefer to say so. I can tell you what I saw, if you want to hear, hum, hoom, toom.'\
\
His rumbling ends, and there is silence. You decide that he is waiting for you to answer.","Talk to Aarnikka in Lehmä-koti","'I will tell you some of what I saw. No one will speak of the one who remained if I do not.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'I have studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang. It bears a powerful corruption, but it was not made in the land of Mordor. It came from elsewhere, and the corruption that envelops it stems from its long stay in the Black Land. If this evil could be cleansed, I believe that Elrond could imbue it with a powerful and vital force for Good.\
\
'Before that can happen, however, we must do something about the corruption that Mordor has worked upon it. There are different methods to accomplish this, though the Wise disagree upon the effectiveness of each. My preferred means for such a cure is to bring the corrupted item to the place where it was made, or to places of some significance upon its path, and to thereby diffuse the foul touch of Mordor that has, in the interim, claimed it. We must learn the story of this heirloom before it came to Mordor.'\
\
The Wizard turns the object over in his hands, studying it for some clue to its origin. To your eye it is a simple bag of leather, sealed with a strap of cord tied in a simple-looking knot. Mithrandir sets his fingers to untying the knot, but the cord resists his efforts. He frowns.\
\
'There is more here than appears at first, ${PLAYER}, for untying this knot should be a simple matter, yet is not. There is some power at work here that keeps the bag sealed. When I shake it I hear a sound as of small stones; the bag is not empty, but what it contains will remain secret until the bag is opened.\
\
'I have seen bags of this type in the possession of Earth-kin, such as those that live at Lehmä-koti in the Ram Dúath, south of Angmar. Speak to their chief and perhaps he will be able to open the bag and remove the corruption that surrounds it.'","Defeat evil-fascinated Wargs at the pond near Kar Lak (${NUMBER}/3)","You hear the snarls of a pack of hunting Wargs, drawn by the corruption","Talk to Santtu in Lehmä-koti","'I know why you have come, ${PLAYER}. If you are to journey beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, you will need the aid of a light that can pierce the darkness.'\
\
Elrond takes the pouch from you and easily unties the cord that kept it shut. With a solemn expression, he shakes the contents of the pouch onto his palm: a number of unusual seeds.\
\
'I have not seen seeds such as these for thousands of years, ${PLAYER}. How came they to survive? It must have taken a dedicated caretaker to ensure they were not lost or destroyed, for many seeds are not properly valued if the fruit of their growth is not clear or known. I shall see that these seeds are planted. May they last beyond the Age!'\
\
Elrond holds the empty pouch and dips it into the font beside him. When it emerges from the glowing circle, light drips soundlessly from it and pools like water in the basin. An image rises unbidden in your mind: Trotsiv standing alone against the others of his kind, only he remembering the duty with which they were charged. Now the pouch he carried shines as brightly as his defiance; his duty will be fulfilled at last. Elrond smiles, and his voice contains both determination and joy when he speaks again.\
\
'With the Light of Eärendil, you will be able to walk where the shadows lie, and overcome them.'","'I will meet you at the Haven of Orladion, ${PLAYER}.'","Rhothlas is standing among the trees near the pond in Nan Amlug East, below Kar Lak.","Talk to Rhothlas by the pond near Kar Lak","You have found an Ent near a pond in the North Downs.","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","'There is more here than appears at first, ${PLAYER}, for untying this knot should be a simple matter, yet is not. There is some power at work here that keeps the bag sealed. When I shake it I hear a sound as of small stones; the bag is not empty, but what it contains will remain secret until the bag is opened.\
\
'I have seen bags of this type in the possession of Earth-kin, such as those that live at Lehmä-koti in the Ram Dúath, south of Angmar. Speak to their chief and perhaps he will be able to open the bag and remove the corruption that surrounds it.'","Aarnikka and Santtu can be found in the village of Lehmä-koti and may know something about the corrupted pouch.","'What do you have? Where did you find pouch belonging to Trotsiv?'\
\
Santtu sees your puzzled expression and tries to explain.\
\
'Many Jorthkyn used to have pouches like that, but that was long time ago. Only Trotsiv still had his, very fond of it. Went away to pond where skulls gather, to south-east, but that is near Kar Lak. Trotsiv did not return. If you have pouch now, I think Trotsiv never coming back.'"},
[3028]={"Talk to Morhald in Haragmar","'This sculpture was carved from a bone or tusk, but I cannot say what creature lent the material used in its manufacture. Some of the details have worn away with the passage of time or ill treatment. The face, for example, may once have been carved but now cannot be distinguished. There seem to be some runes on the base of the carving, but they are quite faded and I cannot read them clearly.\
\
'But this is not the first such carving I have seen! No, I have seen others of its type drawn from the swamps of the Lone-lands. The Eglain plumb the depths of the marsh for artifacts and trinkets, and in the muck they have found similar sculptures. Go to Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands, and ask Frideric the Elder what he can tell you about this heirloom.'","Talk to Aric the Stone-speaker and travel to the Spring of the Red-maid","'This carving is well-made, and very beautiful despite the grooves and scratches of wear, but as I gaze upon it I am overcome with an unpleasant sensation. Were it not for the sickening feeling with which it fills me, I would say this was very similar to other carvings my people have pulled from the swamp. Even now, some of the Eglain search the damp muck and tussocks of earth for artifacts such as this. Find Morhald and Cólbyr in Haragmar, and they may be able to tell you more of this carving's making.'","'Did you see this writing? The words are very faded and I cannot make them out, but an expert in such things might fare better. Seek Aric the Stone-speaker, far to the south in Harloeg. He may be able to tell you more.'","Talk to Walgar in Haragmar","Morhald and Cólbyr search the Haragmar east of Ost Guruth for artifacts such as the one that has come into your possession.","'This is a beautiful carving, ${PLAYER}! What a shame that the swamp has worn away some of the details, for it seems to me that the subject of the sculptor's gaze was quite striking. See too the martial skill with which she raises the spear, ready to face some unseen foe? This must have been carved from life, or the artist was a master to have carved from memory.\
\
'The sight of it makes me uncomfortable, but I do not understand why. Is it the knowledge that such a work is beyond my skill or some other unknown reason? Take it away, I do not wish to look upon it any longer!'","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Eglain","Aric the Stone-speaker is at Ost Haer, far to the south of Haragmar.","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Image of the Champion, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Frideric the Elder is in Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands.\
\
Mithrandir believes that the corrupted heirloom you have recovered has some connexion to the Eglain of the Lone-lands.","'Welcome, ${PLAYER}. It has been many a day since you last came to the Ruin-hold! You must have learned much in your travels and faced many dangers! What has turned your steps back to the humble home of the Eglain?'\
\
You show the corrupted heirloom to Frideric and he grimaces.\
\
'This carving is well-made, and very beautiful despite the grooves and scratches of wear, but as I gaze upon it I am overcome with an unpleasant sensation. Were it not for the sickening feeling with which it fills me, I would say this was very similar to other carvings my people have pulled from the swamp. Even now, some of the Eglain search the damp muck and tussocks of earth for artifacts such as this. Find Morhald and Cólbyr in Haragmar, and they may be able to tell you more of this carving's making.'","'Why do you search for me with such concern, ${PLAYER}? I am one of the Eglain, hearty and proud walkers of the wilderness. What do you have there?'\
\
You show Walgar the sculpture of the spear-wielding woman. As he takes the carving, he shudders briefly, but sets aside the momentary revulsion and continues with his examination of the sculpture.\
\
'It is hard to say for certain, but I believe I have seen carvings such as this before. Do you see the distinctive strokes on the arm that holds the spear? The definition of the muscle can plainly be seen, despite the passage of Time and the harsh work of the elements. A master craftsman once lived in this land, and though his name has been forgotten, this is clearly his work. Other statues and carvings made by his hand have been found in Haragmar and elsewhere.'\
\
Walgar turns over the carving and squints at the base.\
\
'Did you see this writing? The words are very faded and I cannot make them out, but an expert in such things might fare better. Seek Aric the Stone-speaker, far to the south in Harloeg. He may be able to tell you more.'","Talk to Cólbyr in Haragmar","Bring the Image of the Champion to Elrond in Rivendell","'Did you find this sculpture among the reeds of Haragmar? It appears well-made, if soiled by the passage of Time and the mistreatment of the swamp.'\
\
Morhald shudders and withdraws his hand, recoiling as if stung by a biting insect.\
\
'A feeling of evil emanates from this object! Where did you find it, and why have you brought it to me?'","Habla con Aric el Intérprete de Piedras en Harloeg","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption, it could be empowered with a force for Good.","'Ah, you have found a carving of the warrior-woman!'\
\
Aric takes the sculpture and studies it closely.\
\
'I have spent long enough in the company of the Dead to learn something of their history and secrets, ${PLAYER}. This is a carving of Darothild, a great champion who lived in this land, long ago. When the Lady of the Fountain fell to evil, Darothild was one of the few who sought to challenge her when no others would. Great champion though she was, she never returned from the Spring. Some of the Eglain still tell her story to their children, though doubtless many of the details have changed over the years.\
\
'Many carvings of Darothild have been found, but none have been as wreathed in evil-feeling as this. Perhaps if you bring it to the site of her last battle, the corruption could be cleansed? If not, at least you might leave it there in memory of her. Speak to me and I will find strong Eglain to accompany you.'","'I have studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang. It bears a powerful corruption, but it was not made in the land of Mordor. It came from elsewhere, and the corruption that envelops it stems from its long stay in the Black Land. If this evil could be cleansed, I believe that Elrond could imbue it with a powerful and vital force for Good.\
\
'Before that can happen, however, we must do something about the corruption that Mordor has worked upon it. There are different methods to accomplish this, though the Wise disagree upon the effectiveness of each. My preferred means for such a cure is to bring the corrupted item to the place where it was made, or to places of some significance upon its path, and to thereby diffuse the foul touch of Mordor that has, in the interim, claimed it. We must learn the story of this heirloom before it came to Mordor.'\
\
The Wizard turns the artifact over in his hands, studying it for some clue to its origin. To your eye the heirloom is a small carved sculpture of a woman. One hand is raised before her, as if in warding, and in the other she holds a spear ready to throw.\
\
'This sculpture was carved from a bone or tusk, but I cannot say what creature lent the material used in its manufacture. Some of the details have worn away with the passage of time or ill treatment. The face, for example, may once have been carved but now cannot be distinguished. There seems to be some runes on the base of the carving, but they are quite faded and I cannot read them clearly.\
\
'But this is not the first such carving I have seen! No, I have seen others of its type drawn from the swamps of the Lone-lands. The Eglain plumb the depths of the marsh for artifacts and trinkets, and in the muck they have found similar sculptures. Go to Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands, and ask Frideric the Elder what he can tell you about this heirloom.'","Talk to Frideric the Elder in Ost Guruth","'I will meet you at the Haven of Orladion, ${PLAYER}.'","'I will find strong Eglain to go with you. Me? No, not me! I am a scholar, not a warrior! But some may be found who can accompany you. We will see if Walgar has returned to Ost Guruth and would like to go with you. He will be very interested to learn that this is a carving of Darothild, about whom he surely heard tales when he was a child.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Aric the Stone-speaker is in Harloeg, far south of Ost Guruth.","'I know why you have come, ${PLAYER}. If you are to journey beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, you will need the aid of a light that can pierce the darkness.'\
\
Elrond takes the Image of the Champion from you and dips it into the font beside him. When the artifact emerges from the glowing circle, light drips soundlessly from it and pools like water in the basin. Not since she stood alone against the Red-maid has Darothild shined as brightly. Elrond smiles at the sight, and his voice contains both determination and joy when he speaks again.\
\
'With the Light of Eärendil, you will be able to walk where the shadows lie, and overcome them.'","More of the Eglain may be imperiled in the swamp of Haragmar."},
[3029]={"Talk to Gwíniel in Annúminas","'I have studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang. It bears a powerful corruption, but it was not made in the land of Mordor. It came from elsewhere, and the corruption that envelops it stems from its long stay in the Black Land. If this evil could be cleansed, I believe that Elrond could imbue it with a powerful and vital force for Good.\
\
'Before that can happen, however, we must do something about the corruption that Mordor has worked upon it. There are different methods to accomplish this, though the Wise disagree upon the effectiveness of each. My preferred means for such a cure is to bring the corrupted item to the place where it was made, or to places of some significance upon its path, and to thereby diffuse the foul touch of Mordor that has, in the interim, claimed it. We must learn the story of this heirloom before it came to Mordor.'\
\
The Wizard turns the artifact over in his hands, studying it for some clue to its origin. To your eye the heirloom is a small badge or medal, reminiscent of tokens worn by soldiers standing at their posts.\
\
'There is a a slight depression here, ${PLAYER}, but it has been worn smooth by the passage of Time and the edges are difficult to discover. Even so, I can feel enough of the indentation to state with certainty that it was once in the shape of a star with five points.\
\
'To my mind, that marks this badge as having once belonged to a guard of High King Elendil, perhaps at Annúminas, the seat of his power in the North. Bring it to that city, and see if you can cleanse the corruption that now encircles it. Techeron of the Dúnedain has returned to Annúminas to keep the peace there and may be able to help you.'","Techeron sent you to find the Steadfast Sisters in Annúminas, to see if they have seen any badges identical to the one that came out of Mordor.","Talk to Línneth in Annúminas","Bring the Badge of Ariant to Elrond in Rivendell","'There is a a slight depression in the centre of the heirloom, ${PLAYER}, but it has been worn smooth by the passage of Time and the edges are difficult to discover. Even so, I can feel enough of the indentation to state with certainty that it was once in the shape of a star with five points.\
\
'To my mind, that marks this badge as having once belonged to a guard of High King Elendil, perhaps at Annúminas, the seat of his power in the North. Bring it to that city, and see if you can cleanse the corruption that now encircles it. Techeron of the Dúnedain has returned to Annúminas to keep the peace there, and may be able to help you.'","Colm Fettering is a tomb-robber of some notoriety on the island of Rantost, in Lake Evendim, and may tell you more about the corrupted badge.","Techeron returned to Echad Garthadir in Annúminas following the War of the Ring.\
\
Mithrandir believes that the corrupted badge came at first from Annúminas in the days of High King Elendil.","'It is good to see you again, my friend! The life of a warden is never uneventful, for there are always good folk that need defending. How many minutes of celebration did we have before Aragorn began to worry that the folk of his kingdom were still not secure from threat? Two? Three?'\
\
Techeron laughs.\
\
'Ours is a life of service, ${PLAYER}, and I would have it no other way. I never had the patience for tending crops or raising animals, but I could stand in a spear-line opposed to evil for days without complaint. But what brings you hither?'\
\
You show the corrupted badge to Techeron and he studies it closely.\
\
'I have seen medals similar to this in the old city! They were worn by the soldiers of Elendil, and served as identification for his guards. But I cannot say that I have seen one exactly like this, for there are some curious markings beneath the depression, here. One unfamiliar with the workings of the soldiery could easily have missed it.\
\
'Several of my fellow Rangers are on patrol throughout the city. Bring it to Línneth, Carastír, and Gwíniel in Annúminas, and see if the Steadfast Sisters have seen any badges identical to this.'","Talk to Techeron and walk with him to the Bridge of Ariant","Gwíniel is near the gate of Adannon, in Annúminas.","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","'I cannot tell you where it might have been worn, but Annúminas has long had a problem with looters. If the defenders of the city cannot identify these markings, perhaps a tomb-robber can tell you where he has looted badges with similar markings. They have a camp on Rantost, an island in Lake Evendim, and may tell you what we cannot!'","'We are well-met, ${PLAYER}. What brings you to the City of Kings?'\
\
You show Gwíniel the corrupted badge and she crinkles her nose as if smelling a foul odour.\
\
'This badge is held in the grip of a powerful evil, but I can recognize that it was once worn proudly by defenders of the High King in this very city! Did you show it to my sisters? I can imagine their responses. Mine, however, may be of a more practical bent.\
\
'I cannot tell you where it might have been worn, but Annúminas has long had a problem with looters. If the defenders of the city cannot identify these markings, perhaps a tomb-robber can tell you where he has looted badges with similar markings. They have a camp on Rantost, an island in Lake Evendim, and may tell you what we cannot!'","'What have you brought to this city? I sensed its evil even before you approached!'\
\
You show the corrupted badge to Línneth, and she scowls.\
\
'This is the type of medal that was worn by defenders of this city at the height of its glory, but it has become encircled by darkness! That is a cruel hurt, but it is a common one in these days, where fell forces take things of beauty and nobility and bring them low. That it happens frequently makes it no less of an insult to me.\
\
'If we could read these symbols, we might know where guards wearing this badge were stationed, but I am unable to make sense of them. Perhaps one of my sisters could tell you more? We pride ourselves on our patience, but that patience does not always extend to remaining in each other's company. You will find Carastír and Gwíniel elsewhere, but still in the city.'","Talk to Colm Fettering on Rantost","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the High King","Techeron is at Echad Garthadir, in Annúminas.","You take back the corrupted badge","'You learned from the Steadfast Sisters that badges of that type were worn near the Bridge of Ariant? That is very near, ${PLAYER}!'\
\
You tell Techeron that you obtained the information not from the Dúnedain, but from a brigand named Colm Fettering, who sought to kill you when he learned the badge might be valuable.\
\
'That sadness is all too common these days, my friend. The badge is old, it is true, but I cannot say it has much value to any but the Dúnedain, or to scholars of history. What unhappy road led Colm Fettering to that end? Could he have turned aside? Sauron may be gone, but Colm Fettering was not guided by the hand of the Dark Lord, or by schemes hatched in the Dark Tower. He was a man only, and guided by the difficulties of the poor and the desperate.'\
\
Techeron sighs.\
\
'Speak to me when you are ready and we can walk to the Bridge of Ariant. Let us see if we can cleanse the corruption from that badge, at least. There will be bigger and more troubling challenges on the morrow, and they may be more difficult to fix.'","'I know why you have come, ${PLAYER}. If you are to journey beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, you will need the aid of a light that can pierce the darkness.'\
\
Elrond takes the Badge of Ariant from you and dips it into the font beside him. When the artifact emerges from the glowing circle, light drips soundlessly from it and pools like water in the basin. You are reminded that even though the promise of High King Elendil was submerged by darkness, it was restored by the defeat of Sauron and the return of a king to Gondor. You think of Colm Fettering and hope that one day the hearts of men like him will shine as brightly, restored similarly from darkness.. Elrond smiles at the sight of the glowing heirloom and his voice contains both determination and joy when he speaks again.\
\
'With the Light of Eärendil, you will be able to walk where the shadows lie, and overcome them.'","Talk to Techeron at Echad Garthadir, in Annúminas","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Badge of Ariant, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Talk to Carastír in Annúminas","'I will meet you at the Haven of Orladion, ${PLAYER}.'","'I have seen medals similar to this in the old city! They were worn by the soldiers of Elendil, and served as identification for his guards. But I cannot say that I have seen one exactly like this, for there are some curious markings beneath the depression, here. One unfamiliar with the workings of the soldiery could easily have missed it.\
\
'Several of my fellow Rangers are on patrol throughout the city. Bring it to Línneth, Carastír, and Gwíniel in Annúminas, and see if the Steadfast Sisters have seen any badges identical to this.'","'I am ready to go with you to the Bridge of Ariant. Let us see if we can remove the corruption that encircles the badge that was once worn there!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'What do you want? You here to pinch some of my loot? Aye or nay, and answer quickly or I'll stick you with my best knife, and bury you in the surf, shallow-like!'\
\
Grimacing, you show Colm Fettering the corrupted badge and ask him to pay special attention to the markings, and if he's seen any others of its type. The tomb-robber gets a crafty look in his eye.\
\
'Aye, I've seen badges like this one, plenty of 'em, all around the bridge those dirty ruffians call Ariant. Are you sayin' these are worth something? I could give this one back to you, it's true, and let you make a tidy profit. That's one option, aye.'","'What is that? You have brought evil here, as if this city has not seen enough darkness in recent months! Explain yourself! Is that some artifact of shadow? Scions of Angmar still hope to bring that evil kingdom once more to prominence, and we will stand against them!'\
\
You show the corrupted badge to Carastír, and she shakes her head.\
\
'I have never seen one exactly like this. My advice is for you to destroy it. This might once have been an heirloom of a beautiful kingdom, a kingdom I am sworn to honour and cherish, but now it has fallen to evil and is a reminder of our failures.'"},
[3030]={"Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Necklace of the Ordinary, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","'What are... what are you doing here, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You hold up the broken necklace and Umín nearly falls off the rock.\
\
'Why did... why did you bring it back to me?'\
\
You hastily hide the necklace from his sight, and he takes a moment to calm himself. You ask what has him so troubled, and he frowns.\
\
'Need you ask? You remember that heirloom of my family, the thief-stolen necklace we at last recovered from the tomb in the caverns beneath the Forsaken Inn? It guided my thoughts for so long, and when I finally unearthed it, the spirit held within so dominated my mind that I turned upon my friends! I was powerless to resist the spirit of the necklace, but worst of all... now that they are gone, spirit and necklace both, I do not know what to do! And now you have returned with the necklace that so occupies my every waking minute....'\
\
You tell Umín that you found this necklace in Mordor. For it to be the same as the one that so troubled him seems unlikely, but Gandalf believes it might be possible to cleanse the corruption that envelops it.\
\
'But it is so like the other. What if this corruption is the result of another spirit's presence, ${PLAYER}? What will we do then?'","'I will meet you at the Haven of Orladion, ${PLAYER}.'","'I know why you have come, ${PLAYER}. If you are to journey beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, you will need the aid of a light that can pierce the darkness. So it was with those who coveted this necklace when it contained malevolence, or the promise of direction. Now that it is just a necklace, perhaps it will aid you as it did not aid them.'\
\
Elrond takes the Necklace of the Ordinary from you and dips it into the font beside him. When the artifact emerges from the glowing circle, light drips soundlessly from it and pools like water in the basin. Elrond smiles at the sight, and his voice contains both determination and joy when he speaks again.\
\
'With the Light of Eärendil, you will be able to walk where the shadows lie, and overcome them.'","'There is a foulness about this necklace. If you find Umín, he may help you to cleanse the corruption enwreathing it. I say it is time for you to return to the Forsaken Inn, my friend. Anlaf the Forlorn may know where you can find this Umín now.'","'I returned to those caverns once, ${PLAYER}. The riddle doors were open, the spike traps deactivated. It was as if the guiding force that hindered our progress had undone itself, its purpose spent. I came all the way to the ship, but like me it remained an empty vessel. I returned to the surface, aimless and disappointed.'\
\
You ask Umín why he went back underground after his experience with the haunted necklace, and he stares off into the distance.\
\
'I think I did it hoping the spirit would return, and tell me what to do... but I received no such guidance. In the weeks that followed I came often to the Forsaken Inn, waiting for someone to tell me what to do, someone to give me direction, but no one ever did.\
\
'I will go with you now, ${PLAYER}, if you let me carry the necklace. If I can help you cleanse the corruption from it, perhaps my aimless days will be ended.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'Umín was just here, actually. If you leave the Inn you might see him across the way. Whatever stupor he's in isn't caused by my drink, that I do know... he's just a defeated man!'","'I have studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang. It bears a powerful corruption, but it was not made in the land of Mordor. It came from elsewhere, and the corruption that envelops it stems from its long stay in the Black Land. If this evil could be cleansed, I believe that Elrond could imbue it with a powerful and vital force for Good.\
\
'Before that can happen, however, we must do something about the corruption that Mordor has worked upon it. There are different methods to accomplish this, though the Wise disagree upon the effectiveness of each. My preferred means for such a cure is to bring the corrupted item to the place where it was made, or to places of some significance upon its path, and to thereby diffuse the foul touch of Mordor that has, in the interim, claimed it. We must learn the story of this heirloom before it came to Mordor.'\
\
The Wizard turns the artifact over in his hands, studying it for some clue to its origin. To your eye the heirloom is a golden necklace, ordinary save for the large ruby in its centre. The chain is broken and cannot have been easily worn for some time. It looks familiar to you.\
\
'Familiar, you say?' Gandalf asks, stroking his beard. 'How so?'\
\
You tell him that the necklace shares a resemblance with one worn by a man called Umín in tunnels beneath the Forsaken Inn of the Lone-lands. Umín had been ensnared by the villainous spirit inhabiting a necklace just like this one, and breaking its hold upon the man had not been easy.\
\
'Let us hope no such spirit bedevils this necklace, ${PLAYER}, but there is some foulness about it all the same. If you find this Umín, he may help you to cleanse the corruption enwreathing it. I say it is time for you to return to the Forsaken Inn, my friend. Anlaf the Forlorn may know where you can find this Umín now.'","'You say you're looking for Umín? Why'd you want to do that?'\
\
Anlaf scowls.\
\
'He comes in here from time to time, lookin' for all the world as if he's thinkin' to just curl up in the corner and never move again! Doesn't buy so much as a single mug of ale, neither! He just sits, and stares, and eventually he gets up and every time he leaves I think I'll never be seein' him again... but I've never had the luck before and still haven't!\
\
'He was just here, actually. If you leave the Inn you might see him across the way. Whatever stupor he's in isn't caused by my drink, that I do know... he's just a defeated man!'","Bring the Necklace of the Ordinary to Elrond in Rivendell","Anlaf told you that Umín just left the Forsaken Inn, and if you hurry you might see him outside somewhere.","Anlaf the Forlorn tends the bar of the Forsaken Inn, in the Lone-lands.","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Ordinary","Habla con Anlaf el Despojado en la Posada Abandonada","Bring the corrupted necklace to Umín somewhere outside the Forsaken Inn","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption, it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Talk to Umín and return to the ship in the caverns beneath the Forsaken Inn","Umín has struggled greatly since his encounter with the spirit of the necklace in the caverns beneath the Forsaken Inn."},
[3031]={"Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Vengeance of Folca and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Talk to Eldmath north-east of Aldburg","Defeated Wargs drawn by the corruption (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to the expert jeweller in Snowbourn","'This was once part of a porcine tusk, from a boar or similar animal. These have been known to chip or splinter during combat.\
\
'That would not ordinarily be a cause for interest, but there are markings carved near the base of it, faded and hard to read. Perhaps an expert jeweller in Minas Tirith can use his tools to read them for you.'","One jeweller sent you to another. Perhaps the expert jeweller in Snowbourn, the city of Rohan in the Sutcrofts, will be able to read the markings on the corrupted tusk-shard.","'I have studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang. It bears a powerful corruption, but it was not made in the land of Mordor. It came from elsewhere, and the corruption that envelops it stems from its long stay in the Black Land. If this evil could be cleansed, I believe that Elrond could imbue it with a powerful and vital force for Good.\
\
'Before that can happen, however, we must do something about the corruption that Mordor has worked upon it. There are different methods to accomplish this, though the Wise disagree upon the effectiveness of each. My preferred means for such a cure is to bring the corrupted item to the place where it was made, or to places of some significance upon its path, and to thereby diffuse the foul touch of Mordor that has, in the interim, claimed it. We must learn the story of this heirloom before it came to Mordor.'\
\
The Wizard turns the artifact over in his hands, studying it for some clue to its origin. To your eye the heirloom is a small shard of bone or tusk, splintered smoothly from a larger piece, and you say so.\
\
'I deem that you are right, ${PLAYER}, but I will narrow the scope of your deduction. This was once part of a porcine tusk, from a boar or similar animal. These have been known to chip or splinter during combat.\
\
'That would not ordinarily be a cause for interest, but there are markings carved near the base of it, faded and hard to read. Perhaps an expert jeweller in Minas Tirith can use his tools to read them for you.'","'What is this thing you have brought to me? It raises in me an unpleasant sensation, as if it were capable of great evil or indeed had already committed such! I will not fashion a necklace or amulet out of this, unless the price be most convincing!'\
\
You tell the jeweller that you are here for another purpose and explain that you would like him to read the tiny markings near the base of the tusk-shard. He grunts reluctantly and takes out his glass.\
\
'Even now they are very difficult to make out, and anyway are symbols with which I am unfamiliar. The words look Rohirric to me, but I am an expert in fashioning beautiful adornments and trinkets, not in unravelling languages! Bring to the Rohirrim that which concerns them, that is my rule! I once knew a jeweller from the Sutcrofts who learned his trade at the same time I did, and planned to repair in their city of Snowbourn when he became an expert. You should look for him and see if he can read these Rohirric words.'","Bring the Vengeance of Folca to Elrond in Rivendell","Eldmath has run into some trouble","Eldmath ran off during the fighting, and you should find him. He cannot have gone far.","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Riddermark","'I know why you have come, ${PLAYER}. If you are to journey beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, you will need the aid of a light that can pierce the darkness.'\
\
Elrond takes the Vengeance of Folca from you and dips it into the font beside him. When the artifact emerges from the glowing circle, light drips soundlessly from it and pools like water in the basin. An image rises unbidden in your mind, of the light of stars glittering in the heavens, extinguished by the coming of day but rekindled every night without fail. So it was with the vengeance of Folca, who would not live to see the rise of Rohan's star after a long night and a fresh dawn, but rise it did. Elrond smiles at the shimmering light, and his voice contains both determination and joy when he speaks again.\
\
'With the Light of Eärendil, you will be able to walk where the shadows lie, and overcome them.'","You should defeat the Wargs drawn by the corruption of the tusk-shard, or they might prove a danger to Eldmath or the people of the Eastfold.","'This might not be the right place, ${PLAYER}. I have sung the tale of Folca and the Boar so many times, but the layout of the land seems very different when you're actually there. Everything is so much larger than it seems in the tales; I feel as if we have been walking all day!'\
\
Eldmath turns the corrupted tusk-shard over in his hands and shudders.\
\
'This does have a vile, unlucky feeling about it, doesn't it? I am ready for some excitement, if only to dispel the tedium of all this walking!'","An expert jeweller in Minas Tirith may be able to use his tools to read the markings on the corrupted shard for you. Such a jeweller plies his trade on the southern side of the Fourth Circle, after the battle.","The jeweller in Snowbourn sent you to the village of Aldburg, in the Eastfold, to ask a Bard of Rohan about the tusk-shard.","Talk to the expert jeweller in Minas Tirith, on the southern side of the Fourth Circle, after the battle","Eldmath has been captured by a raiding party of Orcs.","'I will meet you north-east of Aldburg! Adventure!'","Talk to the bard in the tavern in Aldburg","'I will meet you at the Haven of Orladion, ${PLAYER}.'","Catch up with Eldmath","Talk to Tharbag and look for an opportunity to rescue Eldmath","'Would you like to hear a song? I would be a traitor indeed if I did not allow you to rearrange your skills, but what would be the point of that? Aye, no point, and yet all the points! Relegated to music am I, but still I long for the adventuring life! No song for me, but all the songs of others!'\
\
Unsure that this will prove at all fruitful, you show the bard the corrupted tusk-shard. His eyes light up when you explain that the markings near the base appear to be tiny Orkish scrawls, and they mention Folca.\
\
'Ah, the call of adventure beckons! If you wish to unravel the mystery of this heirloom, you have come to the right place, for I know of the tale! I will bring you to the site where it is said King Folca slew the beast and was slain in turn. I will be a bard no more, but a warrior and a quester! Meet me north-east of Aldburg, my friend, and let us do deeds worthy of the great heroes of old!'","'You've got a look about you, ${RACE}. Seen some battle, eh? Well, you won't try nothin' if you know what's good for your friend here. You're comin' with us, and no funny business or we'll stick him before you can move.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'Welcome to Snowbourn, can I provide you with any assistance? I fashioned pieces of such beauty that Théoden King himself would marvel at my craft, and I am certain Éomer King, now elevated, will do the same!'\
\
You explain that an expert jeweller in Minas Tirith referred you to him, believing that he might be able to read the Rohirric words that adorn the base of the tusk-shard.\
\
'You will not be disappointed, and when next I see my friend I will be sure to thank him for sending you to me. He has always had a discerning eye, and his finest quality is knowing when to say he does not have sufficient expertise in a field. I, however, am clearly the man for the task. Give it here. My, it does possess an unpleasant air, doesn't it?'\
\
The jeweller of Rohan squints at the tusk-shard through his glass for a moment and then snorts with disgust.\
\
'Hooves at a gallop! Did I say my friend was a man of discernment? He is a fool, and always has been! Dress him in motley, it is all he deserves! These are not Rohirric words! If these be words at all, then they are words scrawled in a foul and Orkish tongue!\
\
'It could be that this one here reads \\qFolca,\\q if you sound it out, and that tells me that if you wish to follow the trail, such as it is, you should search in the Eastfold. Perhaps a bard can tell you of the story of Folca and the Boar of Everholt, for it seems relevant to this tusk-shard. Go to Aldburg and find a bard. The tavern seems a safe place to look.'","Eldmath has gone ahead into the field, inspired by the promise of adventure and planned to meet you north-east of Aldburg.","Defeat Wargs drawn by the corruption (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","The tusk-shard's corruption draws evils to it"},
[3032]={"'I have studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang. It bears a powerful corruption, but it was not made in the land of Mordor. It came from elsewhere, and the corruption that envelops it stems from its long stay in the Black Land. If this evil could be cleansed, I believe that Elrond could imbue it with a powerful and vital force for Good.\
\
'Before that can happen, however, we must do something about the corruption that Mordor has worked upon it. There are different methods to accomplish this, though the Wise disagree upon the effectiveness of each. My preferred means for such a cure is to bring the corrupted item to the place where it was made, or to places of some significance upon its path, and to thereby diffuse the foul touch of Mordor that has, in the interim, claimed it. We must learn the story of this heirloom before it came to Mordor.'\
\
The Wizard turns the artifact over in his hands, studying it for some clue to its origin. To your eye the heirloom is a small brooch made of bone, encircled by what appears to be a curved piece of antler. It reminds you of the Lossoth of Forochel. Mithrandir seems to pick up on your assessment.\
\
'Yes, ${PLAYER}, this brooch was clearly fashioned by Lossoth hands. In material and in style this brooch of bone began its journey near the Ice-bay. That is where you should bring it, for reminding it of its origin may help to cleanse the corruption that enveloped it within Mordor.\
\
'Go to the city of Sûri-kylä, and find Lothrandir of the Dúnedain. He returned to Forochel after the fall of Sauron, and he may be able to help you cleanse the brooch of its evil.'","Search for the missing Lossoth warriors east of Sûri-kylä","Talk to Terho","Talk to Lothrandir in Sûri-kylä, in Forochel","'The storm came up suddenly, and I was separated from Âtos and Îkka. We did not know where we were... can we really have been so close to the city? But there is no time for that now... I am pursued! Help me!'","'Quickly, my friend! Something is not right about this!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'I know why you have come, ${PLAYER}. If you are to journey beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, you will need the aid of a light that can pierce the darkness.'\
\
Elrond takes the Brooch of Bone from you and dips it into the font beside him. When the artifact emerges from the glowing circle, light drips soundlessly from it and pools like water in the basin. You are put in mind of a blazing hearth, a beacon shining in the darkness of a crisp and clear winter's night, calling all travellers home for warmth and welcome. Elrond smiles at the sight of the glowing heirloom, and his voice contains both determination and joy when he speaks again.\
\
'With the Light of Eärendil, you will be able to walk where the shadows lie, and overcome them.'","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Brooch of Bone, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","'Several warriors have not returned from excursions among the snows, and I went with some hardy men to seek for them, to no avail. We searched to the north, but had not yet gone to the east. If you will search for them in that direction, I will show this brooch to people in Sûri-kylä and see if they recognize it.'","Lothrandir returned to Sûri-kylä in Forochel following the War of the Ring.\
\
Mithrandir believes that the corrupted brooch came from Forochel and returning it there may help cleanse the corruption that befell it in Mordor.","Terho is south-east of Sûri-kylä, calling for help!","Bring the Brooch of Bone to Elrond in Rivendell","Lothrandir asked you to search east of Sûri-kylä while he showed the corrupted brooch to folk in the city.","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. There are always dangers, even after the fall of Sauron, and it is our duty to face them. The hazards of Forochel are more to my liking than those we faced in the south-lands, however. What has caused you to make this long journey, my friend?'\
\
You tell Lothrandir of the bone brooch you recovered and the corruption that grips it.\
\
'I can sense its evil power. It puts me in mind of the dread that weighed upon me in the dungeons of Isengard; that is not a feeling I am eager to revisit! That this is a Lossoth brooch cannot be denied, for there are many like it in Sûri-kylä alone, but the real question is this: does the brooch belong to one of those who have gone missing in recent days and are currently unaccounted? If it does, this brooch may bring ill tidings to the missing man's family. That should not deter us. It should be delivered.\
\
'Yes, several warriors have not returned from excursions among the snows, and I went with some hardy men to seek for them, to no avail. We searched to the north, but had not yet gone to the east. If you will search for them, I will show this brooch to people in Sûri-kylä and see if they recognize it.'","Lothrandir returned to Sûri-kylä in Forochel following the War of the Ring.","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Snowmen","You found some of the missing Lossoth. Suddenly, you hear shouts from the south-east!","'I will meet you at the Haven of Orladion, ${PLAYER}.'","Lothrandir returned to Sûri-kylä in Forochel following the War of the Ring.\
\
Lothrandir gave the corrupted brooch to its rightful owner, but he fears that if the corruption remains it might do her some harm.","'This brooch was clearly fashioned by Lossoth hands. In material and in style this brooch of bone began its journey near the Ice-bay. That is where you should bring it, for reminding it of its origin may help to cleanse the corruption that enveloped it within Mordor.\
\
'Go to the city of Sûri-kylä, and find Lothrandir of the Dúnedain. He returned to Forochel after the fall of Sauron, and he may be able to help you cleanse the brooch of its evil.'","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","Talk to Lothrandir in Sûri-kylä and go to see the widow","'I heard that you found the bodies of two of the missing men, ${PLAYER}, but I am glad you were able to save Terho. He spoke of a sudden storm that overtook the warriors not far from Sûri-kylä. It happens from time to time, although I did not notice such a storm since my return. The cold can work a madness on even the well-prepared, however.\
\
'While you searched for the missing Lossoth, I discovered the rightful owner of the brooch. A woman named Pinja, recently-widowed, told me that the brooch belonged to her slain husband, Oiva.'\
\
You ask Lothrandir if he is not concerned that the corruption in the brooch might work some harm upon the widow. He seems to consider it for the first time.\
\
'That... that is a good point, ${PLAYER}. I do not know why I did not think of that when I gave her the brooch. Now that I think on it, I confess that I cannot remember actually handing it to her at all! That is most strange. We had better go to see her at once, ${PLAYER}! I hope I have not done ill through my desire to do right!'"},
[3033]={"'The fragment you showed to me is part of a bone needle used by tailors in the fashioning of clothes and garments. It does seem to be very old, but it is reminiscent of the sort that are used still in Lhanuch. Go to the Hall of Making in Lhanuch, and ask the tailors what they can tell you of it.'","An expert tailor in the Hall of Making in Lhanuch may know something about the needle that came into your possession.","Lhunog is on a hill outside the village of Lhanuch.","Talk to Helû outside the village","'What do you have there, stranger?'\
\
You show the bone fragment to Hûdh and he furrows his brow with thought.\
\
'You say this might have broken off the tip of a spear? It is possible, but I would say it is not likely. The Stag-clan has used bone for weapons of various sort, but my people generally prefer stone for the greater durability on impact. If this fragment did come from a spear, I think it would have happened on the first strike, and such a spear would be of little use for a true hunter.\
\
'No, I do not think this is from a spear-point, but I cannot tell you anything else.'","Hûdh of the Caru-lûth and Cufrus of the Avanc-lûth are in Galtrev and may know more of the bone fragment you carry.","Bring the Needle of Many Leagues to Elrond in Rivendell","'Take it away! Whatever that fragment might be, it seems wholly evil to me!'","'One of the other tribes in Galtrev may know more of that cursed thing, but it is not welcome in Lhanuch!'","'What brings you to this village, ${PLAYER}? I will not call you duvodiad, but even Suvulch can tell an ill wind brings you here. Do not make me regret this welcome, as others would!'\
\
You show the bone shard to the warrior, and he raises his hand as if in warding.\
\
'What is this, a fragment of a spear-point? It must have been used in the slaughter of something vile, for the sight of it alone is enough to raise in me great feelings of dread and of sickness! Take it away!'","Talk to Lhunog on a hill outside Lhanuch","Talk to Suvulch in the village of Lhanuch","Helû has come out of the village for further investigation of the bone fragment.","Talk to Cufrus of the Avanc-lûth, in Galtrev","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Tribes","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Needle of Many Leagues, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","'It has been more than fifty years since I last saw a needle such as that one! Can it be the very same? It must be, for Deilur made all her needles herself, and that mark was her own. No other tailor in all the years of my long life ever took such pains as she to add such an adornment. It served no practical purpose, but Deilur fashioned all her needles in that way.\
\
'I am Raiglud. I am the oldest woman in the village and by my count I am the oldest member of the Uch-lûth by many years. Do you want to know the tale of that needle you carry? Speak to me and you will hear it. It is a sad tale, but to see that needle once again I think it may be worth remembering, and this old woman would enjoy the telling of it and the reminder of her youth, long ago.'","Talk to Hûdh of the Caru-lûth in Galtrev","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","'I know why you have come, ${PLAYER}. If you are to journey beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, you will need the aid of a light that can pierce the darkness.'\
\
Elrond takes the Needle of Many Leagues from you and dips it into the font beside him. When the artifact emerges from the glowing circle, light drips soundlessly from it and pools like water in the basin. The needle travelled many leagues before it meted out Deilur's vengeance upon the Orc that took her life, but until now it did not shine as brightly as did Deilur in the memory of a child. Elrond smiles at the sight, and his voice contains both determination and joy when he speaks again.\
\
'With the Light of Eärendil, you will be able to walk where the shadows lie, and overcome them.'","With a sudden coughing laugh, an old woman demands your attention","Talk to the expert tailor in the Hall of Making, in Lhanuch","'Long ago, when I was just a girl, the Uch-lûth had not yet settled at Lhanuch...'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Helû in Lhanuch","'This thin piece of bone is jagged on one side, but the other is smooth and I see signs that it was carved for some purpose. The tip appears to me to have been broken off and lost. It is a pity, for if we could see the shape entire we might better know for what it was used.\
\
'The portion of this artifact that remains tells me that it was fashioned by one of the tribes that hunts in Enedwaith or Dunland, likely for war-like purpose. Speak to a warrior in the village of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith, and perhaps he will tell you of its origin. Once that is known you may have the knowledge you need to cleanse it of the corruption that encircles it.'","'This is similar to the needles we use here, but there is a peculiar notch at the bottom that sets it apart. I do not know why it is there, but it is distinctive. It is a mystery to me.'","Talk to Frestang of the Uch-lûth, in Galtrev","'You bear an artifact of evil, wanderer. I do not wish to become ensnared in anything of the sort, so I will give you a wide berth. But listen to this advice from a well-meaning stranger: do not become involved with the scheming of Wizards, even if they bear gifts! Many in my clan learned this lesson painfully, and too late.\
\
'If you still have an ear for further advice, I say this too: whatever artifact you carry will draw evils to you. Cast it away, and save yourself some trouble!'\
\
As Cufrus hurries away, you decide to hold onto it. After all, Mithrandir believed that it could be cleansed of the evil that surrounded it during its long stay in Mordor and might be turned to Good.","'I will meet you at the Haven of Orladion, ${PLAYER}.'","Helû is a warrior of Lhanuch on the highest rise of the village.","Talk to Raiglud and listen to her tale of long ago","Raiglud, the oldest woman in Lhanuch, has drawn your attention. She is in the Hall of Making, and has a story to tell.","Suvulch is in the village of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith.","'I knew that it was so! Did I not say to you that the bone fragment you carry would draw evil to it? I am glad you listened to my command and quickly brought it out of the village!\
\
'It is not welcome in Lhanuch. Perhaps one of the other tribes, such as those that gather in Galtrev, will tell you something about the cursed object you carry.'","'I have studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang. It bears a powerful corruption, but it was not made in the land of Mordor. It came from elsewhere, and the corruption that envelops it stems from its long stay in the Black Land. If this evil could be cleansed, I believe that Elrond could imbue it with a powerful and vital force for Good.\
\
'Before that can happen, however, we must do something about the corruption that Mordor has worked upon it. There are different methods to accomplish this, though the Wise disagree upon the effectiveness of each. My preferred means for such a cure is to bring the corrupted item to the place where it was made, or to places of some significance upon its path, and to thereby diffuse the foul touch of Mordor that has, in the interim, claimed it. We must learn the story of this heirloom before it came to Mordor.'\
\
The Wizard turns the artifact over in his hands, studying it for some clue to its origin. To your eye the heirloom is a thin shard of bone, possibly broken from the tip of a spear or an arrowhead.\
\
'This thin piece of bone is jagged on one side, but the other is smooth and I see signs that it was carved for some purpose. The tip appears to me to have been broken off and lost. It is a pity, for if we could see the shape entire we might better know for what it was used.\
\
'The portion of this artifact that remains tells me that it was fashioned by one of the tribes that hunts in Enedwaith or Dunland, likely for war-like purpose. Speak to a warrior in the village of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith, and perhaps he will tell you of its origin. Once that is known, you may have the knowledge you need to cleanse it of the corruption that encircles it.'","'Yes? What do you want?'\
\
Helû takes one look at the bone fragment and reacts much as Suvulch did.\
\
'You have brought an object of evil to Lhanuch! Take it outside the village, we do not want it here! You will draw evils to us! If you must show this spear-point to anyone, show it to warriors outside the village where these folk will not be endangered!'","Suvulch was not much help, but others in the village might know more","Frestang of the Uch-lûth is in Galtrev.","Talk to Raiglud in the Hall of Making, in Lhanuch","'You came from Lhanuch? I was born into the Uch-lûth, but I have not been welcome there for many years. Still, I am always glad to hear news of my old home.'\
\
You tell Frestang that you went to Lhanuch seeking information about the bone spear-point that came into your possession. He studies it for a moment and smiles.\
\
'You went to the warriors of Lhanuch and asked them if they recognized this and of course they did not, for they are focused on weaponry and tools of war. No, they would not have known this implement, even though they rely on others like it every day.\
\
'This is not part of a spear-point or an arrowhead. This is part of a bone needle, used by tailors in the fashioning of clothes and garments. It does seem to be very old, but it is reminiscent of the sort that are used still in Lhanuch. Go to the Hall of Making in Lhanuch, and ask the tailors what they can tell you of it.'","'I give you my welcome, wanderer. I know a hunter when I see one striding among the hills and fields with such purpose! What brings you here?'\
\
You show Lhunog the bone fragment and ask him if he can tell you anything about it.\
\
'I see why you have come to Lhanuch, for this does seem to have been crafted by one of the tribes of Enedwaith or Dunland. I cannot say if it was made by our tribe, but this feeling of evil is so overpowering that I refuse to believe it was made by one of the Algraig!'\
\
Lhunog suddenly straightens and he smells the breeze.\
\
'Something is not right, wanderer. We are hunted.'"},
[3034]={"Bring the Memento of Bhai-buri-Ghân to Elrond in Rivendell","Talk to Ghân-buri-Ghân at Drû Bhûta","Talk to Khôr-buri-Ghân by the river and travel with him to the island cave","'I have studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang. It bears a powerful corruption, but it was not made in the land of Mordor. It came from elsewhere, and the corruption that envelops it stems from its long stay in the Black Land. If this evil could be cleansed, I believe that Elrond could imbue it with a powerful and vital force for Good.\
\
'Before that can happen, however, we must do something about the corruption that Mordor has worked upon it. There are different methods to accomplish this, though the Wise disagree upon the effectiveness of each. My preferred means for such a cure is to bring the corrupted item to the place where it was made, or to places of some significance upon its path, and to thereby diffuse the foul touch of Mordor that has, in the interim, claimed it. We must learn the story of this heirloom before it came to Mordor.'\
\
The Wizard turns the artifact over in his hands, studying it for some clue to its origin. To your eye the heirloom is a small sculpture carved from stone, in the shape of a squat humanoid figure.\
\
'This carving is very similar in shape to the Púkel-men that guard the road to Dunharrow, in Rohan, but I have never seen one carved so small. It is said that those figures are carved in the likenesses of the Drúedain, the Woses, the Wild Men, and the forest in Taur Drúadan is home to similar statues of enormous size.\
\
'If this is so, perhaps the Woses will be able to tell you from where this sculpture came, and aid in the cleansing of its evil. But take heed! They hate Orcs and everything touched by Orcs, and may not receive you kindly if they deem that heirloom has been ruined by Mordor and is beyond saving.'","'We have not seen enough gorgûn for our plan. Maybe too close to village? It is hidden, and they not know where, but maybe they know here dangerous.\
\
'I keep thinking about brother Bhai-buri-Ghân. He was eldest, and seemed very picture of Wild Man to me. Maybe that is why Khôr-buri-Ghân always try to do better. Wanted to prove something, maybe.\
\
'Now Bhai-buri-Ghân only in memory. Wild Men supposed to think of dead only at Blood-cloak, but Khôr-buri-Ghân think of brother all the time.'","'I know why you have come, ${PLAYER}. If you are to journey beneath the shroud that covers Gorgoroth, you will need the aid of a light that can pierce the darkness.'\
\
Elrond takes the Memento of Bhai-buri-Ghân from you and dips it into the font beside him. When the artifact emerges from the glowing circle, light drips soundlessly from it and pools like water in the basin. You are reminded of the light in Khôr-buri-Ghân's eyes when he beheld the multitude of figures his brother had fashioned and left behind, a tangible mark of his time in the world; that light will never go out, for as long as Bhai-buri-Ghân is remembered. So too is the light that now shines in Elrond's hand, and when he speaks again his voice contains both determination and joy.\
\
'With the Light of Eärendil, you will be able to walk where the shadows lie, and overcome them.'","Talk to Khôr-buri-Ghân at the Blood-cloak, in Drû Bhûta","'Ready to go? Will get wet, but that all right to see favourite place of Bhai-buri-Ghân.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Look for Orcs north of the road by Drû Bhûta, in Taur Drúadan","'${PLAYER}, what brings you to village of Wild Men? What is that?'\
\
You show Khôr-buri-Ghân the small stone sculpture, and he marvels at it.\
\
'This look like statues all around village and in forest, but different. Those feel like comfort, warm presence. This one ruined by cold feeling and hate! Father Ghân-buri-Ghân wants to use this to trick gorgûn? I think idea is good one. Gorgûn killed brother Bhai-buri-Ghân. If this carving of Wild Man can bring sadness to gorgûn, Khôr-buri-Ghân will be glad.\
\
'Let us look for gorgûn at two places, north of the road by Drû Bhûta, and further north-east of there. Then we trick them with sculpture as bait!","Khôr-buri-Ghân suggested that you look for Orcs at another place in Taur Drúadan, north-west over a hill.","Mithrandir has studied the artifact that Ayorzén stole from the vault of Durthang and believes that if it might be cleansed of its corruption it could be empowered with a force for Good.","'Not enough gorgûn here for plan. Need many to make worth it!\
\
'Bhai-buri-Ghân used to walk in woods alone, all the time. Sometimes asked Khôr-buri-Ghân to walk too, sometimes did not. Sometimes when asked, Khôr-buri-Ghân said no. He wishes now he had not said 'no' so many times.\
\
'Need another place to look for more gorgûn. Deeper in woods. Maybe north-west.'","Look for Orcs further north-east in the woods, in Taur Drúadan","Khôr-buri-Ghân is at the Blood-cloak, east of the great waterfall in Drû Bhûta, atop a large rocky cliff. It is the location where the Wild Men perform their funerary rites.","Khôr-buri-Ghân has remembered a cave that his brother told him about and wants to find it. He is by the island in the river, waiting for you to speak with him.","'You return to home of Wild Men. But now bad feeling come with you! Smells of gorgûn trick!'\
\
You show Ghân-buri-Ghân the small statue, and he wrinkles his nose with distaste.\
\
'This statue of Wild Man, but it has evil feeling. What is meaning of this? Well-made, by hand of skill, but poisoned by gorgûn or friends of gorgûn? Ghân-buri-Ghân cannot tell you more of this, but he have idea. Sculpture may be used to trick gorgûn. They think it theirs. Maybe use it as bait. Kill many gorgûn before they know. Speak to Khôr-buri-Ghân. He at Blood-cloak. He remembers his brother. He remember Bhai-buri-Ghân.\
\
'Khôr-buri-Ghân always ready to kill gorgûn.'","'I will meet you at the Haven of Orladion, ${PLAYER}.'","'This statue of Wild Man, but it has evil feeling. What is meaning of this? Well-made, by hand of skill, but poisoned by gorgûn or friends of gorgûn? Ghân-buri-Ghân cannot tell you more of this, but he have idea. Sculpture may be used to trick gorgûn. They think it theirs. Maybe use it as bait. Kill many gorgûn before they know. Speak to Khôr-buri-Ghân. He at Blood-cloak. He remembers his brother. He remember Bhai-buri-Ghân.\
\
'Khôr-buri-Ghân always ready to kill gorgûn.'","'This carving is very similar in shape to the Púkel-men that guard the road to Dunharrow, in Rohan, but I have never seen one carved so small. It is said that those figures are carved in the likenesses of the Drúedain, the Woses, the Wild Men, and the forest in Taur Drúadan is home to similar statues of enormous size.\
\
'If this is so, perhaps the Woses will be able to tell you from where this sculpture came, and aid in the cleansing of its evil. But take heed! They hate Orcs and everything touched by Orcs, and may not receive you kindly if they deem that heirloom has been ruined by Mordor, and is beyond saving.'","Chapter 2.1: Heirloom of the Wild Men","Elrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House.\
\
You have cleansed the corruption from the Memento of Bhai-buri-Ghân, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.","Khôr-buri-Ghân suggested that you look for Orcs at two places in Taur Drúadan, forth of Drû Bhûta and further north-east of there, in the woods.","Ghân-buri-Ghân is the leader of the Drúedain and may know the origins of the corrupted carving. He is at Drû Bhûta, in Taur Drúadan.","'Not enough gorgûn here for trap, but look!'\
\
Khôr-buri-Ghân points across the water to a wooded island, sheltered in the tree-shadows.\
\
'There cave on island, favourite place of Bhai-buri-Ghân! He asked Khôr-buri-Ghân to come along and see, but Khôr-buri-Ghân never go. Once he asked, twice he asked. Never asked third time, and now dead and cannot ask.\
\
'Did feet of Khôr-buri-Ghân come here on purpose, but head not know? Speak again, ${PLAYER}, and together we seek for cave of Bhai-buri-Ghân.'","Look for Orcs to the north-west, over a hill and by an island in the river, in Taur Drúadan"},
[3035]={"'Onward to Misthallow, then. The sooner we accomplish this task, the better: not only because it was commanded of us, but because my patience may not survive these dwarves for long!'","Defeated beasts or other dangers in Misthallow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'None of us want to be travelling together, Glóin, but each of us has reason to hate the Orcs. Let that purpose unify us, and in a day or two, once the raiding-party is destroyed we need not remain companions.\
\
'Let us look forward to that, and we should have little reason to complain. The Wells of Langflood await us, and after we can return to our own concerns.\
\
'I have never seen the lands along the Langflood, but we should keep watch for places at which we might camp, sheltered from the wind and from threats that might roam near.'","This camp-site location is shaded by dense vegetation, but might serve","'Aye, this place will do.'","'Do not speak to me as if I were a mere child, Glóin. You are my elder in years, it is true, and your beard is white, but you spent no time in the dungeons of Sauron, as I have. Doubt not that I will match both you and ${PLAYER} in courage!\
\
'A raiding-party of Orcs? I have proven far better against much worse. So do not treat me as some youthful stripling!\
\
'Once we arrive in Misthallow we will need to find a place to camp, and that means fighting whatever aggressive beasts stray near our prospective camp-site. I will slay my share of the creatures, so long as you pull your own weight.'","Chapter 2.1: The Settling Fog","Talk to Venko at the entrance of the pass to Misthallow","Explore potential camp-site location east of Hlithseld","Your travelling companions have found a suitable camp-site south-east of Hlithseld in Misthallow.","In order to find a safe camp-site, you will need to slay aggressive beasts in Misthallow and scout for possible places to shelter out of the wind.","Imák has pointed out a spot that might make for a suitable camp-site.","It is time for you and your travelling companions to cross into Misthallow, the foggy basin in the northern reaches of the Wells of Langflood.","'We will need to work together if we are to see this task accomplished. Imák? Venko? Do you not agree?'","'What say you? Can we work together in this matter, or will your squabbling continue?'","You have been given a task to complete, and although your companions are not pleased to be travelling together, the four of you intend to see it successfully done.","Imák nods appreciatively. 'This will do,' he says","Cross into Misthallow, the northern reaches of the Wells of Langflood","Your companions suggested that you find a safe place to camp in Misthallow","Explore potential camp-site location south-east of Hlithseld","Defeat beasts or other dangers in Misthallow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Aye, this will do. Let me find my tinder-box and I will get a fire started.'","Imák and Venko are at the entrance to the pass that leads to Misthallow, east and south of the broken Rushgate.","Explore potential camp-site location beside the rocks south-east of Hlithseld","This camp-site location is sheltered on one side by sheer rock","Talk to Imák at the entrance of the pass to Misthallow"},
[3037]={"Talk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate","Elrond has imbued the artifact that came out of Mordor with the Light of Eärendil and gave you a powerful gift.","Chapter 2.2: The Light of Eärendil","'Ah, you have cleansed the corruption from the artifact that Ayorzén brought from Durthang. I never doubted you would be equal to the task, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The Light of Eärendil will serve you well within Gorgoroth. I deem that few of the commanders of which Ayorzén spoke will be able to endure its presence, and none will enjoy it. It will bring them discomfort and aid you in piercing the shadow.\
\
'It is time to press further into Mordor.'","Mithrandir is outside the Black Gate.","'Eärendil was a mariner, ${PLAYER}, and he braved storm and roaring wave; he bore shining light out of the darkness. He voyaged through sadness and woe, cresting the waves of his sorrow and braving the winds of wrath to bring hope from afar. He travels still upon his errand, not upon the seas of the world but those of heaven, the light of the Silmaril on his brow showing the way.'\
\
Elrond falls silent and gazes up at the sky, remembering distant memories.\
\
'For all the Eldar, the light of Eärendil's star is counted most precious. It is a sign of hope for all who labour against the Great Enemy or the multitude of his servants. For me it is something more.\
\
'Eärendil was a mariner, but he was also my sire. When I look to the stars, I remember much that has now gone beyond the circles of the world, and the joy of memory is tinged with the sorrow of loss. I give you this gift so you may bear the light of Eärendil with you, and it will be a shining lamp in the darkness.'","'For all the Eldar, the light of Eärendil's star is counted most precious. It is a sign of hope for all who labour against the Great Enemy or the multitude of his servants. For me it something more.\
\
'Eärendil was a mariner, but he was also my sire. When I look to the stars, I remember much that has now gone beyond the circles of the world, and the joy of memory is tinged with the sorrow of loss. I give you this gift so you may bear the light of Eärendil with you, and it will be a shining lamp in the darkness.'"},
[3038]={"'Is that... is that the King? What is he doing here?\
\
'Have we done something wrong, stranger? What could bring one such as he to our little village? Is he here to punish us? Have we not suffered enough?\
\
'Oh, if only Lord Forlong had returned from the fighting! He would speak to the King and tell him we have done all we should!'","King Elessar has decided to travel next to the town of Arnach, south of Imloth Melui.","'The people of Lossarnach will need to provide for themselves until another lord is raised to the station, and I doubt not they will; but it will take time to replace such a hole as Forlong leaves. Let us travel south to Arnach and see what the people there need.'","King Elessar is working in the village of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Berry bushes can be found to the south-east of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Arwen hands you the bow she borrowed from her brother Elrohir","Talk to King Elessar in Arnach, King's Gondor","'She need not prove her hunting skill to me, though perhaps it is the folk of Gondor she thinks need convincing? Thank you once again for the return of my bow and quiver.'","'Will you return Elrohir's bow and quiver while I finish preparing this meat? It has been some time since I had such a task, but I do know how it is done. He will be somewhere within Arnach, working alongside my husband.'","The hunter who brought down this deer steps out from behind a rock","The folk of Arnach stare at King Elessar and his travelling companions","'Will you speak with Baranor and learn if there is aught else we can do before departing? Perhaps he will have news of villages in Upper Lebennin that can guide our course?'","'This was my berry bush, ${PLAYER}. No, it is fine. The bounty of all these bushes will end up in the Arnach store-house. Mind not that I picked the finest berries from this bush before you arrived.\
\
'While I chose to pick these berries, my sibling is more of a hunter, and brought down a deer not far from here. Perhaps you can start preparing the meat to bring back to Arnach? The deer should be just to the south-east of here.'","Queen Arwen is hunting south-east of Arnach.","'My sibling is more of a hunter, and brought down a deer not far from here. Perhaps you can start preparing the meat to bring back to Arnach? The deer should be just to the south-east of here.'","Chapter 2.2: Without Their Lord","'What do the folk of Arnach need us to do, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Elessar that some of the folk believe he is here to punish them, as Kings and Stewards rarely came to their village before, but that others planned to pick berries and hunt for game to fill the village store-house.\
\
'I am not going to punish them! They and their lord did more than could be expected of anyone during these past few months! We will help them with their tasks, my friend, and when we move on we will leave their store-house filled. Is that clear enough?'","'That is King Elessar! I would know him anywhere!\
\
'My family attended the royal wedding, stranger. Well, we were among the crowd, but even at so great a distance I could tell the King and his Elf-bride would be so happy in each other's arms, and would rule Gondor fairly and well.\
\
'But I did not expect either of them to come to Arnach! He's going to get mud all over his fine clothes! Oh dear, I am so ashamed!'","Elladan stands picking berries to the south-east of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","'There should be some berry bushes south-east of the village.'","Elrohir is working alongside King Elessar in the village of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Baranor in the centre of Arnach, in King's Gondor","Bring Elrohir's bow and quiver to him in Arnach, King's Gondor","Folk of Arnach gather in the main square of the village, staring at the King and his party.","'The King wishes to know of news from Upper Lebennin? I have been in contact with Captain Imladir of Tumladen, and he says now the war is over the refuge is emptying, but slowly. Other than that I have heard little.'","Elladan asked you to begin preparing the meat of the slain deer just to the south-east.","'Ah, I see my sister has finished with the bow and quiver I lent to her. I hope she was not too disappointed not to bring down any prey.'\
\
You tell Elrohir that Arwen is even now preparing the meat from her fruitful hunt, and he laughs.\
\
'Even after so many years she has the skill for it? I had thought residing in Imladris these past years might have driven how it is done from her memory, but I suppose it is not so! She need not prove it to me, though perhaps it is the folk of Gondor she thinks need convincing? Anyway, thank you for the return of my bow and quiver.'","Pick berries from bushes to the south-east of Arnach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Picked berries from berry bushes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Prepare meat of the slain deer to the south-east of Elladan","'We do appreciate the work you have all done for us, of course we do. It is just that... well, the folk of Arnach are a little uncomfortable with their King doing such labour. It is not unwelcome! They are just unused to such things.\
\
'They have taken hard the death of Forlong. If you encountered him in a tavern, he might buy ales for everyone in the place, and spin tales you couldn't help but believe, no matter how incredible they seemed! But he was one of us. Good old Forlong. This King and his Elf-queen... they seem well-intentioned, but it will take time for the people to warm to them. You understand.\
\
'The King wishes to know of news from Upper Lebennin? I have been in contact with Captain Imladir of Tumladen, and he says now the war is over the refuge is emptying, but slowly. Other than that I have heard little.'","'Aye, Baranor surely speaks truth: Tumladen must be emptying of refugees now that the War of the Ring has ended and the people of Gondor return to their homes. I would like to hear how that proceeds, but perhaps we need not bring the company there in its entirety.'","The town of Arnach is located to the south of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Queen Arwen south-east of Arnach, in King's Gondor","Talk to residents of Arnach in the main square (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Baranor is in the centre of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","Travel to the main square of Arnach, south of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor","'That is the King? Doesn't he know he is supposed to stay in his tower? What's he doing here in Arnach? I don't think he's a very good King if he doesn't know what he's supposed to be doing.\
\
'We're supposed to be picking berries and hunting deer to fill the store-houses, now that the men have come back from the war. He's not going to do that, surely?'","King Elessar is in the main square of the village of Arnach.","'Lady Vanyalos is not the only resident of Lossarnach who grieves the loss of Forlong; he was a most popular figure, and treated all the folk of the lands within his governance as if they were his own children. Sometimes he treated me in this way, despite the difference in our ages!\
\
'\\qGood old Forlong,\\q they used to cheer. We fought together on more than one battlefield, ${PLAYER}, and he was always a true friend, and big-hearted. Aye, and his frame grew to match! Good old Forlong. Alas for war!\
\
'The people of Lossarnach will need to provide for themselves until another lord is raised to the station, and I doubt not they will; but it will take time to replace such a hole as Forlong leaves. Let us travel south to Arnach and see what the people there need.'","Talk to Elessar in the main square of Arnach","'I borrowed this bow from my brother Elrohir. I may be Queen, but I think it is important for the folk of Gondor to see that I work to provide for them, as does my husband. Will you return his bow and quiver to him while I finish preparing this meat? It has been some time since I had such a task, but I do know how it is done.\
\
'Elrohir will be somewhere within Arnach, working alongside my husband.'","'Thanks to our efforts, the folk of Arnach will be well provided for in the weeks to come. I hope this will be a comfort to them, and to the memory of Forlong.\
\
'Will you speak with Baranor and learn if there is aught else we can do before departing? Perhaps he will have news of villages in Upper Lebennin that can guide our course?'","Talk to Elladan south-east of Arnach, in King's Gondor"},
[3039]={"'I understand you fought alongside my son Gimli at a number of recent battles, ${PLAYER}, and I look forward to hearing about them! Every people has its own way of recording the history of war, but there is none so detailed or pleasing to the ear as that of the dwarves; my people have had a great deal of practice at both the conduct of war and its description! Yes, I have lived a life of battle, and would prefer no other!\
\
'I told you before that I fought at the Battle of Azanulbizar. Others of my kind earned glorious epithets like \\qOakenshield\\q or \\qIronfoot,\\q and the dead were so numerous they could not be entombed; instead they were burned, and the honour of the Burned Dwarves of Azanulbizar will not be forgotten. I slew my share of Orcs in the Dimrill Dale, and I dare say I made my father proud. I expect it will be the same with Gimli when he shares his account of his own fighting in the south!\
\
'Azanulbizar closed that war, but it was not the only such war between Dwarves and Orcs; nor would it be the last. It was the sixth, sometimes called by my people the Great Orc War. We held Gundabad again during that war, but only briefly, and after the losses at Azanulbizar King Thráin had neither the heart nor the warriors to reclaim it. The Longbeards became a people in exile.'","Talk to Glóin at your camp-site in Misthallow","Imák and Venko are at your camp-site in Misthallow, and they have some thoughts about Glóin's tale.","The conversation ebbs once again, and your companions eat and drink in silence","'I meant no offence, my companions. I did not forget the contributions of the other clans at Azanulbizar! ${PLAYER} will vouch for me: did I not speak of these very contributions to Durin before we departed from Skarháld? I did!\
\
'Indeed, the other clans are not descended from Durin the Deathless, but they revere him still as the eldest of dwarves, the first to awake. Any insult to his heirs is an insult to all dwarves, and no dwarf-clan would permit such a cruelty as that done by Azog, the fearsome Orc that slew Thrór, the father of Thráin. Each of the clans responded, and so it was that Azog met his doom.\
\
'There was glory enough for all, of course there was, and triumph not just for Durin's Folk but for all! You know that to be true. I did not mean to offend.'","Talk to Imák at your camp-site in Misthallow","Silence has fallen upon your camp-site, and your companions eat and drink in silence.","No stranger to the adventuring life, Gimli's father Glóin reflects upon his past campaigns and eagerly awaits the next.","'Azanulbizar closed that war, but it was not the only such war between Dwarves and Orcs; nor would it be the last. It was the sixth, sometimes called by my people the Great Orc War. We held Gundabad again during that war, but only briefly, and after the losses at Azanulbizar King Thráin had neither the heart nor the warriors to reclaim it. The Longbeards became a people in exile.'","Chapter 2.3: A Life of Battle","'I know that tale, for dwarves of my clan fought in that war as well. Not so many as the Longbeards or the other dwarf-clans, perhaps, but there was glory earned by Stout-axes at Azanulbizar. Indeed, I would claim a greater share of the glory, for what was Khazad-dûm to the Stout-axes? Theirs was a selfless battle, borne out of friendship with the other clans and hatred for their shared, ancient enemies.\
\
'The Longbeards might do well to remember the heroism of my people in those years, and treat them with greater respect!'","Talk to Venko at your camp-site in Misthallow","Drink in silence, leaving your companions to their thoughts","'Bah! I spoke poorly, and without thought. I know the other clans were crucial to our victory, of course I know that.'","Eat in silence, leaving your companions to their thoughts","'Pah! I spoke over-hastily, for I am skilled with my axe but less so with words. If Gimli were here he would speak with more polish. He has always been more well-spoken than I, and he has a better grasp of the niceties than his father ever has.\
\
'By my beard, ${PLAYER}, what is this expression you wear? Have you not found that to be true?'","'Glóin speaks as if only Longbeards fought at Azanulbizar, but it was not so. Warriors from every dwarf-clan came together to fight the Orcs, and my people too numbered among the Burned Dwarves.\
\
'Indeed, the Zhélruka know the pain of a life in exile as well as the Longbeards ever did, and we still do.'","Glóin is at your camp-site in Misthallow."},
[3040]={"'I will go with the rest of the travelling party to Pelargir, but I ask that you journey first to Tumladen and speak with Captain Imladir. If he has need of you, do what you can to assist him in my name; when he can assure you that the situation at the refuge is well in hand, then I will see you again at Pelargir. I have much to discuss with Sirgon, as you know, and I would prefer to speak with him sooner instead of later.'","'You go now to see King Elessar in Pelargir? Tell him of the agreement you brokered with Furukzahar, and also that the refuge of Tumladen stands strong, its purpose fulfilled, and with good fortune it will not need to be used again for many years.'","'I cannot tell you how pleased I am that Lady Terenis has returned to Minas Tirith, now that the need for safe refuge from the war has passed... but there are fresh difficulties to replace the old ones, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'A group of dwarves has come from Furukzahar with a proposal, but I am not certain I have the authority to grant it. Perhaps you will speak with them, since you have come lately from the King? You may better know his mind and what he would think of their proposal.\
\
'They are to the south-east, and intended to survey the buildings of Tumladen.'","Talk to King Elessar on the eastern docks of Pelargir, in King's Gondor","Imladir asked you to find the dwarves from Furukzahar where he saw them last, to the south-east.","A nearby resident of Tumladen stares at the dwarves with anger in his eyes.","King Elessar has asked you to proceed on to Tumladen in order to learn of the situation there before meeting up with the rest of the travelling party in Pelargir.","Talk to Asitám in Tumladen","Calm the dwarves and prevent violence (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Captain Imladir in the centre of Tumladen, in King's Gondor","Talk to Captain Imladir in Tumladen, King's Gondor","'I ask that you journey first to Tumladen and speak with Captain Imladir. If he has need of you, do what you can to assist him in my name; when he can assure you that the situation at the refuge is well in hand, then I will see you again at Pelargir. I have much to discuss with Sirgon, as you know, and I would prefer to speak with him sooner instead of later.'","An expedition of dwarves has come from Furukzahar with a proposal for the people of Tumladen.","Setényil curses but does not attack","'It is good to see you back, my friend! How stands the refuge of Tumladen?'\
\
You tell Elessar about the situation in Tumladen and of the expedition of Temámir Dwarves that came there to survey the state of the buildings, as well as the resentment felt toward them by some of the Gondorians.\
\
'I understand their feelings, even as I wish it was not so. Perhaps I should accept the invitation of Furukzahar, ${PLAYER}, in order to repair the relations between my kingdom and theirs. But first there is work to attend to in Pelargir.'","Find the dwarves from Furukzahar to the south-east of Captain Imladir, in Tumladen","The dwarves stare at you warily.","'I hope the King of Gondor appreciates your work on his behalf, ${PLAYER}, for most of his folk may not. Would they think to aid us, if our stronghold was directly threatened while their own towns and villages were not? I know the answer, though they believe otherwise. Thank you for helping us here keep the peace.\
\
'I will bring my report back to Hámisar, and will tell him that the King has, for now, agreed to these repairs. Our price will be fair, and the friendship between our folk... well, there is more to be repaired than just stone, it seems. Will you convey an invitation to your King on Hámisar's behalf? He is welcome to visit us at Furukzahar at his earliest convenience. After all, it is one thing to do business between reliable intermediaries such as you and I, but when rulers can meet face to face it seems to me much more can be accomplished, better and more quickly.\
\
'Good day to you, my friend.'","Defári scowls angrily at you and the Tumladen resident","The dwarves from Furukzahar stand in Tumladen, waiting for a friendly <rgb=#00FF00>bow</rgb> of greeting.","You have prevented violence between the dwarves from Furukzahar and residents of Tumladen, and should now speak to Asitám.","Survey debris within Tumladen further up the slope to the north-west","<rgb=#00FF00>Bow</rgb> to the dwarf-expedition from Furukzahar","The dwarves from Furukzahar intend to survey the debris deeper within Tumladen to the north-east.","King Elessar would not appreciate any violence between the Dwarves of Furukzahar and the residents of Tumladen.","Asitám shakes his head and clucks his tongue as he studies the debris","A nearby resident of Tumladen mutters something under his breath","Survey debris within Tumladen up the slope to the north-east","Survey debris deeper within Tumladen to the north-east","'I am not surprised to hear your report of the dwarves from Furukzahar, for I have heard the mutterings around Tumladen. The folk here wonder why the doors of the dwarves remained shut during the war and only opened when the danger had passed. I say they wonder, but that is not the truth; they know the reason, and resent the dwarves for it. Where was this help when it might have saved lives?\
\
'I know each folk must look first after its own, but we could have used the assistance of Furukzahar before now. It is good you prevented the insults from turning to bloodshed; we have seen enough of it this year, at least, even if the Temámir stayed safely in their mountains and saw none.\
\
'You go now to see King Elessar in Pelargir? Tell him of the agreement you brokered with Furukzahar, and also that the refuge of Tumladen stands strong, its purpose fulfilled, and with good fortune it will not need to be used again for many years.'","'It is a pleasure to make your acquaintance, and I trust you speak with the king's own authority? The captain with whom we spoke earlier did not, and he spent many words telling us so, wasting his time and our own. I am pleased you have taken his place.\
\
'My fellows and I were sent here by Hámisar, ruler of the Temámir folk who dwell in Furukzahar, stronghold of the White Mountains. Long have we worked alongside the people of Gondor, helping to repair and rebuild their cities, but the recent devastation is worse than any in our memory, and requires a good deal more effort and resources if it is to be made right.\
\
'To that end, Hámisar wishes to send more crafters and dedicate more blocks of stone to the work. Defári, Setényil, and I have come to survey the needs of this refuge. Can you assure us that the King of Gondor will give us appropriate payment for any work we here perform?'\
\
You tell Asitám that King Elessar is known for his fair dealings, and he greatly desires that Gondor be restored. The dwarf smiles broadly.\
\
'Then he will not regret hiring the Temámir Dwarves of Furukzahar, my new friend! Let us continue deeper into the refuge and see how much work will be required.'","Captain Imladir is in the centre of the refuge of Tumladen, located to the west of Arnach, in King's Gondor.","'Good day to you, my friend.'","Captain Imladir is in the centre of Tumladen, in King's Gondor.","The dwarves from Furukzahar eye you cautiously","The dwarves from Furukzahar intend to survey the debris within Tumladen, further up the slope to the north-west.","Talk to Asitám in Tumladen, King's Gondor","'Perhaps you will speak with the dwarves from Furukzahar, since you have come lately from the King? You may better know his mind and what he would think of their proposal.\
\
'They are to the south-east, and intended to survey the buildings of Tumladen.'","King Elessar stands by the eastern docks of Pelargir, in King's Gondor.","A nearby resident of Tumladen sighs loudly as the dwarves study the debris","The dwarves from Furukzahar intend to survey the debris within Tumladen, up the slope to the north-east.","Chapter 2.3: High Walls, Closed Doors"},
[3041]={"Defeat enemies in Dor Amarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Isenmouthe is guarded, but when has that ever proved a hindrance to you?","Brungos is on the other side of the Isenmouthe, in Dor Amarth.","You have found Covadil, staring up at the Spire of Lûghash","'Adventurers of the Free Peoples have set foot into Udûn, but the fortress of Carach Angren has hindered further passage. The eruption of Orodruin melted the doors of the Isenmouthe and they cannot be shut, but enemies still hold the channel between Udûn and Dor Amarth.\
\
'Some few have managed the passage: Rangers, Elves, and others utilizing the arts of stealth. I believe that you can advance into the Doomfold of Dor Amarth. Pass through the guarded Isenmouthe and find Brungos on the other side. He will tell you somewhat of what he has done, and what has yet to be accomplished.'","'Did I not tell you? Digging in the debris is never a waste... not for a scholar of history!\
\
'This broken piece of metal is unremarkable, save for this marking right here. Do you see it? That is half of a sigil of Gondor. Nay, not even a half! It may be more of a small portion of a small portion, but even a portion's portion is a delight to one who thirsts for knowledge!\
\
'This tiny remnant of history has emerged from the ash, a reminder to us of Gondor's resilience. My master will surely find value in this discovery, even if I was not supposed to adventure here. The House of Lore will benefit from this, I do not doubt it! This is much more interesting than anything I might have found in Osgiliath, so close to Minas Tirith. This is a land of danger, an unknown land, and the rewards are greater to match!'","'There is no shortage of enemies stalking Dor Amarth. Defeat any you find and the land will be made not safe, but safer at the least.'","Pass through the Isenmouthe and find Brungos in Dor Amarth","Covadil asked you to search among the old ash piles outside Lûghash for some sign of the Gondorian presence.","Travel to the Isenmouthe in the fortress of Carach Angren","'Welcome to the Doomfold of Dor Amarth, ${PLAYER}, but even as I bid you this greeting, the words rebel upon my lips. Welcome? Who could be welcome in this place?\
\
'It is the way of my people to survive in the wilderness, hunting game and foraging for food even when the land seems barren. Those skills would be well-tested in this place! Luckily, it should not be necessary; I have brought supplies enough to last me, and in any event I would not trust anything that could grow here.\
\
'Was this valley once fertile? I cannot imagine it, but mortal eyes are oft quick to judge, given how little we see of the great span of Time. Before Sauron came, was this land green and growing?'\
\
Brungos dismisses the thought with a shrug.\
\
'Mayhap I will consider further when we are safely away from here, ${PLAYER}. For now, the land is dead and full of enemies, and we should ask pointed questions with dagger and blade, and set aside any questions that do not fell our foes!'","'I believe that you can advance into the Doomfold of Dor Amarth. Pass through the guarded Isenmouthe and find Brungos on the other side. He will tell you somewhat of what he has done, and what has yet to be accomplished.'","Find Covadil near Lûghash, in Dor Amarth","Dig in the ash piles outside Lûghash (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dug in the ash piles outside Lûghash (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated enemies in Dor Amarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Brungos in Dor Amarth","'There was once a Gondorian fortress there, the Peace-hold of Sídhost. I wonder if there might still be signs of it. You should do what we scholars of the House of Lore often do when we want to unearth lost knowledge. We dig about in the debris, ${PLAYER}! You never know what you might find!\
\
'Search the old ash piles all around the Spire, and see if you can find some remnant of the Gondorian presence here. For knowledge, and for knowing!'","'Will you look at that, ${PLAYER}? A fortress was built there upon the lowest slopes of Ered Lithui when Gondor established its watch upon Mordor. It was called the Peace-hold of Sídhost, and nothing moved on Orodruin without alerting the attention of its defenders.\
\
'But the vigilance of Gondor failed, in time, and it was abandoned. The Orcs burrowed beneath its foundations, and the earth shook, and Sídhost crumbled into ruin. The Spire of Lûghash arose in its place. That is it right there! If it weren't for the scholarly pursuit of knowledge, you would think that was merely an evil tower, but now you know some of its history. Isn't that fascinating?\
\
'But there was once a Gondorian fortress there, and I wonder if there might still be signs of it. You should do what we scholars of the House of Lore often do when we want to unearth lost knowledge. We dig about in the debris, ${PLAYER}! You never know what you might find!\
\
'Search the old ash piles all around the Spire, and see if you can find some remnant of the Gondorian presence here. For knowledge, and for knowing!'","Talk to Covadil near Lûghash","Chapter 2.3: Lands of Doom","Now that you have acquired the Light of Eärendil, Mithrandir has asked you to press further into Mordor.","'I have faced many foes here myself, but still my mind worries at the subject about which we spoke, ${PLAYER}. Can it be that this land was once much the same as any other, but the coming of Sauron laid waste to it? There are countless reasons to rejoice that he is gone, but even for one among many it must approach the top of the list.\
\
'If he could do this to Mordor, could he not have worked such a change upon Gondor, or upon Rohan, or upon Eriador? I deem that he could. Further I contend that the transformation of Dor Amarth to this blasted plain was not accidental. I believe he did it purposefully, with malicious intent, if not for some scheme then merely for the hateful joy of it.\
\
'I spoke about this with Covadil, who dared the passage of Isenmouthe with me; I think it was she who first planted these thoughts in my mind, and now I cannot stop thinking on them! She intended to travel north-east to Lûghash. I warned her to be careful, but she found that mirthful and laughed at my warning. She is a scholar, and a bit odd, but I do hope she is being careful all the same. Perhaps you could find her and see how she fares?'","Bring the broken metal pieces to Covadil near Lûghash","The Isenmouthe is the gate between Udûn and Dor Amarth, and it is built into the fortress of Carach Angren.","The Gondorian scholar Covadil is near the Spire of Lûghash, in Dor Amarth.","Brungos is in a small ruined settlement in Dor Amarth.","You have found Brungos in the Doomfold","'Covadil intended to travel north-east to Lûghash. I warned her to be careful, but she found that mirthful and laughed at my warning. She is a scholar, and a bit odd, but I do hope she is being careful all the same. Perhaps you could find her and see how she fares?'","Fierce enemies stalk the Doomfold of Dor Amarth, and Brungos asked for your help defeating them.","Covadil went north-east in Dor Amarth, intending to see Lûghash."},
[3042]={"Glóin directed you to meet up with him on the rocky spur to the west, on which stands the old town of Framsburg, from where the forebears of the Rohirrim once hailed.","These ruins are filled with worm nests, but no sign of the raiding-party","'There is only one way onto or off of this rocky spur, ${PLAYER}, and the raiding-party is no longer here. You found this badge close to the southern cliff's edge? It seems to me the Orcs stood there for a time, scouting their course, and this badge fell unnoticed as they did. I think they must have followed the river south. That is where our path leads!'","Explore the northern ruins on the Framsburg promontory","Find some disturbed earth among the ruins of Framsburg","Find more tracks somewhere to the south, along the river","Glóin is on the rocky spur on which stands the ruins of Framsburg.","'What is this? Hmm... I have seen metal badges of this type before. The Orcs carry them, most likely to identify the tribe to which they belong. No dwarf would need such a thing! Can you imagine a Longbeard needing to carry a marker to remind himself he is a Longbeard?'\
\
You consider pointing out the numerous symbols engraved on Glóin's weapons and clothes, but decide against it.\
\
'I confess to you this symbol is not one I have encountered,' Glóin continues. 'It looks like a thundercloud to me. Perhaps that is the identity of the band to which our raiding Orcs belong: the Downpour of Woe, or the Deluge of Pain, or some other Orkish nonsense.\
\
'There is only one way onto or off of this rocky spur, ${PLAYER}, and the raiding-party is no longer here. You found this badge close to the southern cliff's edge? It seems to me the Orcs stood there for a time, scouting their course, and this badge fell unnoticed as they did. I think they must have followed the river south. That is where our path leads!'","Drakes, worms, and other creatures have taken up residence within the ruins of Framsburg, and Glóin thinks you should defeat the creatures while you search within Framsburg for some sign of the Gundabad raiding-party.","Bring the thundercloud badge to Glóin on the eastern side of the Framsburg promontory","Wind whistles among the cracked stones, but there is no sign of the raiders","Glóin thinks the raiding-party from Gundabad may have passed near Framsburg, and the old dwarf believes you should begin your search near its abandoned ruins for the Orkish threat.","Talk to Glóin on the Framsburg side of the bridge","Chapter 2.4: A Home Long Abandoned","The raiding-party descended from Framsburg and came south, following the river","Imák stands by the tracks he found south of Framsburg.","Defeat creatures near the ruins of Framsburg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated creatures near Framsburg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I think that is enough rest for now. Let us find the raiding-party before this old dwarf trips upon his own beard and offends our companions further!\
\
'Few people live in these lands, but I understand the forebears of the Rohirrim once lived alongside the Anduin somewhere in Misthallow. Their town was named Framsburg, and I expect it lies on the rocky spur to the west of us. Let us see if anyone lives there now, and find out what they may know of the raiding-party from Gundabad.\
\
'I will help put away our camp-site and meet you there, ${PLAYER}.'","Glóin is on the rocky spur on which stands the ruins of Framsburg. The old dwarf will be interested in the metal badge you discovered.","Meet up with Glóin at the rocky spur on which stands the ruins of Framsburg","From the mud you pry a metal badge marked with a thundercloud symbol","'These tracks were definitely made by the raiding-party. They scouted a course from high above, by the ruins of Framsburg, and they followed it.'","'The town may still speak to us of the Orcs' passage. Search for signs of the raiding-party within the ruins of Framsburg, ${PLAYER}, and slay these crawling terrors while you do. Men may not live in Framsburg now, but Durin has his sights set upon Gundabad to the north, and these creatures will pose a threat to any army passing nearby. Thinning their number can only be a boon for our future course.'","Glóin believes the Orc raiding-party scouted its path from the Framsburg promontory and continued south, following the river.","Talk to Imák by the tracks south of Framsburg","The town of Framsburg has long since fallen into disrepair","'Few people live in these lands, but I understand the forebears of the Rohirrim once lived alongside the Anduin somewhere in Misthallow. Their town was named Framsburg, and I expect it lies on the rocky spur to the west of here. Let us see if anyone lives there now, and find out what they may know of the raiding-party from Gundabad.\
\
'I will help put away our camp-site and meet you there, ${PLAYER}.'","Explore the north-east side of the Framsburg promontory","'When I hoped this town might be inhabited, I was thinking of Men, not worms, drakes, or beasts! These creatures may not have willingly allowed the raiding-party to pass, but neither will they tell us anything of use. A few Orcs may wander among the ruins, but we seek not one or two; we are looking for a more substantial force!\
\
'We did not come here for nothing. The town may still speak to us of the Orcs' passage. Search for signs of the raiding-party within the ruins of Framsburg, ${PLAYER}, and slay these other foes while you do. Men may not live in Framsburg now, but Durin has his sights set upon Gundabad to the north, and these creatures will pose a threat to any army passing nearby. Thinning their number can only be a boon for our future course.'","'Framsburg fell into ruin long ago, but that does not mean it will be empty. Be wary!'","'Look at this, ${PLAYER}! Tracks... and these were made by creatures walking on two legs, not on four. Orcs!'"},
[3043]={"King Elessar and Sirgon are overseeing ship repairs in south-eastern Pelargir, King's Gondor.","Faltharan is to the north-west of the auction house in Pelargir, King's Gondor.","'I do not know if I have the fortitude to follow my father as the Lord of Lebennin, but I will do my duty as best I can, ${PLAYER}. I have begun by trying to stamp out the brigands with whom my brother Lorvegil sought to seize the city, but they are many and well-hidden. Some may be allies of the Heirs of Castamir, and I have heard whispers that a new power rises in Umbar... I think they might seek to court it, if they can.\
\
'But my father is right. If we are to resist foes from Umbar, we must repair and rebuild our ships. He planned to show the King how the work progresses, and you should catch up with them at the dry dock to the south-east.'","Defeated brigand toughs in Pelargir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to King Elessar at the dry dock in Pelargir, King's Gondor","Sirgon stands along the eastern docks of Pelargir, in King's Gondor.","King Elessar and Sirgon, Lord of Lebennin, consider the poor state of the Gondorian navy following the events of the War of the Ring.","'The work progresses, but it progresses slowly, and I fear not as quickly as does the situation in Umbar.'","Defeat brigand toughs on the western side of Pelargir, King's Gondor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'My son has his own task: clearing out the unsavoury folk that have taken to preying upon the folk of Pelargir. Ships cannot be built without craftsmen, and craftsmen cannot work if they are being burgled and harassed whenever they cross the city! Will you aid my son with his task, and make the port-city more safe for my workers and for their families?'","'Sirgon has been showing me the state of the Gondorian navy, ${PLAYER}, and I confess to you that it is worse than I feared. The Corsairs of Umbar knew where to strike and with precisely how much force, and the ships that were once the pride of Gondor lie now at the bottom of the bay, or burned along the coast. It is true we seized some of their own vessels, without which we could not have arrived at Minas Tirith in time, but most of those were in poor shape, or are now.\
\
'We do not know how much of Umbar's sea-power has been inherited by the Kindred of the Coins, but unless it is very little we have scant hope of repelling it, should the Kindred cross the bay with ships of their own. I have accepted Sirgon's suggestion that he step down as the Lord of Lebennin in favour of his son Faltharan, but there is a condition: he must supervise the rebuilding of Gondor's ships, and he must do it with utmost haste.'","Chapter 2.4: Low Tide","'I have accepted Sirgon's suggestion that he step down as the Lord of Lebennin in favour of his son Faltharan, but there is a condition: he must supervise the rebuilding of Gondor's ships, and he must do it with utmost haste.'","Talk to Sirgon on the eastern docks of Pelargir, in King's Gondor","'My King has done me the great honour of allowing me to step down, and I will do the best I can to repay him for it tenfold, as will my son Faltharan! Gondor's fleet is at its lowest ebb now, but I hope to restore its glory to such a height as has not been seen in hundreds of years! Perhaps then I shall set sail once again, as I do in my dreams....\
\
'But I have a task, and it will occupy my every waking moment. My son has his own task, and it involves clearing out some of the unsavoury folk that have taken to preying upon the folk of Pelargir. Ships cannot be built without craftsmen, and craftsmen cannot work if they are being burgled and harassed whenever they cross the city!\
\
'Will you aid my son with his task, and make the port-city more safe for my workers and for their families?'","Brigand toughs on the western side of Pelargir have made problems for Sirgon's shipbuilders, and he wants you to help his son Faltharan deal with them.","Talk to Faltharan north-west of the auction house in Pelargir, King's Gondor","'If we are to resist foes from Umbar, we must repair and rebuild our ships. My father planned to show the King how the work progresses, and you should catch up with them by the dry dock to the south-east.'","King Elessar and members of his travelling party observe the repairs","'There are a lot of brigand toughs on the western side of the city, if you're willing to help us thin their numbers.'","King Elessar is at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, King's Gondor.","Find King Elessar and Sirgon at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, King's Gondor"},
[3044]={"Rhogrin shakes his head and seems to see you for the first time","'Something about that great pit infused Rhogrin with a type of madness, and he attacked us. We, his faithful friends! As if years of service and kinship meant nothing! Pah!'","'There's something terrible about the wreckage of Sauron's tower, the ruins of Barad-dûr. Enormous pieces of it fell to the ground when the Dark Lord was destroyed, and the land all around has an unpleasant air.\
\
'But I never thought it could work such a change on one of my fellows! Rhogrin was just as he always was on the journey out, but when we approached the terrible pit, that great abyss...'\
\
Fairanc falls silent.\
\
'That abyss was the site of Barad-dûr, when still it stood. Something about it infused Rhogrin with a type of madness, and he attacked us. We, his faithful friends! As if years of service and kinship meant nothing! Pah!'","A tremendous feeling of evil emanates from the bones of Barad-dûr and adversely affects those unready for its touch.","Mithrandir is outside the Black Gate.","'I know that name! I spoke with Rhogrin at the Black Gate, and he seemed a nice enough sort. He did not seem the type to attack his friends, for treasure or for no. I think Fairanc is right: the abyss where Barad-dûr once stood is still surrounded by corruption, and it drove Rhogrin to madness.\
\
'You have to find him before he harms any others, or himself, but do not kill him! Remember the lesson of the metal scrap from the ash pile: even good things once buried can be unearthed again!\
\
'Find Rhogrin by the abyss, and knock some sense back into him! But kill him not, for that is not easily undone.'","Covadil is on the road east of Lûghash.","A number of soldiers are hurrying down the road towards Lûghash.","'I can't see why Rhogrin would strike out at his fellows like that. Never known him for a turncoat, not until today!'","Chapter 2.4: Madness at Barad-dûr","Talk to Thorvíl on the road east of Lûghash","Talk to Covadil on the road east of Lûghash","'There are people approaching from down the road, and they sound as if they are in a tremendous hurry!'","'You won't get me! Invisible foes, flitting all about us! You can't see them, but they can see you... they're all around!\
\
'Stay back! I'll kill you!'","'${PLAYER}? What are you doing out here? In point of fact, what am I doing here? I last remember standing on the road somewhere near Lûghash, but that is many miles away, is it not? I remember...'\
\
The colour drains from his face.\
\
'My friends... I think I attacked them! I didn't mean to do it, but there was such an overwhelming feeling of... of... I do not know how to describe it. My will was overmastered. Did I think I had the strength of Gondor? I was driven to madness like a common Orc, and set upon my fellows!\
\
'I am shamed, ${PLAYER}. I did not understand the potency of Sauron's evil. Even after his fall, the lands that he touched remain marred by the memory of him. I must find my friends and apologize. I hope they will understand that I was not myself. I have to leave this place. I am not equal to it.'","Find Rhogrin on the road to the great abyss east of Lûghash","Covadil has come up to the group of soldiers on the road east of Lûghash.","Rhogrin stands near the great abyss in Dor Amarth.","'Did you find Rhogrin? You have to go back and make sure he is all right!'","Talk to Rhogrin on the road to the great abyss","'You saved Rhogrin from himself? I am glad to hear it, and your story confirms to me something I had suspected!\
\
'Sauron instructed his servants to build him a kingly castle, a stronghold on a hill that was called Amon Dûr. Over the long passage of years, his servants expanded the castle to cover all of the hill, and it grew with new construction until it towered into the air. It became Barad-dûr, the Dark Tower, and reached so high that only Sauron's magic could keep it aloft.\
\
'But the tower did not only reach skyward. Beneath Barad-dûr, the Orcs delved fathomless dungeons for their master, until the Ered Lithui were riddled with pits and chasms. When the tower fell, the land gave way and a great abyss opened where Barad-dûr once stood. Sauron's dungeons were exposed to the sky: the Abyss of Mordath.'\
\
Covadil shivers.\
\
'Brrrrr! Knowledge can be frightening! Anyway, Sauron may be gone, but he dwelt at Barad-dûr for so long that the land has not forgotten him. It sounds to me as if he left his impression on the Abyss and the lands around it. You should find Mithrandir and tell him this, and I think it is time I returned to the House of Lore. I am not afraid of danger... in moderation. But this is more than moderately terrifying!'","'I am shamed, ${PLAYER}. I did not understand the potency of Sauron's evil. Even after his fall, the lands that he touched remain marred by the memory of him. I must find my friends and apologize. I hope they will understand that I was not myself. I have to leave this place. I am not equal to it.'","Talk to Fairanc on the road east of Lûghash","'Find Rhogrin by the abyss, and knock some sense back into him! But kill him not, for that is not easily undone.'","Rhogrin stands on the road to the great abyss, unaware of your presence","Talk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate","'Sauron may be gone, but he dwelt at Barad-dûr for so long that the land has not forgotten him. It sounds to me as if he left his impression on the Abyss and the lands around it. You should find Mithrandir and tell him this, and I think it is time I returned to the House of Lore. I am not afraid of danger... in moderation. But this is more than moderately terrifying!'","'You don't want to go this way, friend! Ours was a small company of soldiers aiming to plunder the ruins of Barad-dûr for treasure, and each man was to have a share of the loot. But one of our number turned on us, he did, and thought to slay us!\
\
'I don't know why he attacked us. Wanted our shares of the treasure, most like, but I can't see as why Rhogrin would strike out at his fellows like that. Never known him for a turncoat, not until today!'","Rhogrin is near the great abyss east of the Spire of Lûghash, in Dor Amarth.","'The tidings you bring of Barad-dûr do not surprise me, but they will need to await proper consideration. Something has happened.\
\
'A messenger has come.'","'Hold on. Do you hear that? There are people approaching from down the road, and they sound as if they are in a tremendous hurry!'","Rhogrin is standing on the road to the great abyss in Dor Amarth, and seems to be himself again."},
[3045]={"'If the dwarves think to test our patience, I am determined not to fail the challenge, ${PLAYER}. Please make sure Gimli says nothing we will regret.'","Queen Arwen is at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, in King's Gondor.","'We are here on a mission of friendship, ${PLAYER}, and therefore we will do what custom and tradition demand of us. Let us hunt some of the wild game to be found in this valley, and may the Temámir enjoy what bounty we can bring to them.\
\
'I trust the game animals of this vale are plentiful, Sékhel of Furukzahar?'","Sékhel stands guard outside the entrance to Furukzahar.","'You will want me along on this mission, of course. The Dwarves of Furukzahar are not Longbeards, but you cannot best a dwarf when it comes to speaking with other dwarves! They will want to hear what I have to say, even as they spare not a moment for the King of Gondor.\
\
'It's true that you don't see Temámir in the North very often, but they did answer the call of the Sixth War of Dwarves and Orcs, and suffered losses as severe as any other house. Their stronghold of Furukzahar is hidden in a cleft of the White Mountains to the north of Pelargir? Then let us be off, and see if the hospitality of the Temámir is to be as noteworthy as their wisdom!'","Gimli has grown impatient and is not pleased at being made to wait outside the entrance to Furukzahar.","'This is intolerable! How long do they intend to make us wait? We did not come here to be made to stand on the doorstep like common peddlers! Should any Temámir come to Thorin's Halls, would they be kept outside for the merest whim? I think they would not!'\
\
Elessar gives Gimli a meaningful look, and the dwarf glowers at him.\
\
'I am sorry, my friend, but this endless waiting is intended as an insult! You cannot see it? Did they not invite the King of Gondor to visit them? Or did they do so in order to slight you in this fashion? No Longbeard would stand for it, and I should think the King of Gondor would have more demands upon his time than would allow him to waste such time as this!'","Another dwarf emerges from the stronghold and speaks quietly to Sékhel","Travel to the entrance of Furukzahar in the White Mountains north of Pelargir, in King's Gondor","King Elessar stands outside the entrance to the Temámir fortress of Furukzahar, in the White Mountains.","King Elessar has decided to answer the invitation of the Dwarves of Furukzahar, stronghold of the Temámir in the White Mountains.","'Do dwarves usually make folk wait like this?'","'I hope the dwarves will accept these gifts from us in the spirit of their custom, and as tokens of friendship from Gondor.'","Hunt animals in the valley outside Furukzahar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The stronghold of Furukzahar is hidden in a cleft of the White Mountains to the north of Pelargir? Then let us be off, and see if the hospitality of the Temámir is to be as noteworthy as their wisdom!'","A dwarf of the Temámir stands guard at the entrance to Furukzahar","'But I sadly admit that staring at the ships under construction will not speed up the process. Gondor must now depend on the skill of her craftsmen and the quality of their work, and her King must look to other matters. If the Kindred of the Coins turns its gaze upon our shores in the next few months, we will need Gondor's fleets, buildings, and quays repaired... but we will also need to repair the bonds of friendship between Gondor and her neighbours.\
\
'Let us accept the invitation of the Dwarves of Furukzahar, ${PLAYER}. We will visit them in the White Mountains and negotiate a fair arrangement between their people and my kingdom. We may need true-hearted allies in the days to come, and Gondor's stone-work could use the attention of such as these dwarves. What does my Queen say to this proposal?'","Talk to Kutúkh at the entrance to Furukzahar","Bring the gifts of meat to Sékhel at the entrance to Furukzahar","Talk to Gimli outside the entrance to Furukzahar","'This is ridiculous! How long must we wait until they permit Elessar to go inside?'","The Dwarves of Furukzahar expect a gift from those who visit them, and the guard Sékhel suggested that you hunt the game to be found in the valley for that purpose.","The dwarf Sékhel stands guard at the entrance to Furukzahar.","Talk to King Elessar outside the entrance to Furukzahar, in King's Gondor","'Allow me to convey Hámisar's deepest apologies for the wait. He is of course delighted to meet with the King of Gondor and his companions, and regrets only that the meeting has not happened before now.'","'Let us hunt some of the wild game to be found in this valley, and may the Temámir enjoy what bounty we can bring to them. I trust the game animals of this vale are plentiful, Sékhel of Furukzahar?'","'My husband speaks the truth: if ties of friendship are neglected, they can slip loose entirely. It sounds to my ear that the affection between the people of Gondor and the Dwarves of the White Mountains is already strained, and threatens to become worse.\
\
'The King should take a smaller party than the one with which he left Minas Tirith. You should go with him, ${PLAYER}, and Gimli, and I suggest too that he bring the company's scribe, Caebar. Should any records be drawn about the meeting between my husband and the ruler of Furukzahar, Caebar will have the tools necessary.\
\
'The rest of the company will stay for a few days in Pelargir, but we will rejoin your small band at Ost Anglebed, and continue onward together.'","Gimli is at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Queen Arwen at the dry dock in Pelargir, King's Gondor","'And still we wait! With whom do these dwarves think they are dealing? This is Elf-like behaviour, if you ask me!\
\
'Perhaps you will refrain from telling Legolas I said that, friend? But this is ridiculous!'","'Do dwarves usually make people wait this long?'","Hunted animals in the valley outside Furukzahar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Sékhel at the entrance to Furukzahar","'The King should take a smaller party than the one with which he left Minas Tirith. You should go with him, ${PLAYER}, and Gimli, and I suggest too that he bring the company's scribe, Caebar. Should any records be drawn about the meeting between my husband and the ruler of Furukzahar, Caebar will have the tools necessary.\
\
'The rest of the company will stay for a few days in Pelargir, but we will rejoin your small band at Ost Anglebed, and continue onward together.'","Wait until Sékhel says King Elessar is permitted inside Furukzahar","'If the Dwarves of Furukzahar think to test my patience, I am determined to pass the test, ${PLAYER}. Give no sign of displeasure, my friend, and we will weather this challenge.'","'Yes, this gift will do nicely. It is good you have done as my people expect, and our ruler Hámisar will be pleased to learn that the King of Gondor does not think himself above such customs as we hold in Furukzahar.'\
\
Sékhel permits himself a small smile, and then shakes his head regretfully.\
\
'However, it pains me to tell you that we are not yet ready to allow the King of Gondor inside. You will have to wait a little longer.'","Talk to Gimli at the dry dock in Pelargir, King's Gondor","Chapter 2.5: Being Neighbourly","Sékhel, the guard outside Furukzahar, has regretfully informed you that King Elessar is not yet permitted inside. He will have to wait a little longer.","'Welcome to Furukzahar, stronghold of the Temámir in the White Mountains. All are welcome within, of course, but affairs of state are such that the arrival of the King of Gondor demands a little extra preparation! I ask that you wait until I hear word from my brethren inside that you may enter.\
\
'I do not wish to inconvenience you... but it is also customary to bring a gift when you arrive here. Perhaps some meat from the game that is to be found in this valley? I do not wish to impose a burden upon you, but it will be my great shame if I were to allow you inside without such a gift, and you were thought to be discourteous. I cannot allow that to happen, if it might be prevented!'","'Let us accept the invitation of the Dwarves of Furukzahar. What does my Queen say to this proposal?'","'I do not wish to inconvenience you... but it is also customary to bring a gift when you arrive here. Perhaps some meat from the game that is to be found in this valley? I do not wish to impose a burden upon you, but it will be my great shame if I were to allow you inside without such a gift, and you were thought to be discourteous. I cannot allow that to happen, if it might be prevented!'","Kutúkh has emerged from the stronghold of Furukzahar."},
[3046]={"Travel toward the town of Limlók, to the north-east","Imák wants you to follow the river southward in search of the raiding-party.","'Keep following those tracks! I will be right behind you.'","'There lies the village, but it seems peaceful. We know the raiding-party came this way... but where has it gone?'","'Stay back, vermin! You are no better than the treacherous slime that stabbed me, but Natsatúg was surrounded by a company of his fiercest warriors, and you are not!\
\
'They left me here to die, but I have strength enough to cut your throat before my own life ends!'\
\
Thrúgord's head sinks to his chest, and his sudden, barking laugh seems to cause him a great deal of pain. Even so, he bares his teeth in a smile.\
\
'If you are able to slay me, do me this favour: go to the village of the Bear-folk and slay Natsatúg, the wretched villain!'","Continue southward along the river in search of more tracks","Talk to Venko in view of Limlók","The Beorning village of Limlók lies peacefully to the north-west","'Follow the river south, and remain alert for further sign of the Orcs!'","Thrúgord spoke of a village of 'Bear-folk' to which the raiding-party planned to go. He must have meant the town of Limlók, to the north-east.","As Thrúgord dies, he bares his fangs at you in a mocking smile","You find more tracks in the dirt by Hengi's Leap","The blood and the footprints both lead eastward","You find more tracks, but these are speckled with blood","If the raiding-party intended to cross the river here, the broken bridge prevented it","'Nothing about these tracks convinces me that the raiding-party changed its chosen course, ${PLAYER}. We should continue following the river south, but not without caution! Let us remain alert for further sign of the Orcs!'","You and your companions discovered evidence that the raiding-party travelled south from the ruins of Framsburg. Where has it now gone?","Venko looks out upon the Beorning village of Limlók, the obvious question on his lips: where is the raiding-party?","'The village seems safe, for now.'","Chapter 2.5: Danger Downriver","By Hengi's Leap you found more tracks left by the raiding-party, but the broken bridge likely prevented them from crossing the river. They may have continued south instead.","Continue following the river south in search of more tracks","Bloody tracks led eastward, away from the river.","Find the source of the blood-spattered tracks"},
[3047]={"An emissary from Dulgabêth has come to treat with Gondor.","Yadêphal is at the Black Gate, waiting to bring Aragorn to treat with his master.","Aragorn is at the Black Gate.","'He has come to the Black Gate under a flag of peace, and he desires to speak to the king of Gondor. I do not think that is wise.\
\
'I ask that you speak with this emissary on Aragorn's behalf, ${PLAYER}. Remember that he is not to be harmed, and it would be imprudent to be rude. But learn what he wants, and then present his requests to Aragorn.'","Chapter 2.5: Mouth of Gondor","'I am Yadêphal. I bring a message from Dulgabêth, the Black Word of Mordor and Heir of Sauron. I was commanded to bring my message directly to the king of Gondor!'\
\
Yadêphal's face twists with hatred, but it soon gives way to doubt.\
\
'I will not return with my task uncompleted. The message is this: \\qDulgabêth, once Mouth of Sauron but now Sauron's Heir, requests an audience with the king or steward of Gondor.\\q I am to bring him to the bones of Barad-dûr, where Dulgabêth will meet with him and propose terms of the peace.\
\
'Deliver him this message, and I will bring him to Dulgabêth!'","Talk to Yadêphal and meet with Dulgabêth","'I reject his terms, as you knew I would. I will not elevate any of Sauron's servants, whether they swear allegiance to my rule or not. Dulgabêth and the others like him were evil under Sauron, and they are evil now. Tell the emissary I am not interested in this offer, and return to me when he has gone.'","'The message I was commanded to bring is this: \\qDulgabêth, once Mouth of Sauron, but now Sauron's Heir, requests an audience with the king or steward of Gondor.\\q I am to bring him to the bones of Barad-dûr, where Dulgabêth will meet with him and propose terms of the peace.\
\
'Deliver him this message, and I will bring him to Dulgabêth!'","Yadêphal has come to the Black Gate, an emissary from his master.","'I ask that you speak with this emissary on Aragorn's behalf, ${PLAYER}. Remember that he is not to be harmed, and it would be imprudent to be rude. But learn what he wants, and then present his requests to Aragorn.'","Aragorn is waiting at the Black Gate to hear the terms of Dulgabêth's peace.","'Bring the terms of my master's peace to the king. I will wait here for his acceptance of them.'","'So the king of Gondor is not only a coward, he is a fool as well! He has placed his own seal on the order of his death. It is no matter to me. Dulgabêth will remember this when he has conquered all of Mordor and comes to Gondor to finish what Sauron had begun!'","Talk to Yadêphal at the Black Gate","'I do not trust this emissary, or Dulgabêth his master, but I do wish to hear the terms he would propose. I suspect they will be no more acceptable than the last, though these come not from Sauron, but from a servant made bold by the absence of his former lord.\
\
'I can trust only you with this responsibility, ${PLAYER}. Will you treat with Dulgabêth on my behalf? Tell the emissary you speak with my voice and my authority.'","'You speak with the king's voice? Pah! Is the king of Gondor so cowardly that he dares not stand before Dulgabêth in all his majesty? He sends others where he is too frightened to go? This does not surprise me.\
\
'You, then, I will bring. We go to Barad-dûr, where my master waits.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Aragorn at the Black Gate","'What did the Mouth of Sauron propose this time, ${PLAYER}? I doubt the terms of his peace are any more acceptable than they were before the downfall of Sauron.'\
\
You describe Dulgabêth's offer of peace, and Aragorn maintains a solemn expression while he listens to your account. When you have finished, a slight smile lightens his features.\
\
'You would not think he was on the losing side of the conflict with these terms, would you? His master lost the war, and all we have to do is wrap up Sauron's land with a festive bow and gift it to his former servant? Actually, there is more than that: the Mouth also wants us to help him put down the several challengers to his rule? Have any won sovereignty with less effort than this, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'I reject his terms, as you knew I would. I will not elevate any of Sauron's servants, whether they swear allegiance to my rule or not. Dulgabêth and the others like him were evil under Sauron, and they are evil now. Tell the emissary I am not interested in this offer, and return to me when he has gone.'","'That offer of peace may have been unacceptable, but Dulgabêth revealed the matters about which he is concerned, and by so doing he has given us a valuable weapon to use against him.\
\
'The weapon is information, ${PLAYER}.'","Yadêphal, emissary of Dulgabêth, is at the Black Gate."},
[3048]={"Talk to Asitám in Furukzahar","Hámisar smiles at King Elessar indulgently","'I ask that you wander elsewhere, stranger. There's nothing for you here.'","'What did they call themselves? The Kindred of... the something?'","Talk to King Elessar in the throne room of Furukzahar","King Elessar and Hámisar of the Temámir speak together in the throne room of Furukzahar.","Explore the armoury of Furukzahar","Talk to Hámisar inside the throne room of Furukzahar","Curiously, you feel a strange sensation of dread as you approach the door","Chapter 2.6: Dwarves of Furukzahar","The armoury bustles with activity and the sound of dwarves working at the forges","Find Hámisar in the throne room of Furukzahar","'What has brought you to Furukzahar? I hope you do not think to involve us in your wars? The Temámir of Furukzahar have always welcomed visitors from the other dwarf families, but Hámisar shut the gates for a reason. He did not intend to invite Gondor's war to our doorstep.'","'You may enter. Hámisar awaits you within.'","Hámisar has invited you to meet the people of Furukzahar while he speaks with King Elessar.","The ruler of Furukzahar awaits you and the King of Gondor in his throne room in the north-western reaches of the fortress.","Talk to Zimikál in Furukzahar","The delicious aroma of cooking food fills the kitchens of Furukzahar","'Enjoy yourself, my friend. I will ask Caebar to stay and document the proceedings, but you and Gimli are free to meet with Hámisar's people.'","Talk to Gúlkhu in Furukzahar","Explore the kitchens of Furukzahar","'They are called the Kindred of the Coins, Elessar, but feel no shame at forgetting it. The name is fresh in my mind, for a member of their company visited Furukzahar some weeks ago with a proposal for me.'","'Enjoy the sights of Furukzahar while the King of Gondor and I speak about the ongoing relationship between our peoples.'","Explore the rooms south of the throne room in Furukzahar","'Hámisar and I have come to an arrangement for the continued relations of his people and mine, ${PLAYER}. During the discussion... something revealed itself to me.'\
\
Elessar holds your gaze with a stern eye.\
\
'Hámisar spoke to me of a group arising in Umbar, across the Bay of Belfalas. He says they call themselves... the Kindred of... something. What was it?'","Hámisar rules Furukzahar from his throne room in the north-western reaches of the fortress.","'Hámisar awaits you within.'","Talk to Hámisar in the throne room of Furukzahar","'Welcome, King Elessar, to the stronghold of Furukzahar. How shameful that our folk have remained neighbours for so long without you coming to visit us here. I mourn that it took the fighting of a war to bring us together... but at least something did so.'\
\
Hámisar turns his attention to you.\
\
'I gave my greeting to the King, but of course his companions are welcome here as well! He and I have matters to discuss concerning the ongoing relationship between our peoples and how the Temámir can best aid in the rebuilding of his kingdom. I would not think to bore you with such matters! I hope you will explore the beautiful corridors of Furukzahar and meet with my folk.'","King Elessar has been invited to visit Furukzahar, a stronghold of the Temámir dwarves in the White Mountains.","Hámisar nods his head to Elessar in greeting","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. I did not expect the King of Gondor to accept the invitation to visit Furukzahar so swiftly! It reflects well upon him for respecting the will of Hámisar, and upon you for bringing word to him with such haste!\
\
'I hope you enjoy your stay here, and that King Elessar and ruler Hámisar are able to arrive at a fair and equitable arrangement that will enrich both of their folk.'"},
[3049]={"Venko does not believe that Limlók is safe, and the Zhélruka warrior wants to investigate.","'Why has this raiding-party not shown itself? Perhaps the villagers have seen something of use to us.'","Chapter 2.6: Limlók Under Attack","Imák stands in the centre of Limlók, satisfied with the day's fighting.","You have come to the Beorning village of Limlók with your travelling companions, but there is no sign of the raiding-party from Gundabad.","Talk to Imák in Limlók","'And so our mission is at an end, ${PLAYER}! Had I known at the outset how little time we would need to spend together before its successful conclusion, I might not have complained so loudly! Ah, it is a jest only.\
\
'You performed admirably during the attack, ${RACE}. Indeed, Venko and Glóin also proved themselves most able in battle. These folk are fortunate that we were here.'","Talk to Venko and search Limlók for the vanished raiding-party","'Do you remember the metal badge marked with the thundercloud symbol? The one you found among the ruins of Framsburg that the Orcs must have dropped? Glóin showed it to me while we journeyed south. I do not know about you, ${PLAYER}, but I do not generally think thunderclouds are known for being stealthy.\
\
'No, Thrúgord's fellows are around here somewhere. That they have not shown themselves reveals a more worrying purpose than I believed they could possess. If they are not mere pillagers... what are they?\
\
'We should go down into the town. Is it too much to hope that they have already turned aside these raiders?'"},
[3050]={"'Should this new Lord of Gundabad send another batch of raiders, they too will be slain. I do not see why this need be any different.'","Chapter 2.7: A Thirst for Blood","'Why do your companions wear these solemn expressions? Nothing has changed: Orcs have long been a threat by the Wells of Langflood, and this is not the first raiding-party whose blood has watered the ground near Limlók. A new Orc-lord in Gundabad means little to me or my people.\
\
'Should he send another batch of raiders, they too will be slain. I do not see why this need be any different.'","Glóin barely notices your approach. What troubles the old dwarf?","'But where has the old Longbeard gone? Does he not wish to celebrate this victory with the rest of us, and with the people of the village?'","Talk to Glóin at the edge of Limlók","Runerik Knotbeard stands in the village of Limlók.","'I have made up my mind, ${PLAYER}. Gorgar the Ruthless prepares for war. Whether he is motivated by vengeance or traditional Orkish hatred does not matter. It cannot matter. Whatever his reasons, this new Lord of Gundabad must be stopped before he is ready to strike.\
\
'I will send messages back to Durin at Skarháld and to King Thorin at the Lonely Mountain. We cannot wait for Gorgar to attack. We must assemble our armies before he is made ready. Durin was right, ${PLAYER}. We must retake Gundabad from its new master. It is no longer a mere dream. It is now a matter of survival.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>The story continues in future updates!</rgb>","Return to Runerik Knotbeard in the village of Limlók","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard in Limlók.","Talk to Glóin in Limlók","Talk to Imák in Limlók","'I understand Runerik's position, for Orcs have always threatened his lands and he sees no difference here. Would you ask me to be newly-afraid of the worms and drakes of the Grey Mountains, or would I respond as he does?'","Join Glóin at the edge of Limlók","'I do not like it... no, not at all...'","Imák stands in the village of Limlók.","'I am sorry, my friend. I should celebrate with the others, for the raiding-party is destroyed and Limlók is safe, but the words of Natsatúg as he lay dying have embedded themselves in my heart like a knife.\
\
'The name he spoke is known to me, for his lineage is long and cruel and has troubled Durin's Folk for all the years of my life. I spoke to you of Azog, who led the Orcs against us during the Great Orc War, and perished beneath Dáin's heel at Azanulbizar? A son he had, Bolg, who commanded the Orcs at the Battle of Five Armies. Bolg died before the Lonely Mountain, but his line did not end there. Two were the sons of Bolg. One was named Gorgar, and if the words of Natsatúg can be trusted he calls himself now the Lord of Gundabad.\
\
'Bolg's other son was Mazog, ${PLAYER}, the same Mazog who was slain by my old companion Bofur's grandson Broín, wielding the mithril axe Zigilburk. This new Lord of Gundabad possesses no shortage of grievance against the dwarves, but the death of his brother Mazog can only fuel that most powerful of desires: a thirst for blood, and vengeance.'","Glóin has walked away from your companions and stands now at the edge of Limlók, deep in thought. What troubles the old dwarf?","The Blade-feast raiding-party has been defeated and the village of Limlók is safe, but the news that Gundabad has a new lord can only mean further troubles ahead for the region washed by the Langflood.","Glóin remains silent, contemplating the words of Natsatúg.","'I think Runerik is twice-wrong about this. Something about this new Lord of Gundabad smells wrong to me, and my nose is never wrong. Second, he says his people will simply stand against whatever raiders come his way? I say he is wrong! Without our assistance Limlók would be a smoking ruin by now, and he had best not forget it!'","Talk to Venko in Limlók","Runerik looks pleased with himself and with the bravery of his folk","Glóin has returned to Limlók.","Glóin has walked away from your companions and stands now at the edge of Limlók, deep in thought.","'Where has the old Longbeard gone?'"},
[3051]={"Talk to Gimli in the guest rooms of Furukzahar","King Elessar is in the throne room of Furukzahar.","'We will accept your gracious offer of hospitality, Hámisar, and I thank you for dealing with the emissary of the Kindred of the Coins as you say. Gondor does not wish for war, and if Umbar does not offer violence, we will have no need to respond with such.\
\
'Come, my friends. We will retire to our guest rooms and leave Hámisar to think upon the matters we discussed. No doubt he values the friendship of Gondor, and understands the importance of such a relationship for Furukzahar, and for his people.'","'I do not like this, ${PLAYER}. Hámisar is hiding something. I think he would have preferred not to speak to us of the Kindred of the Coins, and had we left him the choice he would not have spoken of them at all. I believe this Khôltekh came to Furukzahar, but I am less certain the meeting was as Hámisar presented it.\
\
'We should remain on our guard while we are here. Something about this situation does not feel right.'","Gangur Farwend, a Longbeard visiting from the north, has quietly called for your attention.","'Let us retire to the rooms Hámisar has provided.'","King Elessar is in the guest rooms of Furukzahar on the eastern side of the fortress.","'Hámisar told you this emissary of the Kindred departed, but I think he is still here; it is the dread of the artifact he bears that you sensed outside the door where he shelters. I do not know why the Temámir became so cold to me after he arrived, or why their leader lies to the King of Gondor, but I thought you should know. I will speak with King Elessar briefly, if it can be arranged in secret, but I think you should all leave this place before it is too late. Furukzahar may not be safe for you.'","Caebar is in the guest rooms of Furukzahar.","Talk to Gangur Farwend by the suspicious door in Furukzahar","'This is all so overwhelming. How did I come to be here?'","The guest rooms of Furukzahar are on the eastern side of the fortress.","Investigate the suspicious door south of the throne room in Furukzahar","Talk to King Elessar in the throne room of Furukzahar","'I feel as if I struggle to stay afloat in deep water, and something tries to pull me under. I have felt this way for most of my time in the employ of the King, and the Steward Denethor before him!'","Elessar hands you a parchment on which Caebar has sketched a portrait","'I knew there was something going on when they made us wait on the doorstep for so long. Did I not tell you so?'","Hámisar has provided comfortable rooms for Elessar and his companions","Elessar gave you the sketch Caebar made of Khôltekh the Cunning from Gangur's description.","Find the guest rooms provided for Elessar's party on the eastern side of Furukzahar","'Not here! We should speak inside the armoury, across the water to the north-east. The noise will help to hide our conversation.'","'Please enjoy the hospitality of Furukzahar. Your guest rooms are on the eastern side of the fortress.'","A member of the Kindred of the Coins brought a proposal to Hámisar of Furukzahar in recent weeks.","'This messenger was named Khôltekh, and he claimed that the Kindred of the Coins had overthrown the servants of Sauron who ruled in Umbar. Now they name it a Free City, and seek allies to defend themselves from those who preferred the old order of things... and from Gondor, it must be said.\
\
'It was a proposal of peace and friendship that Khôltekh brought to me. I do not wish to become involved in the affairs of Umbar, so while I did not immediately refuse, nor did I give him the enthusiastic agreement he desired. I sent him on his way, but if he was disappointed he did not show it when he departed. That was a fortnight ago, and he is likely back in Umbar by now.\
\
'But we have spoken now for such a time that my throat is parched and my eyes weary. Accept a guest room and remain here for the night. There is no need for you to depart as speedily as did Khôltekh, after all. A room will be provided for you on the eastern side of the fortress, King Elessar, and I trust your companions will take their rest in comfort. What say you to this?'","Chapter 2.7: Khôltekh the Cunning","Examine the sketch of Khôltekh the Cunning","'We have no choice now, my friends. We should get as much rest as we are able. Whatever Hámisar thinks to keep from us, whether it is the continued presence of Khôltekh the Cunning in Furukzahar or some other deception, we cannot reveal it if he chooses to keep it hidden.\
\
'We will depart in the morning. Rest for now... but lightly.'","'Once you have studied the sketch, you can give it back to Caebar.'","'Do you really think Hámisar is lying to the King? Why would he risk such a dangerous deception? You don't think he's in league with the Kindred of the Coins, do you?\
\
'I am just a scribe, ${PLAYER}, and not especially accomplished at that. I am not an adventurer or a hero like you; I left my home in Ethring a few months before the outbreak of war. Ever since I came to Minas Tirith and the service of the City, I have become embroiled in great events I find myself unable to comprehend.\
\
'It is all very overwhelming to me. What is Hámisar keeping from the King?'","'What is Hámisar keeping behind that suspicious door, ${PLAYER}? Perhaps you can investigate further, but do try not to draw attention to yourself.'","'My hand shook as I drew the sketch, ${PLAYER}. I do not know if I am properly cut out for such an adventure as this! I hope you and the King find the drawing useful. Will you now know Khôltekh the Cunning if you see him?\
\
'If you will not, the fault lies with me... I apologized to the King, for I am only an amateur artist, but he would not hear it. He is too good for such as I am.'","Talk to Gangur Farwend inside the armoury of Furukzahar in the north-eastern reaches of the fortress","'You are a companion of the King of Gondor? Have we met? My memory for faces is not what it once was, and I am far from my home. I am here visiting, but I believe I have information you should know.\
\
'Quietly! We should not speak here. Let us meet inside the armoury, across the water to the north-east. There will be fewer unfriendly ears to hear what I have to say, and the noise of the forges should help to hide our conversation.'","Talk to Caebar in the guest rooms of Furukzahar","'When I first arrived here, the Temámir showed me a great deal of hospitality, and Hámisar gave me his personal welcome. I was most impressed, for while I have been warmly greeted at every dwarf-hold I visited on my travels, Furukzahar outshone them all. But then it all changed.\
\
'A few days ago, an emissary from the Kindred of the Coins arrived. His name you know, for Hámisar told it to you, but he withheld his epithet and the folk to whom he belongs. His full name is Khôltekh the Cunning, and he is a dwarf of the Temámir who hails from some distant land. And yet it was not from Umbar he came, or at least not directly; he came from the west. From conversations I overheard I understand that he received delivery of some artifact from the north, and he brought it with him to Furukzahar.\
\
'Hámisar told you this emissary of the Kindred departed, but I think he is still here; it is the dread of the artifact he bears that you sensed outside the door where he shelters. I do not know why the Temámir became so cold to me after he arrived, or why their leader lies to the King of Gondor, but I thought you should know. I will speak with King Elessar briefly, if it can be arranged in secret, but I think you should all leave this place before it is too late. Furukzahar may not be safe for you.'","Return the sketch of Khôltekh the Cunning to Caebar in the guest rooms of Furukzahar","Gangur Farwend has information for you, but he will only share it if you meet with him inside the armoury of Furukzahar.","'Gangur Farwend was just here, ${PLAYER}, and he told me what he said to you. I asked him to describe Khôltekh, and he did the best he could... he did say his memory for faces is not what it used to be. Caebar sketched a drawing from the description. Here it is.'","King Elessar's small travelling party waits in the guest rooms provided by Hámisar.","As you approach the suspicious door, a nearby dwarf seeks to attract your attention","'That Hámisar is lying to us. I don't know about what, or why he seeks to deceive us, but I can see it as plainly as you can see the beard on my handsome face.\
\
'I knew there was something afoot when he made us wait so long on the doorstep! It was not mere discourtesy... it was villainy of some kind! We have yet to discover what type of villainy, perhaps... but villainy nonetheless!\
\
'Do you think it has something to do with the unpleasant sensation of dread we felt by that door south of the throne room, ${PLAYER}? What is Hámisar keeping in that chamber?'","'You should examine the sketch Caebar made of Khôltekh the Cunning.'","You experienced a sensation of dread near a door located south of the throne room in Furukzahar, and King Elessar thinks you should investigate further.","Talk to King Elessar in the guest rooms of Furukzahar","'Accept a guest room and remain here for the night. There is no need for you to depart as speedily as did Khôltekh, after all. A room will be provided for you on the eastern side of the fortress, King Elessar, and I trust your companions will take their rest in comfort. What say you to this?'"},
[3052]={"Talk to King Elessar in the throne room of Furukzahar","Talk to Hámisar in the throne room of Furukzahar","Something has gravely upset Glindor and others of the travelling party","King Elessar is in the throne room of Furukzahar.","'It is time for us to take our leave, Hámisar of Furukzahar. We thank you for your gracious hospitality, and for your continued friendship. The efforts of your folk on behalf of mine in the days to come will not be forgotten.'","'I share your hopes for the future, King Elessar of Gondor, and have this to say as well. As you return to your kingdom and continue the journey about which you spoke yestereve, let caution guide your steps. There are snakes in the grass everywhere.\
\
'Indeed, even some dwarves may hold treachery in their hearts, and give voice to things they ought not. I had to send one such troublemaker from Furukzahar this very morning; the Longbeard Gangur Farwend is no longer welcome within these walls.\
\
'But it is different for you and your companions, King Elessar! You, of course, are welcome to return at any time should you wish to discuss the continuing relationship of our folk. But remember what I said: beware of snakes in the grass, for they are more likely to strike when you expect it not.'","'Fear not, Hámisar. I will remember your words.'\
\
Elessar gives you a knowing look.\
\
'Come now, my friends. We shall rejoin the rest of our travelling party at the Hall of Ost Anglebed, to the south-west.'","Chapter 2.8: Snakes in the Grass","'It's terrible, ${PLAYER}, just terrible! Queen Arwen is nowhere to be found!'","'May there be continued friendship between the Temámir and the people of Gondor.'","Rejoin Elessar's travelling party outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed","The time has come for Elessar and his companions to leave Furukzahar and rejoin the larger company.","Talk to Glindor outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed","'It's terrible, just terrible!'","The Hall of Ost Anglebed is to be found south-west of Furukzahar, in King's Gondor.","'Remember what I said: beware of snakes in the grass.'","Hámisar is in the throne room of Furukzahar.","'Come now, my friends. We shall rejoin the rest of our travelling party at the Hall of Ost Anglebed, to the south-west.'"},
[3053]={"You found Queen Arwen deep in conversation with Roamingstar","Roamingstar stands beside Queen Arwen, north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.","'If I wore my Ranger garb I could have approached without making any noise, but these garments are much less suited for walking in the wilderness. I hope I did not frighten Roamingstar with my tramping! Arwen has spoken to me of her desire to meet the Maiden of the Gilrain, and I did not wish to interrupt.\
\
'But I have need of you, my friend.'","'Ioreth saw someone wearing the Queen's cloak walking to the north-west of Ost Anglebed, in the direction of the river? You should hurry after her, and see for certain!'","King Elessar has arrived","'I have not seen Queen Arwen today. I hope she is safe!\
\
'Have you spoken with Ioreth? She sees more than you might think, and may know where the Queen has gone!'","Learn where Queen Arwen has gone","'But I hope you will heed my words, Maiden of the Gilrain, and trouble yourself not overmuch. A life is lived as it is lived, and if we grieve for all that has transpired, or for all that will, we could not bear the sorrow. Let it not weigh too heavily upon you, dear one.'\
\
Arwen turns to see you, and smiles.\
\
'I hope I did not worry the company too greatly, ${PLAYER}, but I did not want to burden Roamingstar with the tramping feet of my husband's entire retinue. There were things to be said in private, and I felt certain I could return before Ioreth finished her chattering. I saw her from afar and it seemed she had only recently begun. Even from such a distance I believe she might have become rather enamoured of the groom who keeps the horses.'","Queen Arwen has disappeared, and none know where she might be found.","'I have spoken with the folk up here, and none have seen the Queen. Perhaps you should search the lower levels of the city.'","'There were things to be said in private. I hope the rest of the company did not worry overmuch about me.'","'The Queen is gone? What do you think might have happened to her?\
\
'Do you think she will be all right? What will happen now to Gondor?'","'Someone in Ost Anglebed must know where the Queen has gone!'","Talk to Roamingstar, Maiden of the Gilrain","Queen Arwen is deep in conversation with Roamingstar, north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.","Talk to King Elessar north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor","'Now that you mention it, while we were out I did see someone wearing a cloak very similar to the one the Queen prefers walking north-west of Ost Anglebed, in the direction of the river. Do you think she might have gone that way?'","Talk to Queen Arwen","Find Queen Arwen in King's Gondor","Chapter 2.9: The Queen Is Gone","'I have not seen my sister today, but I am not yet worried. Arwen can take care of herself, if the need arises.\
\
'She will be fine.'","'Arwen has shown me a kindness of the sort I had thought vanished from the world, ${PLAYER}. I do not know what to say.'","'We must not immediately expect foul play, ${PLAYER}. The Queen is likely to be fine.\
\
'But we should speak with those of our company who may have seen her lately, perhaps Grethril, Aphadaer, or Ioreth. They are often together, and may have observed without notice what happened to Arwen.'","'I am sorry I cannot help you, ${PLAYER}! I was deep in conversation with Aphadaer and Grethril a few hours ago, and we only learned the Queen was missing when we returned from our walk! It was such a nice stroll, it was, with the flowers all in bloom... Aphadaer presented me with the finest one he could find, and...'\
\
Ioreth trails off, a faint blush colouring her cheeks.\
\
'Do you know, I think he might be sweet on me? Can you imagine? Oh, to be young again! But now that you mention it, while we were out I did see someone wearing a cloak very similar to the one the Queen prefers walking north-west of Ost Anglebed, in the direction of the river. Do you think she might have gone that way?'","You should ask around Ost Anglebed and learn if anyone knows where the Elf-queen has gone.","'I beg you, ask around Ost Anglebed and find the Queen! The King will never forgive us if we have allowed some harm to befall her!'","King Elessar has rejoined his Queen north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.","Wait for a new arrival","Ioreth told you she saw someone wearing a cloak much like Queen Arwen's walking to the north-west of Ost Anglebed, in the direction of the river."},
[3054]={"<rgb=#FF00FF>Listen</rgb> to the half-orcs","'...halflings are all they care about in - gah! What was that? A spy, might be. Best be moving on, boys.'","You should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion.","Three travel-worn half-orcs stand on the ledge above you, north of the main road in Udûn, talking amongst themselves. You should <rgb=#FF00FF>listen</rgb> to hear some more.","Pippin and Merry are north of the main road in Udûn.\
\
You should talk to Merry and Pippin about the trio of half-orcs you just overheard.","Three travel-worn half-orcs stand on the ledge above you, north of the main road in Udûn, talking amongst themselves. You should continue to listen <rgb=#FF00FF>listen</rgb> to their conversation.","Look for a northward path ahead","'Well, what is it, Pippin?'","'They said yes? I knew they would! Pippin and I have packed our packs. With the help of all these friendly big folk, we are well-provisioned indeed.\
\
'Let us meet within - what's that they call it - the Foothold in Udûn?'","You should talk to Pippin, who says his stomach is growling.\
\
If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.","Habla con Merry","'Pippin and I have just been enjoying the view, wondering if you'd ever arrive! We might as well start on down there, I suppose. Well, no point in loitering, now. Let's be off!\
\
'What do you say we make our way to the first cross-roads on down into the valley? You can make it out from here, only just.'","'Pippin is joking, of course. I am not the least bit ashamed to ask, but he is. Oh, just humour him.\
\
'And before you go, be sure to see the gardens and the baths. It is beyond remarkable, is what it is!'","You have only begun eating when Merry looks up, startled","Habla con Gandalf","Merry has suggested going a bit further along the main road in the Udûn valley, and then look for a way that turns north.\
\
If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.","'Did you hear that too? I am hardly sure of myself, but I thought I heard something... something voice-like, coming from uphill.\
\
'Quickly and quietly, friends, let us see what it was - if it was anything at all.'","'Poke their noses into Mordor? That is exactly how they put it, I imagine. Well, to be honest, I would mislike the thought of those two going in alone. But if you will promise to stay close by and look after them, then they have my blessing.\
\
'To Pippin I do grant leave.'","'Imagine how it must have looked with all the Dark Lord's armies gathered there.'","'A word with you, ${PLAYER}. I know well enough that I have done little to hinder Merry and Pippin an excursion into Mordor. I hope I have lent some gravity to it, however. More importantly, I would ask you to stick by them.\
\
'On this point, I ask a favour of you. Take them into Udûn when you go, and keep a sharp eye open for things that do not belong there. I have some reason to believe you may find something of interest to you and to our two meddling friends, if you do.'","Habla con Pippin","Blow Merry's horn to call him back","Explore to the soldiers' camps","Return to Merry and Pippin","<rgb=#FF00FF>Sit</rgb> down and share in the meal","You should explore further along the main road in the Udûn valley, where the mass of soldiers' tents begins.\
\
If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.","Habla con Aragorn","'There you are, ${PLAYER}! We had been looking for you. What happy luck that you are here now!'","'No sign of either treasure or adventure here, but then I suppose we've only just started. If you ask me, we ought to head up the road and have a look at all the soldiers' tents there.'","'Hush, both of you. I want to hear some more!'","You should talk to Merry, at the picnic spread in Udûn, and find out what startled him.","Habla con Éomer","Pippin has suggested moving to a flat spot just north of the main road in Udûn, and stopping to eat some and rest up.\
\
If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.","Merry and Pippin persist in their determination to venture into Mordor.","You should return to Merry and Pippin in Bâr Thorenion with word that they have Aragorn and Éomer's blessings to go into Mordor.","Find Pippin in Bâr Thorenion","'Will you ask permission for us? We would go ourselves only - somehow it would all be better if you would do it. Aragorn and Éomer are likely just outside the Black Gates, in the Slag Hills.'","Look for the source of the sound","You hear a gruff, familiar throat being cleared behind you","Explore to the cross-roads","You should explore down in the Udûn valley, as far as the first cross-roads, with Merry and Pippin.\
\
If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.","'Which do you think we shall stumble over first, adventure or treasure?'","'All these empty tents only put me in mind of what horrible things war and strife are. Perhaps we should see some of the forgeworks. Let us go on a bit and look for a path heading north.'","Chapter 2: A First Furtive Foray","'I say we set down on that flat patch I saw, just north of the main road and behind some tents. It would be the perfect place to have a bite to eat and restore our weary limbs.'","The two hobbits quickly lay out a considerable amount of food on a thin Gondorian quilt","Both Aragorn and Éomer can be found outside of the Black Gate, in the area of the Slag Hills.\
\
Merry and Pippin have asked you to ask Aragorn and Éomer for permission to venture into Mordor.","'Think of it, ${PLAYER}. We are on the other side. The front porch of the Enemy, you might say, though I am awfully glad he isn't home, nor shall be!'","'To the first cross-roads - then we shall see what we shall see and decide what to do from there.'","'The two Periain, Meriadoc and Peregrin, were here not long past, looking for you. They returned to Bâr Thorenion, but implored that you should join them as soon as you could.'","Go up the northern path from the hobbits' picnic in Udûn and see if you can find what Merry heard.","Merry looks uncharacteristically pale.\
\
'I have lost my appetite for food, and adventure, and any promise of treasure or gold, Pippin. Let us call it a day and head back, shall we?'","'Master Merry Holdwine wishes to see Mordor? I would not deny him it, for all that he has done and been through!'","Stop for a bite to eat","'We have talked it over and made up our minds, Merry and I - but say, before I go into all that, look around you. See what those big folk have done to the place! It's hard to believe we were just here, when it was quite an old ruin. It's no ruin now. Gandalf must have been quite desperate to turn our heads away from Mordor if he felt the need to drag us here before they'd gone to work.\
\
'Ah, silly me! But Mordor is exactly why we wanted to talk to you. We have not abandoned the idea of going only... well... we were hoping you might ask Éomer and Aragorn on our behalf. You see, we've got some things to attend to here before we set off. And if you ask me, Merry couldn't bear to see the disappointed look on Éomer's face if he should disapprove the idea.\
\
'Will you do it? They have both been carrying on their kingly business around the Black Gates. You will find them just outside, in the Slag Hills, I imagine.'","DNT YOU FIND SOME THINGS","You should <rgb=#FF00FF>sit</rgb> down with Pippin and Merry at their Mordor picnic spread, off the main road in Udûn, and share in the meal.","'...hear we've got news about the wizard and what's going on in the halflings' lands, they'll pay, just you wait...'","You should meet Merry and Pippin at the Foothold encampment in Udûn.","DNT merry returns","'...come all this way with news to sell, and we will find a buyer...'","'All this wandering about in the realm of the Dark Lord is well enough, though I don't see why another troll-hole laden with Elven blades hasn't presented itself just yet. But I will not keep this up with our stomachs growling, when so many fine provisions are weighing down my pack.\
\
'You wanted to turn northward, Merry. Why don't we head up that way and stop at that flat bit, there? It doesn't look like anyone should bother us, and we'll restore ourselves properly before moving on.'","DNT summon merry","'Well for one, I hardly imagined the noise - or the stench!'","Meet at the Udûn Foothold","'Then our little plan is advanced? I knew we could count on you, ${PLAYER}.'","Gandalf has appeared nearby to Aragorn and Éomer, outside the Black Gate in the Slag Hills, and has made it clear that he wishes to talk to you.","'Go on ahead, ${PLAYER}. If I really did hear something, it is just up the path here. Pippin and I will be just behind you.'","'Well! You can see what a hard time of things we have been having, Pippin and I. Still, I worry his head may fall off of his shoulders, for how swift and how often it's been turning this way and that!'","'Wizard? Halfling lands? And that voice. I would have sworn it was one of Bill Ferny's friends, come all the way to Mordor.'"},
[3055]={"Glúmur tiene curiosidad por las últimas palabras de los sirvientes de Mazog, sus leales guardias Pûlpum, y quiere que descubras si hay algo de verdad en sus últimas palabras.","Capítulo 2: Un poder mayor","'¿Recuerdas dónde se encuentra Zabadgathol, ${PLAYER}? Estoy seguro de que sí: ¡en Nud-melek! Busca en ese lugar cofres del tesoro que puedan contarnos algo sobre el misterioso aliado de Mazog.'","'Bueno, ¿dónde están los cofres del tesoro?'","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has recuperado algunos cofres del tesoro de Zabadgathol y deberías llevarlos a Bori para que los examine.","'¿Habéis vuelto con los cofres del tesoro? Bien, bien. Veamos qué hay dentro.'\
\
Bori abre un cofre y parece muy sorprendido por lo que ve dentro.\
\
'No son simples baratijas, sino poderosas y valiosas reliquias. ¡Mira esto, y esto otro! Sin duda parecen malvados, y están cubiertos de sellos crueles. Y dos runas: D.G.\
\
'¡Oh no... es peor de lo que pensaba! El misterioso benefactor de Mazog proviene de Dol Guldur, en las profundidades deL Bosque Negro. ¡Esto no augura nada bueno!'","Lleva los cofres del tesoro a Bori","'Pero basta de hablar de Bróin. Con todo lo que ha pasado, se merece un descanso y no quiero perturbar su tranquilidad contándole todos los detalles de nuestros esfuerzos en Zabadgathol.\
\
'Tengo curiosidad por las últimas palabras de esos sirvientes de Mazog, los guardias Pûlpum que derrotasteis. Parece que alguien está aliado con Mazog, pero ¿con qué fin?\
\
'Vuelve a Zabadgathol y busca allí cofres del tesoro. Quiero saber más sobre el misterioso aliado de Mazog.'","Zabadgathol se encuentra en Nud-melek.\
\
Glúmur te ha pedido que regreses a Zabadgathol, la fortaleza de Mazog en Nud-melek, y que busques cofres del tesoro que puedan revelar la identidad de su misterioso aliado."},
[3056]={"Derrota a los Orcos en Zelem-melek o en las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Capítulo 2: Lejos de casa","'¿Qué podría haber atraído a la Mano Blanca a Moria?'","'¡Los Orcos de la Mano Blanca no deberían estar aquí, ${PLAYER}, pero todos los Orcos representan una amenaza. Busca a los Orcos en Zelem-melek y en las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo, y hazles saber lo bienvenidos que son con el mordisco de tu arma!'","'¿Orcos de la Mano Blanca? ¿Aquí? No me gusta.'","Los Orcos se pueden encontrar por todo Zelem-melek y las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo de Moria.\
\
Brogur te ha pedido que derrotes a los Orcos por todo Zelem-melek y las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo, sin importar a qué tribu pertenezcan.","Orcos derrotados en Zelem-melek o en las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:seguro[m]|segura[f]} de que el uruk al que te enfrentaste llevaba la marca de la Mano Blanca?\
\
'Eso es muy inusual, . ¿Qué pudo haber obligado a estas criaturas a entrar en Moria? ¡Ciertamente no entraron por el mismo camino que nosotros! Eso significa que deben haber rodeado las montañas y entrado por el este, pero ¿con qué propósito? Hay una trama sospechosa en marcha, y no me gusta.\
\
'Ah, no importa. ¡Cualquier orco o uruk es una amenaza para nosotros, los de la Mano Blanca no menos que cualquier otro! Busca orcos de cualquier lealtad por todo Zelem-melek y las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo, y derrótalos donde sea posible. ¡El único orco que me gusta es uno muerto!'","Brogur se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has derrotado a muchos Orcos en Moria, y deberías informar ahora a Brogur de tu éxito.","Brogur está preocupado porque un uruk de la Mano Blanca ha estado explorando cerca del campamento de los enanos.","'Gracias de nuevo por tu ayuda. No me gusta que haya tantos Orcos en Moria, y me preocupa especialmente la presencia de los de la Mano Blanca. O nos han seguido de alguna manera, o estaban aquí antes que nosotros. Ninguna de estas posibilidades es buena para nosotros...'"},
[3057]={"Has derrotado a los crebains espías (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los crebains espías (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge garras irregulares (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se pueden encontrar crebains espías a lo largo de las orillas del Sirannon seco, al sureste de la puerta en ruinas en el área cerca de los Muros de Moria.\
\
Tulk te ha pedido que derrotes a los crebains espías a lo largo de las orillas del Sirannon y que le traigas sus garras, que se pueden usar para varios propósitos.","Has recogido garras irregulares (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva las garras irregulares a Tulk","'El Sirannon fue una vez un arroyo ruidoso, pero ya no lo es.'","Capítulo 2: A lo largo del Sirannon","'No habíamos estado aquí mucho tiempo antes de que se hiciera evidente que algún poder estaba vigilando atentamente Acebeda. Criaturas asquerosas llamadas crebains han aparecido en gran número, espiando nuestros esfuerzos y molestando a los trabajadores. No sé para qué se puede usar la información sobre nuestros esfuerzos, pero su presencia ha hecho que Bósi se sienta incómodo, y eso es suficiente para mí.\
\
'Al sur, puedes ver donde el Sirannon solía fluir, pero se ha secado y el lecho del arroyo ahora está vacío. Camina por las orillas, derrotando a cualquiera de los crebains espías que veas allí, y tráeme sus garras. Podemos darle varios usos a las garras de esas aves repugnantes.\
\
'Más importante aún, sin embargo, estarás obstaculizando cualquier plan malvado que el maestro de estos espías pueda estar tramando para mis parientes.'","'No has recogido suficientes garras de los crebains espías, ${PLAYER}. Búscalos a lo largo del Sirannon seco, al sur de donde estamos.'","Has ofrecido tus servicios a la expedición de enanos que ha venido a Acebeda para reclamar las salas de Khazad-dûm bajo las montañas.","Tulk se encuentra al este de la puerta en ruinas en el área cerca de los Muros de Moria.\
\
El enano Tulk espera tu regreso con las garras que has recogido de los crebains espías a lo largo del Sirannon.","'No soporto a los crebains. Son criaturas asquerosas, y demasiado dispuestas a espiarnos.'","'Mira al sur a lo largo de las orillas del Sirannon seco si deseas encontrar a los crebains espías que nos han causado tantos problemas, ${PLAYER}. No sé a quién sirven estas aves asquerosas, pero no creo que su maestro nos quiera ningún bien.'","'Gracias por esto, ${PLAYER}, no solo por las garras, sino por derrotar a los agentes de cualquier poder que cree que los enanos no tienen nada que hacer aquí en Acebeda o en Khazad-dûm.'"},
[3058]={"Has derrotado suficientes orcos en Moria para satisfacer a Haldir","Haldir de Lórien se ha negado a concederte una audiencia con Galadriel a menos que puedas demostrar que eres ${PLAYERNAME:un enemigo[m]|una enemiga[f]} de los Orcos de Moria.","'Si eres realmente ${PLAYERNAME:un enemigo[m]|una enemiga[f]} de mis enemigos, puedes demostrarlo matando Orcos y trasgos dentro de Moria. Completa estas dos hazañas y quizás el recuento de tus enemigos sea suficiente para satisfacer mi escepticismo.'","'Los Orcos de Moria se han despertado. Antes, se contentaban con cavar sus madrigueras entre las raíces de Fanuidhol el Gris, Celebdil el Blanco y Caradhras el Cruel, pero ahora se derraman por las puertas del Foso Oscuro y amenazan nuestros bosques.\
\
'¿Dices que has luchado contra los Orcos y los trasgos de Moria? Si realmente eres su ${PLAYERNAME:enemigo[m]|enemiga[f]}, ¡demuéstramelo! ¿Cuántos has matado en los oscuros túneles de Moria? ¿Me convencerás de que eres ${PLAYERNAME:el amigo[m]|la amiga[f]} que dices ser, y no ${PLAYERNAME:un espía aliado[m]|una espía aliada[f]} con esas fuerzas que nos desean mal?\
\
'Juzgaré tu recuento, pero no te prometo nada.'","Completa la hazaña 'Azote de orcos' en Moria","Haldir se encuentra en su campamento en la frontera de Lothlórien.\
\
Haldir te ha pedido que le demuestres que eres ${PLAYERNAME:un enemigo[m]|una enemiga[f]} de los Orcos y los trasgos de Moria completando dos hazañas: matar a muchos Orcos y trasgos en Moria.","Haldir se encuentra en su campamento en la frontera de Lothlórien.\
\
Has completado dos grandes hazañas dentro de Moria, y podría ser que el recuento de tus victorias sobre los Orcos y los trasgos de Moria sea suficiente para satisfacer a Haldir sobre tus intenciones.","'El registro de tus victorias afirma lo que decías, ${PLAYER}. Lamento haberte dudado, pero estos son tiempos peligrosos. Hemos tenido muchos visitantes extraños en los límites de Lothlórien antes que tú.'","Capítulo 2: Enemistad con los orcos los Orcos","Completa la hazaña 'Azote de trasgos' en Moria","Has derrotado suficientes trasgos en Moria para satisfacer a Haldir"},
[3059]={"'After the destruction of Númenor in the Second Age, Elendil and his sons came to Middle-earth and knew they had to start anew or perish. And so the kingdoms of Arnor and Gondor were founded, Arnor in the north and Gondor in the south.\
\
'At the hill of Erech, in the kingdom of Gondor, Isildur set a great black stone that was brought out of Númenor before its downfall. It is said the stone stands there still, unchanged, even as it was in the latter years of the Second Age.\
\
'That is where -- and when -- our story begins.'","Candaith is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees east of the Uch-luth village of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin.\
\
You have listened to Candaith relate the tale of the Oath-breakers and the Paths of the Dead and should now speak with him.","'If you are ready to listen, I will tell you the tale of the Oath-breakers and the Paths of the Dead.'","Chapter 2: At the Stone of Erech","Talk to Candaith at the grove east of Lhanuch and experience 'Session: At the Stone of Erech' or read the shortened account instead","'The Men of the Mountain sought to escape their curse, fleeing back to their mountain homes, but no word of man relates what became of them in the years since. It is said a shadow lies now on Erech, where they broke their oath, and none now take the Dimholt Road that ran through their gates and into their mountain home.\
\
'The Rohirrim name that peak Dwimorberg, Haunted Mountain, and the passages beneath are known now as the Paths of the Dead. None would take that road, but Elrond bid his sons remember it, and that leads me to worry. I know it lies heavily upon Halbarad's mind.\
\
'And yet Nár knows something of it as well. Have we been watched without our knowledge? But how can that be?'","Candaith is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees to the east of the Uch-luth village of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin.\
\
Candaith has decided to tell you the story of the Oath-breakers and the Paths of the Dead.","In the Second Age, the Men of the Mountain swear an oath at the Stone of Erech to fight the forces of Sauron, but when they break their promise, Isildur levies a curse against them. They will never know rest until they fulfil their oath....","Talk to Candaith at the grove east of Lhanuch","Candaith wishes you to know the story of the Oath-breakers and the Paths of the Dead, so you can appreciate why the Rangers are so disturbed by the words of Nár."},
[3060]={"Bósi está satisfecho de que hayas ayudado a sus enanos con los preparativos, y quiere que hagas lo mismo por los enanos del Corazón de Fuego.","'Entonces, ¿es cierto este rumor de que los orcos están planeando un gran asalto contra nosotros? Tenía miedo de que fuera así.\
\
'No necesito la recomendación de Bósi para saber que eres un activo en nuestros esfuerzos aquí; ¡si no fuera por ti, el Corazón de Fuego todavía estaría sellado para nosotros!'","Capítulo 2: La recomendación de Bósi","'El enano a cargo del Corazón de Fuego es Stóthkell; él escuchará nuestras desgracias y hará lo necesario para preparar la mejor defensa de las forjas, que son tan valiosas para nuestra supervivencia continua.'","Stóthkell es el enano a cargo del Corazón de Fuego, ubicado cerca de la Vía de los Herreros, entre las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Bósi quiere que prestes tu ayuda a los enanos que trabajan en el Corazón de Fuego para que estén preparados si los orcos atacan la Vía de los Herreros.","'Mi corazón se atreve a esperar que estaremos preparados para cuando los orcos lancen su ataque.\
\
'Aún hay tiempo para prepararnos; debemos aprovecharlo al máximo. Viaja a la Vía de los Herreros entre las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata y presta tu ayuda a los enanos que trabajan en el Corazón de Fuego.\
\
'El golpe del martillo podría caer más fuerte allí, si Mazog llegara a aprender la importancia de esas forjas para nuestra resistencia continua. Stóthkell está a cargo del esfuerzo allí; ve a él con mi recomendación de tus méritos.'"},
[3061]={"Candaith is at his camp in the Lone-lands, at the foot of Weathertop.\
\
Elrohir has told you to bring word to the Dúnadan Candaith of the Grey Company's preparations.","The Dúnadan Candaith has a camp near the foot of Weathertop, in the Lone-lands. He must be told the mission of the Grey Company.","'So the time has come at last to stand with Aragorn son of Arathorn, my lord and the chieftain of the Dúnedain. In my heart I knew the day would come, for as the shadows have lengthened, the need for Aragorn to accept his mantle has become all the more pressing.\
\
'I have come to love the lands between The Forsaken Inn and the Last Bridge, and it will grieve me to leave them, but I will do so; I will join the Grey Company and travel south as you have asked.\
\
'While I make ready to leave, will you retrieve a hidden cache of supplies I prepared some time ago? I left a sword, some gloves, and a few other supplies north-east of here, atop a small rise called Echad Sûl, in the shade of a tree. Recover this cache and bring it back to me, for I will have need of it in the lands to the south.'","Locate Candaith's hidden cache at Echad Sûl","Orskdulug falls, his robbery a failure, and you retrieve Candaith's goods","An unsavoury gentleman stands where you thought to find the hidden cache","Candaith is at his camp below Weathertop, in the Lone-lands.\
\
You have recovered the supplies from the hidden cache that were taken by Orskdulug and ruined his plan to rob you with them.","'What are you looking at? It seems to me that these lands should be big enough for you to find a path that takes you out of my sight, little ${RACE}.'\
\
Orskdulug follows your gaze and smirks.\
\
'You like this sword? Found it, I did, and these gloves and a few choice other items. Sometimes you find these little caches in the wild, left by Rangers, I suspect. Easy pickings, if you ask me.\
\
'Looks like you might be easy pickings, too. I'll be taking your gear and your coins, friend. Without a fight, or with one...it is all the same to me!'","Talk to Candaith at Weathertop","'The Dúnadan Candaith has a camp at the foot of Weathertop, in the Lone-lands. Bring him word of the Grey Company's need for him, and he will surely pay it heed.'","Candaith's hidden cache is north-east of his encampment, atop a small rise called Echad Sûl, in the shade of a tree.\
\
The Ranger Candaith has asked you to recover a hidden cache of supplies he prepared some time ago, as he will have need of its contents on the journey of the Grey Company.","'I would have been willing to part with the contents of the cache, ${PLAYER}; items hidden in the wild, once found, should go to their finders. But once Orskdulug sought to use my items to rob you, as far as I am concerned, he gave up his right to them.\
\
'I am pleased to have them back. Thank you.'","'You did not recover the cache?'","'The Dúnedain may be scattered across the wilds of Eriador, but my brother and I know the locations of some few, and from those few will you learn where others may be found.\
\
'The Ranger Candaith was a help to us as we scoured the lands to the south following the rage of the Bruinen; we spoke as often as speed would allow on that journey, and he had many interesting tales to tell of the Lone-lands. You will find his camp there, at the base of Amon Sûl...of Weathertop.\
\
'Tell him that Aragorn has need of his kin. Candaith will be certain to join the Grey Company, for his loyalty to his chieftain cannot be questioned.'","Return to Candaith with the equipment you took from Orskdulug","Candaith's hidden cache at Echad Sûl seems to be gone, and an unsavoury gentleman stands there instead.\
\
Candaith sent you to recover a cache of supplies, but it may now be missing.","'You say that someone may have found the hidden cache and taken its contents for himself? Confront this man, if you would, ${PLAYER}. Some of those items were of great sentimental value to me, and I would have them returned if possible. I understand that what is left in the wild is free to any who chance upon it, but perhaps this man can be persuaded to return the contents of the cache.'","'You will find the hidden cache north-east of here, atop a small rise called Echad Sûl, in the shade of a tree. Recover its contents and bring it to me, and I will go forth to meet the Grey Company.'","Chapter 2: Candaith's Hidden Cache","Talk to Orskdulug at Amon Sûl"},
[3062]={"'Thank you for meeting with the emissaries who have come to Gondor, ${PLAYER}. I have spoken with them now, and we will have further to say on the subject of peace in the future.\
\
'I must be truthful with you, ${PLAYER}. I do not completely trust the men of Harad. It is much easier to sue for peace when your forces have lost in battle, and I do not believe that Hasong or Mauthoi would be so willing to extend peace to Gondor if our positions were reversed. Many good soldiers were slain by weapons of the Haradrim, or trampled beneath the feet of their Mûmakil. Is it a betrayal of those lives to make peace with those who slew them?\
\
'No, I do not think it is, but it is an easier question to ask than to answer. It seems that the delegation from Harad honestly desire peace, and that is a first step. Thank you for your help in this, my friend.'","You have found the emissaries from Harad","The delegation of Elves are just north of the prow, in the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.","Find the Haradrim delegation to Minas Tirith","You have found the Elf emissaries from Lothlórien","'The people of this city have been welcoming, if guarded. They do the name of their city proud in this, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'But I must remember that Elves are not seen in Gondor as often as once they were. These are unusual days for all of us, and there is little doubt the people of Gondor have become more used to unusual sights of late!\
\
'We will not tarry, but will continue upward to the throne room of Elessar. I am eager to speak with him, for I was a friend of his betrothed when we were young, and am still very close with the Lady Arwen.'","The delegation of Haradrim is on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.","Talk to Lalornil of the delegation from Lórien","The delegation of dwarves is on the north-east side of the Fifth Circle in Minas Tirith.","'King Elessar waits at the throne for you, and will be glad to have news of your adventures in Mordor.'","Talk to Mauthoi of the delegation from Harad","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Elessar and the Kingdom of Gondor, and to fight on their behalf in Mordor.","'Delegations have come to the city to meet with me and arrange for renewed ties and alliances, and I will gladly hear their proposals. There is one group that may require some delicacy, however: emissaries have come from Harad, and these men speak not of renewing friendship, for there was none. They speak of making peace where before there was only war. It must be carefully handled.\
\
'Find the dwarf, Elf, and Haradrim delegations in the city and make them feel welcome.'","You have found the dwarf emissaries from Erebor","'King Elessar waits for you in his throne room, and will likely have a task for you to undertake for Gondor, ${PLAYER}. Go and see what the king has for you, and I will await your return.'","'I am Mauthoi, sent by Khas Rûktar for purpose of Kerem-thak. King Gondor will choose if terms of peace are acceptable.'\
\
Mauthoi looks at you with a sly expression on his face.\
\
'You are ${PLAYER}. Great hero, they say. I wonder what might have happened if you encountered Hasong or Mauthoi during battle. Victory... or defeat? Not know now, because of Kerem-thak. I wonder, but not enough to wish it happened. Mauthoi have family back in Yâd Hakar, and tales of ${PLAYER} very convincing.\
\
'Peace best for all.'","The emissaries from Erebor are on the north-east side of the Fifth Circle in Minas Tirith.","King Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.","Talk to Olphadon of the delegation from Lórien","Talk to Hálsi of the delegation from Erebor","Find the dwarf delegation in Minas Tirith","'The folk of this city must have seen a number of dwarves before now, for we have been treated warmly and with kindness, though we be strangers here. This is my first visit so far south, and I am pleased at the quality of the stone I have seen to this point. It could be worked with more skill and more care, but I have always been choosy about such things, as are many of Durin's Folk.\
\
'How much higher must we climb to reach King Elessar's throne? The air thins as we ascend, and it is not to my liking.'","Chapter 2: Embassies from Many Lands","'I am Hasong. I come from Yâd Hakar, great kingdom to the south ruled by the tribe called Sokhûri. Great are our warriors, and greater still is Khas Rûktar, who leads the Sokhûri.\
\
'We met on the field as enemies, for who can foretell the many paths that diverge in war? It is the way of the Sokhûri to fight fiercely when commanded, and fight we did. But in war there is always one who fails. This time, the armies that came from Yâd Hakar are the ones that failed.\
\
'When armies fail, there are two paths. On first path, every man is slain, and army is gone. This is how tribes vanish. Sokhûri cause many tribes to vanish. Khas Rûktar cause it himself, sometimes. Second path called Kerem-thak. This happen when failed army does not want to vanish. Tribe wants to live.\
\
'Hasong and Mauthoi sent by Khas Rûktar to speak to Gondor King. We sent here for Kerem-thak. Khas Rûktar wants peace.'","Find the Elf delegation to Minas Tirith","Talk to Hasong of the delegation from Harad","Talk to King Elessar in his throne room","Talk to Vígmath of the delegation from Erebor","'Messages have been sent from many lands to Minas Tirith, ${PLAYER}, overtures of friendship and words of support for the kingdom. It warms my heart to hear them, and to know that we have allies both near and far.\
\
'Some have sent delegations to the city, and they have begun to arrive. Dwarves, Elves, and Men have come to meet with me and arrange for renewed ties and alliances, and I will gladly hear their proposals. There is one group that may require some delicacy, however: emissaries have come from Harad, and these men speak not of renewing friendship, for there was none. They speak of making peace where before there was only war. It must be carefully handled.\
\
'Find the dwarf, Elf, and Haradrim delegations in the city and make them feel welcome.'","'We bring greetings from Thorin III, King under the Mountain, to King Elessar of Gondor! There will be friendship between Durin's Folk and the Men of Gondor, and let their enemies beware!\
\
'This is the first I have seen of this city, and while there is impressive stonework here there is much that might be improved. If King Elessar wishes it, I am sure there are dwarves among us who would be willing to refine the walls and streets of Minas Tirith.\
\
'I would do it myself if I had a team of dwarves and my tools at the ready, but sadly we have come for diplomacy, not for masonry. Perhaps later!'","'We bring messages of friendship and alliance from the Lord and Lady of the Golden Wood! Many are the preparations, already underway, that will further advance the joined purposes of Elves and Men, and Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel will delight in their completion.\
\
'I have been to this White City, but it was long ago. It is not the shining jewel it was then, but under the rule of King Elessar the Elfstone I believe it can be again.'"},
[3063]={"'I heard that King Thorin has a task for you, ${PLAYER}. You should report to him of your adventures in Mordor and learn what that task might be, and if it is in your power to complete.'","King Thorin III has asked you to deliver news of his ascension to the throne to the following dwarf-leaders throughout Eriador and the Misty Mountains:\
\
Dwalin in Thorin's Hall, Ered Luin.\
Mathi Stouthand at Gondamon, Ered Luin\
Hannar at Othrikar, North Downs\
Avar at Gabilshathûr, East Angmar\
Bósi in the Twenty-first Hall, in Moria\
\
After you have delivered his words to each of these dwarf-leaders, you are to return to the King under the Mountain.","Bósi gives you a stone containing a very small portion of mithril","'Thank you for bringing word from Erebor, ${PLAYER}. I am filled with sadness at the death of Dáin Ironfoot, for he was my king and an inspiration to many of us that undertook this expedition. His son will have my support, of course.\
\
'There have recently been many troubles for us here, and I hope you will put in some good words with King Thorin on our behalf, ${PLAYER}. Tremendous upheavals have shaken the earth in recent days, and many good dwarves have been lost: fallen into pits or separated from their fellows by growing chasms or crumbling ceilings. Something has shaken Khazad-dûm to its very foundations, and I worry that it portends some new evil.\
\
'Tell the new King under the Mountain of our struggles, and remind him of the great wealth that the Iron Garrison hopes to bring to him. Here is a rock containing a small vein of mithril that may encourage him to send help to us. Give it to him with my hopes, my friend.'","'Word travels more swiftly in these days than it did of old, ${PLAYER}, and I know what brings you here. I lived at Erebor for many years, and I would have been there still had I not been charged with oversight of these halls. I am not boastful enough to think that would have changed the course of the battle that was there fought, and yet...'\
\
Dwalin exhales wearily, and strokes his beard.\
\
'I am told Dáin defied the agents of Mordor that came to Erebor seeking news of our old burglar, Bilbo. Perhaps that refusal sealed his fate, and perhaps it did not, but I know Dáin would not be glad to have died of years, in his bed. His was always going to be a battle-death.\
\
'His son Thorin may not have proved himself the dwarf that his father was, but in time he will. He will have my support until that day, and beyond it, for he is now King under the Mountain.'","Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.","Talk to Dwalin in Thorin's Hall, in Ered Luin","'Take those proclamations and bring them to the leaders of the following dwarf cities and outposts in Eriador and the Misty Mountains: Thorin's Hall and Gondamon in Ered Luin, Othrikar in the North Downs, Gabilshathûr in East Angmar, and the Twenty-first Hall of Khazad-dûm. They will therefore be notified that I am now King under the Mountain, and I will await their oaths of support. I have sent messengers to other cities and outposts, so you need not concern yourself with any but these five, and I thank you for the service.'","Talk to Avar at Gabilshathûr, in East Angmar","Talk to Bósi in the Twenty-first Hall of Khazad-dûm","Talk to Mathi Stouthand at Gondamon, in Ered Luin","'The King under the Mountain has been slain before the gates of Erebor, but his son survives? We are fortunate that Thorin III did not fall in the battle.\
\
'He will have my support and that of my dwarves, without question or complaint. That is the way of my people.'","Chapter 2: Loyalty for the New King","'It is time you reported back to King Thorin about your activities in Mordor, my friend. Tell him how your adventures are progressing, and see if he has any further requests for you.'","Hrostyr gives you King Thorin's proclamations for delivery to several dwarf outposts","'You bring tidings that there is a new King under the Mountain? Such is the way of things in war. I had great respect for King Dáin, and know little of his son, but I am a Longbeard and I will support him.\
\
'Does he hate the Dourhands? That is all that matters to me, and to the other dwarves that live at Othrikar!'","Talk to Hannar at Othrikar, in the North Downs","'Erebor is a long way from here, and even though Gabilshathûr is no longer encircled by enemies it is still not a place of safety. The King under the Mountain will have my respect and my loyalty as he always has, old or new, but to speak truthfully matters of succession do not have much of an effect on me or the other dwarves here.\
\
'Perhaps if this Thorin were to journey here and aid us against our enemies I would feel differently. Until that day comes he will have my loyalty, whatever it may be worth to him. I would rather he sent warriors to reinforce us.'","'I welcome your return, ${PLAYER}. Know that your journeys in Mordor on behalf of Durin's Folk are appreciated.\
\
'But I have called you here for another purpose. It may seem trivial, but with the death of my father, Dáin Ironfoot, word that I have ascended to the throne must be sent to other cities and outposts of the dwarves. I expect the leaders of these garrisons will respect my ascension to the throne, but until I receive assurances of this I sleep uneasily.\
\
'Take these proclamations and bring them to the leaders of the following dwarf cities and outposts in Eriador and the Misty Mountains: Thorin's Hall and Gondamon in Ered Luin, Othrikar in the North Downs, Gabilshathûr in East Angmar, and the Twenty-first Hall of Khazad-dûm. They will therefore be notified that I am now King under the Mountain, and I will await their oaths of support. I have sent messengers to other cities and outposts, so you need not concern yourself with any but these five, and I thank you for the service.'","'You have delivered the proclamations? Good, good, very good. What is this?'\
\
You give Thorin the small rock containing mithril, and his eyes brighten when you say it is a gift from Bósi and the Iron Garrison in Khazad-dûm. You tell him also of their recent troubles, but it is difficult to say how closely he listens to that portion of your account.\
\
'There is treasure hidden within Mordor, as you have proven, but only in Khazad-dûm can mithril be found in goodly quantity. The Iron Garrison must simply persevere and mine as much as they can. I am certain such upheavals will quiet after a time. They will need to steel themselves for such difficulties.\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}, once again! Return to your adventures in Mordor on behalf of Durin's Folk, and I will call you if I have need of you again.'","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Durin's Folk and fight on their behalf in Mordor."},
[3064]={"Capítulo 2: El descanso del Portador del Anillo","Frodo Bolsón está en la cima de la colina de Cerin Amroth con algunos miembros de su compañía.\
\
Milwen te ha pedido que hables con Frodo Bolsón, uno de los ocho visitantes que han llegado a Lórien en los últimos días. La doncella elfa está segura de que las noticias de Eriador le interesarán.","Boromir está vagando por los alrededores noroeste del claro donde se alza Cerin Amroth, en el centro de Lórien.\
\
Merry se pregunta si una conversación contigo podría animar a Boromir, quien no parece estar contento con la presencia de la compañía en Lothlórien.","'Antes de que te vayas, , debes saber que no eres ${PLAYERNAME:el único[m]|la única[f]} visitante que ha llegado a Lórien en los últimos días. De hecho, entiendo que eres ${PLAYERNAME:conocido[m]|conocida[f]} por estos invitados y estarán encantados de verte.\
\
El hobbit Frodo Bolsón está descansando con algunos miembros de su compañía en la cima de la colina. No sé qué misión los ha traído al Bosque de Oro, ni si te han confiado ese conocimiento, pero estoy seguro de que estará feliz de verte.'","'¿${PLAYER}? Es muy extraño verte aquí, ya que la última vez que te vi fue la noche en que Elrond de Rivendel te confió la defensa continua de Eriador. ¿Ya está tan segura esa tierra?\
\
Boromir suspira y vuelve a cuadrar los hombros.\
\
Lo siento, ${PLAYER}; mis palabras nacieron de la frustración, no de la antipatía. Cada hora que pasamos aquí sin hacer nada es una hora en la que la sombra se acerca más a mi ciudad.\
\
He visto poco a Aragorn, y aún menos a Gimli; el enano parece haber superado fácilmente su desconfianza hacia los Elfos. Ahora mismo está con Legolas, en lo alto de uno de los árboles en la cima de la colina de Cerin Amroth. Habla con él y compruébalo tú mismo.'","'¡Hola, ${PLAYER}! ¿Yo, conspirador? No es así en absoluto, Sr. Frodo, y sabes que no soy bueno guardando secretos, a pesar de tus bromas.\
\
Es solo que ya nos han pasado tantas cosas extrañas, y este lugar es tan élfico y todo eso, que casi he dejado de sorprenderme cuando ocurre algo fuera de lo común. ¡Y aquí aparece ${PLAYER} saliendo del bosque, justo como debe ser!\
\
Deberías encontrar al Sr. Merry en algún lugar de esta colina, ${PLAYER}; sé que estará encantado de verte. Está dando uno de sus paseos y puede que esté descansando en un jardín privado cercano.'","Gimli está en la plataforma en la cima de Cerin Amroth, en el centro de Lórien.\
\
Boromir, algo molesto por la creciente confianza de Gimli en los Elfos, te ha pedido que hables con el enano.","Samsagaz Gamyi está de pie en la cima de la colina de Cerin Amroth junto a Frodo.\
\
Frodo te ha pedido que le cuentes a él y a Sam las noticias de Eriador.","'El Sr. Merry está dando un paseo por los alrededores de Cerin Amroth. Sé que estará feliz de verte y de escuchar tus noticias. Planeaba descansar en uno de los jardines privados cercanos.'","Meriadoc Brandigamo está dando un paseo en los alrededores de la colina de Cerin Amroth, y puede que ahora esté descansando en un jardín privado cercano.\
\
Frodo y Sam se alegraron mucho de verte en Lothlórien y saben que Merry también lo estará.","'¡Hola, ${PLAYER}! Debo admitir que no pensé encontrarte aquí en Lórien. ¡Estás en el lado equivocado de las montañas, ¿no?! ¡Como todos nosotros!\
\
El rostro de Merry se ilumina mientras ríe largo y fuerte.\
\
Pippin está por aquí, creo que está echando una siesta. No, no lo despertaría; imagino que tendremos tiempo de sobra para ponernos al día. ¡Lothlórien es tan pacífica que es difícil recordar lo duro que será nuestro camino, y lo que ya ha sido!\
\
Me pregunto si podrías buscar a Boromir; no parece estar pasándolo tan bien aquí como el resto de nosotros. Creo que está impaciente por partir de nuevo, pero tal vez verte de nuevo lo anime. La última vez que lo vi fue en los límites noroeste del gran claro donde se alza Cerin Amroth.'","'¡! Cuando Milwen me dijo que ${PLAYERNAME:otro viajero[m]|otra viajera[f]} de más allá de las montañas había llegado a Lothlórien, no tenía idea de que serías tú. ¡Hemos recorrido un largo camino, ¿verdad?! Todavía queda mucho por recorrer, pero aquí en Lothlórien me ha resultado difícil preocuparme demasiado por el camino que queda por delante.\
\
¡Tienes que contarnos a Sam y a mí lo que ha pasado desde que nos separamos, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}! Parece que ha pasado una vida desde que dejamos Rivendel, y varias al menos desde la última vez que vi Bolsón Cerrado.\
\
Pero Sam no parece tan sorprendido de verte como yo, . No te habrás convertido en el principal conspirador de otra conspiración, ¿verdad, Sam?'","'El hobbit Frodo Bolsón descansa con algunos miembros de su compañía en la cima de Cerin Amroth. Sé que estará encantado de hablar contigo y de escuchar noticias de Eriador.'","'Boromir no parece estar contento con nuestra estancia en Lothlórien. Me pregunto si se alegrará al verte, ${PLAYER}.\
\
La última vez que lo vi fue en el extremo noroeste del claro donde se alza Cerin Amroth. ¡Encuéntralo y ve si puedes animarlo!'","'¡Por la barba de Durin! No esperaba verte de nuevo tan pronto, ${PLAYER}. ¡Me alegra la sorpresa!\
\
Legolas me ha estado mostrando los bosques de Lothlórien, y la majestuosidad de estos árboles, tan parecidos a pilares tallados en piedra bajo las montañas, llena de asombro a este enano. Pero incluso en una tierra de maravillas, su Dama es la mayor de todas.\
\
Aun así, estoy listo para volver al suelo. Si me preguntas, los árboles se admiran mejor desde abajo, en vez de entre sus ramas.'","'Gimli está en los árboles sobre la cima de la colina de Cerin Amroth. Habla con él y ve si ya está listo para dejar estos bosques. No habría esperado que un enano confiara tan fácilmente en estos Elfos, pero así lo ha hecho.'","'¡Todavía me cuesta creer que realmente estés aquí, ${PLAYER}! A menos que me equivoque, parece que Sam no está tan sorprendido. No te habrás convertido en el principal conspirador de otra conspiración, ¿verdad, Sam?'","Milwen te ha hablado de varios visitantes de Lórien que estarán interesados en hablar contigo."},
[3065]={"'Ya veo. Admiro la determinación de los Martillogrís y estoy seguro de que Luth y el resto de su familia serán de gran ayuda para la Hueste Dorada, pero espero que dedique más tiempo a sus tareas y menos tiempo a explicar las diversas rencillas que tiene contra los Orcos.\
\
'Todos hemos sufrido a manos de ellos, y Luth no más que el resto de nosotros. Achardor podría decir que ha sufrido menos que algunos.\
\
'Mazog rendirá cuentas por todas las ofensas a su debido tiempo, tanto reales como imaginarias. Raddir habló conmigo mientras buscabas al enano. Es hora de llevar a Mazog más adentro en el Bosque Negro.'","'¿Has encontrado un comunicado destinado a Mazog en el cofre del jefe de los Orcos, en Ashurz Maufulug? Déjame ver qué dice, ....\
\
'La fortuna está de nuestro lado, mi ${PLAYERNAME:aventurero[m]|aventurera[f]} : estos Orcos aún no saben que hemos capturado a Mazog y lo hemos traído al Bosque Negro. Ellos piensan que todavía reside en Moria; la misión de la Guardia Oculta sigue siendo secreta.\
\
'Surgió un problema mientras estabas ausente. Lúth Martillogrís, un enano de la compañía de Bróin, se ha vuelto cada vez más inquieto por los planes de la Hueste Dorada. Habla con él aquí en Echad Sirion, si quieres, y asegúrate de que estamos haciendo todo lo posible para que este viaje sea seguro. Su familia tiene muchas quejas contra los Orcos, pero temo que los Martillogrís nos hagan daño si no mantienen la calma.'","Encuentra un cofre que contenga información sobre Mazog en Maudhûl-ulur o Ashurz Maufulug","Orcos o trasgos Taughâsh derrotados en los Lindes Oscuros (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Por fin, alguien que me escuchará! Podría haber sabido que serías tú, . Mis señores Bósi y Brogur te tienen en gran estima y has demostrado ser ${PLAYERNAME:un amigo[m]|una amiga[f]} de la Guarnición de Hierro. ¡También serás ${PLAYERNAME:un amigo[m]|una amiga[f]} de los Martillogrís!\
\
'¡Estos Elfos no tienen la experiencia con los Orcos que nosotros, los Martillogrís, tenemos! Oh, parecen comprender cuando relato los muchos agravios que mi familia ha sufrido a manos de Mazog y sus antecesores, pero puedo notar que piensan que exagero. ¿Exagero la herida de mi abuelo Thormar en Azanulbizar, que caminó con una cojera desde entonces? ¿O la maldición impuesta a mi padre Tandri por el propio Bolgo, que nunca más encontraría mineral valioso en las profundidades?\
\
'Solo quiero que estos Elfos reconozcan lo peligroso que es Mazog, incluso en cautiverio, y que coloquen un centinela Martillogrís dondequiera que se le mantenga. Ve y díselo a Alfirimbes. Mi familia merece este honor después de todos los daños que Mazog y sus parientes han causado a la mía.'","Lleva el informe sobre Mazog a Alfirimbes","Capítulo 2: Rumor de Mazog","Alfirimbes cree que el éxito de la misión de la Guardia Oculta depende de mantener la presencia de Mazog en secreto frente a los Orcos del Bosque Negro.","Dentro del cofre encuentras una carta dirigida a Mazog","Alfirimbes está en Echad Sirion, el campamento de la Hueste Dorada en los Lindes Oscuros, al norte de Maudhûl-ulur y Ashúrz-maufulug.\
\
Has encontrado un comunicado destinado a Mazog en el cofre de un jefe orco y deberías llevarlo ahora a Alfirimbes.","Derrota a los Orcos o trasgos Taughâsh en los Lindes Oscuros (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Aún no has encontrado ningún plan de los Orcos que mencione a Mazog?'","Buscas en el cofre, pero no encuentras nada que mencione a Mazog.","Habla con Lúth Martillogrís en Echad Sirion","Orcos Taughâsh y viles trasgos pueden encontrarse por todos los Lindes Oscuros. Cofres que pueden contener mensajes orcos pueden encontrarse dentro de los campamentos de Maudhûl-ulur y Ashúrz Maufulug, al sureste de Echad Sirion.\
\
Alfirimbes te ha pedido que busques en las fortificaciones orcas de los Lindes Oscuros para saber si los Orcos del Bosque Negro se han enterado de la presencia de Mazog.","'El destino de los Martillogrís está estrechamente ligado a la línea de Orcos de Mazog y lo ha estado durante muchos años. ¡Merecemos ser sus carceleros ahora! Ve y díselo a Alfirimbes. No seremos excluidos de este deber, de quedarnos de brazos cruzados y dejar que Mazog escape del juicio que se le avecina.'","Alfirimbes está en Echad Sirion, supervisando cautelosamente la defensa del campamento.\
\
Luth Martillogrís ha exigido que un miembro de su familia sea asignado como centinela para vigilar al líder orco cautivo.","'Creo que el éxito de la misión de la Guardia Oculta depende del secreto. Debemos asegurarnos de que los Orcos del Bosque Negro no se enteren de la presencia de Mazog bajo los aleros, o seguramente lanzarán un ataque contra nosotros en un número que no podremos repeler.\
\
'Al sureste hay dos fuertes desde los cuales los Orcos del Bosque Negro vigilan esta parte del bosque. Busca en cualquier cofre que encuentres en Maudhûl-ulur y Ashúrz Maufulug mensajes de los Orcos y derrota a cualquier Taughâsh que encuentres en los Lindes Oscuros mientras lo haces.\
\
'Si puedes regresar a mí con cualquier plan o mensaje que mencione a Mazog, podremos determinar cómo proceder. Si saben que lo hemos sacado de Moria, es posible que necesitemos actuar rápidamente para sobrevivir.'","'Luth Martillogrís deambula por el campamento de Echad Sirion, mostrando sus sentimientos sobre esta empresa. Habla con él y mantenlo tranquilo, ${PLAYER}. Podría hacernos daño sin darse cuenta si persiste en su inquietud.'","Luth Martillogrís está mostrando sus malos sentimientos mientras deambula por Echad Sirion.\
\
Alfirimbes quiere que tranquilices a Luth Martillogrís diciéndole que se están tomando las medidas necesarias para garantizar que la misión de la Guardia Oculta se lleve a cabo de manera segura y que la cautividad de Mazog no esté amenazada.","Habla con Alfirimbes en Echad Sirion","'Los Taughâsh tienen un firme control sobre esta zona, ${PLAYER}, lanzando incursiones desde sus campamentos hacia el sureste. Derrota a estos Orcos y a sus primos trasgos dondequiera que los veas y busca en Maudhûl-ulur y Ashúrz Maufulug cofres que contengan información sobre Mazog.\
\
'Si encuentras alguna comunicación de la que podamos aprender si saben que hemos capturado a Mazog, tráemela para que podamos prepararnos.'"},
[3066]={"La Cámara del Conocimiento, la Cámara de la Sabiduría y la Cámara de la Reflexión Profunda se pueden encontrar en algún lugar dentro de la Gran Excavación de Moria.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que busques en tres antiguos almacenes de la Gran Excavación páginas, tabletas o tomos que le permitan aprender más sobre los Días Antiguos.","Encuentra y busca en la Cámara del Conocimiento","Encuentras una tableta rota dentro del cofre fuerte; su inscripción aún se puede discernir","'No me has traído lo que necesito.'","Lleva los registros históricos a Bósi","'¡Grandes secretos yacen en estas cavernas. Los desenterramos!'","'¿Quién sabe cuánta sabiduría se perdió en Moria, hace mucho tiempo?'","Encuentras algunas páginas marchitas dentro del cofre fuerte; la escritura aún es legible","'Los gredbyg representaban un peligro terrible, y a pesar de tus esfuerzos, sin duda volverán con el tiempo, pero no podemos pasar demasiado tiempo lidiando con esta amenaza menor. Erradicarlos por completo implicaría recursos más allá de lo que puedo proporcionar. Debemos centrarnos ahora en otros asuntos, y defendernos de los gredbyg que regresen donde sea necesario.\
\
'Lo que realmente deseo por encima de todo es la oportunidad de echar un vistazo a los registros e historias de los Días Antiguos. ¿Quién sabe qué secretos se esconden bajo el polvo: páginas, tabletas y tomos que se pueden encontrar en las cavernas de Moria?\
\
'Debería haber almacenes ubicados dentro de la Gran Excavación de Moria, y así se llaman: la Cámara del Conocimiento, la Cámara de la Sabiduría y la Cámara de la Reflexión Profunda. Encuentra estos almacenes dentro de la Gran Excavación y búsquelos todos para encontrar registros de los Días Antiguos. Regresa a mí cuando hayas encontrado algo de cada área.'","Encuentras un tomo desgastado dentro del cofre fuerte; parte de su texto aún se puede descifrar","Encuentra y busca en la Cámara de la Sabiduría","'¡Excelente, ${PLAYER}! Estos registros e historias son muy antiguos y probablemente albergan muchos secretos antiguos. ¡Seguro que serán tremendamente valiosos!'\
\
Bósi examina cada uno de los registros por turno, y su rostro se descompone un poco mientras los lee.\
\
'Registros de bienes comprados y vendidos, inventarios de hierro y otros metales... esto es de algún interés, sin duda, pero....'\
\
Bósi se queda pensativo, y luego se ilumina.\
\
'Espera un momento, ${PLAYER}. Podrías tener algo aquí después de todo.'","Capítulo 2: Almacenes de las Galerías Occidentales","Bósi te ha pedido que busques tres almacenes dentro de la Gran Excavación de Moria e intentes recuperar cualquier registro o historia que haya sobrevivido.","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación de Moria.\
\
Has reunido antiguos registros de Moria de tres almacenes en la Gran Excavación y deberías llevárselos a Bósi.","Encuentra y busca en la Cámara de la Reflexión Profunda","'Los tres almacenes de los que hablo se llaman la Cámara del Conocimiento, la Cámara de la Sabiduría y la Cámara de la Reflexión Profunda. Búscalos en algún lugar de la Gran Excavación de Moria y tráeme registros o historias de cada uno.'"},
[3067]={"Chapter 2: The Assault on Azanulbizar","Talk to the Iron-folk messenger at Ashmargathâl","'As we heard at the council last night, King Thráin has ordered the Seven Houses to aid upon the fringes of the dale.\
\
'Among them, the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, and Temámir have travelled to Zirakazhâr on the slopes of Zirakzigil. Once it is reclaimed from the Orcs, I fear they shall have to contend with the trolls we spied from afar.\
\
'As for the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu... they have a harder path to take. If they can break through the Orkish outpost blocking the way to Tharkh Shathur, they intend to claim Ashmargathâl and set siege to Atrad-zarakh, the old warding-spire of Khazad-dûm.\
\
'It is far too much, indeed, to ask of any one of the Seven Houses, but together, we will triumph! By Durin's beard, Azog will not live to see the morrow!'","'Lord Náin suspected you would be here, Hermáth. I am certain our cousins from the East have been grateful for your aid, but I come with orders from King Thráin himself!\
\
'King Thráin and his vanguard make ready to set out, and we of the Iron-folk have been commanded to rally to Khur Azan.\
\
'There is no time to waste! Follow me!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You will swiftly travel to Khur Azan when you advance this quest.</rgb>","Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Khur Azan","Dwarves of the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, and Temámir can be found at Zirakazhâr on the slopes of Zirakzigil to the north-west of Amdân. Dwarves of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu can be found at Ashmargathâl, far to the north of Amdân on the slopes of Bundushâthur.\
\
Dáin has asked you to aid the other Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ. You should aid the dwarves in Amdân, as well as those who have battled to Zirakazhâr and Ashmargathâl.","Aid the Dwarves of the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, and Temámir at Zirakazhâr","As you continue to read Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar, you begin the second chapter in which the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ of Thráin wake to a dark winter's day and the battle is joined.","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Khur Azan, the Dim-crossing.\
\
After learning of how Hermáth Stormhammer aided the dwarves who battled upon the slopes of Zirakzigil and Bundushâthur, Hermáth Stormhammer interjects and calls your attention to events at Khur Azan, the Dim-crossing.","An Iron-folk messenger can be found at Zirakazhâr or Ashmargathâl.\
\
After aiding the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ, a messenger of the Iron-folk has arrived bearing urgent news for you.","Talk to the Iron-folk messenger at Zirakazhâr","Aid the Dwarves of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu at Ashmargathâl","'Lord Náin suspected you would be here, Hermáth. I am certain our cousins from the Blue Mountains and those of the East have been grateful for your aid, but I come with orders from King Thráin himself!\
\
'King Thráin and his vanguard make ready to set out, and we of the Iron-folk have been commanded to rally to Khur Azan.\
\
'There is no time to waste! Follow me!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You will swiftly travel to Khur Azan when you advance this quest.</rgb>","'As the battle continued on the slopes of Zirakzigil and Bundushâthur, I was recalled to Khur Azan. It seemed that Dáin's ruse had not gone as unnoticed as he thought, but more pressing matters were at hand.\
\
'Indeed, the Iron-folk had marched forth from Amdân at last—not yet to join the battle, but to stand closer in reserve after King Thráin's vanguard burst through the Orkish encampment of Kamaz-kala, the furthest border of Azog's would-be realm.'"},
[3068]={"'When will this standard fly, I wonder? And what will that day signify for the Dúnedain?'","Chapter 2: The Grey Company in Rivendell","'This may be a perilous road, especially once we reach the plains of Enedwaith. Many of the Dunlending tribes will be hostile to us.'","'Are the words of my father correct? Is the time coming when we must no longer defend against the Enemy's moves, but strike against him with all the strength we can muster?'","'The road south will be long. We must ride swiftly and be wary of its dangers.'","The Grey Company prepares to depart from Rivendell for the wide southern lands and needs your help to make sure that all is ready.","'My horse Legimbod is rested from the ride out of Angmar, and he is ready to undertake the next leg of the journey. His saddlebags are as light as I could make them, while still keeping the supplies we will need.'\
\
Golodir takes a small pendant from one of his pockets and idly passes it from one hand to the other as he looks about the yard.\
\
'This refuge has not changed in the many years since I last came here, but surely I, myself, must be unrecognizable. So much has happened, and so little of it good. But the ride here was a marvel, and I could feel the weight of the past falling from my shoulders with the feel of the breeze upon my face. Legimbod delighted in the speed, and I delighted with him! The southward journey will do both of us some good. I am ready to be off again.'","Habla con Elrohir","Habla con Golodir","'It is almost time to go, ${PLAYER}. Our road leads south.'","'Glorengúr did not break a sweat in the short ride from Thorenhad here to Rivendell. He was ready to begin even yesterday.\
\
'I could say the same for myself. I returned to Thorenhad to say good-bye to Elweleth, but I could not find her anywhere at the camp. I had meant to return this hairpin she had given me, but perhaps she feared the farewells. I suppose I did as well.\
\
'We will soon set forth. I do not know what the future will bring, but I will do my duty with no complaint, and Glorengúr will do the same.'","Candaith is outside the gate by the stables in Rivendell.\
\
You have spoken with several of the Rangers of the Grey Company in Rivendell and should now speak with Candaith.","'All is nearly ready, ${PLAYER}. While I finish the final preparations for our departure, I ask that you speak with some of those who will accompany us south. Ensure that they are prepared for the road and rested enough for the first leg of our journey.\
\
'I saw Golodir just to the north-east some minutes ago, speaking with Elrohir. Radanir was just to the east of the two of them, beneath the foot-bridge.\
\
'Lothrandir is just across the way, speaking to his horse Mithúl. He knows a great deal about the lands through which we must pass. Ask him if he has any further information about the road which may help us move with haste. Once you have spoken with those four, find Candaith by the stables gate and speak to him about what lies ahead.'","Golodir, Lothrandir, Radanir, and Elrohir are preparing to depart in and around the stables of Rivendell.\
\
Halbarad has asked you to check with several members of the Grey Company about their final preparations.","Talk to Candaith in Rivendell, outside the gate by the stables","'Mithúl is ready for the next leg of the journey, ${PLAYER}. Indeed, his kind may be more prepared for what awaits us than the others of this Company! After all, Mithúl's eyes will be to the road underfoot, watching for loose stones and wind-blown branches; the eyes of the Dúnedain must be to the horizon, keeping watch for foes that may seek to slow our errand.\
\
'I have spoken with Halbarad and the sons of Elrond about the road we will take: south through the Trollshaws and into Eregion, there to rest at Echad Eregion before passing south into Enedwaith.\
\
'A number of Dunlending tribes called the area home when last I journeyed those lands. Some were friendly to outsiders, but most were not. The Draig-lûth, the Hebog-lûth... they are those you would be wise not to cross, and I will do my best to ensure the Grey Company does not entangle with them.'","'It will be many days before we come to Aragorn. May we be not late!'","Talk to Lothrandir","Talk to Radanir","'Everyone is nearly ready to ride: the Dúnedain, the sons of Elrond, and ${PLAYER}, loyal ${RACE}.\
\
'Are you familiar with our history, ${PLAYER}? As you are joining us on this journey, surely to go down in the annals of the Dúnedain, I would have you hear some of it, if you have not all ready.\
\
'We have some moments. Let me tell you some of our history, that you may understand the weight of that which we are about to do.'","Aragorn's standard will remain furled until the time is right","'My father had some curious words for me on the eve of this, our departure for the southern lands, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Elrohir gazes down the hill, deep in thought.\
\
'He said that the time is approaching when we can no longer hold back, when we must do more than defend against the actions of the Enemy. He said that the time is coming when we may need to wager everything on a final throw, and by so doing we will have done all that we can. Better a death in far off lands in the service of a chance, however small, than death at home a certainty.\
\
'We may not return from this journey, ${PLAYER}. My brother and I are at peace with that. I hope that you and these Dúnedain are as well, for I would counsel any who are not to stay behind.'","'Legimbod is ready, and so am I. Together we will uphold our duty to Aragorn, our chief.'"},
[3070]={"Some Elves sing as they work, their voices sweet and strange and also, somehow, sad","Gather parcels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Found books (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring parcels to Tordúril","Helped packing Elves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gathered parcels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You wish to help, ${CLASS}? Such good will among the free peoples!\
\
'I have sent down several requisitions to the market and someone is needed to carry those things down to the forges for packing in crates and barrels. You will have to ask around among the merchants and artisans. I am afraid some other goods have been left lying about. Everyone is so busy.'","'Many hours have I laboured over these fine and resplendent raiments. See that they are handled gently and packed well. I am to travel with Lord Elrond and Lady Arwen and will see them on the other side, so I will know!'","You should visit Elrond Half-elven. He stands in the library of his house in Rivendell.","Carry the goods down to the Rivendell Forges","'Ah, those are all the parcels. Good, now lay them down there. Let me tally them.\
\
'Yes... that is well... indeed, they are all accounted for. \
\
'Excellent. Now you may pick up the pile and carry them to the forges to be boxed for transport.'","Chapter 2: The Time Before Travelling","You should bring the parcels you gathered to Tordúril in the Rivendell Market.","Find Arwen in Imlad Gelair","You should help Elves packing throughout Elrond's house in Rivendell.","Elrond stands in his customary spot, brow furrowed, directing Elves in all manner of packing, provisioning, and planning","'These are table-knives and wood-axes for the travelling party. What, did you think all I ever made were swords for adventurers?'","'I little thought to see you here, so soon, ${PLAYER}. It gladdens my heart, for you can only have come bearing happy tidings!'\
\
The Elf with whom he was speaking looks meaningfully and a shadow crosses Elrond's brow.\
\
'I fear there are several matters to which I must attend, and they cannot wait. Forgive this discourtesy, ${PLAYER}. If you will return shortly I would speak more with you.\
\
'Why do you not pay a visit to Bilbo the Halfling? He would be as glad to see your face as I. He will be in the Hall of Fire as he always is.'","Find the books Arwen named (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We are indebted to you, ${PLAYER}. If you are not done being helpful, you might look for Pethelen just outside the house. I believe he is charged with tasks of provisioning.'","Elrond has suggested you visit Bilbo, who can be found in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House in Rivendell.","Talk to Hammadelen","Talk to Galdor","'${PLAYER}, it is you after all. I thought I must have heard wrong, when word came that you were in Rivendell.\
\
'Oh, I could ask you a thousand questions - but no, I shall forbear. I know that our greatest fears are averted, and that is enough. I shall look forward to hearing the tale told in full at the journey's end.\
\
'You know the purpose of this pilgrimage, do you not? We make for Gondor, where in time Aragorn - I mean Elessar - and I shall be wed, as we were trothed to be long ago.\
\
'Do you see, Eliaril? I have not forgotten or neglected the wedding that lies at the end of our travels. Perhaps you can persuade her it is not a thing to waste worry or care upon, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Pethelen outside Elrond's House","Parcels delivered","Lindir can be found in the Hall of Fire in Elrond's house in Rivendell.\
\
You should ask Lindir how you can help with the preparations.","Lady Arwen has asked that you visit her in Imlad Gelair, below the falls in Rivendell.","You should go to Rivendell's Market and gather provisions and goods requisitioned for the journey. You will need to ask among the merchants and artisans and also look for some requisitions left lying around.","Arwen and Eliaril stand in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell.\
\
Hear Arwen's response to Eliaril.","Talk to Eliaril","Received parcels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Arwen and Eliaril stand in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell.\
\
You should talk to Eliaril, Arwen's maid-in-waiting, and see if you can calm her down.","Habla con Elrond","Return to Pethelen","'I was handed these parcels of goods to be barreled for the journey without so much as a word of where to take them. Here, they are yours!'","You find Arwen flanked by maids-in-waiting","Talk to Arwen","Judging on the piles and number of busy hands, no few Elves are going on this journey","Received a parcel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Here, these are all the ropes and weavings that were asked of me. May they grant a swift and easy journey.'","'Here you have all the blankets and feed required for the trip. Steady now, it is a heavy load!'","You should bring the pile of parcels next to Tordúril from the Market down to the Rivendell Forges.","'While we here plan and wait and you brave the dim ruins of the Enemy's land, Elrond, his daughter Arwen, and much of their house prepare for a journey. Can you guess to where?\
\
'Few travel fleet as you do, friend. Will you speed to Rivendell and see how things are going? If they were braced in battle, just as we were, they may need help. Elrond, also, may have wise words of guidance in the search for Glorfindel. Whichever the case, Lord Elrond will surely be hungry for news of happenings in Gondor and beyond. Especially from you, who have seen so much of it with your own eyes!'","Arwen laughs lightly, a tinkling of bells. \
\
'Perhaps I am negligent, Eliaril, but I must thank you for reminding me of the seeds. Here, ${PLAYER}. Take these, seeds of the Celebég Blossom. They are a gift from Rivendell to the king-to-be. For that shall come before he is my groom-to-be.\
\
'I would ask you to do another thing for me, ${PLAYER}. There are several books upon my father's shelves that I would not have left behind. Some pertain to matters of present import, others give guidance for the challenges my Elfstone shall face as king. Will you see that they come into my father's hands?'\
\
'Farewell, ${PLAYER}. I will see you in Gondor, if not sooner, I hope.'","You should return to Pethelen, before Elrond's house in Rivendell, now that you have gathered the parcels as he asked.","'There is our fleet-foot traveller! I have set aside some time for you. Come, tell me of events in the East.'\
\
You tell Elrond of all that you witnessed in Gondor, from the Paths of the Dead, through Pelargir, the Pelennor, and on to the Black Gates themselves; of the fall of Théoden, the Last Debate, and what bits you know of Sam and Frodo's own journeys. You speak some of what you have seen within the broken land of Mordor. Finally, you relate the news of the Battle Under the Trees, and how Lothlórien awaits the arrival of Glorfindel.\
\
Elrond is silent while he listens, and when you finish, he nods.\
\
'Much of this I guessed at, but not the whole of it, nay, not even the half. That Glorfindel gave his word to come to Lothlórien and is not there troubles me. I do not fear the worst, and yet - I feel, somehow, that your path is intertwined with his, and that the two of you have a role to play in these events that shall soon unfold.\
\
'Give to me these books that Arwen bade you gather. She is right to call me back to serious matters, even in this happy hour. In exchange, take these seeds. They are a gift for the king-to-be in Gondor, which shall come some while before he is Arwen's groom-to-be.\
\
'Now farewell, ${PLAYER}. Until we meet again.'","'You gathered all the parcels and then delivered them at the Forges?'\
\
Pethelen laughs.\
\
'You have done as much as any here to prepare for this journey, I think. No more labours for you, friend! While you were in the market, Lady Arwen heard of your arrival and begged to see you. She is within Imlad Gelair.\
\
'Do not worry if you have never been there. You shall be admitted on her word now.'","'Do you wish me to escort you to Lady Arwen? She awaits you, I know. Very good, I will take you now.'","You should talk to Elrond Half-elven. He stands in the library of his house in Rivendell.","Talk to Anornaneth","Visit Bilbo Baggins","'It is fine and well for the bride-to-be to sit and dream of the future. But how shall the dress be all fitted and altered in time, before we set off? Or if it is not, how shall it be carried in pieces? And what flowers have they in far-off Gondor? Are lilies to be stitched onto the hems of the gown when blue-bells and who knows what strange blossoms will garland the path?\
\
'Much wisdom and lore is there in Rivendell, but how the Men of Gondor mark their nuptials is not among it, written or spoken. \
\
'There is nothing to be done but bring everything and make do when we are there! Meanwhile, her Ladyship worries more about books and seeds!'","Talk to Dúrvenel","Help packing Elves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have helped a number of packing Elves and should return to Lindir in Elrond's house.","'All this going about and fussing and bothering! I tell Lindir here it is most un-Elvish of them, but he only asks me if I would leave home without MY pipe and handkerchief. Hmph!\
\
'Well I'm not going, even though I shall miss seeing the old Dúnadan in all his crown and glory. Frodo and his friends I will see again, for they shall pass this way. Elrond assures me of it. \
\
'Ah, but all this talking has made me tired, ${PLAYER}. I am glad I have got to see YOU! But now I think I must return to being quiet, and staring into the fire, and working out the words to this new song. \
\
'Why don't you ask Lindir here if you can help out. Nearly everyone but me is pitching in!'","Lindir suggested you look for Pethelen outside Elrond's house in Rivendell, to help with more preparations for the journey.","Lindir laughs.\
\
'It is true, you cannot plead infirmity and age as Master Bilbo here does! We will indeed not turn away help that is offered, for we wish to set out on our journey with some happy haste. Anywhere within these walls you see packing, you are welcome to lend a hand!'","Return to Lindir","Talk to Ladrochan, the Stable-master","You should check in on Elrond in his library in Rivendell to see if he is ready to talk to you.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}! We stand here peering into the dim ruins of the Enemy's land, while leagues behind us our father Elrond, our sister, and many others of our house prepare for a journey. Can you guess to where? \
\
'Few travel fleet as you do, friend. Will you speed to Rivendell and see how things are going? A fear troubles me that my home was braced in battle, just as Lórien was. And another thought comes to me too: that my father Elrond may have wise words of guidance in the search for Glorfindel. Nor do I doubt that he will be hungry for news of happenings here, as well. Especially from one who has seen so much of it!'","Habla con Lindir","Pay a visit to Rivendell. Learn what has happened there, what Elrond knows of Glorfindel, and why the house prepares for travel.","Even from outside, the Last Homely House is astir with a new kind of bustling life","Arwen has asked you to find several books in Elrond's library in Rivendell.","Visit Elrond in Rivendell"},
[3071]={"'Mucho de lo que dijo Mazog en las profundidades de Rushdurinul podría haber sido pura fanfarronería, las amenazas y jactancias de un animal enjaulado. Pero una cosa que dijo me preocupa más que cualquier otra: la revelación de que la recompensa que busca es el dominio de otro reino. Durante mucho tiempo los orcos y los enanos han luchado en las cavernas bajo las Montañas Nubladas, y la línea de Mazog ha estado al frente de ese conflicto.\
\
'Si Mazog, descendiente de Azog a través de su hijo Bolgo, ha decidido abandonar el dominio de Moria, solo puede ser porque siente que Moria ya no será apta para gobernar. ¿Qué gran mal debe haber puesto en marcha su aliado Gorothúl en las profundidades para devastar tanto ese vasto reino y hacerlo inadecuado incluso para el dominio de los orcos?\
\
'Regresa a Gwathrendath en las Fundaciones de Piedra y habla con Lenglammel y Forglinn allí. Han pasado mucho tiempo en las profundidades y pueden saber algo sobre lo que podríamos estar enfrentando.'","'Tus palabras confirman lo que he estado escuchando de Lenglammel y Magor, ${PLAYER}: Gorothúl puso algo en marcha antes de partir hacia Dol Guldur con los enanos cautivos y el hacha de mithril de la Guarnición de Hierro.\
\
'¿Acaso hizo algún mal para permitir que los sirvientes de la Sombra y la Llama recuperaran su fuerza y regresaran a lugares que antes se creían libres de su peligro?'","'¿Vas a hablar con Bróin sobre este nuevo peligro? Me alegra; debe ocuparse de la posibilidad de que no todo esté bien en Moria antes de partir a rescatar a su primo Bori.\
\
'Bróin se encuentra en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada a lo largo del Camino de Durin.'","Issuriel se preocupa de que las palabras de Mazog puedan revelar una amenaza oculta para los Elfos de Lothlórien y los Enanos de Moria.","Lenglammel y Forglinn se encuentran en Gwathrendath, el puesto avanzado de los Elfos en las profundidades de las Fundaciones de Piedra, en Moria.\
\
Issuriel cree que Gorothúl puede haber puesto en marcha algún mal que podría devastar Moria de tal manera que incluso Mazog esté buscando otro reino para gobernar.","Habla con Lenglammel en Gwathrendath","Habla con Forglinn en Gwathrendath","Capítulo 2: Lo que dejó Gorothúl","Habla con Bróin en la Senda Pacífica","Bróin se encuentra en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada junto al Camino de Durin.\
\
Los Elfos de Gwathrendath están de acuerdo con la evaluación de Issuriel de que Gorothúl puso en marcha algún mal antes de partir hacia Dol Guldur. Bróin debe ser notificado de esto, ya que concierne a la Guarnición de Hierro y puede afectar sus planes para el rescate de Bori.","'Es bueno verte de nuevo, ${PLAYER}, porque comparto las preocupaciones de Issuriel: el interés de Gorothúl por Moria esconde algo que aún no hemos descubierto.\
\
'Grandes terrores habitan en los lugares profundos, esto lo sabemos, porque has enfrentado a varios de ellos: bestias sin nombre que temen la luz del sol, pero también los sirvientes del gran espíritu que reinó en Moria y terminó con el reino de los enanos. El Balrog de Moria ahora está derrotado, pero a costa de la vida de Mithrandir y la vasta extensión de su poder.\
\
'Pero los sirvientes de la Sombra y la Llama fueron derrotados no por el poder de Mithrandir, sino por tu coraje y el de tus aliados. No te ofendas por esto, ${PLAYER}, pero tus habilidades ni siquiera se acercan a las del Mago. Temo que tu derrota a los sirvientes del Daño de Durin no tenga la permanencia que tuvo la derrota de su maestro.'","'Había esperado verte de nuevo en las orillas del Anduin, ${PLAYER}, bien encaminados a intercambiar al rey de los Orcos por la libertad de mi primo Bori, pero aún no era el momento. Los Elfos de Gwathrendath tienen razón: Gorothúl parece haber puesto algún plan en marcha aquí en Khazad-dûm.\
\
'Después de que regresaste a Lothlórien para hablar con Celeborn, Orvar volvió a las profundidades de Buzun-ghâr. Dijo que tenía una \\qsensación\\q, alguna idea de que las cosas no estaban del todo bien. La putrefacción marchita ya estaba comenzando a retirarse, pero todavía sentía alguna presencia vil, y debajo del saliente donde derrotaste hábilmente a Grawulun el Caerog, Orvar descubrió una terrible reliquia cubierta de runas indescriptibles. Sintió que llamaba, llamaba hacia las profundidades, y la golpeó con su hacha hasta que fue destruida.\
\
'Creo que Gorothúl dejó esta reliquia en Buzun-ghâr para atraer a Grawulun el Caerog hacia ella, ${PLAYER}. Grawulun no encontró ese lugar por accidente, amigo ${CLASS}. Fue atraído allí.'","'Bróin sigue en la Senda Pacífica, el lugar de descanso establecido por la Guarnición de Hierro en el Camino de Durin. Deberías hablar con él sobre este nuevo peligro que sospechamos que está creciendo, ya que afectará su planificado rescate de Bori.'","'El puesto avanzado de los Elfos en las profundidades de las Fundaciones de Piedra de Moria puede contener algunas respuestas sobre el peligro que temo que Gorothúl haya levantado. Habla con Lenglammel y Forglinn allí y escucha lo que han aprendido.'"},
[3074]={"Caebar is in the central yard of Lond Cirion. He seems worried about something.","'Lady Marra's scouts patrol the lands hereabout in search of Corsair raiding parties, and I have offered to them the assistance of my travelling companions, many of whom are deadly with weapons of every sort. I count you in this number, ${PLAYER}, and would greatly appreciate your aiding the scouts as they seek such foes as trouble Anfalas.\
\
'The scouts have gone in three directions: to the north, the east, and to the south.'","'You are here to help oppose the enemies of Anfalas? I am pleased to hear it, for I surprised a number of Corsairs creeping about those rocks, and I believe they will soon return!'","'Corsairs sometimes try to approach Lond Cirion from this beach, so we must remain always vigilant.'","Talk to Caebar in the central yard of Lond Cirion","Return to Lond Cirion to report of your successes","Borion thanks you for the help","King Elessar has offered the help of his companions in the defence of Anfalas, and that includes any assistance you can provide to Lady Marra's scouts.","Galleth thanks you for the help","Talk to Borion north of Lond Cirion","Talk to Galleth on the beach south of Lond Cirion","Gilvenel thanks you for the help","Chapter 3.10: Enemies of Anfalas","Now that you have aided the scouts, you should return to Lond Cirion.","Caebar calls you over to him. He seems worried","Talk to Gilvenel on the hill east of Lond Cirion","'Lady Marra's scouts patrol the lands hereabout in search of Corsair raiding parties, and I have offered to them the assistance of my travelling companions, many of whom are deadly with weapons of every sort. I count you in this number, ${PLAYER}, and would greatly appreciate your aiding the scouts as they seek such foes as trouble Anfalas.\
\
'The scouts have gone in three directions: to the north, east, and south.'","'Oh, I am glad you have returned, ${PLAYER}. King Elessar asked for me to attend to some business about an hour from now, and I am consumed with worry about what it might be. I am trying not to be nervous, but it is... well, it is difficult.'","Lady Marra's scouts can be found outside Lond Cirion to the north, east, and south.","'Corsair scouts have been spotted inland, and we must always remain on our guard.'"},
[3075]={"Talk to Caebar in the central yard of Lond Cirion and accompany him to the King","'Why did you break the seal upon your husband's last wishes, Marra?'","'Will you accompany me, my friend? The King did not prohibit it, so far as I know, and I cannot imagine he would not allow you to be present at... whatever this duty turns out to be!\
\
'I would just feel better if you were there, ${PLAYER}. Tell me you will come with me.'","King Elessar is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.","'I have to ask you something, Marra, and I do not wish to give you offence or cause you any further upset... but I feel that I must ask it.'\
\
Elessar fixes his gaze upon the Lady of Anfalas. When next he speaks, his voice is gentle, but his eyes are stern.\
\
'Why did you break the seal upon your husband's last wishes, Marra? The parchment was not found only today, as you suggested. The paper was in your possession ever since Golasgil departed, and you knew its contents before now.'","Talk to King Elessar in the main hall of Lond Cirion","Chapter 3.11: Last Wishes of the Lord of Langstrand","Talk to Marra in the main hall of Lond Cirion","'I am grateful for your discretion earlier, my King, for Coruchon would seek any advantage he could from this, and Golasgil would never forgive me should a widow's weakness endanger Orgolas's claim!\
\
'But I broke the seal and read my husband's last wishes out of fear that he would do as he has indeed done: granted to his son and mine that cursed ship, Wave-hunter! How often did he speak of his intention for Orgolas to follow in his own steps, and become a great mariner like his father? Too often, and every time it cut me deeply! The Wave-hunter was harboured upstream in Pinnath Gelin during the war, to protect it from the Corsairs, and I have refused to summon it back here to keep Orgolas as far from its threatening decks as I can!\
\
'When I saw such a bequest had been made, I did not know what to do. But I cannot disobey the command of the King of Gondor. Hindering Golasgil's wishes was bad enough, but I fear for my son's safety! He is so young, my King. You must understand.'","King Elessar has called upon Caebar to provide a service for Lond Cirion, and the scribe is worried about it.","'Thank you, my friend! I will not forget this!\
\
'Let us meet with King Elessar at the appointed hour, and until that time comes I will try not to worry overmuch.'","'I am sorry, but it was very hard to hear these things. My husband was a man of great bravery and courage, and a generous heart, but to think of him writing these things, alone, without first taking my advice...\
\
'I will shed no more tears. I wish this letter had not been read here today.'\
\
Marra falls silent, her face a mask.","Marra stares forward and says nothing.","Lady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.","Caebar is in the central yard of Lond Cirion, where he has confided in you that he is worried about the service King Elessar has asked him to provide."},
[3076]={"'This is my suggestion: let your son come with our travelling party as we journey to Pinnath Gelin. It is my belief that Orgolas will see this land with new eyes, and he will grow into the responsibility he must one day have.'","Talk to Orgolas outside the keep of Lond Cirion","Daeram is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.","'I understand this request you have of my husband, Marra, but I fear you may do more harm with the asking of this boon than you will prevent. Your son will not be kept from leaving your home if that is the purpose of his heart. Though the command be in the King's voice, Orgolas will know who wrote the words, and that knowledge can only breed resentment.\
\
'You say Golasgil was a fine mariner, and I do not doubt he was! But what I have learned of your husband from my own is that he cared deeply for the people of Anfalas, and did not sail from them, or from you, without great need. Perhaps if Orgolas understood the cares and concerns of the folk he will rule when he comes of age, he will make the same choice, and the Wave-hunter will remain at its dock.\
\
'This, then, is my suggestion: let your son come with our travelling party as we journey to Pinnath Gelin. It is my belief that Orgolas will see this land with new eyes, and he will grow into the responsibility he must one day have.'","'I gave you my thanks for not speaking what you suspected in front of Coruchon, King Elessar, but you will have my thanks a hundredfold if you do this now: I entreat you to forbid Orgolas from leaving Lond Cirion, no matter what his father has gifted to him. Already it is nearly impossible to keep him from sneaking beyond the walls, but perhaps a command from the King of Gondor would stay his steps?'","Talk to Marra in the main hall of Lond Cirion","Orgolas is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.","Talk to Daeram outside the keep of Lond Cirion","'I am surprised to learn that Lady Marra has agreed to allow Orgolas to depart with the King and Queen, but Pinnath Gelin is not far from here. I will do what I can to keep the boy safe among the green hills. Perhaps he will be less likely to slip my watch if he feels that he is on an adventure, and need not go in search of another one himself!'","'I do not know.'\
\
Marra looks from the Queen to the King, and back again.\
\
'What if this journey gives life to embers that might otherwise have been cooled? I do not see how such an adventure could prevent that which I fear for my son.\
\
'But if you permit Daeram to also join your travelling party, that he may attend my son and keep him safe, I suppose I cannot refuse.'","Lady Marra has entreated the King to forbid her son from leaving Lond Cirion.","Lady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.","Chapter 3.12: Grief and Duty","'If you permit Daeram to also join your travelling party, that he may attend my son and keep him safe, I suppose I cannot refuse.'","Talk to Queen Arwen in the main hall of Lond Cirion","Queen Arwen has something she wishes to say to Lady Marra.","'Is it true? I am to depart with the King's party for Pinnath Gelin? That is wonderful news! That is where the Wave-hunter is currently docked, ${PLAYER}! Are we going to see the ship that my father left to me?'"},
[3077]={"The bear cub snorts in your direction, but you cannot guess at its meaning. Is this Vídar? You hope so, both for your sake and his!","Glóin has made his decision: he must send message-ravens to Skarháld and to the Lonely Mountain bearing word of this new Lord of Gundabad.","The dwarves have gathered behind Runerik and Yrsa's lodge to release the messenger-ravens.","'Do they fly very high? How do they know where to go? What's the farthest they've ever flown before?'\
\
Vídar pauses for air, and you manage to interject a question. The child considers it briefly.\
\
'Have I any chores that need doing? Well, yes, I suppose. I am nearly a man grown, after all, and Mother says it is my job to scout outside Limlók once a week. I will go do that now, if you will let her know! You have already met her, yes? Her name is Yrsa.\
\
'All right, I am leaving now. But I want to learn more about the ravens when I get back!'","Talk to Vídar","'I do not understand why your friend is so concerned about the one called \\qGorgar the Ruthless.\\q One Orc is much the same as any other, in my experience and that of my kind.\
\
'But I can spare some parchment for him to write the frightened warnings he wants to send back home. There is a box of paper near the task board, and my people use its contents to post requests and other messages on the board. You can give him some parchment from that box, if you must.'","Watch the departure of the messenger-ravens","The messenger-ravens will bear word of the new Lord of Gundabad to Durin at Skarháld and to King Thorin in the Lonely Mountain.","Runerik Knotbeard is outside his lodge in the village of Limlók.","Glóin grunts without commitment","Chapter 3.1: A Matter of Survival","Find Glóin and his ravens in the centre of Limlók","Talk to Imák behind Runerik's lodge","The bear cub hurries away in triumph!","The dwarves have gathered to watch Glóin release the ravens","The box of scrolls is near the task board in Limlók.","'Find Vídar on his patrol and ensure he does not run into harm. There are three places he enjoys to scout, to the south-east, south, and south-west of the village. Look for him at one of these locations and safe-guard Vídar, and I will remember your good-hearted assistance.'","Yrsa Spearwife is in south-east Limlók.\
\
According to her son Vídar, Yrsa has tasked him with scouting outside the village once a week.","'I am troubled by this news that Gorgar, brother of Mazog, now rules in Gundabad, but do not mistake me! I do not fear him. The line from which he springs has long troubled Durin's Folk, but have we not laughed last in every case? We are not unprepared to deal with Gorgar, now that we know we must.\
\
'We must send messages to Durin in Skarháld and to King Thorin at the Lonely Mountain, warning them of Gundabad's new leader. It is for this very purpose I brought messenger-ravens with me on this journey, ${PLAYER}, though I did not guess at the content of the messages they needs must bear!\
\
'Will you ask Runerik for some parchment upon which I can write these messages of warning? I brought the birds, it is true, but I seem to have left my papers behind.'","Yrsa Spearwife is in south-east Limlók.","Bring the small parchments to Glóin in Limlók","Yrsa told you to scout the wild lands south of Limlók with her son Vídar. You will find the Beorning boy at one of three different spots: to the south-east, south, or south-west of the village.","Take some small parchments from the box of scrolls","Talk to Yrsa Spearwife in Limlók","Imák is behind Runerik's lodge to watch the release of the messenger-ravens.","'I need to think, and these constant questions are not helping!'","Glóin is in the centre of the village, preparing his ravens to carry messages to Skarháld and the Lonely Mountain.","'Vídar returned and spoke of your prowess! Thank you for keeping an eye on him, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
You are relieved to learn that the bear cub was Yrsa's son Vídar after all. On the journey back to Limlók you had not been entirely certain.\
\
'Your friends have gathered behind the lodge to release the messenger-ravens. You should join them.'","'The ravens have been sent? Fine, fine.'\
\
Runerik's brows crease with a new thought.\
\
'I should have read the messages before your dwarf friend released the ravens. He has not called an entire company of dwarves here, has he?'","You remove suitable papers from the box, leaving some for the folk of Limlók","Find the dwarves behind Runerik and Yrsa's lodge","Glóin is focused on preparing the ravens. He has not noticed you.","'Ah, these will do nicely, thank you. I need to decide how to phrase this message, and then copy it onto each of these papers. I need to...'\
\
Glóin looks up with barely-disguised irritation.\
\
'I need to concentrate, and this child has peppered me with questions ever since I began! Yes, yes, I told you once! This one is Vaka, and this one is Telgja. Their names mean Vigilant and Cutter, if you must know.'\
\
Glóin masters his tone, and speaks again to you.\
\
'And this one here is Hjála, which means Chatter, and I daresay he and this Beorning child have much in common! Can you keep this child entertained while I prepare these messages, ${PLAYER}? I need to think, and these constant questions are not helping!'","'There is a box of parchment near the task board, and the people of Limlók use its contents to post requests and other messages on the board. You can give him some parchment from that box, if you must.'","'Will you ask Runerik for some parchment upon which I can write these messages of warning? I brought the birds, it is true, but I seem to have left my papers behind.'","'Are they ready or not? What is the delay?'","Talk to Vídar at one of his three favourite scouting locations","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard outside his lodge in Limlók","'Your friends have gathered behind the lodge to release the messenger-ravens. You should join them.'","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard in Limlók","'It is true, I told Vídar that as he grows into a man he must shoulder further duties around the village. That includes scouting the wilderness outside Limlók, but I did not expect him to choose to do so immediately after an attack by an Orc raiding-party!\
\
'He has always been a bold boy. I should have expected it, after all! Perhaps you can ease a mother's worries by finding him on his patrol and ensuring he does not run into harm? There are three places he enjoys to scout, to the south-east, south, and south-west of the village. Look for him at one of these locations and safe-guard Vídar, and I will remember your good-hearted assistance.\
\
'It will also keep him out from underfoot your dwarves, which I know they will appreciate. Vídar always has so many questions.'","A young Beorning child stands nearby, fascinated by Glóin and the messenger-ravens.","'The messages are sent. Now it is up to the Longbeards to do what must be done. I will decide for myself whether to continue with this endeavour.'","'I am almost ready to go!'","Glóin has attracted some attention while he readies his ravens","'Did you find the parchment you needed?'"},
[3078]={"'I saw Yadêphal ride away, muttering curses to himself. I take it that Gondor didn't surrender to his master? Amusing. I never liked him, or any of Dulgabêth's knights.'\
\
You ask Ayorzén what he knows of Ugrukhôr and of the Gúrzyul.\
\
'Ah, I know enough. Ugrukhôr and Dulgabêth hate each other. If they spent less time quarrelling between themselves and more time opposing Gondor, the war might have gone differently. They say that once, long ago, Ugrukhôr plotted to ambush and murder Dulgabêth and place the blame on Gondor. Sauron learned of it before the plan could be executed, and he fed all of Ugrukhôr's servants to the Fire. When he was the only one left, Sauron held him to the flames; the pain was to serve both as punishment and as a reminder not to plot against Sauron's chosen servant. It left Ugrukhôr scarred and twisted, on the outside as already he was on the inside.\
\
'How do I know this? To this day Ugrukhôr still speaks of it! While Sauron lived, the Captain of the Pit knew not to move against Dulgabêth, but now Sauron is gone. It cannot be long now before his simmering revenge comes to a boil, and one of them will die at the hands of the other.\
\
'As for the Gúrzyul, I know the name but nothing more. Why don't you ask your Wizard?'","Mithrandir is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","'I have just finished speaking of the Gúrzyul to Harthalín, as Ayorzén well knows! I will not repeat myself for the amusement of one such as he, ${PLAYER}! Speak to Harthalín to learn what we know of them, which is admittedly quite little.\
\
'I leave the choice of path to you. Learning of Ugrukhôr and Cirith Ungol will take you into Lhingris. This dwarf, Atli, has designs on exploring Lhingris, and he will accompany you there. I believe exploration of the Gúrzyul will require exploring to the south of Orodruin, in Talath Úrui. Harthalín wishes to go there, and will accompany you thither.\
\
'Follow both of these leads to their ends, and we will be well-equipped to deal with Dulgabêth.'","Aragorn believes that you learned two useful pieces of information from Dulgabêth that should guide your further adventures in Gorgoroth.","Mithrandir has asked you to follow both of the leads you have uncovered, accompanying Atli into Lhingris and Harthalín into Talath Úrui.","'Ugrukhôr and Dulgabêth hate each other. If they spent less time quarrelling between themselves and more time opposing Gondor, the war might have gone differently. They say that once, long ago, Ugrukhôr plotted to ambush and murder Dulgabêth and place the blame on Gondor. Sauron learned of it before the plan could be executed, and he fed all of Ugrukhôr's servants to the Fire. When he was the only one left, Sauron held him to the flames; the pain was to serve both as punishment and as a reminder not to plot against Sauron's chosen servant. It left Ugrukhôr scarred and twisted, on the outside as already he was on the inside.\
\
'How do I know this? To this day Ugrukhôr still speaks of it! While Sauron lived, the Captain of the Pit knew not to move against Dulgabêth, but now Sauron is gone. It cannot be long now before his simmering revenge comes to a boil, and one of them will die at the hands of the other.'","Complete 'Chapter 3.3: The Gúrzyul' in Talath Úrui","Chapter 3.1: The Dread Lands","Complete 'Chapter 3.2: The Second Garrison' in Lhingris","'I believe you learned two useful pieces of information from Dulgabêth. The first is this: the forces of Mordor are not unified, and they might be turned against one another. Indeed, they may already be doing so on their own, without our assistance! He seems most concerned about his rival, who sent forces to reinforce Cirith Ungol. This rival is the one he called Ugrukhôr, the Captain of the Pit, and I have heard tell of him before. He is cruel and without mercy, and it was he who promised the Thandrim of Durthand peace and gave them slaughter instead.\
\
'The second piece of information Dulgabêth unwittingly gave to us might not be as immediately useful, but still I want to learn what it signifies. He spoke of the Gúrzyul, and the name makes me uneasy for its evocation of the Nazgûl. The Nine are slain, destroyed alongside Sauron, and few could rival them in malice or power, but we should tread carefully near any reminder of them.\
\
'I understand that Ayorzén the Wily refused my offer of a place in Gondor, and has been haunting the pass of Cirith Gorgor just inside the Black Gate. See what he makes of the information we have learned, ${PLAYER}, and follow that knowledge where it leads.'","Complete 'Chapter 3.2: The Valley of Webs' in Lhingris","Ayorzén the Wily is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","Talk to Mithrandir in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate","'We learned two useful pieces of information from Dulgabêth. The first is this: the forces of Mordor are not unified, and they might be turned against one another. Indeed, they may already be doing so on their own, without our assistance! He seems most concerned about his rival, who sent forces to reinforce Cirith Ungol. This rival is the one he called Ugrukhôr, the Captain of the Pit, and I have heard tell of him before. He is cruel and without mercy, and it was he who promised the Thandrim of Durthand peace and gave them slaughter instead.\
\
'The second piece of information Dulgabêth unwittingly gave to us might not be as immediately useful, but still I want to learn what it signifies. He spoke of the Gúrzyul, and the name makes me uneasy for its evocation of the Nazgûl. The Nine are slain, destroyed alongside Sauron, and few could rival them in malice or power, but we should tread carefully near any reminder of them.\
\
'I understand that Ayorzén the Wily refused my offer of a place in Gondor, and has been haunting the pass of Cirith Gorgor just inside the Black Gate. See what he makes of the information we have learned, ${PLAYER}, and follow that knowledge where it leads.'","'Your adventures in Lhingris and Talath Úrui have proven most informative, but they raise further questions. Why would the Ghâsh-hai pledge to support Ugrukhôr? What has become of Borangos following the defeat of Sauron? And to what end does Urudanî walk the land once again, so changed?\
\
'These questions must wait. I have heard worrisome tidings from Agarnaith, the Bloody Gore. Few have gone there, but those who have returned speak of a dangerous and growing threat.'","'I leave the choice of path to you. Learning of Ugrukhôr and Cirith Ungol will take you into Lhingris. The dwarf Atli has designs on exploring Lhingris, and he will accompany you there. I believe exploration of the Gúrzyul will require exploring to the south of Orodruin, in Talath Úrui. Harthalín will accompany you thither.\
\
'Follow both of these leads to their ends, and we will be well-equipped to deal with Dulgabêth.'","Complete 'Chapter 3.3: Fate of the Stonemaiden' in Talath Úrui","Talk to Ayorzén in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate"},
[3080]={"Venko is at the north-western point of the White Mare.","Runerik Knotbeard followed you to the White Mare with some of his people. Why?","Add the flood-broom to the boiling water in the north room of Runerik's lodge","Bring the unspent arrows to Yrsa Spearwife in Limlók for her inspection","Some unexpected visitors have come north-west of the White Mare, across the river from your dwarf companions. Why have they followed you here?","Bring the flood-broom tea to Runerik Knotbeard inside his lodge","'Poison? Yes, I thought so.\
\
'I have set some water boiling by the fire in the north room. Add the flood-broom to it and let it steep for a little while.\
\
'You did gather the flood-broom, did you not?'","Hjála's wing is broken, pierced by an arrow","'My husband brought your birds inside the lodge. Find him there and tell him the arrows used by the Orcs in this area are poisoned, as he believed.'","Vaka lives, but has lost several feathers and a lot of blood","Talk to Glóin behind Runerik's lodge","Runerik is inside his lodge, tending to the wounded messenger-ravens.","'You brought me some arrows from the Orcs? Let me see them.'\
\
Yrsa inspects the arrows, sniffing the arrowhead and grimacing.\
\
'Yes, these are coated with a thin poison. It is not enough for such foes to injure or maim, they seek to attack their enemies from the inside as well! My husband instructed you to gather flood-broom? That tells me he suspected poison, for that herb has effectively treated such vile substances for us before. But it is good to know for certain.\
\
'He has brought your birds inside the lodge. Find him there and tell him the arrows used by the Orcs in this area are poisoned, as he believed.'","'I will feed this tea to the ravens, and with luck it may halt the poison. I have done what else I could for them, and with rest it is to be hoped they will recover.\
\
'I am pleased you did not abandon these creatures when they were of no more use to you. I admit I expected worse of you, and of your dwarf allies.'","Collect unspent arrows from Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard inside his lodge in Limlók","Collected flood-broom (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect the flood-broom tea inside Runerik's lodge","'I have been more than welcoming up to this point, but if a whole troop of dwarves come to Limlók....'\
\
Runerik's further complaint is halted by the sound of sudden commotion behind the lodge.\
\
'What is that noise? Your companions do not sound pleased about something, ${PLAYER}.'","'We have a problem, ${PLAYER}. As my ravens flew above the White Mare on their errand, arrows sped from the ground and brought them down! I do not know if any of my birds survived this assault, or if any of the messages will reach their destinations.\
\
'Go to the White Mare, north of here, and recover the fallen ravens. We must know which of them did not escape the Orkish volley.'","The flood-broom will take some time to steep in the boiling water.","'We are being watched. No, not by Orcs.\
\
'They are to the north-west, across the river. Go see what they want, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I don't like it.'","Runerik Knotbeard will meet you inside the lodge to treat the injured messenger-ravens.","The flood-broom tea is now prepared, and waits for you to bring it to Runerik.","Chapter 3.2: Runerik's Request","Yrsa Spearwife is in south-east Limlók.","'If you wish to aid your injured, you will collect some of the herb we call flood-broom. It grows beside rivers and streams in the Floodfells, and possesses healing properties that may help. Collect too some unspent arrows from the Orcs. My wife will inspect them back in Limlók, and she may learn from them something of which I can make use when healing these ravens.'","Some of the ravens were shot from the sky by Orc archers! You have to retrieve them from the White Mare and learn if any of Glóin's messages escaped the Floodfells.","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard north-west of the White Mare","All dwarves everywhere are threatened by the presence of a new Lord of Gundabad. Glóin's warning must reach them!","Retrieve injured message-ravens from the White Mare","'I will meet you inside.'","Talk to Venko at the north-western point of the White Mare","'What was that noise? Your companions do not sound pleased about something.'","'Why have they come here? I do not like it.'","'Your ravens... do they still live?'\
\
Runerik gently takes the birds from you and sniffs their wounds.\
\
'They are grievously wounded, and will die if they are not treated. But I understand one of the ravens escaped the arrows of the Orcs, and winged away with the message it bore? Does your interest in these poor creatures then end? They are of no more use to you; do you then discard them?'\
\
You make clear that you want to heal Hjála and Vaka of their hurts, if you can.\
\
'If this is true, you will collect some of the herb we call flood-broom. It grows beside rivers and streams in the Floodfells, and possesses healing properties that may help. Collect too some unspent arrows from the Orcs. My wife will inspect them back in Limlók, and she may learn from them something of which I can make use when healing these ravens.'","Glóin is behind Runerik's lodge, and from there you heard a great commotion. What has happened?","Flood-broom can be found alongside rivers and streams throughout the Floodfells. Runerik also wants his wife Yrsa to examine unspent arrows carried by Orcs in the area, and has asked you to collect some.","Wait for the flood-broom tea to properly steep","Runerik stands before some of his assembled people north-west of the White Mare, and demands to speak with you.","Confront the unexpected visitors north-west of the White Mare, across the river","Collected unspent arrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect flood-broom by rivers in the Floodfells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Runerik has prepared a pot of boiling water in the north room, and he wants you to add the flood-broom you collected to it.","'Go to the White Mare, north of here, and recover the fallen ravens. We must know which of them did not escape the Orkish volley.'"},
[3081]={"'It is good to be owed favours and coin by Kings and Princes, ${PLAYER}. I accept your offer. I have not been the guest of a royal court such as this before. Well, not an invited one, anyway.'","You have encountered the Corsair Jajax in Dol Amroth and he has a tale to tell.","'I said to keep an eye on him, not to bring him to my court, ${PLAYER}. Why should I trust these things he says of Umbar, or of the Kindred of the Coins? How do we know he is not one of them?\
\
'Why should I trust one of the Corsairs who so troubled our coasts during the war, and who continues to do so even now? Have you taken leave of your senses?'","'My brother Daxamat and I believed we were done with Gondor when we bid you farewell, ${PLAYER}. I thought we would return briefly home, to Umbar, and after finding a new ship and a new crew we would set sail once again in search of treasure.\
\
'It was a fine plan, but... well, that is the story, is it not?'","Chapter 3.2: The Adventures of Jajax and Daxamat","Talk to Jajax in Dol Amroth and hear his story","Talk to Prince Imrahil in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor","Prince Imrahil is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.","Talk to Jajax in Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor","Jajax stands on a tree-shaded street in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.","'It was oar-work alone that allowed us to escape, but if good fortune permitted it, ill fortune was soon to follow. A sudden storm rose up and swamped the boat, and when at last I came to shore it was back to Gondor I had been delivered. Of Dax there was no sign. I am certain my brother lives, for he has survived much worse than that, sturdy crab that he is.'\
\
You tell Jajax that Prince Imrahil and King Elessar should be told of the situation he encountered in Umbar, and the Corsair tilts his head, weighing your suggestion against the potential for reward.\
\
'It is good to be owed favours and coin by Kings and Princes, ${PLAYER}. I accept your offer. I have not been the guest of a royal court such as this before. Well, not an invited one, anyway.'","'Much has happened to me since I saw you last. Do you want to hear of my adventures?'"},
[3082]={"Find a message addressed to Ugrukhôr somewhere in Cirith Ungol","Atli Spider-bane is not far from the approach to Cirith Ungol, in Lhingris.","'If you are of a mind to explore the tower, now might be the best time to get on with it! Orcs are given to fighting among themselves even at the best of times, but when they must deal with spiders as well, why, that must be the best of times indeed! For us, at least. Not for them, no indeed!\
\
'Enter the tower and remind the Orcs that spiders are not the only thing they need to fear when there's a hero or two on the loose!\
\
'What did you say you were looking for? Information on Ugrukhôr? I wouldn't say that Orcs are my area of skill, but I expect if you're looking for news on someone high up the chain of command, you'll want to climb higher up in the tower. It stands to reason, doesn't it?'","Bring the message for Ugrukhôr to Atli Spider-bane outside the Tower of Cirith Ungol <rgb=#00FF00>(The message can be read from your inventory)</rgb>","Atli Spider-bane believes that you should enter Cirith Ungol while the Orcs are dealing with the newly-crazed spiders of Lhingris.","'You have nothing for me? Some would say that is a waste of time!'","This message addressed to Ugrukhôr speaks of loyalties and infighting","Stairs ascend to the higher levels of the tower","'What is this message you found? It speaks of loyalty, and infighting, and treachery? Hmm.\
\
'Bah! I hope you are satisfied with what you learned, for it means nothing to me. This is why I enjoy fighting spiders. There's no intrigue, no complex loyalties. You always know what side you're on, with spiders!'","Something has stirred up the spiders of Lhingris, and they have begun attacking the Orcs of Cirith Ungol.","'Enter the tower and remind the Orcs that spiders are not the only thing they need to fear when there's a hero or two on the loose!'","You see a crumpled parchment discarded by the fire","Chapter 3.2: The Second Garrison"},
[3083]={"This Orc is alive, but he is very near to death","'There are many bodies on the approach, Orcs and spiders both. Spiders tend to be honest concerning when they are dead or not, but Orcs are more given to play-acting. You may want to ensure they are really dead before you set them at your back.'","This Orc is not pretending. He is truly slain","An entrance to Lhingris can be found in Durthang or by passes in Udûn or Dor Amarth.","'There your tower lies. I am sure you have your reasons for wanting to see it, but I will not stick my nose into your matters. I do not need to know why you adventure in Mordor to lend you the aid of my axe, and to speak plainly I am happier not hearing the lengthy details!\
\
'There are many bodies on the approach, Orcs and spiders both. Spiders tend to be honest concerning whether they are dead or not, but Orcs are more given to play-acting. You may want to ensure they are really dead before you set them at your back.'","'Ah! Do you smell that? That is the reek of spider you smell! Every one of the creatures has a different and distinctive odour, and they are all most foul. When you have fought the terrors for as long as I have, you learn to identify such things.\
\
'We will handle my business first, and then continue on to yours. Let us slay spiders, as many as we can! Then we will find this tower you seek. Cirith Ungol, did you say? We will go there when we have left a trail of dead spiders behind us, and when we come back this way we can tread upon them like a carpet! Ha! Ha! Ha!'","Talk to Atli Spider-bane at the approach to Cirith Ungol","Talk to the mortally-wounded Orc while he yet lives","Defeated spiders in Lhingris (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You found one alive? What did I tell you?\
\
'You might as well ask him what he knows. If you wait too long you will miss the chance to do so, for he will not cling to life in order to help a ${RACE}, ${PLAYER}!'","Spiders can be found throughout Lhingris, to Atli's delight.","Atli Spider-bane is in north-eastern Lhingris, near the pass to Dor Amarth.","Atli was right: the bodies of Orcs and spiders litter the approach to the tower","'I understand that you have business in Lhingris? I do as well, for I must introduce the crawling terrors of the Valley of Webs to the axe of Atli Spider-bane! I will not waste the renewed vigour of my twilight years staying at home. To adventure, ${PLAYER}! Let us enter Lhingris from Dor Amarth and see what waits for us there.'","Atli Spider-bane is not far from the approach to Cirith Ungol.","Atli Spider-bane is within view of the the approach to Cirith Ungol.","Talk to Atli Spider-bane in northern Lhingris","Defeat spiders in Lhingris (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Atli thought you should more closely inspect the approach to Cirith Ungol, ensuring that the Orcs that lie in death before the tower are truly slain.","Atli Spider-bane, with renewed health and vigour, has heard rumours of a spider-infested valley in Gorgoroth and wishes to see it for himself.","'We will handle my business first, and then continue on to yours. Let us slay spiders, as many as we can! Then we will find this tower you seek. Cirith Ungol, did you say? We will go there when we have left a trail of dead spiders behind us, and when we come back this way we can tread upon them like a carpet! Ha! Ha! Ha!'","One of the Orcs lying on the approach to Cirith Ungol lived still, but he is close to death. What might he tell you of the situation in Lhingris?","Atli calls for you to halt and smells the air","Atli thought you should more closely inspect the approach to Cirith Ungol.","With a final gasp, Sárnazt succumbs to his wounds and can speak no more","'There are many bodies on the approach, Orcs and spiders both. Spiders tend to be honest concerning whether they are dead or not, but Orcs are more given to play-acting. You may want to ensure they are really dead before you set them at your back.'","'Have we met before? You have a familiar face, for a ${RACE}, but it is hard to say for certain. Now, if you were a spider, I would remember every detail, and count the days until I could clear you from the face of this Middle-earth!\
\
'I believed my days were soon to be over, but I have experienced a resurgence of health and vigour, ${PLAYER}. I heard that the Land of Mordor was opened and the Dark Lord defeated, and that meant little to me. But when news came to me of a valley in the shadow of the Morgai fence that was crawling with spiders, I had no choice but to take notice!\
\
'I understand that you have business in Lhingris? I do as well, for I must introduce the crawling terrors of the Valley of Webs to the axe of Atli Spider-bane! I will not waste the renewed vigour of my twilight years staying at home. To adventure, ${PLAYER}! Let us enter Lhingris, either from the fortress of Durthang or the other passes, and we will see what waits for us there.'","Chapter 3.2: The Valley of Webs","'If I... if I had not suffered this wound... you would be dead... ${RACE}! I would make you regret... taunting Sárnazt!'\
\
Sárnazt coughs weakly, and blood bubbles on his lips.\
\
'Wretched spiders! They rarely... bothered the Orcs of the Tower.... but something changed. They used to take... one or two of the weakest... but not like this! So many... there were so many!\
\
'When the Mountain erupted and the earth shook... many of the tunnels were exposed... and the creatures... swarmed from their pits!\
\
'Róglarg thinks he can... keep them out...'\
\
Sárnazt is seized by a long fit of coughing, and when he speaks again it is for the last time.\
\
'No one knows... what happened to Shelob...'","Examine the approach to Cirith Ungol","'Seems like the Orcs and the spiders had an arrangement, but something's happened and they're not getting along so well these days. Ha! Serves 'em both right, don't it? That's what happens when you try to make nice with a spider. Can't keep watch on all those eyes and all those legs at once, can you?\
\
'It sounds as if this Shelob must have been the one keeping these spiders under control. I guess it falls to me and my axe to do the job now!'","Find Atli Spider-bane in northern Lhingris, east of the Durthang entrance"},
[3084]={"Imák wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Venko's skills. Venko is by the south-east entrance of Limlók.","'What is it? What can you tell of me, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
<u>Venko, Zhélruka Home-seeker</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Axe-wielding:</rgb> 60\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Sword-wielding:</rgb> 75\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 80\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Resolve:</rgb> 80\
\
'Yes? You seem to be developing an eye for skill! It is true, I am not as accomplished with axes as I am with swords. The sword is a Zhélruka weapon. We will swing axes, if that is what we have at hand, but we do not prefer them. Let the Longbeards prize their axes; we will use whatever is necessary to achieve victory, whether that be sword, axe, or knife.'","Find Glóin in Limlók and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> his skills","Find Venko by the south-east entrance to Limlók and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> his skills","Once again <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Yrsa Spearwife inside the lodge","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Yrsa Spearwife inside the lodge","'Try it on me, ${PLAYER}. Look at me and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> my skills, and I will tell you if you succeed to my satisfaction.'","Glóin wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Imák's skills. Imák is on the western side of Limlók.","'Well? Let us see if Yrsa has trained you well in the art of appraisal. What can you tell of me?'\
\
<u>Runerik Knotbeard, Beorning Chief of Limlók</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Skin-changing:</rgb> 95\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Herbalism:</rgb> 85\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 85\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Resolve:</rgb> 85\
\
'You have made good progress, ${PLAYER}. So too have the injured ravens. I am pleased to tell you that with time enough to rest, they should fully recover from their wounds. They were fortunate for my knowledge of herbs and for your quick action: the flood-broom tea has already counteracted the poison.\
\
'Your agreement to care for these ravens had another effect: it caused me to change my own appraisal of you. You are welcome to remain in Limlók, if you wish, and so too can these dwarves. But I hold firm to one thing. I refuse to host an entire company of dwarves in my village! You need no special skill at appraisal to know I mean it!'","Practice makes perfect! Yrsa has asked you to once again try and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> her skills.","'You wish to learn the art of appraisal, by which you may determine the skills and abilities of the people you meet? It is not difficult to learn the basics, but it does take some practice if you are to become a master of observation. The trick is to relax your eye and consider every aspect of your subject as a unified whole: every detail is in some way related to the larger sum that is your subject.\
\
'Try it on me, ${PLAYER}. Look at me and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> my skills, and I will tell you if you succeed to my satisfaction.'","'Why not try this on your dwarf friends next? If they are like others I have known, they will be interested in your appraisal of their talents. You may find it useful to learn of their strengths and weaknesses, as well.'","'You have a good eye, friend. With practice perhaps you will become even more skilled at the art of appraisal.'","'Are you surprised to learn I possess such skill in the healing arts and mastery of herb-lore? You should not be. Were you to exercise your powers of observation, you should be able to discern such skills in others. Indeed, I believe it is a latent ability you already possess.\
\
'Yrsa can tell you more. Consider such training as she can provide a repayment for aiding my son Vídar with his chores. Aye, he told me you were an able fighter, and was pleased to have the company.\
\
'My wife came inside to inquire about the ravens. Find her in the other room and see what she can teach you.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Runerik Knotbeard outside the lodge","Talk to Glóin in Limlók","Talk to Imák in Limlók","Yrsa waits for your assessment of her skills and abilities. You consider what you have learned.\
\
<u>Yrsa Spearwife, Beorning Woman of Limlók</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Skin-changing:</rgb> 95\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Observation:</rgb> 90\
\
She sighs as your provide your account, but there is humour in it.\
\
'You say I have great skill at skin-changing? Whatever gave you that idea? Ah, it is only a jest. Try it once again, and perhaps you can notice details you missed before. The signs are there for one who knows what to seek. <rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> me once again, and concentrate.'","Find Imák on the western side of Limlók and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> his skills","Yrsa has asked you to try and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> her skills.","Remembering the words of Yrsa, you decide to next appraise Runerik Knotbeard","Yrsa waits patiently for your second assessment. You consider what you have learned.\
\
<u>Yrsa Spearwife, Beorning Woman of Limlók</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Skin-changing:</rgb> 95\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Observation:</rgb> 90\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 80\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Resolve:</rgb> 90\
\
She nods, pleased at your success.\
\
'You have done well, ${PLAYER}, and will improve with time and practice! Why not try this on your dwarf friends next? If they are like others I have known, they will be interested in your appraisal of their talents. You may find it useful to learn of their strengths and weaknesses, as well, for there is little doubt that danger still lies ahead of you all.\
\
'After you have done that, perhaps you can impress my husband with your newfound talent.'","'<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Venko and see if I am wrong! It is no competition, of course. I am merely curious.'","'Yes? To what do I owe such scrutiny?'\
\
<u>Glóin, Hero of the Lonely Mountain</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Axe-wielding:</rgb> 80\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Fire-making:</rgb> 95\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 90\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Resolve:</rgb> 85\
\
'Ah ha! You are practicing the art of appraisal! My cousin Balin was quite skilled at that, and Thorin relied on both his observant eye and his wisdom. It is a pity what happened to him in the end.\
\
'You should <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> the other members of our travelling party! Begin with Imák, for I think he will be the most difficult to read.'","Yrsa is inside the lodge, waiting to speak with you.","'What are you doing? Have you got something in your eye?'\
\
<u>Imák, Stout-axe Survivor of Mordor</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Perception (Smell):</rgb> 90\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Trap Construction:</rgb> 80\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 95\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Resolve:</rgb> 90\
\
'I trust you are suitably impressed by what you have seen? Life in the pits of Mordor was hard, and not every Stout-axe had the fortune to escape the chains of Sauron. But those that did were made strong, toughened by the experience. So it was with me. Those who did not suffer in Mordor were not tempered as I was!\
\
'<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Venko and see if I am wrong! It is no competition, of course. I am merely curious.'","Glóin is in Limlók, wondering why you have been studying him so closely.","Runerik thinks you may be able to develop one of your latent abilities, and wants you to consult with his wife Yrsa for further instruction along that line.","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard outside his lodge in Limlók","Imák is in Limlók, and he wants to know why you have subjected him to such scrutiny.","Chapter 3.3: An Eye for Skill","The real test of your appraisal ability will be to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Runerik Knotbeard outside his lodge.","Talk to Venko in Limlók","'Try once more, and perhaps you will notice details you missed before. The signs are there for one who knows what to seek. <rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> me once again, and concentrate.'","Runerik Knotbeard is outside his lodge and interested to know your appraisal of his skills.","'My wife came inside to inquire about the ravens. Find her in the other room and see what she can teach you.'","Venko is in Limlók, and he is suspicious of the recent attention you have given him.","Yrsa has asked you to try and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Glóin's skills. The old dwarf should be somewhere outside in Limlók.","Talk to Yrsa Spearwife inside her lodge","'You should <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> the other members of our travelling party! Begin with Imák, for I think he will be the most difficult to read.'"},
[3085]={"'The Prince wants to know where I am going? That is my own concern. Being his guest has already grown tiresome.\
\
'Farewell, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps I will see you again. Perhaps not.'","Jajax turns to leave, and Prince Imrahil calls for him to halt","Jajax snorts, a rude sound that echoes in the hall","'Evil tidings have come to Dol Amroth from the coastline of Anfalas, tidings that harden my heart against such men as this Jajax. But you need not hear of them from me. Speak instead to Captain Maeral, for he left Outer Gondor just days ago... afoot and without ship. Tell ${PLAYER} why this was your manner of travel, Captain.'","Jajax says nothing further, but he looks very satisfied with himself.","Prince Imrahil is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.","Prince Imrahil calls for everyone to be quiet","Talk to King Elessar in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor","Captain Maeral is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.","Talk to Jajax in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor","'The King should make preparations to return to Minas Tirith.'","'I value your words, Prince Imrahil, but I cannot heed the warning they contain. The suffering of Anfalas makes it a more necessary destination for me, not a lesser one. I will see the state of things in Outer Gondor with my own eyes, and I will aid the people there as best I can, despite the danger... or perhaps because of it.'","'You can tell this weepy old sailor that I was not involved with the burning of his precious ship, ${PLAYER}, and my proof is that he still lives. If I had been there, he and his crew would have been spared...'\
\
Jajax grins.\
\
'Aye, they would have been spared... spared the walk back to this city! Tell him this, too: I did not burn his ship, but if he gets another he would be wise to steer it far from Jajax in the future!'","'He may not have been responsible for the burning of the Alphroval, ${PLAYER}, but I think it need not matter. How many good men do you think he has slain during his life as a Corsair? Whether he fights on behalf of the Heirs of Castamir or the Kindred of the Coins or for himself, does it really matter to the men whose lives he takes, or whose ships he burns?\
\
'Watch that one carefully if your paths cross again.'","King Elessar is in the Palace of the Swan, in King's Gondor.","Jajax has decided to leave.","Chapter 3.3: Burning Ships","'You need not hear these tidings from me. Speak instead to Captain Maeral, for he left Outer Gondor just days ago... afoot and without ship. Tell ${PLAYER} why this was your manner of travel, Captain.'","'Halt! Someone stop that man.'","Jajax is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.","'A pox on all Corsairs... but especially this grinning villain!'","A tense situation arises in the Palace of the Swan with the arrival of Jajax.","'If you command me to speak, my Prince, I will, but the pain is fresh and the losses I suffered there will haunt me to the end of my days. I came afoot because my ship, the Alphroval, was burned off the coast of Anfalas by Corsairs of Umbar just days ago. Some of my crew survived and made the journey back to Dol Amroth overland with me, but too many good sailors died to fire and water and Corsair blade.\
\
'I demand to know why you now host in this palace one of the monsters who set my ship aflame!'","'I will not change my plan. I will go to see the state of things in Anfalas.'","'Silence! I will allow no fighting in the Palace of the Swan!\
\
'King Elessar, these tidings of Anfalas make it clear to me that you should make a change in the plan we discussed. If the Corsairs of Umbar remain active along the coast of Langstrand, it is too dangerous for you to continue that way. Instead you should make preparations to return to Minas Tirith. I will allocate a number of swan-knights to attend you on the journey, if you so desire.'","Talk to Prince Imrahil in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor","'What says this villain to that?'","Wait for Jajax to leave","Talk to Captain Maeral in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor"},
[3087]={"Talk to Harthalín outside Fushaum Bal","Defeat Easterlings in Talath Úrui (${CURRENT}/8)","Talk to Harthalín outside Nargroth","'I do not trust this spirit, but perhaps we can make use of it to learn that which we seek and be safely away before it works some treachery upon us!'","The presence remains within the stone: Zaghárog, watching you silently, waiting.","Talk to the spirit in the stone","You find a scorched parchment clutched in the hand of the fallen Easterling","The sound of raised voices comes from within Fushaum Bal","The lawless settlement of Fushaum Bal is south-west of Orodruin, in Talath Úrui.","'Lawlessness runs rampant throughout Fushaum Bal, but some of the Easterlings within might be high enough in the hierarchy to have information of use to us.'","You found a crumpled parchment on the body of an Easterling in Talath Úrui.","The spirit in the stone outside Nargroth showed you the location of a scorched skull within a cell in Naerband. If you understood its wish correctly, it has promised to tell you about the Gúrzyul if you return with the skull.\
\
You witnessed that Naerband consists of three large chambers, connected by hallways and subdivided by walls and iron bars. The skull is on the floor of a cell in the south-western corner of the largest, northernmost chamber. The iron door to the cell was half-open, and you saw flame-spirits floating over the fog-covered floor.","Harthalín is outside Fushaum Bal, in Talath Úrui.","A watching-stone outside the Caverns of Fire has taken an interest in you.","'Do you feel that? Something lurks within this statue! I sense it watching us.\
\
'Use caution, ${PLAYER}! Watching-stones are oft the home of fell spirits, bound there for eternity, and they bear no love for such as we!'","Bring the scorched skull to the watching-stone outside Nargroth","A watching-stone outside the Caverns of Fire has taken an interest in you, and awaits delivery of the skull you agreed to bring to it.","'I understand you wish to add to our store of knowledge concerning the Gúrzyul? I will travel with you into Talath Úrui. Let us first find the settlement of Fushaum Bal. Reports indicate it is a lawless settlement on the south-western side of Orodruin.'","The prison that was shown to you is called Naerband","You feel a presence regard you from within the carven stone","'This is the road that leads to Nargroth, but I have discovered something else that might prove of use to us, ${PLAYER}. There is a watching-stone a short distance to the north of here, and I sense that it may have seen something concerning the Gúrzyul!'","Chapter 3.3: The Gúrzyul","'There is nothing for me?'","'If the Ghâsh-hai reported to Urudanî at Nargroth, we may learn more if we dare the caverns. It will not be easy to reach them, for when the southern face of Orodruin exploded, it created a lake of fire between here and there: the Ghâshghurm.'","Bring the orders concerning Nargroth to Harthalín outside Fushaum Bal <rgb=#00FF00>(The orders can be read from your inventory)</rgb>","Meet up with Harthalín outside Fushaum Bal, in Talath Úrui","Malice emanates from the skull. Scorched by heat, it has neither splintered nor cracked","The images return: you see the prison once again, and know that it is the prison of Naerband, south of the Ghâshghurm. Once again the spirit shows you the certain cell, and the scorched skull in the corner. Then the images recede, but the watchful presence remains.","Nargroth, the Caverns of Fire, can be found on the eastern side of Talath Úrui, beyond the Ghâshghurm.","Find the scorched skull in a cell within the prison of Naerband <rgb=#00FF00>using the information in your quest journal</rgb>","Harthalín wishes to see the slopes of Orodruin again, disbelieving that Sauron is truly gone, and will accompany you as you search Talath Úrui for knowledge of the Gúrzyul.","'What did you find, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
Harthalín takes the parchment and reads it. When she is done, she gazes off to the east.\
\
'So Urudanî Stonemaiden was one of the Gúrzyul, after all. I thought it possible, for she was a Black Númenórean and fought against us during the Siege of Barad-dûr. But she had not been seen since then; I thought she was dead.\
\
'There is something else familiar in these orders. Nargroth, the Caverns of Fire, are located on the eastern side of Orodruin. If the Ghâsh-hai reported to Urudanî at Nargroth, we may learn more if we dare the caverns. It will not be easy to reach them, for when the southern face of Orodruin exploded, it created a lake of fire between here and there: the Ghâshghurm.'","You place the skull at the base of the stone, and the images return.\
\
Once again you see the prison of Naerband, but something this time is different. It takes you a moment to reconcile what has changed, but held in the grip of the spirit it is impossible to tell how long the moment might have been. The prison stands in the shadow of Orodruin, and then you see it: the southern slope of the Mountain is intact; the Ghâshghurm has not yet been made.\
\
The images flicker behind your eyes, and you see that Naerband is filled with prisoners. Downtrodden Nurnhoth, rebellious Easterlings, and Haradrim deserters rattle the cages of their cells. Their jailors walk the corridors of Naerband, and they tap their weapons on the iron doors, and they scrape their blades on the iron walls, and they tap their boots on the iron floor. You are seized by a sensation of eager anticipation, but it does not belong to you. It comes from the whispering spirit, and fills you with revulsion and dread.\
\
Then the Mountain blazes, and the southern slope explodes in a shower of rock and flame. The torrent flows inexorably down the side of Orodruin, and the rocky plain becomes a lake of fire: the Ghâshghurm.\
\
The images become sharper and more distinct, as if the spirit seeks to draw your attention. At last you understand. As the lava pooled at the foot of Orodruin, the iron prison of Naerband became super-heated by its proximity to the lake of fire. Naerband became more than a prison. It became an oven.\
\
You close your eyes to shut out the sight, and at last the spirit relents, its price paid.\
\
'Zaghárog,' it says to you: the name of the spirit in the stone.","'It is so strange to me, ${PLAYER}. This place is both alike to and very different from when I last was here at the close of the Second Age. For all the tumult within its heart, Orodruin seemed as if it would always endure. And yet, even the Mountain of Fire has changed since then: the southern face blown open, a lake of fire spilt onto the plain.\
\
'This settlement was not here then, but I recognize its type. Military encampments have a sense of order and of place about them. Well do I know it, for I served beneath High King Gil-galad at Dagorlad and during the Siege!\
\
'But once the campaign is ended, all such order is discarded alongside the attention of the commanders. This settlement, Fushaum Bal, has that air about it. Many inhabit it now, and lawlessness runs rampant, but some of the Easterlings within might be high enough in the hierarchy to have information of use to us. Hunt them down around Fushaum Bal and its environs, and see what they might know of the Gúrzyul.'","'Use caution, ${PLAYER}! Watching-stones are oft the home of fell spirits, bound there for eternity, and they bear no love for such as we!'","Find the road that leads to Nargroth, on the eastern side of Talath Úrui","'Mithrandir spoke at length to me about the Gúrzyul, but much of what he had to say was speculation. We do not know very much about them.\
\
'They seem to have been Black Númenóreans that swore to serve Sauron during the later years of the Second Age, before the Last Alliance of Elves and Men besieged Barad-dûr. Many were the cruel Men who sought to serve the Dark Lord in those days, but few only won his favour. Mithrandir would not say how he came to know this, but he believes Sauron bled his favourites with the edge of Gulthauk, his prized morgul-knife.\
\
'They need no longer fear the passage of time, for by this act they were made Deathless. They are like to the Nazgûl, but lesser in power, and unlike those wraiths they can be slain. There will be no returning from death for such as they.\
\
'I understand you wish to add to our store of knowledge concerning the Gúrzyul? I will travel with you into Talath Úrui. Let us first find the  settlement of Fushaum Bal. Reports indicate it is a lawless settlement on the south-western side of Orodruin.'","Easterlings can be found around Fushaum Bal, in Talath Úrui.","Defeat Easterlings in Talath Úrui (7/8)","You tell Harthalín what the spirit in the stone showed to you, and she spends a moment in thought.\
\
'From your description it sounds to me that this skull will be found in the prison of Naerband, south of the Ghâshghurm. But why would this spirit wish for you to find this skull, ${PLAYER}, if that is truly what it wants?\
\
'I can see no immediate harm from completing this task, but remain alert. Spirits such as the one bound to this stone have a reputation for deceit.'","Harthalín is by the watching-stone outside Nargroth, on the eastern side of Talath Úrui.","Defeated Easterlings in Talath Úrui (${CURRENT}/8)","The carven stone is dreadful in form, and it does not seem out of place within Gorgoroth. But there is something else that sets it apart, a cold and watchful presence. And then, there is more: a voice that whispers in your head. Images rise unbidden behind your eyes. They are drained of colour, as if the one who creates them has no knowledge of shade or hue.\
\
You see a place of darkness, and a tiny point of light flickering high above. Then, below, there is a knife held in a cruel fist. It descends in an arc, and blood flows from a wound. The darkness deepens.\
\
The voice in your head speaks no words, but you are suddenly awash on a questioning sea.\
\
You recover your own words enough to reply, 'Yes, the Gúrzyul.'\
\
The interrogative waves vanish as quickly as they had arrived. In their place is an overwhelming sensation: the promise of knowledge and secrets held close for centuries. As you try to express that such knowledge will be welcome, it is whisked cruelly away, dangled just out of reach.\
\
The giving sensation is gone, replaced with a taking desire. You see a prison in your mind's eye, and the details are so clear you know it is a real place. The spirit shows you a certain cell in this prison, and a scorched skull in one corner. The images fade, and the whispering voice returns. It speaks a single word, but the word is enough. The word is 'want.'\
\
You are released from the spirit's hold and the whispering in your head fades away. The presence remains, regarding you silently.","'What did you see, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You recount the terrible images, and Harthalín glares at the watching-stone with disgust.\
\
'It is a spirit fell and cruel, of that there can be no mistake. Am I right in thinking that you have paid its price?'"},
[3088]={"Search for Raneleg to the north, west of the road","Talk to Ayorzén at Cirith Gorgor, inside the Black Gate","Learn if Arodrog is alive or dead","You found the adventurers that entered Agarnaith from the northern approach","Defeat foul creatures in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You found adventurers in Agarnaith, and should hear what they have encountered within the Bloody Gore.","'Agarnaith may be approached from the north or from the south, and adventurers have sought to gain entrance from either direction. You may do the same, ${PLAYER}.'","Linadar is just north of the junction with the eastern road, in Agarnaith.","You agreed to meet up with the adventurers again on the road, near where the eastern path leads away into the swamp.","Defeated foul creatures in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Agarnaith may be approached from either the north or the south.","Mithrandir has heard an unsettling rumour of a threat growing in Agarnaith, the Bloody Gore, on the eastern side of Gorgoroth.","'Keep an eye on your surroundings as you adventure within the marsh. Dangers could lurk anywhere: in the water, up among the trees, within the twisted grasses. This is a foul place. The air smells foul and tastes worse.\
\
'The creatures here don't seem to mind it. Indeed, it seems to lend them a curious strength! Test your mettle against them, and I will meet you further south along the road.'","'Some vile work is being conducted in Agarnaith, and we must learn what it signifies for Gondor and for Middle-earth. I find it curious that our well-informed Easterling has not spoken of Agarnaith to us. Does he keep the secrets of that land with the hope of blinding us to the threat it poses?\
\
'I do not like his silence on this matter. You must go to Agarnaith and learn what transpires within, but do not go alone! I believe you should bring Ayorzén with you, and find out what he knows about the Bloody Gore.'","'I am not surprised to hear that Arodrog was dead, for the creature that attacked him was a terrible, rotting thing. I can still hear its awful cry echoing in my head! But what of Raneleg? You found his sword, but no sign of the man himself?'\
\
You tell Linadar that the sword was stuck blade-first in the mud, as if Raneleg dropped it from a height as he was carried aloft by some flying creature. Linadar's eyes are saucers, wide with horror.\
\
'I... I cannot stay here, ${PLAYER}! I cannot abide this swamp for a single moment longer! I did not think myself a coward, but who could remain in this land and keep his wits? Let the shame follow me back to Gondor! I care not! At the least I will keep my life!\
\
'Please help me back to the Gate, ${PLAYER}! I cannot bear to go alone!'","The creatures of Agarnaith seem to draw strength from the foetid air, and you must oppose them for the good of those who adventure in the marsh.","Search for Arodrog just south of the eastern road","Talk to Mithrandir in Cirith Gorgor, inside the Black Gate","Bring Raneleg's sword to Linadar in Agarnaith","Chapter 3.4: A Change of Heart","'It is a pity that I will be unable to accompany you to the Bloody Gore. Perhaps another time.'","'Please help me back to the Gate, ${PLAYER}! I cannot bear to go alone!'","Ayorzén the Wily is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","Raneleg and Arodrog ran into trouble off the road to the north and south, and Linadar has asked you to learn if they yet live.","Talk to Linadar on the road in Agarnaith","'Have you come to aid us, ${PLAYER}? This swamp is a place of horror, and there are too few of us to feel secure within it, but having you here will be a great help! Arodrog planned to rejoin us shortly, but he has not yet arrived.\
\
'Keep an eye on your surroundings as you adventure within the marsh. Dangers could lurk anywhere: in the water, up among the trees, within the twisted grasses. This is a foul place. The air smells foul and tastes worse.\
\
'The creatures here don't seem to mind it. Indeed, it seems to lend them a curious strength! Test your mettle against them, and Linadar and I will meet you further south along the road.'","Talk to the adventurer you found inside Agarnaith","Linadar made it to the meeting location, but where is the other adventurer?","'This is a terrible place! I do not like it! Why did we ever come here?'","Arodrog's body lies in the muck","'Can you search for Raneleg, at least? And mayhap see if Arodrog survived his wound? I cannot imagine that he did, but if there is a chance that he lives we should not abandon him! My courage is spent! What good is a man of Gondor who runs from peril? And yet there is peril all around us in this horrible swamp!'","'I hate this place, I hate it!'","'We should never have come here, ${PLAYER}, we should never have come! This place is not fit for good folk! It hates us, and will strive evermore until we are slain, and the marsh will never give back our bodies... it will jealously drag us down beneath the surface and never let us go!\
\
'Arodrog was slain by a terrible creature to the south, not far from here, and Raneleg is missing and nowhere to be found! I ran, to my shame, but shameful or not I am still here and they are not!\
\
'Can you search for Raneleg, at least? And mayhap see if Arodrog survived his wound? I cannot imagine that he did, but if there is a chance that he lives we should not abandon him! My courage is spent! What good is a man of Gondor who runs from peril? And yet there is peril all around us in this horrible swamp!'","Only Linadar met up with you at the arranged meeting place in Agarnaith.","Gain entrance to Agarnaith from the north","Linadar is so shaken that you agree to see him safely out of Mordor","'You have not sought my help in some time, ${PLAYER}. I was beginning to think you had fallen into a hole, or blundered into the fire-lake, or forgotten the way back here. What is it you want?'\
\
You tell Ayorzén that you need his help on the next leg of your journey, and ask him to accompany you to Agarnaith. A sudden look of panic crosses his face, but it passes just as quickly. When next he speaks, his voice is loud and confident, and no sign of his seeming fright remains.\
\
'I have come to a decision, my friend! I will be happy to accept your previous and very generous offer of a place in Gondor! Your forgiveness and acceptance of Ayorzén the Changed will become a thing of legend, ${PLAYER}, and will be spoken of for centuries as an example to all!\
\
'I will let the waggon-driver know. Sadly, I will be unable to accompany you to the Bloody Gore. Perhaps another time.'","Gain entrance to Agarnaith from the south","'Enemies lurk everywhere in the swamp, and they can ensnare you even before you know they are there! They are such horrors as I have never seen before!\
\
'If the tales I have heard of you are true, you should be able to best even them, ${PLAYER}... I hope it is so! Defeat any you can, and I will meet you further north along the road.'","Mithrandir is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","'I do not like our Easterling's silence on this matter. You must go to Agarnaith and learn what transpires within, but do not go alone! I believe you should bring Ayorzén with you, and find out what he knows about the Bloody Gore.'","Learn the fate of Raneleg","Raneleg is gone, but his sword remains: sticking straight up in the mud","You found the adventurers that entered Agarnaith from the southern approach","'Are you here to help us, ${PLAYER}? Did Mithrandir send you to us? Only a Wizard could know the trouble we have been in ever since we arrived, and send aid such as you in time! Raneleg planned to rejoin us soon, but he has not yet found us.\
\
'Enemies lurk everywhere in the swamp, and they can ensnare you even before you know they are there! I have never seen horrors such as these before, and I am no stranger to bogs unpleasant and mires malicious!\
\
'If the tales I have heard of you are true, you should be able to best even the foes that stalk this swamp, ${PLAYER}... I hope it is so! Defeat any you can, and Linadar and I will meet you further north along the road, not far from where the eastern road runs away into the swamp.'","'This is a terrible place! Why did we ever come here?'","Arodrog has succumbed to his wounds. He is dead","Meet up with the adventurers near the junction with the eastern road, in Agarnaith","Did the sword fall from Raneleg's hand as he was borne aloft?","'Well, what did you learn of Agarnaith? Are the rumours true? Many are the explorers who have returned from that land shaken, robbed of their courage.'\
\
You recount what you beheld of the festering swampland, and the Wizard is most interested to hear of the vile creatures that you encountered.\
\
'I am made uncomfortable by your description of these beasts, ${PLAYER}. That they suffer from some malady is clear, but there are one or two points about which I desire clarification. Something affects the creatures within Agarnaith, and it is no natural rot. It lurks in the air and the water of that land, a pestilence affecting the animals and the plants of the Bloody Gore. I must return to Minas Tirith to conduct my study, and I ask that you come with me.'"},
[3089]={"Travel through Calembel in King's Gondor","Travel through Dínadab in King's Gondor","'I have said what I can. At least the King will take the time to prepare before he comes within reach of the Corsairs that pillage Anfalas.'","Your companions look to the summit of the Hill of Erech","Lothgobel has not yet fully recovered from its scars","Hearing about Corsair activity along the coast of Anfalas, King Elessar is more determined than ever that his journey across Gondor should continue.","King Elessar is in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor.","Talk to King Elessar in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor","'The Hill of Erech. We have seen it before, but in different circumstance.'","'If I cannot convince you not to travel to Anfalas while it remains threatened by Corsairs of unknown loyalties, my King, I beg that you will consider delaying long enough to prepare for the journey. The store-houses and armouries of Dol Amroth are yours to make use of as you will. Take the time to prepare, for I will not have it said that I sent you on to the outer fiefs without adequate supplies or warning!'","King Elessar suggested that you travel to the Hill of Erech in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor.","'Whichever road you choose, your destination will be easily seen from afar: the Hill of Erech towers above the Blackroot Vale.'","Chapter 3.4: A Choice of Road","The folk of Dínadab seek to restore their peaceful lives","Calembel seems to have achieved a measure of peace after the war","'You will go to Blackroot Vale, ${PLAYER}? With you I send Legolas, Gimli, and my scribe Caebar. There are two roads by which you may reach the Vale, but I leave to you the choice of which to take: the shorter but more dangerous road through Tarlang's Crown, or the longer but safer road through Lamedon to the east, through Calembel, Lothgobel, and Dínadab. Whichever road you choose, your destination will be easily seen from afar: the Hill of Erech towers above the Blackroot Vale.'","'I understand Prince Imrahil's concerns. Let this, then, be the compromise.\
\
'I will remain for a few days' time in Dol Amroth, preparing to travel to Anfalas, but some of the company will instead journey north to the Blackroot Vale. The people there, and their lord Duinhir, lost much in the defence of Gondor. After the folk of the Vale have had some of their needs met and their concerns heard, this smaller group will rejoin the larger travelling party outside Anfalas, and we will together visit the Langstrand.\
\
'You will go to Blackroot Vale, ${PLAYER}? With you I send Legolas, Gimli, and my scribe Caebar. There are two roads by which you may reach the Vale, but I leave to you the choice of which to take: the shorter but more dangerous road through Tarlang's Crown, or the longer but safer road through Lamedon to the east, through Calembel, Lothgobel, and Dínadab. Whichever road you choose, your destination will be easily seen from afar: the Hill of Erech towers above the Blackroot Vale.'","Legolas stands at the base of the Hill of Erech.","Travel to the base of the Hill of Erech in the Blackroot Vale, King's Gondor","Travel through Lothgobel in King's Gondor","Defeated enemies in western King's Gondor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","King Elessar has given you a choice of road north into the Blackroot Vale: either to fight your way through Tarlang's Crown, or to take the longer, safer road through Lamedon.","Defeat enemies in Lamedon and Blackroot Vale, King's Gondor West (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Legolas at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor"},
[3090]={"Talk to Venko on the grassy slope east of Sundergrót","'Stand with me, ${PLAYER}, and together we will answer all our foes! Let them fear my blade, and I will sharpen it on their hides!'","Glóin is at Sundergrót, waiting to discuss your companions' exploits at Sundergrót.","Collected weapons at Sundergrót (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Very good, my friend, very good! If the goblins of Gundabad put up as little fight as those of Sundergrót, the Zhélruka will have the home that was promised to them before the week is out! And my sword-arm has grown even stronger with the practice!'\
\
<u>Venko, Zhélruka Home-seeker</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Axe-wielding:</rgb> 60\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Sword-wielding:</rgb> <rgb=#00FF00>76</rgb>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 80\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Resolve:</rgb> 80\
\
'Gorgar the Ruthless is less than nothing to me, and soon he will be just a memory. If Prince Ingór commanded me to face him in a duel of swords, I would do so, and gladly! I would do so even if it was to be a contest of axes, should my prince command it.'","'Your friend Glóin told me one of his ravens escaped the arrows of the Orcs, and bore away his message. If that is true, your dwarves will soon march upon the very gates of Gundabad, there to face Gorgar the Ruthless. I wish you good fortune. You have proven to possess a more caring heart than I expected, and I do not wish for you to needlessly throw your life away on a doomed errand.\
\
'And yet, I too have some training in appraisal: your own hardiness and resolve are not to be underestimated! Perhaps you will yet see victory at Gundabad, ${PLAYER}!'","Defeat goblins at Sundergrót (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I would like for us to climb to the summit, ${PLAYER}. High above Sundergrót is a place of great interest for the Longbeards, and while we are here I would like to see it.'","Defeated goblins at Sundergrót (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Venko south of the gorge of Sundergrót","Talk to Glóin and climb with him to High Sundergrót","Talk to Durin along the road between the Wells of Langflood and Elderslade","'Our companions counselled that we travel to the gorge of Sundergrót to hone our skills. Will you join us? The assault on Gundabad will sorely test us, and each of us had best be prepared for the trials ahead!'","'Ah! It feels good to fight again! I may be old, but I can still go axe-to-skull with the common goblin of the mountains, and three of his friends!'\
\
Glóin's brow furrows with thought.\
\
'Do goblins have friends? Better to say allies, perhaps, for I have seen little proof of friendship among Azog's kind or his descendants. Then again, my axe does the talking for me, and he is a sharp conversationalist: swift and pointed with every argument!'\
\
<u>Glóin, Hero of the Lonely Mountain</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Axe-wielding:</rgb> <rgb=#00FF00>81</rgb>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Fire-making:</rgb> 95\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 90\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Resolve:</rgb> 85\
\
'Oh, that was a good one! I will have to remember that, and tell Gimli when next I see him! But listen to me, ${PLAYER}. Now that we have gotten some exercise, I think there is something we should do while we are here at Sundergrót.'","The sound of goblin-cries echoes among the crags near Sundergrót","Glóin is outside the lodge in Limlók.","One of the messenger-ravens bore Glóin's warning to Skarháld, and now the dwarves wish to exercise their skills in preparation for the battles to come.","'I would choose a contest of swords over one of axes, if I have any say in the matter. But I will do as Prince Ingór commands, of course.'","Talk to Glóin outside the lodge in Limlók","Talk to Imák beyond the bridge of Skerabrygg","'It seems fortune is with us, my friend! The journey was uneventful. And yet we cannot rest, for war and danger lies ahead of us!\
\
'But do not worry: victory and triumph lies that way too.'","'Do you smell that? Ah, the goblins have attempted to reinforce the gorge since they were last opposed in this land, ${PLAYER}. They cannot evade my nose, no matter how they try to cover their foul scent!'\
\
<u>Imák, Stout-axe Survivor of Mordor</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Perception (Smell):</rgb> <rgb=#00FF00>91</rgb>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Trap Construction:</rgb> 80\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 95\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Resolve:</rgb> 90\
\
'I feel more accomplished already! This sojourn to Sundergrót has proven fruitful already!'","Venko is south of the gorge of Sundergrót, eager to discuss his combat training.","'One of my ravens escaped the arrows of the Orc archers, and even now Telgja is winging to Skarháld to warn Durin about the new Lord of Gundabad. I do not think it will dissuade him. You heard the fire in his voice when he spoke before the Anvil of Winterstith! No Orc chieftain, not even the brother of Mazog, will keep Durin from seeking to reclaim Gundabad. But our message will still serve an important purpose, for he will not march blindly beneath the Three Peaks.\
\
'There is something else about which we should speak, ${PLAYER}. I was talking to Imák and Venko, and they are not yet ready to go their separate ways. They have decided to see what waits in Gundabad, and because of that they want to hone their skills. It seems your appraisals of them were not quite to their liking, and now they desire further training! To speak honestly, I too could use a bit of exercise.\
\
'Our companions counselled we travel to the gorge of Sundergrót to hone our skills. Will you join us? The assault on Gundabad will sorely test us, and each of us had best be prepared for the trials ahead!'","Sundergrót is far to the west of Limlók, and your companions are interested in testing their skills among its rocky crags.","Chapter 3.4: Pilgrimage to Sundergrót","Glóin is interested in climbing to the summit above Sundergrót, and he waits for you to speak with him.","'I wish you good fortune in the mountains, ${PLAYER}.'","You have travelled with Durin to the road that enters Elderslade, where many of his dwarves have begun to prepare for their war on Gundabad.","Collect discarded weapons at Sundergrót (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Venko shouts in triumph and goes in search of more goblins","Meet up with Imák south of the gorge of Sundergrót","Talk to Glóin south of the gorge of Sundergrót"},
[3091]={"Examine the arrow embedded in the tree","'What is wrong with these people, ${PLAYER}? Do they not know we are here to help them? Do you think the Heirs of Castamir are to blame?'","Gimli stands at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor.","'You dare speak to me, after bringing such death to Morlad? I will not stand for this!'","Duinhir stands outside his home at the highest point of Morlad, in King's Gondor.","'I do not wish to climb this hill again, ${PLAYER}; the memory is grim. When last we stood atop the summit, a great host gathered about King Elessar. They were those who broke their oath to Isildur, and they came to his descendant that they might fulfil it, and have peace.\
\
'Many were the shades of dead Men that followed in our train when we departed Erech, and they were the fighters who wrested control of Pelargir for the Grey Host. Without this army of the Dead, we could not have seized the Corsair ships that bore us to the Harlond, and Minas Tirith.\
\
'The shades who gathered about King Elessar atop this Hill redeemed their oath, and recovered their honour. Should that make it pleasing to recall for we who were there? I do not believe it does. Speak with Caebar and Gimli, and afterwards we will proceed to Morlad on King Elessar's business.'","Inconvenienced Ruthless Dead in the Blackroot Vale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The memory of losses suffered during the War of the Ring remains to trouble the people of the Blackroot Vale.","You hear someone shouting for help from outside the entrance to Morlad","'Oh, am I glad to see you, ${PLAYER}! A gang of toughs surprised me a few minutes ago and I had to run and hide. What if they come back?'","'Do what you came here to do, then.'","Lady Rosfin looks at you with sad, cold eyes, and says nothing.","'I have told Rosfin over and over again that there was nothing I could do to save our sons, but she will not listen.'\
\
Duinhir lowers his voice so he can speak only to you, out of his wife's hearing.\
\
'Sometimes when I lie awake in the silent watches of the night, ${PLAYER}, I wonder if it is the truth I speak to my wife. I raised Duilin and Derufin to be bold and to be valiant, and they made me proud every day of their lives. But if I had raised them to be... less bold... to be less valiant...'\
\
Duinhir chokes on his words and stifles a sob, turning his back on Rosfin to hide his face.\
\
'Would my boys be alive today, ${PLAYER}, if I had not raised them to hold dear the same things as I? No, stop. Enough. You are here on the King's business. You are not here to listen to the ramblings of a sad old man. Speak to the people of Morlad. Do what you came to do.'","Talk to Gimli west of Morlad in King's Gondor","Legolas and Gimli stand at the ready to the west of Morlad.","Talk to Duinhir outside his home in Morlad, in King's Gondor","'Do what you came here to do.'","'Supporters of the Heirs of Castamir? No, I do not think they are responsible for this; not in the Blackroot Vale.'\
\
Duinhir looks directly into your eyes and holds your attention.\
\
'My people have suffered much, as have we all, and King Elessar did not take the time to visit Morlad himself. There is no conspiracy here, ${PLAYER}. The folk of the Vale grieve, and their grief has made them angry. I understand it, for I am angry too.'","'I've got nothing to say to you. Move along.'","'The King would expect us to slay any such members of the Ruthless Dead that we encounter in the Vale... or whatever passes for slaying such spirits. I am not entirely clear on that point. Legolas has tried to explain it to me, but it all seems rather complicated.\
\
'What do I know? I know that if any of the Ruthless Dead think to trouble us or the folk who live nearby, we will inconvenience them. We will inconvenience them with sword or bow or axe, and let them return if they dare!\
\
'They are sure to haunt the Hill of Erech at night, but they will be along the road to the Paths of the Dead at all times, I wager!'","Their oaths forever broken, the Ruthless Dead now haunt the Blackroot Vale with renewed hatred for the living. Gimli thinks you should inconvenience them, since he isn't certain they can be slain. Ruthless Dead can be found atop the Hill of Erech at night, and on the road to the Paths of the Dead at any time.","It is fortunate this arrow was not loosed with more skill","Talk to Legolas west of Morlad, in King's Gondor","Caebar is south-west of the entrance to Morlad, in King's Gondor.","Talk to Caebar at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor","'The shades who gathered about King Elessar atop this Hill redeemed their oath, and recovered their honour. Should that make it pleasing to recall for we who were there? I do not believe it does. Speak with Caebar and Gimli, and afterwards we will proceed to Morlad on King Elessar's business.'","Talk to Gimli at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor","Talk to the surly Morlad resident down the hill to the north","'We should now go to Morlad. That is the main settlement in the Blackroot Vale, is it not?'","Talk to Rosfin outside her home in Morlad, in King's Gondor","Talk to Duinhir in Morlad, in King's Gondor","'Oh, ${PLAYER}, a pall lies upon the Blackroot Vale, for it was caught in the grip of war, and all her young men were drawn away eastward. My sons, too, were caught in the whirlpool, and Duilin and Derufin will not come home again. My husband Duinhir thinks to spare me the details of what befell my boys... but there is evil in not knowing! If only I knew they perished quickly, and without pain...'\
\
Lady Rosfin entreats you through eyes filled with tears, but when you hesitate she looks away.\
\
'No, I will not ask it of you. I know Duinhir thinks to spare my feelings, the hard-headed man! I am stronger than he knows, and have always been so! It is not lost on me that he was not able to save our sons from death, he with his strong sword-arm and his thick shield, and I was forced to remain behind in Morlad; I, who might have been able to keep them safe!\
\
'Life can be cruel, ${PLAYER}, but it is crueller still for a mother in time of war. I keep thinking I will hear the sound of my sons boasting and laughing on the wind, and then I will see Duilin and Derufin climbing the path through the village, alive and well and happy. But it is not to be so.'","Chapter 3.5: Ruthless","Caebar thanks you and hurries away to safety","Duinhir stands by his wife Rosfin in Morlad, in King's Gondor.","Legolas and Gimli stand at the ready, their weapons drawn","'You are here on the King's business. You are not here to listen to the ramblings of a sad old man. Speak to the people of Morlad. Do what you came to do.'","'This story that Legolas and Gimli speak about... it fills me with fright, ${PLAYER}! I am gratified to learn that the King made use of the shades that betrayed his mighty forebear, and so gave them the redemption that was once denied them, but...'\
\
Caebar frowns deeply and casts nervous glances toward the summit of the Hill of Erech.\
\
'You say that some of the shades did not fight on behalf of the King? How ruthless must those dead Men now be, knowing there is to be no redemption for them? How much must they hate the living, now that the chance for peace has come and passed them by?\
\
'I do not want to go up there. King Elessar would understand if we do not, surely!'","Inconvenience Ruthless Dead in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find Legolas and Gimli to the west of Morlad in King's Gondor","Talk to Caebar south-west of the entrance to Morlad in King's Gondor","'I do not want to go up there. King Elessar would understand if we do not, surely!'","Caebar stands at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor.","'Someone loosed an arrow at me from hiding, ${PLAYER}. I am fortunate indeed that this is a town of Men and not of Elves, or it might have hit its mark.\
\
'These folk are not happy to see us.'","'I am not afraid, you understand, but there is little reason for us to climb again to the summit.\
\
'The King would expect us to slay any such members of the Ruthless Dead that we encounter in the Vale... or whatever passes for slaying such spirits. I am not entirely clear on that point. Legolas has tried to explain it to me, but it all seems rather complicated.\
\
'What do I know? I know that if any of the Ruthless Dead think to trouble us or the folk who live nearby, we will inconvenience them. We will inconvenience them with sword or bow or axe, and let them return if they dare!\
\
'They are sure to haunt the Hill of Erech at night, but they will be along the road to the Paths of the Dead at all times, I wager!'","Talk to the angry Morlad resident down the hill to the east","Rosfin, wife of Duinhir, stands outside their home at the highest point of Morlad, in King's Gondor.","Legolas and Gimli are to the west of the entrance to Morlad, in King's Gondor.","You should hear the concerns of the folk of Morlad, in King's Gondor."},
[3092]={"Chapter 3.5: The Song of Sweet Lara","Talk to Ayorzén at Cirith Gorgor, inside the Black Gate","Talk to Ayorzén on the parapet overlooking the city on the south-eastern side of the Fifth Circle","Find a scholar with kingsfoil to spare in the Houses of Lore","Mithrandir is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, just south of the entrance to the city.","'I hoped it was not so, but it is no longer safe to doubt, ${PLAYER}. Lhaereth the Stained has come to Mordor, and she has taken the fortress of Seregost for her own. For all of his bluster, I can see no reason for Ayorzén to lie to you about this.\
\
'More than a thousand years ago, Lhaereth created the Great Plague in service of Sauron. It was tested in the lands of the East, and then it was unleashed upon Gondor. But it was not yet perfected. The plague, while deadly, could be treated with athelas. Kingsfoil slowed its progress, and aided with the defeat of the disease.\
\
'Now Lhaereth has returned, and she is trying to finish her master work. Within the fortress of Seregost she seeks to create a strain of the plague that cannot be cured with athelas. She seeks to perfect the Great Plague.'","'You are ready? Then we will depart for the city.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'Go to the Houses of Lore on the southern side of the Fifth Circle and look for any scrolls or tomes that concern the Great Plague that so troubled Gondor earlier in the Age. Ask a scholar there for some kingsfoil, if any can be spared. They have found it lately of use, but they still should have some to give to you.\
\
'Once you have done this, you should see if Ayorzén has anything else to say to us concerning this matter. Whether he can be trusted or no, he seems more willing to speak to you than to any other.'","'At last we have arrived. I am accustomed to haste, and Rathnor's horses were incapable of anything faster than a slow trot! Shadowfax might have done that in his sleep, but I did not wish to leave you behind. I have need of you now, and it would not do to arrive quickly and then wait for you to report at Rathnor's leisurely pace!\
\
'Ayorzén has given us little reason to trust him, ${PLAYER}, but your account of Agarnaith confirms some of my suspicions. The remainder require corroboration by other sources, but these can be found in the city.\
\
'Go to the Houses of Lore on the southern side of the Fifth Circle and look for any scrolls or tomes that concern the Great Plague that so troubled Gondor earlier in the Age. Ask a scholar there for some kingsfoil, as well, if any can be spared. They have found it lately of use, but they still should have some to give to you.\
\
'Once you have done this, you should see if Ayorzén has anything else to say to us concerning this matter. Whether he can be trusted or no, he seems more willing to speak to you than to any other.'","Bring the kingsfoil to Mithrandir in the First Circle, south of the entrance to the city","'${PLAYER}! It is good to see you again, safe and sound! Did you tire of danger already? Well, what is it that brings you to the Houses of Lore? I am ready and available to help you with whatever you might need!\
\
'Kingsfoil? Yes, I do have some here. It's very useful for treating headaches and other minor maladies. Has prolonged exposure to the foul air of Gorgoroth been giving you headaches? I am sorry to hear that, but perhaps this will help!'","'I await the ride to the city with interest, my friend. You will arrange passage with the waggon-driver?'","Mithrandir desires to return to Minas Tirith and spend some time studying one or two matters that trouble him concerning the state of Agarnaith.","A book concerning the Great Plague and a scholar willing to part with kingsfoil must both be found within the Houses of Lore, on the southern side of the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith.","The waggon-driver Rathnor can be found near the Black Gate.","Talk to Rathnor the waggon-driver","Talk to Mithrandir in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, south of the entrance","'What does the Easterling have to say?'","Covadil gives you a small packet of kingsfoil and a smile","'I will be glad to have you on the waggon as we travel to the city, ${PLAYER}. I do not trust that Easterling, and I know some of the soldiers who will travel with us do not either.\
\
'Speak to me when you are ready to leave and we will depart.'","You learned that athelas was helpful for treating some victims of the Great Plague","'After you have visited the Houses of Lore, you should speak with the Easterling. He appears more willing to speak to you than any other.'","Ayorzén is on the parapet overlooking the city on the south-eastern side of the Fifth Circle, in Minas Tirith.","Ayorzén is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","Talk to Rathnor and travel to the city on his waggon","'I have never seen this city from the inside before. It is... it is quite a sight, ${PLAYER}. I believed that Sauron's armies were so near to victory, but now I am not certain. The city appears much stronger from up here.'\
\
Ayorzén stands silently, gazing out over Minas Tirith. When he speaks again, his voice is low and quiet.\
\
'I fought on the field down there. It is hard to tell, but I think I can see where my sworn men joined the battle. I slew many men myself, wielding swords, wielding axes. That is the way of war; if it was not to be their blood, it would have been mine. Eventually, things began to go wrong. Some of my sworn men were themselves slain. Others turned and ran.\
\
'I ran with them. Later, when we formed up again, word came down that some of the leaders were dead: the Lord of the Nazgûl, maybe others. And I thought to myself, \\qWhy should I die as well?\\q I thought to take my men and go home, leave the war behind... but I received new orders. I was to set an ambush for the force that had started to march in the direction of Mordor.\
\
'I left that task for the Orcs. I tried to lead my men home, and I was betrayed on the road. It was Ortakûl who betrayed me, the treacherous dog. He was rewarded with my command, and I was brought to Udûn, there to rot.'\
\
Ayorzén clenches his fist.\
\
'The Captain of the Pit, Ugrukhôr, did not plan to keep me there for long. He planned to send me to Agarnaith. Durthang was a nightmare, but it would be a pleasant daydream compared to that. Sweet Lara is there, ${PLAYER}. She is still there, and she is working on something behind the walls of Seregost. If you had not opened my cell, I would have been sent to Seregost, and death could not come quickly enough for Ayorzén the Unlucky.\
\
'Once Sweet Lara got her claws in me... once she made me drink of her concoctions, her vile potions... I do not think I would be Ayorzén anymore. So I... I thank you for freeing me, ${PLAYER}, if for nothing else.\
\
'Now that is done, and we will speak of it no more.'\
\
Ayorzén shakes his head abruptly and laughs.\
\
'Perhaps I was wrong! This city is not so strong after all. Do you see the cracks there, and there? Another hour or two, and Sauron would have had it quite in hand. You are lucky that his commanders were not as capable as I, Ayorzén the Strategic! You are lucky indeed in this, ${PLAYER}. So very lucky.'","'You are lucky to have a friend such as Ayorzén the Knowing, ${PLAYER}.'","'The creatures that walk in Agarnaith and the vegetation that grows there suffer from a rotting disease; worry has begun to gnaw at me concerning this disease. There are scrolls and tomes within Minas Tirith that may dispel my concerns. I hope they do. I will need your help, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The waggon-driver, Rathnor, prepares soon to leave. He will bring you to the city, with some others, and Shadowfax will bear me alongside.'","'You and the Wizard will be coming to the city as well? That is most fortuitous, ${PLAYER}. All know that Wizards are stand-offish sorts and do not make friends easily. He will be glad to have you there as we travel to the City of the Invaders.'\
\
Ayorzén looks at you slyly, and then he laughs.\
\
'Ah, you must pardon me, truly I am Ayorzén the Blunderer! I should not speak ill of the city, for it is so tall and only a small portion of it was damaged by the war. Only one third of it, yes? The battle would have had to last an hour or two more for the rest to be made to match!\
\
'I await the ride to the city with interest, my new friend.'","Find a book about the Great Plague in the Houses of Lore","This musty tome provides a dry account of the Great Plague that ravaged Gondor beginning in the year 1636 of the Third Age. The forgotten scholar that wrote these pages noted that the plague arose somewhere in the East and many of the folk there were consumed by the disease before it spread to the Northmen of Rhovanion.\
\
The account spends slightly longer detailing the effect of the Great Plague on the rule of Gondor, including the deaths of King Telemnar and all of his children, and the abandonment of Osgiliath for lack of men healthy enough to man its defences. The author of these pages mentions in passing that the watches at Minas Ithil, the Morannon, Ost Daethír, and Durthand were severely undermanned as a result of the disease, and you cannot help but wonder if he foresaw the problems that would cause in future days.\
\
The account further notes the discovery that the leaves of the athelas plant were found to have a beneficial effect upon the progression of the plague, and that the disease finally ran its course in Gondor by the year 1637."},
[3093]={"Stóthkell's good eye lights up with recognition as you approach","The war camp bustles with activity","The war-camp called Annâk-khurfu is north-west of the bridge between the Wells of Langflood and Elderslade, and serves as a gathering place for the arriving armies of dwarves.","Meet with dwarves on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu","Prince Ingór of the Zhélruka nods at your approach","'I commanded the establishment of a war camp from which we will launch our assault upon Gundabad. Let us find it! Many old dwarf-keeps dot the foothills of Elderslade, and my warriors are certain to have chosen one of these. I do not know which one, but I do know the name it will be given: Annâk-khurfu, the camp of return, for is this not the first step in the return of my people to the Mountain-home?\
\
'The war camp is likely to the north-west of here, inside one of the old dwarf-keeps.'","'So you made it,' Prince Ingór says flatly. He hefts his weapon, testing its balance, and stares at you silently for a moment. When he speaks again, there is an edge to his words.\
\
'Your deeds are well-known to all, even to the Zhélruka, and I do not doubt your mettle. But you are a friend of Durin and his Longbeards. Will you fight with such fervour on behalf of Zhélruka too? My brother Ótek is king now in the lands to the east, but he did not send me here to fight for Longbeards or their friends. He sent me here to reclaim the delvings that were promised to our ancestors of old.\
\
'If you will help me and my people in this, we will have no difficulty fighting by your side. If not...'\
\
The Zhélruka prince weighs his axe-handle thoughtfully, and turns away.","The war camp is bustling with dwarves preparing for their upcoming assault on Gundabad.\
\
You should speak to the dwarves assembled on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu.","The war camp is bustling with dwarves preparing for their upcoming assault on Gundabad.\
\
You should speak to the dwarves assembled on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","Great armies of dwarves have answered Durin's call, and they assemble in Elderslade in preparation for their assault upon Gundabad.","'Hail, my friend! Once again we are on the doorstep of danger! We last met in the cave of Filgogân outside the walls of Moria, and you helped me learn the fate of my friend Lofrik: dead, alas! But he is here too, in a way, for I embedded his golden tooth in the haft of my axe, as I promised to do.\
\
'Together Trausti and Lofrik will slay many Orcs on behalf of Prince Durin! Gundabad will be ours again!'","Chapter 3.5: The War Camp","'Look for the war camp, my friend. I commanded it be established within one of the abandoned keeps that dot the foothills of Elderslade, and it is likely to be found north-west of here.'","Durin is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu, addressing the assembled force of the dwarves.","'Find Annâk-khurfu and see the great host that musters for the assault on Gundabad, ${PLAYER}.'","Meet with dwarves on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","Thettmárr and Líkmund are playing a runic dice game and gambling","'I feared our paths would not cross again, friend! We have all come quite a distance from Hrimbarg!\
\
'Thorgest has recovered from his poisoned wound, but if you believed the experience would end his desire for adventure, well... you would be wrong! We received word that the son of King Thorin planned an assault upon Gundabad, and before you could say \\qhammers in the deep\\q Thorgest was on his way, and I behind him.\
\
'I have done what I can to provision the armies, but such a number of fighters threatens to overmatch my supplies! I will need to amass more goods and food if we are to keep this force in prime fighting shape. And not only that, but if I do not keep watch over Thorgest, who will? Every day brings with it a challenge that needs meeting, ${PLAYER}, as you well know.'","Thorgest and Afwald greet you warmly and ask for news of your adventures","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","'You still live, ${PLAYER}! I take it your adventures had you clear of Khazad-dûm before the great resurgence of creatures that pushed us out? Ah, if you had been there perhaps things would have been different. No, that is probably folly. The Orcs were there in numbers far greater than any I had ever seen before, and they were the vanguard only. Behind them were worse things, glimpsed fleetingly by the survivors. If any saw their full horror, those dwarves are dead. Aye, I can tell you that: the dead saw them, and I do not envy them the sight. It chills me to think of it even now, here by the heat of the forge!\
\
'There is no end to the work, my friend. I will continue to forge weapons for the Longbeards until my own furnace is extinguished, and I dare say that day is not yet upon us. And yet, this forge does not compare to the one I left behind in Khazad-dûm!\
\
'Ah, the Heart of Fire. No forge ever burned as brightly or as hot as those in the Heart of Fire! I miss them dearly. But I was not about to let the Orcs or their vile allies have access to those forges! I sealed the door before we fled for the surface. The Heart of Fire, at least, will remain unspoiled until the very end of the world. It makes me smile to think of it there, hidden beneath the mountains, locked behind a name no Orc will know. Perhaps it is the little things after all, ${PLAYER}.'","'Well if it isn't ${PLAYER}! Are you here to join Durin's great assault upon Gundabad? Perfect, perfect! Do you remember when we set afire to that goblin camp near the High Pass? Good times, my friend, great memories! I do not suppose you still have any of Gandalf's flammable draught with you, do you?\
\
'Ah, pity. We will just have to make do with what we can, and find new and interesting ways to burn up the schemes of Gundabad. I have no doubt we will think of something, my combustible friend!'","'So many have come to fight for us: Longbeards, Zhélruka, and even a number of Stout-axes! The Orcs who squat within Gundabad will tremble before this great force, this Gabil'akkâ! The Mountain-home is nearly ours again!'","The upper level is filled with dwarves preparing to undertake missions","'Welcome to Annâk-khurfu, ! This is not nearly so lonely an outpost as Hrimbarg, is it? So many doughty warriors have come to fight alongside Durin in his quest to reclaim Gundabad, many of them great heroes, but he will be most pleased that I and Afwald have made the journey!'\
\
Thorgest throws his head back and laughs, drawing attention from several nearby dwarves. When he has again collected himself, he wears a more solemn expression.\
\
'Ah, but I wish Thorkell was here. When we were just lads, we never suspected that Gundabad might one day be back in our grasp. And yet here I am, near to the doorstep, with one campaign left to fight before that happy day! But my brother is slain and will not see it. A pox on the worms of the Misty Mountains!\
\
'I am glad you are here, ! You will not believe me, but Afwald is always going on about you. \\qWhat do you think ${PLAYER:she[f]|he} is up to right now?\\q Afwald is always asking me. Well, now he can ask you himself, and not pester me with the question, day after day!'","'I am glad to see you are safe, ${PLAYER}. I was not in Khazad-dûm when the Iron Garrison fell, and it is hard to come by news of what happened within. I have heard enough to know it sounds bad.'\
\
Slagvi shakes his head.\
\
'I had gone back to the Iron Hills to collect some drawings I left in Járnfast. It is such a foolish reason! I wanted to compare the design of the Cooling Chamber with some plans I remembered drawing in my youth... and that is why I was not there when the Garrison failed. It may be why I am still alive today, and so many of the workers and miners with whom I toiled are not.\
\
'When I learned that Prince Durin was assembling a great force to reclaim Gundabad, I could not refuse his call. Is this why I was spared? Perhaps, friend, perhaps. But I am glad to know you are here too. We accomplished much in the Great Delving, ${PLAYER}... for a time.'","Enter the war camp of Annâk-khurfu in one of the old dwarf-keeps"},
[3094]={"'Go downstairs to greet our new arrivals, ${PLAYER}. All are welcome if it is in their hearts to hate Orcs, and I understand that these dwarves hate Orcs more than most!'","Bróin is just north of Annâk-khurfu.","'That is not good enough. I can wait,' Bróin insists","Bróin did not follow his cousin upstairs. Where did he go?\
\
Bori believes Bróin might be outside, just north of Annâk-khurfu.","Bróin stands alone, gazing into the distance","'I cannot hear you,' Bróin complains, arching an eyebrow","Talk to Bori on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu","Chapter 3.6: Survivors","Bróin is just north of Annâk-khurfu.\
\
Bróin has asked that you <rgb=#00FF00>agree</rgb> not to tell Durin about his worries.","Talk to Bróin on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu","'Bróin did not follow us upstairs? Where did he go?'","'Where is Bróin? Did he go back outside?'","'¿Si?'","'I do not want to disappoint King Thorin or his son. I hope I will not.'","'The leaders of the Iron Garrison will be a strong addition to the Gabil'akkâ as we begin our assault on Gundabad, but...\
\
'Can I ask you a question, ${PLAYER}? Do they seem in good spirits, despite the failure of the Iron Garrison to hold Moria? Do they still possess the courage I saw on their faces when they departed the Iron Hills on their expedition? Perhaps you can <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> them and learn if they possess the stomach for this endeavour.\
\
'I will await the results of your observation.'","'So the leaders of the Iron Garrison are prepared to fight again?'\
\
You tell Durin that Bósi's son Bori is particularly eager to see victory in Gundabad.\
\
'I am pleased to hear it, for I too am ready to reclaim the Mountain-home! Indeed, all Longbeards will rejoice to see it done! These new arrivals know a thing or two about war, and this is what I know: it will spell trouble for the Orcs!'","Bróin smiles nervously, and raises his axe in a pleased salute","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Bósi on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","Durin is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","'I am not surprised to see you here, ${PLAYER}, but it warms my heart all the same. I was at the Lonely Mountain when Durin sent word to his father that he intended to reclaim Gundabad from the Orcs, but I wanted no part of it. I feared to join him. No, not out of cowardice!'\
\
Bósi frowns unhappily.\
\
'I was tasked to secure Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}, but the Iron Garrison failed and my cousin Brogur was slain, along with many other good dwarves. How could I hold my head high after that? I feared my presence at Gundabad would bring nothing but ill fortune.\
\
'And yet... King Thorin deemed otherwise, and commanded me to join his son. So I am here. May things go otherwise in Gundabad than they did in Moria.'","Concerned about the dwarves of the Iron Garrison, Durin wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Bósi's mood and skills.\
\
Bósi has followed you to the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","Talk to Bróin just north of Annâk-khurfu","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Bróin outside Annâk-khurfu","Talk to Bósi on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu","<rgb=#00FF00>Agree</rgb> not to tell anyone of Bróin's worries","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Bori on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","'What thinks my son of this army Prince Durin has assembled?'","'My father has had a difficult time since the Iron Garrison was defeated in Moria, ${PLAYER}. I have told him repeatedly not to despair, but he pays me little heed. Did I despair at my imprisonment in Mirkwood, when the sorcerer Gorothúl held me captive within the dungeons of Dol Guldur?'\
\
Bori gives you a wry smile.\
\
'You are right: I did! But it turned out all right in the end, did it not? You saved my skin, and now both Gorothúl and his ally Mazog are slain. My point is this: do not close the book when things seem most drear, for it may be you are not at the end at all, but only the middle! The failure of the Iron Garrison is a tough defeat, but it may be the reclamation of Moria still lies ahead of us, and perhaps Gundabad will be the first step on that road.\
\
'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","Greet more arriving dwarves on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu","Bori is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You are a good friend.'","Talk to Bori on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","Bósi is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","Durin has asked you to greet the arriving dwarves on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu.","Dwarves of the Iron Garrison have come to Elderslade to join the great force preparing for the assault on Gundabad.","Talk to Bósi on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","More dwarves have come to Elderslade for the assault on Gundabad, and Durin is eager to welcome the new arrivals.","'I have just received word that more dwarves have arrived to swell my army's ranks! Go downstairs to greet them, ${PLAYER}. All are welcome if it is in their hearts to hate Orcs, and I understand that these dwarves hate Orcs more than most!'","Some familiar dwarves have arrived at Annâk-khurfu","'Hello, ${PLAYER}. I am here.\
\
'My father Brogur would have come to fight alongside Prince Durin, if he could. I am here in his stead, for he will never again leave Khazad-dûm.\
\
'I wish things were different.'","'Please, my friend, I beg you will tell no one of these worries. I bind you to secrecy on this matter. Will you do this? Will you <rgb=#00FF00>agree</rgb> not to tell Prince Durin of my mood or my fears? Please, ${PLAYER}.'","Concerned about the dwarves of the Iron Garrison, Durin wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Bróin's mood and skills.\
\
Bróin did not follow his cousin upstairs, and now he stands by himself outside Annâk-khurfu.","'I do not know what to do, my friend. I am consumed by a great sense of... I do not know how best to describe it.'\
\
<u>Bróin, Mazog's Executioner</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Axe-wielding:</rgb> 95\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Survival:</rgb> 85\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 65\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Resolve:</rgb> 15\
\
'I do not think I am ready for another war, ${PLAYER}. Yes: I say \\qanother.\\q Make no mistake: the Iron Garrison was at war in the depths of Moria, and it was a war we lost. Not only is that foothold gone, but so too are many of the brave warriors with which it was claimed in the first place. I mourn my father most of all, but Brogur was not the first good dwarf to perish within Moria, nor the last, though he may have been the bravest. He was bolder by far than his son, that much is certain!\
\
'Will I regain my courage before we pass through the gates of Gundabad? I survived my encounter with the Watcher in the Water within the Drowned Treasury, after all, and then I was alone, with only the dead for company. No, I was not entirely alone, for it was there I found Zigilburk, with which I kept the beast at bay. But the mithril axe is sealed away, never again to be wielded by anyone. It seemed the right choice then... but what if my courage was sealed away in the darkness with Zigilburk? Will I never find it again?\
\
'Please, my friend, I beg you will tell no one of these worries. I bind you to secrecy on this matter. Will you do this? Will you <rgb=#00FF00>agree</rgb> not to tell Prince Durin of my mood or my fears? Please, ${PLAYER}.'","'The Orcs of Gundabad will surely quake before this great army of dwarves!'\
\
<u>Bori, Survivor of Dol Guldur</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Axe-wielding:</rgb> 75\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Memory:</rgb> 90\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 75\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Resolve:</rgb> 90\
\
'Have you seen my cousin Bróin? I do not think he followed us upstairs.'","Find Bróin somewhere outside, just north of Annâk-khurfu","'Would you be willing to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> the leaders of the Iron Garrison and learn if they possess the stomach for this endeavour?\
\
'I will await the results of your observation.'","Concerned about the dwarves of the Iron Garrison, Durin wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Bori's mood and skills.\
\
Bori has followed you to the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","'Durin has gathered a mighty force with which to reclaim Gundabad. Will it be enough?'\
\
<u>Bósi, Leader of the Iron Garrison</u>\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Diplomacy:</rgb> 75\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Sagecraft:</rgb> 85\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 60\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Resolve:</rgb> 20\
\
'It will have to be enough, ${PLAYER}. It simply must.'"},
[3095]={"Talk to Harthalín just north of the eastward-running road in Agarnaith and collect samples (0/60)","Collected samples from animals in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'What did you find? That Orc carried a message?'\
\
Harthalín takes the crumpled parchment from you and quickly reads the message.\
\
'I do not like the sound of this, ${PLAYER}. A meeting of the Masters of Mordor can signal nothing but trouble and ill omen for us!'","Collected samples from plants in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'There you are, ${PLAYER}! Did you collect your samples? I have mine right here. But I need to tell you something.\
\
'Just before you returned, I saw movement in the brush over there. I recognized the shape of an Orc, and had pulled my bow-string taut before it could react. It's lying over there, in the water to the north-east. Go see if it lives!'","Chapter 3.6: The Next Great Plague","'We need to learn how near Lhaereth has gotten to achieving her goal. Return to Agarnaith and take samples of material from the animals, plants, and water of that land. You should retain the kingsfoil; combine it with the samples and see if there is any effect. We need not be overly concerned until the kingsfoil ceases to affect the disease, but by then it may be too late.\
\
'You know Harthalín. She intended to venture to Agarnaith. Look for her in the swamp and I am certain she will aid you in this.'","Bring the samples to Harthalín by the road in Agarnaith","Harthalín is by the eastward-running road in Agarnaith.","If Lhaereth the Stained is truly attempting to perfect the Great Plague, Mithrandir wants you to learn how far along she has gotten in the process.","'Your descriptions of Agarnaith tell me that Lhaereth's experiments have had an adverse effect upon her land. It may be that a study of the plants and creatures within it will shed light upon her progress, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'We need to learn how near Lhaereth has gotten to achieving her goal. Return to Agarnaith and take samples of material from the animals, plants, and water of that land. You should retain the kingsfoil; combine it with the samples and see if there is any effect. We need not be overly concerned until the kingsfoil ceases to affect the disease, but by then it may be too late. Sixty samples should be enough.\
\
'You know Harthalín. She intended to venture to Agarnaith. Look for her in the swamp north of the eastward-running road to Kala-gijak and I am certain she will aid you in this.'","'Mithrandir wants us to collect samples of flesh, and stem, and water from Agarnaith? How very unpleasant! I will aid you in this; we can each collect half of what Mithrandir wanted, and then we will meet back here.'","'Just before you returned, I saw movement in the brush. I recognized the shape of an Orc, and had pulled my bow-string taut before it could react. It's lying over there, in the water. Go see if it lives!'","Collect samples from animals in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","The Orc is dead. You remove a parchment from its hand","Harthalín is north of the eastward-running road in Agarnaith, on the way to Kala-gijak.","Harthalín shot an arrow at an Orc attempting to pass north-east of her location in Agarnaith. She wants you to see if it still lives.","Bring the parchment to Harthalín by the road in Agarnaith <rgb=#00FF00>(The parchment can be read from your inventory)</rgb>","Mithrandir asked you to collect samples from the plants, animals, and water in Agarnaith in order to determine the progress of Lhaereth's experiments.","Collect samples from plants in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Examine the Ghâsh-hai shot by Harthalín in Agarnaith, to the north-east","Collect samples of water in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected samples of water in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'This place is foul, and I would rather be anywhere else, but that is precisely why we need to watch this land. Mithrandir believes that the Bloody Gore will be the birthplace of the next Great Plague? If such a disease is to spring forth anew, it will be from here, ${PLAYER}! I mean, look around you!\
\
'Mithrandir wants us to collect samples of flesh, and stem, and water from Agarnaith? How very unpleasant! I will aid you in this; we can each collect half of what Mithrandir wanted, and then we will meet back here.'"},
[3096]={"The time has come for you to rejoin King Elessar on the road to Anfalas.","King Elessar and Queen Arwen greet you warmly as you approach","Chapter 3.6: Word of Their Lord","Talk to King Elessar on the road to Anfalas, in King's Gondor","Talk to Anoradan in Melgobas","'This is the road to Anfalas, ${PLAYER}, westernmost fief of my husband's kingdom. He has spoken to me of its ruler Golasgil, who marched to the defence of Minas Tirith with a number of soldiers and his household guard. He perished at the Battle of the Morannon, moments before the defeat of Sauron, and Elessar grieves that he sacrificed so much and never saw the victory for which he died.\
\
'I understand he asked you to bring to his people word of his bravery in the face of death?'","The town of Melgobas is to the west along the coast in Anfalas.","'I will go to the Blackroot Vale and hear Duinhir's concerns myself after we have returned from Anfalas.'","Anoradan is in the centre of the fishing village of Melgobas, in Anfalas.","'Thank you for going on my behalf to Morlad, ${PLAYER}! How fares the Lord of the Blackroot Vale and his wife and people?'\
\
You give your account of the grim sentiment that pervades the Vale, and the words of its ruler. Elessar nods.\
\
'Duinhir and Rosfin suffered much during the war, and the wound that is the loss of their sons can never truly be mended. I knew it was so, but I let my other concerns guide me and erred by sending you there. I should have gone as well, ${PLAYER}. On my return journey, after we see Anfalas, I will go to the Vale and speak with them personally.'","Travel south of the Blackroot Vale in King's Gondor, and rejoin Elessar on the road to Anfalas","'Golasgil asked you to bring word of his death to his people? If it will bring comfort to them, I encourage you to do this.'","'Who are these fine folk?'","You planned to rejoin King Elessar south of the Blackroot Vale in King's Gondor, on the road into Anfalas.","'I bid you farewell, then, and I will try to master my grief and that of my people. But King Elessar would do well to remember that not all the folk of Gondor are as stern or as cold as the Elves he loves, and if he does not take care his kingdom may slip away. And when it does, if it does, it may not be to the fires of the Corsairs but to the fury of his own people. You tell him that, ${PLAYER}. He has my loyalty, for I am sworn to Gondor, but these are true words I speak, and he would do well to heed them.'","Talk to Queen Arwen on the road to Anfalas, in King's Gondor","The smell of salt and the cries of gulls hang over the fishing village of Melgobas","Travel to the town of Melgobas, in Anfalas","'King Elessar would do well to remember that not all the folk of Gondor are as stern or as cold as the Elves he loves, and if he does not take care his kingdom may slip away. And when it does, if it does, it may not be to the fires of the Corsairs but to the fury of his own people. You tell him that, ${PLAYER}. He has my loyalty, for I am sworn to Gondor, but these are true words I speak, and he would do well to heed them.'","King Elessar is on the road to Anfalas, in King's Gondor."},
[3097]={"'You took care of the beasts that threaten Melgobas, lynx and Corsairs both? Perhaps the King and Queen knew what they were doing when they brought you with them to visit the Langstrand!\
\
'But there may be something more serious afoot than even those foes. A guard has come to Melgobas from Lond Cirion, and he looks worried. Perhaps he will share with a member of the King's travelling party what has brought him here?'","The people of Melgobas are endangered by more than just the Corsairs that drew the King to Anfalas.","Daeram is in the centre of the fishing village of Melgobas.","Talk to Anoradan in Melgobas","Defeated lynx near Melgobas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Are you here to help us? We could use assistance thinning the lynx and dealing with the Corsairs hereabouts, you know.'","Corsairs and lynx threaten the folk of Anfalas in the vicinity of Melgobas.","'The King and Queen have come to Anfalas? I never thought I would see such a day as this, for the Langstrand is so far from the White City and it seemed we were just as distant from their minds, if not further! It must be they were impressed by the swords and spears that Lord Golasgil brought to bear during the war. He is greatly missed.'\
\
You tell the man that Golasgil fought bravely on behalf of the King, and brought honour to Anfalas. He smiles and holds up a hand.\
\
'I rejoice to hear you say so, stranger, but it is unnecessary. His quality was well-known to his people, and though his son Orgolas is still young, there are none who doubt he will grow to be his father's equal. But do you bring pleasing words alone, or are you here to help us? We could use assistance thinning the lynx hereabouts, and the Corsairs have been even more of a problem of late.'","'You have come with the King's travelling party? If you have the trust of King Elessar, I suppose you have more than earned my own. I hope I do not step wrong by telling you this, or the Lady Marra will have my head.\
\
'I am seeking Orgolas, the young heir of Lord Golasgil. He has gone missing.'","Defeat Corsairs near Melgobas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Corsairs near Melgobas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Daeram in Melgobas","Chapter 3.7: The Cliffs of Langstrand","Defeat lynx near Melgobas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'There may be something more serious afoot than even such foes. A guard has come to Melgobas from Lond Cirion, and he looks worried. Perhaps he will share with a member of the King's travelling party what has brought him here?'","Anoradan is in the town of Melgobas."},
[3098]={"It is possible the tracks were left by a child's shoes, but it is hard to say","Daeram asked you to search for Orgolas along the beach to the south of Melgobas.","King Elessar kneels outside Barad Faen, studying the ground intently","'This is not the first time Orgolas has slipped his keepers' watch and escaped to tour the countryside, but with the Corsairs still harrying the coast... I need not tell you that once harmless excursions have become more dangerous than before.\
\
'Will you help me look for him? Search along the beach to the south and I will ask around the fishing village to learn if anyone has seen him of late.'","Chapter 3.8: The Missing Heir","Daeram says Barad Faen to the west is such a place","'Will you help me look for Orgolas, Golasgil's young heir? Search along the beach to the south of Melgobas and I will ask around the fishing village to learn if anyone has seen him of late.'","Search for Orgolas along the beach to the east","'I cannot return to Lond Cirion without him! Where can he have gone?'","King Elessar kneels outside Barad Faen, studying the ground. It seems the life of a Ranger can be hard to escape!","Meet up with King Elessar outside Barad Faen, in Anfalas","There is no sign of Orgolas along the beach","Search for Orgolas atop Barad Faen","'What do you make of these tracks?'","'What do you want? I am not ready to return to Lond Cirion, and you cannot make me! I have not yet even seen any of the Corsair ships up close!'","'Aye, this is just the sort of place I expected.'","King Elessar stands in Melgobas, considering Orgolas's disappearance.","'You found no sign of the boy? No one around the village has seen him of late. I cannot return to Lond Cirion without him!'","Daeram is in the centre of the fishing village of Melgobas.","Search along the beach at the bottom of the steps in Melgobas","Daeram was sent from Lond Cirion to search for the missing heir of Anfalas.","Search for Orgolas further east along the beach","Talk to King Elessar in Melgobas","'Will you help me look for Orgolas, Golasgil's young heir? Search along the beach to the south and I will ask around the fishing village to learn if anyone has seen him of late.'","'Is there a tall watch-tower of some sort along the coast? Golasgil's heir might have climbed such a tower in order to get a better view of the Corsair ships out in the bay. Such a sight might be difficult for a young boy to refuse, if my own childhood is to be any indication!'","'Aye, this is just the sort of place I expected. What do you make of these tracks, ${PLAYER}?'","There is no sign of Orgolas here either","King Elessar steps forward to speak","King Elessar has found tracks of some sort outside Barad Faen.","Talk to King Elessar outside Barad Faen","There is no sign of Orgolas here","Barad Faen is west of Melgobas, in Anfalas.","'I believe we will find our quarry atop Barad Faen, ${PLAYER}.'","Tracks indicate Orgolas might have climbed Barad Faen.","Daeram asked you to search for Orgolas along the beach to the south, down below the fishing village of Melgobas.","Examine the tracks outside Barad Faen","'Do not despair before there is need, my friend. We have seen no sign of Orgolas, but neither is there evidence that he ran afoul of danger.'\
\
Elessar strokes his chin and gazes out over the waves.\
\
'Is there a tall watch-tower of some sort along the coast? Golasgil's heir might have climbed such a tower in order to get a better view of the Corsair ships out in the bay. Such a sight might be difficult for a young boy to refuse, if my own childhood is to be any indication!'","Talk to Daeram in Melgobas","Daeram asked you to search for Orgolas along the beach to the south."},
[3099]={"Find a guardsman on the bridge north-west of Lond Cirion","Find Orgolas by the docks of Lond Cirion","'Ho there, ${PLAYER}! I come here often to watch the soldiers training! One day I hope to have as much martial prowess as they do! I will be as good a fighter as my father was. Nay, I shall be even better!\
\
'Mother says the war is over, but Aerhant showed me a ship far off in the bay that must have been full of Corsairs sailing from Umbar. I hope they are not all dealt with before I have finished my sword-training!'","'Master Orgolas is very excited, but you and the King should make yourselves known first to the Lady Marra. It would be proper.\
\
'She will be inside the hall.'","Find the main hall of Lond Cirion","'Wait... who is that man? Is he... King Elessar? My mother brought me to the King's wedding this summer, but I only saw him from afar, and we did not stay long. Can he really have come to Anfalas?'\
\
You tell Orgolas that Elessar joined the search to find him, and the boy's eyes widen in amazement.\
\
'Truthfully? He came here to seek me? I cannot believe it! I simply must show him to my home! Yes, I will return to Lond Cirion, and at once! King Elessar! Mother will be so surprised!'","'This way, my King! My home is to the west!'","Orgolas watches the soldiers training with sword and with bow","Chapter 3.9: Orgolas","King Elessar is in the main hall of Lond Cirion, speaking with Lady Marra.","'I simply must show King Elessar to my home! Yes, I will return to Lond Cirion, and at once! The King of Gondor! Mother will be so surprised!'","'I saw you and King Elessar when you arrived at Lond Cirion in the company of young master Orgolas. He is a frequent visitor to this bridge, and often wants news from me concerning distant lands.\
\
'The news is poor, of late. Corsair ships are often seen along the coast, and they endanger the fisherfolk and peasantry of Anfalas. Do they not know the war is over?'","The bridge offers a breathtaking view of the water","Talk to Orgolas at the entrance to Lond Cirion","Find the Lond Cirion library inside the keep","'Lead on, young master Orgolas. ${PLAYER} and I will follow you to Lond Cirion.\
\
'It is located to the west, ${PLAYER}, and was named Ciryalondë by the Men of Númenor who settled there during the Second Age. It is the oldest Númenórean settlement in Gondor, but its original name fell out of use and now it is Lond Cirion. It was Golasgil's ruling seat, and now his widow Marra holds it until their son comes of age.'","Marra suggested you become familiar with the layout of Lond Cirion and those who reside there.","Talk to King Elessar in the main hall of Lond Cirion","Talk to Coruchon in the library of Lond Cirion","'The Lady Marra and I have come to an understanding, ${PLAYER}, and she knows we did as much for her husband as we could, and mourn with her that it was not enough. She has my promise that we will work to defend her people, as Golasgil desired.'","'You and your travelling party are welcome to Lond Cirion, King Elessar, and all of you will enjoy the hospitality of my house. Please feel free to explore the Anfalas as you wish, but know that the Corsairs of Umbar trouble the long shore, even despite the war's ending; my guards cannot ensure your safety if you stray near the coast.\
\
'But I understand this ${RACE} was present when my husband fell? Would you... would you speak to me of what befell my dear Golasgil in the King's service?'\
\
You speak of Golasgil's bravery before the Black Gate of Mordor, and that you repaid with death the great Olog that gave him his mortal wound, moments before the defeat of the Dark Lord Sauron. Marra's eyes brim with tears, but she wipes them away with her sleeve and her expression hardens.\
\
'So near to the end, then? I worried it might have been so. What need was there for my husband to die, if the Men of the West were so near to their victory? My Golasgil had not the attention of Sauron; he was but one man among hundreds. Whose sword-arm failed to slay the Olog that killed my husband before it could reach him, ${PLAYER}? Was it yours? Was it the King's?\
\
'You may leave me, ${PLAYER}. I have words to speak to Elessar, but they are not for your hearing. See the comforts of Lond Cirion, and know that Golasgil will not enjoy them again.'","Lady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.","'Here we are! Now, you've probably seen impressive places on your journey across Gondor, and Minas Tirith is of course very large... but my teachers say that Lond Cirion is older than all of them! Let me show you around, King Elessar!'","Lond Cirion is to the west of Barad Faen.","Talk to King Elessar at Barad Faen","The library of Lond Cirion smells of dust and candle wax","Talk to Marra in the main hall of Lond Cirion","'You may see the rooms of Lond Cirion and meet its people while I speak with the King. I have much to say to him.'","'Daeram always spoils my fun. That is the duty with which my mother always charges him, anyway!'","The main hall of Lond Cirion is located just inside the entrance to the keep.","Talk to Orgolas by the docks","The Lady Marra motions for you to come forward","Talk to Aerhant on the bridge to the north-west of Lond Cirion","Travel to the entrance of Lond Cirion","Daeram clears his throat and calls for your attention","Orgolas is at the entrance of Lond Cirion, in Anfalas.","You have found Orgolas, the son of Golasgil and heir to Anfalas. The question now is what should be done with him?","'The King has come here to resolve the line of succession, hasn't he? Golasgil's heir is too young to rule, and has ceded some of his authority to his mother Marra, but there are some in Lond Cirion and elsewhere who believe she is not fit to govern in these trying times, and she still in mourning.\
\
'There is another matter of some curiosity, stranger. It is known that before he departed for the war, Golasgil prepared a parchment containing his last wishes... but it cannot be found. I have spoken with Marra about this, and she brushes away my questioning. There is something untoward going on. You should tell the King, for the safety of Anfalas is affected, and that imperils the kingdom.'","Daeram is at the entrance to Lond Cirion, in Anfalas.","'Lond Cirion is located to the west, ${PLAYER}, and was named Ciryalondë by the Men of Númenor who settled there during the Second Age. It is the oldest Númenórean settlement in Gondor, but its original name fell out of use and now it is Lond Cirion. It was Golasgil's ruling seat, and now his widow Marra holds it until their son comes of age.'","Orgolas leaps around excitedly","King Elessar stands by Orgolas, at Barad Faen.","Talk to Daeram at the entrance to Lond Cirion"},
[3100]={"'Come, I will lead you to the Lady in her garden.'","Orophin will take you from the Lothlórien Court to see Lady Galadriel in her garden.","Lady Galadriel wishes to speak to you.","'It is time you returned to Lothlórien, friend. I have received word that Lady Galadriel wishes to speak to you. You should return to her court as soon as you are able.'","Habla con Legolas.","Talk to Orophin in the Court of Lothlórien","'You seem shaken, friend. Are you well?'\
\
Legolas gazes into your face and seems to understand something.\
\
'I too have spent a moment with the Lady in her garden and seen the others of The Company do the same. I have some inkling of your mind, perhaps! Best, I think, to let it pass. Let us return to Mordor. Let action replace reflection for a time!'","Chapter 3: A Faltering Reflection","Legolas wishes to talk with you in the Court of Lothlórien.","'It is good you are here, ${CLASS}. The Lady Galadriel wished to see you as soon as you arrived. Orophin, would you lead our friend to her Ladyship?'"},
[3101]={"Destruye el regalo de Gorothúl en Lumul-nar","Una ola de temor te recorre mientras la reliquia es destruida, luego desaparece.","'¡Lo sabía, ${PLAYER}! Sabía que encontrarías la reliquia de Gorothúl en Lumul-nar. Es bueno que la hayas destruido. Deberíamos ser capaces de mantener a raya a los merrevail; si la reliquia hubiera atraído a Grawulun u otro Caerog a Lumul-nar, nuestro éxito podría no ser tan seguro.'","Habla con Bróin en la Senda Pacífica","La entrada a las Salas de los Espejos de Lumul-nar está afuera, en el lado de Zirakzigil cerca del cráter arruinado donde yace el Balrog aún humeante.\
\
Bróin cree que una de las reliquias que Gorothúl dejó en Moria fue dada a los merrevail que infestan las Salas de los Espejos de Lumul-nar y quiere que la destruyas.","Bróin está en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada entre Zirakzigil y el Camino de Durin.\
\
Has destruido la reliquia que Gorothúl dio a los merrevail en Lumul-nar y ahora deberías regresar con Bróin.","Capítulo 3: Una reliquia en Lumul-nar (Grupo)","'La entrada a las Salas de los Espejos de Lumul-nar está afuera, en el lado de Zirakzigil cerca del cráter humeante. Lleva contigo una pequeña comunidad de aliados, ya que los merrevail en Lumul-nar son enemigos peligrosos.'","'Ahora que Orvar ha destruido la reliquia oculta que Gorothúl dejó en Buzun-ghâr, esa cueva debería estar libre de peligro. No tenemos que temer que Grawulun u otros de su clase regresen a ese lugar.\
\
'Pero Gorothúl puede haber dejado otras reliquias de maldad por toda Moria; de hecho, creo que es probable, y los informes recientes de nuestros exploradores indican un lugar así: las salas de los espejos de Lumul-nar. Los merrevail han corrompido los espejos de Lumul-nar que una vez alimentaron la luz del exterior hacia las profundidades de Khazad-dûm; la luz ya no brilla. Un número de exploradores se aventuró a Lumul-nar para investigar. Pocos regresaron, informando que los merrevail de ese lugar han recibido gran valor; su desafío es fuerte. ¿Qué más les han dado, me pregunto? ¿Una reliquia de Gorothúl?\
\
'La entrada a Lumul-nar está en el lado de Zirakzigil, entre la nieve. Encuentra la reliquia dentro, si existe, y destrúyela. Lleva uno o dos aliados contigo, ${PLAYER}. ¡Se requerirá una pequeña comunidad de valientes para encontrar la malvada reliquia allí!'","Bróin cree que Gorothúl dio una reliquia maligna a los merrevail que infestan los Espejos de Lumul-nar."},
[3102]={"Habla con Bróin y viaja a las Salas de los Espejos de Lumul-nar","'¡Lo sabía, ${PLAYER}! Sabía que encontrarías la reliquia de Gorothúl en Lumul-nar. Es bueno que la hayas destruido. Deberíamos ser capaces de mantener a raya a los merrevail; si la reliquia hubiera atraído a Grawulun u otro Caerog a Lumul-nar, nuestro éxito podría no ser tan seguro.'","'Haré que un explorador te guíe hasta las Salas de los Espejos de Lumul-nar.'","La entrada a las Salas de los Espejos de Lumul-nar está afuera, en Zirakzigil, cerca del cráter en ruinas donde yace el Balrog humeante.\
\
Bróin cree que una de las reliquias que Gorothúl dejó en Moria fue dada a los merrevail que infestan las Salas de los Espejos de Lumul-nar y quiere que la destruyas.","Habla con Bróin en la Senda Pacífica","Bróin está en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada entre Zirakzigil y el Camino de Durin.\
\
Has destruido la reliquia que Gorothúl dio a los merrevail en Lumul-nar y ahora deberías regresar con Bróin.","'Ahora que Orvar ha destruido la reliquia oculta que Gorothúl dejó en Buzun-ghâr, esa cueva debería estar libre de peligro. No tenemos que temer que Grawulun u otros de su clase regresen a ese lugar.\
\
'Pero Gorothúl puede haber dejado otras reliquias de maldad por toda Moria; de hecho, creo que es probable, y los informes recientes de nuestros exploradores indican un lugar así: las salas de los espejos de Lumul-nar. Los merrevail han corrompido los espejos de Lumul-nar que una vez alimentaron la luz del exterior hacia las profundidades de Khazad-dûm; la luz ya no brilla. Un número de exploradores se aventuró a Lumul-nar para investigar. Pocos regresaron, informando que los merrevail de ese lugar han recibido gran valor; su desafío es fuerte. ¿Qué más les han dado, me pregunto? ¿Una reliquia de Gorothúl?\
\
'La entrada a Lumul-nar está afuera, en el lado de Zirakzigil cerca del cráter humeante. Encuentra la reliquia dentro, si existe, y destrúyela. ¡Lleva uno o dos aliados contigo, ${PLAYER}!'","Capítulo 3: Una reliquia en Lumul-nar (Solo)","Bróin cree que Gorothúl dio una reliquia de maldad a los merrevail que infestan los Espejos de Lumul-nar."},
[3103]={"'Hola, ${PLAYER}.'","'Gracias por traerme esto, ${PLAYER}, y también por tus esfuerzos en nuestro nombre. Nuestro trabajo aquí ha ido más lento de lo que esperábamos.\
\
'Mi primo Brogur y yo decidimos buscar a Balin dentro de Moria hace algunos meses, pero nos llevó muchas semanas reunir una expedición de enanos dispuestos a acompañarnos. Elegimos un camino tortuoso sobre las montañas para hablar con el señor Glóin, un amigo cercano de nuestros padres, sobre Khazad-dûm.\
\
'Sus palabras fueron sombrías; no creo que él crea que nuestra expedición tendrá éxito. 'Ha pasado demasiado tiempo sin noticias', nos dijo, 'para que Balin hijo de Fundin siga vivo dentro de las Minas'. Estoy empezando a percibir la probabilidad de su advertencia, ${PLAYER}.'","Lleva el informe de Tulk a Bósi","Tulk te ha pedido que lleves un informe a Bósi, el líder de la expedición de enanos. Los parientes de Bósi han venido a Acebeda con el propósito de entrar en Moria.","'He escrito un informe para que lo lleves a Bósi, ${PLAYER}. Muéstrale este documento y él decidirá la mejor manera de utilizar tu ayuda.\
\
'Encontrarás a Bósi cerca de algunos carros más allá del afloramiento rocoso al sureste. Solo sigue el camino mientras serpentea alrededor del afloramiento y gira al noreste.'","'Si sigues el camino al sureste mientras serpentea alrededor del afloramiento rocoso que ves allí, encontrarás a Bósi junto a los carros cuando el camino gire al noreste.\
\
'Llévale el informe que te di. Él encontrará algo para que hagas y así ayudar en nuestros esfuerzos aquí.'","'¿Cómo va el trabajo, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}?'","'Me pregunto qué nos espera dentro de Moria'","'Gracias por llevar mi informe a Bósi.'","Capítulo 3: Bósi el Enano","Bósi supervisa algunos carros a lo largo del camino a través de Acebeda, al sureste de la Puerta y luego girando al noreste.\
\
Tulk te ha dado un informe para que lo lleves a Bósi, uno de los enanos que lideran la expedición a Acebeda."},
[3104]={"Dáin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
After the defeat of Urro One-hand, the Iron-folk have arrived at Durin's Stone. You should talk to Dáin.","'Hermáth! I thought you were lost! Are you all right?'\
\
Dáin embraces you.\
\
'Grandfather Grór was right to sound his horn-call when he did! If we had waited any longer, I... no matter.'","Thromur can be found at Amdân.\
\
After repelling the Orcs at Kamaz-kala, you should find Thromur and investigate what kept him from joining the vanguard.","Ah, Hermáth! Though I tried to convince my father otherwise, he insisted on sending those messengers to find you.\
\
'While you were off aiding the others, there was a bit of tension in the vanguard. It seems King Thráin's son, Frerin, and his esquire had something of an argument, and he sent that dwarf back to Amdân on some errand. Before Thromur could return, Frerin had no choice but to set off with the vanguard. Thromur! That was the esquire's name!\
\
'Lord Grór has asked us to repel the Orcs at Kamaz-kala should we be needed in the dale, but once that is done, you should find out what has been keeping Thromur. He ought to hurry up or the battle will be over!'","Dáin can be found at Khur Azan.\
\
After arriving at Khur Azan, you have spotted your friend, Dáin. You should talk to Dáin.","An uneasy dwarf appears to be searching Amdân for something","Defeat Orcs at Kamaz-kala (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Orcs at Kamaz-kala (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","As you continue to read Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar, you begin the third chapter in which the Dwarves of the Haban’akkâ of Thráin press onward into the dale and the vanguard faces a grave setback.","The Iron-folk can be found at Khur Azan.\
\
You have returned to Khur Azan and should now muster to the Iron-folk waiting in reserve.","Chapter 3: Death in the Dale","'As King Thráin and his vanguard battled down the Great-way, we of the Iron-folk stood ready to answer the horn-calls of our brethren. None were more eager to join the fight than Náin Orcsfoe, but Grór forbade his son from following the vanguard to Khazad-dûm. With the Black Mattock in hand and his horn at his side, the Lord of the Iron Hills knew well his duty, but if news did not soon come of victory, he would sound the horn-call himself and send the full fury of the Iron-folk against Azog.\
\
'Alas, in the vanguard's wake, the Orcs had reassembled at Kamaz-kala and yet unknown troubles were stirring at Amdân.'","Talk to Dáin at Khur Azan","Talk to Dáin at Durin's Stone","Thromur can be found at Amdân.\
\
You have discovered a likely culprit in the theft of Urro's hand. You should aid Thromur.","Thromur can be found at Amdân.\
\
You have found Thromur and should aid him in completing his errand.","Talk to Thromur and forge 'Bonds of Oak and Iron'","Kamaz-kala can be found slightly north-west of Khur Azan at Azanulbizar.\
\
Lord Grór has asked the Iron-folk to repel the Orcs at Kamaz-kala should the battle need to be joined.","Among the many Iron-folk who have marched to Khur Azan, you spot Dáin","Find Thromur at Amdân","Muster to the Iron-folk at Khur Azan","Aid Thromur"},
[3105]={"'This is a welcome surprise, ${PLAYER}! I heard you had pledged to fight on behalf of Durin's folk, but I did not expect to see you within the Hall under the Mountain! I am here for only a short time, if King Thorin will favour my undertaking.\
\
'I await now his word. He has considered my proposal, and sits now in judgement of it.'","King Thorin beckons for you to approach","'Thank you for putting in that kind word for me, ${PLAYER}! Now we must assemble some dwarves who desire to help me establish a dwarf colony in the Glittering Caves. It is a long way from here, but I am certain there are many who are up to the task! Help me find these dwarves!'","Talk to Gimli in the throne room in the Hall under the Mountain","Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.","'You may help Gimli select the dwarves that will accompany him to the Glittering Caves, if you are of a mind to do so.'","Chapter 3: Gimli's Request","Find dwarves of Erebor willing to accompany Gimli to the Glittering Caves (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Dwarves pledged to Gimli for the expedition (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dwarves of Erebor that may wish to accompany Gimli to the Glittering Caves can be found throughout the Hall under the Mountain.","'I understand you know Gimli, son of Glóin? He has returned to Erebor after much time away, and is speaking with King Thorin.'","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain","Gimli, son of Glóin, has come to Erebor to speak with the King under the Mountain.","Go to Thorin's throne room in the Hall under the Mountain","Gimli beams with pride and accepts the task","'You have arrived at a useful time, ${PLAYER}, for I understand that you have stood in battle with Gimli and know somewhat of his character. Is he steadfast and loyal? Does he hold to his word?'\
\
You assure Thorin that Gimli is honourable to his friends and shows no mercy to his enemies.\
\
'That is good to hear, and it meets my own expectation. Glóin's son has requested permission to lead a company of dwarves far to the south, to a place he names the Glittering Caves, where he will establish a new dwarf colony. The tale he has told is one of great beauty, but even greater is the promise of the beauty he thinks to make there.\
\
'I have arrived at my decision. Gimli, son of Glóin, by my authority as King under the Mountain I give to you all rights necessary to establish your colony and to be named the Lord of the Glittering Caves, with all the responsibilities that entails. Work for the betterment of Durin's folk, and report to me of your progress. Take such dwarves with you as you deem necessary for the success of this endeavor.'","'I daresay it is time you reported once again to King Thorin about your adventures in Mordor. Tell him how things progress, and see if he has any further requests for you.'","'Thank you for your help finding dwarves willing to accompany me, my friend. I have found a number of willing allies as well, and together they have formed a good company. There are still many preparations to make, but the promise of the Glittering Caves has put a spring in my step and a fire in my heart!\
\
'We will make a great work there, and fashion the Glittering Caves into a wonder even more beautiful than it began! I thank you again for your words on my behalf. You will always be welcome at the Glittering Caves, once our work there is done! Take care in Mordor, my friend. It would be a terrible pity if you were slain before you beheld my masterwork, ${PLAYER}! Ha! Ha! Ha!'","Gimli is near the provisioner in the Hall under the Mountain, arranging for the things he will need on his expedition.","Talk to Gimli by the provisioner in the Hall under the Mountain","'I await now the word of the King under the Mountain. He has considered my proposal, and sits now in judgement of it.'","A familiar figure stands before the throne: Gimli, son of Glóin","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Durin's Folk and fight on their behalf in Mordor."},
[3106]={"Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 1 March 3019","<rgb=#FF00FF>Listen</rgb> to Saruman","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 9 August 3017","Saruman wishes only to seize power and rule of Mordor for his own","You discovered many more barrels of pipe-weed than Merry and Pippin had found, and packaged over the course of nearly two years, as well. You should return to Treebeard where he stands before the west face of Orthanc in Flooded Isengard.","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 25 June 3017","Habla con Merry","'MY VAST WISDOM HAS OTHER USES. I MIGHT TEACH IT, BRINGING WISDOM AND PROSPERITY TO THE FREE PEOPLES'","You should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion to learn what serious matters they have been discussing.","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 22 Sept 3017","'If you remember, the Ents are supposed to have kept watch on him up in his tower, where he is a prisoner of sorts. Perhaps you will see some of our Ent-friends when you are there. If you do, give them our regards and find out how they are doing for us. At this rate, it feels that it may be a long while before we might see them again.'","Treebeard and another Ent stand before Orthanc on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
You have heard Saruman's three pleas and seen through each ploy. Now you should return to Treebeard and see what he has to say.","Pippin and Merry have asked you to visit Flooded Isengard and look in after Saruman, the Ents, and anything that will reveal what the three half-orcs were talking about.","'FOOL! I WILL KEEP TO MY TOWER THEN AND THE REST OF YOU MAY ROT!'","Habla con Pippin","Consider the Free Peoples","You should return to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion with word of all that you have seen and heard.","'It is good you are here, just when we've wanted you, as usual, ${PLAYER}. We have some grave matters to discuss.'","'MORDOR IS UNTHRONED, YES? WHO BETTER THAN I KNOWS HOW TO CLEANSE IT OF THE SHADOW AND CORRUPTION GATHERED THERE?'","'FREE ME FROM THIS PRISON AND I WILL MAKE AMENDS TO FANGORN AND ROHAN. I SHALL HEAL, REGROW, AND REPAIR THE WRONGS DONE IN MY NAME.'","Consider dethroned Mordor","'Hrum, brum, hroom! You have not had such a courteous conversation with old Saruman after all, have you?'\
\
You tell Treebeard what Saruman said and what you judge he meant by it. The old Ent's eyes grow sad.\
\
'Yes, hrm. Well, hm. Perhaps letting him go just now would be a bit hasty, after all. I feel sorry for him at times, for I do not like to cage any creature of any temperament in stone as he is caged. And yet you have shown us that he is unbroken and might still try to do much harm if he were freed. \
\
'No, hm. I shall not release him. Not just now, at any rate.\
\
'I am delighted that you have paid us this visit all the same, ${PLAYER}, and you must send my regards to the halflings Pippin and Merry, and remind them that they are always welcome in my woods!'","'Hm, hoom! Here is ${PLAYER} again. Remarkable that you should show up just as we were discussing all the events that had led to this.'\
\
Treebeard indicated the flooded waste around them.\
\
'And what, really, should be done with Saruman. Oh, yes, I know, hm, hm, Mithrandir bade us keep him up there. And now that we have settled in, we are not in any mood to be hasty, hoom! But still the question remains, for how long? And by whose reckoning? A ${RACE}'s such as yours? That is a while, I suppose. It all, even the Elves', seems hasty to we Ents, and so we find it exceedingly difficult to judge. Hm, hm! And yet, all the same, I cannot help but feel it has been long enough and that we should release him.\
\
'But come, I am being most inhospitable. Tell me, what has brought you to us here today, hm?'\
\
You tell Treebeard the riddle of what you overheard in Mordor.\
\
'Saruman? It might very well be Saruman, hoom hom! He is hiding somewhere within his rock just now, but will be out upon that high place there very soon, I believe. Why don't you look around for anything else to explain this little mystery, until he is out, and then we shall see what we shall see.'","Saruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
Saruman has suggested that he could employ his vast wisdom to bring prosperity to the Free Peoples. You should consider how this possibility might turn out.","'How we would love to go with you and see old Treebeard and Quickbeam again. But that should require yet more leave from Lieges, and besides, we are much in demand among the Gondorian just now. It would be quite impossible!'","Return to Pippin and Merry","Habla con Bárbol","Find the other Ents","What Isengard was and the waste it has become swiftly dispel Saruman's lie","'The ${PLAYER} returns, and so soon! Hm, hm, but not too late, either, I think, for there is Saruman up high upon his tower. You have come all this way. Why not you go and see what he has to say? We may hope he may answer your riddle, and if he does not, perhaps you can help us decide the question of whether we have kept him locked in there too long.'","Saruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
You should <rgb=#FF00FF>listen</rgb> one last time to Saruman's plea.","'Why if it isn't our little friend the ${RACE}. What has brought you all the way back here, I wonder? For the last I heard of it, you and many others had gone east, far east, to deal with matters quite out of the soil of Ents. \
\
'Perhaps it is to some message you bear to Treebeard? Or to question that Wizard. Or... former Wizard? I am not quite sure what he is now, or how to name him. Well, as it happens you will find both of them up ahead, for Treebeard and several other Ents have just been gathered to watch him. They have only been there several days, and might be gone in several more, so you are lucky to catch them.'","Search for clues (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Masters Peregrin and Meriadoc have been asking after you once again, ${PLAYER}. You would do well the hasten to Bâr Thorenion, for they were grave of countenance.'","You have found Quickbeam in the waters of Flooded Isengard, who has told you that Treebeard and several other Ents are gathered up ahead on the western side of Orthanc, discussing Saruman.","Merry and Pippin have been pondering the revelations of their last foray into Mordor, and come to some conclusions.","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 11 July 3018","Treebeard suggested that you search for other clues around Flooded Isengard, while you wait for Saruman to emerge from Orthanc.","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 14 May 3018","Saruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
You should <rgb=#FF00FF>listen</rgb> once more to Saruman's plea.","Saruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
Saruman has suggested that he could aid in the subjugation and cleansing of Mordor, still covered in the corruptions, lieutenants, and shadow of Sauron as it is. You should consider the dethroned land and what Saruman might do there.","'Do you remember what those squinty fellows said? The ones we caught talking to each other in Mordor? They wanted to sell news, and that news, as best as Merry and I could tell, had to do with a Wizard and the Halfling Lands. Gandalf and the Shire, we asked ourselves? Well, if it was not the Shire, then we're both dwarves. But Gandalf? That just didn't feel right. \
\
'And then we tried to think of any other Wizards, and the first that came to mind was that snake, Saruman. And then it all began to fall suspiciously into place. Did we not see fellows just such as those three among Saruman's rabble? I think we did.\
\
'Well and that brings us around to the favour we hoped to ask you. Someone has got to go back there and see what that old, white sweet-talker is up to. And poke around and see if there is anything to explain any more of what those three were talking about.'","Go back to Treebeard","Return to Treebeard","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 5 July 3018","(A VOICE COMES FROM ABOVE)\
'A VISITOR? OR A RUSE? WILL YOU LISTEN TO MY PLEA WITH A FAIR AND OPEN HEART, TRULY?'","'Saruman is not out yet, but he will be in a little while, hoom! Why don't you poke around this place and find what you can find, then come back here.'","You shudder at the vision of toiling hobbits, whose lives need little improvement, only to be left alone in peace","Return to Flooded Isengard","Hornblower Pipe-weed, packaged 3 August 3018","Saruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
Saruman has said that if you free him, he will heal, regrow, and make reparations for the wrongs done in his name. You should <rgb=#FF00FF>look around</rgb> to consider the weight of his words.","Chapter 3: High and Low","<rgb=#FF00FF>Look around</rgb> you","You should approach Orthanc from where the Ents stand on the western side of Flooded Isengard and see if Saruman will speak with you.","You have found Quickbeam in the waters of Flooded Isengard, who has told you that Treebeard and several other Ents are gathered on the western side of Orthanc, discussing Saruman.","Saruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard.\
\
Saruman has asked you to <rgb=#FF00FF>listen</rgb> to his plea.","'Why, if it isn't ${PLAYER}! Have you been to Isengard? And you are back already? You must tell us all you saw.'\
\
As you tell it, the two hobbits' eyes go wide with amazement.\
\
'Slippery old snake, Saruman is,' Pippin says at last. 'But I'll tell you what I do not like: it is that bit about helping the Free Peoples. Something about it makes the hair stand up on the back of my neck.\
\
'And then there is the matter of those pipe-weed barrels. There were many more than the two we found, somewhere, I suppose. It was very clever of you to take note of the dates stamped on them. We must think about that, Merry. It is quite a lot of time between early summer of two years ago and the first of this very March. What's he up to, do you suppose?'","Approach Orthanc","Treebeard and other Ents are indeed gathered before Orthanc, talking together"},
[3107]={"Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Brogur se ha mostrado profundamente perturbado por la historia registrada en el Libro de Mazarbul, y te ha pedido que lleves el siniestro tomo a Bósi.","'La Cámara de Mazarbul, o la Cámara de Registros, se encuentra a la derecha del pasillo que sale de la Sala Vigesimoprimera hacia el norte. Wárr te ha estado esperando allí.'","Lleva el Libro de Mazarbul a Brogur","'La cámara está llena de escombros, ${PLAYER}. ¿Quién sabe lo que podrían estar escondiendo los escombros?'","Brogur te ha dicho que los trabajos de excavación de la Cámara de Registros avanzan a buen ritmo, aunque le preocupa la presencia de la Mano Blanca en Moria.","Wárr se encuentra en la Cámara de Mazarbul, situada a la derecha del pasillo norte que sale de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Brogur te ha dicho que Wárr ha estado pidiendo tu ayuda con algo en la Cámara de Mazarbul.","Brogur toma el libro de tus manos y hojea con cuidado las páginas frágiles. Su respiración se detiene al comprender lo que tiene entre sus manos.\
\
'Este es el Libro de Mazarbul, y parece contener un registro del asentamiento de Balin. Es una lectura sombría, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Si fueras tan amable de llevarlo a mi primo Bósi, él querrá verlo. Siempre ha tenido más estómago que yo para registros como este. No quiero leer sobre su horrible final. Para mí es suficiente saber que están muertos.\
\
'Bósi todavía está en la Cámara de la Encrucijada en el Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.'","'La Mano Blanca tendrá que esperar, ${PLAYER}, porque Wárr me ha dicho que necesita tu ayuda. Recuerdas a Wárr, ¿verdad? Supervisó la apertura de la Puerta de Acebeda, y tiene una muy alta opinión de ti, al igual que todos nosotros, por supuesto.\
\
'Su equipo de trabajadores está excavando la Cámara de Mazarbul, también conocida como la Cámara de Registros, ubicada al norte de la Sala Vigesimoprimera y a la derecha.\
\
'Ve allí y habla con Wárr sobre la tarea que quiere que hagas. Hablaremos del problema de la Mano Blanca a tu regreso.'","Buscas entre los escombros pero no encuentras nada de interés.","'¿Hay algo que quieras mostrarme?'","Busca entre los escombros de la Cámara de Mazarbul","'¿No me has traído nada?'","Buscando entre los escombros, encuentras un libro dañado.","Brogur se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has encontrado un libro misterioso entre los escombros de la Cámara de Mazarbul y deberías mostrárselo a Brogur sin perder un instante.","Capítulo 3: Dentro de la Cámara de Mazarbul","'¿Qué me has traído, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} ?'\
\
Bósi hojea el libro, y una profunda tristeza se refleja en su rostro al comprender lo que dicen las frágiles páginas.\
\
'Este es un registro de la expedición de Balin, y cuenta su triste final. Al menos ahora sabemos lo que les pasó a nuestros parientes en Moria -- ¡El foso oscuro, de hecho! O eso parece en mi dolor. Lo leeré desde el principio, pero mientras tanto me gustaría que me ayudaras con otro asunto para que pueda dedicar toda mi atención a esto.'","'Ahí estás, ${PLAYER}. Tengo un trabajo para ti, si no te importa ensuciarte las manos.\
\
'Este lugar se llama la Cámara de Mazarbul porque una vez almacenó importantes registros de su época. En algún momento durante los largos años en que Moria estuvo vacía, el techo parece haberse derrumbado. Como puedes ver, toda la habitación se ha llenado de escombros y restos.\
\
'Estamos tratando de buscar entre los escombros cualquier cosa interesante que podamos encontrar. Ayuda a mis enanos con esta tarea y tráeme cualquier cosa digna de atención.'","Los escombros cubren la Cámara de Mazarbul, situada a la derecha del pasillo norte que sale de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Wárr te ha pedido que busques entre los escombros de la Cámara de Mazarbul cualquier cosa de interés que pueda ser útil para los enanos.","Wárr hojea las páginas dañadas del libro y se pone tan blanco como una sábana.\
\
'Deberías llevar esto inmediatamente a Brogur, ${PLAYER}. Esto... esto no es nada bueno.'","'No, no quiero volver a ver el Libro de Mazarbul. Ya he visto suficiente.\
\
'Llévaselo a mi primo Bósi, en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.'","Lleva el Libro de Mazarbul a Bósi"},
[3108]={"Dúnor is on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith.","Talk to Legolas in the throne room of King Elessar","Find the gift of the dwarves on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith","You have found Gimli's gift: a statue carved in the likeness of Boromir, hero of Gondor","Chapter 3: Many Voices","'You have returned at an opportune moment, ${PLAYER}, for Legolas and Gimli have come to the city and will be pleased to speak with you. They may know somewhat of your adventures in Mordor, but I am certain there is more to tell.'","'You can see the gift I brought to the city on the south-east side of the Second Circle, my friend.'","The crowd threatens to become violent. You should try and help Dúnor","Legolas and Gimli have come to the throne room of King Elessar and wish to speak with you.","Dúnor is on the south-east side of the Second Circle in Minas Tirith, and is having trouble dealing with an unruly crowd.","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Elessar and the Kingdom of Gondor, and to fight on their behalf in Mordor.","Speak to members of the unruly crowd and try to calm them down","The gift of the Elves Legolas brought to Minas Tirith is currently on the south-east side of the Second Circle.","Dúnor has asked for your help in calming the unruly crowd on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith.","'What is happening in the Second Circle, ${PLAYER}? I have heard reports of unruly crowds in the city, threatening violence?'","'People of the city, listen to me! You must remain calm. There is no call for violence!'\
\
Dúnor sees you and motions at the crowd.\
\
'${PLAYER}, I need your help! These people are angry that the king has allowed the Haradrim into the city, and if he does make peace with them I don't like to think what these folk will do! This situation threatens to get out of hand. Will they listen to you?'","'Legolas and Gimli will enjoy hearing of your exploits in Mordor, ${PLAYER}, as I have.'","'Go to the king and tell him that the Withered Tree has stirred up further trouble, but we have it mostly in hand for now.'","King Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.","The gift of the dwarves Gimli brought to Minas Tirith is currently on the south-east side of the Second Circle.","'King Elessar waits at the throne for you. He will be pleased to have your assistance.'","'${PLAYER}, how goes the adventuring in Mordor? I hope you have found plenty of Orcs to slay!\
\
'I have returned to the city with gifts for Aragorn and Gondor, but the finest gift will have to wait until my plan to settle the Glittering Caves has been carried out. I hope to repair and rebuild the gate of the city with mithril, but that will have to wait for a time. Still, I have already done a great deal of the planning in my head, and trust me when I tell you it will be magnificent!\
\
'But you can see one of the gifts already! When you are finished catching up with me and Legolas here, you can see it in the Second Circle, further down in the city.'","'King Elessar waits for you in his throne room, and will be glad to see you again.'","'We are met in friendship, ${PLAYER}. Like Gimli with the dwarves, I have brought gifts for the city from the Elves, though our gifts are of a different sort: flowering trees and plants with which to enliven the various levels of Minas Tirith. You can see some of the things we brought in the Second Circle, once you are done conversing with Gimli and me.\
\
'I asked Aragorn if he desired a replacement for the White Tree, since a dead tree does not seem well-suited for Minas Tirith's future, but he refused. He responded that there can be no replacement for it in all of Middle-earth, to his sorrow. He is not wrong, but I wish it were otherwise.\
\
'Still, the many plants I have brought to the city should help to brighten the scenery and the outlook of the people who live here, and I hope they will also bring a measure of happiness to its king.'","'The Withered Tree has been sowing discord since my coronation, ${PLAYER}, but my allowing the Haradrim embassy into the city has stirred them into a tempest. They are a group of malcontents who think Gondor is doomed to ruin, and they are not allowing the defeat of Sauron to change their opinion!\
\
'I do not completely trust the Haradrim, but in my heart I know that we must make peace with them if Gondor is to maintain its safety. I understand that this is not easy for my people, but I believe that it is right.\
\
'I will do what I can to ensure the Withered Tree do not stir the townspeople to violence. Good fortune to you, ${PLAYER}! I look forward to your return, and hope that by then this matter will be settled and we will have peace.'","'I need your help! These people are angry that the king has allowed the Haradrim into the city, and if he does make peace with them I don't like to think what these folk will do! This situation threatens to get out of hand. Will they listen to you?'","Talk to Dúnor on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith","Talk to King Elessar in his throne room","Find the gift of the Elves on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith","'I think that may have defused the worst of it, but they are still angry. I cannot say I blame them, to be truthful with you. These Haradrim are only suing for peace because they lost the battle and the war. If they had won, they would have put us all to the sword and destroyed the White City stone by stone.\
\
'But Elessar is my king, and I will do as he commands. I only hope the people of the city will do the same!'","Talk to Gimli in the throne room of King Elessar","'You can see the gift I brought to the city on the south-east side of the Second Circle, ${PLAYER}!'","You found Legolas's gift, but your attention is seized by the sound of an unruly crowd"},
[3109]={"'¡La tragedia nos acecha a cada paso! ¿Fue mi sobrino un tonto por desafiar a Mazog de esa manera? Tal vez, pero es un Enano. ¡Cómo no iba a desafiar al engendro de Azog, maldito tres veces por los Enanos!\
\
'Perder tanto a Bori como al hacha Zigilburk es un duro golpe, y temo pensar en lo que este hechicero, este Gorothúl, puede tener preparado para nosotros. Parece claro que aunque los ejércitos son de Mazog, Gorothúl es quien hace los planes.'","Habiendo aprendido que una fuerza de Dol Guldur se ha aliado con los Orcos de Mazog, Bori está aún más decidido a lanzar un asalto sobre Zabadgathol.","Capítulo 3: Mazog","'Si Dol Guldur y Mazog están realmente aliados, no hay tiempo que perder, ${PLAYER}. Atacaremos Zabadgathol antes de que sus planes puedan llevarse a cabo. Con un solo golpe, mataremos a Mazog y pondremos fin a esta guerra entre Orcos y Enanos antes de que cualquier fuerza de Dol Guldur pueda usar nuestro conflicto para su ventaja.\
\
'¡Será como nuestra incursión en Stazgnâkh, solo que esta vez empuñaré Zigilburk, y marcharemos abiertamente hacia la victoria! Nuestros enemigos perecerán bajo la mordida del hacha de mithril; ¡esto es para lo que sirve, mi amigo! ¡Por eso vuelve a salir de la oscuridad!\
\
'Dime cuando estés listo, y asaltaremos Zabadgathol y mataremos a Mazog. Elegiré a algunos otros para que nos acompañen.'","'¡Atacaremos Zabadgathol y derrotaremos a Mazog, ${PLAYER}, y seremos héroes! No podrá resistir el poder de Zigilburk... ¿qué Orco podría?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario, y no se puede completar con una Comunidad.</rgb>","Habla con Bori y ataca Zabadgathol","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bori ha decidido un nuevo plan: atacar la fortaleza de Mazog, empuñando Zigilburk, y matar al malvado Orco antes de que la fuerza de Dol Guldur pueda aprovechar la situación entre los Orcos y los Enanos.","Brogur se encuentra en el Camino Profundo.\
\
Después del asalto fallido de Bori sobre Zabadgathol, Brogur se ha trasladado al Camino Profundo donde llora la pérdida tanto de su sobrino como de Zigilburk."},
[3110]={"Alfirimbes se encuentra en el campamento élfico de Echad Sirion en los Lindes Oscuros.\
\
La Guardia Oculta está lista para comenzar la primera etapa del viaje para llevar a Mazog a Dol Guldur, pasando por el Bosque Ahogado. Alfirimbes te llevará a ellos.","'La Guardia Oculta parte hacia el recorrido de Raddir a través del Bosque Ahogado a medianoche, . Espero que estés ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para unirte a ellos.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no se puede completar con una comunidad.</rgb>","Capítulo 3: Medianoche en el Bosque Ahogado","Habla con Alfirimbes y viaja con la Guardia Oculta","'No sé qué podemos hacer, ${PLAYER}. Solo Raddir sabía por qué caminos planeaba llevarnos a Dol Guldur con nuestro cautivo, y sin él, los caminos secretos están velados para nosotros. Me temo que nuestra misión está al borde del fracaso antes de haber comenzado.'","'¡No puedo creer que Raddir esté muerto! ¿Cómo pudo suceder esto? ¿Y qué será de la misión de la Guardia Oculta ahora?'","Cúcheron está en el porche de la Posada Embrujada, lamentando la pérdida de Raddir.\
\
Raddir puede haber desaparecido, pero la misión de la Guardia Oculta debe continuar. Cúcheron te dirá qué se debe hacer mientras los Elfos intentan reagruparse tras la pérdida de uno de los suyos.","La misión de la Guardia Oculta comienza cuando llevan a Mazog en la primera etapa del viaje a través del Bosque Negro, trazado por Raddir.","'Raddir ha trazado un camino a través del Bosque Negro que evita algunos de sus peligros más evidentes, pero esta primera etapa puede ser traicionera. El camino que ha elegido serpentea a través de los pantanos fétidos del Bosque Ahogado. Lo llama Râd Cened y me dice que debería estar libre de Orcos.\
\
'Pero Raddir habló de otros peligros, de los cuales no podemos prever: tierra esponjosa que se adhiere al pie, zarzas que atraparán la ropa y la armadura y romperán tu concentración, grandes charcos de agua estancada que pueden ralentizar tu progreso hasta un arrastre. Tú y los otros miembros de la Guardia Oculta deberán tener cuidado con estos y otros peligros. Pocos viajan por el Bosque Ahogado, a menos que tengan muy buenas razones para hacerlo. Mantenerse fuera del alcance del Enemigo hasta que Mazog esté a su puerta es una de esas razones.\
\
'Habla conmigo de nuevo, y te mostraré al resto de la compañía para esta etapa del viaje.'","Habla con Cúcheron en el porche de la Posada Embrujada"},
[3111]={"Wadu's favourite tree is on a rise west of Lhanuch, overlooking the ox-pens.\
\
Nona has asked you to recover the Rohirrim sword she left at Wadu's favourite tree. It was found with Wadu's body and she thought to leave it there as a remembrance, but has changed her mind.","'Were you able to offer words of comfort to Nona? She told you to recover Wadu's sword from the tree where she left it? We all manage our grief differently, ${PLAYER}. If that is what she wants, then it should be done. She said the tree is on a rise overlooking the ox-pens, west of Lhanuch? That is where you should go, I expect.'","Nona is in the north-eastern corner of Lhanuch.\
\
Candaith has asked you to check on Nona to see how she is dealing with the death of her brother.","'Nona... told me... about the mighty gwiber. The one he... the one my son killed. I did not think he had the spirit for that.'\
\
Suvulch falls silent and does not speak again.","'Nona wishes to join your company? It seems that she will, then. There is no man among you of sterner stuff than my daughter, and she will not be refused when she has set her mind to a thing.'","'Go to Wadu's favourite tree and recover his sword, ${PLAYER}. I have changed my mind. Wadu would want me to use the sword, as he did. It should not go unused. The tree is on a rise overlooking the ox-pens, west of Lhanuch.'","'Nona wishes to ride with us when we leave Lhanuch? I do not think Halbarad will allow it. You can ask him, but I feel certain he will refuse. He is among the huts on the western side of the village.'","'What is it? The Uch-lûth woman has a request?'\
\
Halbarad listens as you recount Nona's desire to travel with the Grey Company, but his response is quick and unyielding.\
\
'No, absolutely not. This I must refuse. This is not open for debate.'\
\
Halbarad shakes his head.\
\
'But there is something urgent, ${PLAYER}. Radanir found something.'","'The man named Halbarad leads your company, does he not? Tell him I will go with your Rangers when they depart Lhanuch. He is just to the west of here in the village, I am sure of it.'","Talk to Nona in Lhanuch","Collected Wadu's sword","'Thank you for bringing me my brother's sword, ${PLAYER}. It was a sword of Rohan, true, but to my eyes it is no longer the weapon of my people's ancient enemies. It is now my brother's sword, the sword with which he slew the mightiest gwiber anyone has ever seen, and I will use it in his memory.'\
\
Nona nods sternly and looks around at the huts of Lhanuch.\
\
'I have a request, ${PLAYER}. Go to the leader of your company, the man called Halbarad, who has spoken at length with Glynn Brenin, and tell him that I will go with your people when they leave Lhanuch. It is my desire to avenge the death of my brother on the enemies of the Uch-lûth and on the Wizard Saruman, and our road lies together for a little while. Your man Halbarad is in Lhanuch, is he not?'","Chapter 3: Nona's Request","Nona, the Dunlending girl you helped beneath Zudrugund, has been mourning the death of her brother Wadu, and Candaith wants to make sure she is comforted.","'We need the friendship of the Uch-lûth if we are to pass peacefully through Enedwaith into Dunland. Please check on Nona and see how she is dealing with the death of her brother. She is in the north-eastern corner of Lhanuch.'","Halbarad is in Lhanuch, among the huts on the western side of the village.\
\
Nona has asked to accompany the Grey Company when it departs Lhanuch and travels south.","Nona is in the north-eastern corner of Lhanuch.\
\
You have recovered the sword from Wadu's favourite tree and should now bring it to Nona as she requested.","'You have brought me nothing?'","Talk to Halbarad in Lhanuch","'These worries endanger our haste; we must not tarry overlong. But I would not forget the pains of those we have encountered along the way.\
\
'The Uch-lûth girl who helped us as we came to Lhanuch: Nona. She lost her brother Wadu, ambushed by a hostile Dunlending clan, and she must be feeling the grief most keenly. Please go to her in the north-east corner of Lhanuch and lend whatever comfort you can.\
\
'I do not want the Grey Company to wear blinders like those Erebrandir wore in his youth, before he was befriended by Saeradan. We must be aware of the hurts happening around us and do what we can to help.'","Recover the sword from Wadu's favourite tree","'It is very unusual for a Dunlending to have and use a sword of Rohan, ${PLAYER}, but that seems to be the case. I wonder what the story of this sword might be? Well, there is no time to find out; Nona is waiting for it in the north-eastern corner of Lhanuch, correct?'","Bring Wadu's sword to Nona in the north-east corner of Lhanuch","'What is it you want?'\
\
Nona laughs, a harsh and humourless sound.\
\
'Concern? Do not be concerned for me. I was lost after the death of my brother, but that was before I learned of the glory he had attained before his death. Those who slew him were right to do so from hiding; they must have been able to sense that he had become a great warrior and would have bested them.\
\
'There was a tree Wadu loved, atop a rise by the ox-pens, west of Lhanuch. I left his sword there, to honour his memory, but I think he would rather I used it to attain even half the glory with it he did. Go to the tree and bring me the sword.'","Suvulch remains downcast, lost in thought."},
[3112]={"Rink Martillofuerte se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego, a un lado de la Vía de los Herreros, entre las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Stóthkell te ha pedido que ayudes a su teniente con los preparativos para la defensa del Corazón de Fuego.","Has ayudado a Rink Martillofuerte con sus preparativos","Stóthkell se alegra de contar con tu ayuda para preparar el Corazón de Fuego para la tormenta que se avecina.","Habla con Stóthkell en el Corazón de Fuego, a un lado de la Vía de los Herreros","Capítulo 3: Preparativos para el Corazón de Fuego","'Ya me he enterado de lo que has hecho aquí, un excelente trabajo ayudando con los preparativos para nuestra defensa.\
\
'Tienes mi agradecimiento, aunque empiezo a preguntarme si los orcos siquiera se atreverán a atacarnos.'","Ayuda a Rink Martillofuerte con sus preparativos","Stóthkell se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego, a un lado de la Vía de los Herreros, entre las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Has ayudado a Rink Martillofuerte con sus preparativos y ahora deberías informarle a Stóthkell sobre tus éxitos.","'Mi teniente te dirá cómo ayudarnos mejor con los preparativos, ${PLAYER}. Confío ciegamente en Rink Martillofuerte. Pregúntale qué debe hacerse y hazlo.\
\
'Nosotros, aquí en el Corazón de Fuego, nos mantendremos firmes contra los orcos hasta el final. Y entonces, si todo parece perdido, cerraremos la puerta.\
\
'Sin embargo, solo lo haremos en caso de extrema necesidad. Ayuda a Rink con los preparativos para nuestra defensa, y el tiempo hasta que tengamos que cerrar la puerta puede retrasarse mucho.'","'Habla con Rink Martillofuerte aquí en el Corazón de Fuego sobre los preparativos para nuestra defensa.'"},
[3113]={"Rink Martillofuerte se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego, cerca de la Vía de los Herreros, en las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Has interrumpido la red de comunicación de los trasgos en las Obras Hidráulicas y ahora debes regresar con Rink Martillofuerte.","Derrota a los corredores trasgos en las Obras Hidráulicas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Viaja a las Obras Hidráulicas y derrota a los corredores trasgos allí. Interrumpiremos sus comunicaciones y dejaremos sus planes en desorden. ¡Pero ten cuidado! Estas criaturas pueden correr y nadar a gran velocidad.'","'Los trasgos pueden moverse rápidamente cuando quieren. Las asquerosas criaturas no son muy inteligentes, pero aún así pueden causar mucho daño si coordinan sus ataques. Si interrumpimos su capacidad de comunicarse, podrían ser menos efectivos para organizar un ataque serio contra el Corazón de Fuego.\
\
'Los exploradores han informado que los corredores trasgos se están moviendo por las Obras Hidráulicas, corriendo, nadando, arrastrándose y gateando. Si derrotas a muchos de estos corredores, serán menos capaces de señalar el momento de su ataque.\
\
'Cuanto más tiempo tengamos para construir barricadas y otras defensas, mejor será para nosotros. Interrumpir la comunicación de los trasgos en las Obras Hidráulicas nos dará este tiempo.'","Rink Martillofuerte está preocupado por la red de mensajeros que los trasgos han establecido en las Obras Hidráulicas y quiere que la interrumpas.","Corredores trasgos derrotados en las Obras Hidráulicas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los mensajeros trasgos transmiten los planes del enemigo a través de las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Rink Martillofuerte te ha pedido que derrotes a los mensajeros trasgos para interrumpir la red de comunicación de estas criaturas en las Obras Hidráulicas.","'Buen trabajo. Sin duda, los trasgos están en desorden y les resultará difícil montar un ataque efectivo durante algún tiempo.'","Capitulo 3: Corredores en las profundidades"},
[3114]={"Habla con Rúmil","Capítulo 3: Rúmil y Orophin","Orophin está a punto de hablar cuando algo lo distrae de repente.\
\
'¡Yrch!' sisea.","'He enviado un mensaje a la Dama Galadriel, ${PLAYER}. Ella juzgará si tu necesidad es grande y determinará qué papel jugarán los Elfos en estas nuevas hazañas en Moria.\
\
'Mientras tanto, agradecería tu ayuda para patrullar los límites del bosque. Habla con mis hermanos Rúmil y Orophin y ofréceles tu ayuda; hablan poco la lengua común, pero el odio a los Orcos será entendido por todos los enemigos del único Enemigo.\
\
'Los encontrarás en las lejanas orillas del Nimrodel, al norte. Si caminas por las riberas del río, encontrarás a mis hermanos.'","'Habla con Rúmil y Orophin, a lo largo de la orilla norte del río Nimrodel, y ofréceles tu ayuda. Quizás cuando regreses haya recibido noticias de la Dama Galadriel.'","Rúmil inclina la cabeza ante ti y señala hacia la distancia, lejos de los límites de Lórien. Luego, se encoge de hombros y pone una mano sobre su arco.\
\
Puede que no hable la lengua común, pero su mensaje es claro: por el momento, su puesto está tranquilo. La amenaza orca se ha ido, por ahora.","Haldir ahora cree que eres ${PLAYERNAME:un enemigo[m]|una enemiga[f]} de los trasgos y los Orcos, y quiere que ayudes a defender los límites del Bosque de Oro mientras se envía un mensaje a Galadriel para informarle de tu necesidad.","Rúmil y Orophin están apostados a lo largo de los límites de Lothlórien. Haldir te dijo que caminaras por la orilla norte del río Nimrodel para encontrar a sus hermanos.\
\
Haldir te ha pedido que les prestes tu ayuda a Rúmil y Orophin. No hablan mucho la lengua común, así que si no puedes hablar con ellos en élfico, tu odio mutuo hacia los Orcos debe trascender la necesidad de palabras.","'Te agradezco que hayas ayudado a mis hermanos, ${PLAYER}, y por haber protegido los límites de Lórien.\
\
'La Dama Galadriel me ha enviado su respuesta sobre tu petición y el destino de los enanos. Te transmitiré su mensaje.'","Haldir se encuentra en su campamento en los límites de Lothlórien.\
\
Has hablado con sus hermanos y repelido un ataque de los Orcos, así que deberías volver ahora con Haldir.","Habla con Orophin","Has defendido con éxito a Orophin"},
[3115]={"Uchdrud smiles coldly and dismisses your plea for mercy","'Barliman will not understand, as he bears little goodwill for the Rangers, but I want him to be vigilant for any dangers that may arise while the Dúnedain are away in the south. Go now to The Prancing Pony, in Bree, and give him my warning. I hope it will put him on his guard, for dark days may be ahead for Bree.'","'What did you say to me? I have as much a right to this table as anyone here. More so, once the rest of my friends get here! Oh, there will be changes around here, I don't mind telling you.'\
\
Uchdrud scowls at you.\
\
'Are you still here? You've made me mad, and now you're going to pay for it! I will see you outside, by the North-gate of Bree, if you have any courage at all. We won't be bothered there. I will teach you a lesson about respecting Uchdrud and his boys...a lesson this whole town is going to have to learn!'","'I am sorry you have gotten tangled up with this, ${PLAYER}, but this sort of thing has gotten more and more common lately! What is happening to Bree these days?\
\
'Uchdrud says he'll teach you a lesson outside the North-gate of Bree? I don't think he knows what he's gotten himself into, ${PLAYER}, but be careful. You never know how dangerous that sort of fellow might be, bark or bite!'","'One more trip should do it, ${PLAYER}. There should be a pumpkin in one of those crates in the parlour, so you just run that out here and we should be all set, and a job well done it will be!'","Talk to Saeradan in Bree-land","'I don't want you to make a scene, but I'd just as soon have this Uchdrud out of the Pony. He's loud and coarse and is scaring the rest of the guests! He's at that table over there.'","Talk to Uchdrud at The Prancing Pony Inn","'You must bring your message to Saeradan, in Bree-land. Look for him at his cabin, east of Thornley's Work-site in the Northern Breefields.'","Meet Uchdrud outside the North-gate of Bree","Barliman Butterbur is the proprietor of The Prancing Pony and can be found by its bar, in the town of Bree.\
\
Saeradan has agreed to travel south with the Grey Company, but he wants you to ask Barliman Butterbur to be careful while the Rangers are gone.","'You should next bring your message to Saeradan, in Bree-land. He is more settled than some others of my kin, but no less a vital part of the Grey Company. We will have need of Saeradan's calming wisdom on the road south, for though we have need of haste, so too do we need to keep our wits about us. Too often can the hasty road lead to carelessness. Saeradan will help prevent this.\
\
'Look for him at his cabin near the town of Bree, in Bree-land. He lives east of Thornley's Work-site, in the Northern Bree-fields.'\
\
Candaith gives you a wistful smile.\
\
'It is true, we don't know what we will find as we ride south. I look out over these Lone-lands and wonder what will happen to them when we have gone. But this is something we must do. Each of us has sworn an oath to Aragorn our chief, and none of us will break that oath. We know the risks. None of us would join the Grey Company if we felt its errand was not important enough to brave those risks. For my part, I will not give in to fear of the unknown. We all have our role to play, and I hope only that when I have played mine, the world will have been better for my having been in it.'","'That fellow Saeradan does come to the Pony from time to time, and we talk about the state of things in Bree. Not as often as I'd like, of course! For every moment of peace there are ten things that need doing, and no way to make them all fit in the time available! Still, I do what I can, and wouldn't trade the Pony for anything!\
\
'Folk say Saeradan's a Ranger, but if he is, he's more respectable than most. Has a cabin just near Bree, you know, and even spares a smile for his neighbours, which is more than I've seen from some others of that kind.\
\
'Will you look at me, going on and on like this! There's no time for idle chatter...there are foodstuffs sitting in one of the parlours that need to be brought out here for preparing. Will you go and fetch some of them? Apples, pears, mushrooms...you'll see the crate, you will, and you'll be a big help to me if you hurry!'","Barliman Butterbur is in the main room of The Prancing Pony.\
\
You have carried several loads of foodstuffs from one of the Pony's parlours out to the main room and should speak now to Barliman.","'Thank you! You've been a great help to me today, and I won't forget it. So much to do, so very much to do, but you're welcome to stay as long as you like. Join the company, sing a song, warm yourself by the fire!'\
\
Barliman pauses and his eyes pass briefly over the crowd.\
\
'There is one more thing, actually, ${PLAYER},' he says in a hushed tone.\
\
'There have been a few rude types come to Bree lately, and they've been scaring off some of the townsfolk who like to come to the Pony of a night; regular visitors, you know, good folk who come by for a spot of ale and some cheer.\
\
'Do you think you might have a word with the fellow at that table there? Uchdrud, I think his name is, and he's a coarse sort. Maybe you can encourage him to finish his mug of beer and find somewhere to go for the night? Only he hasn't rented any lodgings here, and I'd just as soon he took his loud friends somewhere else. I would tell him myself, but there's so much to do....'","'It's a start, but that's not all of it, ${PLAYER}! Return to the crates in the parlour and bring me some more of the foodstuffs you find within.'","Uchdrud is waiting somewhere by the North-gate of Bree for you to answer his challenge.\
\
You did as Butterbur asked and told Uchdrud to finish his beer and leave the Pony, and he reacted angrily, challenging you to meet him outside the North Gate of Bree.","Habla con Saeradan en su cabaña","Uchdrud is sitting at a table in the main room of The Prancing Pony.\
\
Barliman Butterbur has asked you to encourage Uchdrud, an unruly and coarse sort, to vacate the premises.","Chapter 3: Saeradan's Watchfulness","'Are you still here? I will first finish this beer, and then I will meet you outside the North-gate of Bree to teach you a lesson you won't soon forget!'","Saeradan is at his cabin in Bree-land, east of Thornley's Worksite in the Northern Bree-fields.\
\
Candaith has told you to travel next to tell Ranger Saeradan of the Grey Company's road.","'What is happening to Bree? So many coarse and unruly sorts, like that Uchdrud, are coming to the town. There will be trouble come from it, mark my words! Ah, we will weather it, we always do. The Pony will be here forever, and a Butterbur will be running it, so long as I have any say in the matter!'","Crates of foodstuffs are waiting in one of the parlours of The Prancing Pony.\
\
Barliman has heard the warning you brought from Saeradan, but he seems to have already forgotten it, and has asked you to carry foodstuffs out to the main room of the Pony.","'I was right to worry, then? I feared it was so. Very few of these people know that the safety they feel is the result of the tireless work of the Dúnedain.\
\
'And yet our road must take us south, into lands far away from the well-meaning proprietor of the Prancing Pony. He may not trust Rangers, but my people are no less fond of him and his simple life than they are of their own sons and daughters. I hope his town and his inn will remain safe until we return...if return we can.'","Uchdrud has challenged you to meet him outside the Pony","Talk to Barliman Buttebur at The Prancing Pony Inn","Habla con Cebadilla Mantecona en la Posada del Poney Pisador","'I didn't think you'd show, ${PLAYER}. We're going to own this town in a couple weeks, and that fat innkeeper in there will have to beg for table-scraps from Uchdrud and his boys.\
\
'Just like you'll need to beg for mercy in a few moments, ${RACE}. I may even grant it!'","Saeradan is at his cabin outside the town of Bree.\
\
You have done as Saeradan asked and should now return to him at his cabin.","Retrieve foodstuffs from a crate in the Pony","You have brought word to Candaith that the Grey Company assembles, but now Saeradan in Bree-land must be notified.","'You'll find the stack of crates in one of the parlours, ${PLAYER}. Bring me the foodstuffs you find inside: plates of apples, pears, mushrooms, and a pumpkin. You may need to take a few trips!'","Uchdrud begs for mercy! Saeradan was right: trouble lies ahead for Bree","'I see, ${PLAYER}. I will travel south with as many of the Dúnedain as can be gathered in haste. Aragorn has need of us, and that is all that we need know.'\
\
Saeradan looks wistfully around the yard.\
\
'I fear for the people of this land, ${PLAYER}, without the Dúnedain to protect them. Great numbers of an unruly sort have already come to Bree, and the brigands of the countryside will have no want for members while the Rangers are not around to keep their ranks in check.\
\
'I will make ready to depart. While I do so, will you speak with Barliman at the Prancing Pony? He does not think much of Rangers, but I would have you ask him to take especial care of his Inn and the town for the next several months, if it comes to that. He will not understand, but I want him to have at least some warning that troubles may lie in store for Bree.'"},
[3116]={"Wafi te dio una lista de lugares para buscar entre los escombros que podrían contener armas reutilizables que los artesanos del Corazón de Fuego podrían fundir.\
\
Wafi necesita materias primas para fabricar equipo para la defensa del Corazón de Fuego y te ha pedido que busques entre los escombros de Moria armas reutilizables.","Lleva las armas adecuadas y la lista a Wafi","Busca entre los montones de armas viejas para encontrar materiales reutilizables (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Wafi se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego, cerca de la Vía de los Herreros, entre las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Has encontrado muchas armas que pueden ser fundidas en las forjas del Corazón de Fuego.","'¡No me has traído nada!'","'El catálogo que te di debería indicarte los lugares donde buscar entre los escombros. Nuestros exploradores creen que estos lugares podrían contener armas adecuadas para la fabricación de equipo aquí en el Corazón de Fuego.'","Wafi quiere que busques entre los escombros de Moria armas reutilizables que puedan ser rescatadas para su uso por los artesanos del Corazón de Fuego.","'Estas armas servirán muy bien, aunque no para luchar, por supuesto, ya que son muy viejas y no están en condiciones de combate, pero sí para fundirlas en las forjas del Corazón de Fuego.\
\
¡Vamos a ponernos a fabricar armas y armaduras de mejor calidad de inmediato! ¡Gracias por tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}!'","Capítulo 3: Rebuscando entre las armas","'No hay nada más frustrante para un hábil artesano enano que tener a su disposición una gran forja como esta sin suficientes materias primas para aprovecharla. Y si hay algo más molesto que eso, es saber que cuando los orcos ataquen, es posible que no hayamos podido equipar a nuestro pueblo con suficientes armas y armaduras.\
\
Tengo entendido que ayudaste al hijo del Señor Bósi a tomar armas, armaduras y cascos de los orcos para que su asalto contra la Mano Blanca en Moria fuera victorioso. Entonces eres el ${RACE} perfecto para el trabajo.\
\
Hemos enviado exploradores por toda Moria, y han catalogado una lista de lugares probables para encontrar tales armas. Te daré este catálogo para que puedas llevar un registro de los lugares donde has buscado armas reutilizables.'","Encontraste algunas armas reutilizables adecuadas para los propósitos de Wafi."},
[3117]={"'¿Qué dices, Legolas? Estoy seguro de que ${PLAYER} querría acompañarnos en un recorrido por los bosques.''","Legolas y Gimli han estado caminando por los bosques de Lothlórien, vigilando a los orcos que intentan infiltrarse en los límites.","Gimli está en una plataforma entre los árboles sobre la colina de Cerin Amroth, en el centro de Lórien.\
\
Celeborn ha aceptado ayudar a la Guarnición de Hierro a superar sus problemas en Moria, y deberías hablar con Gimli sobre lo sucedido.","'Me encantaría que te unieras a nosotros, ${PLAYER}. La belleza de Lothlórien se aprecia mejor cuando se comparte, aunque todos debemos permanecer alerta, incluso al caminar entre los árboles de Lórien, pues los orcos de Moria han bajado a Nanduhirion y a veces pueden escabullirse más allá de las fronteras.\
\
'Avísame cuando estés listo para partir.'","'Desearía poder ayudar a la Guarnición de Hierro con sus esfuerzos en Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}. Las Minas me han traído una gran tristeza, pero me gustaría verlas restauradas, y la Guarnición de Hierro necesitará enanos sanos y fuertes si eso va a suceder.\
\
'Pero no puedo. Mi camino está con Frodo, y veré esta tarea hasta el final antes de regresar a las Minas. La necesidad de la Guarnición de Hierro es grande, pero el hijo de Glóin no se aparta de una carga para comenzar otra.'\
\
La frente de Gimli se frunce, y luego sus ojos se iluminan con asombro.\
\
'Siento que la dama Galadriel puede que ya supiera de las noticias de Bósi. En mi primer encuentro con ella, me pareció que ofrecía una elección; una elección entre continuar la misión y dejarla en manos de otros. ¡Y aquí llega justo tal punto de decisión!'","Capítulo 3: Hijos de la hoja y la piedra","Habla con Legolas y viaja con él a través del Bosque de Oro","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para ir, ? Será un placer para mí recorrer los bosques tanto contigo como con Gimli, y también buscaremos orcos que puedan haber escapado más allá de los límites.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no se puede completar con una comunidad.</rgb>","Legolas está junto a Gimli sobre la plataforma encima de la colina de Cerin Amroth.\
\
Has sido invitado por Gimli a patrullar los bosques de Lothlórien con él y Legolas, y deberías hablar con Legolas cuando estés listo para partir.","Legolas está junto a Gimli sobre la plataforma encima de la colina de Cerin Amroth.\
\
Has sido invitado por Gimli a patrullar los bosques de Lothlórien con Legolas y él mismo, y deberías hablar ahora con el Elfo sobre la excursión.","'Legolas y yo estábamos a punto de dar otro paseo entre los árboles de Lothlórien en busca de orcos patrullando, ${PLAYER}. ¿Por qué no vienes con nosotros?\
\
'¿Qué opinas, Legolas? ¿Hay lugar en nuestro grupo para un tercero? Seguro que ${PLAYER} disfrutará de la belleza del bosque, y la posibilidad de abatir uno o tres orcos solo hará más atractiva la excursión.'","'No culparé a Gimli si decide ayudar a la Guarnición de Hierro con sus dificultades. El señor Elrond no nos impuso ningún vínculo para acompañar a Frodo más allá de lo que quisiéramos.\
\
'Es una decisión de Gimli.'"},
[3119]={"Candaith is by the stables in Rivendell.\
\
You have listened to Candaith describe some of the history of the Dúnedain and should speak to him now for the conclusion.","'This is the tale of the Dúnedain that travelled north to Forochel to reclaim the heirlooms of the House of Isildur following the loss of Arvedui.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Candaith in Rivendell and experience 'Session: The House of Isildur' or read the shortened account instead","'The early years of the Third Age saw the deaths of Isildur and his eldest sons, but his line was not ended, for his youngest son was kept safely here in Rivendell. He was raised far from danger and came to rule the North Kingdom. His descendents would not know peace, for the Nazgûl were to reappear, and their chief would wage war upon the Men of the West.\
\
'In the year Nineteen Seventy-four of the Third Age, the armies of the Witch-king seized Fornost. The North Kingdom was no more, and its ruler Arvedui fled northward, to Forochel. But there he was lost, along with the heirlooms of his house.\
\
'Some of the Dúnedain journeyed into the icy wastes to recover them. Do you wish to hear of their quest?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Candaith in Rivendell","The history of the House of Isildur is full of dangerous escapes, glorious triumphs, and near brushes with tragedy, but even after so long the line remains strong. Three thousand years after the death of Isildur, Aragorn, son of Arathorn, is prepared to fulfill his destiny...","Chapter 3: The House of Isildur","Candaith is at the stables of Rivendell.\
\
Candaith has offered to tell you of key moments in the history of the Dúnedain.","'And so it was that Aragorn, Heir of Isildur through unbroken line down the long years, began his friendship with Gandalf, the Grey Pilgrim. He will be known by the sword that he bears, Andúril, Flame of the West, and by the Ring of Barahir, once lost but since regained.\
\
'It is the task of the Dúnedain, and indeed of all friends of Aragorn, to ensure he safely comes into his birth-right. We will not question if this is the time for his ascension to the kingship. It must be so.\
\
'Ride with us, ${PLAYER}, for we ride into history. Laegened and Haerdor, Corugúr and Glangon, all are remembered for the parts they played in the great drama of the Age. So it will be with us.'","Candaith wishes to tell you some of the history of the Dúnedain so you may recognize the importance of the errand upon which you are about to embark."},
[3120]={"Capítulo 3: Zigilburk el Inigualable","Habla con Bori","'Estas páginas mencionan algo realmente curioso, ${PLAYER}: un hacha hecha completamente de mithril, lo suficientemente ligera para ser manejada con una mano pero lo suficientemente fuerte para derribar a cualquier enemigo o desgarrar cualquier armadura con un solo golpe. Zigilburk, se llamaba, y parece haber sido forjada en la época de Durin por alguien llamado Ongli. Hm. No he oído ese nombre antes. ¿Cómo es posible que alguien tan hábil no sea recordado en la leyenda?\
\
'Hay más que aprender en estas páginas. ¿Podría ser que Zigilburk aún pueda ser encontrado?\
\
'Mi hijo Bori ha estado destrozado por el dolor desde que Bróin fue asesinado frente a las Puertas de Durin. Llévale estas páginas y cuéntale sobre Zigilburk. Le hará bien tener otros pensamientos sobre los cuales reflexionar. Sube las escaleras del lado este de la cámara y pasa por la puerta hacia la Cámara de Comando; mi hijo Bori está allí, y Brogur también.'","Katûb-zahar, la Cámara de las Palabras de Durin, se encuentra en algún lugar del lado este de la Gran Excavación, al norte de una gran estatua de Durin.\
\
Bori te dijo que si puedes encontrar el lugar llamado Katûb-zahar, podría descubrir la ubicación del misterioso hacha de mithril, Zigilburk.","'¡Ojalá Bróin estuviera aquí, ${PLAYER}. Este es el tipo de aventura que él habría disfrutado. Aún así, puede que pueda ayudarte, aunque no lo haré con mucho entusiasmo.\
\
'Parece que el enano que buscaba forjar Zigilburk apreciaba su privacidad, y por la gracia de Durin se le dio una forja secreta donde trabajar. Estas páginas no revelan la ubicación de la forja, pero sí mencionan un truco de algún tipo que abriría la puerta. La naturaleza de este truco se ha perdido, pero estas páginas indican que fue registrado en Katûb-zahar, la Cámara de las Palabras de Durin.\
\
'Katûb-zahar se suponía que estaba en el lado este de la Gran Excavación, en algún lugar al norte de una gran estatua de Durin. Lo siento, pero no hay mucho más con lo que guiarte. Encuentra la ubicación y vuelve a verme, y quizás pueda desentrañar un poco más del misterio.'","'Katûb-zahar, la Cámara de las Palabras de Durin, estaba en algún lugar del lado este de la Gran Excavación, al norte de una estatua de Durin. Sé que no son las indicaciones más útiles; hay muchas estatuas de Durin en Moria.'","Esta placa rota está descolorida, pero aún se puede leer 'Katûb-zahar.'","'Nâr-khelab, el Corazón de Fuego. ¿Podría ser que Zigilburk todavía esté allí?'","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Mando; es la habitación que se encuentra subiendo las escaleras del este en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en el extremo sur del Camino de Durin. Se puede acceder desde la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has localizado una placa que marca la ubicación de Katûb-zahar y deberías regresar con la noticia a Bori.","'No has encontrado aún Katûb-zahar, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}.'","'Katûb-zahar estaba en algún lugar del lado este de la Gran Excavación, al norte de una estatua de Durin.\
\
'Encuentra alguna evidencia de este lugar, la Cámara de las Palabras de Durin, y devuélvemela. ¡Recuperar el hacha de mithril mencionada en esas páginas, si es que alguna vez se fabricó, sería un logro tremendo!'","'Sube las escaleras en el lado este de esta cámara y atraviesa la puerta allí. Mi hijo Bori está en la Cámara de Mando con Brogur.'","'¿No me has traído nada digno de mención?'","Lleva las páginas polvorientas a Bori","Bósi ha descubierto la mención de una poderosa hacha hecha de mithril en uno de los registros que encontraste y busca saber si aún podría encontrarse.","Bori se encuentra en una pequeña habitación en el lado este de la Cámara de la Encrucijada.\
\
Bósi te ha devuelto las páginas polvorientas que contienen pistas sobre la ubicación de Zigilburk, con la esperanza de que tu entrega pueda levantar el ánimo de su hijo.","'¿Encontraste la ubicación de Katûb-zahar, la Cámara de las Palabras de Durin? Estoy profundamente impresionado. Es una pena que tu informe hable de una gran infestación de garras profundas y garras de cueva; espero que las bestias no hayan arruinado demasiados de los registros e historias guardados en ese lugar.\
\
'Parece que Ongli, el gran artesano que pudo haber forjado Zigilburk, era muy protector de su privacidad. Durin le concedió una forja secreta donde trabajar: Nâr-khelab, el Corazón de Fuego. El camino a Nâr-khelab estaba bloqueado por medio de algún truco conocido solo por unos pocos de confianza.\
\
'Estas páginas no mencionan la ubicación de Nâr-khelab, pero sí dicen que el truco para abrir el camino se guardaba en Katûb-zahar. Ahora que has encontrado la Cámara de las Palabras de Durin, puedes buscar este truco.'","Encuentra evidencia de Katûb-zahar","'¡Ojalá Bróin pudiera compartir esta aventura con nosotros!'"},
[3121]={"Defeated beasts or spirits in Thingast (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to King Elessar outside the keep of Lond Cirion","Defeat beasts or spirits in Thingast (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","King Elessar's travelling party has arrived at Iáphel","Chapter 4.1: Among the Green Hills","'Young Orgolas says the road we must take through Thingast may be haunted? I have not heard this before, though it is true that folk once dwelled there and now only their ruins remain. They were called the Orodhoth by the Dúnedain, but they had another name for themselves that I cannot recall.\
\
'As we travel through Thingast, let us remain alert for any dangers that might threaten the safety of the company: spirits, beasts, or raiding Corsairs. Two of these seem more likely to me, but I will not discount the possibility that the folk of Anfalas know more about these lands than we do, and Thingast may truly by haunted by shades. I tell you I have had my fill of spirits.'\
\
Elessar smiles.\
\
'My companion Hirluin was lord of Pinnath Gelin, ${PLAYER}, and he and I adventured with Forlong in days long ago. Forlong would say he could never have his fill of spirit, and Hirluin would laugh and laugh; no room could be empty of cheer that had the two of them in it. But they are gone now, and cheer seems hard to come by. At least the memory of their jesting remains with me, and I cherish it.'","'Thank you for these, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'No, we cannot open these now! We must save them for the right time! I am certain they will live up to their reputation, but if we were to drink them now, in the field, we would truly be wasting the opportunity to enjoy them! Perhaps when the King's business in Pinnath Gelin is done.\
\
'Where does he intend next to travel?'","'I have studied the maps, you know, and the road to Pinnath Gelin leaves Lond Cirion to the west. It passes through Thingast before turning north, and folk say Thingast might be haunted! I will have my sword at the ready. Will you tell King Elessar that I am not afraid?'","Bring the wine bottles to Grethril by the entrance to Iáphel","Iáphel is located north of Thingast, in Tûm Rost.","Gwindir is waiting for you to return with the grapes you picked.","'As we travel through Thingast, let us remain alert for any dangers that might threaten the safety of the company: spirits, beasts, or raiding Corsairs. Two of these seem more likely to me.'","'Do you have a moment for me, ${PLAYER}? I know we have come to Pinnath Gelin for matters most serious, but I beg a small boon of you and the King, for we have come to a place of which I have heard a great deal, and all of it good!\
\
'This is Iáphel in Tûm Rost, and word of the high quality of its grapes has reached the ears of wine-lovers across all of Gondor, even in distant Minas Tirith. Do you think you might see if one of the vintners here might gift us a bottle or two of their finest? I do not know what it is that makes the wine here so renowned, but this is like to be my only chance to sample it!'","'Where does the King intend next to travel?'","Bring the grapes to Gwindir in Iáphel","Picked grapes from the vines at Iáphel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to King Elessar at Iáphel","'You have done very well with the work! Should you wish to aid us in the future, I would not refuse the assistance! But I suppose the King has other tasks for you.\
\
'I set aside some bottles for your company. Bring them to the King's provisioner, and be sure to tell her that if she wishes to purchase more for the cellars of Minas Tirith, the vintners of Iáphel will give her a fair price. The King should have the finest of wines for his table. Don't you agree?'","'Do you think there will be fighting? They say the war is over, but from the tower I saw Corsair ships off in the distance, and the guards report that they sometimes send raiding parties inland to slay and to steal!\
\
'I have studied the maps, you know, and the road to Pinnath Gelin leaves Lond Cirion to the west. It passes through Thingast before turning north, and folk say Thingast might be haunted! I will have my sword at the ready. Will you tell King Elessar that I am not afraid?'","'I set aside some bottles for your company. Bring them to the King's provisioner, and be sure to tell her that if she wishes to purchase more for the cellars of Minas Tirith, the vintners of Iáphel will give her a fair price. The King should have the finest of wines for his table. Don't you agree?'","Gwindir is north-west of the entrance to Iáphel.","Vine trellises can be found on the western side of Iáphel.","Grethril is at the entrance of Iáphel in Tûm Rost.","Pick grapes from the vines at Iáphel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Orgolas is very excited to join King Elessar's travelling party as he journeys into Pinnath Gelin.","Selected wines for the King's company (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","King Elessar is in Iáphel.","'This is Iáphel in Tûm Rost, and word of the high quality of its grapes has reached the ears of wine-lovers across all of Gondor, even in distant Minas Tirith. Do you think you might see if one of the vintners here might gift us a bottle or two of their finest? I do not know what it is that makes the wine here so renowned, but this is like to be my only chance to sample it!'","Grethril will know how best to store the wine bottles. She is by the entrance to Iáphel.","Select wines for the King's company (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Welcome to Iáphel, the most fruitful field among all the green hills of Pinnath Gelin! I understand your company came to Tûm Rost by the road from Anfalas? You saw, then, how dry that land can be, despite how near to the Sea it lies? I will of course gift to the King and his party some bottles of our finest wine, for you must all be so parched!\
\
'Our land is quite different than the Langstrand to the south. Where that is a place of dry, salt-scarred cliffs, ours is a green, rainy country. The mist off the Sea comes to the mountains as low clouds, leaving fog in the hollows; it gives to our grapes a rich, full taste, and the wine we make from them is without compare!\
\
'Aye, we will gift you some bottles. But first I ask that some among your company help us with our work. Not the King or Queen, of course! But we have grapes to pick, and you surely will not refuse when such quality wine is to be the reward?'","Gwindir offered you three of the wines stored nearby.","Travel to the entrance of Iáphel in Tûm Rost","'Yes, I am ready to continue onward, ${PLAYER}. Our next destination is Ost Arndír, stronghold of the Lord of the Green Hills. It was the keep of my friend and companion Hirluin the Fair, but I understand after his death at Pelennor his daughter now rules from that seat.'","King Elessar is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.","Talk to Grethril by the entrance to Iáphel","'We will gift you some bottles. But first I ask that some among your company help us with our work. Not the King or Queen, of course! But we have grapes to pick, and you surely will not refuse when such quality wine is to be the reward?'","Talk to Gwindir north-west of the entrance of Iáphel","Thingast has a reputation for being haunted, and the folk of Lond Cirion will appreciate if you face some of the dangers there as you journey north."},
[3122]={"'It seems there may be some Angmarim cultists readying for one of their loathsome rituals at Caivád Sâr, to the north. Can I ask you to go there to investigate, defeating any of the cultists you find and adding their camp to your map? Prince Durin will want to know the extent of the Angmarim force allied with the Orcs of Gundabad.'","'Hmm. I am worried that both the Orc and Angmarim presence may be larger than my initial scouting indicated, ${PLAYER}. You are certain these numbers are accurate?\
\
'And where did all these cultists come from? I thought their kingdom was ended!'","You quickly sketch Caivád Sâr on your map, noting the Angmarim presence","You quickly sketch the Orkish defences at Zarkul-sulûn","Talk to Thálfi at Zudramdân, north-east of the lake that borders the foothills","Thálfi is at Zudramdân, the forward camp of Durin's great force. Zudramdân is north-east of the lake that borders the foothills of Elderslade.","Defeat Angmarim in Elderslade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Prince Durin has need of our mapping skill in the war effort, ${PLAYER}. Take this parchment and scout the ruins and camps nearby: two old dwarf ruins, one to the north-west and one to the south-west. When you arrive at these, I ask that you draw them on the map. I think there must also be a warg den further north-west, so map that too! In this way, Durin can fashion a plan of attack. Good fortune to you, and when you have finished I will meet you at Zudramdân, the site that will be our foothold further ahead!'","Bring the map back to Thálfi at Zudramdân","You add a brief sketch of the paths of Howlers' Notch to your map","Use the map-ready parchment to add Zarkul-sulûn to the map","'My army will need to cross Elderslade before we can wage war upon the gates of Gundabad, and I want to know what we are up against beforehand! Biraisbij tharâkh, my friend. Find Thálfi beside the river just north-west of Annâk-khurfu and help him with this task.'","You sketch the outside of Shakal-atrâd, but all seems quiet","Thálfi wanted you to add the Angmarim presence at Caivád Sâr to your map, and to defeat any of the cultists that cross your path. Caivád Sâr is to the north of Zudramdân.","'I heard you would fight alongside us to reclaim Gundabad, ${PLAYER}, and I am pleased to learn that was not just a rumour! You see, I wanted to thank you: I believe you saved my life!\
\
'When the great mass of goblins and Orcs erupted from the deep places beneath Moria in that last great flood of evil that spelled defeat for the Iron Garrison, I was separated from my comrades. I was lost and alone in the darkness, cut off from my friends, and it seemed my end was truly at hand. But wait! I still had the map you helped me to prepare of the Winding Way, and by making use of it I was able to find my way back to my retreating allies... so I thank you once again!\
\
'Prince Durin has need of our mapping skill in the war effort, ${PLAYER}. Take this parchment and scout the ruins and camps nearby: two old dwarf ruins, one to the north-west and one to the south-west. When you arrive at these, I ask that you draw them on the map. I think there must also be a warg den further north-west, so map that too! In this way, Durin can fashion a plan of attack. Good fortune to you, and when you have finished I will meet you further ahead at Zudramdân.'","Use the map-ready parchment to add Shakal-atrâd to the map","'Oh, this map is quite well-done, ${PLAYER}, in both artistry and knowledge.\
\
'I heard some troubling news, however. It seems there may be some Angmarim cultists readying for one of their loathsome rituals north of here, at Caivád Sâr. Can I ask you to go there to investigate, defeating any of the cultists you find and adding their camp to your map? Prince Durin will want to know the extent of the Angmarim force allied with the Orcs of Gundabad.'","Chapter 4.1: Plans of Attack","Thálfi is at Zudramdân, the forward camp of Durin's great force, south of Caivád Sâr.","Use the map-ready parchment to add Caivád Sâr to the map","'We have the fighting spirit, my friend, but we will need more than that if we are to reclaim Gundabad. We need information! To that end, I dispatched Thálfi the scout to be my eyes and ears in Elderslade. Look for him beside the river just to the north-west of Annâk-khurfu and help him survey the location of the enemy forces among the foothills.\
\
'My army will need to cross Elderslade before we can wage war upon the gates of Gundabad, and I want to know what we are up against beforehand!\
\
'Biraisbij tharâkh, my friend. Biraisbij tharâkh.'","The great force of dwarves is ready for the assault, with more arriving every day. Now Durin seeks to formulate a battle plan that will bring this force across Elderslade to Gundabad.","Thálfi is beside the river just north-west of Annâk-khurfu, preparing to scout the mountainous region in advance of the assault.","Talk to Thálfi beside the river just north-west of Annâk-khurfu","Thálfi sent you to add three locations to the parchment he gave you: two old dwarf ruins to the north-west and south-west, and a warg camp further north-west.","Use the map-ready parchment to add Howlers' Notch to the map","Defeated Angmarim in Elderslade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[3123]={"You have found record of a sighting of Urudanî","Orcs and evil Men of every variety near the Spire of Lûghash, the settlement of Fushaum Bal, the tower of Cirith Ungol, and the camp outside Naerband may carry messages from their masters to Lhaereth the Stained.","You have found orders for Róglarg","You have found the acceptance from Ugrukhôr","'Lhaereth has requested the Masters of Mordor to attend her in Seregost, and they have sent their responses to her in the hands of runners such as the one I killed. Other responses must be on their way to her, and we must learn of their disposition.\
\
'Defeat Orcs and evil Men of every variety near the following sites, and you may intercept communications intended for Lhaereth. I suggest the Spire of Lûghash, the settlement of Fushaum Bal, near the tower of Cirith Ungol, and the camp outside Naerband. Good hunting to you, ${PLAYER}!'","Harthalín is by the eastward-running road in Agarnaith.","'I will retain the samples we obtained from the swamp and test them with the athelas given to you by Mithrandir, and I will give to you another task. We need information, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The creature that gave this message to the Ghâsh-hai I slew was named Dolgrist, and the words were on behalf of Borangos, of whom we have learned little. I propose that Lhaereth has requested the Masters of Mordor to attend her in Seregost, and they have sent their responses to her in the hands of runners such as the one I killed. Other responses must be on their way to her, and we must learn of their disposition.\
\
'Defeat Orcs and evil Men of every variety near the following sites, and you may intercept communications intended for Lhaereth. I suggest the Spire of Lûghash, the settlement of Fushaum Bal, near the tower of Cirith Ungol, and the camp outside Naerband. Good hunting to you, ${PLAYER}!'","You have found the acceptance from Dulgabêth","Intercept a message near Fushaum Bal","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","Intercept a message from Orodir, the camp outside Naerband","Intercept a message near the Spire of Lûghash","<rgb=#00FF00>All intercepted messages can be read from your inventory</rgb>","Chapter 4.1: The Meeting of the Masters","Bring the intercepted messages to Harthalín by the eastward road in Agarnaith","Intercept a message near the Tower of Cirith Ungol","Harthalín's quick bow-string has slain an Orc carrying word of a meeting of the Masters of Mordor, and she thinks it important to learn more.","'Very well done, my friend! These messages shed enough light on the situation for us to determine a course of action. Mordor is tumultuous enough that each of the Masters wishes to consolidate his power; they are willing to meet, but they do not wish to do so in any of their rivals' strongholds. I cannot blame them for this lack of trust! Indeed, it seems wise for each of them to exercise an abundance of caution!\
\
'But they each want the ascendancy of Mordor; this meeting will happen. But where will they finally agree to meet?'"},
[3124]={"You decide to leave the boys to their game, and see if Hebron has any work for you","Find Thorongil's room inside the keep of Ost Arndír","Te doy la bienvenida.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, you are looking for something to do while the King and Queen speak with Lady Nauriel? I am glad to hear it, for there is always something that needs doing in and around Ost Arndír.\
\
'Can I ask you to deal with any of the foes that encroach upon our lands? There is no shortage of threats throughout many of the Green Hills.'","Hebron is outside the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír.","Thorongil and Orgolas run up, shouting and bickering","Thorongil and Orgolas stand uncertainly together","'I understand you have brought Golasgil's heir Orgolas with you on this visit? My son Thorongil will be delighted to entertain a boy of his own years! Perhaps this ${RACE}, ${PLAYER}, will show Orgolas to my son's chambers? You will find them to the north-east, through the door on the right.'","'Hello. So you are a ${CLASS}? Are you a good one?'\
\
Thorongil dismisses your answer with a casual wave, and turns to Orgolas.\
\
'I am going to train to be a knight when I'm old enough. It won't be very long from now, just a year or two! I have already been practicing my sword-play with sticks and with implements from the kitchens. Do you want to see? We can pretend to duel, and whoever wins gets to be the King of Outer Gondor. I wager King Elessar will be very impressed with us!'","The entrance to Ost Arndír is to the north-east of Iáphel, in Pinnath Gelin.","King Elessar's next destination is to be Ost Arndír in Pinnath Gelin.","Orgolas is in Thorongil's room in Ost Arndír.","According to Hebron, various dangers can be found in the vicinity of Ost Arndír, and the folk of the town would appreciate you helping deal with them.","Talk to Thorongil inside his room in the keep of Ost Arndír","Chapter 4.2: A Knight of the Green Hills","'I am pleased to see you among the Green Hills, King Elessar and Queen Arwen! You and all your company are welcome to stay for as long as it pleases you. Know that there are dangers still in Pinnath Gelin, for Haradrim fighters were transported here on Corsair ships during the war, and my knights have not yet found them all. Raiders from Umbar, too, have come up the rivers in small boats and harry our people. But I see warriors among your company, and if they exercise caution they should fear little.\
\
'I understand you have brought Golasgil's heir Orgolas with you on this visit? My son Thorongil will be delighted to entertain a boy of his own years! Perhaps this ${RACE}, ${PLAYER}, will show Orgolas to my son's chambers? You will find them to the north-east, through the door on the right.'","'Hirluin's daughter is named Nauriel, and she is high in the order of knights that protects Pinnath Gelin; it is the tradition in this land that women may also wield sword and sceptre. She is married to Carandolion, who is the brother of Duinhir of the Blackroot Vale, though I recall the two are quite different in temper. The son of Nauriel and Carandolion is named Thorongil, and must now be about ten years old.'\
\
Elessar nods.\
\
'Yes, I am afraid Hirluin spoke often of our campaign in Umbar, and while it has been many years since I wore the name \\qThorongil,\\q his grandson was given that name in remembrance of me. I would prefer you not speak of it to Nauriel or her son. There must be few in Outer Gondor these days who know the warrior Thorongil and the King Elessar for the same man, and I would like to keep it that way.\
\
'Ost Arndír is to the north-east of Iáphel. Let us travel there now before Grethril burdens our pack-horses with more bottles of wine than we need. To speak honestly, this may have happened already.'","Travel to the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír, north-east of Iáphel","Talk to Hebron in Ost Arndír","Talk to Thorongil outside the keep of Ost Arndír","Defeat foes throughout Pinnath Gelin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Back home in Lond Cirion, Aerhant often lets me climb the tower and look out over the Sea, and I have seen a great many Corsair ships going here and there across the waves! Once when the sky was clear I thought I could see all the way to Umbar, but he said that wasn't possible. But I have very sharp eyes, just like my father did, and he was a great mariner and fought bravely at the Black Gate of Mordor.\
\
'I will be fine, ${PLAYER}. You can go now.'","Hebron nods in welcome","The Lady Nauriel is inside the main hall of Ost Arndír, located upstairs inside the keep.","Defeated foes throughout Pinnath Gelin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Hebron outside the keep of Ost Arndír","'You have taken care of some foes of Pinnath Gelin? I am grateful for your service on behalf of Ost Arndír and the Lady Nauriel. I see why the King has made you a part of his travelling company!'","'Can I ask you to deal with any of the foes that encroach upon our lands? There is no shortage of threats throughout many of the Green Hills.'","Hebron is outside the northern entrance to the keep of Ost Arndír.","Talk to Orgolas in Thorongil's room inside the keep of Ost Arndír","Talk to Lady Nauriel in Ost Arndír","'I have been practicing my sword-play. I am already very skilled, ask anyone!'","Thorongil is in his room north of the main hall, inside the keep of Ost Arndír.","Thorongil is outside the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír.","'I will be fine, ${PLAYER}. You can go now.'","'Welcome to Ost Arndír, home of the Lady Nauriel, Knight of the Green Hills and Lord of Pinnath Gelin. She awaits you inside the hall.'","Talk to Hebron outside the northern entrance of the keep in Ost Arndír","Hebron is outside the northern entrance of the keep in Ost Arndír.","Nauriel's son Thorongil's room is to the north-east, through the door on the right.","'I am afraid Hirluin spoke often of our campaign in Umbar, and while it has been many years since I wore the name \\qThorongil,\\q his grandson was given that name in remembrance of me. I would prefer you not speak of it to Nauriel or her son. There must be few in Outer Gondor these days who know the warrior Thorongil and the King Elessar for the same man, and I would like to keep it that way.\
\
'Ost Arndír is to the north-east of Iáphel. Let us travel there now before Grethril burdens our pack-horses with more bottles of wine than we need.'","'Do you often befriend liars, ${PLAYER}, and encourage them to speak untruths? Because Orgolas here has told me something surprising, and there is no way it could be true!\
\
'He says that King Elessar adventured with my grandsire Hirluin in Umbar, many years ago, and that he is the \\qThorongil\\q for whom I was named!'","'What is this tumult?'"},
[3125]={"Imák snorts rudely","Defeat Angmarim in Elderslade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Thálfi is at Zudramdân in Elderslade.","Extensive palisades and Orkish totems bolster the defences before Gundabad","'Are all Longbeards so trusting, so willing to rely upon blind faith? A Stout-axe does not sit idly by, waiting for the tide of fortune to turn. He takes action!'","Imák is at Zudramdân in Elderslade, and he wishes to speak with you.","Talk to Imák at Zudramdân in Elderslade","The Angmarim have established a settlement in the shadow of the three peaks","Defeated Orc-kind in Elderslade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Thálfi wants you to scout enemy camps nearer to Gundabad and to defeat any Orcs and Angmarim you find on the way. This time he has not asked you to draw the locations on a map, and will rely instead upon your report. Crossing the bridge in front of Gundabad and exploring past the central courtyard on your way to the buildings beyond the entrance should be sufficient.","Thálfi is worried that the forces defending Gundabad need a more thorough scouting, but they will not give you the benefit of leisurely adding their camps to your map.","Defeat Orc-kind in Elderslade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Find those camps nearer to Gundabad and see what there is to see, slaying whatever Orcs are foolish enough to cross your path. Trouble not to draw these camps on the map; I will rely upon your report and not your artist's hand!'","'What is this Stout-axe trying to say?'","Scout the central courtyard in front of Gundabad","Chapter 4.2: No Time To Draw!","Scout the bridge in front of Gundabad","Scout the settlement of Dûn Traikh beyond the entrance to Gundabad","Talk to Thálfi at Zudramdân in Elderslade","The bridge before Gundabad crosses a raging river: a defensible position","'I need you to scout the camps nearer to Gundabad now, ${PLAYER}. Trouble not to draw these on the map, for I suspect the enemy presence at these locations will afford you no time to draw! No, this time I ask you simply to observe the situation nearer to Gundabad, and then report back to me what you saw.\
\
'Perhaps it goes without saying, but please be careful. And this too: defeat any Orcs and Angmarim in your way!'","Defeated Angmarim in Elderslade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Thank you, my friend! What did you learn of the enemy presence nearer to the gates of Gundabad?'\
\
You give Thálfi your report, and he makes some notations on the map.\
\
'Yes, I see. We were both right: there is no shortage of foes! Perhaps by studying this information Prince Durin will find some weakness in the line. Hmm... no such vulnerability makes itself known to me, but I am only a scout, and not a master strategist. I have faith in the prince and his advisors. One of them will surely see something.'"},
[3126]={"Zaghárog told you to walk to the north-west. Will this provide your answer?","Talk to Harthalín by the road to Nargroth","The watching-stone inhabited by the spirit Zaghárog is on the road to the Caverns of Fire, in Talath Úrui.","The creature falls dead. May this be enough for Zaghárog","'They will meet to the north-west? That is all he has given us?'","Mount Doom fills your vision, and you know at once: the Masters will meet on the slopes of Orodruin","'You have done as the spirit asked. Now let us see if he will do as he promised.'","There is silence in your mind for so long you begin to doubt that Zaghárog will speak to you. Then, just as you are about to turn away, the presence returns. The questioning sea buffets you as before.\
\
'Where will the Masters seek to meet?' you ask of the spirit. The only reply is silence.\
\
'Have such meetings occurred before?' you try again, but Zaghárog does not reply. The questioning sea recedes, leaving behind only sand and silt. Skeletal fish wriggle madly on the dry bed, gasping and dying.\
\
Then you notice their number: nine fish die in the water's absence. The presence in the darkness that is Zaghárog watches you closely, and the fish are gone. A sudden flash of light blinds you with its brilliance, and you recognize a flat space with sparse trees near many falls, in the southern reaches of Lhingris. Hateful chittering fills your ears, and you know there is a malevolent creature behind you, but you are unable to turn and face it. Then you hear the voice of Atli Spider-bane, and you know he hunts the creature that stalks you.\
\
Zaghárog makes his demand, and his desire fills your mind and echoes in your ears.\
\
'Kill,' he says.","Zaghárog told you to walk to the north-west","'Where will the Masters meet?' you ask once again, and Zaghárog shows you the nine dying fish, inexplicably and inexorably breathing their last.\
\
Finally, the images fade, and your feet are compelled to walk to the north-west. Zaghárog remains, nursing his disappointment, but you are confident that he has given you what you need.","'Thank you for finishing the job, ${PLAYER}! That was quite a fight!'","Chapter 4.2: The Only Place","The images return. You recognize a flat space with sparse trees near many falls, in the southern reaches of Lhingris. Hateful chittering fills your ears, and you know there is a malevolent creature  behind you, but you are unable to turn and face it. Then you hear the voice of Atli Spider-bane, and you know he hunts the creature that stalks you.\
\
Zaghárog makes his demand, and his desire fills your mind and echoes in your ears.\
\
'Kill,' he says.","Find the area in Lhingris near the falls, and fulfill Zaghárog's demand","Harthalín believes the meeting of the Masters will take place, but if you are to make use of this information you must learn what location each of them might trust.","'Of course! How did I not see it? Orodruin stands between the lands the Masters of Mordor have claimed for themselves, and on the slopes of Mount Doom they will feel most secure from the treachery of their rivals!\
\
'That is where the meeting will take place, I am certain of it.'","'I do not trust this creature, but he may have seen that which is hidden to us.'","Unlike your previous visit, Zaghárog does not make you wait this time. He is present immediately, with a hungering and eager need.\
\
'The spider is slain,' you say, and Zaghárog's confusion is apparent. You see the hidden gully in Lhingris once again, and feel the stalking shadow, and hear Atli Spider-bane bellow his battle-cry. A feeling of great insistence spears at you, over and over.\
\
'The spider,' you say once again, and Zaghárog responds at once: 'The dwarf.'\
\
'No,' you respond.\
\
You are buffeted by disappointment and anger. The spirit's rage is a crushing ceiling that presses down on you. It is a cauldron of boiling fire that scalds you. It is a torrent of icy rain that freezes and pierces your skin. It passes, and Zaghárog's rage is replaced with a sullen resentment.\
\
'Where will the Masters meet?' you ask once again, and Zaghárog shows you the nine dying fish, inexplicably and inexorably breathing their last.\
\
Finally, the images fade, and your feet are compelled to walk to the north-west. Zaghárog remains, nursing his disappointment, but you are confident that he has given you what you need.","'Zaghárog has proven he gives nothing for free, ${PLAYER}. What has he asked you to do this time?'","'There is one who has demonstrated a familiarity of this land to us. Do you remember? I do not trust him, for who truly could, but he has watched the movements of our enemies and knows somewhat of their motivations.\
\
'I speak of Zaghárog, ${PLAYER}. The spirit in the stone may have seen more than we, and know of the place the Masters will settle upon for their council.'","Harthalín is by the road to Nargroth, on the eastern edge of Talath Úrui.","Zaghárog showed you a particular area in Lhingris and asked you to kill the creature there.","'I have had an idea, ${PLAYER}. Each of the Masters of Mordor has walked this land longer than either of us, and they know its out of the way corners better than we could ever hope to do. Even I, who fought during the Siege of Barad-dûr at the end of the Second Age and saw the shape of the land then, cannot pretend to the knowledge of those who seek to rule Mordor now.\
\
'But there is one who has demonstrated such knowledge of this land to us. Do you remember? I do not trust him, for who truly could, but he has watched the movements of our enemies and knows somewhat of their motivations.\
\
'I speak of Zaghárog, ${PLAYER}. The spirit in the stone may have seen more than we, and know of the place the Masters will settle upon for their council.'","Talk to Zaghárog outside the Caverns of Fire, in Talath Úrui"},
[3127]={"'I told him not to do it, but he would not listen to me. Now he is halfway up the rigging of the Wave-hunter, even though I told him he should not climb it! It is my ship, ${PLAYER}, given to me by my father, and Thorongil should do what I say, and not what I forbid, concerning it!'","'You worry too much, ${PLAYER}. I was not in any danger, but even if I was I would not be afraid. I am no coward!\
\
'I was named for the great hero Thorongil, sword-brother of my grandsire Hirluin and mighty hero of Gondor! He warred with Umbar, many years ago, and I have heard from the men-at-arms of Ost Arndír that even today the Umbarrim tremble when they speak his name! I am going to follow in his footsteps as soon as I am old enough to become a Knight of the Green Hills. And that is the truth, unlike whatever lies Orgolas insists on telling! To think King Elessar might be the same man as Thorongil of old? Pig slop!\
\
'I tire of this ship, anyway. Orgolas's mother sent the Wave-hunter here during the war, and it did not even see any fighting! What a waste that is!'","'Thorongil and I are about the same age, but I think he is... I don't know...'\
\
Orgolas kicks a small stone into the water, and the ripples run up against the side of the Wave-hunter before dispersing.\
\
'He is rather childish, isn't he? He says he will soon become a Knight of the Green Hills, but I think he is too rash, and too unthinking, and too... I don't know. A proper knight should not be any of those things, ${PLAYER}! He does not give a thought for any of his people, and speaks only of his own glory. And I was telling the truth about King Elessar!\
\
'I suppose we should return to Ost Arndír.'","The northern entrance to the keep of Ost Arndír is west of the Wave-hunter.","There is no stopping them","Thorongil is high above your head in the rigging of the Wave-hunter.","You should tell someone where they plan to go","Orgolas stands near the Wave-hunter.","Orgolas is near the Wave-hunter, peering up at the rigging.","'We should get him to come down, if we can.'","'I tire of this ship. It bores me.'","Daeram is near the Wave-hunter.","The boys have run off on their adventure.","Return to the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír, west of the Wave-hunter","Hebron stares at you with apprehension","Orgolas is outside the keep of Ost Arndír.","'The boys are safe? Thank the Valar!\
\
'A scout has just arrived from Tûm Rost, driving his horse beyond exhaustion. The Corsairs have attacked in force!'","'What if he falls, ${PLAYER}? At least Orgolas had sense enough to stay on solid ground! I am not burdened with the duty of protecting Thorongil.\
\
'Still... I do not want him to fall. But thank the Valar it is not Orgolas up there. Lady Marra would cook me on a spit and serve me to her guests.'","'He should not be up there! The Wave-hunter is my ship!'","'Why should I?' Thorongil calls down to you","Wait for Thorongil to come down","Hebron is outside the keep of Ost Arndír.","'That is not far from here to the east. Quickly now!'","From the deck of the Wave-hunter, <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> for Thorongil to come down","'Orgolas must think I know nothing at all if he believes I will fall for this falsehood!'","'What? Orgolas has left the keep with Nauriel's son? Already? We only just arrived! How can he have already slipped my watch and disappeared?'\
\
You tell Daeram that the boys intended to see the Wave-hunter where it is docked, and he breathes a sigh of relief.\
\
'That is not far from here to the east. Quickly now!'","'Look there!'","Orgolas and Thorongil intended to go to the Wave-hunter, docked to the east on the lake in Pinnath Gelin.","'I suppose we should return to Ost Arndír.'","Talk to Hebron outside the keep of Ost Arndír","Chapter 4.3: His Namesake","Talk to Orgolas near the Wave-hunter","Find Daeram at the keep's kitchens in Ost Arndír and tell him where the boys planned to go","Talk to Orgolas outside the keep of Ost Arndír","'But it is true! I am not lying! I heard King Elessar say he was the very same Thorongil that adventured with Hirluin and Forlong in Umbar so many years ago! It is true! Tell him, ${PLAYER}! I wish Thorongil would believe me! But he is going to take me to see the Wave-hunter where it sits at dock, and I do want to see the ship my father left to me, so...'\
\
You tell the boys they should not go alone, but they pay you no mind.","'He should not be up there!'","Thorongil grudgingly descends to the deck of the Wave-hunter","Find Orgolas and Thorongil near the Wave-hunter","'He is just making it up! One look at the King tells me he could not be old enough to have been of fighting age when my grandsire Hirluin adventured in Umbar! To think Orgolas believes I would fall for such falsehoods! I tell you I am smarter than that!'","Orgolas peers up at the rigging of the Wave-hunter","Talk to Thorongil on the deck of the Wave-hunter","Thorongil is eager to show his new friend the sights and sounds of Pinnath Gelin, and to make a memorable first impression.","Thorongil stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter.","From the deck of the Wave-hunter you should <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> for Thorongil to come down.","Daeram is inside the kitchens of the keep in Ost Arndír.","You should cross onto the deck of the Wave-hunter in order to get Thorongil to come down.","Talk to Daeram near the Wave-hunter","High above you, Thorongil clings to the rigging of the Wave-hunter","Cross onto the deck of the Wave-hunter"},
[3128]={"Talk to Mithrandir at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate","'As I told you already, I will do what I can. I will send the clothes along to you when they are finished.'","'¿Sí? ¿Qué es lo que quieres?'","You have found a group of Nurnhoth trying to become used to their new lives","If you are to attend the meeting of the Masters of Mordor in secret, you will need some way to remain hidden: a disguise.","Chapter 4.3: Raiment of Disguise","'Did you arrange for a disguise? It is nearly time!'","Talk to Mithrandir in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, south of the entrance to the city","Find the group of freed Nurnhoth on the north-east side of the Third Circle","'You wish for me to modify these garments so you may wear them? Are you sure you would not prefer the latest fashions of the city instead? These are little more than dirty rags!\
\
'Very well, I will do what I can. I will send them along to you when they are finished.'","Ayorzén has followed you to the tailor, and is now on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle, seeking to get your attention.","'We are doing the best we can. It is not easy.'","'You are up to something, ${PLAYER}. I overheard your directions for the tailor, and there can be only one reason for you to wear the clothes of the Nurnhoth. You plan to sneak into one of the fortresses in Mordor! Do not try to deny it. Ayorzén knows whatever you might say would be a lie; he is often called Ayorzén the Perceptive, after all.'\
\
Ayorzén looks from side to side and shifts his weight from one foot to the other. When he speaks again, the words come in a rush and a tumble, as if he were embarrassed to speak them.\
\
'There are none in this city that Ayorzén would consider a friend, but you may be nearest to that lofty prize, ${PLAYER}. If you do not get yourself killed climbing the walls of Seregost, or rattling the bars of Naerband, you might hope to achieve my friendship, in time! But Ayorzén does not befriend corpses.'\
\
Ayorzén speaks more softly now, and his words are earnest in a way you have rarely heard from the Khundolar chief.\
\
'I think you are a fool to attempt this, but I will share something with you in the hope that it may improve your chance of survival. The bosses pay no heed to their servants or their slaves, as long as they are obedient. That will change in an instant if the servant disobeys. You must do whatever you are commanded to do, or they will see through your disguise. This should serve you well with Ugrukhôr, Dulgabêth, or any of their minions.\
\
'But there is one you should beware, in any circumstance. Whatever Urudanî has become, I do not think she will be blinded by your appearance. She may be more sensitive to your deception. You must try and keep away from Urudanî, at any cost.\
\
'I have done all I can do, ${PLAYER}. It is more than anyone else would do, but this city is confusing and unpleasant, and if I am stuck here I would rather have someone such as you to hear my complaints. Keep that in mind when you sojourn on your foolish errand, and let it inspire you to subtlety!'","'Use the clothes I gave to you to help put an end to Ugrukhôr and the others like him. May they be of use to you, and I will try not to feel their loss overmuch. It will not be easy, but it will be worth it if this act helps free my people and put an end to their misery and torment in Mordor.'","Ayorzén followed you to the tailor, and now he seeks to get your attention","'I bundled the garments for you. You will have them when you need them.'","'Bring those clothes to the tailor on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle and he will fashion a disguise of the appropriate size for you.'","'We are... we are doing the best we can. It is not easy.'","Hujâ is among a group of freed Nurnhoth on the north-east side of the Third Circle, in Minas Tirith.","'The Gúrzyul, and indeed many others in Mordor, rely upon their slaves for labour and the many menial tasks that keep the iron wheel of Gorgoroth turning. As a result, obedient slaves often pass beneath notice; I suspect that the Masters of Mordor do not even see them, though they rely upon their presence. If you were to obtain the rags worn by the freed Nurnhoth that were brought to the city, a tailor in Minas Tirith might be able to fashion a suitable disguise for you.\
\
'I last saw some of the freed Nurnhoth on the north-east side of the Third Circle, trying to become comfortable in their new home.'","'Yes, ${PLAYER}? What brings you back to the city? Have you learned if Lhaereth is near to achieving her goal?'\
\
You tell Mithrandir that Harthalín is studying the effects of athelas on the samples you collected in Agarnaith, but that you have learned a meeting of the Masters of Mordor will occur on the slope of Orodruin.\
\
'You intend to gain access to this meeting? You might learn much that would be of use, but it will be very dangerous. You will need raiment of disguise if you are to avoid detection. Ah! I know what will serve.\
\
'The Gúrzyul, and indeed many others in Mordor, rely upon their slaves for labour and the many menial tasks that keep the iron wheel of Gorgoroth turning. As a result, obedient slaves often pass beneath notice; I suspect that the Masters of Mordor do not even see them, though they rely upon their presence. If you were to obtain the rags worn by the freed Nurnhoth that were brought to the city, a tailor in Minas Tirith might be able to fashion a suitable disguise for you. I last saw some of the freed Nurnhoth on the north-east side of the Third Circle, trying to become comfortable in their new home.\
\
'I will meet you at Cirith Gorgor when you have arranged for a disguise with the tailor.'","Mithrandir is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, south of the entrance to the city.","The tailor has finished resizing the Nurnhoth garments and bundles them for you","'I think you are a fool to attempt this, but I will share something with you in the hope that it may improve your chance of survival. The bosses pay no heed to their servants or their slaves, as long as they are obedient. That will change in an instant if the servant disobeys. You must do whatever you are commanded to do, or they will see through your disguise. This should serve you well with Ugrukhôr, Dulgabêth, or any of their minions.\
\
'But there is one you should beware, in any circumstance. Whatever Urudanî has become, I do not think she will be blinded by your appearance. She may be more sensitive to your deception. You must try and keep away from Urudanî, at any cost.'","The tailor on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle will be able to fashion a disguise of the appropriate size from the Nurnhoth clothes that were given to you by Hujâ.","Talk to Ayorzén on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle","'It will be easier to gain access to this meeting in the open air than it would be to pass the guards of Seregost, or any of the fortresses of Mordor, but that is not to say it will be a simple matter. You will need a disguise of some kind to get near to any of the Masters without their knowledge, but what sort of raiment will serve that purpose I cannot say.\
\
'Mithrandir may know better than I, ${PLAYER}. Return to him in Minas Tirith and consult the Wizard, and I will continue to monitor Lhaereth's progress in plague-making.'","Bring the Nurnhoth clothes to Lain, a tailor on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle","'You are not here to send us back to Mordor? Promise me!'\
\
Hujâ listens to your request, and slowly his look of fear is replaced with caution.\
\
'You do not want to do this, ${PLAYER}. Arâm and Itli were in the service of Ugrukhôr's table, and the tales they have told of his cruelty are beyond belief. If you try to deceive him, you will be found out, and death could not come swiftly enough for you.\
\
'I retained the clothes I wore in servitude, for some part of me believed I would not long be free of it. There was a part of me, too, that feared to dispose of them. Why? The reason must appear foolish to you, but I thought if I no longer had them at hand I would forget the time I spent in servitude, or the family and friends I lost in those years.\
\
'I will give them to you for this reason, ${PLAYER}: that you will use them to help put an end to Ugrukhôr and the others like him, for Arâm and for Itli and for their families and mine. May they be of use to you, and I will try not to feel their loss overmuch. It will not be easy, but it will be worthwhile if this act helps free my people and puts an end to their misery and torment in Mordor.'","A group of freed Nurnhoth might be found on the north-east side of the Third Circle, in Minas Tirith.","Mithrandir is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","'Every moment that comes I think we will be brought back. I cannot believe this will last.'","'You will need a disguise of some kind to get near to any of the Masters without their knowledge, but what sort of raiment will serve that purpose I cannot say.\
\
'Mithrandir may know better than I, ${PLAYER}. Return to him in Minas Tirith and consult the Wizard, and I will continue to monitor Lhaereth's progress in plague-making.'","With some reluctance but a hopeful smile, Hujâ gives you a bundle of rags","Talk to Hujâ on the north-east side of the Third Circle, in Minas Tirith"},
[3129]={"'I don't know about this, ${PLAYER}. Setting traps? Trying to win a battle through deceit? Imák is not wrong about this, at least: these strategies belong to the Orcs! If it is up to me, I say they can keep them.\
\
'I have finished the scouting map. Here, I give it you so you can deliver it to Durin at Annâk-khurfu. Will you also bring him word of my discomfort with Imák's plan? I do not think dwarves should rely upon traps in this way, and I am sure the prince will agree.'","'I want you to gather heavy rocks from the base of cliffs and some of the explosives carried by goblins throughout Elderslade. Depriving our enemies of these items will surely help to tilt the field in our favour.'","Talk to Prince Ingór on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu","Collect loose rocks from the base of cliffs in Elderslade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Thálfi is at Zudramdân in Elderslade.","Imák is at Zudramdân in Elderslade.\
\
You have collected a number of sapper-bombs and loose rocks and should bring them back to Imák.","Collected sapper-bombs for Imák (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have returned with tidings from Thálfi?'\
\
You hand Durin your map of Elderslade with Thálfi's annotations. While he studies the defensive layout before Gundabad, you tell him about Imák's plan to use traps against the enemy forces.\
\
'The Stout-axe is not wrong: given the opportunity, the Orcs would prefer not to face us in a fair fight. That is not the Longbeard way. It is not my way.'\
\
He draws some lines on the map with a bit of charcoal and hands it back to you.\
\
'But we must reclaim Gundabad, at any cost. If the traps Imák has devised will help us in this, I will not command him otherwise. Do not think the battle will be won with deception alone! The greatest share of the burden will fall upon the swords and axes of my Gabil'akkâ!\
\
'Show that map to Prince Ingór downstairs, and have him agree that his Zhélruka will move in these marked formations when the fighting begins. It is nearly time to begin the assault!'","Collected loose rocks for Imák (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Durin is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.","Goblins carry sapper-bombs that Imák wants for his plan. He also wants you to collect some loose, heavy rocks from the base of cliffs north of Zudramdân in Elderslade.","'Durin sends you to ME with a plan for the first attack? Why should he not wait for my plan? I have my own scouts, and I trust their word more than any of his!'\
\
Prince Ingór takes the map from you and studies it with distaste. Then he produces his own piece of charcoal and obscures Durin's notes with his own.\
\
'I have some reservations with this plan. Take this map back to the Longbeard and tell him I have improved it.'","Talk to Thálfi at Zudramdân","'Victory is a step closer now. Even this Longbeard should see it. Or does he not wish to reclaim Gundabad after all?'","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu","'We are out of time, ${PLAYER}! I have received word that an army of Orcs has emerged from Gundabad, and they march now on our position!'\
\
You give him the map marked with Prince Ingór's annotations and he hands it to one of his lieutenants.\
\
'The time for planning is over! The war is upon us!'","Thálfi catches your eye. He seems unhappy about something","'Deliver that map to Durin at Annâk-khurfu. Will you also bring him word of my discomfort with Imák's plan? I do not think dwarves should rely upon traps in this way, and I am sure the prince will agree.'","'Durin's Longbeards, like this scout here, must be willing to do whatever it takes if they are to have victory in Gundabad. Their combat prowess will not be enough, not by itself. Do you think the Orcs will face the dwarves in a fair fight? No! They will do whatever they can to gain an advantage, and so too should we.\
\
'It is a lesson I learned in Mordor, and I learned it well: Durin must think like his foes if he is to have the greatest chance of success. If he wants to have the victory, he will need to think like a goblin!\
\
'I have a plan, ${PLAYER}. I want you to gather heavy rocks from the base of cliffs and some of the explosives carried by goblins throughout Elderslade. Depriving our enemies of these items will surely help to tilt the field in our favour.'","'These will do nicely, ${PLAYER}. I have in mind a number of traps that will prove most harmful for our enemies, and surely turn the tide in our favour.\
\
'Victory is a step closer now.'","Chapter 4.3: Think Like A Goblin","Imák does not believe that the Longbeards are adequately prepared for the assault on Gundabad, and he wants to adopt a different approach.","Collect sapper-bombs from goblins in Elderslade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Prince Ingór is on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu.","'Show that map to Prince Ingór below, and have him agree that his Zhélruka will move in these marked formations when the fighting begins. It is nearly time to begin the assault!'","Bring the goblin-bombs and loose rocks to Imák at Zudramdân","'Bring my misgivings back to Durin.'"},
[3130]={"'Then let us depart for Tûm Rost with all haste!'","'I think there is reason to believe the Corsairs will not harm Thorongil, Nauriel. They will see value in keeping him alive to use in a potential bargain with Gondor. If we act rashly we might endanger the boy's life; we must not risk that.\
\
'I want to send someone to follow the ships. We must track them from shore, and see where they sail. It is not certain they will return directly to Umbar, and if they put in at a cove along the Langstrand we may be able to rescue Thorongil before he is brought back to the Kindred of the Coins.\
\
'What say you, ${PLAYER}? Are you prepared for a chase?'","Talk to Nauriel in Ost Arndír","Talk to King Elessar in Ost Arndír","Chapter 4.4: Raiders In Tûm Rost","'This outrage cannot stand! I will wage such war upon the Corsairs that they will not sail within sight of Gondor for a thousand years! I will call to arms every knight that has ever raised sword within Pinnath Gelin to follow me and rescue my son!'","Talk to King Elessar in the keep of Ost Arndír and join the defence of Tûm Rost","Talk to King Elessar in the main hall of the keep of Ost Arndír","King Elessar hopes to bring his own fighters to join the defence of Tûm Rost against the Corsair raiders.","Talk to Nauriel in the main hall of the keep of Ost Arndír","Nauriel is inside the main hall of the keep in Ost Arndír.","'I will dispatch our soldiers at once. Are you with us, Elessar?'","'We will fight alongside you to defend the Green Hills, Nauriel. Count my warriors among your number!\
\
'Are you prepared for this, ${PLAYER}? Tell me when you are ready to depart for Tûm Rost.'","'The Lady Nauriel prepares a response to deal with the Corsair raiders. Hurry now to her side, for there is little time to waste if we are to save the folk of Tûm Rost!'","'A number of Corsair ships have sailed in secret up the Hathollant river, and now they pillage the farms and villages of Tûm Rost. I will dispatch our soldiers at once. Are you with us, Elessar?'","Tûm Rost has been attacked by Corsair raiders, and now the folk of Pinnath Gelin must spring to its defence.","'I will slay every Corsair that thinks to keep my son from me!'","King Elessar is inside the main hall of the keep in Ost Arndír.","King Elessar is inside the main hall of the keep of Ost Arndír."},
[3132]={"Talk to Mithrandir at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate","'You learned much of value at Amon Thaur, but it has not eased my worries! Indeed, it has caused them to increase in potency. Where before the Masters of Mordor vied among themselves for control, and it seemed they might waste years on their infighting, now they have set aside many of their differences, at least for the time being.\
\
'This is the worst outcome for Gondor, my friend. Mordor has been united beneath a common purpose. I... I do not know what to do, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
His words hang in the air, unexpected and unwelcome.\
\
'I need to think, my friend. I will call for you when I have decided what can be done. It cannot be long. It must not.\
\
'Lhaereth and her allies will not wait for us to be ready.'","Mithrandir is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","The Meeting of the Masters is about to commence, and you have arranged for a disguise that should allow you to attend in secret.","Talk to Mithrandir and travel to the meeting of the Masters of Mordor","Chapter 4.4: Union of Evil","'Exercise caution, ${PLAYER}. You will go into danger and must remain below their notice or none will be able to save you.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'You have returned just in time, for it seems the meeting is soon to commence. Spies have reported large enemy groups moving toward Orodruin from different strongholds in Gorgoroth. They appear to be making for Amon Thaur, a structure on the side of Mount Doom.\
 \
'Are you prepared? Speak to me when you are ready to leave, but do not take too long! Time is short, and you must not miss this meeting!'"},
[3133]={"Chapter 4.5: Hammer, Axe, and Sword","You hear the sound of many dwarves shouting to the north","'There was a great sound of shouting to the north-west! Perhaps my cousin is there?'","'There was a great sound of shouting from the north-west! Perhaps my cousin is there?'","'The Zhélruka release their weapons only when slain! Collect the weapons by their corpses and store them in a barrel at the trench to the north-west so they can be wielded by Longbeards who cast aside their own weapons when the fighting turned fierce!'","Bori, standing nearby, calls your name","Bring the Zhélruka weapons to the weapon crate in the trench to the north-west","Find the retreating dwarves Bósi saw near the trench to the north","You found Trausti in a trench not far from the lakeside while the fighting rages all about him and the War of Three Peaks continues.","Bori is in the trench north-west of Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks.","Bori wanted you to look for his cousin Bróin or his father Bósi north-west of his trench. He has not seen them since the fighting began, and he is worried for their safety.","Trausti calls to you as you approach","Bósi told you he saw dwarves retreating from thick fighting to the north. You should search there for Bróin.","'Ready yourself, ${PLAYER}! They prepare for another assault!'","Collect fallen Zhélruka weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I thought Gundabad had unleashed all of its defenders upon us, but it was not so! Another wave of enemies emerged from the mountain, forcing us to give ground!'","Defeat enemy forces during the War of Three Peaks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated enemy forces (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Trausti in the trench not far from the lakeside during the War of Three Peaks","Collected Zhélruka weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Bori in the trench north-west of Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks","'I have not been able to get north-west of this trench. Perhaps my father or cousin were pushed that way during the fighting!'","Prince Ingór wants you to pick up weapons dropped by his slain warriors as proof that the Zhélruka are shouldering their own share of the war's burden. You should also slay any enemies that break through the line.","Ingór is furious at Durin's suggestion that the Zhélruka prince kept his forces in reserve during the initial assault of the War of Three Peaks.","'I bristle at these accusations, and refute them! My Zhélruka have fought and died as bravely as any two Longbeards, and if Durin calls me coward he will answer to my axe! He seeks proof that my Zhélruka have paid the price? Look then upon the corpses of my slain, and gather their fallen weapons! Then you will see that my own folk have done their share... nay, more than their share!\
\
'The Zhélruka release their weapons only when slain! Collect the weapons by their corpses and store them in a barrel at the trench to the north-west so they can be wielded by Longbeards who cast aside their own weapons when the fighting turned fierce! Durin speaks to me of cowardice? He should look to his own!'","Find Bróin or Bósi north-west of Bori's trench","'${PLAYER}, have you seen my father or cousin? I lost track of them after the first assault, and I have not been able to find them amid the chaos. Can you look for them? I want to make sure they are still all right.\
\
'I have not been able to search beyond this trench to the north-west. Perhaps they were pushed that way during the fighting!'","A crate for storing spare weapons can be found in a trench north-west of Prince Ingór's defensive position during the War of Three Peaks."},
[3134]={"A mighty Ent stares at you from within the curious, deep wells of his eyes.","Search the grove to the south-west for sign of the Corsairs","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> out over the water for the fleeing Corsair ships","Talk to Arasdil on the coast of Thingast","Arasdil stands nearby, and has something to say to you.","'My son is depending upon your haste, ${PLAYER}. Do not fail him.'","Talk to the Ent in the shady grove","You have found a spot from which you might see distant ships","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> out over the water for the fleeing Corsair ships from the coast of Thingast","King Elessar directed you to hurry south along the coast of Anfalas, in pursuit of the fleeing Corsair ships.","There seems to be no immediate sign of Corsairs at this grove","'I want you to return to Anfalas as quickly as you can, my friend, and to look for sign of the retreating Corsair ships from the coast of Thingast. If it can be managed, we need to know what direction they sail as they leave the river.\
\
'We will follow after you, but a larger company must move more slowly than one ${RACE}. Once you determine the direction of the Corsair ships, you will find me at Lond Cirion. Go with utmost haste, my friend! Much depends on what you can learn of their course.'","Another location on the coast to the west may allow you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over the water in search of the fleeing Corsair ships.","Examine the high-quality bow on the stone block","'I have not seen these Corsair ships return, but I did see them going up-river a few days gone. From hiding I watched their crew come ashore, bearing torches and shouting commands. They visited the haunted grove to the south-west... foolish idea, of course, that's a place decent folk don't go, and still haven't! Who would count a Corsair decent, after all?\
\
'Anyway, they were inside for just a quarter of an hour or so, and when they emerged they reboarded their ships and sailed up the river. I told the town guard back home, so do not think I haven't done my share! But I am just a fisherman, and even the guardsmen knew better than to get mixed up with two ships of Corsair raiders!\
\
'You think they might keep a secret store of goods or weapons in that grove? Strangdene it is called by my people, and I tell you again it is haunted. You won't see me creeping about in there, and if you've more wisdom than foolish courage, you won't go inside either! Good day to you.'","Arasdil told you he saw Corsair activity at the haunted grove to the south-west before the ships sailed toward Pinnath Gelin.","You feel the sudden sensation of being watched.","Find a spot further to the west from which you might spy distant ships","You can't quite make out what the distant shapes on the water might be","This is a good spot from which to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for distant ships","A deep, rumbling sound seems to come from all around you","'Fleeing Corsair ships? No, I have not seen anything of that sort today, for I have only just arrived from Melgobas. You say they would be coming down the river?\
\
'Doubtless these are not the tidings you need, but I did see your ships going up-river a few days gone. From hiding I watched their crew come ashore, bearing torches and shouting commands. They visited the haunted grove to the south-west... foolish idea, of course, that's a place decent folk don't go, and still haven't! Who would count a Corsair decent, after all?\
\
'Anyway, they were inside for just a quarter of an hour or so, and when they emerged they reboarded their ships and sailed up the river. I told the town guard back home, so do not think I haven't done my share! But I am just a fisherman, and even the guardsmen knew better than to get mixed up with two ships of Corsair raiders!\
\
'You think they might keep a secret store of goods or weapons in that grove? Strangdene it is called, and I tell you again it is haunted. You won't see me creeping about in there, and if you've more wisdom than foolish courage, you won't go inside either! Good day to you.'","The hazy sky over the water hides from your sight any retreating ships","Mantente en guardia","From this location on the coast you should <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over the water in search of the fleeing Corsair ships.","Travel to the southern coast of Thingast, south-west of Lond Cirion, in Anfalas","This bow is of unusually high quality and is in fine repair","Chapter 4.5: The Chase","A high quality bow rests on a stone within the grove here.","'You there... small one...\
\
'Have you come here to Tumbamálë... to bring tidings of my friend... Nestinanessornë...?'","King Elessar wants you to travel with haste to the coast near Thingast, south-west of Lond Cirion, in Anfalas."},
[3135]={"Bróin helps Slagvi to safety!","It might be a good idea to check on the goblin-bombs, just in case","The dwarf Afwald stands near the empty crate where Imák stored the goblin-bombs, in Zarkul-sulûn. You should ask him what happened to the explosive devices.","'${PLAYER}! By Durin's beard, I am glad to see you!\
\
'Slagvi and I fought against wave after wave of Orcs, but we were forced back by the sheer ferocity of their attack. During a break in the onslaught, as we prepared to rejoin the others, Slagvi tripped over some hidden cord and was partially buried beneath this fall of stones! It must be some goblin-trick, set here to ensnare us!\
\
'Help me lift these stones from him, ${PLAYER}!'","Bróin is trying to help free Slagvi from the rocks that have him trapped","Meet up with Slagvi in a trench to the south while the War of Three Peaks continues.","'The tide of battle turned against us, and we were forced back! This is not a defeat, nay, but we need time to regroup. We must steel ourselves and return to the fray!\
\
'You are looking for Bróin? I did not see him during the retreat. When last I saw him he fought alongside Slagvi, north of here. Did he not escape with the rest of us?'","Slagvi has been trapped by a fall of stones, and Bróin is trying to free him from the heavy rocks.","'Are you looking for something, ${PLAYER}? I heard the battle might be turning against us, but as long as you are still fighting I think victory must still be within reach!'\
\
You tell Afwald that you are looking for a number of items that Imák stored in this crate. He nods.\
\
'Oh, the goblin-bombs? I did wonder why they were being saved. Eywind came by and gathered them up. He seemed very excited about them, now that I think about it.'\
\
Afwald sees something in your expression.\
\
'Is that a problem?' he asks.","'Did I hear you rightly? That trap was set not by the Orcs, but by Imák the Stout-axe? Is this true? Is he a fool, or has he been stricken with some madness? We have difficulty enough fighting the Orcs without having to worry about running afoul of traps set by our supposed allies!\
\
'I cannot believe this! A pox on the Stout-axes! You must make this right! Find Imák and ask why he has chosen to fight dwarves and not Orcs! Does he not have enough enemies from which to choose that he must attack his supposed allies too?'","Meet up with Slagvi several trenches to the south during the War of Three Peaks","'These Longbeards should save their breath! They will not cease hurling insults and threats at me, but I have weathered worse winds than these! What is the Greymaul Rebellion to me? They think I care about the stories of ancient dwarves? Bah. They are nothing to me!\
\
'They think I was wrong to set traps for the Orcs? If these Longbeards paid more attention to their surroundings they would not blunder into one of my devices! You would not think they wanted to reclaim Gundabad at all, so unwilling are they to dirty their hands!\
\
'Well, they will be happy to know this: I did not have time to put the rest of my plan into motion before the defenders emerged from Gundabad and marched on our position. I lacked the time to set the goblin-bombs you collected, so I stored them in a crate inside Zarkul-sulûn. It is a shame, for those explosives could have claimed the lives of many Orcs if I had placed them as I wanted.'","With a mighty roar, a ferocious Orc charges forward!","Fighting during the War of Three Peaks has turned against the great force of Durin and Prince Ingór, and their warriors will need to stand together if they are to have the victory. Can they set aside their differences and achieve the triumph they seek?","'You must make this right! Find Imák and ask why he has chosen to fight dwarves and not Orcs! Does he not have enough enemies from which to choose that he must attack his supposed allies too?'","'Help me lift these stones from him, ${PLAYER}!'","Collect and defuse the goblin-bombs from the crate where Imák stored them, inside Zarkul-sulûn","Find Imák outside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks","Imák is outside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks, surrounded by an angry group of Longbeards.","Talk to Afwald by the empty crate in Zarkul-sulûn, during the War of Three Peaks","'You are looking for Bróin? I did not see him during the retreat. When last I saw him he fought alongside Slagvi, north of here. Did he not escape with the rest of us?'","The crate is empty. The goblin-bombs are gone!","As Haukbuz falls, Bróin leads Slagvi to safety!","Trausti last saw Bróin and Slagvi fighting side-by-side to the north, while battle raged on all around them.","Slagvi cannot believe his ears: the trap in which he was caught had been set by the Stout-axe Imák? He demands that you find Imák and ask why he has chosen to fight dwarves and not Orcs.","Find Bróin somewhere to the north, where Trausti last saw him","Talk to Imák outside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks","Help free Slagvi from the stones and defend him from attacking enemies","Slagvi has been trapped by a fall of stones, and Bróin is trying to free him from the heavy rocks.\
\
Bróin wants you to help him free Slagvi from the rocks, and he will need you to defend them while he works!","Talk to Bróin as he works to free Slagvi from the rock trap","'I lacked the time to set the goblin-bombs you collected, so I stored them in a crate inside Zarkul-sulûn. It is a shame, for those explosives could have claimed the lives of many Orcs if I had placed them as I wanted.'","Chapter 4.6: A Fall of Stones","Imák is surrounded by a group of angry Longbeards","Imák has reluctantly agreed not to use the goblin-bombs you collected. He sent you to collect the bombs from the crate where he stored them, inside Zarkul-sulûn, and render them unusable."},
[3136]={"King Elessar is inside the main hall of the keep of Lond Cirion, and should hear what you learned from Leafshade.","'There have been many strange happenings... of late...' the Ent rumbles. He slowly turns his head to look past the trees of the grove, and falls silent. After a long moment, he seems to realize you are still here. A long, windy sigh escapes from his mouth.\
\
'It is most unusual... for so much to happen... to the Ents,' he murmurs, sleepily.\
\
'I am called...' he begins, and after a time you realize that the sound rolling out among the twigs and branches of the grove, making them restless, is actually a long name spoken languidly in Old Entish.\
\
'But you may call me Lathlum... or Leafshade...' he continues, his voice little more than a sigh.","You cannot tell if Leafshade remains awake or if he has heard your words.","The Ent Leafshade is at the grove of Tumbamálë.","'Yesterday I saw... the ships return...\
\
'They sailed south until they disappeared... over the horizon...'\
\
Leafshade's words rise in intensity until their booming shakes the branches of the trees of Strangdene.\
\
'I hope you will... ensure Nestinanessornë is safe...'\
\
Leafshade ceases his trumpeting, and quiet returns once again to Tumbamálë.\
\
'He is... a friend...' he murmurs. 'So many others went away...'\
\
You assure Leafshade that you will do what you can to help him, but the Ent says nothing more.","Leafshade appears in no hurry to speak any further, so you ask about the Elf-bow in the centre of his glade.\
\
'Hrum, hoom! That is the bow of my friend, Nestinanessornë! He left it here when he... went away.'\
\
The Ent sighs heavily, the breeze of his exhalation rustling the leaves of the trees.\
\
'There was a gathering of my folk some... what is the word your kind would use, hm? Months, hoom. Some months ago. On my return, I came across a dying creature suffering from a poisoned wound. He reminded me of an old friend, an Elf I once knew. Ah, Ferien. Hm, hoom. She lived among the beeches, and sang so beautifully. Hoom...'\
\
Leafshade stands in silence, his story unfinished, and you wonder if you should prompt him to continue.","'But you did not know Ferien, hm? No, you would not have. The lives of Ents are measured differently, hoom, hoom. Months! Months are the blink of an eye, or less, hm! I was thinking of Ferien when I carried this wounded creature, this Elf, back here to my home. I did not know if he would live, hoom. For Ferien I would try to save him. In time he did recover his strength, hm, hm, and that is when I named him Nestinanessornë, which is sapling-who-is-healed in the words Ferien taught to me.'","'We have only just arrived at Lond Cirion, ${PLAYER}. Did you learn where the ships are bound?'\
\
You tell Elessar that the Corsair ships left the river and sailed south until they disappeared over the horizon.\
\
'So Nakási does make for Umbar. I was not certain that would be so. It seems she knows the value of her captive to the Kindred of the Coins. But something else troubles you, my friend. I can see it in your expression.'\
\
You tell Elessar, more briefly than it was told to you, of Leafshade's account of the past few months. The King puts a comforting hand on your shoulder.\
\
'Your friend Corudan lives, ${PLAYER}, but he is in need of rescue. As it happens, we were already planning such a mission, for young Thorongil must be freed from his imprisonment as well. I feel in my heart this is the way it must be: both of these captives are being brought to Umbar, the City of the Corsairs. A small party of adventurers might infiltrate the city and rescue Thorongil and Corudan where a larger group must surely fail. I want you to lead this small party, my friend. I know you are the right choice for this task, though it prove most dangerous.\
\
'You say that Corudan's sister Sigileth intended to investigate his disappearance near Helm's Deep? I will send a message to Erkenbrand that she be found and told of these new tidings.'","Chapter 4.6: Nestinanessornë","The Ent Leafshade might know what transpired when the Corsair ships came this way, but getting him to tell you about it might be challenging.","Talk to Leafshade at Tumbamálë","The Ent Leafshade is at Tumbamálë, and he has much to say.","Talk to King Elessar inside the main hall of the keep of Lond Cirion","Talk to Leafshade at Tumbamálë and learn what you can from the Ent"},
[3137]={"Some dwarves remain dangerously close to the path where Eywind has set his stolen goblin-bombs! Eywind will not evacuate them, so it falls to you.","'The last goblin-bomb must have already been placed, but where? The goblin's boots were wet? That tells me he must have left the bomb somewhere near the lake to the south-west...\
\
'Check the trenches near the lake, ${PLAYER}!'","'Yes, my friend, yes! This war will soon be ended, and Durin will have the victory! I have set a number of goblin-bombs on the path to the north-east, and in mere moments the Orcs and their Angmarim allies will be consumed by a conflagration of their own devising! Reinforcements will no longer be able to use that path to come to the defence of Caivád Sâr, and it is all thanks to my foresight and ingenuity! This conflagration may not be as impressive as the fire we set at Ghâshru, but it will serve. Ah, if only we had some of Gandalf's draught left! That made for a truly spectacular inferno!\
\
'What's that? How close will the fires be to our fighting dwarves? Hmm... good question, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps you should tell them to back up a bit!'","'Return to Durin inside Zarkul-sulûn and learn what is to be our next plan of attack. The fighting turns once again in our favour!'","Tremendous explosions thunder behind you, shaking the earth!","Eywind is somewhere near Caivád Sâr as the War of Three Peaks continues.","Durin is inside Zarkul-sulûn while the War of Three Peaks continues.","Dwarves evacuated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Eywind's satisfaction has turned to displeasure: for some reason not all of the bombs exploded. Did goblin-sappers recover some of the bombs, and do they now plan to use them against the dwarves? You should try and recover these twice-stolen goblin-bombs, while there is still time. Goblin-sneaks can be found in Eywind's vicinity near Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks.","Recovered twice-stolen goblin-bombs (${CURRENT}/3)","'It may be a good idea for you to find Eywind and ensure he is using caution, ${PLAYER}. He said something about the Angmarim tower of Caivád Sâr, so you should begin your search near there.'","'You quenched the last goblin-bomb? Good. It is a pity we were not able to turn it against its creators, but at least we made effective use of the others!\
\
'Return to Durin inside Zarkul-sulûn and learn what is to be our next plan of attack. The fighting turns once again in our favour!'","Return to Eywind south of Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks","You quench the fuse on the goblin-bomb as Eywind hurries to your side","Recover twice-stolen goblin-bombs from goblin sneaks (${CURRENT}/3)","Chapter 4.7: Elderslade Aflame","'Do you think it is possible some goblin-sneaks managed to retrieve some of the bombs I set and think now to use them against us?\
\
'There are three goblin-bombs for which I cannot account, ${PLAYER}! Go find them, and steal back the stolen bombs they stole from us!'","The goblin-sneak probably set his stolen bomb somewhere near the lakeside trench to the south-west, hoping to do as much damage to the dwarves as possible. You have to find and defuse it as quickly as you can!","Talk to Durin inside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks","Talk to Eywind in the lakeside trench during the War of Three Peaks","Recover twice-stolen goblin-bombs from goblin sneaks (2/3)","'Do you think it is possible some goblin-sneaks managed to retrieve some of the bombs I set and think now to use them against us?\
\
'There are three goblin-bombs for which I cannot account, ${PLAYER}! Steal back the bombs they stole from us! Yes, the ones we stole from them first!'","'We were pushed back on our heels, ${PLAYER}, but we did not give up hope, and now we are rewarded: the tide of battle has once again turned in our favour!\
\
'Victory is at hand!'","Eywind is south of the Angmarim tower of Caivád Sâr, and you should return to him quickly. You do not know how long his goblin-bombs will remain undetonated.","'Oh, he does like setting things aflame, doesn't he? As long as he is careful and vigilant, perhaps he will make good use of those goblin-bombs against our foes.\
\
'It may be a good idea for you to find him and ensure he is using caution, ${PLAYER}. He mentioned something about the Angmarim tower of Caivád Sâr, so you should begin your search near there.'","The dwarf Eywind has a long history of setting goblins on fire. But will he prove able to distinguish friend from foe amid the chaos of the War of Three Peaks?","Convince dwarves to evacuate the north-eastern road targeted by Eywind (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find and quench the hidden goblin-bomb somewhere near the lakeside trench","'Ha ha! Tremendous! Did you see that? What a beautiful sight! It serves those goblins right for trying to use such weapons against us... how do you think they like the power of the devices they fashioned?\
\
'But... there were not as many explosions as there should have been, friend. Do you think it is possible some goblin-sneaks managed to retrieve some of the bombs I set and think now to use them against us?\
\
'There are three goblin-bombs for which I cannot account, ${PLAYER}! Steal back the bombs they stole from us! Yes, the ones we stole from them first!'","Eywind is south of Caivád Sâr, admiring his handiwork.","This goblin's boots are wet with lake-water, but he placed his bomb already!","'Well? How did it go?'","Talk to Eywind south of Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks","Eywind is in the lakeside trench during the War of Three Peaks.","'How close will the fires be to our fighting dwarves? Hmm... good question. Perhaps you should tell them to back up a bit!'","Talk to Eywind near the Angmarim tower of Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks"},
[3138]={"Talk to King Elessar outside the keep of Lond Cirion","You remember Golasgil, Lord of Anfalas and father of Orgolas.","Talk to Orgolas inside the keep of Lond Cirion","Consider your memory of Golasgil in Minas Tirith before the siege of the White City","You remember finding Golasgil on the Pelennor Fields after the great battle, surrounded by the corpses of the Orcs that ambushed him. You recall too the look on his face when he learned how many of his friends perished before the walls of Minas Tirith, but such sorrow did not keep him from marching to the Black Gate with the Men of the West when his King required it.","'We cannot choose the times that call upon us, can we? Someone needs to rescue Thorongil, and I suppose it falls to me. I am not a warrior or a sailor, but how... how hard can it truly be? I have watched the men training, and I can swing a sword nearly as well as they can. And the Wave-hunter has a crew who will do the actual sailing, I trust...'\
\
Orgolas chews his lower lip with worry, and you are reminded he is only twelve years old.\
\
'I don't... I don't know what to do, ${PLAYER}. I want to help, and to prove that I am strong and brave enough to do what my father would want of me... but I also know I cannot leave my mother alone. I share some of the blame for Thorongil's capture. Should I not also be responsible for helping rescue him, if such a thing might be possible?'\
\
Orgolas sighs unhappily.\
\
'The King asked me \\qWhat would your father tell you?\\q but I confess that I don't know. Do you... do you have any idea what my father Golasgil would want me to do? What would he say to me?'","Find Orgolas in his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion","Gather your thoughts concerning Golasgil","'I am pleased with the decision of Orgolas, ${PLAYER}. I will not say I expected it with complete certainty, but I believed the son of Golasgil was enough like his father to arrive there after some deliberation. The folk of Anfalas will be in good hands once the Lady Marra instructs her son about what she has learned of rule: a considerable amount!\
\
'But our paths must now diverge, my friend. I charge you with the rescue of Thorongil and of Corudan, and look forward to your successful return aboard the Wave-hunter. Do try not to fan anew the flames of war with Umbar, ${PLAYER}. This must be a mission carried out in secret.'","'The Wave-hunter was given to me by my father, and if he had not died in service of Gondor, one day he would have taught me to be a great mariner, as he was. But that was not meant to be. Instead, I give command of the Wave-hunter to you until Thorongil is returned safely to his hall. Use it well and wisely, and may the memory of Golasgil go with you, and fill the sails with wind to speed you on your journey! When Thorongil is rescued, and the threat of the Corsairs is ended, perhaps you will teach me what you have learned of sailing, and I will drive the Wave-hunter upon the Great Sea.\
\
'But that will be in days yet to come! For now I must find how to protect the folk of Anfalas I will one day rule, and that is a lesson I will learn from my mother.'","'I know I can rely on you for this, ${PLAYER}, but you will need a ship to carry you and the crew you choose to bring to Umbar. I have already spoken with Orgolas about this, and have given the heir of Golasgil a number of things to consider, but as you will lead the expedition across the Bay you should be the one to hear what he has decided.\
\
'I believe you will find him in his bedroom somewhere upstairs.'","Consider your memory of Golasgil during the Battle of the Black Gate","Orgolas is inside his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion.","Wait for Orgolas to consider what you have told him","You remember Golasgil at the Battle of the Black Gate as he stood face to face with the mighty Olog that would give him his mortal wound, and you recall his final words.\
\
'If there is a day to come after this,' he said, 'look to the people of Anfalas. Tell them their lord...'\
\
You cannot say for certain what the Lord of Anfalas intended, for then he died, only moments before the fall of the Dark Lord Sauron and the rout of Mordor's armies. You relay his father's words to Orgolas, and Golasgil's heir rubs at a smudge on the floor with his shoe.","'Oh, it's you.'","You remember Golasgil standing in the White City before battle was joined on the Pelennor Fields, unafraid of the hard times ahead, trying to remember the words of an old travelling song.","Consider your memory of Golasgil on the Pelennor Fields after the battle","'My father's last thoughts were not for himself, or for what he was about to lose, but for the folk of Anfalas, so far away? How can that be true, ${PLAYER}? He left us behind to go to the war. If he truly cared would he not have remained here?'\
\
You remind Orgolas that his father counted his family, his son, and his wife among those people of Anfalas he sought to protect, and it was on their behalf that he followed the King to war. Orgolas sighs again.\
\
'Is that what you are telling me? To be a good ruler, you have to put the needs of your people ahead of your own? Is that what it means to be the son of the Lord of Anfalas? Is that what it means to be the heir of Golasgil? But it is so difficult. Thorongil would cast all that aside and charge off to battle, hoping to achieve glory, and before today I might have done the same. But I am not a fighter, not yet, and if I were seized by Umbar as was Thorongil... what would that mean for the people of Anfalas? I have to stay here. I have to help my mother and be here for my people. My father was a great mariner, and a mighty warrior, but I have not yet grown into the man he was. I must serve my people in another way.'","'I will remain behind to help protect Anfalas and Pinnath Gelin from further attack by the Corsairs, for that is the best way for me to aid my people... but the King is right that someone must sail to Umbar and rescue Thorongil, if it can be done in secret. He has chosen you for this, ${PLAYER}, but you need a ship.'\
\
Orgolas stands at attention and studies you seriously.\
\
'The Wave-hunter was given to me by my father, and if he had not died in service of Gondor, one day he would have taught me to be a great mariner, as he was. But that was not meant to be. Instead, I give command of the Wave-hunter to you until Thorongil is returned safely to his hall. Use it well and wisely, and may the memory of Golasgil go with you, and fill the sails with wind to speed you on your journey! When Thorongil is rescued, and the threat of the Corsairs is ended, perhaps you will teach me what you have learned of sailing, and I will drive the Wave-hunter upon the Great Sea.\
\
'But that will be in days yet to come! For now I must find how to protect the folk of Anfalas I will one day rule, and that is a lesson I will learn from my mother.'","Orgolas is inside his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion, and he has made up his mind.","You remember Golasgil, Lord of Anfalas,as he was in life","Orgolas considers what you have told him of his father Golasgil, who perished at the Black Gate of Mordor.","King Elessar is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.","Orgolas looks at you with resolve in his eyes","King Elessar has given you an important duty, and he believes your leadership will be crucial in the weeks ahead.","You try to gather your thoughts and tell Orgolas what he needs to hear.","Orgolas looks at you with a crestfallen expression as you arrive","Chapter 4.7: What Your Father Would Tell You","'I know I can rely on you for this, ${PLAYER}, but you will need a ship to carry you and the crew you choose to bring to Umbar. I have already spoken with Orgolas about this, and have given the heir of Golasgil a number of things to consider, but as you will lead the expedition across the Bay you should be the one to hear what he has decided.\
\
'I believe you will find him in his bedroom, somewhere upstairs.'"},
[3140]={"'Farewell, ${PLAYER}! Líniel and I will watch out for the King on his return to Minas Tirith. You take care of yourself, for my heart tells me you are about to be in far greater danger than the rest of us!'","Talk to Ioreth at Lond Cirion","Talk to King Elessar outside the keep of Lond Cirion","Talk to Aphadaer at Lond Cirion","Caebar waits for you in the library of Lond Cirion, inside the keep.","'You sail into dangerous waters, ${PLAYER}, and in Umbar you will be beyond my help. Rescue young Thorongil, and Corudan, and return to Gondor as soon as you may. I leave the choice of your crew to you, but I have asked my scribe Caebar to assemble some notes on folk who might be well-suited for the task. Speak to him in the library inside the keep and hear his suggestions.\
\
'Good-bye, my friend. I will see you again, but it may be many days hence, and far from here. Haste and good fortune go with you!'","'Good fortune go with you, ${PLAYER}, and may you rescue the young heir of Pinnath Gelin from his captivity.\
\
'You need not take my advice, but if you have a willing ear I might suggest that you bring my brothers with you when you assemble your crew. Elladan and Elrohir remained behind to aid the folk in Pinnath Gelin for a few days, but I know that they would be happy to accompany you when they have done there what they wanted.'","Talk to Lady Marra outside the keep of Lond Cirion","'I hope you know what you are doing, ${PLAYER}. Ioreth says you plan to sail to Umbar, and most of what I have heard of that place is... frightening. The King says Sauron is gone, and I have no reason to think he is wrong about that, but Sauron was worshipped for a long time in the City of the Corsairs. Can you be certain his cult is gone?\
\
'Glindor and I will do what we can to keep the King safe. I hope the crew you assemble for your mission will do the same for you!'","'Now bid farewell to the travelling company, ${PLAYER}, for we each have our own roads to walk and it may be some time before we see each other again.'","Talk to Caebar in the library of Lond Cirion","'I feel it will be some time before we see each other again.'","Caebar is in the library of Lond Cirion, inside the keep.","'My heart goes out to Nauriel and to her husband. I hope you are able to rescue their son from the Corsairs who have stolen him away. If Golasgil were here, I know he would welcome you aboard the Wave-hunter... indeed, he would have set sail at once, as soon as he had a course to follow!\
\
'Good fortune go with you and with the crew you choose. Long have I borne resentment for my husband's ship in my heart, but now I place upon its wooden frame my most fervent hope that you will return soon and safely, with young Thorongil in tow.'","Talk to Líniel at Lond Cirion","Return to the library of Lond Cirion inside the keep","Talk to Glindor at Lond Cirion","'So this is farewell.'\
\
Elessar clasps your arm and looks into your eyes.\
\
'You sail into dangerous waters, ${PLAYER}, and in Umbar you will be beyond my help. Rescue young Thorongil, and Corudan, and return to Gondor as soon as you may. I leave the choice of your crew to you, but I have asked my scribe Caebar to assemble some notes on folk who might be well-suited for the task. Speak to him in the library of Lond Cirion and hear his suggestions.\
\
'Good-bye, my friend. I will see you again, but it may be many days hence, and far from here. Haste and good fortune go with you!'","'The Wave-hunter was harboured upriver in Pinnath Gelin to protect it from the Corsairs during the War of the Ring; a decision that must have rankled Golasgil even as he saw the need for it. The ship's crew is likely eager to sail again, and you will need their talents and knowledge of the Bay to bring you to Umbar in secret.\
\
'But your arrival at the City of the Corsairs will only be your mission's beginning, ${PLAYER}. To that end, I suggest you add to the Wave-hunter's complement of sailors such folk as you can trust or as have a stake in the quest's successful conclusion. You will not be able to keep Nauriel away, I think, and as a Knight of the Green Hills her combat prowess may be of use to you. Legolas and Gimli will go with you gladly, of course, and I think Sirgon of Pelargir will be no less eager to sail again; his knowledge of the Bay and of the folk that dwell along its shores may prove valuable. If you believe that Corudan's sister Sigileth will begin her search for him at Helm's Deep, the messages I have dispatched to Erkenbrand should reach her, and she will likely make her way to Gondor as soon as she can.\
\
'There is another you should add to your crew, my friend, but I advise you to watch him carefully. I speak of the Corsair Jajax. It may be helpful to have him near as you adventure in Umbar... if you can trust him. Now bid farewell to the travelling company, ${PLAYER}, for we each have our own roads to walk and it may be some time before we see each other again.'","Chapter 4.8: The King Departs","'I understand you are leaving us, ${PLAYER}? Good luck to you, and to young Thorongil, the heir of Pinnath Gelin! I hope you are right, and the Corsairs will not harm their young captive. I would volunteer to come with you if I was not charged with maintaining the provisions for the King's travelling party, but what use could I be on such a quest? I am no fighter.\
\
'But I do know food, ${PLAYER}. The fruits of Umbar are apples, dates, figs, grapes, melons, and plums. Vegetables include beets, cabbage, eggplant, fennel, onions, and turnips. The diet of the Umbarrim contains a great deal of fish and shellfish, but also beef, goat, mutton, and poultry, in lesser quantities.\
\
'I don't suppose that helps you at all? I will miss you, friend.'","'You are leaving us on a secret errand, ${PLAYER}? Ioreth says you go to rescue young Thorongil from the Kindred of the Coins? No, do not seek to deny it! We both know it is true.\
\
'If you do encounter any members of this Kindred, do not stay the killing stroke! They need to be taught not to interfere with the rule of Gondor.'\
\
You tell Aphadaer you hope to rescue Thorongil without undue bloodshed, and he snorts.\
\
'I am sure that is your hope, but nothing so risky was ever accomplished without bloodshed. When it proves impossible, you will remember my words, I warrant.'","Talk to Grethril at Lond Cirion","'I may have misjudged both you and the King, ${PLAYER}. I felt certain the two of you would encourage my son Orgolas to follow in his father's footsteps, luring him away from Anfalas and into danger... but you have done the opposite. I am surprised.\
\
'My heart goes out to Nauriel and to her husband. I hope you are able to rescue their son from the Corsairs who have stolen him away. If Golasgil were here, I know he would welcome you aboard the Wave-hunter... indeed, he would have set sail at once, as soon as he had a course to follow!\
\
'Good fortune go with you and with the crew you choose. Long have I borne resentment for my husband's ship in my heart, but now I place upon its wooden frame my most fervent hope that you will return soon and safely, with young Thorongil in tow.'","You should speak with the members of the travelling party who will leave Anfalas in the company of King Elessar.","King Elessar is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.","Lady Marra is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.","Talk to Queen Arwen at Lond Cirion","'Dearie me, ${PLAYER}, do take care of yourself! I hope the things I have heard about the City of the Corsairs are untrue, for it sounds a frightful and violent place! How do Corsairs behave when they are at home? I cannot even imagine!'\
\
You tell Ioreth that your mission is supposed to be a secret, and she gives you a dramatic wink.\
\
'My lips will remain sealed. You can count on me!'\
\
She suddenly smacks her forehead with one palm.\
\
'It is going to be very warm there. You will need to dress for the weather! A change of clothes may be warranted, ${PLAYER}! Umbar, can you imagine?'","'This is really happening? When the King asked me to accompany you to Umbar, I thought he was joking. I thought he said it in jest! But it was not so.\
\
'I will do my best, ${PLAYER}. You have shown me kindness, and I will do what I can in return. But do not ask me to steer the ship! I would fetch us up upon the rocks, or on a reef, or...\
\
'Oh, I feel suddenly faint.'","King Elessar is about to leave Anfalas with his travelling party, but he has entrusted you with a different mission of grave importance."},
[3141]={"'We were so near to victory, ${PLAYER}! What cruel chance has brought Hrímil Frost-heart here to rob us of our triumph? How came she to escape her icy prison?\
\
'This is not a defeat. We will not stray from our course! We will regroup and mount one last offensive, and no Orc or dragon will stand before the might of my armies! I am descended from the line of Durin, and I will prove the glory of my name and the rightness of my cause!\
\
'Rally my forces. When all is ready, we will storm the gates, and Gundabad will once again be ours, at last!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>The story continues in the Gundabad expansion!</rgb>","Chapter 4.9: The Lord of Gundabad","Durin is inside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks, still reeling from the events of his assault on the steps before Gundabad.","Durin's assault up the steps of Gundabad intends to reclaim the Mountain-home from the new Lord of Gundabad, but such a prize cannot be claimed so easily.","Talk to Durin inside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks","'Let us follow after Durin, my friend! We will lend what aid we can, and be among the first to venture within the Mountain-home in victory!\
\
'I have an idea. Let us take another path to the steps of Gundabad. In that way we will obtain the element of surprise, and may be of greater help to the prince and to his warriors!'","Bori is outside Zarkul-sulûn, eager to follow after Durin's assault up the steps. Can victory be close at hand?","Talk to Bori outside Zarkul-sulûn and go with him to confront the Lord of Gundabad","'Quickly! We must follow Durin and his warriors! Thálfi told me of a path near Dûn Traikh that will allow us to gain access to the threshold of Gundabad from the other side!'"},
[3142]={"Has defendido a Sweina de los trasgos","Capítulo 4: Un rencor contra los trasgos","Bósi te ha pedido que te ocupes de un pequeño asunto mientras él lee el Libro de Mazarbul.","Habla con Sweina","'Uno de mis enanos, un minero llamado Sweina, se ha tomado la libertad de atacar a los trasgos de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata. Tiene la fuerza de brazo para igualar su naturaleza testaruda, pero hay demasiados trasgos en ese lugar incluso para que él pueda conquistarlos solo.\
\
'¡Espera! No te vayas a Gamil Filik todavía, porque ese no es el lugar al que ha ido mi enano. Sweina cree que los trasgos tienen su hogar en las Obras Hidráulicas, y lo escuché jurar que seguiría las vías mineras que recorren las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata hasta las profundidades inundadas. Busca las vías más al sur en tu mapa; ¡encontrarás a Sweina buscándolos allí!\
\
'Continuaré leyendo el Libro de Mazarbul, ${PLAYER}, pero debes viajar a la parte más al sur de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata para disuadir a Sweina de su misión temeraria. No dudo que matará a muchos trasgos, pero no sabrá cuándo retirarse. Debes encontrarlo y rescatarlo de su propia locura.'","'Sweina estará en algún lugar cerca de las vías mineras más al sur de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata, cerca de la entrada de las Obras Hidráulicas, buscando trasgos para matar. Encuéntralo y rescátalo, ${PLAYER}, ¡porque se ha metido en un lío!'","'¿Bósi quiere que regrese a la Cámara de las Encrucijadas? ¡No puedo hacer eso ahora, ${PLAYER}! ¡Hay cuellos de trasgo que cortar! ¡Ven, lucha a mi lado!'","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de las Encrucijadas, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has encontrado a Sweina y has luchado a su lado contra muchos trasgos, y deberías regresar ahora con Bósi.","'¿Has encontrado a Sweina? Me alegro, porque es un enano robusto y valiente; lo necesitaremos para los días venideros. Espero que no se meta en problemas antes de eso...\
\
'He seguido leyendo el Libro de Mazarbul.'","Sweina se encuentra en algún lugar de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata, probablemente en la parte más al sur de sus vías mineras, cerca de la entrada de las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que busques y rescates a uno de sus enanos que ha decidido tontamente desafiar a los trasgos de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata. Sweina cree que los trasgos de Gamil Filik tienen su hogar mucho más profundo que las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata, cerca de la entrada de las Obras Hidráulicas."},
[3143]={"Destruye la reliquia de Gorothúl en Nalâ-dûm","'Muy bien hecho, ${PLAYER}. La destrucción de esa reliquia debería evitar que más males se acerquen a las Ruedas de Agua.\
\
'Ahora debemos mirar hacia el futuro.'","'Mi tío Bósi envió un mensaje mientras estabas fuera. Cree que sabe dónde se puede encontrar otra de las reliquias de Gorothúl, y el lugar es tan peligroso como Lumul-nar, si no más: las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm.\
\
'Viaja a la Cámara de la Encrucijada con tus aliados y habla con mi tío para aprender más sobre Nalâ-dûm.'","Capítulo 4: Una reliquia en Nalâ-dûm (Grupo)","Una ola de temor te recorre mientras la reliquia es destruida, luego desaparece.","Bósi cree que otra de las reliquias de Gorothúl puede encontrarse en el fondo de Nalâ-dûm, donde las grandes ruedas de Khazad-dûm yacen dormidas.","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, ubicada junto al Camino de Durin.\
\
Bróin te ha dicho que hables con su tío sobre las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm.","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, ubicada junto al Camino de Durin.\
\
Has destruido la reliquia dejada en Nalâ-dûm por Gorothúl y deberías informar de tu éxito a Bósi.","'La entrada a Nalâ-dûm se encuentra en las obras hidráulicas. Lleva contigo una pequeña comunidad de aliados en busca de la reliquia de Gorothúl.'","La entrada a Nalâ-dûm se encuentra en las obras hidráulicas de Moria.\
\
Bósi informa que una reliquia de Gorothúl yace entre las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm y requerirá un uso cuidadoso de los mecanismos para alcanzarla y destruirla. También recomienda que lleves uno o dos aliados contigo.","'¡Saludos de nuevo, ${PLAYER}! No tuve la oportunidad de agradecerte adecuadamente por ayudar a negociar esta alianza entre la Guarnición de Hierro y los Elfos de Lothlórien. ¡Así que te doy las gracias! En Mazog, tenemos un prisionero digno de intercambiar por aquellos que Gorothúl trajo a Dol Guldur: mi hijo es el principal entre ellos. ¡Oh Bori! ¡Sé fuerte y valiente durante tu tormento!\
\
'Los exploradores informan haber visto una reliquia de maldad incuestionable entre las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm, pero no pudieron dirigir el flujo de los canales de tal manera que pudieran alcanzarla. Debes determinar el funcionamiento adecuado del sistema si quieres encontrar y destruir esta reliquia de Gorothúl.\
\
'Lleva varios aliados a la entrada de Nalâ-dûm en las obras hidráulicas. Adentrarse en las profundidades inundadas será peligroso, ya que los mecanismos son muy antiguos y no se han utilizado durante muchos años.'","'Mi tío Bósi cree que sabe dónde se puede encontrar otra de las reliquias de Gorothúl: entre las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm.\
\
'Ve a hablar con él en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, junto al Camino de Durin, y él te contará más sobre Nalâ-dûm.'","Habla con Bósi en la Cámara de la Encrucijada"},
[3144]={"'Muy bien hecho, ${PLAYER}. La destrucción de esa reliquia debería evitar que más males se acerquen a las Ruedas de Agua.\
\
'Ahora debemos mirar hacia el futuro.'","'Mi tío Bósi envió un mensaje mientras estabas fuera. Cree que sabe dónde se puede encontrar otra de las reliquias de Gorothúl, y el lugar es tan peligroso como Lumul-nar, si no más: las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm.\
\
'Viaja a la Cámara de la Encrucijada con tus aliados y habla con mi tío para aprender más sobre Nalâ-dûm.'","Capítulo 4: Una reliquia en Nalâ-dûm (Solo)","'¡Saludos de nuevo, ${PLAYER}! No tuve la oportunidad de agradecerte adecuadamente por ayudar a negociar esta alianza entre la Guarnición de Hierro y los Elfos de Lothlórien. ¡Así que te doy las gracias! En Mazog, tenemos un prisionero digno de intercambiar por aquellos que Gorothúl trajo a Dol Guldur: mi hijo es el principal entre ellos. ¡Oh Bori! ¡Sé fuerte y valiente durante tu tormento!\
\
'Los exploradores informan haber visto una reliquia de maldad incuestionable entre las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm, pero no pudieron dirigir el flujo de los canales de tal manera que pudieran alcanzarla. Debes determinar el funcionamiento adecuado del sistema si quieres encontrar y destruir esta reliquia de Gorothúl.\
\
'Haré que un explorador te conduzca hasta la entrada de Nalâ-dûm en las obras hidráulicas. Adentrarse en las profundidades inundadas será peligroso, ya que los mecanismos son muy antiguos y no se han utilizado durante muchos años.'","La entrada de Nalâ-dûm se encuentra en las obras hidráulicas de Moria.\
\
Bósi informa que una reliquia de Gorothúl se encuentra entre las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm y requerirá un uso cuidadoso de los mecanismos para llegar a ella y destruirla.","'La entrada a Nalâ-dûm se encuentra en las obras hidráulicas. Enviaré a un guía para que te conduzca hasta la entrada.\
\
'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para continuar tu viaje?'","Bósi cree que otra de las reliquias de Gorothúl puede encontrarse en el fondo de Nalâ-dûm, donde las grandes ruedas de Khazad-dûm yacen inactivas.","'Mi tío Bósi cree que sabe dónde se puede encontrar otra de las reliquias de Gorothúl: entre las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm.\
\
'Ve a hablar con él en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en el Camino de Durin, y él te contará más sobre Nalâ-dûm.'","Bósi está en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, ubicada en el Camino de Durin.\
\
Bróin te ha dicho que hables con su tío sobre las Ruedas de Agua de Nalâ-dûm.","Habla con Bósi y viaja a las Obras Hidráulicas de Nalâ-dûm","Habla con Bósi en la Cámara de la Encrucijada","Bósi está en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, ubicada en el Camino de Durin.\
\
Has destruido la reliquia que Gorothúl dejó en Nalâ-dûm y deberías informar de tu éxito a Bósi.\
\
Has destruido la reliquia que Gorothúl dio a los merrevail en Lumul-nar y ahora deberías regresar con Bróin."},
[3145]={"'Habla con Corunothiel y verás que no me equivoco, ${PLAYER}. ¡Verás que tengo razón!'","Orvar Martillo de Campana está en Buzun-ghâr, el pasaje recién excavado junto al Camino de Durin, ubicado en la pared sur del extremo sureste de Tharâkh Bazân. Tharâkh Bazân está al noreste de la Cámara de la Encrucijada.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que ayudes a Orvar, el enano que trabaja más estrechamente con los Elfos enviados por Celeborn a Moria.","Celeborn ha enviado a varios Elfos para ayudar a los enanos en Moria, y has prometido a Gimli que también seguirás prestando tu ayuda en las Minas.","'Esa es mi decisión. No abandonaré la misión que se me ha encomendado.\
\
Espero que brindes a Bósi y al resto de la Guarnición de Hierro la ayuda que yo les habría dado si estuviera allí, ${PLAYER}. Cuando la tarea de esta compañía termine, espero regresar a una Moria recuperada, y tus esfuerzos ayudarán a que eso sea posible.\
\
Bósi dijo que volvería a la Cámara de la Encrucijada cerca del Camino de Durin, en Moria. Ve ahora con él, y dale tanto mi pesar por no poder regresar como mis mejores deseos de éxito.'","Capítulo 4: Una alianza tensa","Corunothiel está en el campamento dentro de Buzun-ghâr, ubicado junto al Camino de Durin en el extremo sureste de Tharâkh Bazân.\
\
Orvar ha expresado su frustración con los Elfos enviados por Celeborn y quiere que hables con uno de ellos sobre su irritación.","'Escúchame, ${PLAYER}, porque este Orvar no escuchará razones. Algún mal vive en el fondo de esta caverna, y si este lugar no se sella, el mal puede extenderse.\
\
¡Esta es siempre la manera de los enanos! ¿Por qué siempre deben excavar en lugares donde no se supone que deben ir? ¿No estarán satisfechos hasta que no quede ningún mal bajo la piedra y todos hayan salido a la superficie para devastar los hogares de los Elfos y de otras buenas gentes?'","'Desearía poder regresar y ayudar a la Guarnición de Hierro con sus esfuerzos por reclamar Moria, pero no abandonaré a Frodo. Mi camino está con él.\
\
Te agradecería mucho si pudieras prestar tu ayuda a la Guarnición de Hierro. Viaja a la Cámara de la Encrucijada cerca del Camino de Durin, en Moria, y habla con Bósi. Dile que no puedo regresar, pero que continuarás ayudando con sus esfuerzos.'","'${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]} de nuevo a Khazad-dûm, . Estoy decepcionado de que Gimli no haya regresado contigo, pero estoy seguro de que tuvo sus propias razones. Su padre Glóin ha sido durante mucho tiempo un amigo cercano de mi padre y del padre de Brogur, y Gimli seguramente mantiene el honor de sus antepasados.\
\
'Este es mi primer trato con Celeborn de Lothlórien, y debo confesar que no estoy seguro de qué pensar de él. Ha enviado a varios Elfos para ayudarnos, y aunque aprecio la asistencia, parecen quizás demasiado ansiosos por culpar a los enanos por todos los problemas, tanto presentes como pasados.\
\
'Han establecido un campamento con uno de mis enanos, Orvar Martillo de Campana, en un pasaje recién excavado junto al Camino de Durin: Buzun-ghâr. Se encuentra en la esquina sureste de Tharâkh Bazân, en la pared sur, justo cerca de la salida de esos jardines. Encontrarás Tharâkh Bazân al noreste de esta cámara; sí, la zona llena de árboles en tu mapa. Viaja allí y presta tu ayuda a Orvar, él está teniendo... dificultades... para llevarse bien con estos Elfos.'","'Lo siento, pero no soy el Orvar que buscas. Debes estar buscando a Orvar Martillo de Campana, que actualmente está explorando las profundidades de Buzun-ghâr, el pasaje recién excavado junto al Camino de Durin, ubicado en la pared sur del extremo sureste de Tharâkh Bazân. Tharâkh Bazân está al noreste de la Cámara de la Encrucijada. ¡Lamento que hayas salido de tu camino, ${PLAYER}!'","'Me alegra que estés aquí, ${PLAYER}. Estos Elfos han sido enviados por Celeborn para ayudarnos a expulsar el mal de Khazad-dûm, o eso dicen, pero parecen más interesados en repartir culpas que en hacer algo útil.\
\
Esta caverna, Buzun-ghâr, fue encontrada poco después de tu partida, y muchos de los míos quedaron impresionados por su estado. ¡Los jardines aún prosperan! Al menos, aquí arriba; algo pudre y corrompe la vegetación a medida que desciendes.\
\
Pero mientras podríamos usar ayuda real para limpiar la cueva de peligros, estos Elfos hablan a menudo de \\qexcavar demasiado profundo\\q y \\qperturbar cosas que es mejor dejar intactas\\q. Si esto es lo mejor que Celeborn puede ofrecer, ¡preferiría que los mantuviera en los bosques!\
\
Habla con Corunothiel, ${PLAYER}, y verás que no me equivoco!'","'Encontrarás a Orvar Martillo de Campana en Buzun-ghâr, un pasaje recién excavado ubicado junto al Camino de Durin, en la esquina sureste de Tharâkh Bazân, justo cerca de la salida de esos jardines. Encontrarás Tharâkh Bazân al noreste de esta cámara. Encuentra a Orvar y ayúdalo a trabajar con los Elfos enviados por Celeborn de Lórien.'","Bósi está en la Cámara de la Encrucijada cerca del Camino de Durin, en Moria.\
\
Gimli te ha pedido que regreses a Moria para hablar con Bósi y decirle que ayudarás a la Guarnición de Hierro con sus problemas."},
[3146]={"Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Muru Azog","Iron-folk can be found on the field near Durin's Stone.\
\
Dáin has asked you to command the Iron-folk and send them to aid his father at the gates of Khazad-dûm.","Rally warriors of the Iron Hills at Durin's Stone (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'And so, Azog was slain, crushed beneath the boots of Dáin and beheaded. A fitting fate!\
\
'But something had troubled my friend ever since he passed beyond the gates of Khazad-dûm, and I dared not ask what it was. The battle was not yet ended, after all, nor would it be until every last Orc was banished from Azanulbizar.'","'Urro is slain? That is no small feat, my friend, and all the better for us!\
\
'When Bolg fled the field, my father and his guard pursued him towards the gates of Khazad-dûm. Many of the Iron-folk battle on the field here at Durin's Stone, but if ever there was a chance to slay Azog, the time has come!\
\
'Before we set out, order as many of our kin as you can to rally to the Great Gates!\
\
'Go! There is no time to waste, my friend!","As you continue to read Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar, you begin the fourth chapter in which the Dwarves of the Haban’akkâ of Thráin turn the tide of battle and the Iron-folk charge to meet Azog at the gates of Khazad-dûm.","Rallied warriors of the Iron Hills at Durin's Stone (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Muru Azog at Azanulbizar.\
\
After the defeat of Azog, Hermáth Stormhammer interjects and calls your attention to events at Muru Azog. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","Chapter 4: Charge of the Iron-folk","Dáin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
You have ordered the Iron-folk to aid Náin Orcsfoe at the gates of Khazad-dûm. You should talk to Dáin.","Talk to Dáin and confront 'The Lord of Moria'"},
[3147]={"El Refugio Sombrío se encuentra entre las Fundaciones de Piedra bajo Nud-melek.\
\
Galadriel le dijo a Haldir que si quieres salvar a los enanos de Moria, debes trabajar junto con los Elfos que envió a las Fundaciones de Piedra para enfrentarse a un gran mal.","'Un poco antes de tu llegada, un grupo aún más extraño llegó a Lórien. Con los ojos vendados, fueron llevados a Cerin Amroth, porque de ninguna manera pondríamos en peligro la seguridad de nuestra tierra. Trajeron noticias tristes con ellos, y dolor...'\
\
Haldir hace una pausa, y luego continúa.\
\
'La Dama Galadriel envió a un pequeño grupo de Elfos a Moria después de las noticias que esta compañía trajo consigo. Ella dice que si deseas salvar a los enanos, debes ayudar a esos Elfos, porque su tarea en Moria es muy importante. Han establecido un pequeño campamento en Gwathrendath, el Refugio Sombrío, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
'La Dama dice que un mal mucho mayor que la presencia de los Orcos yace debajo de las Fundaciones de Piedra, y debe ser enfrentado si tus enanos van a ser salvados.'","'La Dama Galadriel no me dijo la naturaleza del mal situado bajo Nud-melek, simplemente que debes ayudar a los Elfos del Refugio Sombrío a derrotarlo, o los enanos estarán perdidos.'","Galadriel te ha dicho que al ayudar a los Elfos del Refugio Sombrío, también estarás ayudando a los enanos de Moria.","Capítulo 4: Profundo es el Abismo","'Me gustaría darte la bienvenida al Refugio Sombrío, ${PLAYER}, pero no es una bienvenida alegre; nadie debería desear venir a este lugar. Estamos aquí por orden de la Dama Galadriel.\
\
'Un terror ha hecho su hogar en estas cavernas, y es repugnante y malvado.'","Habla con Lenglammel en el Refugio Sombrío"},
[3148]={"Habla con Golodhon","'We have found Golodhon here, who has come back from out there, and believes he knows where those disreputable fellows should be.\
\
'When we are ready, he will point us on our way. Shall we go?'","You should talk to Merry and Pippin again in Bâr Thorenion, now that you are all safely returned from Mordor.","'I wonder if we shall ever unravel the mystery we stumbled across out in Mordor. Somehow I do not feel much hope, although I expect we shall have to turn homewards sometime, and then we shall see what we shall see. \
\
'I will confess, I am quite down. Yes, I think for a spell we should try to dwell on brighter things.'","Golodhon, Merry, and Pippin can be found in the Foothold camp in Udûn.\
\
You should talk to Golodhon when you are ready to head back into Mordor.","Habla con Merry","Merry and Pippin have grown determined to go back into Mordor once more, this time in search of facts.","'I intend to have some answers before the day is through, no matter the inconvenience.'","Chapter 4: Deeper In","You should meet Merry and Pippin at the Foothold in Udûn.","'When you are ready, ${PLAYER}, Golodhon will point us to where he believes those three churls have got to.'","'There, now that I've had a bit to eat I feel half myself again. If that's all that Mordor has in store for us, you will find me elsewhere! I do hope Merry is all right.\
\
'You seem long about the face, friend. Chin up! We will find some pleasant diversions to wash the taste of all that out, quite.'","'What are we waiting for? Let us be off.'","Habla con Pippin","'I have other duties to which I must attend, but I can go some little way with you, and see that you are headed on the right course.'","'Ah, there you are, ${PLAYER}. You should seek Masters Meriadoc and Peregrin in the Udûn Foothold as soon as you are able. It seems they have resolved to venture back into Mordor.'","'Ah, there you are ${PLAYER}. We are going back into Mordor. We feel that we simply must. Will you come with us? We shall meet in the Udûn Foothold then? Then we are agreed!'"},
[3149]={"Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Mando, la sala en la parte superior de las escaleras del este en la Cámara de los Cruces, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has descubierto algunas páginas que revelan información sobre Nâr-khelab, el Corazón de Fuego.","'Regresa a Katûb-zahar, en el lado este de la Gran Excavación, al norte de una gran estatua de Durin, y busca alguna señal del secreto que abrirá el camino hacia el Corazón de Fuego.\
\
'Si podemos encontrar tanto la ubicación de esa antigua forja como el secreto para abrir sus puertas, podría ser que Zigilburk nos regrese de las tinieblas.'","Derrota a los Rascacuevas o Rascabismos en la Gran Excavación (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Esto parece realmente muy prometedor, ${PLAYER}. Veamos qué puedo aprender de estas páginas.\
\
'Muchas de las palabras están desvanecidas, y el pergamino está podrido... ¡Maldición a los rascacuevas y rascabismos que anidan ahora en Katûb-zahar!\
\
'El uso de este secreto para abrir la puerta parece ser... punible con la muerte... o con prisión. El herrero Ongli podría aprobar la entrada, al igual que Durin, por supuesto... No puedo descifrar la siguiente línea, pero... ah, aquí vamos.\
\
'La puerta permanecerá oculta hasta que... se sigan los siguientes pasos... Esta palabra debe ser \\qOngli,\\q lo que significa que debe ser saludado como un maestro herrero, o felicitado por su excelente trabajo, o... honrado, creo. Y luego, se deben pronunciar las siguientes palabras: \\qBâb kanon zuhûk!\\q\
\
'¡Esto es todo, ${PLAYER}!'","Rascacuevas y Rascabismos derrotados en la Gran Excavación (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","${PLAYERNAME:Enterrado[m]|Enterrada[f]} en el nido, descubres páginas mohosas que mencionan a Nâr-khelab.","Capítulo 4: Enemigos en la Oscuridad Eterna","Busca en Katûb-zahar el secreto para abrir Nâr-khelab","Katûb-zahar, la Cámara de las Palabras de Durin, se encuentra en el lado este de la Gran Excavación, al norte de una gran estatua de Durin.\
\
Bori te ha pedido que regreses a Katûb-zahar para buscar alguna señal del truco para abrir la puerta hacia Nâr-khelab, el Corazón de Fuego.","'¿Qué has hecho con las páginas?'","Lleva las páginas podridas a Bori","Bori te ha hablado de Nâr-khelab, la gran forja en la que podría haberse fabricado el hacha de mithril, Zigilburk. El camino hacia la forja está bloqueado por algún truco secreto, perdido con el tiempo.","'Si podemos encontrar tanto la ubicación del Corazón de Fuego como el secreto para abrir sus puertas, podría ser que Zigilburk nos regrese de las tinieblas.\
\
'Voy a preguntar a los otros enanos de nuestra expedición si han encontrado alguna señal de Nâr-khelab. Tal vez alguien se haya topado con alguna pista, aunque no tengo muchas esperanzas.\
\
'Debes regresar a Katûb-zahar, la Cámara de las Palabras de Durin, y buscar el secreto para abrir la puerta. Los rascacuevas que encontraste no lo harán fácil, pero eres lo suficientemente fuerte para lidiar con ellos. Katûb-zahar se encuentra en el lado este de la Gran Excavación, al norte de una gran estatua de Durin. En algún lugar dentro, entre los nidos de los rascacuevas, podrías encontrar el secreto para abrir el Corazón de Fuego.'","Buscas en el nido maloliente, pero no encuentras nada útil."},
[3150]={"'You found Lhaid Ogo? You need to go inside and search for the Dunlending messenger, if such a messenger exists. I have still not made up my mind about Ergothorn. Return at once to the entrance to Lhaid Ogo, south of here on the right side of the road that runs through the Lich Bluffs!'","'If you find a messenger from the south in Lhaid Ogo, we will know that Ergothorn was telling the truth...about this matter, at least.\
\
'Gather allies you can trust and go to Lhaid Ogo, on the right side of the road that runs south through the Lich Bluffs.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","Habla con Halbarad","The mysterious letter is on a crate by Halbarad.\
\
Radanir found a letter addressed 'To the Rangers' stuck in a tree with a knife, and Halbarad wants you to read it and give your opinion on its truthfulness.","Search Lhaid Ogo for the lost Dunlending messenger","To the Rangers:\
\
I am a man of Gondor, a friend of the Elves and of all good folk. Call me Ergothorn. I see the danger growing in the East and want to oppose it.\
\
Lheu Brenin dispatched a messenger from Tûr Morva in Dunland, but the messenger was beset by foes outside Lhaid Ogo in the Lich Bluffs and was dragged within. If he yet lives, he will have information for you.\
\
I cannot reveal myself to you, but trust that I am a friend. I will contact you again when it is safe to do so.\
\
Ergothorn","'I will be right behind you! Hurry now and lead the way to Glynn Brenin in Lhanuch.'","There are signs of a struggle outside the entrance to Lhaid Ogo","Find the entrance to Lhaid Ogo, in the Lich Bluffs","Chapter 4: Ergothorn Elf-friend","To the Rangers:\
\
I am a man of Gondor, a friend of the Elves and of all good folk. Call me Ergothorn. I see the danger growing in the East and wish to oppose it.\
\
Lheu Brenin dispatched a messenger from Tûr Morva in Dunland, but the messenger was beset by foes outside Lhaid Ogo in the Lich Bluffs and was dragged within. If he yet lives, he will have information for you.\
\
I cannot reveal myself to you, but trust that I am a friend. I will contact you again when it is safe to do so.\
\
Ergothorn","Glynn Brenin is in the Brenin's Hall, atop the hill of Lhanuch.\
\
You have rescued the Dunlending messenger and should return to Glynn Brenin to hear his message.","'Ergothorn steered us true on this matter, but I do not give my trust so easily. Truth often comes before a lie, the better to ensure the lie go undetected.'","'Anirin has given me the message from Lheu Brenin of Tûr Morva, and it fills me with joy, for it means that the Uch-lûth do not stand alone against the Wizard Saruman. We have some few allies still, and that gives me hope.'","Talk to Glynn Brenin in Lhanuch","Radanir found a mysterious note from a purported friend: but can Ergothorn Elf-friend be trusted?","'Read the letter and tell me what you think, ${PLAYER}. I have left it on the crate there for you.'","'Is this Ergothorn a friend? Why will he not show his face? I do not like this, ${PLAYER}. And yet, if he is telling the truth....\
\
'We need to know, ${PLAYER}. Gather allies you can trust and go to Lhaid Ogo, far to the south of here, on the right side of the road through the Lich Bluffs. It may be that a messenger from the south is in trouble, and if so, we could use the information he brings.\
\
'But keep your eyes open. I will not trust Ergothorn without proof. It may be a trap.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","'Radanir found this letter stuck into a nearby tree with a knife, ${PLAYER}. It is addressed 'To the Rangers,' and...well, I have left it on that crate there. Read it and tell me what you think it means.'","Read the letter on the crate by Halbarad in Lhanuch","Somewhere inside Lhaid Ogo, a messenger from Dunland may be in trouble.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","Lhaid Ogo is on the right side of the road that runs through the Lich Bluffs.\
\
Halbarad is not certain that Ergothorn can be trusted, but he wants you to travel to Lhaid Ogo to see if there is any truth to the mysterious letter.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","Halbarad is among the huts on the western side of Lhanuch.\
\
You have read the note from Ergothorn and should now speak with Halbarad about it."},
[3151]={"Completa la Escaramuza: Ataque contra Dannenglor","'Bien hecho, . Dannenglor es nuestro, y se espera que los morrovals no regresen.\
\
'Ve ahora a hablar con Cúcheron en el porche de la Posada Embrujada aquí en Audaghaim y dale las gracias de mi parte. Me alegra que haya enviado a ${PLAYERNAME:un[m]|una[f]}  tan hábil a nosotros, y Dannenglor es prueba de tu valía para la Hueste Dorada.'","'Ya he oído hablar de tu victoria en Dannenglor, ${PLAYER}. Ojalá pudiera darte tan buenas noticias de la Guardia Oculta, pero nuestra situación ha cambiado poco. Issuriel ha pasado horas examinando los pocos mapas que poseemos de esta región del Bosque Negro, pero aún no ha decidido una ruta segura y secreta hacia Dol Guldur.\
\
'Tenemos otra preocupación ahora también. Una preocupación relacionada con un Martillogrís.'","Habla con Dúndurion en Audaghaim","'Ve ahora a hablar con Cúcheron en el porche de la Posada Embrujada aquí en Audaghaim y dale las gracias de mi parte. Me alegra que haya enviado a un ${CLASS} tan hábil a nosotros, y Dannenglor es prueba de tu valía para la Hueste Dorada.'","Las ruinas de Dannenglor son el objetivo de un ataque planificado por Dúndurion.\
\
Dúndurion te ha pedido que participes en el ataque contra las ruinas de Dannenglor ocupadas por los morrovals.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo: Solitario, Duo, Pequeña Comunidad, gran Comunidad o Incursión utilizando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","'Debemos perseverar, ${PLAYER}, aunque lamentamos la pérdida de Raddir. El camino que planeaba tomar es desconocido para nosotros, pero su mente no lo es: sé que se enfadaría si abandonáramos la esperanza.\
\
'Pero necesitamos tiempo para decidir qué hacer. En lugar de centrarnos en nuestras pérdidas, quiero que ofrezcas tu fuerza a Dúndurion aquí en Audaghaim. Ha planeado una serie de ataques contra lugares importantes en el Bosque Negro, y la Hueste Dorada podría usar tus habilidades como ${CLASS}.\
\
'Ayuda a Dúndurion con cualquier escaramuza que haya planeado, luego vuelve a verme. Por el Señor y la Dama, espero que hayamos decidido qué hacer a continuación con Mazog. No podemos quedarnos aquí mucho tiempo sin que el Enemigo se entere de la presencia del líder de los Orcos.'","'La Guardia Oculta necesita decidir un plan de acción. Mientras intentamos recuperarnos de la pérdida de Raddir, creo que tus habilidades serán más útiles para la Hueste Dorada.\
\
'Ve a hablar con Dúndurion aquí, en Audaghaim. Él planea un ataque contra algún lugar aquí en el Bosque Negro, y tu presencia será de gran valor luchando junto a la Hueste Dorada en lugar de esperar aquí mientras la Guardia Oculta decide qué hacer.'","Cúcheron se encuentra en el porche de la Posada Embrujada, en Audaghaim.\
\
Dúndurion te ha enviado de regreso a Cúcheron. Quizás la Guardia Oculta haya decidido qué camino tomar en la próxima etapa de su viaje.","Dúndurion se encuentra en Audaghaim, fuera de la Posada Embrujada, contemplando el paisaje desde los acantilados.\
\
Cúcheron ha decidido enviarte a Dúndurion para ayudar a la Hueste Dorada con sus asuntos militares mientras la Guardia Oculta decide un plan de acción.","Dúndurion se encuentra en Audaghaim, fuera de la Posada Embrujada, contemplando el paisaje desde los acantilados.\
\
Has participado en el exitoso ataque contra Dannenglor y ahora deberías regresar con Dúndurion.","'Mis Elfos se preparan para otra escaramuza: un ataque contra las ruinas de Dannenglor, pobladas por los sucios morrovals. Si eres tan hábil como  como Cúcheron me ha llevado a creer, serás muy ${PLAYERNAME:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} para unirte a nosotros en esta escaramuza. ¡Doble si puedes contar con la lealtad de un soldado competente!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo: Solitario, Duo, Pequeña Comunidad, gran Comunidad o Incursión utilizando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>","Habla con Cúcheron fuera de la Posada Embrujada","Capítulo 4: Primeras Ofensivas","'Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. He sido encargado por el Señor y la Dama para mantener el control sobre los lugares en las áreas occidentales de esta región. No hemos tenido nada más que éxito hasta ahora...¡Por Elbereth, que continúe!\
\
'Mis Elfos se preparan para otra escaramuza: un ataque contra las ruinas de Dannenglor, pobladas por los sucios morrovals. Si eres tan hábil como  como Cúcheron me ha llevado a creer, serás muy ${PLAYER:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} para unirte a nosotros en esta escaramuza. ¡Doble si puedes contar con la lealtad de un soldado competente!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en tamaños de grupo: Solitario, Duo, Pequeña Comunidad, gran Comunidad o Incursión utilizando el Panel de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 60.</rgb>\
\
Antes de lanzar la Escaramuza, debes visitar uno de los Campamentos de Escaramuzas que se encuentran por toda la Tierra Media y hablar con un Capitán de Escaramuzas para entrenar adecuadamente. Los Campamentos de Escaramuzas se pueden encontrar en las siguientes regiones: Ered Luin, las Tierras de Bree, la Comarca, las Tierras Solitarias, las Quebradas del Norte, el Bosque de los Trolls, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria y Lothlórien.</rgb>","La Guardia Oculta está en desorden tras la muerte de Raddir, y Cúcheron ha decidido que deberías ayudar a la Hueste Dorada mientras deciden qué hacer a continuación."},
[3152]={"Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should collect the care package in Vérnozal.","Talk to Prince Ingór","'Ah, thank you for this care package. I am sure that the Longbeards you rescued will be honoured to receive such a gift! My personal thanks for all that you have done, ${CLASS}.'","Collect the care package","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.","Give the care package to the visiting Longbeard emissary","Collected draughts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected bread (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should pack up all the items into a care package in Vérnozal.","You packed up all the items","'Ah, you have returned! I have heard of your success and the safe return of the Longbeard explorers! You have done well to strengthen the bond between all the dwarves in Gundabad.\
\
'I believe we can do more, however! Let us send those explorers a gift to show that the Zhélruka are just as pleased as any Longbeard at their safe return. Some ales, bread, and draughts should do nicely! We can present this package to the Longbeard emissary before he departs.'","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should give the care package to the visiting Longbeard emissary in Vérnozal.","Collected ales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected the care package","Pack up all the items into a care package","'Quickly now, we must hurry! If they remain alive, those Longbeards may not have much longer!'","'Let us send those explorers a gift to show that the Zhélruka are just as pleased as any Longbeard at their safe return. Some ales, bread, and draughts should do nicely! We can present this package to the Longbeard emissary before he departs.'","'The care package has been delivered? Good, good! You have done well today, my friend.'","Chapter 4: Friends of the Longbeards","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to the Zhélruka and to fight on their behalf in Gundabad.","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should collect some draughts, ales, and bread in Vérnozal.","'${PLAYER}, I must speak with you. There are rumours in the hall that a group of Longbeard explorers has gone missing while excavating a perilous cavern. Apparently one of the old tunnels gave way and the dwarves did not return. I believe they might be trapped, but still alive. We must search for them and assist the Longbeards!'","Collect bread (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect draughts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect ales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[3153]={"Talk to Halros and help him decide whether to stay in the Shire or to travel south with the Grey Company","Deal with the trouble-maker in the Green Hill Country","Trouble-makers can be found on the road through Green Hill Country, and in the village of Stock, in the Shire.\
\
Halros has asked you to walk the road through Green Hill Country and to visit the town of Stock to deal with the bold trouble-makers that have appeared there.","'Hey! I've got orders from Up Top that say I can do what I like here in these lands, and I plan to do just that! I fancy this house, and no ${RACE} is going to stand in my way, neither!\
\
'It's too small to live in, but I could use it to store the haul my boys plan on getting in the next several weeks. You'd best move along if you know what's good for you!'","Dealt with the trouble-maker in Stock","'I will take it upon myself to gather several others of the Dúnedain that may be found within Bree-land, but you should make your way to the Shire. At a camp by the Greenfields, you should find Halros.\
\
'Halros loves the Shire and its people and has watched over them for many years. It may not be easy for him to leave them, even upon an errand as urgent as that of the Grey Company.'","'Welcome, ${PLAYER}. So long as there are goblins beneath the Greenfields, I will maintain my watch over the Shire. That is my duty, given to me by my chieftain, Aragorn.'\
\
Halros listens intently as you tell him of the need for the Grey Company to assemble and ride south.\
\
'I see, ${PLAYER}. I...I need time to prepare. I had been just about to deal with a particular matter when you arrived. If you can take care of it for me, that will give me time to set things in order.\
\
'There are trouble-makers loose on the road that runs through the Green Hill Country. I fear they may do some real harm before they are stopped. Can you walk the road and visit the town of Stock, ending the threat of the trouble-makers there? I fear they may be brigands, or worse, and these are more bold than they have been in the past. Return then to me and we can talk again.'","'I am worried about this recent increase in trouble-makers in the Shire. Deal with them along the road through the Green Hill Country and in Stock, then return to me and we can discuss things.'","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. There have been more trouble-makers on the road in recent days, and I fear they will do some harm to the peace-loving folk of the Shire if I travel south with the Grey Company.\
\
'And yet, my loyalty is to Aragorn, and I know that if he has need of the Dúnedain, it is my duty to go to him with as much speed as can be mustered!\
\
'I do not know what to do, ${PLAYER}. What do you advise? Can you help me make this decision?'","'Halros loves the Shire and its people, ${PLAYER}. He may be reluctant to join the Grey Company.\
\
'Find him at his camp among the Greenfields, in the north-east corner of the Shire.'","Halros has a camp in the Greenfields, in the north-east corner of the Shire.\
\
Halros has asked for your help in making the decision whether to travel south with the Grey Company or to maintain his vigil over the Shire.","Dealt with the trouble-maker in the Green Hill Country","Chapter 4: Halros, Ranger of the Shire","Halros has a camp in the Greenfields, in the north-east corner of the Shire.\
\
You have discouraged the trouble-makers in the Green Hill Country and Stock, as Halros asked, and should return now to the Ranger.","Saeradan has sent you to bring word of the Grey Company's errand to Halros, a Ranger currently watching over the Shire.","Halros has a camp in the Greenfields, west of Bree-land, in the Shire.\
\
Saeradan has told you where to find the Ranger Halros and has warned you that Halros may find it difficult to leave the Shire, even for so important an errand.","Deal with the trouble-maker in Stock","'You'd better be careful, you! I've got friends making plans in the hills around here, and these halflings aren't included in 'em! You'll be in for a fight if you mess with me and my gang!'","Talk to Halros in the Greenfields"},
[3154]={"'Regresas a tiempo para ayudarnos a preparar las defensas; y no solo las defensas, porque no me quedaré aquí sin hacer nada mientras los Orcos hacen sus propios preparativos. ¡Los hostigaremos incluso mientras nos preparamos para defender Zelem-melek!'","Capitulo 4: Apresúrate a la sala Vigesimoprimera","'Reporta a Brogur en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la sala Vigesimoprimera en Zelem-melek. Si puedes brindarle al menos la mitad de la ayuda que nos diste, los enanos allí no tienen mucho que temer de los Orcos.'","'El Corazón de Fuego ya está listo para la guerra, ${PLAYER}. Hemos comenzado a fabricar equipo de alta calidad para los defensores y fuertes barricadas para ayudar a nuestra posición, y debemos mucho a tu gran ayuda.\
\
'Pero no podemos perder la sala Vigesimoprimera. Debes regresar con Brogur en la Cámara de Liderazgo y brindarle una asistencia igual.\
\
'¡Los Orcos seguramente se sorprenderán por nuestras excelentes defensas! Apostaría a que están confiados en que nos tomarán desprevenidos.'","Stóthkell está satisfecho con el trabajo que has hecho para ayudar a preparar el Corazón de Fuego para la guerra, y quiere que hagas lo mismo por los enanos de la sala Vigesimoprimera.","Brogur se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la sala Vigesimoprimera en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has ayudado a los enanos del Corazón de Fuego a preparar la defensa, y Stóthkell quiere que hagas lo mismo por los enanos de la sala Vigesimoprimera."},
[3155]={"'King Elessar will have need of you in Minas Tirith, ${PLAYER}. You should return to him and see if you can be of service there as well as in Mordor.'","Chapter 4: Judgements of the King","King Elessar's guard Malthengil is near the throne.","'I thank you for your report, ${PLAYER}. It is good to know that Mordor is being explored and the evil within it combatted.\
\
'I am not entirely comfortable remaining in the city while others adventure in dangerous lands. Perhaps one day I will join you, ${PLAYER}, but for now the city and the kingdom require more managing.\
\
'I await your return, my friend, and the tales you will bring with you!'","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Elessar and the Kingdom of Gondor, and to fight on their behalf in Mordor.","Talk to Malthengil and witness the pronouncements of King Elessar","'Ah, ${PLAYER}. King Elessar was looking forward to a report from you about your further adventures in Mordor, but you have arrived in time for him to make a number of pronouncements. Speak to me if you would like to attend, and you can witness the judgements of Elessar.'","Talk to King Elessar in his throne room","King Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.","'King Elessar is about to pronounce his judgements in a number of important matters. Present yourself to Malthengil and you may be able to attend.'","King Elessar is about to pronounce his judgements on a number of important matters, and his guard Malthengil has offered that you be allowed to watch.","Talk to Malthengil by King Elessar's throne","'It should not be long, ${PLAYER}, but there are a few matters to which the king must attend.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>"},
[3156]={"'¿Dónde está mi almuerzo? ¡Seguro que no lo has olvidado!'","Los trabajadores enanos se encuentran al norte del campamento de Bósi, a lo largo del camino sinuoso que sube a la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que entregues almuerzos a los enanos encargados de desenterrar los escombros frente a la Puerta de Acebeda, y luego que hagas tu reporte a Wárr.","'Este almuerzo será justo lo que necesito para refrescarme después de mi largo trabajo, y te lo agradezco.\
\
'No habríamos seguido a cualquiera aquí a Acebeda y a las tinieblas de Khazad-dûm. Los señores Bósi y Brogur son jóvenes, es cierto, pero son valientes de corazón y sus padres ganaron gran renombre como parte de la Compañía de Thorin. Esta podría ser nuestra oportunidad de lograr una gloria del mismo tipo.'","'¡Ah, un almuerzo preparado! El señor Bósi está haciendo un gran trabajo manteniéndonos alimentados y descansados. Le pagaremos a él y al señor Brogur con todo nuestro esfuerzo, y estaremos fuera de estos escombros en un santiamén.\
\
'Me pregunto qué encontraremos más allá de esta puerta?'","'Gracias por entregar esos almuerzos. Ahora deberías hablar con Wárr, que supervisa el trabajo en la Puerta de Acebeda.'","'Hola, y gracias por este almuerzo. Mi estómago estaba empezando a gruñir.\
\
'Mis parientes se preguntan qué encontraremos dentro de Khazad-dûm: ¿el señor Balin, vivo y bien? ¿Grandes riquezas de mithril? ¿Incontables orcos y trasgos?\
\
'Supongo que lo veremos, pero espero que sea el mithril.'","'Oh, ya veo. Estos picos están rotos, lo que significa que a menos que podamos conseguir repuestos para Wárr, todo el trabajo para excavar la Puerta de Acebeda se suspenderá. Tenemos que hacer algo al respecto, ${PLAYER}, ¡y rápido!'","'Lleva esos almuerzos a los trabajadores a lo largo del camino al norte de aquí que serpentea hasta la Puerta de Acebeda. Necesitarán el sustento para mantener sus fuerzas.'","Bósi te ha pedido que ayudes a reabastecer con almuerzos a los trabajadores que intentan desenterrar la Puerta de Acebeda para mantener su ánimo alto.","'¿Dónde está mi almuerzo? Lo necesitaré cuando termine mi turno, ¿sabes?'","Lleva los picos rotos a Bósi","Entregaste almuerzos preparados a los trabajadores enanos (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Gracias por este almuerzo. Lo comeré en un momento.\
\
'Hay algo sobre este lago que no me gusta, pero no puedo descubrir qué es. Me pone nervioso.'","'Quiero un almuerzo, y no me has traído uno.'","'Gracias por el almuerzo. Realmente tienes coraje para ayudarnos así... o ¿no has oído aún la historia del Daño de Durin?\
\
'En cualquier caso, ¡tienes mi agradecimiento!'","'Vas por el camino equivocado, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}; estas escaleras están bloqueadas en la parte superior por un lago de agua estancada. Si buscas el camino que sube a las Puertas de Durin, debes dar la vuelta. Mantén la piedra gris de los acantilados a tu derecha, y síguela de regreso por donde viniste, hacia mi tío Bósi.\
\
'Si sigues la línea de los acantilados, manteniéndolos a tu derecha, encontrarás el camino que serpentea hasta las Puertas.'","'Lleva esos picos al señor Bósi y pide que te los reemplace, o tendremos que abandonar el trabajo aquí en la Puerta de Acebeda hasta que podamos fabricar más herramientas.'","Bósi supervisa algunos de los carros cerca de las orillas del Sirannon seco, al sur de la carretera que serpentea hasta la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Wárr te ha pedido que entregues un suministro de picos rotos a Bósi y que le pidas que los reemplace.","'No he tenido noticias de Wárr por algún tiempo. Me pregunto cómo le han ido las provisiones. ¿No tenía un mensaje para mí?'","Has entregado almuerzos preparados a los trabajadores enanos (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Te agradezco por el almuerzo, pero tendré que comerlo cuando termine mi turno.\
\
'Desenterramos esta puerta en un santiamén. Es extraño, sin embargo; mi pico me dice que estos escombros aún no se han asentado. Apostaría un carro de plata de Moria a que este derrumbe ocurrió recientemente.'","El enano Wárr se encuentra en la Puerta de Acebeda, supervisando el trabajo de los obreros allí.\
\
Ahora que has entregado los almuerzos a los trabajadores enanos a lo largo del camino que conduce a la Puerta de Acebeda, deberías hablar con Wárr para que te asigne otras tareas.","'Cuando llegamos a la Puerta de Acebeda hace algunos días, encontramos las Puertas de Durin selladas por escombros y restos. Parece que hemos elegido mal nuestro camino ahora; me pregunto si la Puerta del Arroyo Sombrío en el lado este de las montañas está abierta.\
\
'Los enanos de nuestra expedición han estado trabajando para desenterrar la puerta, pero es un trabajo arduo y hambriento. Llévales estos almuerzos para que puedan tener fuerzas para los trabajos por venir.\
\
'Viaja hacia el norte por la pendiente entre las paredes rocosas y encontrarás trabajadores descansando a lo largo del camino hacia la Puerta de Acebeda, y hay más a lo largo del borde del agua antes de las puertas. Habla con Wárr en la puerta cuando hayas hecho esto, y él tendrá más tareas para ti.'","'Ah, gracias por esto. ¡Temía que me fuera a morir de hambre si no tenía algo para comer pronto!\
\
'Desenterramos la Puerta de Acebeda antes de mucho, pero no es un trabajo fácil. Trabajamos por turnos para hacer el trabajo lo más eficientemente posible.'","Capítulo 4: Fuera de la puerta","Has recogido picos rotos","'Llegas justo a tiempo, ${PLAYER}. Estamos realmente gastando muchos picos aquí, y si rompemos más, eso retrasará nuestro progreso para desenterrar la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
'Lleva estos picos rotos al señor Bósi, y dile que necesitaremos algunas de repuesto, y rápido, si queremos seguir avanzando con buen ritmo.\
\
'Lo encontrarás cerca de las orillas del Sirannon, al sur de la carretera sinuosa que termina aquí en la puerta.'","'¿No me has traído un almuerzo?'","'¿No hay almuerzo para mí? ¿Qué locura es esta?'"},
[3157]={"'Some of the Dúnedain have already begun to ride, ${PLAYER}. Speak with Halbarad at the stables to see if he has any advice before the rest of us depart.'","The first leg of the Grey Company's journey will take them south through the Trollshaws and into Eregion.","'Many of our friends have already departed. I am about to go.'","Talk to Halbarad at the stables in Rivendell","Saeradan is at Gwingris, in Eregion.\
\
The farrier Londan has thanked you for your aid, and he has asked you to speak with Saeradan.","The Grey Company begins its ride south. Halbarad has determined that the Rangers will rest at Gwingris, in Eregion.\
\
You should ride south to Gwingris, either on your own mount or on one engaged from Rivendell.","'Ride south into Eregion, ${PLAYER}, on your own mount or on one engaged from Rivendell. We will all gather again for a rest at Gwingris.'","Talk to Londan the farrier, who will be waiting for you back at Gwingris","'Erebrandir is ready to go once more! His new shoe fits perfectly, a testament to the skill of Londan. I am worried about these uruks, though. If it is true that many of the creatures have come north through Enedwaith into Eregion, our ride south may quickly become more difficult than it has been to this point.\
\
'Are they solely here for plunder, or is there another purpose that drives them?\
\
'Londan gave to me the shoe he took from Erebrandir. It is yours, if you want it; some people believe a shoe such as this brings good fortune. I do not think that is the case, but I leave you to make up your own mind.'","'Our preparations are complete, and some of the Dúnedain have already mounted their horses and begun to ride. You do the same or engage one of the horses at these stables, and we will be off!\
\
'Lothrandir and I have chosen a course that will take us south in several legs, the first of which leads south through the Trollshaws and into Eregion.\
\
'We will meet up at Gwingris, in Eregion, ${PLAYER}, and we will have a rest.'","'I have fit a new shoe to Saeradan's horse, ${PLAYER}. He will have no problems now.\
\
'I wonder if the same can be said for the few who live in these lands. Those uruks spoke as if more would be coming, and we have no reason to doubt them. There has been much more activity among those creatures, many more of them on the roads in recent weeks. I do not like it.\
\
'Well, give Saeradan my thanks for sending you my way, friend ${RACE}. I would have been in a great deal of trouble if you had not come along when you had, and the price of a new horse-shoe is a small price to pay indeed!'","'There are many more uruks in this land than there ever were before, ${PLAYER}. Tell Saeradan to use caution if he and his fellows insist on riding south.'","'I am about to ride south with the rest of the Grey Company. You too should ride now!'","'Many of our friends have already departed. Speak with Halbarad at the stables here to see if he has any final words for you.'","Find Londan the farrier and talk to him","Talk to Saeradan at Gwingris","Chapter 4: Riding South","You have protected Londan the farrier from the uruks","Talk to Saeradan at Gwingris, in Eregion, after riding south","Londan should still be in Eregion. He left Gwingris heading east.\
\
Saeradan has asked you to find the farrier Londan and convince him to return to Gwingris so that he may repair Erebrandir's shoe.","Halbarad is at the stables of Rivendell.\
\
Candaith has asked you to speak with Halbarad to see if he has any final words before you join the rest of the Rangers on their ride south.","'The first leg of our journey is complete, but not without incident: my horse, Erebrandir, has drawn up lame. There is something wrong with one of his shoes, and he cannot go on unless something is done.\
\
'Halbarad says I should just engage another horse, but I have been speaking to the Elves here and they have given me another idea. Apparently a skilled farrier has recently passed through Gwingris. This farrier, Londan by name, could certainly repair Erebrandir's shoes.\
\
'I understand that Londan left Gwingris heading east. If you find him and convince him to return, we will have been delayed but little.'","'Londan left Gwingris heading east. He is surely still in Eregion and could find time to repair Erebrandir's shoe if you are able to find him without delay.'","'Thank you for finding Londan, ${PLAYER}! Both I and Erebrandir thank you, for he has been able to fit my Lonely Wanderer with a new shoe. You should speak with him.'","'Careful, stranger! There is a group of uruks in these parts, of great size and strength. I saw them not two hours ago.\
\
'They were passing north, and though I could understand little of their cruel speech, it seems to me they were seeking treasure. There are ruins throughout these lands, you know. These uruks would like nothing better than a chance at plunder.'\
\
Londan listens to your account of Saeradan's plight and agrees to tend to the needs of his horse Erebrandir. His face then freezes in a mask of fear.\
\
'The uruks! They're coming back! Prepare to fight!'","Londan the farrier will be waiting for you back at Gwingris, in Eregion.\
\
You have rescued Londan from the Sharkúnakh uruks that he encountered and should return to Gwingris."},
[3158]={"Bósi te mira por un momento y luego cierra los ojos.\
\
'¿Hemos terminado, ${PLAYER}? Todos los enanos de esta expedición se regocijaron cuando Zigilburk fue traído desde las profundidades, pero aún más por el regreso seguro de mi sobrino Bróin. ¡Todo parecía posible! Pero ahora...'\
\
Suspira profundamente.\
\
'Mi hijo se ha ido. ¿Cómo puedo esperar liderar a mi pueblo hacia la victoria ahora? No puedo. No tengo la voluntad.'","'No... no sé qué hacer, ${PLAYER}. A pesar de todos nuestros preparativos y de la fuerza de nuestras armas, Mazog y su aliado Gorothúl nos han golpeado directamente en el corazón.\
\
'Quizás Bósi sepa qué hacer, pero temo que esté tan perdido como yo. Bróin regresó a nosotros desde la oscuridad, pero no estoy tan seguro de que Bori haga lo mismo.'","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en el extremo sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Brogur te ha pedido que consultes a Bósi para que te dé alguna idea de qué hacer a continuación, ahora que los enanos han perdido gran parte de su esperanza de victoria en Moria.","Brogur no sabe qué hacer tras la pérdida de Bori y Zigilburk, y teme que el tiempo de los enanos en Moria esté cerca de su fin.","Capítulo 4: Las penas de Khazad-dûm","'Debes ir a preguntarle a mi primo qué hacer, porque estoy completamente sin ideas. No sé cómo podríamos resistir a Mazog y Gorothúl sin el poder de Zigilburk.'"},
[3159]={"Return to Legolas in the Court of Lothlórien with the many gifts of seed.","Lady Galadriel suggested you begin by visiting Certhíril in Mirobel and ask her about Glorfindel and a gift of seeds.","Now you should show the record you found in Tham Giliath to Lady Galadriel.","Visit Certhíril in Mirobel","Talk to Lady Galadriel","'It is strange! Just yesterday a pupil, or rather a disciple of Glorfindel's stood where you stood and asked what you ask: have I seen him? Alas, I have not.\
 \
'I sent her on to Imladris, for I have heard he has often spent time there, lately, standing in contemplation below Elrond's House and above the waterfall. I suggest you follow her, and if you do not find both, you might find one.\
\
'Your other boon meets a more fortunate answer: these are seeds of the Gaerthond Vine, with leaves of shining silver, and morning-blooming flowers of dusky blue and gold.'","Look for Glorfindel, or his disciple, at his accustomed spot in Rivendell, below Elrond's House and above the waterfall.","'Why, what is this? You have quite outdone yourself, ${PLAYER}. I will find a suited vessel for this gift and bear it to Gondor, to give to our friend, the new king!'","You should ask Legolas about the nature of the request he has for you.","The Elf woman blinks at you in disbelief.\
\
'Is it you... ${PLAYER}? It is I, Glathlírel. Do you not recognize me? I have exchanged my fine armour for the traveller's garb.\
\
'Does this mean that you, too, have come looking for Glorfindel? I do not know whether to take heart from the coincidence or take it as a darker sign. But tell me, why have you come?'\
\
You tell Glathlírel of the Battle Under the Trees and war council in the Court of Lothlórien.\
\
'Then you have better cause to find him than I, who have come looking only because of a troubling dream. Have you heard of the Elves who live hidden in a cave in Belfalas? The Avorrim, they are called. Why do you not seek one called Dorthaneth there? She is wise beyond years. I will go west, to Lindon and look for him there. Then we shall meet back at Galadriel's Court.\
\
'Oh, and lastly, by strange coincidence, I do indeed have a seed-gift for your friend, Legolas. These will grow into Rithlas, and are from Annúminas. I know it will mean much to Gondor's new king.'","Seek Dorongur in Duillond","Someone is standing in Glorfindel's spot, but it is not he","Show the record to Gildor","Seek Gildor in Tham Giliath","'Ah, my friend. I have been thinking on the gift of seeds you were entrusted with in Imladris. I must confess I am struck with envy. Why, if I could gather some dozen of the ferns and blossoms found in Mirkwood... but this journey has taken me far enough from Mordor and my friend, Gimli.\
\
'If you are setting out for places where Elves dwell, however, perhaps you might ask them for such gifts. We will gather them together, and what a fine garden the new king Elessar will have!'","'I have pondered the things you and I saw in my pool, ${PLAYER}, and some clarity has come to my mind as to their meaning. Lord Elrond's advice was indeed true: you have a role to play in the events unfolding and, I think in bringing Glorfindel to our council.\
\
'This I would ask of you: see places where my kind, the Elves, dwell, and ask after him. He is far-travelled and known to many. But where should you begin? Perhaps... Mirobel. Yes. Seek Certhíril there. She has seen much and knows even more.\
\
'Ah, but before you go, speak to your friend, Legolas. He, too, has something to ask of you, I believe.'","Visit Glorfindel's spot in Rivendell","'Radiant Glorfindel? I have not seen his face or heard his fair words for many lives of Men. His name has come to me here, where I stand, from time to time, however.\
\
'Here is my advice to you, young ${CLASS}. Do not attempt to find an Elf the likes of Glorfindel, for he will not be found if he does not wish to be. Follow instead what he sought. If I am not mistaken, one Dorongur in Duillond knew of the thing Glorfindel seeks, and may even know where he has gone.\
\
'Ah ha ha. Do not go leaping off just yet. You came for a second reason and that you shall have without riddles. These seeds are Tuilloth. It grows to cover the ground, and the fine white flowers it bears make it like a mirror of the night sky beneath your feet.'","Checked book-shelves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should talk to Lady Galadriel in the Court of Lothlórien.","'Indeed, you may certainly do both at once. Go, gather seeds, and learn what you can of Glorfindel as you go.\
\
'Begin with Certhíril and I think your path will unfold itself before you.'","Seek Dorthaneth near Edhellond","Travel to the places where Elves dwell, seeking word of Glorfindel and gifts for Aragorn's taking of the throne.","Gildor has suggested you look around Tham Giliath for a clue as to what Glorfindel found.","Show the record to Lady Galadriel","Deliver the seeds to Legolas","Dorongur has suggested that you travel to the library in Lin Giliath and look for Gildor Inglorion, whom you can ask about Glorfindel and a gift of seeds.","'Ah, ${CLASS}. You are like the gull who flies after the wind-wafted sail. Glorfindel has been here and gone again. I greeted him but in passing, but I believe he left here having found what he sought. Perhaps it was one of the texts here? Look for yourself and see if you can find it.'","'Well met, ${RACE}. Let me look into your eyes. I see no deception or ill will there, so I shall tell you what I know. Glorfindel came some few days past to consult on words Gil-galad spoke very long ago, when first he set foot in the Havens of Lindon. They concerned times to come, times that he would not live to see.\
\
'I myself knew little of this speech, nor was I certain who had heard it in its entirety. Therefore I pointed Glorfindel toward Lin Giliath. I felt that if it had been written down, some record might be there. Go to Tham Giliath and speak to Gildor Inglorian. He will know if Glorfindel came that way or no.'\
\
Then, with a twinkle in his eye, Dorongur produces a small pouch.\
\
'Nor could I forget these, a fair gift fairly asked for. Lodeledh will grow tall and with sweet-scented leaves cast dappled shade beneath its boughs.'","'Hail, friend ${CLASS}. It is time for you to return again to Lothlórien's Court, for you are wanted there.'","'Hail, friend ${CLASS}. I am glad you have returned to Lothlórien's court, for you are wanted here. Go, speak with her Ladyship.'","'What is this? It is a very old record, indeed. I think it likely you have found what you sought. I would bring this to Celeborn and Galadriel in Lórien, if I were you. They will know full well what to make of it.\
\
'But before you do, have these. They are Parthríf pods, and will grow into ferns of uncommon intricacy and form. It is a fine gift for a new king.'","You should talk to Galadriel once more before you go.","You should show the record that you found to Gildor in Tham Giliath.","Dorthaneth suggested that Dorongor, in Duillond, might know something of what Glorfindel seeks and where he has gone. You should ask him about that and also a gift of seeds.","Seek Dorthaneth in the caves of the Avorrim, near Edhellond, in Belfalas, and ask her about Glorfindel and a gift of seeds.","Chapter 4: The Wandering and the Lost","'What is this you have found, ${PLAYER}? A clue to Glorfindel's whereabouts? This record is old indeed. Lord Celeborn and I shall need some time to pore over it. We will send for you when we are done. And - you have my heartfelt gratitude for all you have done.'","Check the book-shelves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Legolas."},
[3160]={"Search near the base of Lûghash for Mogi","Search to the north for Mogi","'It seems Mogi has left no trace behind. A thousand curses upon him!\
\
'Return to King Thorin and tell him that Dómor will keep searching for the traitor. I will come back to the Hall under the Mountain when I have avenged this insult, or when I have found treasure worthy of the king. Perhaps I will pluck the fine ruby from Mogi's cold hands, eh?'","'${PLAYER}! King Thorin has been betrayed! No, not him alone, all of Durin's Folk have been insulted and maligned!\
\
'Just to the north of here, I encountered Eirek and Mogi quarrelling over treasure. It was a red gem embedded in a loose rock. Any dwarf might improve the quality of this ruby with careful labour, but a skilled dwarf could do much more! It would be a fine gift to present to King Thorin, and Eirek said as much, but then Mogi slew him where he stood! He stole the ruby and fled. I would have given chase, but a band of Orcs came near at that moment and I was forced to retreat.\
\
'But now that you are here, we can hunt him down and bring Thorin's wrath upon the traitor! We must find Mogi and make him pay for this treachery! You search to the north, and I will search to the south and see if he snuck that way, and perhaps we can snare him. The ground is treacherous, and you may need to go out of your way to properly search for Mogi. Look for him on both sides of the chasm to the north, and to the south-east of Lûghash! One of us must find him and make him pay for his treachery!'","Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.","Dómor has gone to the road south of Lûghash. Did he find Mogi?","If Mogi was here, he is gone now","Talk to Dómor south of Lûghash, in Dor Amarth","'I think it is time you reported back to King Thorin about your adventures, wouldn't you say? He may have another task for you.'","You found Dómor in Dor Amarth. Does he know where the other dwarf heroes have gone?","'Well, ${PLAYER}, have you found any word from these so-called heroes?'\
\
You tell King Thorin what you learned from Dómor of Mogi's treachery.\
\
'This is an insult to me, and to all dwarves! I want that traitor found! My axe will take his life, but not before his beard is shorn and he is made an object of ridicule. I will give my subjects someone else to mock, someone who deserves it!\
\
'Eirek was on the king's business, and it is an insult to the king to interfere with such! Unacceptable, ${PLAYER}, unacceptable! May Dómor find this traitor and bring him here. I wish you good fortune on your own adventures, and if you find Mogi first I trust that you will bring him before me with all speed!'","'I am pleased to see you return, ${PLAYER}, for you are the only adventurer who has properly reported back to me! I understand that Mordor is full of danger, but surely these heroes understand that their king needs updates!'\
\
King Thorin scowls through his beard.\
\
'They mock me with \\qStonehelm,\\q but if I did not have the responsibilities of kingship I would be among the first dwarves seeking glory in Mordor! Alas, I must stay here. You, however... yes, you must return to Mordor and see what has happened to these so-called adventurers. The last word I had from Mogi placed him in Dor Amarth, south of Lûghash, so that is where you should begin your search.'","There is no sign here of Mogi","You see no sign that Mogi was here","Search near the road for Mogi","You have found Dómor, one of the dwarf heroes Thorin sent into Mordor","'You must return to Mordor and see what has happened to these so-called adventurers. The last word I had from Mogi placed him in Dor Amarth, south of Lûghash, so that is where you should begin your search.'","Dómor asked you to search to the north, in the direction of Lûghash, for the treacherous Mogi.","Find the missing dwarf heroes in Dor Amarth, in Mordor","'I heard that King Thorin is worried about something, but I do not know what it might be. You should report to him of your adventures in Mordor and learn what so concerns him.'","The dwarf heroes sent into Mordor by King Thorin have not reported back in some time, and are missing somewhere in Dor Amarth, south of Lûghash.\
\
King Thorin has sent you to find the missing dwarf heroes in Mordor.","'Hmm, I do not see him anywhere, ${PLAYER}.'","'Return to King Thorin and tell him that Dómor will keep searching for the traitor. I will come back to the Hall under the Mountain when I have avenged this insult, or when I have found treasure worthy of the king. Perhaps I will pluck the fine ruby from Mogi's cold hands, eh?'","Chapter 4: Treachery in Mordor","Talk to Dómor south of Lûghash, near the road","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Durin's Folk and fight on their behalf in Mordor."},
[3161]={"Talk to Mithrandir at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate","Harthalín is west of Faltor Gâm, in Agarnaith.\
\
Mithrandir asked you to find Harthalín in Agarnaith and hear her report.","'Ah, I am all right now, do not trouble yourself. I engaged in battle with a party of Orcs, but the fighting went against me and I sustained this injury. I thought my days were done, but the creatures did not stay to ensure it. Their leaders called them away before they made sure I would not recover. To think I would have names such as Plákash and Durkhlát to thank for my life, but that is now so!\
\
'The Orcs were looking for someone. They spoke of \\qthe Weeping Warrior\\q as they departed. Their language is harsh and guttural; I could not make sense of much of their talk, but I think Ugrukhôr ordered them to find this warrior at any cost. They split into two groups as they left me, and Plákash and Durkhlát planned to return to Durthang and Cirith Ungol to regroup.\
\
'Do not worry about me, ${PLAYER}. I am mostly recovered from my injury. I give thanks to no Orc, but still I am grateful that Ugrukhôr's minions feared his commands enough to leave me carelessly behind, still alive!'","Thenca is south of Agarnaith, by the road in Talath Úrui.\
\
Mithrandir asked you to find Thenca in Talath Úrui and hear his report.","'I am pleased to see you, ${PLAYER}, for I encountered something peculiar and wanted to hear your thoughts! Not far from here I tracked a company of Ugrukhôr's Orcs through the swamp, intending to surprise them at the right moment and make them corpses. Before such a moment presented itself, I was robbed of my prey. Another party fell upon the Orcs and rended them all to pieces!\
\
'The ambushers were merrevail, ${PLAYER}. They swooped down from the height and left no Orc alive. But I thought Ugrukhôr and Lhaereth were allies? Why are their minions slaying each other?'\
\
Harthalín smiles grimly.\
\
'I do not complain. But there is something strange in this, and if we learn what has them at odds we might turn it to our advantage.'","'Why are the minions of Ugrukhôr and Lhaereth fighting among themselves if their masters are united? There is something strange in this, and if we learn what has them at odds we might turn it to our advantage.'","'${PLAYER}! I did not expect to see you. Has this sudden movement of troops drawn your attention too? It has not? Then allow me to tell you what I have seen, and perhaps you will know what has caused it.\
\
'Orcs and evil men have been stirred into sudden wakefulness by some directive that is unknown to me. Small groups of these foes have travelled across Udûn and Dor Amarth since I came to this inhospitable place, but never in such numbers. I believe they received urgent orders from one of their leaders, and it has compelled them to depart the Doomfold with some haste. But I cannot say where they have gone, for I do not know it.\
\
'But this I do know: they go where they can do the most damage to Gondor or her allies. How can it be otherwise? Other scouts may know more. Go to them with speed to match that of our foes!'","Talk to Harthalín west of Faltor Gâm, in Agarnaith","'Scouts of many lands and many backgrounds adventure even now in Gorgoroth, and seek the knowledge that will bring about the undoing of these Masters. Seek first Gwedhir in Dor Amarth, and then look for Harthalín in Agarnaith. On your way back to me, pass through Talath Úrui and consult with Thenca. These three reports will help us to form an effective strategy, ${PLAYER}.'","'This is why I like you, ${PLAYER}. Before it seemed the forces arranged against us had the upper hand, but now you return with information we can use to oppose our enemies. What has caused this rift between Ugrukhôr and Lhaereth, and for what fell purpose do Ugrukhôr's Orcs seek the Weeping Warrior?'","Talk to Thenca south of Agarnaith, along the road in Talath Úrui","'Orcs and evil men have been stirred into sudden wakefulness by some directive that is unknown to me. Small groups of these foes have travelled across Udûn and Dor Amarth since I came to this inhospitable place, but never in such numbers. I believe they received urgent orders from one of their leaders, and it has compelled them to depart the Doomfold with some haste.\
\
'Perhaps other scouts will know more. Go to them with speed to match that of our foes!'","'I have given the situation some thought, but a Mordor united against us does not lend itself to easy solutions. Before the meeting of the Masters, I feared the ascendancy of Dulgabêth, the Mouth of Sauron. Now he is dead and there are others arrayed before us, wielders of powerful weapons and forgers of unexpected alliances. Lhaereth the Stained, Borangos the Horror, Ugrukhôr of the Gúrzyul... these names are to be feared individually, but when they share our destruction as a common purpose we must not fear them... we must fight them.\
\
'Rather let the Masters of Mordor fear us. Are we not united against them? Scouts of many lands and many backgrounds adventure even now in Gorgoroth, and they pursue knowledge that might bring about the undoing of these Masters. Seek first Gwedhir of Gondor near the ruins of Díngarth in Dor Amarth, and then look for Harthalín west of Faltor Gâm, in Agarnaith. On your way back to me, pass through Talath Úrui and consult with Thenca of the Rohirrim. These three reports may help us to form an effective strategy, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Gwedhir south-west of the ruins of Díngarth","Mithrandir is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","'The Orcs were looking for someone. They spoke of \\qthe Weeping Warrior\\q as they departed. Their language is harsh and guttural; I could not make sense of much of their talk, but I think Ugrukhôr ordered them to find this warrior at any cost. They split into two groups as they left me, and Plákash and Durkhlát planned to return to Durthang and Cirith Ungol to regroup.'","Gwedhir is south-west of the ruins of Díngarth, in Dor Amarth.\
\
Mithrandir asked you to find Gwedhir in Dor Amarth and hear his report.","Chapter 5.1: A Question of Purpose","Unsure of how best to combat the Masters of Mordor in their unification, Mithrandir turns to you to gather the information that will allow him to form a strategy."},
[3162]={"Glóin expressed his surprise and dismay at the artists and craftsmen that have answered Durin's call and come to Zarkul-sulûn. You should speak with these new arrivals and learn why they have come to such a place of war.","'What's that? The mountain is not yet taken? What has Prince Durin's army been up to, then? I should have thought Gundabad would be well in hand by now!\
\
'But you will not dissuade me. I have come all this way and will not return empty-handed. The Mountain-home has been held by the Orcs for too long, and it will take a sculptor's careful hand to restore the beauty it once possessed. Imagine the great works of art that must lie within, covered by the dust of years and ignored by the dismissive Orcs! Yes, the prince will need warriors... but he will need artists too, and I have answered the call he did not think to make. He will thank me, eventually.\
\
'For now I need my luggage brought inside the fortress. You can help my apprentice with this task. Eskil! Carry my things! On the double, lad!'","<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Glóin during the War of Three Peaks when you accept this quest.</rgb>\
\
'We are so near to achieving our goal, ${PLAYER}! Gundabad belongs to my people, and neither Orc nor dragon will keep it from them any longer! Should Gorgar stand before us, he will be cut down! Should Hrímil Frost-heart seal the entrance with ice, as she has done, we will break through it... and then we will take her head and ensure she can never hinder us again!\
\
'Every day, more dwarves arrive to swell this great force, this Gabil'akkâ of mine. Speak with Glóin and assess these new arrivals, and we will set them on tasks with which the Mountain-home shall be reclaimed!'","Talk to Eskil Bloodthumb outside Zarkul-sulûn","Stáli has directed you to speak to his apprentice, Eskil Bloodthumb, outside Zarkul-sulûn.","'I need my luggage brought inside the fortress. You can help my apprentice with this task. Eskil! Carry my things! On the double, lad!'","'Sometimes I wonder why my brother Eskil agreed to become Stáli's apprentice. He does not seem to enjoy the experience.'","Stáli the Hewer stands outside Zarkul-sulûn. Why has the sculptor come to such a dangerous place in time of war?","Talk to Prince Ingór downstairs in Zarkul-sulûn","You set the luggage down as Stáli arrives. You notice he carries nothing","Talk to Stáli the Hewer on the upper floor of Zarkul-sulûn","'I hope you and my apprentice were careful with these! I have brought a number of pieces from Erebor, some which are quite fragile, and if any of them have suffered cracks or scratches I shall see that the prince hears about it.'","Chapter 5.1: Many Masters","Talk to Glóin outside Zarkul-sulûn","Stáli clearly does not remember you","Stáli the Hewer glances at you imperiously, without recognition","Durin will not be dissuaded from reclaiming the Mountain-home. He commands the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ to break through the frozen wall that now blocks the gates of Gundabad.","Stáli the Hewer has ordered that Eskil Bloodthumb carry his master's luggage to the upper floor inside Zarkul-sulûn. You have decided to help Eskil in this task, so the apprentice need not carry everything by himself.","'Oh, you will help me carry some of my master's luggage? Thank you, friend. That will save me a trip or two up the stairs.\
\
'When I agreed to become Stáli's apprentice, I thought there would be rather more instruction in the craft than such labour as this....'\
\
Eskil looks around nervously.\
\
'I am not complaining! No, not at all! I had better get going. I will find a place for the luggage upstairs in the fortress, if you truly wish to help.'","Glóin stands outside Zarkul-sulûn, watching as more dwarves arrive for the conquest of the Mountain-home.","'My luggage needs to be brought inside the fortress. My apprentice will show you where on the upper floor to leave it.'","Meet with the new arrivals outside Zarkul-sulûn","'Thank you again for agreeing to help me carry my master's luggage. I will find a place for it inside the fortress, somewhere on the upper floor.'","Talk to Stáli the Hewer outside Zarkul-sulûn","Pick up some of Stáli's luggage","'There you are, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I wanted to remind you that my people have a claim upon Gundabad, and I expect Prince Durin to respect this claim when the mountain is won. I want you and Durin to understand that my Zhélruka are not fighting for nothing.'","Stáli the Hewer has arrived on the upper floor of Zarkul-sulûn.","'It is so difficult to find good help these days, no matter where I look!'","'Tell Stáli to return to Erebor. He is an artist, not a warrior, and there are still battles to be won before he will do us any good here.'","'The prince is right: more dwarves arrive every day. But I daresay he has not looked closely upon these new arrivals, or he should not speak so confidently of the help they will provide to us.\
\
'These are not warriors! Most of the dwarves arriving now are peaceable folk: artists, craftsmen, and traders. They were lured here by the promise that Gundabad will once again be ours, and aye, so shall it be, but they seem to believe the war is done and the mountain is already ripe for the taking!\
\
'Do you see there? More dwarves arrive, and I recognize one of their number from the halls of Erebor. Stáli the Hewer is so-named for his skill at sculpting, not for severing limbs from his foes! He is no fighter. Go tell him he has come too early, and should depart.'","You decide to leave Stáli before you damage the irksome artist himself","Prince Ingór is downstairs in Zarkul-sulûn, waiting to speak with you.","'Greetings to you. Did you fight in the war? It does seem to still be going on!'\
\
Fastrith looks at Eskil Bloodthumb, currently puzzling how best to carry his master's luggage, and sighs.\
\
'Sometimes I wonder why my brother Eskil agreed to become Stáli's apprentice. He does not seem to enjoy the experience very much.'"},
[3163]={"Complete 'The Crew: The Boon Companions'","Talk to Caebar in the library of Lond Cirion when you are satisfied with your crew","Chapter 5.1: The Crew of the Wave-hunter","'I will be fine in a moment. Let me just... breathe for a bit.'\
\
Caebar rubs his eyes and steadies himself.\
\
'All right, ${PLAYER}. To business, to business. The Wave-hunter already has a complement of sailors, and they will best know how to bring us to Umbar, but you will want to fill out the crew with trusted and accomplished folk. After all, there will still be a rescue to manage once we arrive at the City of the Corsairs! King Elessar suggested several additions to the crew, and if you deem these enough we can sail as soon as you have returned with them: Lady Nauriel of Pinnath Gelin, the boon companions Legolas and Gimli, Lord Sirgon of Pelargir, Corudan's sister Sigileth, and the Corsair Jajax. I have compiled notes on each of these, and on others who might be willing to sail with us on the Wave-hunter. Consult my notes in the book on the table there, and may it prove useful as you assemble your crew.'","Caebar has written some notes about potential crew-members for the Wave-hunter. Consult the book on the table in the library of Lond Cirion, and let it guide you as you assemble your crew.","'The Wave-hunter already has a complement of sailors, and they will best know how to bring us to Umbar, but you will want to fill out the crew with trusted and accomplished folk. After all, there will still be a rescue to manage once we arrive at the City of the Corsairs! King Elessar suggested several additions to the crew, and if you deem these enough we can sail as soon as you have returned with them: Lady Nauriel of Pinnath Gelin, the boon companions Legolas and Gimli, Lord Sirgon of Pelargir, Corudan's sister Sigileth, and the Corsair Jajax. I have compiled notes on each of these, and on others who might be willing to sail with us on the Wave-hunter. Consult my notes in the book on the table there, and may it prove useful as you assemble your crew.'","Recruit any other members of the crew you wish","Complete 'The Crew: The Sea-longing Lord'","Complete 'The Crew: Knight of the Green Hills'","'Have you assembled a crew for the Wave-hunter?'\
\
You tell Caebar about the crew you have recruited for the mission to Umbar, and he nods.\
\
'They sound quite capable, ${PLAYER}. I think you have done very well, and I am glad to have been of service. I suppose it is nearly time for us to depart.'","Complete 'The Crew: The Corsair Jajax'","Elessar has charged you to carry out a dangerous rescue mission to the City of the Corsairs, and for that you will need a willing crew.","Complete 'The Crew: She Who Remained'","Caebar has written some notes about potential crew-members for the Wave-hunter. Consult the book on the table in the library of Lond Cirion, and let it guide you as you assemble your crew.\
\
When you are satisfied with the crew you have assembled, return to the library of Lond Cirion and speak with Caebar."},
[3165]={"Chapter 5.2: Making Ready To Depart","'Time is wasting.'","'The rest of your crew must have arrived at the Wave-hunter by now, and they surely wait for you to join them. Yes, I am coming too. I hope that the brave men and women you have recruited will have courage enough to spare some for me, for the spectre of this voyage fills me with trepidation!\
\
'I will be fine, ${PLAYER}. I have to be. Lead on!'","Sigileth readies for the departure of the Wave-hunter.","Travel to the Wave-hunter where it is docked in Pinnath Gelin","Talk to Sirgon on the deck of the Wave-hunter","'The sailors were up before dawn, making the ship ready to sail, but it seems that was still not enough! When will be the last of these unending delays? My son is still in the hands of the Kindred of the Coins, and must be rescued with all speed!\
\
'My husband will see to the safety of Pinnath Gelin while I am away, but as you are the one King Elessar has chosen for this mission, you will be responsible for the lives of all those aboard the Wave-hunter, ${PLAYER}. I care not for my own life; I care only for that of my son Thorongil. Bring me to his captors and I will do what is necessary.'","Talk to Sigileth beside the Wave-hunter in Pinnath Gelin","'Lead on! The Wave-hunter is docked on the lake to the east of Ost Arndír, in Pinnath Gelin.'","'You may be responsible for the lives of all those aboard the Wave-hunter, ${PLAYER}, but I care not for my own. I care only for that of my son Thorongil. Bring me to his captors and I will do what is necessary.'","Nauriel and others of the crew prepare to depart","'It seems we are once again to be the Hidden Guard, ${PLAYER}, journeying in secret to rescue a captive. Nay, for this time the captives number two, and one of them is my own brother. Let it be a consolation to us that the place we must go can shelter no evil as great as that which lurked within the walls of Dol Guldur.\
\
'I do wish I had my knives for this mission. Lanchigil and Egnassigil would make short work of the Kindred of the Coins, although I understand Elessar is hopeful we can return Thorongil and Corudan without bloodshed. I think that is unlikely.\
\
'I have been training with this blade, just in case. I have not yet given it a name.'","Sirgon stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter, lost in his thoughts, as he prepares for the voyage.","The Wave-hunter is docked on the lake outside Ost Arndír.","Nauriel readies for the voyage of the Wave-hunter where the ship is docked in Pinnath Gelin.","'I rose with the dawn and helped the sailors prepare the Wave-hunter for its voyage. Thank you once again, and a million times more, for allowing me to sail with you, my friend. I feel alive again, and the feel of the deck beneath my feet has given back to me the vigour of my youth!\
\
'To sea, to sea! At last!'","Talk to Nauriel beside the Wave-hunter in Pinnath Gelin","'I understand Elessar is hopeful we can return Thorongil and Corudan without bloodshed. I think that is unlikely.\
\
'I have been training with this blade, just in case. I have not yet given it a name.'","The time has come for you and your trusted crew to depart for Umbar on the Wave-hunter."},
[3166]={"Talk to Mithrandir at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate","Find Plákash in Durthang","Lady Galadriel and Lord Celeborn have come with the Golden Host to Dol Guldur, in preparation for the fortress's destruction. You will find them outside the fortress of Thangúlhad in the Gathbúrz area of Southern Mirkwood.","'Why does Ugrukhôr seek the Weeping Warrior now, and for what purpose? Find one of the leaders of whom Thenca spoke, either Plákash or Durkhlát, and you may learn why they search for Karazgar. Thenca believed the Orcs made for Durthang or Cirith Ungol. Go to one of these towers and compel the Orc to divulge his orders.'","'My patience is at an end, ${PLAYER}. For too long has this den of evil festered beneath the trees. Not content to remain behind the walls of the fortress, that evil spread throughout the forest. Mirkwood was made of it, as should never have been. If the forest is to be renewed and its beauty restored, the fortress of the Necromancer must be razed to its very foundation and its remaining corruptions brought into the light. There they will wither and die, their malice slain and their potential for evil undone.'","Find Galadriel and Celeborn outside Thangúlhad in the Gathbúrz area of Southern Mirkwood","'You made a mistake coming here. Now you will pay the price of it! Speak your last words, and may your death serve as a lesson to others of your kind not to tread too near to Cirith Ungol, or to cross paths with Durkhlát!'\
\
You stand your ground and demand to know his business with the Weeping Warrior. Durkhlát bares his teeth and eyes you warily.\
\
'Karazgar, eh? Why should I tell you anything? Ugrukhôr wants him. Weeping Warrior knows something about the artifact Bugdatish, and the Captain of the Pit is going to make him talk. My boys know where he went: hill of sorcery in the old woods, where the Big Bosses used to tramp. I'll go there next, but first I'll deal with you! Ready yourself for death, foolish ${RACE}!'","'Did you learn why Ugrukhôr seeks the Weeping Warrior, or where the Orcs have gone in search of him? I see from your expression that you learned something of use, but perhaps not the entirety of what we sought?'\
\
You recount what you were able to learn, and Mithrandir briefly considers the Orc's words.\
\
'It is better than I feared, ${PLAYER}. There are still gaps in our knowledge, but the Orc has given us more than I expected. It appears that Ugrukhôr expects to find Karazgar at the \\qhill of sorcery,\\q a phrase used in relation to the fortress of the Necromancer. Yes, I speak of Dol Guldur. That must be where Karazgar has gone, and it would appear he searches for an artifact, something called Bugdatish. I have never before heard this name, but that means little. There is room among the dark arts of Sauron for such mysteries.\
\
'If you are to search for Karazgar at Dol Guldur, you will need to make haste! The Lord and Lady of Lórien have entered Mirkwood and prepare to raze the fortress. The final mission of the Golden Host is underway, and if you are to find the Weeping Warrior and get some answers about this relic he seeks you must leave at once! Do not stand around gawking at me, ${PLAYER}. Go, and quickly!'","Plákash can be found somewhere within Durthang. Durkhlát can be found outside Cirith Ungol.\
\
Mithrandir asked you to find one of the Orcs that seek the Weeping Warrior and compel him to divulge the purpose for his search.","You have uncovered a course of investigation that Mithrandir hopes will lead to some means of fighting the Masters of Mordor: Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, is sought by Ugrukhôr for some unknown purpose.","Talk to Lady Galadriel outside Thangúlhad","Chapter 5.2: The Warrior Missing","'Yes, I know of the one called Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior. He is numbered among the Gúrzyul and has crossed my path before, though not for many years. I have known him to be active primarily in the East and in the North, but in times of great strife I have heard reports that he was seen further afield and in unexpected places. I find it curious that none have seen him in Gorgoroth of late, and you did not see him at the meeting of the Masters. He is missing, and his absence troubles me. Why did he not come to Gorgoroth when Sauron had need of him, as did others among the Gúrzyul?\
\
'Why does Ugrukhôr seek him now, and for what purpose? Find one of the leaders of whom Thenca spoke, either Plákash or Durkhlát, and you may learn why they search for Karazgar. Thenca believed the Orcs made for Durthang or Cirith Ungol. Go to one of these towers and compel the Orc to divulge his orders.'","The Lord and Lady of the Golden Wood have come to the fortress of Dol Guldur","Find Durkhlát outside Cirith Ungol","'I am glad you have returned to us, ${PLAYER}. The brave advance of the Malledhrim into the forest has borne fruit, our siege proven successful. With the defeat of Sauron, the time has come to cleanse the lands that felt his foul touch. It is not enough to besiege Mirkwood and the fortress that stands atop this hill of sorcery. We must scour this place of his mark and his memory.\
\
'This was the fortress of the Necromancer, the guise Sauron wore when he sought to recover his strength and regain the advantage while our sight was veiled. It was the mission of the Golden Host to seize the fortress, but that mission has changed. The fortress must now be destroyed.'\
\
You tell Celeborn you have reason to believe Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, might seek a powerful artifact somewhere within Dol Guldur. He smiles grimly at you.\
\
'He must seek it quickly, or this artifact will be forever buried and beyond his reach. So too might he, if he ignores the fury of the Elves. It comes now to the fortress and will not abate.'","'Ha! What did you hope to gain by coming here? A quick death? Plákash will be happy to give it to you, as he has given death to so many other fools who dared the fortress of Durthang. Speak your last words, and I will spill your guts and inspect them for both fearlessness and foolishness!'\
\
You stand your ground and demand to know his business with the Weeping Warrior. Plákash bares his teeth and eyes you warily.\
\
'Karazgar, eh? Why should I tell you anything, brazen ${RACE}? Ugrukhôr wants him. Weeping Warrior knows something about this artifact Bugdatish, and the Captain of the Pit is going to make him talk. My boys found out where he went: hill of sorcery in the old woods, where the Big Bosses used to tramp. My boys have already set out, and I'll follow them next, but first I'll take care of you! I'll open you up and see what makes you bold enough to ask questions of Plákash!'","Mithrandir is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.","'If you are to search for Karazgar at Dol Guldur, you will need to make haste! The Lord and Lady of Lórien have entered Mirkwood and prepare to raze the fortress. The final mission of the Golden Host is underway, and if you are to find the Weeping Warrior and get some answers about this relic he seeks you must leave at once! Do not stand around gawking at me, ${PLAYER}. Go, and quickly! You will find them outside the fortress of Thangúlhad in the Gathbúrz area of Southern Mirkwood.'","Talk to Lord Celeborn outside Thangúlhad"},
[3168]={"'These isles are not deserted, ${PLAYER}, and the men who live here may seek to do us harm.'","Talk to Caebar by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles","'Are you ready to give the order? None but you can give it, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Is it time to leave your familiar shores behind?'","'We are lucky to be alive, ${PLAYER}. The storms that arise in the Bay of Belfalas can be fearsome, and these isles are often lashed by the worst of them. Ours is not the first ship to run aground on these isles, and I cannot believe it will be the last.\
\
'I have been to one of the southernmost islands in this chain before. Zamarzîr it was called. My brother and I sheltered for a time among the freebooters who live there, but Jajax did not want to stay, and I could not remain by myself. We were very young then, only children; it must have changed in the years since.\
\
'But our arrival has attracted some attention. Look, among the trees! These isles are not deserted, ${PLAYER}, and the men who live here may seek to do us harm.'","The men stare at you warily","'Our arrival has attracted some attention. Look, among the trees! These isles are not deserted, ${PLAYER}, and the men who live here may seek to do us harm.'","Talk to Daxamat at Voyage's End in the Shield Isles","'An unguarded wreck is free to all who dare search it. Perhaps Mattân and I will come back tomorrow.'","'I knew I did not like sailing, ${PLAYER}! How can it be that Sirgon missed it? A sailing-ship is a hateful thing, as unpleasant a creation as I have ever known!'\
\
You remind Caebar that were it not for the strong hull of the Wave-hunter and its brave crew, he would not have survived the storm. Caebar shakes his head.\
\
'Yes, yes,' he mumbles. 'I suppose it could always be worse. But I am done with ships! You mark my words, ${PLAYER}! From this day forward I will take the land-road, no matter how out of the way it may run!'","Caebar stands by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.","Chapter 5.3: Voyage of the Wave-hunter","You feel eyes upon you from the tree line","'The storm chewed up your ship and spat you out, stranger... but it must not have liked the taste of you. Most of the ships devoured by Shedax Khîn arrive upon the Shield Isles in more pieces than this, and with fewer survivors.\
\
'Shedax Khîn? That is the Umbari word for the rocks that surround the island of Bakhjâd. It means \\qthe Grinding Jaws,\\q and theirs is the smile that welcomes strangers to these isles. But someone else must smile upon you and upon your crew, for while your ship will not sail again, you have your life, and that is more than some retain when they come here.'","Someone watches you from the tree line to the west of the Wave-hunter.","Daxamat has left the ship and awaits your orders.","Talk to Mattân to the west of the Wave-hunter","Confront the men watching you from the tree line to the west","'Very well, my friend!\
\
'Ready the sails! It is time for the Wave-hunter to ride the river down to the sea, and then to make for the City of the Corsairs!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'You are more fortunate than most who come here, stranger.'","Talk to Ozâl to the west of the Wave-hunter","'¿Qué?'","Now that your preparations have been made, it is time for the voyage of the Wave-hunter and the completion of your secret mission.","'Mattân and I listened to the driving rain of the storm last night and it told the two of us a new wreck would decorate the islands this morn. We arose early, before any others, and came here in haste... but we were rewarded with disappointment. The isles have their new decoration, aye. But the Grinding Jaws did not finish their meal, and too many survivors guard the wreck.\
\
'There will be little for us to salvage today. But I tell you this: life in the Shield Isles is hard, and not all who arrive here as you have can endure it. You survived the storm, but will you survive the week? Will you survive the day?\
\
'Oh, it is no threat, stranger. I am simply making conversation.'","Two residents of the Shield Isles watch you with suspicion in their eyes.","Talk to Sirgon and give the order for the ship to set sail to Umbar","Sirgon stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter, eager for the ship to set sail."},
[3169]={"'This place must be the Sorcerers' Stores, but I made it my own. From here I launched my own attacks against the forces of the Dark Lord that tried to hide from the Golden Host. They could not hide from me, not even in this isolated and secret dungeon. I stalked my foes in their own domicile, bringing death to them on stealthy feet. I struck swiftly and faded again into the darkness, and kept a tally of my slain foes. Did I once belong to the Hidden Guard? Now have I truly become the Hidden Guard, ${PLAYER}. All the others are gone, but I remained behind, and I never stopped fighting.'\
\
Sigileth laughs, but there is little amusement in it. You tell her that everyone thought she died in the Battle of the Tower. At this she does smile.\
\
'On the stair my wounds were grievous, the pain severe enough that I dropped my knives: beloved Lanchigil and keen-edged Egnassigil. I slipped from the landing and my body fell into the depths. When I awoke, I found myself in this secret wing, cut off from the Golden Host. I sought to return to the surface, but the intense shadow of the Room of Voices prevented me from passing beyond.\
\
'You say everyone believed I was dead? Not everyone, ${PLAYER}. I heard the voice of Lady Galadriel in my mind, and she said it was time for me to leave the fortress. I braved the Room of Voices one last time... and that is when I found you.'","Talk to Gladhel within Dol Guldur","Chapter 5.3: Whispers from the Long Years","'The Lady has come to Dol Guldur? Then it is true. The mission of the Golden Host nears its end! These are happy tidings indeed!\
\
'We will make our way from the fortress, as you ask. There is another sentry post ahead where our brothers and sisters stand vigil against new incursions of the enemy. Go to them and deliver your message, and we will see you again at the base of the hill!'","Talk to Sigileth in her hideout","'I can bring down the walls of the fortress, but I will not endanger those of my people who remain within. I ask you to climb the hill and recall those of the Golden Host who remain. Tell them to leave the fortress, for soon it will no longer darken the hill upon which it stands. Their vigil is no longer needed.'\
\
Galadriel pierces you with her bright eyes.\
\
'Bring them all from the fortress, ${PLAYER}. All of them. Leave no one behind.'","Find Elves of the Golden Host within Dol Guldur","The Lord and Lady of Lórien have joined the Golden Host for the final destruction of Dol Guldur.","'I can bring down the walls of the fortress, but I will not endanger those of my people who remain within. I ask you to climb the hill and recall those of the Golden Host who remain. Tell them to leave the fortress. Leave no one behind.'","'Seek out the secret of the shadowy wing and then return. I will ask the Lady to delay until you have emerged safely from the dungeons! The secret stairway is down the slope and beyond the raised portcullis. Look to the left after you pass through, and you will see the door that leads to the secret stair.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Using the door to the secret stair will begin a Solo quest that cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'${PLAYER}! I hear your message and will lead my warriors down the hill and to safety, but I wonder if you will first do something for me. This morning we found a covered passage leading to a hidden stair. We sought to explore its depths, but my warriors encountered powerful shadow and turned back.\
\
'But you wield the Light of Eärendil, and its luminance might help you keep your spirits aloft even in the deepest darkness. Will you investigate the hidden stair and the room of shadow? Only a work of great evil could have left such a powerful mark upon this secret wing of the fortress. The Lady will soon raze Dol Guldur, but I do not want to leave this mystery unexamined. Seek out its secret and return. I will ask the Lady to delay until you have emerged safely from the dungeons!\
\
'The secret stairway is down the slope and beyond the raised portcullis. Look to the left after you pass through, and you will see the door that leads to the secret stair.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Using the door to the secret stair will begin a Solo quest that cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Sigileth is in her hideout deep beneath Dol Guldur.","You found some Malledhrim sentries within the walls of Dol Guldur","'There is another sentry post ahead where our brothers and sisters stand vigil against new incursions of the enemy. Go to them and deliver the message you brought to us, and we will see you again at the base of the hill!'","Talk to Bánoth within Dol Guldur","Explore the room of shadow at the bottom of the secret stair","Elves of the Golden Host can be found within the walls of Dol Guldur.","'Mae govannen, friend!'","You found another group of sentries within the walls of Dol Guldur","This must be the entrance of which Bánoth spoke.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Find Elves of the Golden Host deeper within Dol Guldur","Bánoth asked you to investigate the secret stairway his warriors discovered down the slope, behind the door on the left."},
[3170]={"You have found Sigileth in a secret wing beneath Dol Guldur, and she wishes to help you complete your mission before the fortress is destroyed.","Defeated Orcs within Gostador (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Servants of Sauron and evil relics can be found throughout the halls and chambers of Gostador.","Defeat Orcs within Gostador (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected runed tomes within Gostador (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sigileth is in her hideout at the Sorcerer's Stores, in Gostador.","'I have never seen such deep shadow as that which blankets the Room of Voices, and the fell whispers that still lurk there confound the mind and caused even my heart to quail. Some work of great evil must have been conducted there, and the memory of it has scarred that chamber.'\
\
You tell Sigileth your belief that the spirit of Sauron spent the years following his defeat by the Last Alliance recovering in that chamber beneath the fortress.\
\
'That explains the shroud that hangs upon it. Now he has fully regained his strength, his shadow will continue to grow, and fester.'\
\
You explain, briefly, that Sauron has been defeated, and you came to Dol Guldur in search of the Bugdatish, an artifact prized by his Gúrzyul. Sigileth stares at you with wonder.\
\
'Gurth dan i ngúdrim! I am filled with amazement, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps the end of the Dark Lord will serve to lessen the shadow that lies upon the Room of Voices, rather than increase it! It is clear you have many tales to tell since battle drew us apart, but those can wait until we escape from the fortress. I am unfamiliar with the name Gúrzyul, or with this Bugdatish, but many are the relics that lie within Gostador. Let us search for these, and lay waste to any of Sauron's remaining servants. Then we will escape together.'","Collect runed tomes within Gostador (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the relics and tomes to Sigileth in the Sorcerer's Stores, in Gostador","'We have gathered a number of relics and tomes, but it will be up to others to examine them. Is one of these the artifact you seek, the Bugdatish? We will not find out here.'","Collected hoarded relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I am unfamiliar with the name Gúrzyul, or with this Bugdatish, but many are the relics that lie within Gostador. Let us search for these, and lay waste to any of Sauron's remaining servants. Then we will escape together.'","Collect hoarded relics within Gostador (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Chapter 5.4 She Who Remained"},
[3171]={"'I should have known you would adventure here, ${PLAYER}, for it seems you truly fear nothing! My father sent you to help me clean these mirrors? I have already restored this one, but still I appreciate the company.\
\
'Whenever I see one of these devices I marvel at it, here no less than in Moria where first I beheld such a thing. For my ancestors to have made a weapon of light in this fashion... that is truly a feat of craft and skill!'","Clean the south-western mirror mechanism at Vâr Nuchur","Talk to Bori north-west of Vâr Nuchur","This dirty mirror is covered in filth and no longer reflects light","Bósi directed you to the west, where he spoke of more mirrors in need of cleaning.","'There you are! I should have known you would adventure here, and fear nothing!'","You scrub filth from the dirty mirror until it gleams","Searching for mirrors to clean, you have found Bósi's son Bori north-west of Vâr Nuchur.","You scrub the dirt of years from the mirror until it shines once again","Clean the eastern mirror mechanism at Vâr Nuchur","Clean the mirror south-east of Bósi's location","'The prince has charged me with sending dwarves to scout the further reaches of Máttugard. There is no shortage of eager explorers among both the Longbeards and the Zhélruka, to their credit! I confess to a certain hesitation when it came to sending forth dwarves who fought with the Iron Garrison in Moria, but Bósi assured me that they were fully-prepared to face the dangers ahead. I believe him, but perhaps you can follow him and make certain my trust is not misplaced?\
\
'Bósi and some of his kin went to the west, planning to skirt the southern side of the great pit.'","Find the dirty mirror of which Bósi spoke to the south-east","'¡Aquí, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}!'","'I sent Bori looking for other mirrors to restore, but it would not surprise me to learn that he became distracted from the task and instead went in search of enemies to slay. Follow in his steps and restore the mirrors he has not, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'I intended for him to clean the mirrors to the west.'","'Look at this, ${PLAYER}! Even so far underground, this troll has been turned to stone by the ingenious workings of dwarves! By the clever use of mirror mechanisms, my people redirected sunlight through the halls of Máttugard, and at some point during the long years of the mountain's abandonment, this troll ran afoul of the trap! We saw much the same in Moria, did we not?\
\
'The device that ensnared this troll has become encrusted with dirt and filth, and no longer reflects the light as once it did. Can you clean it of grime and restore the mirror's effectiveness?'","You will find Bósi along the southern side of the great pit in the centre of Máttugard.","Clean the mirror mechanism north-west of Vâr Nuchur, and down a level","Chapter 5.4: A Weapon of Light","Glóin has asked you to aid the dwarves of the Iron Garrison he sent to scout the further reaches of Máttugard.","After a good scrubbing, the mirror mechanism once again reflects light","The mirror mechanism to the south-east once kept the trolls at bay, but now it is filth-covered and non-reflective. Bósi asked you to clean the dirty mirror and restore its troll-hindering potential.","The mirror mechanism south of the great pit once kept the trolls at bay, but now it is filth-covered and non-reflective. Bósi asked you to clean the dirty mirror to the south-east and restore its troll-hindering potential.","As you approach the mirror, you see that someone has already cleaned it of grime","'The device that ensnared this troll has become encrusted with dirt and filth, and no longer reflects the light as once it did. Can you clean it of grime and restore the mirror's effectiveness?'","'Ah, very good! That is a start. There are other similar mechanisms throughout the halls. I sent Bori looking for them, but it would not surprise me to learn that he became distracted from the task and instead went in search of enemies to slay. Follow in his steps and restore the mirrors he has not, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'I intended for him to clean the mirrors to the west.'","Bósi stands here, studying a troll-shaped stone statue","Look for Bósi south of the great pit in Máttugard","'I sent Bori looking for other mirrors to restore, but it would not surprise me to learn that he became distracted from the task and instead went in search of enemies to slay. Follow in his steps and restore the mirrors he has not, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'I intended for him to clean the mirrors to the west of here.'","You have found Bósi south of the great pit in Máttugard, studying a troll that has been turned to stone.","Now that you cleaned the mirror as he requested, you should return to Bósi in Máttugard, north-west of the cleaned mirror.","'Bósi assured me that the dwarves who fought for the Iron Garrison were fully-prepared to face the dangers ahead. I believe him, but perhaps you can follow him and make certain my trust is not misplaced?\
\
'Bósi and some of his kin went to the west, planning to skirt the southern edge of the great pit.'","Talk to Bósi south of the great pit in Máttugard","Talk to Bósi to the north-west in Máttugard"},
[3172]={"Talk to Sirgon by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles","Sirgon has joined you and Caebar by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.","Talk to Caebar by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles","Complete 'The Isles: Keen-eyed Sigileth'","Complete 'The Isles: The Corsair Daxamat'","Complete 'The Isles: Gimli and Legolas'","Chapter 5.4: The Shield Isles","Complete 'The Isles: The Knight Nauriel'","'I am sorry to interrupt, ${PLAYER}. But... I overheard you speaking with Caebar, and I thought I heard the boy speak a name that... well, a name I have not heard in many years.\
\
'Did you speak the name Belondor? Or have I misheard you?'\
\
Caebar shrugs apologetically and responds that \\qBelondor of the Fleet-fast\\q was listed as one of the bounties for which Saklaphêl would pay a valuable reward. Sirgon nods, a haunted look in his eye.\
\
'I see. It couldn't be... and yet perhaps it could.'","Complete 'The Isles: Sirgon the Explorer'","Eager to obtain a secure foothold from which to continue the mission, some of the Wave-hunter's crew have scattered across the Shield Isles and must be found.","Think it over","'Many members of the crew have returned to the Wave-hunter, ${PLAYER}, and I know we have you to thank for that! Did their scouting turn up anything of use to us?'\
\
You tell Caebar what you learned about the Widow Saklaphêl and the Heirs of Castamir, and the bounty she has placed upon the leadership of the Kindred of the Coins. He smiles wryly.\
\
'I suppose that might be one way to complete our mission: get one of these bounty-hunters to slay the folk responsible for capturing Thorongil and Corudan, and mount a rescue mission during the ensuing chaos. What were the names of the targets? Azagath the Sea-shadow, Belondor of the Fleet-fast, and Hármelak Golden-hand? They sound... lovely.'","Each member of your crew has gone in search of some way to help, but now many of them are scattered across the various islands that make up the Shield Isles.","Sirgon joins you and calls for your attention","'¿Qué es?'","'Nauriel declared she could not wait, and pressed through the trees to the south, and I saw Sigileth wading through the waves to the south-east of here. As for Gimli and Legolas, I heard the Elf calling for Gimli to follow him to the south-east in search of game animals, but I do not know how far they might have travelled. I think they may have gone as far as Zamarzîr.'","'Waiting for the rain to end was a burden for some of the crew, and of that number many of them have already gone to scout the neighbouring isles. Nauriel declared she could not wait, and pressed through the trees to the south, and I saw Sigileth wading through the waves to the south-east of here in search of... I know not what. Does she think the ship carrying her brother to Umbar ran afoul of the rocks as we did? As for Gimli and Legolas, I heard the Elf calling for Gimli to follow him to the south-east in search of game animals, but I do not know how far they might have travelled. I think they may have gone as far as Zamarzîr.\
\
'The rest of the crew may be scattered across any of the Shield Isles, ${PLAYER}! We need them to return so we can decide what to do next!'","Caebar is by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.","Sirgon is interested in your conversation with Caebar."},
[3173]={"Find the location to the west where Sirgon wants to talk with you","'Let us not speak of it here. Meet me to the west.'","Sirgon has asked to meet you to the west so he can discuss something with you.","'The Steward Denethor came to believe that Belondor cared more for the people of Umbar than he did for his native Gondor, and he distrusted the man he had named Warden of the Firth. He believed Belondor had fallen under the sway of the Church of the All Seeing, a religion that had at the time a small, though growing, presence in the city of Umbar. This was impossible to believe, and even today I do not believe it, but the Steward had other reasons to distrust Belondor.\
\
'My old friend had fallen in love with an Umbari noblewoman named Mêshka. I do not know how the Steward came to learn of this, but the rumours eventually came even to the White City. There must have been spies aboard one or more of Belondor's ships, or lurking in the court of Mêshka's home... but I cannot say for certain. When paired with Belondor's recent missives, which counseled mercy and fairness for the Umbari people, these whispers painted a clear picture of betrayal that the Steward of Gondor could not disbelieve.\
\
'He commanded the master of his navy to pursue the traitor Belondor, relieve him of his duties, and bring him back to Gondor. I could not refuse the command, ${PLAYER}.'","Sirgon has fallen silent once again.","'Let us not speak of it here. Meet me to the west of here, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'It may be I am worried for nothing, and it is not the same man. But my heart says it must be.'","'I am not a man for whom deceit comes easily, ${PLAYER}, but I could not think my old friend a traitor without good cause. On any other day, a call to dinner at my manor-house would have been the signal for a time of merriment and joyful reunion, but on this day it was a lure. Belondor answered the summons, for he had no reason to suspect the orders given to me by the Steward Denethor. Over dinner I asked him where lay his loyalties... and his answer did not dispel my worries.\
\
'\\qThey lie with Umbar Baharbêl, the City of Sails, my old friend,\\q he said to me. \\qThey lie with my Mêshka, to whom I am betrothed. And only then do they lie with Gondor. Can a man not serve three loves equally in his heart, if he is wise and fair?\\q\
\
'\\qThe Steward Denethor does not think so,\\q I told him, and our raised voices would have proven to me that our friendship was at an end, even if the drawn swords had not followed. Each of us sustained injuries in that duel, and Belondor fled through the shadowed streets of Pelargir to where his ship lay moored. For three days I pursued him in my own vessel across the tumultuous Bay, when at last he dared draw too near the Grinding Jaws; among the rocks of Shedax Khîn his ship perished. Some of his crew we rescued, but of Belondor there was no sign, and I believed him drowned, lost at sea. The Steward Denethor praised me for the pursuit, but I mourned lost Belondor, and cursed the duty that made me drive my friend to his death. But I cursed it silently, for still I served the Steward.'","Sirgon seems ready to conclude his tale","Sirgon is west of Voyage's End, ready to continue his tale.","'Thank you for indulging me in this, ${PLAYER}. I owe you so much for allowing me to join the crew of the Wave-hunter and come with you on this voyage. I would follow you to the very ends of the earth, know that I would, and never complain or say to you a cross word. I have always done my duty as I saw it, first for the Steward of Gondor and then for the King Elessar, and now for you, as the leader of this mission. So I will not still my tongue now, and I will tell you the source of my fear. May it prove without base!\
\
'The name spoken by the young scribe: Belondor. I knew a Belondor when I was a young man. He was born in Anfalas and grew up along the Langstrand, and we both served at the command of the Steward Denethor. Belondor and I were well-nigh inseparable, and together sailed this very Bay of Belfalas and up the coast of Gondor to more distant shores. He was at my wedding, by the Valar, and gave the toast before all the gathered company! Celebros had me keep the stuffed birds he gave us for a wedding-gift in my hall of keepsakes, even when later events made their reminder a painful one.\
\
'We rose in the estimation of the Steward. Even as I was made master of the fleets of Gondor, Belondor was named Warden of the Firth, and worked faithfully to keep the city of Umbar under guard, its pirates quelled and under control. He was an empathic guardian of the city, fair and just to the Umbari people, and they loved him. But this love proved to have a cost.'","Sirgon is west of Voyage's End, waiting to speak with you.","'Gracias.'","Wait for Sirgon to gather his thoughts once again","Chapter 5.5: Belondor of Langstrand","Sirgon seems ready to continue his tale","Sirgon's joy of exploring the Shield Isles has soured a little with the arrival of some new information.","Sirgon has fallen silent.","Wait for Sirgon to gather his thoughts","Talk to Sirgon on the rocky outcropping","Sirgon stands on the rocky outcropping, staring out at the water","Sirgon is west of Voyage's End, ready to conclude his tale."},
[3174]={"Talk to Sigileth on Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin","'I thank you for helping to lead Sigileth from the depths of Dol Guldur. I was not aware she still lived before we came to this hill of sorcery, but as we approached the wall I sensed her in the darkness. I could not have left her there, ${PLAYER}, though Sauron himself survive within. I thank you for bringing her forth. Many of my people died in service of the Golden Host, and I mourn for every one.","Talk to Thranduil on Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin","'With you by my side, ${PLAYER}, even the whispers in the Room of Voices cannot stay my advance. Onward, brave ${RACE}! Our mission is fulfilled!'","Talk to Galadriel on Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin","Galadriel has cast down the walls of Dol Guldur and laid bare its pits, and now she wishes to speak with you.","Sigileth is on Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin.","Chapter 5.5: The Walls Brought Down","'The weeks I spent as the Hidden Guard within Gostador, levying vengeance upon the Orcs, are not pleasant to recall and neither shall I miss them. But I am proud to have done my Lady's work. Let us escape now from the fortress, and she will fulfill her own obligation and raze this place to its foundation!\
\
'With you by my side, ${PLAYER}, even the whispers in the Room of Voices cannot stay my advance. Onward, brave ${RACE}! Our mission is fulfilled!'","'The Golden Host achieved its aim, and so too did the Hidden Guard. I am proud of our accomplishments, ${PLAYER}. My brother Corudan will be pleased to hear of them, if he is home in Lórien and not away, walking the river as is his wont.'\
\
You tell Sigileth that you journeyed with Corudan for a time in Rohan, but he vanished while scouting outside Helm's Deep and you do not know his fate.\
\
'My brother was always given to journey, but he was fond of the Anduin and did not stray far from its banks. Rohan? It seems there is another tale for you to tell, but it must wait. You thought me dead, ${PLAYER}, but I was not. So too might it be with Corudan. I will return to the Golden Wood for a brief time, but not to mourn.\
\
'I go there to prepare. I will call for you when I am ready, and we will find my brother. We will find Corudan River-walker, and compare our tales of adventure.'","'We are well-met on this hill of ruin, ${PLAYER}. My realm in the north of the wood came under threat, but despite fire and battle I seized the victory. I came south then, and beneath the trees I met Celeborn of Lórien in friendship and in peace. He agrees, as do I, that the time of the Mirkwood is over. Together we call it by a new name, Eryn Lasgalen, and may it bear that name ever onward. From this day forth it will be the Wood of the Greenleaves, and we will work to cleanse the mark of Sauron from every corner, and heal the hurts he worked upon it by his presence.'\
\
Thranduil surveys the ruin of the fortress, but when he turns his gaze upon you, he speaks more warmly than you expected.\
\
'I understand you befriended my son Legolas, ${PLAYER}. In token of that friendship, I open my land and my halls to you. Tell me what you seek, and I will do what I can to help you achieve it.'","'You thought me dead, ${PLAYER}, but I was not. So too might it be with Corudan. I will return to the Golden Wood for a brief time, but not to mourn.\
\
'I go there to prepare. I will call for you when I am ready, and we will find my brother. We will find Corudan River-walker and compare our tales of adventure.'","'At last the fortress has been cast down. Its dark walls can no longer hide the works of Sauron. Rejoice with the Golden Host, ${PLAYER}, for a time of trouble and woe has come to its ending, and you played your part in it with grace and with skill.\
\
'I thank you too for helping to lead Sigileth from the depths of Dol Guldur. I was not aware she still lived before we came to this hill of sorcery, but as we approached the wall I sensed her in the darkness. I could not have left her there, ${PLAYER}, though Sauron himself survive within. I thank you for bringing her forth. Many of my people died in service of the Golden Host, and I mourn for every one.\
\
'But Dol Guldur stands no more, and that is a testament to their sacrifice.'","Thranduil the Elvenking has come to Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin.","Galadriel has laid waste to the fortress of Dol Guldur, bringing an end to its capacity to nurture the evils of Sauron."},
[3175]={"'Did you find anything? Alas, neither did I. If this was once a troll-hoard, it is no longer, for Orcs or others of similar ilk have looted it of whatever treasures it once might have held. A pity... that looter could have been me! Just a jest, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'But I do owe Thettmárr a rather sizeable debt, and I could have used these treasures to pay him. He graciously offered to play me in one more game of Hammers and Bones, so that I could win back my losses... but that was five games ago! Now I am so deep in his debt, and my luck has turned so poor, that I do not trust myself to approach the gambling-table ever again!\
\
'I have seen goblins sneaking about. Do you think you could wrest some of their coin-purses from them? You would be making these halls more safe for the Gabil'akkâ, and at the same time you would be helping me with my own problem, ${PLAYER}. That way everyone is happy, except for the goblins, and what ${RACE} should care about the happiness of goblins? Once you have found three coin-purses, bring them to Thettmárr south-west of Maergrind for me, and I will be in your debt. Figuratively-speaking, that is!'","Talk to Líkmund outside the grodbog-infested troll-hoard, to the north-west","'I have a few spots in mind that might once have served as possible troll-hoards. Will you investigate and see if any treasures remain? Try searching first to the south, and afterwards look far to the east, beyond the great pit in the centre of Máttugard.'","You root around in the debris, but find nothing of value","'Hallo there, friend. Are you also looking for treasure?\
\
'The gredbyg have moved into this tunnel, but it seems to me it was once a troll-hoard. What valuables might still remain inside?'","This might also once have been home to trolls and their treasure","Talk to Bróin at Maergrind, the Noble Gate","'I hope that Líkmund's ill fortune will not affect our efforts here in Gundabad!'","Bori has two locations in mind that might once have served as troll-hoards full of treasure. The first is a short distance to the south of his position.","Bróin catches your eye, a haunted expression on his face","Bori has two locations in mind that might once have served as troll-hoards full of treasure. The second is far to the east, beyond the great pit in the centre of Máttugard.","'The sight of all these trolls turned to stone in the halls of Máttugard has raised in me a curiosity, ${PLAYER}. When these creatures were petrified, what happened to their treasures? Might there be valuables hidden away in their hoards? The contents of such a hoard, once ill-gotten, might be cured of that defect when found by good-hearted folk such as us!\
\
'I have a few spots in mind that might once have served as possible troll-hoards. Will you investigate and see if any treasures remain? Try searching a short distance to the south, and once you have done that try looking far to the east, beyond the great pit in the centre of Máttugard.'","'I have a few spots in mind that might once have served as possible troll-hoards. Will you investigate and see if any treasures remain? Try looking first to the south, and then afterwards far to the east across the great pit, friend.'","A foul reek emanates from an entrance in the western wall: the odour of troll?","This coffer has been emptied of any treasure it might once have held","Collect coinpurses from goblins throughout Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find and search the second possible troll-hoard far to the east, beyond the great pit","Líkmund thinks the goblins lurking in the shadowy reaches of Máttugard might have coins they stole during their occupation of Gundabad.","'What have you brought to me, ${PLAYER}? Oh, I see. Líkmund thinks to satisfy his gambling debt to me with these goblin coin-purses? These coins are filthy. Yuck.\
\
'There is good coinage mixed with the bad, but can I tell you something? Líkmund and I have been playing Hammers and Bones for many months now, and I have never seen a streak of ill fate like the one under which he labours now. He cannot seem to win, and I cannot seem to lose. I have begun to wonder if my friend might be cursed!\
\
'I will accept these coins in partial satisfaction of Líkmund's debt to me, but I would consider it paid in full if he simply promised never to play Hammers and Bones ever again! There is something unnatural about his poor luck at that game, and I fear it may spill over into the rest of his life, or affect our efforts here in Gundabad!'","'Do you think you could wrest coin-purses from the goblins? You would be making these halls more safe for the Gabil'akkâ, and at the same time you would be helping me with my own problem, ${PLAYER}. That way everyone is happy, except for the goblins, and what ${RACE} should care about the happiness of goblins? Once you have found three coin-purses, bring them to Thettmárr at Maergrind for me, and I will be in your debt. Figuratively-speaking, that is!'","Find and search the first possible troll-hoard to the south of Bori's position","Bróin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.","Bori wonders whether any of the trolls that were turned to stone by the mirror mechanisms throughout Máttugard might have kept treasure-hoards nearby, and wants you to investigate.","This box contains only dust, looted of treasure long ago by Orcs","Collected goblin coinpurses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Oh, I am sorry, my friend. I am just a little unsettled by the strange familiarity which surrounds me. I remember Thettmárr and Líkmund arguing over games of Hammers and Bones while we sought to reclaim Moria. We were, all of us, members of the Iron Garrison, and we thought to restore the Dwarrowdelf to prominence and glory.\
\
'It was not to be. So many were lost...'\
\
Bróin's voice trails away, and you know he is thinking of his father Brogur, who perished during the escape from Khazad-dûm. Then he shakes his head and looks you in the eye.\
\
'But Gundabad is not Moria, and the Gabil'akkâ will not share the fate of the Iron Garrison. I should not be troubled by the reminder that Thettmárr and Líkmund played their game in Moria, and they play it here too; I should be heartened that they both live to play it still! Thank you for providing a kindly ear, ${PLAYER}. I will be all right now.'","If the debris of centuries once contained treasure, it does no longer","Bring the coinpurses to Thettmárr south-west of Maergrind in Máttugard","Líkmund is standing by this one-time troll-hoard, waiting to hear of your discoveries.","Líkmund asked you to bring the coinpurses to Thettmárr south-west of Maergrind in partial payment of his gambling debt.","Chapter 5.5: Treasure in a Troll-hoard","'Bring those coin-purses to Thettmárr, south-west of Maergrind. It will likely not satisfy my whole debt, but I wager it will be a good start!\
\
'You know what I mean, ${PLAYER}!'"},
[3176]={"Nauriel believes you should ask the folk who live in Halrax, on the island of Zamarzîr, what they know about the bounty hunters recruited by Saklaphêl.","'I must ask you to tell the Lady Nauriel what I have told you. If her son may be further endangered by this account, she deserves to know of it.'","'You have the look of someone who bears bad tidings, ${PLAYER}, but with our current situation as it is I cannot imagine what could be worse.'\
\
You tell Nauriel, briefly, of Sirgon's belief that \\qBelondor of the Fleet-fast\\q may have once been a friend of his. She raises an eyebrow at you and puts her hand on the hilt of her sword, toying with the favour tied there by her husband Carandolion.\
\
'It matters not to me, ${PLAYER}, unless Sirgon thinks to stand with the Kindred of the Coins against us when the time comes to rescue my son. Do you think he might?\
\
'But that is still some time away; we must first leave these islands and reach the City of the Corsairs. Daxamat and some others of the crew have gone to the settlement of Halrax on the southern island of Zamarzîr to see what they can learn of the bounty-hunters Saklaphêl has likely employed. Can I ask you to also speak with residents of Halrax about this? Once we have learned what we can about them, we may be able to make use of them in our rescue of Thorongil, as we discussed.'","'Nauriel sent you here to ask for information about Saklaphêl's bounty-hunters? How did you fare?'\
\
You reluctantly tell Daxamat that the folk of Halrax were less than helpful. He puts a reassuring hand on your shoulder, and then quickly removes it.\
\
'I am sorry, ${PLAYER}. I did have more success than you, but remember that I did grow up here! There are not many folk who remember me, but there are a few. I learned from them that perhaps a dozen bounty-hunters met with Saklaphêl's man Galadaith, but of that number only three seemed serious about it. One of these I heard talk about even when I was just a child: the Blade-twist, who must be an old man by now, surely. The other is a woman, Cruel Dancer, and of those I spoke to she is believed to have the greatest chance of actually claiming any of the bounties.\
\
'It seems the Blade-twist and Cruel Dancer have already departed the islands, but the third bounty-hunter may still be here. He is a man they call Driftwood, and he lives here in Halrax. Perhaps you can speak to Manadhon, the man who tends the bar here, and learn where we can meet with Driftwood? You are certain to redeem yourself in the eyes of the crew, ${PLAYER}! Oh... my apologies!'","Talk to Manadhon on the upper level of Halrax and complete 'The Isles: Driftwood'","'Daxamat and some others of the crew have gone to the settlement of Halrax on the southern island of Zamarzîr to see what they can learn of the bounty-hunters Saklaphêl has likely employed. Can I ask you to also speak with residents of Halrax about this? Once we have learned what we can about them, we may be able to make use of them in our rescue of Thorongil, as we discussed.'","'It seems the Blade-twist and Cruel Dancer have already departed the islands, but the third bounty-hunter may still be here. He is a man they call Driftwood, and he lives here in Halrax. Perhaps you can speak to Manadhon, the man who tends the bar here, and learn where we can meet with Driftwood? You are certain to redeem yourself in the eyes of the crew, ${PLAYER}! Oh... my apologies!'","Nauriel is back at the Wave-hunter, waiting for information about the bounty hunters recruited by Saklaphêl.","Belondor is not the first wayward voyager to return from death among the Shield Isles, and he will not be the last.","Talk to Nauriel at Voyage's End","Asked about Saklaphêl's bounty hunters (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Nauriel has returned to the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles and will surely have a plan.","'The Belondor that belongs now to the Kindred of the Coins may not be the same man... but in my heart I know he must be. Did he survive the wreck of his ship during my pursuit, and come to make a desperate living upon the wild Shield Isles? He did not hold hatred for Gondor in his heart before that night, whatever the Steward may have believed, but afterwards...? No man could do otherwise.\
\
'I cannot know by what paths he returned to Umbar, but when he did it seems he found others who shared his mind. Did he rise through the ranks of the Kindred, or perhaps he was there at its founding? Now, at least, he holds a position with enough standing to warrant one of Saklaphêl's bounties!'\
\
Sirgon stares at you unhappily.\
\
'I was so pleased to sail again, ${PLAYER}. I had consigned these feelings of guilt to the past, and let the passing of the years dull their pain. But if Belondor did not drown on that night, if he now leads the Kindred of the Coins that hold Thorongil and your Elf-friend captive... I fear that the history between us may put both of those lives in greater danger than we believed. And all because I thought I missed the Sea... but I earned my own share of guilt upon the waters, ${PLAYER}. I had thought it gone, but it is never truly gone, is it?'\
\
You tell Sirgon that it is the mission of the Wave-hunter to rescue Nauriel's son Thorongil and your friend Corudan from the Kindred of the Coins, no matter who comprises its membership. He nods, reluctantly.\
\
'Aye. It must be so. But you must tell the Lady Nauriel what I have told you. If her son may be further endangered by this account, she deserves to know of it.'","Ask residents of Halrax about the bounty hunters recruited by Saklaphêl (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Chapter 5.6: A Place for the Lost","Manadhon, the bartender at Halrax, may be willing to tell you about Driftwood, one of the bounty hunters hired by Saklaphêl.","Talk to Daxamat on the eastern side of Halrax, at the bottom of the hill","Daxamat has come to Halrax in search of more information, and can be found at the bottom of the hill on the eastern side of the city.","'When I suggested that one of Saklaphêl's bounty-hunters might help us with our rescue of my son, I did not envision you asking one of them to join the crew, ${PLAYER}. If this Driftwood proves himself useful, that is one thing... but if he did not even set forth for the City of the Corsairs already, how serious can he be about opposing the Kindred of the Coins?\
\
'But I will trust your decision.'"},
[3177]={"'Then let us no longer delay! I am eager to stand atop the Steepset and behold the great hall of the dwarves from that place of honour and history!'","Durin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.","Talk to Durin at Maergrind","'It is my hope that the light of the Zabad'ibîn will remain undimmed, and perhaps their shining radiance will guide us to them! They may yet emerge, and when they do I will place them once more atop the Steepset, a treasure of the Mountain-home restored.'","Durin stands atop the Steepset, considering the progress of his people as they seek to reclaim the halls of Gundabad.","Chapter 5.6: High Seat of the Dwarves","Durin has called for the leaders of the Gabil'akkâ to ascend to the Steepset.","'Listen here, ${PLAYER}. I overheard the words of Prince Durin, and they stirred in me a desire to find the Zabad'ibîn, no matter the danger. Once they are found, I will gift them to the prince and earn myself a noble place in the annals of Gundabad's reclamation!'","Stáli the Hewer is at the Steepset.","'Report to Durin at Maergrind, my friend, and I will join you once I find these few others.'","Talk to Durin at the Steepset","Stáli the Hewer waves you over to him","Talk to Durin and ascend to the Steepset with the Gabil'akkâ","'Bróin found you, then? Very good. I know it was your appraisal of the lad that he weathered the hardships faced by the Iron Garrison in Moria and emerged from them no worse for wear, but all the same I have seen fit to assign him simple, easy tasks, for now. I will turn no dwarf away who vows his aid, but I do not wish to break such valuable implements with uncareful use.\
\
'He is a bearer of messages, for now. That is a useful service, and as we acquire more victories perhaps the shadow of Khazad-dûm that blankets him will shrink.\
\
'But I had Bróin send you to me for a purpose! Are you ready to climb with me to the Steepset, the High Seat of the Lord of Gundabad?'","'But enough of my own troubles! I was supposed to send leaders of the Gabil'akkâ to join the prince as he climbs to the Steepset. Yes, he counts you in that number... and why should he not? You have already proven a great help to us in this campaign, and surely will in the days to come!\
\
'Report to Durin at Maergrind, my friend, and I will join you once I find these few others.'","'I am saddened by the loss of the Zabad'ibîn, but I am not surprised. Who knows how long ago the clutching fingers of the Orcs might have prized them from their settings in the Steepset, and to what vile hole they might have been brought?\
\
'But it is my hope that the light of the Zabad'ibîn will remain undimmed, and perhaps their shining radiance will guide us to them! They may yet emerge, and when they do I will place them once more atop the Steepset, a treasure of the Mountain-home restored.'","With the first foothold of the dwarves in Gundabad assured, Prince Durin calls for the leaders of the Gabil'akkâ to ascend to the Steepset.","Talk to Stáli the Hewer at the Steepset"},
[3179]={"You should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion to learn what sort of expedition they are setting off on now.","Merry and Pippin propose a very different kind of expedition.","'If you ask me, ${PLAYER}, that visit was long overdue. Now we must get the two of them up here sometime soon. \
\
'Don't you worry, either. We shan't break our promise to Frodo. Although... I have not quite finished puzzling over the riddles those fellows left for us. I have a queer feeling it may not be a closed book quite, when all is said and done.'","'The Periain were looking for you once more. In fact, they were here only shortly before you arrived, and very excitable about some kind of expedition, it seemed to me.'","'We are going down to Cormallen - to see Frodo and Sam! It has been a little while and they sent word that they are both feeling much recovered.\
\
'Will you come and join us for a simple meal? Do not worry, you will feel just like one of the hobbits. There is always more room at a round table, as my uncle used to say!'","Chapter 5: A Meal in Cormallen","'You are coming, aren't you? Of course you are!'","Habla con Merry","'Oh... I have over-eaten, I am afraid. Now I am done with food, adventuring, and most other things for a good while! A good doze is the answer. And then who knows what may come up after I wake?'","'${PLAYER}! How would you feel about a very different sort of expedition?'","You should talk with Merry and Pippin now that you have returned to Bâr Thorenion from your meal, and hear their thoughts on the discussion that took place."},
[3180]={"'I have done nothing wrong! He says that I stole his goat, but he is wrong! I won it, legitimately, in a game of Hammers and Bones! I bet this Zhélruka liar doesn't even own a goat!\
\
'Go ask that dwarf, Igrit. She is always playing Hammers and Bones and was there when I won this goat!'","Talk to Prince Ingór","'If that is not the most luckless story I have ever heard, I could not tell you!\
\
'Here, Néchek, take your goat back. I do not need it, and honestly, it looks as if you might. I do not know what that gift is, but I would sure like to try winning it tonight in another game of Hammers and Bones!'","Chapter 5: An Ordinary Squabble","Talk to Víglund","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.","'Now then, have you settled the disagreement? Good! There is no place for bickering in a Zhélruka hall. My word is final!\
\
'Now that calm has returned to Vérnozal, perhaps you should put some of your other skills to use and assist Ausma and Hórin with a mission.'","You question Igrit about both Víglund and Néchek.\
\
'You might find this odd, but they are both telling the truth! Víglund swept up at Hammers and Bones last night, with the goat as the main prize. I could not tell you where the goat came from, however. I think it wandered over and looked quite without an owner, so we all thought the goat would sweeten the pot, you know.'\
\
'Néchek, on the other hand, he never gambles. If that goat does belong to Néchek, you might want to check the stables.'","Search for the missing rope","The rope is tied around some sort of gift","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should talk to Víglund in Vérnozal.","Talk to Néchek","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should show the gift to Néchek in Vérnozal.","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should talk to the arguing dwarves in Vérnozal.","Bring the gift to Igrit","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should talk to Igrit in Vérnozal.","You show Néchek the gift tied with missing rope from the stables.\
\
'Oh my, I am such a fool! Not only is that rope indeed the one used to tether my goat, that gift is also mine.\
\
'I have been trying to profess my love to someone special. I procured the perfect gift, but I lacked anything with which to tie it up! In my haste I must have taken the rope from the stalls without thinking and forgot to latch the gate! Oh, this is all my fault... and for all this unpleasantness my love did not even open the present! Please take the gift away! I do not wish to see it again!'","Complete a Gundabad Mission with either Scout-master Ausma or Hórin","'That Longbeard stole my goat! I would know my goat anywhere and that goat is certainly mine! How can he have won my goat in a game of runic dice? I do not gamble! There is no way I would have sold my goat or gambled it away!'\
\
'Go ask that dwarf, Igrit. She knows me well, and one thing she knows for certain is that I never gamble!'","This feed is fresh and untouched","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should bring the gift to Igrit in Vérnozal.","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to the Zhélruka and to fight on their behalf in Gundabad.","Search for signs of the goat at the stables (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should search for the missing rope in Vérnozal.","These goat droppings are at least a day old","Show the gift to Néchek","Talk to Igrit","Scout-master Ausma and Hórin can both be found at Vérnozal in Máttugard.\
\
You should complete a Gundabad Mission with either Scout-master Ausma or Hórin.","'Oh, is this for tonight's Hammers and Bones pot? You know, this is the second time someone has given me this exact same gift.\
\
'Néchek, that fool! He confessed his love for me, can you believe it? But it is hopeless: how could I love someone who doesn't gamble?'","'${PLAYER}, do you hear that bickering within the hall of Vérnozal? It appears a Longbeard and a Zhélruka are in the midst of a heated conversation! This arguing goes against my decree that all must work together for the continued peace of Gundabad!\
\
'Go and put a stop to it. I would go myself, but I assure you that things would only get louder in the hall if I did!'","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should search for signs of the goat at the stables in Vérnozal.","'Thank you for assisting Ausma and Hórin with a mission. You have done much on this day. Still, there is much more to be done. I will spend the time until you return deciding just what to do next!'","There should be a rope here to tie up the goat, but it is missing!"},
[3181]={"'Lord Duinhir would not have done it himself, ${PLAYER}. He must have paid yonder victim to do the deed, and once it was done he silenced the murderer and made his escape. I will take some of my best men and apprehend him. You bring word to King Elessar that the culprit has been found.'","The Haven tavern is on the south-east side of the Third Circle of the city.","'This must be carefully handled or it will mean war. The murderer must be found. I will try to keep the situation from getting any worse, but I understand Hasong's feelings. They came here under a banner of truce, and someone betrayed that peace. This is a grave injustice, and it must be set right!\
\
'Learn from Hasong what you can, and then go in search of the murderer. Only his blood can save the infant peace now.'","'Mauthoi went by himself to tavern in your city, trusting the laws of Kerem-thak would hold. He trusted that people of Elessar's city would respect the wishes of Elessar... if those wishes are true. Or is it that Elessar sends another message, hiding his real intent behind others, and secretly laughs at death of Mauthoi, ordering it be done? Dhûrto!\
\
'If ${PLAYER} came to Yâd Hakar, spoke to the Khas, and was promised safety... how would Elessar react to murder of ${RACE}? Would it mean war? Hasong asks, \\qWhy should this be different?\\q Prove to me that this was not done by Elessar, or I will return to Khas Rûktar with words of Gondor's true face: no different than lies... no different than Mordor! Dhûrto most vile!\
\
'Mauthoi was killed at tavern called \\qHaven\\q in Third Circle of city.'","Parthadan looks up at you with haunted eyes, and you know at once that he is guilty of the crimes.\
\
'I know why you're here, ${PLAYER}. I have been wandering around the city, looking for reasons to go on, but I found none. It all seemed so clear to me, once, but I cannot recapture that feeling no matter how long I walk.\
\
'I saw Duinhir cleaning his knife, and I thought of his sons, and I knew with complete certainty that the men of Harad had to die. But I serve on the Council of Gondor! I am the Warden of the Green! Who will speak for the folk of Pelennor who lost their homes during the war, if not I? So I took Duinhir's knife when he left it behind, and I paid a man in coin for the deed, and when one of the Haradrim emissaries went to the tavern, my man cut him down.\
\
'It seemed so clear to me: if he lived he would speak my name, in time. So I took the knife from him and slew him too, but the clarity was already going. He was a man of Gondor; why did he need to die, when it was men of Gondor for whom the Warden of the Green sought to provide?'\
\
You ask Parthadan how long he has been with the Withered Tree, and the haunted look is replaced with a confused expression.\
\
'The Withered Tree? Oh, no, you've gotten it wrong, ${PLAYER}. I have never been one of those malcontents. Everything I did... I did for the good of Gondor. I would never join those villains. I wish I could explain to you where it went wrong, but it's just not clear to me anymore. We were at war, and then we weren't, and somewhere along the way I lost something important. I can't remember now what it might have been, but there was a time when I knew this was the right thing to do. It's gone now, though, and I don't think it's ever coming back. I wish I could tell Duinhir I was sorry. I think this is his fault, somehow.'","'It's a terrible thing, just a terrible thing. I've been cleaning up some of the blood spatters. I figure some of the patrons might have accidentally stepped in some before anyone knew what was going on. There are bloody footprints heading for the door.'","Duinhir turns his tear-stained face to you.\
\
'I did not do this, ${PLAYER}! Tell him! You have to tell him I am not guilty of this crime! I hate the Haradrim for what they did to my boys, but I would not kill one, not like this! Let them face me in combat, man to man, and I would show no mercy, but I would not kill any among them like this, like a coward! How could I face Rosfin, having done this and brought shame to my king? I could not! You must believe me!\
\
'My knife... my knife... someone took my knife and used it for the crime! I cannot remember when last I saw it, but I must have set it down somewhere. Yes, I remember cleaning it... was that the last time I held it in my grip? I remember looking out over the city and thinking of my sons... where was that? Maybe it was on the parapet on the north side of the... of the Fifth Circle? Go there, good friend, go there and someone may know something! I am depending on you, ${PLAYER}, and so too are Rosfin and the memory of my boys!'","'The unthinkable has happened, ${PLAYER}. Mauthoi, one of the Haradrim emissaries, has been murdered. He was under my protection! He was in my city! The Withered Tree have gone too far this time, and they have endangered the peace we so desperately need.\
\
'This must be carefully handled or it will mean war. The murderer must be found. I will try to keep the situation from getting any worse, but I understand Hasong's feelings. They came here under a banner of truce, and someone betrayed that peace. This is a grave injustice, and it must be set right!\
\
'Learn from Hasong what you can, and then go in search of the murderer. Only his blood can save the infant peace now.'","Talk to Duinhir in King Elessar's throne room","'${PLAYER}! You have to tell him I did not do this! You know me! I did not kill them!'","This tavern was once a place of cheer, but now the mood is somber","Find the location where Duinhir believes he last saw his knife","Dúnor is in the Haven tavern.","You found a body and a knife hidden a short distance from the tavern. Is this another victim, or the murderer? Or is he both?","'My knife... my knife... someone took my knife and used it for the crime! I cannot remember when last I saw it, but I must have set it down somewhere. Yes, I remember cleaning it... was that the last time I held it in my grip? I remember looking out over the city and thinking of my sons... where was that? Maybe it was on the parapet on the north side of the Fifth Circle? Go there, good friend, go there and someone may know something! I am depending on you, ${PLAYER}, and so too are Rosfin and the memory of my boys!'","You have found another body! A knife lies at his side","Parthadan, the Warden of the Green, is outside the Dome of the Sun on the north-east side of the Sixth Circle.","'I will bring Parthadan to the dungeons. You should return to King Elessar and tell him we have found the murderer.'","Hasong is in King Elessar's throne room.","Talk to Dúnor outside the Dome of the Sun","'I didn't see anything I haven't already told Dúnor. This place is usually all a-bustle, even if the Lords of Gondor haven't been themselves since the battle on the field. First thing I noticed was that fellow lying on the ground there, and I figured he was well in his cups. When I went over to him I saw the blood, and called for the guards.\
\
'You think the Withered Tree did this? It's not right to kill a fellow as wants peace, but you do have to wonder how many good soldiers died at his hands, or at the hands of folk like him. Not excusin' it, mind, just something to weigh, I'd say.'","'What vile snakes live in this country! We came to this place for Kerem-thak, as was our need, and this is how you return our trust? Dhûrto! Betrayal!\
\
'Mauthoi went by himself to tavern in your city, trusting the laws of Kerem-thak would hold. He trusted that people of Elessar's city would respect the wishes of Elessar... if those wishes are true. Or is it that Elessar sends another message, hiding his real intent behind others, and secretly laughs at death of Mauthoi, ordering it be done? Dhûrto, most foul, betrayal of the highest order!\
\
'If ${PLAYER} came to Yâd Hakar, spoke to the Khas, and was promised safety... how would Elessar react to murder of ${RACE}? Would it mean war? Hasong asks, \\qWhy should this be different?\\q Prove to me this was not done by Elessar, or I will return to Khas Rûktar with words of Gondor's true face: no different than lies... no different than Mordor! Dhûrto most vile!\
\
'Mauthoi was killed at tavern called \\qHaven\\q in Third Circle of city.'","'My knife... my knife... someone took my knife and used it for the crime! I cannot remember when last I saw it, but I must have set it down somewhere. Yes, I remember cleaning it... was that the last time I held it in my grip? I remember looking out over the city and thinking of my sons... where was that? Maybe it was on the parapet on the north side of the... of the Fifth Circle? Go there, good friend, go there and someone may know something! I am depending on you, ${PLAYER}, and so too are Rosfin and the memory of my boys!'","Chapter 5: Dhûrto","Confront Parthadan outside the Dome of the Sun","'Ah, ${PLAYER}. It is good to see you again. I have not forgotten how you helped me calm the unruly crowd the other day. Not enough, it seems; one of them took matters into his own hands. Did King Elessar ask you to look into the Haradrim murder?\
\
'I have already spoken with some of the folk here, but you are welcome to see if they have remembered anything. I haven't moved his body yet, so you can check and see if there's anything I missed. He's over there.\
\
'I have no love for the Haradrim, but this wasn't right. Curse the Withered Tree, they've gone and made things worse!'","Talk to folk near the spot Duinhir described","This Gondorian man was stabbed in the front, and it appears he struggled with his attacker","'Someone here might have seen something. If you talk to them, it could be they will remember something they forgot to tell me. Unlikely, but possible.'","'It is a long chance, ${PLAYER}, but it is a chance. Go to the parapet on the north side of the Fifth Circle and see if anyone there saw anything.'","Duinhir is in King Elessar's throne room.","A Gondorian man seeks to get your attention on the parapet on the north side of the Fifth Circle.","Look for bloodstains outside the tavern and follow them","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Elessar and the Kingdom of Gondor, and to fight on their behalf in Mordor.","Talk to tavern-goers in the Haven (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'You say you found something? Well, don't dawdle here! Go examine the new evidence and bring anything you find back to me!'","It might be innocent, or the blood might have dripped from the murder weapon!","'The guards have been and gone, ${PLAYER}. Duinhir has been released, and Parthadan will die for the murders of two men. It is not enough for Hasong, and it is not enough for me. This should never have happened.\
\
'Hasong will return to his Khas with the knowledge that justice was meted-out upon the murderer, but it will not change this truth: they came here under a banner of peace, and Gondor betrayed them.\
\
'Sauron is gone, but he gave us many unwanted gifts before the War of the Ring came to a close. Dhûrto, ${PLAYER}. I cannot abide the sound of the word, but I know that this day, Gondor deserves it.\
\
'I thank you for what you have done, my friend. An innocent man was spared, and for that we should be thankful. I will await news of your return, and hope that your adventures progress well, and simply. How is it that war can be so clear, and peace be so confused?'","Bring the knife to Dúnor in the Haven tavern","A tavern-worker has begun to clean up some of the blood. Did he see anything?","'Duinhir was brought before me and he claims innocence of the crime. What say you to this, ${PLAYER}? I have heard his words, but I would hear what you think as well.'\
\
You give Elessar your opinion, and he nods.\
\
'There is no doubt that Duinhir keenly feels the loss of his sons beneath the trampling feet of the Mûmakil, the beasts wielded in war by the Haradrim. But why would he pay a man to commit this murder, only to leave behind his dagger, distinctive as it is? If the killing was fueled by a desire for vengeance, would he not wish to carry it out himself? Further, this act has now claimed two lives, one of whom can carry no burden for the deaths of Duilin and Derufin, no matter how slight.\
\
'I will not rush to exonerate him; neither will I render hasty judgement. Speak to him, ${PLAYER}, and hear what he has to say of this. If there is anything he knows that may point to another, he should provide it, for Hasong will not wait long before returning to his country with a call for war.'","Dúnor has come with you to apprehend Parthadan.","'It was dark in here. It's always pretty dark, so that isn't unusual. I can't be sure, but I think I saw a cloaked figure moving for the door a moment before anyone noticed the dead man. He may have had a limp, or an odd way of walking? I can't say for certain, but the more I think about it the more I wonder if this fellow might be the culprit.\
\
'He might have had a beard? Maybe not. It was dark in here! I wish I had paid more attention, but you never think of that at the time, do you?\
\
'I can't be certain about the limp, or the beard. I think he was cloaked, but it was awful dark in here.'","'You should speak to the king. Something terrible has happened; I have never seen him like this.'","Enter the Haven tavern and talk to the guard in charge","Examine the discarded knife","'I've never seen anything like it, ${PLAYER}. I've heard tales of fell spirits and shades controlling the bodies of their victims, but that's not what is happening here. I think Parthadan knew what he was doing, but once it was done he couldn't come to terms with it in his head. I think it broke him.\
\
'I will bring him to the dungeons, but I do not expect he will be there long. Go to King Elessar and tell him what we found.'","Duinhir may have last seen his knife at the parapet on the north side of the Fifth Circle, but he does not really remember.","'The body is right over there. I haven't moved him yet, but I don't want to leave him there for too long.'","Talk to tavern-worker","King Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.","Talk to Hasong in the throne room","Examine the second victim","'No one has remembered anything especially useful, ${PLAYER}. Whether there really was a cloaked or hooded figure here or not, it seems to me everyone has created one in their memory: a member of the Withered Tree brandishing a knife, slipping away before anyone thought to look at him.'","'That word, \\qdhûrto\\q... it is the word Hasong uses for \\qbetrayal.\\q But the Haradrim emissaries are not the only ones who stand betrayed. This treachery is a betrayal of Gondor, and of me, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I want the murderer found. We cannot let this crime against Gondor stand unpunished. Search the tavern where Mauthoi was killed for any trace of the murderer. It is the Haven, and it is on the south-east side of the Third Circle of the city.'","Examine Mauthoi's body","Parthadan is a broken man","You examine the knife, and note a distinctive black circle on the hilt","'I hope I have not done wrong by cleaning up some of the blood! I was only trying to help.'","'It was Parthadan, the Warden of the Green, who offered to return Duinhir's knife. I saw him only a moment ago, outside the Dome of the Sun on the north-east side of the Sixth Circle.'","The tavern-worker has scrubbed blood-stains near the door, but does the trail continue out of the tavern?","You tell Dúnor of the second murdered man and hand him the knife. He studies it with dawning realization.\
\
'${PLAYER}... I know this knife. It is finely decorated, and gilt front and rear. This is the weapon of a lord, not of a common man. Do you see the black circle here on the hilt? That is a symbol of the Blackroot Vale, or I am a Mûmak. This is the personal dagger of Lord Duinhir. I would know it anywhere. The Lord of the Blackroot Vale murdered the Haradrim emissary. But why would he do this?'\
\
You think of the fate that befell his sons, Duilin and Derufin, and wonder.\
\
'He would not have done it himself, ${PLAYER}. He must have paid yonder victim to do the deed, and once it was done he silenced the murderer and made his escape. I will take some of my best men and apprehend him. You bring word to King Elessar that the culprit has been found.'","Mauthoi's body is on eastern side of the Haven tavern.","A cursory examination is enough to reveal the cause of Mauthoi's death. He was stabbed in the back by a short, bladed weapon, probably a knife or a dagger. It seems that his killer then carefully lowered him to the floor so as not to attract too much attention.\
\
The murderer must have taken the weapon with him, because there is no sign of it.","'It is time you returned to King Elessar in Minas Tirith, ${PLAYER}. Tell him how the conquest of Mordor progresses.'","Several of the people in the Haven might have seen something when Mauthoi was murdered.","Talk to King Elessar in his throne room","Parthadan stares at you with haunted eyes. You have seen many unsettling things in your adventures, but this is among the worst.","'Ho there, ${PLAYER}! I have heard of your many deeds, and it is a pleasure to meet you at last! You are a friend of Lord Duinhir of the Blackroot Vale, are you not? Did his knife ever come back to him?'\
\
You boggle at the man, your mouth agape.\
\
'Did I say something odd? He comes here to this spot to clean and sharpen his knife, but it has been a few days since last I saw him. He left his knife behind, an accident of his recent grief, I expect. I would have brought it to him, but before I had properly decided, another volunteered for the task.'\
\
You ask the man who it was who volunteered to return Duinhir's knife.\
\
'Why, it was Parthadan, the Warden of the Green. I saw him only a moment ago, outside the Dome of the Sun on the north-east side of the Sixth Circle.'","This is the location Duinhir described to you"},
[3182]={"Ha llegado el momento de que los enanos se enfrenten a los orcos de Moria, pero Bósi y Brogur han perdido la esperanza de que puedan lograr la victoria bajo las montañas.","Has defendido el Camino Profundo de los ataques","'¡Me has dejado sin palabras, ${PLAYER}! ¡Con tu ayuda, vivimos para luchar otro día!\
\
'Pero, ¿y si los orcos regresan, como seguramente lo harán? No podemos enfrentarnos a ellos para siempre; ¡son simplemente demasiado numerosos!'","Capítulo 5: Tambores en las profundidades","Stóthkell se encuentra en la Vía de los Herreros.\
\
Ahora que el Camino Profundo ha sido asegurado, deberías ofrecer tu ayuda a Stóthkell.","Has defendido la Vía de los Herreros de los ataques","Habla con Stóthkell y defiende la Vía de los Herreros","Habla con Bósi en la Cámara de la Encrucijada","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en el extremo sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has ayudado a repeler los ataques iniciales de los orcos en las barricadas de los enanos, y deberías informar de tu éxito a Bósi.","Habla con Brogur y defiende el Camino Profundo","'Debes hablar con los siguientes enanos una vez que hayas reunido a tus aliados.\
\
'La defensa de la Vía de los Herreros está en manos de Stóthkell. Habla muy bien de ti y hará lo que le ordenes.\
\
'Brogur debe luchar por la protección del Camino Profundo. Dile que cuento con su fuerza, y él se mantendrá firme todo el tiempo que sea necesario para luchar contra las hordas de orcos.\
\
'Wíli supervisará las barricadas en la Sala Vigesimoprimera; luchó valientemente como parte de la fuerza de distracción durante el asalto de mi hijo a Stazgnâkh.'","Brogur se encuentra en el Camino Profundo.\
\
La supervivencia de los enanos de Moria ahora depende de la capacidad de ti y tus aliados para defender estos lugares de los ataques. Se te pidió que hablaras con Brogur primero.","Has defendido la Sala Vigesimoprimera de los ataques","Wíli se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Con el Camino Profundo y la Vía de los Herreros asegurados, deberías dirigirte a la Sala Vigesimoprimera y ayudar a Wíli a defenderla.","'Ahora depende de ti y de tus amigos. Debes reunir a mi pueblo y coordinar la defensa de Moria. Nos hemos preparado para la guerra en tres lugares clave: el Camino Profundo, la Vía de los Herreros y la Sala Vigesimoprimera; si estos lugares caen, estamos perdidos.\
\
'Brogur debe luchar por la protección del Camino Profundo. Dile que cuento con su fuerza, y él se mantendrá firme todo el tiempo que sea necesario para luchar contra las hordas de orcos. Habla con él primero.\
\
'La defensa de la Vía de los Herreros está en manos de Stóthkell. Habla muy bien de ti y hará lo que le ordenes. Deberías hablar con él una vez que el Camino Profundo esté asegurado.\
\
'Wíli supervisará las barricadas en la Sala Vigesimoprimera; luchó valientemente como parte de la fuerza de distracción durante el asalto de mi hijo a Stazgnâkh, y... lo siento. Wíli lo hará bien. Este será el último y más vital bastión que debes defender. Nuestra supervivencia está en tus manos.'","Habla con Wíli y defiende la Sala Vigesimoprimera"},
[3183]={"Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.","Bósi is in the Hall under the Mountain. Khazad-dûm, and much of the Iron Garrison, is lost.","'I cannot believe we failed, ${PLAYER}. I thought the Iron Garrison would prove successful, in the end.'","Chapter 5: Flight from Khazad-dûm","'You should return to King Thorin, ${PLAYER}. It seems there is trouble brewing, and he will want your help with it!'","'Messengers have come from the Iron Garrison, ${PLAYER}! There is trouble afoot in Khazad-dûm, and the king is sending me with a group of warriors to come to their aid! Quickly, speak with King Thorin and see if he wishes for you to come with us!'","'I am glad you returned when you did, ${PLAYER}, for I have received worrisome news from the Iron Garrison! A tremendous upheaval in the depths has shaken Khazad-dûm to its foundations, and the Expedition's foothold is slipping in the face of constant attack by terrible foes.\
\
'I fear Khazad-dûm will be lost if we do not reinforce them. I have sent for many fine warriors to go to their aid, and I desire for you to go as well! I have not forgotten the mithril that Bósi sent to me. If we lose Khazad-dûm, our best source of mithril will be gone!\
\
'Talk to Foldgráf and he will arrange for your transport!'","'You should return to King Thorin as soon as you can!'","'The Iron Garrison needs our help. I only hope it is not already too late!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Bósi in the Hall under the Mountain","'Quickly now, speak with King Thorin!'","Talk to Foldgráf in the Hall under the Mountain and go with him to Khazad-dûm","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Durin's Folk and fight on their behalf in Mordor.","'I do not know what happened, ${PLAYER}. I thought we had well-fortified our defences, and repelled enough foes to prove that the Iron Garrison could not be moved... and yet still it was not enough! I have never seen so many Orcs, and other foes even more terrible.\
\
'Cousin Brogur will remain within Khazad-dûm, there to lie until dwarves once again open the doors and claim what is ours. One year hence? A hundred? Who can say how long it will be, my friend? May it bring him happiness, whenever that may be. He is with Zigilburk now.\
\
'I have torn my beard enough for the failure of the Iron Garrison. I will do as my king commands.'","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain","'Sauron may be no more, but I see his hand in the turmoil that shook Khazad-dûm. What else could it be? The Iron Garrison had established more than a mere foothold, but still it was swept away like a clay castle on a river-bank! I smell sorcery and evil intentions!\
\
'I want Khazad-dûm retaken! There is mithril to be mined, and Durin's Folk have the right to mine it! I cannot ask Bósi to lead another expedition there, even if he would go willingly. The death of his cousin, and so many of his fellows, will weigh heavily upon him. I do not like this, ${PLAYER}. Will my people blame me for this failure, even as they call me \\qStonehelm\\q and whisper behind their hands?\
\
'I need time to think. I will call for you when I have decided what is to be done. Durin himself would have trouble with these struggles, ${PLAYER}!'","Foldgráf is assembling a group to come to the aid of the Iron Garrison, in Khazad-dûm."},
[3184]={"'I do not know why Halbarad is so intent on helping these dwarves, ${PLAYER}. I cannot begrudge it of him, even if it seems needless, given our haste. You should follow the tracks at the site of the attack to the east.'","'Hail to you, ${RACE}! You are in pursuit of the uruks? Your trail ends here, I am afraid: the ruins of Minas Elendúr that you see atop the cliffs here are crawling with the creatures, and with worse besides!\
\
'Still you intend to scour the ruins? You are brave, my friend! If I cannot dissuade you, I at least will tell you what I have learned of the place. I will not myself journey there again, not for any sum! There are strange doings going on inside Minas Elendúr and its cursed cellars, and I have seen enough to last me!","Find the site of the attack on Fúsi and Fúni Gem-cutter","'The rest of the Dúnedain have gone on ahead. They wait now for us!\
\
'We will meet up with the Company for the next leg of our journey further south of here, at Echad Eregion. May the wind at your back speed you onward! Erebrandir and I will see how stands up the work of Londan.\
\
'Until we meet again at Echad Eregion, ${PLAYER}.'","'Ride forth to Echad Eregion, ${PLAYER}, and we will all meet up again for the next leg of the journey.'","The tracks at the fallen pack lead east. It is in that direction that Fúni Gem-cutter must have been taken.\
\
You have learned in what direction the Ninkoth uruks have taken Fúni Gem-cutter and should follow the tracks.","A confusion of tracks surround the fallen pack and lead off to the east","Fúsi Gem-cutter's father Fúni was attacked somewhere east of Echad Eregion.\
\
Fúsi has asked you to find the site of the attack and determine where his father has been taken by the Ninkoth uruk.","'Dwarves cannot travel through this land free of danger? It is an outrage!'","Chapter 5: Forces at Work in Eregion","Talk to Radanir at Echad Eregion","'I cannot believe those uruks thought to trouble us!'","Find information about the Ninkoth uruks east of the fallen pack","'We have called a halt, ${PLAYER}, and it may be for longer than we originally intended. We have received a call for aid from a dwarf coming north from the White Mountains, and Halbarad has determined it to be serious enough to justify a stop.\
\
'The dwarf's name is Fúsi -- Fúsi Gem-cutter -- and he will speak to you about his problem. He will speak to anyone, it seems!'","The ride of the Grey Company continues, with the Dúnedain travelling further south into Eregion.","'If you can find this Ninkoth uruk, you may be able to find my father! We were attacked somewhere to the east of here!'","'Yes, who are you? You are no Ranger, I can see that. It is an outrage, I tell you, when dwarves cannot take the road north from the White Mountains without fear of harassment!\
\
'There we were, my father and I, when out from behind one of the large stones you see scattered everywhere in these lands jumps the largest uruk you've ever seen. He beat his chest with a gloved hand, shouted the name of his clan -- I'll never forget it -- then knocked out my father Fúni and dragged him off!'\
\
You ask him in what direction the Sharkúnakh uruk took his father, and his brow furrows with puzzlement.\
\
'Sharkúnakh? No, no. The name he shouted was Ninkoth. In all the confusion I can't remember what direction he went, but if you can find the site of the attack, which was to the east of here, you may see some tracks or something.'","'You found tracks leading east from the site of the attack? Why have you not yet followed them, ${PLAYER}? It is the least you can do, is it not? I say that it is! I do indeed!'","'Fúsi Gem-cutter is here at Echad Eregion, and his problem is serious enough that Halbarad has extended our halt here. Talk to Fúsi and see what he needs.'","Talk to Fúsi Gem-cutter at Echad Eregion","The next leg of the journey will take the Grey Company to Echad Eregion, and it is there that they will meet up with you again.","Fúsi Gem-cutter is at Echad Eregion.\
\
Radanir has asked you to speak with Fúsi Gem-cutter about his serious problem, a problem which has brought the Grey Company to a halt.","'Halbarad wants us to help this dwarf Fúsi. I do not know why he thinks it so important.'"},
[3185]={"'Mi sobrino me ha hablado de esta loca búsqueda, ${PLAYER}. ¿Cómo podemos estar seguros de que Nâr-khelab, este Corazón de Fuego, existió alguna vez? Seguramente habríamos oído hablar de una forja así. Y Zigilburk: ¿un hacha hecha completamente de mithril? Ridículo. Esto seguramente habría sido mencionado en muchas de nuestras historias antes de ahora, ya que todos los enanos cantarían sus alabanzas hasta el fin de los tiempos.\
\
'Tendrías más suerte atrapando una cabra salvaje del Cuerno Rojo que encontrando esta ridícula forja. Este \\qsecreto\\q para abrir la puerta que has recuperado no es más que las divagaciones de un enano loco.'","Lleva las páginas podridas a Brogur","Brogur está en la Cámara de Mando, subiendo las escaleras del este dentro de la Cámara de la Encrucijada.\
\
Bori te ha pedido que consultes con su tío Brogur sobre el Corazón de Fuego.","Capítulo 5: Medio Enigma","'Entonces, ¿dónde están estas páginas?'","Has descubierto el secreto para abrir la puerta de Nâr-khelab, la forja donde se fabricó Zigilburk, pero aún no sabes la ubicación de la puerta.","'Mi tío Brogur podría ayudarnos a encontrar el Corazón de Fuego. ¿De qué sirve la llave si no puedes encontrar la puerta?'","'Ahora tenemos el secreto para abrir las puertas del Corazón de Fuego, pero no la ubicación de las puertas en sí. Esto es un giro frustrante.\
\
'Habla con mi tío Brogur sobre esto, si quieres. Está ocupado, como siempre, organizando nuestros esfuerzos aquí dentro de Moria, pero puede que tenga alguna idea que se nos haya escapado.\
\
'Brogur es sabio y tiene un gran conocimiento en esa vieja cabeza suya. Estaría muy feliz de que él también pensara en esta aventura, porque su aporte seguro que será valioso.'"},
[3186]={"Has ayudado a Bori con su tarea","Ramas gruesas recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bósi se encuentra al oeste de las escaleras que conducen al lago fétido, que se extiende frente a la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Bósi está deseando hablar contigo ahora que se han reunido suficientes materiales para fabricar nuevos picos.","Capítulo 5: Manejar la situación","Las ramas gruesas se pueden encontrar en la base de los árboles en el área alrededor de la Puerta de Acebeda. Es probable que Bori esté hablando con su amigo Bróin en las escaleras al este de Bósi.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que recolectes ramas gruesas con las que fabricar mangos de picos resistentes y que ayudes a su hijo Bori con la tarea de reunir piedras para afilar.","'No teníamos forma de saber que la puerta estaría en este estado, ${PLAYER}, y no pensamos en traer picos extra con nosotros. Sin embargo, esta área tiene muchos árboles robustos que deberían proporcionar ramas fuertes, perfectas para los mangos de los picos. Nosotros mismos afilaremos las cabezas de metal y las uniremos a los nuevos mangos.\
\
'Envié a mi hijo Bori a recoger piedras sobre las cuales podríamos afilar nuestros picos, pero aún no me ha traído ninguna. Recolecta ramas de los árboles y ayuda a mi hijo a reunir suficientes piedras para afilar, y vuelve a verme cuando hayas hecho ambas cosas. Bori probablemente esté perdiendo el tiempo con su amigo Bróin en las escaleras al este de aquí. ¡Esos dos se preocupan más por contar historias que por trabajar!'","'Te doy las gracias una vez más, ${PLAYER}. Todos los materiales han sido reunidos y mis enanos comenzarán a fabricar nuevos picos de inmediato.'","Ayuda a Bori con la tarea que le dio Bósi","'Es muy importante que tengamos las ramas necesarias para reparar los picos. ¿Cómo si no podríamos despejar los escombros que bloquean las Puertas de Durin?'","Bósi te ha encargado la tarea de reunir los materiales necesarios para fabricar nuevos picos, para reemplazar las que han sido rotos por los enanos que trabajan en la Puerta de Acebeda.","Lleva ramas gruesas a Bósi","'Todavía queda mucho trabajo por hacer.'","Recolectar ramas gruesas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Llevaremos esos picos a los trabajadores de inmediato.'","'Aún no me has traído suficientes ramas gruesas, ${PLAYER}. Búscalas al pie de los árboles alrededor de esta zona.'"},
[3187]={"'Nuestras defensas estarán listas para cuando los orcos nos ataquen, pero me sentiría mucho más seguro si tuviéramos más barricadas. Está claro que Stóthkell y los artesanos del Corazón de Fuego tienen las manos llenas haciendo suficientes para su propia defensa; no podemos sobrecargarlos más.\
\
'No, necesitaremos reunir barras de hierro y listones de madera para la construcción de nuestras propias barricadas. Busca estos objetos en las Profundidades Llameantes, ¡y acosa a los orcos de los Ghâsh-hai mientras lo haces!'","Barras de hierro y listones de madera se pueden encontrar por las Profundidades Llameantes de Moria, donde los orcos de los Ghâsh-haï se preparan para la guerra.\
\
Brogur quiere que recolectes materiales que puedan usarse para hacer barricadas para defender la Sala Vigesimoprimera.","Has derrotado a los orcos de los Ghâsh-haï en las Profundidades Llameantes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge listones de madera (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva materiales para barricadas a Brogur","Brogur quiere que acoses a los orcos en las Profundidades Llameantes mientras reúnes materiales para construir barricadas para la defensa de la Sala Vigesimoprimera.","'Los orcos de los Ghâsh-haï se preparan para la guerra en las Profundidades Llameantes de Moria. Derrota a estas criaturas viles y recoge barras de hierro y listones de madera de sus campamentos para que podamos construir barricadas efectivas.'","Has recogido listones de madera (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Estos materiales son justo lo que necesitamos, ${PLAYER}, pero me alegra aún más el daño que has hecho a las filas de los Ghâsh-haï.'","Capítulo 5: En el fuego","Has recogido barras de hierro (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Acosar a los orcos de los Ghâsh-haï en las Profundidades Llameantes, al sur de Anazârmekhem.\
\
Brogur quiere que acoses a los orcos después de recoger los materiales que pueden usarse para hacer barricadas para defender la Sala Vigesimoprimera.","Brogur se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has encontrado materiales para ayudar a construir barricadas efectivas y has hecho un gran número de víctimas entre los Ghâsh-haï.","Derrota a los orcos de los Ghâsh-haï en las Profundidades Llameantes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge barras de hierro (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'No has encontrado suficientes materiales de construcción para nuestras barricadas.'"},
[3188]={"'¡Perfecto! Estas piedras son justo lo que mi padre quería que recogiera, y seguramente afilarán nuestros picos a un punto fino.\
\
Bróin y yo no podemos esperar para entrar en la Moria propiamente dicha; ¡ahí es donde nos espera la verdadera gloria! No quiero menospreciar el trabajo que todos están haciendo aquí afuera, pero la verdadera aventura nos espera en las profundidades. Peligros sin medida, no lo dudo, pero tesoros en igual cantidad, y honor, y renombre.\
\
Gracias por tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}.'","'Busca piedras a lo largo del lecho seco del Sirannon, pero ten en cuenta que no todas las piedras serán lo suficientemente afiladas para el propósito de mi padre.'","Lleva piedras de Eregion afiladas a Bori","Bori se encuentra en la base de las escaleras que conducen al lago fétido frente a la Puerta de Acebeda. Se pueden encontrar piedras a lo largo del lecho seco del Sirannon, pero no todas las piedras son lo suficientemente afiladas.\
\
Bori está esperando que le traigas suficientes piedras para afilar los picos necesarios para los trabajadores que están desenterrando la Puerta de Acebeda.","Recoge piedras de Eregion lo suficientemente afiladas para Bori (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Has recogido piedras de Eregion afiladas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Capítulo 5: Mantenerse afilado","Recoge piedras de Eregion afiladas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡La verdadera gloria nos espera detrás de los muros de Moria!'","'Me habría encargado de recoger esas piedras yo mismo, pero me distraje.'","Bori fue encargado de reunir piedras adecuadas para afilar los picos de los trabajadores de la Puerta de Acebeda.","Se pueden encontrar piedras a lo largo del lecho seco del Sirannon, pero no todas las piedras son lo suficientemente afiladas.\
\
Bori está esperando que le traigas suficientes piedras para afilar los picos necesarios para los trabajadores que están desenterrando la Puerta de Acebeda.","'Hola, ${PLAYER}. ¿Mi padre te ha enviado para supervisar la tarea que me ha dado? Para decirte la verdad, no me ha ido muy bien.\
\
'Se suponía que debía encontrar piedras adecuadas para afilar los picos de los trabajadores de la Puerta de Acebeda, y encontré dos de ellas, pero luego me distraje un poco. Mi amigo Bróin y yo hemos estado discutiendo sobre los tesoros que podríamos encontrar dentro de Moria, y perdí la noción del tiempo.\
\
'Te daré estas dos piedras que ya encontré, si quieres. Encuentra el resto por mí y no lo olvidaré. Tuve algo de suerte buscando a lo largo del lecho seco del Sirannon, pero no todas las piedras allí son lo suficientemente afiladas.'"},
[3189]={"Daervunn is in Esteldín, the hidden Ranger-camp in the North Downs.\
\
Halbarad has sent you back to tell Daervunn to gather as many Rangers for the Grey Company as can be spared without jeopardizing the safety of the people of the North Downs.","Talk to Daervunn at Esteldín","Halbarad can be found near the entrance to Tham Úmdúr, in the North Downs.\
\
You have destroyed three of the idols prized by the Angmarim and should return now to Halbarad, as he asked.","Now that Halros has made his decision, it is time to gather more of the Dúnedain to join the ranks of the Grey Company on its mission.","Talk to Halbarad at Tham Úmdúr","'I know that Halbarad will wish to travel with the Grey Company, but he is often away from Esteldín. Speak with Daervunn there, his second-in-command, to learn the current location of Halbarad.'","Destroyed statue of Amarthiel","'You will find Daervunn still in Esteldín, I expect. Tell him to gather as many Rangers as can be spared without jeopardizing the safety of the people of the North Downs.\
\
'I will return shortly.'","'Halbarad went to Tham Úmdúr, a cave located in the shadow of Ost Crithlanc, far to the east of Esteldín, in Nan Amlug East, where foes fleeing Carn Dûm following the defeat of the False King hope to lay the foundations for a new Angmar. You should go to him at once, for the gathering of the Grey Company is of great importance, and he will wish to be a part of it!'","'You bring worrisome tidings, ${PLAYER}! What danger has Aragorn encountered in the distant south that makes the Dúnedain his closest allies? Perhaps I misspeak. Perhaps it is not that the Dúnedain are closest, but instead that they be the most true.\
\
'Halbarad must hear what you have to say, but he left this morning to deal with a serious danger. Word came down to us that a number of foes fleeing from Angmar in the days following the defeat of the False King sought to establish a settlement in a cave in the North Downs.\
\
'Halbarad travelled to this cave, now called Tham Úmdúr, to attempt to forestall or defeat these foes before they can use the relics they plundered from Carn Dûm to make the foundations of a new Angmar. Find Halbarad at Tham Úmdúr, in the shadow of Ost Crithlanc, far to the east of Esteldín, in Nan Amlug East, and give him your message. Help him end their plans before they begin.'","Destroy statue of Amarthiel","The Ranger Daervunn can be found in Esteldín, the hidden Ranger encampment in the North Downs.\
\
Halros has told you to next bring your message to Halbarad, but since the Ranger is often away seeing to the elimination of threats, you should speak first to his second-in-command, the Ranger Daervunn.","'My mind is made up, ${PLAYER}, and now it is time for you to continue with the task Lord Elrond of Rivendell has set before you: to gather more Dúnedain to swell the ranks of the Grey Company as it travels south to the aid of Aragorn.\
\
'Your next journey should take you to Esteldín, the hidden encampment of the Rangers in the North Downs. Halbarad will surely wish to travel south with the Grey Company, but he is often away from Esteldín; speak with the Ranger Daervunn instead, and he will tell you where Halbarad may be found.\
\
'Daervunn is often in the centre of Esteldín, seeing to the general defence of the people who live in the North Downs.'","Destroy statue of Mordirith","Halbarad is in Tham Úmdúr, in the shadow of Ost Crithlanc, far to the east of Esteldín, in Nan Amlug East.\
\
Daervunn told you that Halbarad has gone to investigate a cave where foes fleeing from Carn Dûm following the defeat of the False King hope to create a new Angmar. If you are to enlist Halbarad's help as part of the Grey Company, you will need to travel to Tham Úmdúr.","Three stone idols of great significance to the Angmarim can be found throughout Tham Úmdúr.\
\
Halbarad has already destroyed three of the idols, but three remain, and he wants you to deal with them.","'I will do as Halbarad wishes. I too do not wish to endanger the people of the North Downs by our absence.\
\
'I will speak with the rest of my kin here at Esteldín. Other lands wait for your message.'","Destroy statue of the Witch-king","Destroyed statue of the Witch-king","'I have already destroyed three of the idols the Angmarim brought out of Carn Dûm, but there are more of them. I leave these to you as I rest from my efforts. Return to me when they have been destroyed.'","Destroyed statue of Mordirith","'You have completed what I started, ${PLAYER}, and I am grateful for that! You have my thanks, too, for bringing me word of Aragorn's need for the Dúnedain. We will ride to him with all the haste that can be mustered, through whatever perils await.\
\
'Return now to Daervunn, in Esteldín, with this command: he is to select as many of the Rangers of that camp as he feels can be spared without jeopardizing the safety of the people of the North Downs. We ride to Aragorn, but I will not allow us to dismiss our responsibilities in Eriador.'","'For long years have the Dúnedain wandered in the wilderness, ${PLAYER}. Your message confirms what I have long suspected: the hour is near at hand when my people must come forth. I will ride to the aid of my friend and chieftain, Aragorn son of Arathorn, and let no Man or beast stand in the path of the Grey Company!\
\
'There is evil still here, ${PLAYER}, and if we Dúnedain leave Eriador to fend for itself, what then? We win little if, when all the deeds of the Age are done, the northern lands are lost to evil, their peoples destroyed.\
\
'Daervunn told you why I have come to this place? Already I have destroyed three idols the Angmarim brought out of Carn Dûm, but I believe three remain. Destroy these statues of their most-prized leadership and the Angmarim here may abandon hope of raising Angmar into prominence again. Return to me when you have done so, and we can speak again.'","Chapter 5: Loose Ends in the North Downs"},
[3190]={"'Los Pûlpum Globsnaga pueden seguir teniendo sus órdenes, ${PLAYER}. Arráncaselas y tráemelas, si puedes. Debemos saber por qué Mazog ha hecho este movimiento.\
\
'Encontrarás a los Pûlpum especialmente en las cercanías del gran lago subterráneo.'","Los Pûlpum atrapados por la corrupción de los Globsnaga se pueden encontrar por todas las Fundaciones de Piedra, pero especialmente en las cercanías del lago subterráneo en sus profundidades.\
\
Dithaliwenn quiere saber para qué ha enviado Mazog a tantos de sus Orcos a las Fundaciones de Piedra, ya que parece un movimiento poco característico. Quiere que derrotes a los Pûlpum Globsnaga y les arrebates cualquier orden que puedan seguir teniendo.","Dithaliwenn se encuentra en el campamento de Gwathrendath, el Refugio Sombrío en las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Has recogido órdenes de los Pûlpum Globsnaga corrompidos y deberías llevarlas a Dithaliwenn en Gwathrendath.","'Los enanos que buscan recuperar Moria, por tontos que sean, no merecen el destino que les han reservado los ejércitos de Mazog. Pero ¿por qué ha enviado Mazog a todo un regimiento de orcos a las Fundaciones de Piedra, cuando podría usarlos para atacar las defensas de los enanos?\
\
'Hay un propósito oscuro detrás de todo esto, ${PLAYER}, y creo que está relacionado con Gorothúl, el hechicero de Dol Guldur. Mazog no habría hecho esto por sí mismo; ¿qué otra razón podría tener para dividir sus fuerzas?\
\
'Busca a los Pûlpum enviados por Mazog a las Fundaciones de Piedra. Aunque ahora sean Globsnaga, corrompidos por el mal que infesta el lugar, es posible que aún tengan las órdenes que recibieron. ¡Tráemelas si existen! Encontrarás a los Pûlpum especialmente en las galerías cerca del gran lago subterráneo y en las pocas rocas que sobresalen de su superficie.'","Dithaliwenn quiere saber por qué Mazog ha enviado a sus Orcos a las cavernas de las Fundaciones de Piedra.","Lleva las órdenes de los Pûlpum a Dithaliwenn","Capítulo 5: Los Buscadores de Mazog","'No me has traído las órdenes que busco, ${PLAYER}.'","Recoge las órdenes de los Pûlpum Globsnaga (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Órdenes de Pûlpum recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Es difícil aprender mucho de estas órdenes, pero esto puedo discernir: Mazog busca esclavizar a algunos de los horrores sin nombre que habitan bajo Moria. Pero por qué desea hacer esto sigue siendo desconocido para mí, ya que no necesita aliados sin nombre para aplastar a los enanos; ya están cerca de la destrucción tal como están.\
\
'No, debe tener algún otro objetivo. Me temo que podría ser el Bosque de Oro, hogar de mi Señor Celeborn y la Dama Galadriel. Mazog no tiene la visión para un plan así. Esto debe venir de Gorothúl de Dol Guldur.\
\
'Gracias, ${PLAYER}. Hemos aprendido mucho de tus esfuerzos que nos será útil a nosotros y a los enanos también.'"},
[3191]={"The Brehur and Brehures can be found in the Brenin's Hall in Lhanuch.\
\
Glynn Brenin has asked you to speak with his advisors about the words of Anirin the messenger and about the events of his rescue.","'I spoke against the promises of Saruman for many days! That was the course of wisdom. How few of the clans listened to my advice? Too few.\
\
'But Anirin brings us hope from Dunland. He will return to Tûr Morva with word that Lhanuch also stands against Saruman; let that strengthen our cousins' resolve!'","'Are all duvodiad so trusting? How do you know this man Ergothorn is a friend? You know nothing about him beyond what he wishes to tell you, and that not even in person!\
\
'I say \\qhe,\\q but you know not even that! Ergothorn could be a woman, and that could be the least of her deceptions!\
\
'It matters not to me that the messenger Anirin was found where Ergothorn said he would be. One truth is nothing.'","'I am pleased by Anirin's message from Lheu Brenin. If Tûr Morva still stands against the Wizard, we must remain strong in our resolve as well!\
\
'It is good to know that some of our brothers in Dunland have not believed the promises of Saruman. We are not without friends, as was my worry.'","Halbarad is among the huts on the western side of Lhanuch.\
\
You have spoken with the Brehur and Brehures of Lhanuch and should return to Halbarad with their words as Glynn Brenin wished.","Chapter 5: News from Dunland","'Your people, these Rangers, are duvodiad, but unlike others I have seen. This man Halbarad reminds me of Glynn Brenin: stern, willing to listen to the advice of others, but given to decisive action when it is necessary.\
\
'Know that the road through Dunland will not be safe for you. It is good that Lheu Brenin still stands against the Wizard Saruman, but there are other clans in Dunland that do not have leaders as strong, and for them, the promises of the Wizard may be hard to refuse. Tell your people to be wary on the road south.'","Talk to Nona in Lhanuch","Nona is in the north-eastern corner of the Dunlending village of Lhanuch.\
\
Halbarad has remembered that you did not bring his refusal to Nona and wants you to tell her that he cannot allow her to travel with the Grey Company when they depart.","'My Brehur and Brehures have heard the messenger Anirin's words. They will decide what must be done in this matter of Saruman.\
\
'Speak with them and hear what they have to say. They will wish to know the events that led you to find this stray messenger, as well, so leave nothing out. They will decide, too, what course of action to recommend to your people.\
\
'Once you have heard my Brehur and Brehures, bring their advice to your leader Halbarad. He and I have spoken already on this, and their council will complete the argument.'","'There is glory in standing strong to the end, ${PLAYER}, though that end be a sad one. We will stand with our brothers in the south against the threats of the Wizard Saruman.'","'I trust no man I cannot see. If Ergothorn will not meet you duvodiad face to face, you should not listen to his words. Tear them up, unread, and you will be the happier for it.'","'I have spoken with your leader Halbarad about these matters. Once you have heard the wisdom of my Brehur and Brehures, bring their words to him.'","Talk to Halbarad in Lhanuch","'The Wizard Saruman will never command the Uch-lûth! We will stand against him, no matter the cost!'","'I understand the concerns of the Brehur and Brehures, ${PLAYER}; they are fair points. When we depart for Dunland, we cannot let our caution wane for even an instant.\
\
'The business with Ergothorn's letter drove from my mind the request of the Dunlending girl. Go now to Nona and tell her that I cannot allow her to travel with the Grey Company. She is here in Lhanuch, and here she will stay.'","The messenger from Dunland has given hope to Glynn Brenin that other Dunlending clans are standing against Saruman.","'The words of my Brehur and Brehures should be heeded. Bring their advice to your leader Halbarad.'","'Anirin's tidings are welcome, but not all of the clans of Dunland will have the strength of will to stand against the wishes of the Wizard. If Saruman seeks to dominate the Dunlending clans and command them in battle, he will not remain opposed by many.'","'Nona will be disappointed, but she must understand that there is no place for her on our journey south. Speak with her here in Lhanuch and tell her this.'","'Your leader Halbarad does not know what he says! Too dangerous? He is a fool if he thinks I cannot stand with the best man in his company!\
\
'A fool, then. We will see who has the greater glory, when the tally of battle is finished. It will be Nona of the Uch-lûth, sister to Wadu Gwiber-slayer!'"},
[3192]={"'Dile a Lenglammel en Gwathrendath que no estoy satisfecho con el requisito de no llevar a Mazog a Lothlórien en el camino hacia el Bosque Negro. En su lugar, tomaremos el camino largo, perdiendo días preciosos en el proceso, únicamente para complacer los requisitos ridículos de los Elfos de Lothlórien. ¡Dile eso y no omitas ninguna de mis palabras!'","Bróin está en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada junto al Camino de Durin.\
\
Has recogido las cadenas que se utilizarán para asegurar a Mazog durante el viaje a la Tierra Media y ahora deberías llevarlas a Bróin.","'Recuerdas dónde está el Corazón de Fuego, ${PLAYER}, ¿verdad? Está junto a la Vía de los Herreros, entre las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata. Habla con Stóthkell y pregúntale si las cadenas para Mazog ya han sido fabricadas.'","Capítulo 5: Cadenas para Mazog","'¿Las cadenas no están listas? ¡Esto está tomando demasiado tiempo!'","'Ah, las cadenas. Sí, parecen muy resistentes. Mazog no podrá romper estas como lo hizo en Rushdurinul, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Hemos tenido un... desacuerdo... con los Elfos de Lothlórien sobre el plan para llevar a Mazog a Dol Guldur a cambio de la libertad de mi primo. Celeborn se ha negado a permitirnos llevar al Orco al Bosque de Oro, aunque claramente es la ruta más directa. En su lugar, quiere que rodeemos el bosque, ¡un viaje que tomaría mucho más tiempo!\
\
'Lenglammel en Gwathrendath espera mi respuesta. Dile eso, a regañadientes: tomaremos el camino largo con Mazog, aunque me desagrada tremendamente. Dile también que confío en que los Elfos asumirán parte de la responsabilidad de esta inconveniencia. ¡El retraso que esto causará es intolerable y se nos pide que lo soportemos! Lo haré, por el bien de Bori.'","'Bróin me contó sobre tu captura de Mazog en Rushdurinul, y me quedó claro que si Mazog debe ser llevado a Dol Guldur a cambio de la libertad de mi hijo, necesitaremos cadenas más poderosas para mantenerlo. Pudiste someter al rey de los orcos cuando se liberó una vez; no podemos arriesgarnos a que sea necesario de nuevo.\
\
'Por lo tanto, ordené a los herreros del Corazón de Fuego que forjaran nuevas cadenas para Mazog. Tenemos poco mithril, pero deberían haber podido hacer bandas muy fuertes mezclando pequeñas cantidades de este con otros metales.\
\
'Habla con Stóthkell en el Corazón de Fuego y ve si las cadenas están listas.'","Habla con Stóthkell en el Corazón de Fuego","Lleva las cadenas de mithril a Bróin, en la Senda Pacífica","Habla con Lenglammel en Gwathrendath","Bósi te ha enviado a recuperar las cadenas de mithril que se están fabricando en el Corazón de Fuego para contener a Mazog.","'Te he dado las cadenas, ${PLAYER}. No sabía que había tiempo que perder; ¿por qué no las has llevado a Bróin a la Senda Pacífica?'","Stóthkell se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego, junto a la Vía de los Herreros, entre las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que vayas al Corazón de Fuego para ver si las cadenas para Mazog han sido fabricadas.","'Lo siento, ${PLAYER}. Las preocupaciones de Bróin son reales y comprensibles, pero llevar a Mazog a Lothlórien es simplemente inaceptable. Incluso encadenado, no se puede permitir que Mazog entre en el Bosque de Oro.\
\
'Hablamos antes sobre las marcas que Gorothúl dejó en ciertos lugares de Moria, ${PLAYER}, y has hecho bien en eliminar algunas de ellas. Magor me informó mientras estabas fuera que al menos una de ellas sigue ahí...'","Lenglammel se encuentra en Gwathrendath, el campamento de los Elfos en las profundidades de las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Bróin te ha enviado a decirle a Lenglammel que los enanos no llevarán a Mazog a través de Lothlórien en su camino hacia el Bosque Negro, sino que rodearán el bosque. También quiere que expreses su descontento con este requisito.","'Sí, ${PLAYER}, sí. Combinamos una pequeña cantidad de mithril con otros metales para hacer estas cadenas. De hecho, algunas de las armas y armaduras que recogiste previamente para mis herreros fueron fundidas y utilizadas en su fabricación.\
\
'Estas cadenas asegurarán a Mazog durante el viaje al Bosque Negro. No podrá liberarse de ellas, o me avergonzaría llamarme Stóthkell de la Guarnición de Hierro.\
\
'Llévalas a Bróin para su aprobación. Está descansando en la Senda Pacífica, preparándose para el viaje.'"},
[3193]={"'La podredumbre que invade las zonas bajas de Buzun-ghâr no es natural, ${PLAYER}, y eso nos da el deber de eliminarla. Si Orvar no escucha nuestro consejo y sella el pasaje, debemos destruir la fuente de la podredumbre marchita antes de que se extienda por Moria y se convierta en una amenaza mayor.\
\
Creo que tengo los medios para hacerlo, ${PLAYER}. Este berilo capturará la luz pura, incluso en su forma más tenue, y la reflejará sobre las paredes corrompidas del pasaje. Si lo colocas sobre una piedra en la zona más profunda de Buzun-ghâr, será como un faro para el mal de la podredumbre, atrayendo lo que sea que se oculta tras la podredumbre marchita, en agonía.\
\
En ese momento debes destruir la fuente de la podredumbre, ¡pero ten cuidado! Debes permanecer cerca del berilo o sus efectos no debilitarán al maestro de la podredumbre, sea lo que sea.'","Nimpheleg cree que es posible acabar con la corrupción de la podredumbre marchita dentro de Buzun-ghâr.","'Debes colocar el berilo que te di sobre una piedra en las zonas más profundas de Buzun-ghâr, pues eso puede atraer al maestro de la podredumbre para que pueda ser derrotado. No te alejes del berilo una vez que lo hayas colocado, porque la piedra debilitará a cualquier criatura que corrompa este lugar.'","'Somos afortunados, ${PLAYER}, de que Grawulun el Caerog, ya debilitado, pudiera ser aún más debilitado por la luz del berilo que usaste para atraerlo. Ya no marcará los jardines de Buzun-ghâr ni se extenderá por Moria.\
\
Me preocupa que más y más fuertes de su especie acechen en las profundidades, pero poco podemos hacer si eso es cierto.\
\
Me alegra haber ayudado a combatir la fuente de esta podredumbre, ${PLAYER}. ¡Que los enanos aprendan la lección!'","Habla con Nimpheleg","Nimpheleg está en Lossathrod, el campamento en las zonas altas de Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Has atraído y derrotado la fuente de la podredumbre dentro de Buzun-ghâr, un espíritu debilitado: Grawulun el Caerog.","'¿No has devuelto el berilo que te di, ${PLAYER}?'","Derrotaste a Grawulun el Caerog","Atrae y derrota la fuente de la podredumbre en Buzun-ghâr","Una piedra para colocar el berilo de Nimpheleg se encuentra en la zona más profunda de Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Nimpheleg cree que puedes atraer y derrotar la fuente de la podredumbre en Buzun-ghâr colocando un berilo sobre una piedra en las profundidades de la cueva. Te advirtió que permanecieras cerca del berilo una vez colocado, pues solo la piedra disminuirá la ferocidad del maestro de la podredumbre.","Capítulo 5: La fuente de la podredumbre"},
[3194]={"'Mazog ha enviado a todo un regimiento de Orcos a las Fundaciones de Piedra. Parece que están buscando algo, pero aún no sabemos qué es.\
\
'Lo que sí está claro es que no están teniendo mucho éxito. No, estos Orcos han sido poseídos por una locura que los consume como una llama y que se manifiesta de forma horrible en su piel.\
\
'Esta corrupción los hace aún más peligrosos, ${PLAYER}, aunque parecen haber perdido la razón. Estos Orcos se llaman Globsnaga ahora. Elimínalos dondequiera que los encuentres en las Fundaciones de Piedra, porque su falta de razón los hace más crueles e implacables que antes.'","Una locura de mente y cuerpo ha afectado a los Orcos del mando de Mazog que han venido a las Fundaciones de Piedra.","'Busca a los Orcos de Mazog por las Fundaciones de Piedra, corrompidos por el mal misterioso que se ha apoderado de estas cuevas. Se llaman Globsnaga ahora, y aunque no tengan mente, deben ser eliminados.'","'Aún no sabemos qué causa la corrupción que ha afectado a los Orcos de Mazog y los ha convertido en los fieros y sin mente Globsnaga, pero por el momento es suficiente saber que su número es menor.\
\
'Gracias, ${PLAYER}.'","Derrota a los Orcos Globsnaga en las Fundaciones de Piedra (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Orcos Globsnaga derrotados en las Fundaciones de Piedra (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Orcos del mando de Mazog, corrompidos por el mal enfermizo, se pueden encontrar por las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Forglinn te ha pedido que derrotes a tantos Orcos corrompidos de Mazog, los Globsnaga, como puedas. Las criaturas parecen no tener mente, pero siguen siendo peligrosas.","Capítulo 5: Tomados por la locura","Forglinn se encuentra en Gwathrendath, el campamento de los Elfos entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Has derrotado a muchos de los Orcos Globsnaga, y deberías volver ahora con Forglinn."},
[3195]={"Brogur se encuentra en el Camino Profundo.\
\
Has repelido el ataque de las hordas de orcos, ve a hablar con Brogur sobre la victoria.","Completa la escaramuza: La batalla del Camino Profundo","Defended el Camino Profundo frente a la embestida de los orcos, es el pasaje que conecta la Gran Excavación con las Obras Hidráulicas.","'¡Lo hemos conseguido, ${PLAYER}! No pensé que saldríamos vivos de esta, pero lo hicimos, contra todo pronóstico.\
\
'¡Los enanos de Moria se mantienen firmes aunque todos sus enemigos de las profundidades estén sobre ellos!'","'Lamento mis palabras de desesperación cuando hablé contigo antes. Reuniré mis fuerzas, por el bien de Bósi y de todo nuestro pueblo.\
\
'¡Defenderemos el Camino Profundo contra todos nuestros enemigos, ${PLAYER}! Reúne a los aliados que puedas, y nos mantendremos firmes contra los orcos todo el tiempo que sea necesario!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión incluye una escaramuza que se puede completar en solitario, en una Comunidad grande o pequeña utilizando el panel Buscador de Instancias. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 55.\
\
Si esta es tu primera escaramuza, debes visitar uno de los campamentos de escaramuza que se encuentran por toda la Tierra Media y hablar con un capitán de escaramuza para entrenar adecuadamente. Los campamentos de escaramuza se pueden encontrar en las siguientes regiones: Ered Luin, las Tierras de Bree, la Comarca, las Tierras Solitarias, las Quebradas del Norte, el Bosque de los Trolls, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria y Lothlórien.</rgb>","Capítulo 5: La batalla del Camino Profundo","'¡Preparemos nuestras defensas!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión incluye una escaramuza que se puede completar en solitario, en una Comunidad grande o pequeña utilizando el panel de Unión de Escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 55.\
\
Si esta es tu primera escaramuza, debes visitar uno de los campamentos de escaramuza que se encuentran por toda la Tierra Media y hablar con un capitán de escaramuza para entrenar adecuadamente. Los campamentos de escaramuza se pueden encontrar en las siguientes regiones: Ered Luin, las Tierras de Bree, la Comarca, las Tierras Solitarias, las Quebradas del Norte, el Bosque de los Trolls, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria y Lothlórien.</rgb>","Brogur se encuentra en el Camino Profundo.\
\
Una vez que hayas reunido a tus aliados, ve a hablar con Brogur. No tardarán en llegar los orcos."},
[3196]={"Capítulo 5: La batalla de la Sala Vigegimoprimera","Wíli se encuentra en la Sala Vigegimoprimera.\
\
Has defendido con éxito la Sala Vigegimoprimera del ataque de los orcos, y ahora debes hablar con Wíli.","La Sala Vigegimoprimera es un centro importante para la presencia de los enanos en Moria, y debe ser defendida a toda costa.","'Les debemos más gratitud de la que se puede expresar con palabras o saludos. La Sala Vigegimoprimera sigue en pie, y mi gente sigue firme para limpiar la inmundicia que infestaba estas salas dormidas.\
\
'¡Qué día ha sido este! ¡De la retirada y el deshonor brota la gloria y el triunfo! ¡Que Mazog se acobarde ante los Enanos de Khazad-dûm!'","Wíli se encuentra en la Sala Vigegimoprimera.\
\
Ha llegado el momento de defender la Sala Vigegimoprimera del ataque de los orcos. Habla con Wíli para organizar la defensa.","'Esto es lo que hay, ${PLAYER}: si perdemos la Sala Vigegimoprimera, perdemos Moria. Los orcos atacarán pronto, y el golpe será duro y rápido. ¡No podemos caer aquí, o no encontraremos nuestro equilibrio de nuevo!\
\
'Si es necesario, retrocederemos de las barricadas avanzadas. ¡Mejor perder algo de terreno que perder buenos enanos!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en solitario, en grupo pequeño o en grupo usando el panel de búsqueda de instancias. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 55.\
\
Si esta es tu primera escaramuza, debes visitar uno de los campamentos de escaramuzas que se encuentran por toda la Tierra Media y hablar con un capitán de escaramuzas para entrenar adecuadamente. Los campamentos de escaramuzas se pueden encontrar en las siguientes regiones: Ered Luin, las Tierras de Bree, la Comarca, las Tierras Solitarias, las Quebradas del Norte, el Bosque de los Trolls, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria y Lothlórien.</rgb>","Completa la escaramuza: La batalla de la Sala Vigegimoprimera","'¡La Sala Vigegimoprimera no debe caer en manos de Mazog!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en solitario, en grupo pequeño o en grupo usando el panel de unión de escaramuzas. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 55.\
\
Si esta es tu primera escaramuza, debes visitar uno de los campamentos de escaramuzas que se encuentran por toda la Tierra Media y hablar con un capitán de escaramuzas para entrenar adecuadamente. Los campamentos de escaramuzas se pueden encontrar en las siguientes regiones: Ered Luin, las Tierras de Bree, la Comarca, las Tierras Solitarias, las Quebradas del Norte, el Bosque de los Trolls, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria y Lothlórien.</rgb>"},
[3197]={"'Debo confesaros que no pensé que los orcos podrían contrarrestar nuestro plan. Es bueno que estuvierais con nosotros cuando las cosas se torcieron, ¡o este sería un día sombrío para los enanos!\
\
'¡En cambio, victoria! El Corazón de Fuego sigue en nuestro poder, ¡y seguimos vivos para usarlo!'","'¡Debemos proteger el Corazón de Fuego!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en solitario, en pequeña o gran comunidad utilizando el buscador de instancias. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 55.\
\
Si esta es tu primera escaramuza, debes visitar uno de los campamentos de escaramuza que se encuentran por toda la Tierra Media y hablar con un capitán de escaramuza para entrenar adecuadamente. Los campamentos de escaramuza se pueden encontrar en las siguientes regiones: Ered Luin, las Tierras de Bree, La Comarca, las Tierras Solitarias, las Quebradas del Norte, el Bosque de los Trolls, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria y Lothlórien.</rgb>","Completa la escaramuza: La batalla de Vía de los Herreros","Stóthkell se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego.\
\
Has defendido el Corazón de Fuego del ataque de las hordas de Orcos, y ahora deberías hablar con Stóthkell.","Stóthkell se encuentra en el Corazón de Fuego.\
\
Deberías hablar con Stóthkell cuando hayas reunido a tus aliados y estés listo para defender la Vía de los Herreros.","'Estamos con vosotros, ${PLAYER}. Nos mantendremos firmes contra los orcos hasta el final, ya sea hacia la ruina o hacia el triunfo, aunque los orcos tengan sed y babeen por nuestra propia sangre...\
\
'...Y entonces cerraremos la puerta si es necesario. Si llega a eso, vuestra presencia fortalecerá nuestra determinación de todos modos.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión implica una escaramuza que se puede completar en solitario, en pequeña o gran de comunidad utilizando el panel de unión de escaramuza. Esta escaramuza tiene un nivel mínimo de 55.\
\
Si esta es tu primera escaramuza, debes visitar uno de los campamentos de escaramuza que se encuentran por toda la Tierra Media y hablar con un capitán de escaramuza para entrenar adecuadamente. Los campamentos de escaramuza se pueden encontrar en las siguientes regiones: Ered Luin, las Tierras de Bree, La Comarca, las Tierras Solitarias, las Quebradas del Norte, el Bosque de los Trolls, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria y Lothlórien.</rgb>","La Vía de los Herreros, en la que se encuentra la entrada secreta del Corazón de Fuego, debe ser defendida contra los Orcos.","Capitulo 5: La batalla de Vía de los Herreros"},
[3198]={"Talk to King Thráin at Muru Azog","Before the gates of Khazad-dûm, crows pick at Azog's remains","King Thráin can be found at Muru Azog.\
\
You have driven back the Orcs at Muru Azog and found the remains of Azog being picked by crows. You should talk to King Thráin.","Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Amdân","Talk to King Thráin and aid in 'A Final Reckoning'","Defeat Ufúrzrak Orcs at Muru Azog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Ufúrzrak thrug-hai at Muru Azog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Investigate the gates of Khazad-dûm","'And so, the pyres burned away and so the ashen dale of Azanulbizar was abandoned. Although none beheld them at the battle's end, we later learned the Elves of the Golden Wood had borne witness to our deeds, spying the smoke from afar as it rose into the sky above the dale. As King Thráin had named them at Durin's Stone, the Marasrân—the Burned Dwarves came to occupy a place of great honour and reverence among Durin's Folk. Long after, among each of the Seven Houses, all a Dwarf needed to say about his ancestor was 'he was Marasrûn' and it would elicit grave nods and murmurs of respect.\
\
'In time, the other Houses departed back to their homes, bearing the burdens of the arms and amour collected from their dead. As for the Iron-folk, we too departed, making the long journey back to Járnfast. Dáin became the Lord of Iron Hills in all but title, for Grór had become lost in his sorrows, surviving his father, brothers, and now his son alike with not one among them whose bones he could honour.\
\
'Last of all, King Thráin and the exiles departed. They were few now and weary, having lost much and won little in the war, but south they went along the Great-way, until at last they returned to Zudrugund.\
\
'The Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs was ended—the cost too great, the prize too small to hold.'","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Amdân.\
\
You have witnessed the end of the Battle of Azanulbizar. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","'Azog is slain, and the Ironfoot has taken his head. The Orcs should know the battle has turned against them!\
\
'And yet, some of Azog's own clan still cling to their meagre holdings outside the Great Gates. It cannot stand!\
\
'Slay these... Ufúrzrak, and drive the rest of his ilk back beyond the gates of Khazad-dûm! Azanulbizar will be ours!'","Nud-mekhem, the east-gate, can be found to the west of Muru Azog.\
\
Hoping to rout the last of the Orcs at Azanulbizar, King Thráin has asked you to investigate the gates of Khazad-dûm and defeat Orcs of the Ufúrzrak clan.","King Thráin can be found at Muru Azog.\
\
After the defeat of Azog, King Thráin appears intent on routing the remaining Orcs at Azanulbizar. You should talk to King Thráin.","Defeated Ufúrzrak Orcs at Muru Azog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Chapter 5: The Bitterest Victory","As you continue to read Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar, you begin the fifth and final chapter in which the Dwarves of the Haban’akkâ of Thráin must reckon with the cost of victory over Azog.","Defeated Ufúrzrak thrug-hai at Muru Azog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Before the pass leading to the gates of Khazad-dûm, the survivors of the confrontation against Azog gathered anew. After the slaying of Azog, they had withdrawn from the encampment, anticipating another assault from the Orcs who still dwelt within Khazad-dûm. With them, they bore away only the head of Azog and the body of Náin Orcsfoe. Indeed, Náin's mail-collar had withstood Azog's blow, but the same could not be said for his neck. It snapped, and by all accounts, Náin had died in an instant.\
\
'Little comfort this was to Dáin, who had remained silent ever since he ventured beyond the Great Gates. Even so, the head of Azog was the prize King Thráin had sought ever since Nár brought word of Thrór's death to the exiles at Zudrugund. And it had been won!\
\
'Left nearly halt after Urro wounded him at Durin's Stone, King Thráin knelt among his guard, but his eyes would not be turned from Khazad-dûm.'"},
[3199]={"'Este es un lugar sombrío y malsano. El aire es pesado y estancado, y apesta a los terrores invisibles que se arrastran en la oscuridad.\
\
'Pero por la Dama Galadriel nos aventuramos en el Foso Oscuro, y haremos lo que se nos ordene hasta que ya no podamos ser de más utilidad aquí.\
\
'Ella te ha enviado a nosotros por una razón, ${CLASS}. La Dama ve muchas cosas en su Espejo; quizás ha visto el destino que nos espera en el abismo. Ayuda a los Elfos de mi compañía, y veremos todo lo que pueda suceder en este lugar.'","Has ayudado a Dithaliwenn con su tarea.","'Mazog no debe ser consciente del gran mal que se esconde bajo Moria, o no jugaría a juegos tan peligrosos. Sus Orcos no son rival para lo que se encuentra en las raíces de estas montañas.\
\
'O quizás Gorothúl, este hechicero de Dol Guldur, le ha susurrado mentiras envenenadas al hijo de Azog. Puede que crea que sus Orcos tienen la ventaja, pero no es así.'","Ayuda a Dithaliwenn con su tarea","Lenglammel se encuentra en el campamento de Gwathrendath, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra bajo Nud-melek.\
\
Has ayudado a los Elfos de su campamento y deberías hablar con ella de nuevo.","Ayuda a Forglinn con su tarea","Capítulo 5: El Foso Oscuro","Forglinn y Dithaliwenn se encuentran en el campamento de Gwathrendath, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra bajo Nud-melek.\
\
Lenglammel piensa que quizás descubrirás lo que el destino te depara si ayudas a los Elfos de su compañía a combatir las criaturas de la oscuridad.","Para salvar a los enanos de Moria, has venido a ayudar a los Elfos de Gwathrendath, enviados a Moria por orden de la Dama Galadriel.","'Ayuda a Forglinn y Dithaliwenn a combatir los maleficios que se arrastran entre las Fundaciones de Piedra, y quizás descubramos lo que el destino nos depara.'","Has ayudado a Forglinn con su tarea."},
[3200]={"'You are returned! In your eyes I read much - much that has taken place.'\
\
You and Glathlírel tell the assembled council all that happened.\
\
'I see. It has ended well enough, and with time we may know whether the scroll Glorfindel sought was worth the peril you faced. Soon he will be with us and our wait will end. I will find the gift he spoke of and see that you are given it to bring to my grand-daughter, Arwen. It is a good gift, and fitting. Moreover, it is right that she receives it from you.\
\
'Farewell for now, ${PLAYER}. We will see each other soon.'","'${PLAYER}, there you are! Celeborn has grasped the ancient text's meaning and knows where Glorfindel has gone. Fly there with great haste!'","You should talk to Glathlírel in the Court of Lothlórien.","You should ask Celeborn in the Court of Lothlórien about the ancient text.","Talk to Lord Celeborn","'Do you see, ${PLAYER}? The nature of the dream that stirred me from my retreat was not an idle one. I have found my way here, as you have, in time of need.\
\
'Though I tremble at the thought of returning to that place, where the Balrog was fought and subdued, I know we must. A fear, nay, a certainty tells me that danger lurks there as it did before. If the Rift were peaceful and empty, why has Glorfindel not returned?\
\
'Even Lady Galadriel cannot know what lies in that depth. We must go, you and I, and learn the truth of it. That much is certain.'","Chapter 5: The Return","Talk to Lady Galadriel","You should talk to Lady Galadriel in the Court of Lothlórien, and tell her all that happened in the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu.","'I am ready to set out for Nûrz Ghâshu, ${PLAYER}. Give the word and we shall go.'","Learn the meaning of the ancient text you found and to where it led Glorfindel.","'${PLAYER}, there you are! Lord Celeborn has grasped the ancient text's meaning and knows where Glorfindel has gone. You should speak with him at once.'","Go with Glathlírel to the Rift","Talk to Glathlírel","'Know, ${CLASS}, that what Glorfindel sought is what Men or dwarves would call a prophecy: words uttered by Gil-galad in an age past, concerning both the dawn and the dusk of our time in Middle-earth. Few were there to hear it and fewer still are there who walk this earth and recall it in its entirety. Perhaps foreseeing this, the words were inscribed onto eleven scrolls and given out to trusted keepers of lore. \
\
'But the text you found in Tham Giliath was not one of those scrolls. No, it was a mere recounting of the texts penned by one scholar and to where they had been sent. Four of the twenty it mentions were of Gil-galad's speech, and I know well that three of those four were lost forever to calamity, folly, and fire.\
\
'The fourth recording of the prophecy found a home among collected texts in what has come to be called the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu. That place is known to you, ${PLAYER}? It is known well indeed to you, Glathlírel.'","Go with Glathlírel and return to the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu in search of Glorfindel."},
[3201]={"Guerreros Globsnaga derrotados en Buzun-ghâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los guerreros Globsnaga en Buzun-ghâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los hostigadores Globsnaga en Buzun-ghâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Capítulo 5: La podredumbre marchita","'Tomará tiempo antes de que las plantas y jardines dentro de Buzun-ghâr puedan ser restaurados, pero tu derrota de Grawulun el Caerog hará posible lo que antes no lo era.\
\
Has hecho bien, ${PLAYER}, y me alegra que hayas ayudado a salvar a los enanos de su propia obstinación por excavar donde no deberían.\
\
Un enano de la Guarnición de Hierro vino a hablar con Orvar mientras estabas en las profundidades. Creo que tenía un mensaje para ti.'","Corunothiel está en Lossathrod, el campamento de Elfos y enanos en la cima de Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Has lidiado con la podredumbre marchita dentro de Buzun-ghâr y ahora deberías hablar con Corunothiel sobre tus éxitos.","Orvar Martillo de Campana está en Lossathrod, el campamento dentro del pasaje de Buzun-ghâr, ubicado fuera del Camino de Durin.\
\
Corunothiel dijo que un mensaje para ti fue entregado a Orvar mientras estabas en las profundidades de Buzun-ghâr, y deberías hablar con el enano para conocer su contenido.","Hostigadores Globsnaga derrotados en Buzun-ghâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Corunothiel y los otros Elfos de Lórien enviados para ayudar a la Guarnición de Hierro están preocupados por la podredumbre corrupta que se extiende en uno de los pasajes recién excavados.","'No sé si los Globsnaga han sido afectados por la podredumbre marchita o si simplemente los ha atraído, pero deben ser destruidos. Búscalos en Buzun-ghâr y elimina a las criaturas antes de que se acerquen demasiado a este campamento, o peor aún, que encuentren su camino hacia otros hogares de la Guarnición de Hierro.\
\
Asegúrate también de hablar con Nimpheleg; sé que tiene algunas ideas sobre cómo atraer la fuente de la podredumbre y destruirla.'","Nimpheleg está en Lossathrod, el campamento dentro de Buzun-ghâr, ubicado fuera del Camino de Durin. Los orcos Globsnaga se encuentran por todo Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Como Orvar se ha negado a sellar el pasaje recién excavado, Corunothiel te ha pedido que trabajes con su amigo Nimpheleg para localizar y destruir la fuente de la podredumbre marchita dentro de Buzun-ghâr, y derrotar a los Globsnaga que han sido afectados o atraídos por la corrupción.","'Bueno, ${PLAYER}, no fue una gran tarea, ¿verdad? ¿Por qué deberían Corunothiel y Nimpheleg preocuparse tanto por sellar Buzun-ghâr, cuando derrotaste tan hábilmente a Grawulun el Caerog? ¡Ahora este pasaje puede ser de gran beneficio para los enanos!'","Ejecuta el plan de Nimpheleg para destruir la fuente de la podredumbre marchita","'Si Orvar no entra en razón y sella la única entrada a este pasaje, debemos encontrar la fuente de la corrupción y destruirla. Habla con Nimpheleg sobre cómo encontrar esta fuente y tratar con ella.\
\
Hemos visto orcos Globsnaga más profundo en Buzun-ghâr, y tememos que pronto suban hasta aquí. ¿Han sido corrompidos por la podredumbre marchita, o hay otra causa para su aflicción?\
\
Estas preguntas son secundarias respecto al asunto más importante, ${PLAYER}: deben ser derrotados antes de que puedan hacernos daño. Destrúyelos mientras llevas a cabo el plan de Nimpheleg para limpiar la fuente de la podredumbre marchita.'","Ejecutaste el plan de Nimpheleg para destruir la fuente de la podredumbre marchita","'Un mensaje para ti fue entregado a Orvar mientras estabas en las profundidades, ${PLAYER}. Deberías hablar con él para conocer su contenido.'"},
[3202]={"'He decidido vigilar a Mazog personalmente.'","'¿Por qué seguimos esperando aquí sin hacer nada?'","'¡No vine en esta misión solo para esperar en una bodega!'","'Otri Martillogrís se encuentra dentro de la Posada Embrujada, ${PLAYER}. Ocúpate de su problema antes de que empeore, como me temo que seguramente lo hará. ¿No hemos sufrido ya suficientes contratiempos sin los problemas de estos enanos imprudentes?'","Otri Martillogrís está junto a la chimenea en la Posada Embrujada, entre los Troncosombríos.\
\
Has sacado a los hermanos Martillogrís de sus ensoñaciones y ahora deberías regresar con Otri.","'La espera no hace que la decisión sea más fácil.'","'Bróin está en la bodega de esta posada, ${PLAYER}. Dile que mis hermanos están a salvo y pregúntale también si estamos listos para continuar. ¡Espero que sí, porque este bosque no es un lugar para enanos!'","'${PLAYER}, ¿me ayudarás? Más te vale, porque para eso formas parte de esta empresa insensata, ¿no es así? No hablaría mal de los planes de Bósi y Brogur, pero Bróin no ha tenido la experiencia de su tío ni de su padre, ¿verdad? ¡Ni la de los Martillogrís, a decir verdad!\
\
'Ahora dos de mis hermanos han desaparecido en el pantano, y si los Elfos saben la diferencia entre terreno traicionero y suelo firme, ¡han tenido cuidado de no decirnos cuál es cuál!\
\
'Encuentra a Rósar y Stígur Martillogrís, en algún lugar entre los pantanos del Bosque Ahogado, ${PLAYER}, y encuéntralos rápidamente. Hay terrores acuáticos en ese lugar, y ningún enano que se respete estaría contento de quedarse atrapado en un pantano tan vil con la única ayuda disponible de estos Elfos de Lórien.'","'Me preocupaba que los Martillogrís se convirtieran en un problema, ${PLAYER}, pero ¿qué podía decir al respecto? Nada, ¡y ahora se han metido en problemas ellos mismos, y a nosotros también!\
\
'Otri Martillogrís puede contarte más. Lo vi por última vez dentro de la Posada Embrujada, enfurecido junto al hogar, gritando a quien quisiera escucharlo.'","'¿Debería nuestro camino pasar por las Hondonadas Enmarañadas?'","'Mis hermanos fueron a los pantanos del Bosque Ahogado, al sur de los Troncosombríos, y nunca regresaron. ¡Se dice que hay terrores acuáticos en los pantanos del Bosque Ahogado, y lo creo! ¡Se rumorea que un Elfo se perdió a causa de uno de ellos!\
\
'Si algún mal ha tomado a mis hermanos, debo saberlo para poder añadir su nombre a la lista de enemigos de los Martillogrís!'","Habla con Bróin en la bodega de la Posada Embrujada","Encuentra a Rósar Martillogrís y asegura su seguridad","Cúcheron te ha dado la desafortunada noticia de que la misión de la Guardia Oculta sigue estancada y que los enanos Martillogrís han causado otro retraso.","Bróin está en la bodega de la Posada Embrujada, en los Troncosombríos.\
\
Otri te ha pedido que le digas a Bróin que sus hermanos están a salvo y que verifiques si la Guardia Oculta ya ha decidido una ruta.","Habla con Otri Martillogrís en la Posada Embrujada","Rósar y Stígur Martillogrís están perdidos en algún lugar de los pantanos del Bosque Ahogado, al sur de los Troncosombríos.\
\
Otri Martillogrís está desesperado por que encuentres a sus hermanos, perdidos en los pantanos del Bosque Ahogado.","Al fijar la mirada en los ojos vidriosos del enano, te das cuenta de que no se trata de Rósar Martillogrís, sino de una imagen conjurada por los males del pantano. ¡No dejes que te engañe!","'¡Debemos partir de nuevo pronto, o nunca lo haremos!'","'Hola de nuevo, ${PLAYER}. Esta espera ya ha comenzado a cansar, y mi paciencia ya estaba al límite para empezar. Los Elfos aún no han decidido qué camino seguir. Quizás puedas ayudarles a decidir, si es que alguien puede hacerlo.'","Al fijar la mirada en los ojos vidriosos del enano, te das cuenta de que no se trata de Stígur Martillogrís, sino de una imagen conjurada por los males del pantano. ¡No dejes que te engañe!","'Rósar y Stígur estaban justo aquí, ${PLAYER}, y tenían las historias más extrañas que contar. Cada uno de ellos informó haber visto caras familiares entre los arbustos y zarzas enmarañados y haber escuchado voces en el viento, pero cuando se acercaron, llenos de asombro al ver a amigos perdidos en un lugar así, no había señal de nadie. Pero he aquí, más adelante... ¡una alentadora ola y una sonrisa!\
\
'Este lugar me llena de inquietud, ${PLAYER}. Gracias por rescatar a mis hermanos. Sin tu ayuda, temo que habría habido dos Martillogrís menos en este mundo al anochecer, si es que el anochecer alguna vez deja realmente este sombrío bosque.\
\
'Bróin está en la bodega. Dile que mis hermanos están a salvo y pregúntale también si los Elfos han llegado a un acuerdo sobre cómo proceder. Cuanto antes salgamos de este lugar, ¡más feliz estará este Martillogrís!'","'No confío en Mazog. No lo dejaré fuera de mi vista.'","'Deberíamos tomar el camino del sur a través de Taur Morvith.'","'Otri Martillogrís se encuentra dentro de la Posada Embrujada.\
\
Cúcheron te dijo que hablaras con Otri Martillogrís sobre un problema que ha afectado a los enanos.'","Capítulo 5: Luces Traicioneras","Encuentra a Stígur Martillogrís y asegura su seguridad"},
[3203]={"'Brogur todavía se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek. Hazle llegar mi advertencia tan rápido como puedas, porque estas noticias me ponen nervioso.'","Bósi ha leído más del Libro de Mazarbul, y está preocupado por la prisa de Brogur.","Brogur se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bósi está preocupado por lo que ha leído sobre el destino de Balin en el Libro de Mazarbul, y quiere que le adviertes a su primo que sea más cauteloso.","'Mi primo siempre se preocupa demasiado. Balin tuvo un mal final, sí, pero esta vez será diferente. ¡Mira todas las victorias que ya hemos tenido, y en tan poco tiempo!\
\
'Estaremos bien, ${PLAYER}. No hagas caso a las preocupaciones infundadas de Bósi. Siempre hace esto. Moria ya nos ha costado mucho; seguramente lo peor ya ha pasado.'","Capítulo 5: Palabras de precaución","'Es peor de lo que esperaba, ${PLAYER}: el destino final de Balin fue sombrío. No he leído todo aún, pero hay mucho aquí que deberíamos tomar como advertencia. Estaban muy superados en número, pero parecían no darse cuenta de esto hasta que fue demasiado tarde.\
\
'Regresa a la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek, y dile a mi primo Brogur que sea más cauteloso. Me preocupa que si no aprendemos las lecciones de la expedición de Balin, podríamos estar condenados a su destino.\
\
'Quizás estoy reaccionando exageradamente -- de hecho espero que ese sea el caso. De cualquier manera, lleva mi advertencia a Brogur tan rápido como puedas.'"},
[3204]={"'I am too busy to provide such teaching. I am sorry.'","'It is my hope to find one of the Zabad'ibîn, and... no! Why should I aim so low? Say instead that I shall be the one to find all seven of the sacred stones, and let the name Stáli the Hewer echo in every dwarf-hall from here to the Blue Mountains!\
\
'Now that I have spoken the dream aloud, I detect in it a flaw. How am I to deliver seven such valuable stones to Prince Durin? Each of the Zabad'ibîn should be carefully-handled, and I should fear to drop one when the time comes to pass them into the prince's hands....\
\
'Ah-ha! A solution comes. I will not deliver the stones into Durin's care individually, but rather fashioned into a larger work of art! But what? Perhaps a statue of the prince himself, holding aloft one or more of the gems? Mayhap the statue can wear a belt with the seven stones embedded within? Worry not! These problems can be solved.\
\
'There is the small matter of finding the Zabad'ibîn. I sent my assistant Eskil Bloodthumb to search Deepscrave for works of dwarf-art that might be recovered from the Orcs. Find him and tell him he is to also search for these gems!'","Worried that he lacks the necessary training to successfully investigate Deepscrave, Eskil Bloodthumb has asked you to find a teacher at Maergrind willing to help him hone his skills.","Stáli the Hewer is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate.","'Trausti has agreed to teach me what he knows of combat? That is fine news, ${PLAYER}, thank you! Have you seen his axe? That is a dwarf that knows a thing or two about slaying Orcs, and better yet: he knows how to stay alive while he does it!\
\
'It will take some time before I learn what Trausti has to teach me. I will venture into Deepscrave once my new teacher deems me ready to do so, but it might be awhile. Could I ask you to bring word to my master that I will be delayed? You should find him at Maergrind, I expect.'\
\
As you turn to go, Eskil suddenly speaks again.\
\
'One more thing, friend. Make sure... make sure not to sign anything.'","'Tell Eskil that once he has returned to a place of safety I will find him for a second lesson. A dead dwarf is no help to his master or his prince, and with my help he will not become one!'","Chapter 6.1: The Artist and the Apprentice","Eskil Bloodthumb stands at the entrance to Deepscrave, weaponless and ashamed of his clumsiness.","Eskil has dropped his axe, fumbling it while trying to show off his fighting form for you.","'Ah. Thank you, yes. Sorry.'\
\
Eskil looks down at the ground, dejected and ashamed.\
\
'Am I being sent to my death, ${PLAYER}? Reports from Deepscrave make it sound a den of foes, crawling with Orcs and goblins, and you have seen what happens to me when I seek to wield an axe! I am apprenticed to Stáli and must do as he orders, but if I venture into Deepscrave as I am now, I will surely perish, and my master will need another apprentice.\
\
'I know you are busy with your other duties, but do you think you could find a dwarf at Maergrind that might instruct me in the ways of combat? What I need is a good teacher: skilled and patient both!'","Talk to Eskil Bloodthumb at the entrance to Deepscrave","'Oh, hullo there, friend. My master sent me to search Deepscrave for valuable works of dwarf-art he might restore, but I have heard from scouts that the caverns crawl with foes, and the Orcs have a village there.'\
\
You tell Eskil that Stáli has asked him to search also for sign of the Zabad'ibîn that were lost from the Steepset, and the artist's assistant frowns again.\
\
'Oh my. Yes, I will do my best, although I am not very practised at the combat arts. Actually... you are an accomplished adventurer. Do you think you could observe my... fighting style, my combat form, whatever it is you heroes look for... and tell me what I might be doing wrong?\
\
'Thank you so much, my friend! Watch closely and tell me what I need to improve!'","Pick up Eskil's fumbled axe","Eskil Bloodthumb is still at the entrance to Deepscrave, waiting for the news that you found him a teacher.","Observe Eskil's fighting form","Talk to Stáli the Hewer at Maergrind, the Noble Gate","Stáli the Hewer has charged his apprentice Eskil Bloodthumb with searching the caverns of Deepscrave for the Zabad'ibîn, the lost jewels of the Steepset.","'What? You're telling me my apprentice has not yet ventured into Deepscrave? How will he find me the Zabad'ibîn if he refuses to leave Máttugard?'","'Oh, hullo there, friend.'","Stáli the Hewer's assistant, Eskil Bloodthumb, stands at the entrance to Deepscrave.","Eskil fumbles his axe, which clatters clumsily to the ground","'I forge metal into weapons, I do not refine inexperienced dwarves into warriors!\
\
'Find someone else!'","Give Eskil back his axe","Eskil Bloodthumb has asked you to observe his fighting style so you can give him pointers about his combat form.","Eskil Bloodthumb is at the entrance to Deepscrave from Máttugard, south-west of the Steepset.","Eskil reddens with embarrassment","'I sent my apprentice Eskil Bloodthumb to search Deepscrave for works of dwarf-art that might be recovered from the Orcs. Find him and tell him he is to also search for these stones!'","Eskil Bloodthumb frowns nervously as you approach","'I know you are busy with your other duties, but do you think you could find a dwarf at Maergrind that might instruct me in the ways of combat? What I need is a good teacher: skilled and patient both!'","Find a teacher at Maergrind willing to instruct Eskil Bloodthumb in the arts of combat and survival","'You expect me to teach a young Longbeard how to fight? He would not survive the experience, I assure you, even had I the time to spend.\
\
'But if you're looking for someone who does have the time to spare, you should find an idle Longbeard... perhaps the one called Trausti, to the north-east of this camp.'","'Eskil Bloodthumb seeks a trainer in the arts of war? I have seen him following that imperious sculptor through the halls of Máttugard, a cowed and shrinking figure! He is no warrior. Not yet, at least.\
\
'I and my axe will make him a worthy addition to the Gabil'akkâ, much as his master carves unhewn stone into figures of royal shape! By my training's end he will fear nothing... but not before. Bring him my first lesson: \\qget away from Deepscrave! You are not ready for such a place as that!\\q\
\
'Tell him too that once he has returned to a place of safety I will find him for a second lesson. A dead dwarf is no help to his master or his prince, and with my help he will not become one!'","'Don't sign anything Stáli gives you, friend. Trust me.'","Find Eskil Bloodthumb at the entrance to Deepscrave, south-west of the Steepset","'I have little time to spare for such instruction as Eskil Bloodthumb requires, ${PLAYER}. There must be someone else who can teach the lad.'"},
[3205]={"'Enjoy the comforts of my halls and the conversation of my people. My scholars study the artifacts from Dol Guldur, and if any sign of this Bugdatish is found, you will be called. My people have much experience facing the corruption of Sauron. They will be vigilant now, and will learn what they safely may of these artifacts. That done, any that cannot be cured and retained will be destroyed. You need not worry on that score.'","This is King Thranduil's dining chamber, but there is no feast here today","Gondil smiles sadly, remembering days before she left Caras Tilion","Itheron apologizes for his sudden reticence, but he will say no more","You have come to Felegoth, the Halls of the Elvenking, and should make yourself known to Limlang, the guard at the entrance.","Felegoth, the Halls of the Elvenking, can be found in the north-eastern woods of Eryn Lasgalen.\
\
The steed near King Thranduil outside the ruins of Dol Guldur can take you to Eryn Lasgalen with utmost speed.","The air is cool and damp with mist in this river-channel","'I welcome you to Felegoth, ${PLAYER}, and to the greater wood of Eryn Lasgalen. Enjoy the comforts of my halls and the conversation of my people. My scholars study the artifacts from Dol Guldur, and if any sign of this Bugdatish is found, you will be called.'\
\
You express your concern about keeping artifacts from Dol Guldur within his halls, and Thranduil nods.\
\
'You are wise to be wary, but my people have much experience facing the corruption of Sauron. Did they not resist its influence for the many years of darkness that gave this forest the name Mirkwood? They will be vigilant now and will learn what they safely may of these artifacts. That done, any that cannot be cured and retained will be destroyed. Worry not on that score.'","Talk to Gondil in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room","You have found the entrance to the caverns of Felegoth, the Halls of the Elvenking","Talk to Herthír in the dining chamber east of the throne room","Journey to the entrance of Felegoth in the north-eastern reaches of Eryn Lasgalen","'You say the Orcs sought Karazgar at Dol Guldur? Yes, the Weeping Warrior is known to me, for he has troubled my people for many years. He is a dragon-tamer, sly and cruel. I long suspected he had some part in rousing Smaug the Golden from his lair in the Ered Mithrin, but lacked the proof of it. Smaug is long dead, but Karazgar remains, a constant thorn in the side of my people and others in the North. I would be glad to see him slain, but he is elusive.\
\
'Neither have I heard of this artifact Bugdatish. A number of relics from Dol Guldur will be brought back to Felegoth for cleansing and for study. One of these may prove the artifact you seek. You are welcome to journey north with us to Felegoth. There is a horse here on the Hill of Ruin that will bear you swiftly to Eryn Lasgalen. When you arrive at Tham Taerdol in the Green Mountains, travel north-east through the trees. You will find my halls in the caverns beneath the hill of Cerin Dorn. My son also journeys home and will be pleased to see you there.'","'I have been told to expect you. Welcome to the Halls of the Elvenking.'","Chapter 6.1: The Halls of the Elvenking","'I am delighted to see you in my father's halls, ${PLAYER}! I think Gimli would appreciate them as well, if he could put aside the grudges of his sire, who spent some time imprisoned in the dungeons here. Yes, I have heard the story! Glóin and the others of his company are fortunate it was not my duty to guard their cells, or they might be there still! Much mischief might have followed then, and it seems likely Smaug would still trouble the North, so let us be glad the watch on the dwarves was not a princely duty!\
\
'In truth, I have not spent much time at Felegoth, not since I was young. These caves are home, and they remind my father of his own younger days in service to his liege Thingol, but I prefer wooded glens and sunlight. My father seldom emerges from his halls, save to hunt and feast in the nearby woods. Instead he sends me to accomplish his desires in the wider world, and I relish those errands. I would not have attended the Council of Elrond, were it not so, but that is a tale you know!\
\
'I invite you to explore Felegoth while you are here, ${PLAYER}! Visit the dining chamber, the Room of Study, and the water-way bridge, and speak to a number of the Elves you encounter. You will find them pleasant and welcoming, no matter what Gimli and his sire might have led you to believe!'","Legolas invited you to visit the dining chamber, the Room of Study, and the water-way bridge in Felegoth, and to speak to the Elves you find at those locations.","Herthír smiles, anticipating the day the wood-elves will rule Eryn Lasgalen","'How did you enjoy your exploration of my father's halls, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You share your experience of Felegoth and ask Legolas about the Necklace of Girion, mentioned by Itheron. He stares at you in silence.\
\
'That is a subject about which my father prefers not to speak, and I will respect his wishes. I will say only this: the Gweriamir was crafted by dwarves and gifted to the bride of Thingol, my father's liege. When he was murdered, she cast it away in disgust and it was lost for thousands of years. It came in the end to the dwarves of Erebor and seeing it there enflamed my father's anger, as you surely can understand, ${PLAYER}. When Smaug came, my father turned the dwarves away and they became a people in exile.\
\
'I am not proud to recount this to you. The matter was resolved, in time, and I do not wish to dwell upon it. There are dangers and troubles enough to face for now, without dwelling upon old injuries and half-forgotten insults.'","'Our scholars study the artifacts brought from Dol Guldur, hoping to cleanse them of the evil that blankets them. I hope they prove able, for that was once our home.\
\
'It is true. I speak not of the fortress! No, the fortress of Dol Guldur was wholly constructed by servants of the Enemy. But it was built upon the bones of the Elf-hall that once stood atop the bald hill, abandoned at the advice of Curunír the White. He believed the darkening of Mirkwood could not be slowed, and King Thranduil heeded his words and led us north beyond Agordor, the Narrows of the Forest.\
\
'We settled at a rocky spire in the mountains of Emyn Laeg, overlooking the source of the river Lúthond. Thranduil named the hill Caras Tilion, and the hall stands still, but it stands empty. The darkness of Mirkwood spread, and our retreat from the southern reaches of the wood was not to be the last such retreat.\
\
'I do not wish to speak of it, I am sorry. My happiest days were spent in Caras Tilion, and speaking of it now brings the pain of their loss anew.'","'You are welcome in Felegoth, ${PLAYER}. The king himself told us to expect you and to hasten you to him when you arrived.\
\
'There will be time to explore the halls of Felegoth at your leisure! For now, find King Thranduil at his throne in the north-eastern chamber. And be welcome!'","'When the Last Alliance marched through Rhovanion on its way to Mordor, none were turned away who swore to march against the Dark Lord. Men of the Long Lake, dwarves of Khazad-dûm, and Elves of the divided Greenwood, west and east, stood side by side.\
\
'I fought with my brothers and sisters at Dagorlad, but more than half of the wood-elves did not return from the war. Lost too were our kings. Thranduil ascended to the throne, and though he is not a wood-elf, he never forgot the sacrifice of my people. He led us wisely and well during the years since the Battle of Dagorlad. He is the Elvenking, and I am proud to serve him.\
\
'I know he will one day depart for the Undying Lands with the rest of his kin, and leave this land to be ruled by wood-elves. I will celebrate his rule when that day comes and speak much praise for Thranduil Swiftstream! That day is soon approaching.'","Talk to Itheron on the river-bridge, east of the throne room","Thranduil the Elvenking has invited you to visit his halls in the northern reaches of Eryn Lasgalen, where he believes you may find news of Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior.","Talk to Legolas in the throne room of Felegoth","Legolas has come to his father's throne room in Felegoth.","'There will be time to explore the halls of Felegoth at your leisure! For now, find King Thranduil at his throne in the north-east chamber.'","'A number of relics from Dol Guldur will be brought back to Felegoth for cleansing and for study. One of these may prove the artifact you seek. You are welcome to journey north with us to Felegoth. There is a horse here on the Hill of Ruin that will bear you swiftly to Eryn Lasgalen. When you arrive at Tham Taerdol in the Green Mountains, travel north-east through the trees. You will find my halls in the caverns beneath the hill of Cerin Dorn. My son also journeys home and will be pleased to see you there.'","Talk to Limlang at the entrance to Felegoth","This is the Room of Study, where scholars pore over the artifacts from Dol Guldur","'These caverns were carefully shaped over hundreds of years, ${PLAYER}, and now their beauty is a comfort to me. So too is it a reminder that even amid darkness, Wood-elves and Grey-elves working together can achieve works of grace and splendour.\
\
'So too can it be between Elves and dwarves? There has been trade between our peoples, to be certain, but that is a history troubled and long. There may now be friendship and peace between Elves of the Wood and dwarves of the Mountain, but it was not always so.\
\
'In Erebor, the Lonely Mountain of the dwarves, their miners unearthed a shining white jewel of unsurpassed brilliance. King Thranduil believed it must be nothing less than one of the lost Silmarils, and demanded to see it, but Thráin of the dwarves refused. Thranduil shut the gates of Felegoth to the dwarves, and only the council of Mithrandir and his assurance that the white jewel could not be a Silmaril repaired those broken bonds of friendship. They were later strained again, but of the Necklace of Girion it is not my place to speak! Ask the prince Legolas of it if you must, but I will say naught of it now.'","'I invite you to explore Felegoth while you are here, ${PLAYER}! Visit the dining chamber, the Room of Study, and the water-way bridge, and speak to a number of the Elves you encounter. You will find them pleasant and welcoming, no matter what Gimli and his father might have led you to believe!'","King Thranduil is at his throne in the north-eastern chamber of Felegoth.","Legolas is in his father's throne room, in Felegoth.","Talk to King Thranduil at his throne in Felegoth"},
[3206]={"Driftwood, standing nearby, calls for your attention","Retrieve Umbari Book of Romance","Retrieve Umbari Book of Flora","Bring the stolen books back to Jâkin in Jax Phanâl","Talk to Nauriel outside Jax Phanâl","The Haradrim that were pushed out of Jax Phanâl have a camp to the south where they keep the things they stole.","Retrieved Umbari Book of Romance","Defeat Haradrim at Grijâti south of Jax Phanâl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Jâkin is in the settlement of Jax Phanâl, on the Cape of Umbar.","'So this is the Cape of Umbar? The Corsair Daxamat tells me his people call it Umbarkhîl, and it is a land of beauty? For him it may be. For me I see only the land of the folk who stole my son Thorongil away. The sooner we get to the City of the Corsairs, the sooner I will have my vengeance.'\
\
You remind Nauriel that the mission is to rescue Thorongil, not to take revenge, and she gives you a cool look.\
\
'The Corsair Daxamat also says there can be two ways to say the same thing, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps it is the same with this.'","Chapter 6.1: The Road From Jax Phanâl","The settlement of Jax Phanâl is to the east.","Driftwood has accompanied you to Jax Phanâl, on the Cape of Umbar.","You recovered the stolen books and should bring them back to Jâkin in Jax Phanâl.","Defeated Haradrim at Grijâti (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have made the crossing to the Cape of Umbar from the Shield Isles and should now turn your attention toward reaching Umbar Baharbêl.","'I am most grateful for this service you have provided this day! These books are very dear to me, and I could not bear to think of them in the hands of the Ordâkhim, never to be read again. They did not know the worth of the treasures they stole from us!\
\
'You are a friend to the Free City of Umbar; I see that now. I will tell none of your arrival here. The merchant road runs along the coast southward to Rakhatâb, where it turns north and passes by a small fishing village, Khûtra. Umbar Baharbêl lies just beyond the hills past the village, the shining jewel of Umbarkhîl. Go in peace, and with my best wishes for your health and happiness.'","'The Haradrim will have them at their camp to the south. Retrieve my books and defeat any of the warriors you must, and you will prove yourself a helpful sort.'","Nauriel has made the crossing from the Shield Isles to the Cape of Umbar, and you should speak with her outside Jax Phanâl.","Talk to Jâkin in Jax Phanâl","Retrieve Umbari Book of History","Talk to Driftwood in Jax Phanâl","Retrieved Umbari Book of Flora","Retrieved Umbari Book of History","'You have come to Jax Phanâl with a curious group, stranger. I hope you and your friends will cause no trouble here, for if you do, the Kindred of the Coins will see that it is the last trouble you make. Umbar Baharbêl has been made a Free City once again, and under the rule of the Kindred the Haradrim of the Great Southern Empire have been driven out of Jax Phanâl and other villages along Umbarkhîl, the Cape of Umbar. The Empire of Ordâkh has no claim upon us, and never will again. They plundered our valuables when they fled, and even now they muster their warriors at a camp to the south. They have no interest in some of the things they stole... they wanted only to deprive us of them.'\
\
Jâkin studies your face carefully.\
\
'Are you a helpful sort? Or do you only wish to learn what you can and move on, leaving we who struggle here behind when we are not useful to you? Few come to Jax Phanâl without reason, and fewer still leave the Shield Isles without some ill intent. I wonder what my silence might be worth to you? There must be some who would be interested to hear of your little group of travellers. Unless you are a helpful sort. Then it might be different.'","Jâkin eyes you warily as you approach","'I think we should help this man, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'He is not wrong, for in other lands we have done as he said: moved on when we learned what we could, remaining only for as long as we needed to learn where next to journey. Now, it was war! So I do not think we could have done otherwise! But if we can help the folk of Jax Phanâl and also keep our presence hidden from those who watch for us, I believe we should.\
\
'What would Jâkin have us do?'","'You are a helpful sort, then? I smile to hear it!\
\
'When the magistrate's forces drove the Haradrim from Jax Phanâl, the occupiers fled with whatever valuables they could find, but they were not... how would you say it? Choosy. Some of them stole books of great value to me personally, and I would have them back. These are not worth any great amount of Phârzi or Gîmli, but they do contain stories and accounts that are very dear to me, and I want them back.\
\
'The Haradrim will have them at their camp to the south. Retrieve my books and defeat any of the warriors you must, and you will prove yourself a helpful sort.'","'You are a friend to the Free City of Umbar; I see that now. I will tell none of your arrival here. The merchant road runs along the coast southward to Rakhatâb, where it turns north and passes by a small fishing village, Khûtra. Umbar Baharbêl lies just beyond the hills past the village, the shining jewel of Umbarkhîl. Go in peace, and with my best wishes for your health and happiness.'","'It is... almost like it used to be, isn't it?'\
\
He gazes out past the buildings of Jax Phanâl, and you know he is thinking of Nona. He catches you looking at him and gives you a brief smile.\
\
'Well, thank you for listening to me, ${PLAYER}. Let us return to the shore and see if the rest of the crew has made the crossing.'","'Thank you for taking my advice, ${PLAYER}. When every party gets something of value, you can be assured they will each stand by the bargain. I learned this on the river, in my old life, and it was a useful lesson.\
\
'Let us return to the shore and see if the rest of the crew has made the crossing.'","'Are you a helpful sort? Or do you only wish to learn what you can and move on, leaving we who struggle here behind when we are not useful to you? Few come to Jax Phanâl without reason, and fewer still leave the Shield Isles without some ill intent. I wonder what my silence might be worth to you? There must be some who would be interested to hear of your little group of travellers. Unless you are a helpful sort. Then it might be different.'","'This is not the road we expected to take to the City of the Corsairs, ${PLAYER}, but it is now the one we must walk. Let us ask someone in the nearby settlement how best to reach Umbar Baharbêl. The conclusion of King Elessar's mission awaits us there... but we cannot complete this quest until we reach the city.'","Enter the settlement of Jax Phanâl","'Jâkin uses us cleverly, ${PLAYER}. I recognize the tactic from my days of... banditry.\
\
'But he is not wrong about this: his silence will aid us more than an errant word to the wrong folk, and if we might accomplish some good for the people here at the same time, how should I put it? Everyone wins, or at least no one loses more than anyone else, which is a start, and for me a change.\
\
'What would he have us do?'","'Let us ask someone in the nearby settlement how best to reach Umbar Baharbêl. The conclusion of King Elessar's mission awaits us there... but we cannot complete this quest until we reach the city.'"},
[3207]={"Defeated Orcs or goblins in Deepscrave (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Venture into Deepscrave, slay any Orcs you find, and inspect the Berg-beam at several different points to ensure it stands strong, with no sign of weakness. Then return to me with your report, and together we will decide how best to proceed.'","'You should return to the prince and see how you can help the Gabil'akkâ. And while you adventure on behalf of all dwarves, perhaps you will keep your eyes open for works of art that might be of interest to one specific dwarf...?'","Bring the rusted dagger and dirty gem to Stáli the Hewer at Maergrind in Máttugard","Search debris at the upper extent of the Berg-beam","Stáli the Hewer is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate.","Stáli the Hewer is waiting for you to emerge from Deepscrave and bring him the fruits of your search. He is at Maergrind in Máttugard.","'Did you convince my apprentice not to enter Deepscrave? For shame, ${PLAYER}! You had no right to interfere in this matter.\
\
'I will forgive you if you sign this contract agreeing to help me instead. The parchment is right here.'","You search the fallen rubble but find nothing of value","This lower portion of the Berg-beam appears wide and sturdy","'Well, go on, sign the contract agreeing to help me.'","Beneath the pile of refuse you find a dirt-smeared and cloudy gem","Sign the contract or tell him <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>","Defeat Orcs or goblins in Deepscrave (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Search debris at the lower extent of the Berg-beam","Durin asked you to examine the Berg-beam in Deepscrave for signs of weakness and to combat any Orcs you find there. While you are on the prince's business, you may as well keep your eyes open for the jewels sought by Stáli the Hewer.","Talk to Durin at Maergrind in Máttugard","'With your help we have secured Máttugard, and now it is time to push beyond the limits of the last conquest. There was a war to fight, then... now the war is here, and we need not turn our attention elsewhere!\
\
'To the west of Máttugard you will find Deepscrave, an enormous cavern more than a thousand feet tall. Within the vast space, a single column of stone descends into the darkness: the Berg-beam, Pillar of the Mountain. The lords of Gundabad dwelt in Máttugard, but the common folk lived in homes built around the great column. I hear tell that now the dwellings in Deepscrave are home only to Orcs and goblins... a terrible insult.\
\
'Venture into Deepscrave, slay any Orcs you find, and inspect the Berg-beam at several different points to ensure it stands strong, with no sign of weakness. Then return to me with your report, and together we will decide how best to proceed.'","Stáli the Hewer has presented you with a contract requiring you to assist him. It is your choice whether to sign the document or tell him <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>.","This middle portion of the Berg-beam still stands strong","Buried within the fallen debris you find an old and rusted dagger","'Ah, it is nothing, nothing at all. We are all working for the same goal, are we not? Victory in Gundabad helps every interest: mine, Prince Durin's, and yours! That is simply logical, and no one can deny it!\
\
'You should return to the prince and see how you can help the Gabil'akkâ. And while you adventure on behalf of all dwarves, perhaps you will keep your eyes open for works of art that might be of interest to one specific dwarf...?'","Chapter 6.2: Pillar of the Mountain","Search debris near the midpoint of the Berg-beam","This upper portion of the Berg-beam appears sturdy enough","Durin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.","You shake your head, and Stáli laughs off your refusal","Talk to Stáli the Hewer at Maergrind","'What have you found, what have you found?'\
\
Stáli takes the rusted dagger and the dirty gem from you and eyes them carefully.\
\
'Hmm... I will clean these off and have a look, but I am not especially hopeful. Perhaps once I have scrubbed the filth from this jewel it will match an indentation on the Steepset, but I suspect it will not. Still, it may have worth all its own, even should it not prove to be one of the Zabad'ibîn.\
\
'Allow me to give you this reward in token of our mutually beneficial relationship, ${PLAYER}.'","Stáli the Hewer believes you convinced Eskil Bloodthumb not to search Deepscrave for the jewels of the Steepset, and he hopes that you will do so on behalf of his assistant.","You sign the contract and Stáli's grin widens"},
[3208]={"Defeated foes within Caras Tilion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Thranduil in his throne room in Felegoth","Thranduil is in his throne room in Felegoth.","Legolas is eager to help you track down the Orc spies that have been seen creeping throughout Eryn Lasgalen and to learn from them what evils they might be planning.","Find Gardelen and Dínellas south-east of Torech Emel, in Eryn Lasgalen","The hunter Dínellas motions quietly to you and Legolas, drawing you near","'I slew one of the Orc-spies already, and the rest fled into the trees. If you wish to see my handiwork, he lies right over there.'","Show the letter for Karazgar to Legolas near Caras Tilion","Defeated foes in Eryn Lasgalen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Any friend of the prince is friend to me also, ${PLAYER}. I bid you greetings and courtesy, and safety in the wood!\
\
'There are Orc-spies beneath the canopy of the wood, and they have stirred other creatures to wakefulness with the tramp of their filthy boots. I do not know what has brought them hither, but any errand of theirs is certain to oppose the will of Thranduil.\
\
'Dínellas went in search of them, in the direction of Caras Tilion. Before you follow him, will you slay some of the foes the Orcs stirred in their wake?'","'Legolas told me you adventured into Caras Tilion and beheld the ruin it has become. I am glad of your efforts within. Did you learn aught of the artifact Bugdatish or the Weeping Warrior?'","You find a filthy parchment among the Orc's possessions","Search the Orc-spy slain by Dínellas","'I have heard tell of Orc-spies in the forest. We should seek the scouts my father dispatched, and see what they have learned of these spies. Gardelen and Dínellas patrol the wood south-east of Torech Emel. Let us go to them and hear their report!'","The Elf-scout Gardelen calls to Legolas warmly and waves to you","'Gladly will we slay the beasts stirred to anger by the passage of the Orcs, Gardelen!'","'Search the Orc slain by Dínellas, and see if he carries anything to shed light on his purpose here, ${PLAYER}.'","'The Orc carried a letter from its captain? Show it to the prince, for it may contain some information we can use against them!'","Legolas is near the ruins of the Elf-hall at Caras Tilion.","The Orc-spy slain by Dínellas can be found by his position near Caras Tilion.","'This letter is very interesting, ${PLAYER}, but I do not understand what has given rise to it. Are the Gúrzyul of whom Mithrandir speaks not united? This letter, at least, speaks clearly to me: Ugrukhôr and Karazgar are at odds, and the Captain of the Pit seeks knowledge only possessed by the Weeping Warrior. Perhaps they will draw each other's blood and save us the effort!\
\
'I know that is unlikely. If you will enter Caras Tilion and defeat the foes that lurk within, I will set my mind to considering our next steps. I once called Caras Tilion home, and seeing enemies within brings sadness to my heart, though it has been many years since any of my people lived within its walls.'","'If you will enter Caras Tilion and defeat the foes that lurk within, I will set my mind to considering our next steps. I once called Caras Tilion home, and seeing enemies within brings sadness to my heart, though it has been many years since any of my people lived within its walls.'","'Orc-spies have stirred other creatures to wakefulness with the tramp of their filthy boots. Dínellas went in search of them, in the direction of Caras Tilion. Before you follow him, will you slay some of the foes the Orcs stirred in their wake?'","'Dínellas is a skilled hunter. Indeed, I learned much of the craft from his patient lessons!'","Talk to Legolas near Caras Tilion","'It is my pleasure to meet you, ${PLAYER}. Tell me how the prince has fared on your journey beneath the trees, if you can spare the tale. Long ago, at the king's request, I taught Legolas much of his woodcraft. I hope he has lived up to my high expectation!'\
\
Dínellas laughs, and although he is a new acquaintance you can tell his laughter comes easily and often.\
\
'But there is no time for such friendly stories. You have arrived too late to aid me with the Orc-spies! I slew one of them already, and the rest fled into the trees. If you wish to see my handiwork, he lies right over there.'","'Let us instead look to the dangers that await my people in Eryn Lasgalen today! It is mere hours since I returned, and already I have heard tell of Orc-spies in the forest. We should seek the scouts my father dispatched, and see what they have learned of these spies.\
\
'Gardelen and Dínellas patrol the wood south-east of Torech Emel. Let us go to them and hear their report!'","Legolas asked you to defeat foes within his old home of Caras Tilion while he considers the meaning of the letter you discovered.","Find Dínellas near Caras Tilion, in Eryn Lasgalen","Defeat foes within Caras Tilion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have given some more thought to the words of Ugrukhôr, but every avenue upon which my mind travels leads to no answers. This artifact called Bugdatish is not known to me. Indeed, beyond its name I know nothing of it. It seems I share that trait with the Captain of the Pit! Can you not hear the desperation underlying his threats to Karazgar? Whatever this artifact may be, he fiercely desires word of it. Very curious.\
\
'We should return to my father and give him this news. He will be most interested in that which distresses our foes!'","Defeat foes in Eryn Lasgalen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Chapter 6.2: Spies in the Forest","Thranduil's scouts Gardelen and Dínellas patrol the wood south-east of Torech Emel.","'Gardelen is a good friend and a fine tracker. I have known him since he was young.'","Dínellas is near the ruins of the Elf-hall at Caras Tilion.","Dínellas followed a band of Orc-spies through Eryn Lasgalen. Gardelen believed the Orcs were bound for Caras Tilion, and you should seek the hunter Dínellas by the old Elf-hall there.","Show the letter for Karazgar to Dínellas near Caras Tilion","Foes of the Elves have been stirred up by the passage of Orcs through Eryn Lasgalen, and Gardelen has asked you to defeat them if you can."},
[3209]={"'I think we have made life a little more safe for the folk of Rakhatâb, but something still bothers me about the murder of that aged man. Why would one of the Corsairs at Kan Skûrja commit such an act? He was a recent arrival to Rakhatâb, much like we are, and yet they did not depart their encampment to threaten us. Did he possess something they wanted? The guards took the victim's belongings away, and unless we hurry they will put the evidence in a coffer within the keep.\
\
'I have had an idea. I will go keep the guards occupied. You find the evidence coffer and retrieve the old man's belongings from it before they can finish bringing it into the keep!. We may find a clue among them. Let us meet up on the beach to the south-east of the city after you are successful!'","Defeat Corsairs in the Cape of Umbar and at Kan Skûrja, north-east of Rakhatâb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'What have you found, ${PLAYER}? Was Daxamat right? Is there any motivation for the victim's murder to be found among his belongings?'\
\
You unfold the possessions you retrieved from the evidence coffer and study each in turn, handing them to Sirgon after examination.\
\
'A note signed by someone named Galadaith? \\qThere is no information I can give that you have not already been provided, but I assure you that if you offer proof of the deed, you will receive the reward to which you are entitled.\\q That is a familiar name, but why?\
\
'And a knife with a curious insignia on the handle. Is this a snake that coils around itself? See how it goes around the hilt? What does this mean?'","Daxamat motions for you to come speak with him","Daxamat has arrived at your meeting spot south-east of Rakhatâb, and you should show him the evidence you retrieved from the coffer.","Daxamat stands by the crowd in Rakhatâb.","A guard has called for you to step away from the body, and glares at you with distrust.","You agreed to meet with your crew outside Rakhatâb on the south-eastern beach to examine the evidence you retrieved.","Daxamat arrives at the meeting spot. 'Jajax could only have done a little better!' he says","Show the evidence you recovered to Daxamat south-east of Rakhatâb","'No matter what awaits us at the end of the journey, there are still miles to go before we reach it. What is the name of the next settlement along the merchant road to the south? Rakhatâb?\
\
'Then it is to Rakhatâb we must go.'","Examine the body of the victim","Talk to the woman in the crowd","Talk to the man in the crowd","You retrieve the contents of the coffer but should not examine them here","'Murder! Murder!'\
\
The woman tears her gaze from the body lying on the ground and seems to see you for the first time.\
\
'Is nowhere safe anymore? This poor man was slain, right here in the open! I did not get a good look at the man who stabbed him, but he was tall, I do know that. And bearded! He had a great dark beard! One of the Corsairs who camp up the shore to the north-east, I think he was! He must have come here to Rakhatâb with evil in his heart, and death in his mind!\
\
'Did anyone else see this man? Oh, it is terrible!'","Sirgon is at your meeting spot outside Rakhatâb.","Talk to Daxamat outside Rakhatâb","'You there! Stay back. No, I do not suspect you in this, for I saw you arrive. But it is not impossible for the murderer to have had help, so you make sure you keep yourself out of trouble. Guardsmen of Rakhatâb will be watching you.\
\
'Did you say you heard a Corsair might have done this? A tall man, with a dark beard? I am not surprised. Even after the rise of the Kindred of the Coins in Umbar Baharbêl, many of the Corsairs refused to swear oaths of peace and loyalty to the new order. Some of them are camped even now to the north-east along the coast, and sometimes they adventure here to Rakhatâb to cause problems for the workers.\
\
'Might one of them murdered this man? I think it likely.'","'This man was just minding his own business; I heard him cry out as he fell. He was a stranger to Rakhatâb, that is true, but he has been here for a day or two. Why, I think I spoke to him yesterday, but I cannot remember what he was asking about. We spoke about recent events, I seem to recall, and about how the Kindred of the Coins has been dealing with the warriors of Ordâkh that refuse to leave our lands... but the murderer was not one of the Ordâkhim.\
\
'And now this man is dead! Such things were not supposed to still happen after Ordâkh was driven from Umbar! The Kindred promised us peace, and for the most part they have delivered it!'","'I kept the guards talking for as long as I could manage, but I had to leave before they became suspicious. They believe without question that one of the Corsairs from Kan Skûrja is responsible. I see that your own errand was as successful as mine! What have you discovered?'\
\
Daxamat takes the note and the knife from you, and almost drops them.\
\
'What is... no... it cannot be. I know this symbol! This is... this is the knife wielded by The Blade-twist! I have heard tales of him ever since I was a child... but now he is slain, and will collect no further bounties.\
\
'This... this is bad, ${PLAYER}. We knew the identity of three bounty-hunters hired by Saklaphêl to slay the Kindred of the Coins: The Blade-twist, our own Driftwood, and Cruel Dancer. I think Cruel Dancer seeks to eliminate her competition.'","The body of an aged man lies dead on the ground in Rakhatâb.","Chapter 6.2: Whispers In Rakhatâb","Rakhatâb is located on the southern promontory of the Cape of Umbar.","Talk to the guard in Rakhatâb","A crowd has gathered around someone lying on the ground","Nauriel is eager for you to continue along the coast road toward the City of the Corsairs. Your first stop will be at Rakhatâb along the southern promontory.","Search the evidence coffer outside the keep in Rakhatâb","Daxamat is outside Rakhatâb, waiting to hear what you learned from the Corsairs.","A crowd gathers around a body on the ground in Rakhatâb.","'If there are clues to be found among his belongings, I do not understand them.'","'A tall man, with a dark beard? I cannot say I saw him.\
\
'But this man was just minding his own business, and I heard him cry out as he fell. He was a stranger to Rakhatâb, that is true, but he has been here for a day or two. Why, I think I spoke to him yesterday, but I cannot remember what he was asking about. We spoke about recent events, I seem to recall, and about how the Kindred of the Coins has been dealing with the warriors of Ordâkh that refuse to leave our lands... but the murderer was not one of the Ordâkhim.\
\
'And now this man is dead! Such things were not supposed to still happen after Ordâkh was driven from Umbar! The Kindred promised us peace, and for the most part they have delivered it!'","Sirgon waves you over","Before you can learn anything, the guards call for you to step back","Now you can investigate the evidence coffer while Dax distracts the guards","Talk to Sirgon outside Rakhatâb","'The camp of Corsairs to the north-east lies in our path. Perhaps we can help the people here by thinning their numbers, and when we return they may have captured the one who did this. What do you say to this idea?'","Wait for Daxamat to run off","'Did anyone else see this man? Oh, it is terrible!'","Daxamat runs off to distract the guards.","Travel south along the coast to Rakhatâb","Meet up with your crew on the beach to the south-east of Rakhatâb","'Did you say you heard a Corsair might have done this? A tall man, with a dark beard? I am not surprised. Even after the rise of the Kindred of the Coins in Umbar Baharbêl, many of the Corsairs refused to swear oaths of peace and loyalty to the new order. Some of them are camped even now to the north-east along the coast, and sometimes they adventure here to Rakhatâb to cause problems for the workers.\
\
'Might one of them murdered this man? I think it likely.'","Folk in the crowd believe one of the Corsairs from the camp to the north-east, up the coastline, may be responsible for the brazen murder in Rakhatâb.","Defeated Corsairs in the Cape of Umbar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Something smells fishy, ${PLAYER}. If my brother were here he would say \\qit is the right of a Corsair to do as he likes!\\q and think nothing of it, but there is something about this situation that feels wrong to me. Perhaps I am just not as bold a Corsair as my brother.\
\
'But the camp of Corsairs to the north-east lies in our path. Perhaps we can help the people here by thinning their numbers, and when we return they may have captured the one who did this. What do you say to this idea?'","'What is the name of the next settlement along the merchant road to the south? Rakhatâb?\
\
'Then it is to Rakhatâb we must go.'","The coffer containing evidence taken from the victim of the murder in Rakhatâb is outside the keep, to the south-east.","Talk to Daxamat by the crowd in Rakhatâb"},
[3210]={"Has recogido madera de deriva (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Who was that woman, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'What? Cruel Dancer? You are joking!'","Talk to Caebar outside Rakhatâb","Find the woman Bôdo described atop the rocks north-east of Khûtra","'I do not think Cruel Dancer needs to worry that I might steal her bounties from her, but she has no way of knowing that.\
\
'I will remain alert, and I recommend that you do the same. She is notorious, in her own way, and if half of what I have heard of her is true... we may be in some trouble, ${PLAYER}. The murder of The Blade-twist has the effect of removing one of her competitors, but it is also a message to us, a warning to stay out of her way.'","Chapter 6.3: A Message From Cruel Dancer","'This is a poor time to visit this village, stranger. Ever since the great quake shook these lands and the temple on the hill sunk into the earth, an evil has taken the lands hereabout. Famine has come to Khûtra, and disease, and... suspicious folk.'\
\
He stares at you meaningfully. You ask if anyone who has come to the village lately might have inquired about a group such as yours, and he raises an eyebrow.\
\
'Could be so. Could be maybe not. I would have to ask some of my neighbours, and while I'm asking I'm not bringing crab legs back to Khûtra, or collecting driftwood along the shore with which we can smoke the meat and improve the flavour. With the famine going on, that's one of the only reliable sources of food around here, and it is barely edible.'","The bounty-hunter Cruel Dancer may be seeking to eliminate her competition and claim the bounties on the Kindred of the Coins for herself, which endangers Driftwood and any who associate with him.","'We meet again, ${PLAYER}. It is a pleasure to speak with you, as it was before. But you did not know my name then, did you?'\
\
The woman flings one arm dramatically outward and holds the back of her other hand over her eyes.\
\
'Murder! Murder! Is nowhere safe anymore? This poor man was slain, right here in the open! Oh, it is terrible!'\
\
She lowers her arms to her sides and laughs long and loudly.\
\
'It is remarkable how simple it is to make people see what they want to see. I had all the folk of Rakhatâb believing they saw a tall bearded Corsair stab a man to death, right there in the open. Oh, the murder was real enough, and The Blade-twist did not see it coming. Weep not for him. No bounty-hunter should live as long as he did and remain in service. I will have the good sense to hang up my own knife before there is more life behind me than ahead.\
\
'But I wanted to speak with you for a particular reason, ${PLAYER}. I would like to declare for ourselves a truce, and to work together where that is possible. The Blade-twist would share neither money nor information, and slay me with as little regard as I slew him; and that is familiar to me, and in this business that is right. But I observed you speaking with the man called Driftwood in Jax Phanâl, and I could not understand it. For what purpose did he ask you to help the people of that settlement? Not only for their silence. There was something else. I find that most interesting.\
\
'Let us consider the Kindred of the Coins our mutual foe, then? I will help you find them, ${PLAYER}. The bounties belong to me... but it seems to me that you seek them for... other reasons. So long as our aims do not conflict, you may count Cruel Dancer among your allies... if not among your friends. It seems to me you may have friends enough. I trust you chose them carefully?'","'I know what we do. We continue our journey. Our road leads to Umbar Baharbêl, and it seems there is a fishing village between here and the city, a village named Khûtra.","Bôdo told you a woman was looking for you, and could be found atop the rocks north-east of Khûtra.","Collect crab legs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You are not the only visitor to recently arrive at Khûtra. A woman there was, and she asked about folk such as those with whom you travel. I saw her again only moments ago, atop the rocks to the north-east.\
\
'I think she is waiting for you to go to her.'","'We have been through danger before, ${PLAYER}, and I have seen the horrors of war first-hand. What can Cruel Dancer do to me that I have not already suffered?\
\
'Still, we should remain alert. I would prefer she leave us alone. I looked into Saklaphêl's bounties not so I could claim one, but so I could learn what the Heirs of Castamir and the Kindred of the Coins were each, separately, hoping to accomplish, and whether that would endanger the lands across the Bay of Belfalas. I did not think such an inquiry would lead to anything like this, or a reunion with you!\
\
'I am grateful for the latter, of course.'","'There is one other who expressed an interest in the bounties posted by Saklaphêl, ${PLAYER}. Cruel Dancer will not know whether Driftwood's interest was real or just a pretense. He may now be in danger, and so may any who associate with him.'","Bôdo waits for you to return to him in the village of Khûtra.","Permanece alerta","Talk to the woman north-east of Khûtra","A woman has asked to speak with you atop the rocks north-east of Khûtra.","'You did as I asked? This surprises me, stranger.\
\
'The answer to your question is that yes, you are not the only visitor to recently arrive at Khûtra. A woman there was, and she asked about folk such as those with whom you travel. I saw her again only moments ago, atop the rocks to the north-east.\
\
'I think she is waiting for you to go to her.'","Collected crab legs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Driftwood outside Rakhatâb","'I would have to ask some of my neighbours for the information you want, and while I'm asking I'm not bringing crab legs back to Khûtra, or collecting driftwood along the shore with which we can smoke the meat and improve the flavour. With the famine going on, that's one of the only reliable sources of food around here, and it is barely edible.'","You were asked to collect things that may help Khûtra survive the famine with which it has been gripped in recent days.","Caebar is at the meeting spot outside Rakhatâb.","Talk to Bôdo in Khûtra","Collect driftwood along the beach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The village of Khûtra is north-east of Rakhatâb along the coast road that runs to the City of the Corsairs.","Bring the driftwood and crab legs to Bôdo in the village of Khûtra","'Cruel Dancer will not know whether Driftwood's interest was real or just a pretense. He may now be in danger, and so may any who associate with him.'","Travel to the village of Khûtra, north-east of Rakhatâb","You volunteer to do the work and he snorts noncommittedly","Cruel Dancer laughs again, and before you can follow her she is gone","The fisherman stares at you suspiciously, but says nothing","Bôdo is unsure what to make of your arrival to his village.","'What do we do now?'\
\
Caebar looks around nervously, and then surprises himself with a sudden laugh.\
\
'I know the answer, of course. We continue our journey. Our road leads to Umbar Baharbêl, and it seems there is a fishing village between here and the city, a village named Khûtra.\
\
'I do not think I am becoming any braver, ${PLAYER}, but it may be this adventure is making me more used to living through dangerous situations. Let us hope that continues to be so!'\
\
He looks around again.\
\
'But if you see Cruel Dancer lurking about, you will be sure to tell me, won't you?'","Driftwood is outside Rakhatâb.","The woman looks familiar to you, but you cannot determine why","Talk to Gimli north-east of the village of Khûtra","Gimli waits for you north-east of the village of Khûtra.","Cruel Dancer moves swiftly, and then she is gone."},
[3211]={"Ugrukhôr seeks knowledge of the artifact Bugdatish from Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, and Mithrandir has come to Felegoth seeking the same.","'Greetings to you, ${RACE}! Are you lost? Have you become like a barrel upon the Forest River, travelling from the Halls of the Elvenking downriver on your way to Lake-town? But alas! You have fetched up upon the bank, and now it falls to me to dislodge you with my long pole. Hold still and I will set you going again!'\
\
Nembadeth laughs merrily.\
\
'Pardon my jesting, friend, and tell me what brings you to Loeglond. I will set you going again with my words and not my staff, I promise you!'","Thranduil is in his throne room in Felegoth.","Talk to Thranduil in his throne room in Felegoth","Return to Thranduil in the throne room of Felegoth","Mithrandir sees you approach and knits his eyebrows together with concern","'We may have an advantage over Ugrukhôr of the Gúrzyul, ${PLAYER}, for the artifact Bugdatish might have been among those taken by my warriors when we departed Dol Guldur. The scholars of my realm are nearly finished with their study of these treasures. The Wizard Mithrandir has come to Felegoth and speaks with them even now.\
\
'Go to him in the Room of Study south-east of the throne room and learn if any of the artifacts could be the one prized by Ugrukhôr, or if any possess a connexion of some kind to Karazgar.'","King Thranduil eyes you carefully as you approach","Mithrandir asked you to inquire of Thranduil if the Bugdatish might have been part of Smaug's treasure-hoard.","Loeglond, the settlement of the Raft-elves, is in the Dale-lands along the river.\
\
Mithrandir suggested that you visit the Raft-elves on your way to Erebor, seeking news of Karazgar and the Bugdatish.","'The small hoard of relics taken from Dol Guldur is not the only such hoard that has come to this part of Middle-earth. Smaug himself assembled his own hoard of treasure, when he still lived, and when he died some part of it was divided into shares between dwarves and Men, and some came even to Thranduil's Elves. Might the Bugdatish have been a part of that treasure-hoard? Ask the Elvenking of this possibility, ${PLAYER}.'","Find Mithrandir and the scholars of Felegoth in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room","'The hoard and its treasures were divided among the victors following the death of Smaug; they were many and valuable, and included the Arkenstone and the Necklace of Girion. If the artifact Bugdatish had been contained within, it surely would have been accounted in the reckoning of shares. I think the artifact sought by Ugrukhôr cannot be traced to the dragon-hoard, but dwarves and Men may tell you otherwise.'","Mithrandir is in the throne room of Felegoth.","'Thranduil speaks truly. From the hoard he desired the Necklace of Girion, though he knew it not by that name; he coveted no other wealth, not even the Arkenstone. I have an idea about that, ${PLAYER}, but this is not the place to recount it. Suffice it to say that if the artifact Ugrukhôr desires did end up in the dragon-hoard, it is Erebor that must be searched, not Felegoth.'\
\
The Wizard lowers his voice so as not to be heard by Thranduil, and speaks to you in confidence.\
\
'Elves and dwarves have a long and demanding history, and they have often bickered over their treasures and perceived slights. Thranduil said it was the wisdom of Bard the Bowman that the Necklace of Girion be separated into its component gold and gems? He said too that it was Bard's wisdom that the gold and gems be given separately to dwarves and to Elves to repair their sundered bonds of friendship? Such was the advice I gave to Bard, ${PLAYER}! How often must Wizards repair the bridges burned between these two peoples?\
\
'But for now it seems the road leads from Felegoth. Make now for Loeglond, the settlement of the Raft-elves, and seek word of Karazgar and of the Bugdatish. I will follow shortly, and meet you at Erebor after I have concluded my own business with the Elvenking.'","Talk to Mithrandir in the throne room of Felegoth","Travel to Loeglond and seek tidings of Karazgar or the Bugdatish","Talk to Nembadeth at Loeglond","'I grew tired of waiting for news from you, ${PLAYER}, and prevailed upon Gwaihir to bring me hither! I spoke at once with Thranduil. His scholars have been sorting through the artifacts rescued from Dol Guldur, but they say they have not found what I seek. There is no wonder in that! How can they hope to find this artifact, this Bugdatish, while they know nothing of it? \\qSuch things do not come labelled for easy study,\\q they say to me. \\qPah!\\q I said to them, and now I say it to you, ${PLAYER}! Pah!\
\
'We may not know what form the Bugdatish might take, but if the Gúrzyul desire it so badly, I believe the thing will be enwreathed with a powerful aura. But these scholars insist they have not found such a relic in the small hoard of artifacts taken from Dol Guldur.'\
\
The Wizard pauses.\
\
'Hoard, did I say? That is not the only such hoard known in this part of Middle-earth. Smaug himself assembled his own hoard of treasure, when he still lived, and when he died it was divided into shares among dwarves and Men, and some came even to Thranduil's Elves. Might the Bugdatish have been a part of that treasure-hoard? Ask the Elvenking of this possibility, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Mithrandir in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room","'If the artifact Ugrukhôr desires did end up in the dragon-hoard, it is Erebor that must be searched, not Felegoth. Make now for Loeglond, the settlement of the Raft-elves, and seek word of Karazgar and of the Bugdatish. I will follow shortly, and meet you at Erebor after I have concluded my own business with the Elvenking.'","Chapter 6.3: Hidden in the Hoard","'Go to Mithrandir in the Room of Study and learn if any of the artifacts could be the one prized by Ugrukhôr, or if any possess a connexion of some kind to Karazgar.'","Mithrandir is meeting with the scholars of Felegoth in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room.","'Mithrandir has sent you back to me so quickly? Do the artifacts from Dol Guldur hold no answers to his questions, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You offer Thranduil the Wizard's suggestion that the artifact Bugdatish might have been a part of Smaug's treasure-hoard, unremarked-upon and unnoticed.\
\
'I do not like to speak of that hoard, ${PLAYER}, as Mithrandir knows. The dragon-sickness that lay upon it caused much trouble in the hearts of dwarves; indeed, even Men and Elves became embroiled in the fighting over it. The hoard and its treasures were divided among the victors following the death of Smaug; they were many and valuable, and included the Arkenstone and the Necklace of Girion. If the artifact Bugdatish had been contained within, it surely would have been accounted in the reckoning of shares.\
\
'The Arkenstone lies with Thorin Oakenshield in his tomb beneath the Mountain. I saw Bard lay it upon his breast myself. As for the Necklace of Girion, which I knew in elder days as the Gweriamir, it was made of gold and contained five hundred emeralds. It belonged then to the bride of my liege and disappeared for thousands of years until reappearing on the neck of King Thrór, as it should never have done. It was all I desired of the hoard. After the death of Smaug, the necklace went to Bard, but in his wisdom, the Bowman took the necklace apart and gave its gold to the dwarves and the jewels to my people, and so were those bonds repaired.\
\
'I think the artifact sought by Ugrukhôr cannot be traced to the dragon-hoard, but dwarves and Men may tell you otherwise.'"},
[3212]={"Durin has asked you to search Durshulot in Deepscrave to learn what you can about Gorgar the Ruthless and his rule of the Orcs.","'Do not let me keep you from the prince's duties. Aye, both his and mine can be accomplished at the same time!'","With a roar of anger, a ferocious Orc rushes to attack!","Durin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.\
\
You have recovered a number of readable documents that may shed light on Gorgar's rule of the Orcs within Gundabad, and should bring them to Prince Durin for his study.","Recover a litany of complaints from Orcs guarding the north-eastern approach to Durshulot","Talk to Durin at Maergrind in Máttugard","Recover a record of the takeover from Orcs guarding the north-western approach to Durshulot","'What is it, Trausti? What has brought you here with such haste?'","Trausti has suddenly arrived and called for your attention. What has happened?","'You found a great deal of information among the dwellings of the Orcs, I see! I shall peruse these as soon as I am able. I am not accustomed to... so much reading, and in such unpleasant Orkish handwriting, no less!\
\
'Still, I am sure there will be information of use within these papers, and I thank you for finding and delivering them to me.'","Chapter 6.3: Life on the Bridges","Bring the readable pages you recovered from Deepscrave to Durin at Maergrind","Among the papers you find a diary containing goblin scribbles","Trausti arrives suddenly and calls for your attention","Search the mess of assorted papers at a camp-fire inside Durshulot","'I beg you excuse my interruption, Prince Durin, but I bring urgent words for ${PLAYER}.\
\
'My student Eskil Bloodthumb has been captured by Orcs!'","Durin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.","Having searched Deepscrave on behalf of Stáli the Hewer, you should now continue to carry out your work for Prince Durin.","You found a record of the Frost-horde takeover","'I understand you have a report for the prince? Do not let me keep you, my reliable friend!\
\
'And continue to keep your eyes open for any relics that might be of interest to me!'","'You have returned from Deepscrave? How fares the Berg-beam?'\
\
You tell Durin what you observed during your investigation of the large cavern and the pillar of stone descending within it.\
\
'The Berg-beam remains strong, then? Good, good! For the Pillar of the Mountain to retain its stability even after so many centuries of Orc degradation seems a marvel to me. But perhaps it should not surprise me so, for I feel the presence of some enchantment upon the Mountain-home: an enchantment that preserves it from Orkish abasements. Have you not noticed the remarkable resilience of the walls of Gundabad, an unwillingness to suffer the marks of Orc-filth?\
\
'That may be so, but still the Orcs have lived beneath the mountain for many years, and the refuse in which they dwelt may hold useful information for those seeking to combat them. Scour their homes and persons in Deepscrave for useful records, and bring them to me when your search is done.'","You found a litany of Orkish complaints","An enraged Orc bellows with fury and moves to attack!","'Orcs have lived beneath this mountain for many years, and the refuse in which they dwelt may hold useful information for those seeking to combat them. Scour their homes and persons in Deepscrave for useful records, and bring them to me when your search is done.'","Talk to Trausti at Maergrind in Máttugard"},
[3213]={"Trausti is in a ramshackle dwelling along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave, searching for Eskil Bloodthumb.","You feel frightened eyes upon you","Trausti is on the north-western side of the Berg-beam in Deepscrave, near the site where Eskil Bloodthumb was left behind.","'It is my fault. I thought in my company the lad would be safe, and the experience would teach him a healthy caution while venturing in Orc-controlled caverns... but I was wrong. We were on the bridge that extends north-west of the Berg-beam when a party of Orcs attacked and overwhelmed us! I called for Eskil to shelter behind me, but in all the tumult I lost track of him. When I managed to get clear the Orcs were gone, and my student with them.'\
\
Trausti wrings his hands in frustration.\
\
'I also lost my axe during the fighting, the axe in which the golden tooth of my dear friend Lofrík was embedded. Will you help me rescue the young novice and find my cherished axe? If you agree, I will meet you back in Deepscrave when I have recovered a replacement weapon. Bah! No axe can replace the one I have lost, but one must serve!'","Trausti believes Eskil may have been brought through the Orc-village of Durshulot, perhaps to dwellings along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave.","Let loose a mighty <rgb=#00FF00>roar</rgb>!","'Don't hurt me! Don't hurt me! Vorhosh knows nothing, nothing, nothing!'\
\
When Trausti suggests that only an informative goblin-life is worth sparing, the goblin squeaks with terror and changes his tune.\
\
'Wait! Wait, I do know something, I do! You're looking for a dwarf? A captive dwarf, yes? I know where he was taken! Hashdurb's warriors brought him to Vatug-ronk, they did! He won't live for long in that pit, but he was alive when I saw him! Yes, he was, he was! Useful information! Useful!'","'I will meet you back in Deepscrave on the north-western side of the Berg-beam when I have recovered a replacement weapon. Bah! No axe can replace the one I have lost, but one must serve!'","Trausti has returned from Deepscrave with sad tidings: he and Eskil Bloodthumb were attacked and the inexperienced warrior was left behind.","'What did this goblin see? Does he know what happened to Eskil?'","The site of the attack is north-west of Trausti's location. What clues might it hold for Eskil's fate?","The site of the attack is in Deepscrave, north-west of Trausti's location. What clues might it hold for Eskil's fate?","Talk to Trausti in a ramshackle dwelling along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave","Talk to the frightened goblin","Talk to Trausti in the ramshackle dwelling on the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave","Search the site of the attack for clues to Eskil's fate","'That bridge is the way to Durshulot, and we know Eskil did not return to the Berg-beam. I think we can say this of Eskil's fate: it remains uncertain, but there is reason to hope for his survival! I think they shortened a length of rope in order to bind his hands, and he may have been brought alive to Durshulot, or perhaps to other Orkish dwellings along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave!\
\
'Let us search the north-eastern bounds of Deepscrave for further sign of the young novice... and for my axe as well.'","With a frightened squeak, a terrified goblin falls out of hiding","The site of the attack is to the north-west of Trausti's location.","'By all means, friend, you should seek to rescue Eskil Bloodthumb. Warrior or not, he is a part of the Gabil'akkâ and we will not abandon him to Orkish torment.'","'Ah, let him go, ${PLAYER}. We learned something useful, and there will be plenty of time to slay goblins later. If he was telling the truth, Eskil was alive when he was brought to Vatug-ronk. If we hurry, we may be able to keep him that way.'","Chapter 6.4: Eskil Ensnared","'Cowardly eyes are upon us, watching us from some hiding-place. Let us give their bearer a good scare and he may reveal himself.\
\
'Unleash a tremendous <rgb=#00FF00>roar</rgb>, ${PLAYER}. Let us inform this craven watcher we know of his presence!'","'Let us search the north-eastern bounds of Deepscrave for further sign of the young novice... and for my axe as well.'","Trausti is in the ramshackle dwelling along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave, musing over what you have learned.","The goblin is frightened!","Talk to Trausti at the Berg-beam in Deepscrave","Meet up with Trausti on the north-western side of the Berg-beam, in Deepscrave","'Unleash a tremendous <rgb=#00FF00>roar</rgb>, ${PLAYER}. We will teach this craven watcher a lesson!'","Search for Eskil Bloodthumb north-east of Durshulot, among dwellings along the outer wall of Deepscrave","Trausti has urged you to meet him in Deepscrave on the north-western side of the Berg-beam, in sight of where he lost Eskil Bloodthumb.","Orc-blood? Perhaps Eskil managed to injure his attackers","'Investigate the site of the attack and you may learn what befell the young novice, and if he yet lives.'","Talk to Trausti on the north-western side of the Berg-beam, in Deepscrave","'We were attacked just over there, to the north-west. There were many Orcs, more than I could count in the moment, and it was my impression that they were returning from somewhere. Aye, I felt we were not their purpose, though they were satisfied their path crossed with ours.\
\
'Investigate the site of the attack and you may learn what befell the young novice, and if he yet lives.'","Trausti is on the north-western side of the Berg-beam, near the site where Eskil Bloodthumb was left behind.","This short length of cord was cut from a longer rope, but for what reason?","Trausti thinks someone is lurking in the ramshackle dwelling, and if you <rgb=#00FF00>roar</rgb> you may be able to frighten him from his hiding-place.","A frightened goblin cowers in the ramshackle dwelling. Does he know anything about Eskil's fate?","The frightened goblin makes good his escape!"},
[3214]={"Kólfith nods at you, a welcome change from the other townsfolk","Your journey to Erebor searching for news of the Bugdatish or Karazgar the Gúrzyul continues through Lake-town.","'Karazgar? Too often have I heard that name. He is a constant source of trouble in these parts and seems often the well-spring from which our pains come, though he is rarely seen. Whether he buys his agents with coin or with promises I cannot say, but I am certain more hands than his own work our misfortunes. If you ask around town you may learn more. I wish you well, for Nembadeth's sake, but keep your wits about you. I do not want to tell her that the ${RACE} she sent to me met an unhappy end.'","Authi, the dwarf you befriended in the Dragonbone Inn, is just to the north of the tavern.","'The Men of Lake-town may know the names you seek, and I can help you gain their good graces! Travel to the front gate of Lake-town and introduce yourself to Várthrek. He is one of the guards there, and you will know him by his crimson hair and beard. Tell him you have come from Nembadeth of the raft-elves, and he will see you have whatever information you require. I helped him obtain from Felegoth a present for his young son, and he will help you in memory of my aid. Onward to Lake-town, friend barrel! I have dislodged you, and with my help, your course will be swift and sure!'","'The Men of Lake-town may know the names you seek, and I can help you gain their good graces! Travel to the front gate of Lake-town and introduce yourself to Várthrek. He is one of the guards there, and you will know him by his crimson hair and beard. Tell him you have come from Nembadeth of the raft-elves, and he will see you have whatever information you require. I helped him obtain from Felegoth a present for his young son, and he will help you in memory of my aid. Onward to Lake-town, friend barrel! I have dislodged you, and with my help your course will be swift and sure!'","The guards stare at you appraisingly","Talk to Authi Gem-cutter just north of the Dragonbone Inn","'You should be more careful with that name, friend. Folk are on edge hereabout, and it's said the Weeping Warrior has ears everywhere. I might know a thing or two about him you might find of use.'\
\
Kólfith peers into the shadows.\
\
'We should not speak of him here. Go to the Dragonbone Inn, here in town, and tell Fasti outside that you're a friend of Kólfith. We won't be disturbed there.'","Kólfith is on the lower level of Lake-town, just above the water.","As before, the townsfolk fall silent and wait for you to move on","'It was a fine brawl, but such fights are not as good for talking. We will be better able to talk here.'","Ask around Lake-town for tidings of Karazgar","Várthrek told you to ask the townsfolk of Lake-town for tidings of Karazgar.","Travel to the entrance of Lake-town","'We should not speak of the Warrior here. Go to the Dragonbone Inn, here in town, and tell Fasti outside that you're a friend of Kólfith. We won't be disturbed there.'","'These names are unfamiliar to me, friend. Karazgar? Bugdatish? Blame me for focusing on the river and my duties alone, but such curious words are the province of lords and princes, Wizards and adventurers, and not Nembadeth of the raft-elves. Trade is my charge, and in that I excel.\
\
'Still I wish to help you, and help you I shall! Most Elves have few dealings with the Men of the Lake, but the raft-elves cannot stand aloof if the trade is to continue! It may be the Men of Lake-town know the names you seek, and I can help you gain their good graces!\
\
'Travel to the front gate of Lake-town and introduce yourself to Várthrek. He is one of the guards there, and you will know him by his crimson hair and beard. Tell him you have come from Nembadeth of the raft-elves, and he will see you have whatever information you require. I helped him obtain from Felegoth a present for his young son, and he will help you in memory of my aid. Onward to Lake-town, friend barrel! I have dislodged you, and with my help, your course will be swift and sure!'","Kólfith wants to meet you inside the Dragonbone Inn, in the northern section of Lake-town. He asked you to speak with Fasti outside the inn to arrange a safe meeting.","The townsfolk lower their voices and eye you warily","Habla con Várthrek en la entrada de la Ciudad del Lago","'You are a friend of Kólfith? I will show you to a table inside where you can wait for him.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'¿Qué?'","Talk to Kólfith on the lower level of Lake-town, just above the water","Talk to Fasti outside the Dragonbone Inn and meet with Kólfith in secret","'Ho there, stranger. What brings you to Lake-town? I hope you intend no trouble here, for there is turmoil aplenty without adding to it.'\
\
You assure Várthrek you intend to cause no disruption, and Nembadeth of the raft-elves suggested you speak to Várthrek directly.\
\
'Ah, Nembadeth is a friend, and I trust her judgement, though she is more flighty than the others of her kind I have met, and seems more a woman of the Lake than an Elf of the Wood to me! She obtained a very smart wooden carving for my son Saevarr on his past birthday, and he prizes it above all. For Nembadeth I will help you as I may. What do you need, friend?'\
\
You ask Várthrek if he has heard tell of Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, and he grimaces.\
\
'Too often have I heard that name. He is a constant source of trouble in these parts and seems often the well-spring from which our pains come, though he is rarely seen. Whether he buys his agents with coin or with promises I cannot say, but I am certain more hands than his own work our misfortunes. If you ask around town you may learn more. I wish you well, for Nembadeth's sake, but keep your wits about you. I do not want to tell her that the ${RACE} she sent to me met an unhappy end.'","Lake-town is to the north-east of Loeglond.\
\
Nembadeth sent you to speak with Várthrek, a guard at the entrance to Lake-town.","Chapter 6.4: The Dragon's Bones"},
[3215]={"Meet up with your crew further ahead, beside the road to Umbar Baharbêl","'I am sorry. I will pull myself together. I will be fine.\
\
'You say Legolas intended to visit the wreckage of a tower? I believe that is Calatirion, on the hill of Kharn Arâx, to the south-west.'","Travel south-west where you can have a view of the Calatirion's wreckage","'There our destination lies!'","Defeated Dead outside the ruined temple of Sauron (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'There it lies. Calatirion.'","Defeat the Dead outside the ruined temple of Sauron (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah, I had thought to help the people of Khûtra with their difficulties, but as I approached the temple I could not bring myself any nearer than this. Thank you for helping them combat these evils.'\
\
Sirgon sighs heavily, a sound you have become accustomed to ever since the man who was once the Lord of Lebennin came ashore upon the Shield Isles.\
\
'I quail at the sight of the Dead, ${PLAYER}, but there is something I fear even more than such as they, and it is a fear that takes the shape of a Man. I fear the meeting with Belondor that surely awaits me in the city ahead. I fear what he will have to say to me, but worst of all: I fear that I may deserve it.\
\
'The Steward Denethor gave me the command to bring Belondor to justice, but I did not refuse it. When I believed I drove him to his death I felt the shame and the guilt of that pursuit, but to learn that he rose from the waves, that he survived... my shame and my guilt are doubled. Nay, they are trebled. And now he is one of those who leads the Kindred of the Coins against Gondor!\
\
'I am sorry. I will pull myself together. I will be fine. You say Legolas intended to visit the wreckage of a tower? I believe that is Calatirion, on the hill of Kharn Arâx, to the south-west.'","Talk to Legolas in view of the wreckage of Calatirion","Atop its hill, the tower of Calatirion has tumbled into several pieces","Your crew plans to meet on the road to Umbar Baharbêl, and you should join them.","Daxamat stands by the road to Umbar Baharbêl with the rest of your crew.","Chapter 6.4: The Temple and the Tower","The Dead that linger near the ruined temple of Sauron to the east will endanger any who travel to the City of the Corsairs.","'If Cruel Dancer will help us track the location of the Kindred of the Coins, I suppose we cannot turn down her help... but I do not like it! And yet no one asked for my thoughts on the subject, ${PLAYER}, did they?\
\
'But I was looking for you. Several members of the crew were speaking with the folk of Khûtra, and there was a lot of talk about problems further up the road. Some form of festering blight has taken hold of the land to the north-east, and before you can say \\qbest leave well enough alone,\\q Sirgon volunteered to do something about it. He is probably up there right now!\
\
'You should go deal with the Dead that have been reported near the ruins of the temple, ${PLAYER}, unless you think Sirgon can handle himself. Afterward you might want to check on Legolas. He said something about seeing an old tower that fell down in this area some years ago. He said the name of it, but who can remember the Elf-names for such things? It is not like dwarf-names! Now those are easy to recall!'","'This was the beacon-tower of Calatirion, ${PLAYER}, constructed by Elendil as a mighty monument of Númenor. I have heard tales from Glorfindel of the Vandassar that stood within it for much of its history, Airessar, as clear as crystal, shining so brightly it could be seen even from far off in the bay.\
\
'I know it was destroyed by the Bright Company to loosen Sauron's bonds upon the Men of Harad during the War of the Great Alliance. The tower itself survived that battle, and would stand for almost three thousand more years, but it would not stand forever. When the Church of the All-Seeing came to Umbar in the vanguard of the Empire of Ordâkh, there were servants of that church who resented that which Calatirion represented; they were the Nazgûl, with the Forsaken Reaver at their head. With sorcery he and his allies toppled the tower, and the memory of that day has lived on in whisper ever since. Even Glorfindel wished not to speak of it, but he told me the name by which folk of Umbar recall that day: Mût Tadaul, the Death of Light.\
\
'The Forsaken Reaver must have perished with his master when Frodo cast the Ring into the Cracks of Doom, ${PLAYER}. But Calatirion remains toppled. It is a reminder to me that evil deeds are not undone by the destruction of those who wrought them.\
\
'We should continue to the east and then north along the road. We have almost reached the city.'","The wreckage of Calatirion on the hill of Kharn Arâx can be found to the south-west.","Sirgon has come as near to the ruined temple of Sauron as he wishes.","'We are almost there!\
\
'The journey nears its end... and we are still alive, which is more than I expected, if I am being honest with you!'","Legolas looks up at the wreckage of Calatirion, musing about what he has been told of its history.","The road to Umbar Baharbêl runs by two places of significance for the region: the temple of Sauron and the wreckage of Calatirion. Either may pose the threat of watchful guards.","'You should go deal with the Dead that have been reported near the ruins of the temple, ${PLAYER}, unless you think Sirgon can handle himself. Afterward you might want to check on Legolas. He said something about seeing an old tower that fell down in this area some years ago. He said the name of it, but who can remember the Elf-names for such things? It is not like dwarf-names! Now those are easy to recall!'","Talk to Daxamat by the road to Umbar Baharbêl","Talk to Sirgon outside the ruined temple of Sauron"},
[3216]={"'I am as concerned as any of my people about this worrying decline in the skill of the artisans, but I do not know what can be done about it. Dáin before me also did not have a solution. Do you and Gandalf have a suggestion, ${PLAYER}? I am willing to hear any proposal, but I am not confident any solution can be found.'","Travel to the Lonely Mountain, north of Dale, and meet with Authi","Authi Gem-cutter has shared some of his own problems with you and invited you to the Lonely Mountain where you may learn more about your own charge.","'I will meet you at the Lonely Mountain, my new friend!'","'Ah, you know Gandalf? How fortunate for my people that he has come to investigate this decline in our craft-skill!'","'Most of the surviving members of Thorin's Company have come to Erebor, driven by their concerns. Their worries may align with our own, ${PLAYER}.'","'I do not know what has caused this decline in the craft-skill of Durin's Folk, ${PLAYER}. Neither do I know whether entombing the Arkenstone with Thorin Oakenshield is to blame for it, but my suspicion is that it is not. There is another possibility, and in it I see the workings of our enemy.\
\
'What if the Arkenstone has been taken from the tomb of Thorin without the knowledge of the dwarves? It may be that the Arkenstone no longer lies with Thorin Oakenshield, and its departure has adversely affected the skills of Durin's Folk.\
\
'The tomb must be opened, ${PLAYER}, if we are to ensure the Arkenstone remains within. We must ask King Thorin III for permission to do this.'","Habla con Dwalin","'The tomb must be opened, ${PLAYER}, if we are to ensure the Arkenstone remains within. We must ask King Thorin III for permission to do this.'","Talk to Gandalf in the Hall Under the Mountain","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain","Chapter 6.5: Decline and Decay","Authi is not alone. Gandalf stands nearby, and beckons to you","A number of Thorin Oakenshield's surviving companions have come to Erebor","Gandalf has come to Erebor, and he stands outside the entrance to the Hall Under the Mountain.","'You and Authi are not the only recent arrivals to the Lonely Mountain. You will find a number of old friends inside, each of them brought hither from concern. Find them on the way to the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain and you may learn their purpose matches our own.'","Authi Gem-cutter invited you to go to Erebor to consult with King Thorin about the mysterious decline in the craft-skill of the dwarves. He said he would meet you at the Lonely Mountain.","'I invite you to go to Erebor and share what you have learned of the Weeping Warrior with King Thorin. It may be that our problems are related! I encourage you to slay some beasts on the way, my friend. I will as well, and see you there!'","Gandalf is in the Hall Under the Mountain near several dwarves of Thorin's Company who have come to Erebor.","Defeat beasts on the way to the Lonely Mountain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find the visitors Gandalf mentioned on the way to the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain","Habla con Glóin","Talk to Dori","'My travels do not bring me home to Erebor very often, for Dáin made me the Mountain's chief hoard-seeker. I am often away, wandering in the wilderness in search of lost dwarf-holds and treasure-caches. Many are the gold and jewels I have found to swell Erebor's treasuries, but the fading craft-skill of my people means they languish within, unimproved and unused. It is a terrible pity!\
\
'Should the Arkenstone be taken from the tomb of Thorin? Would that restore the craft-skill of my people, and enable them to create great works such as they did of old? I once thought so, but I set aside that belief when my younger brother Ori departed with Balin. The argument filled me with sadness, and I had a job to do. I could not dwell upon the grief. Perhaps the decline of my people could not be prevented, Arkenstone or no.\
\
'I am pleased to see my friends and kinsmen, but I do not think we can recapture our glories of old.'","'I prefer when things are simple, ${PLAYER}. Should we not have entombed the Arkenstone with Thorin? It seemed the right course back then, and no one argued against it. If the craft-skill of my people is fading, who is to say it would be any different if the Arkenstone were not sealed away? Bah! Let the wise-beards discuss it among themselves. Balin believed the Arkenstone should be removed from Thorin's tomb, and he was the wisest of us. But he is dead.\
\
'Now, this Weeping Warrior... that is a subject more to my liking! I say we find him, let our axes and hammers do the talking, and give him something to cry about. Nice and simple. It may not solve everything, but I wager it would not hurt. Not us, anyway.'","'I like you, ${PLAYER}. You are good in a fight, that much is clear! Are you also good at holding things in confidence?'\
\
You assure Authi that you will not betray his trust, and he tugs on his beard thoughtfully.\
\
'I have worked at my craft for a long time, ${PLAYER}. My father and my brothers are jewellers of no small skill, celebrated throughout all the kingdoms of the dwarves, and I too have achieved no small success in that field. For dozens of years, the Gem-cutters had no equal, and the pieces we crafted were so fair even the most judgmental eye could be made to weep at their beauty. You should have seen them, my new friend!\
\
'But something has been happening for the past few years. None of my efforts of late have achieved the same level of success as my earlier work. None of my pieces seem to sparkle as they once did, and others of my kind report a similar waning of their craft-skill. What is happening to Durin's Folk? There is some discussion underway at Erebor, and few can agree on the cause. I have taken to wandering, trying to come up with an explanation for this decay; I was on my way back to the Mountain when we met, ${PLAYER}. I had found no solution, but your quest has given me an idea.\
\
'Could it be that Karazgar is responsible for this decline of our craft-skill? He is active in the area and has no love for Durin's Folk. Perhaps he has worked some evil against us? I invite you to go to Erebor and share what you have learned of the Weeping Warrior with King Thorin. It may be that our problems are related! I encourage you to slay some beasts on the way, my friend. I will as well, and see you there!'","Authi Gem-cutter invited you to go to Erebor to consult with King Thorin about the mysterious decline in the craft-skill of the dwarves. He asked you to defeat troublesome beasts on the way to the Lonely Mountain.","Talk to Gandalf at the Lonely Mountain","Gandalf hinted that some old friends could be found on the way to the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.","'At last you arrive! I have been waiting here for some time now. Authi arrived before you did, and he told me all about your exploits in Lake-town. Perhaps if you spent less time carousing at taverns and more time riding, you would not have kept me waiting so long in the cold!'\
\
The Wizard's tone is gruff, but his eyes sparkle merrily.\
\
'You and Authi are not the only recent arrivals to the Lonely Mountain. You will find a number of old friends inside, each of them brought hither from concern. Find them on the way to the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain and you may learn their purpose matches our own.\
\
'One more thing, ${PLAYER}. In these lands I am known as Gandalf, and not Mithrandir. Let it not confuse you!'","Defeated beasts as a favour for Authi Gem-cutter (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It has been some time since we have all gathered here. It does my heart good to see my friends and distant kin, despite the worries that drew us here. I wish my brother was with us.'\
\
Dwalin sighs heavily.\
\
'Balin believed, as did many good dwarves, that it had been a mistake for the Arkenstone to be entombed with Thorin. He thought the Heart of the Mountain should be proudly displayed, for all to see, and its brilliance would inspire great works of craft and beauty. As the craft-skill of Durin's Folk began to wane, the research Balin conducted convinced him that sealing away the Arkenstone was to blame. He quarreled with Dáin on the matter, and this disagreement caused the King to remove him as counsellor. It was the last injury, and compelled Balin to leave. He took Ori and Óin, as well as many other dwarves, and they sought to reclaim the ancient Dwarf-home of Khazad-dûm.\
\
'I did not side with my brother on this. I remained loyal to Dáin. He elevated me to my position as Steward of Thorin's Hall, but not a day passes where I do not miss my brother and wonder if I should have gone with him. But now Balin is gone, and Khazad-dûm is lost.'","King Thorin III is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.","As Gandalf hinted, a number of Thorin Oakenshield's companions have come to Erebor. What has drawn them here?"},
[3217]={"Talk to Trausti near the base of the Berg-beam","Talk to Eskil Bloodthumb at Maergrind in Máttugard","Talk to Trausti and attempt to rescue Eskil Bloodthumb","'There's nothing for it. I signed a contract to serve as Stáli's apprentice, and wherever he sees fit to send me, there I have to go. You saved me this time, but how often can I count on you to rescue me? I will surely die down here, ${PLAYER}!'","'And keep your eyes open for my axe as well.'","Trausti has suggested that you meet with him at the base of the Berg-beam, at the lowest level of Deepscrave.","Habla con Fastrith Halcomida en Maergrind, en Matugarde","Trausti stands here, surveying the dirt floor of Deepscrave as you approach","Trausti is near the base of the Berg-beam, ready to rescue Eskil Bloodthumb.","Chapter 6.5: Eskil's Escape","You have rescued Eskil Bloodthumb and returned him safely to Maergrind in Máttugard, where he waits to speak with you.","Eskil's sister Fastrith looks at you thoughtfully","Meet up with Trausti by the base of the Berg-beam","'We are here.'","Eskil's sister Fastrith Hawkfeast has asked to speak to you.","'I do not know much about Vatug-ronk, the Groaning Pit, but if that is where the Orcs brought my young novice, that is where we need to go! I believe the pit is on the very lowest level of Deepscrave. Let us meet at the base of the Berg-beam, and then we will decide our next course of action.'","'Well, I thank you again for the rescue, ${PLAYER}, but I think this experience has taught me one thing. I am simply not cut out for the adventuring life. I am no warrior!'\
\
Eskil sighs unhappily.\
\
'But there's nothing for it. I signed a contract to serve as Stáli's apprentice, and wherever he sees fit to send me, there I have to go. You saved me this time, but how often can I count on you to rescue me? I will surely die down here, ${PLAYER}!'","Trausti is at the base of the Berg-beam, preparing for the rescue of Eskil Bloodthumb.","According to the frightened goblin you discovered, Eskil Bloodthumb may have been brought to Vatug-ronk, the Groaning Pit. Trausti is eager to rescue him without delay.","'We are here. Are you prepared to search Vatug-ronk with me for our abducted friend? Let me know when you are ready.'","'I do not know much about Vatug-ronk, the Groaning Pit, but if that is where the Orcs brought the young novice, that is where we need to go!\
\
'I believe the pit is on the very lowest level of Deepscrave. Let us meet at the base of the Berg-beam, and then we will decide our next course of action.'","'Might I have a moment of your time, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'It is clear to me... and I suspect to all!... that my brother is not well-suited for the life of a warrior, but it is also obvious to me that Stáli his master cares little for the dangers into which he sends his apprentice. Eskil needs to obey his master's commands for the duration of his apprenticeship, but were he to somehow slip free of Stáli's contract he would have no further obligation. It might save his life, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Will you help me find some loophole in their agreement, some means of freeing my brother from the servitude that will surely lead to his doom? Tell me you will!'"},
[3218]={"'So this is the City of the Corsairs. I am a long way from home, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Caebar frowns, and you know he is remembering the cold welcome he received from his family and the other folk of Ethring.\
\
'I suppose my home is not what it used to be. I am here at the command of King Elessar, and to help my friends as I can. For those two purposes... I would travel anywhere.\
\
'The rest of the crew will be somewhere within the city now, searching for information that will aid us in the rescuing of Thorongil and your Elf-friend. You will need to search the several districts of the city if you are to find them, I think: the Fleet-fast, the Upper and Lower Wards, and the Sail-haven, at least! I will see you at one of the markets in the Sail-haven when you have learned what there is to be learned!'","'So this is the City of the Corsairs. I am a long way from home.'","You have arrived at Umbar Baharbêl, the City of the Corsairs","Talk to Caebar by the Beacon Gate","Everyone takes their leave and goes to enter the city separately","Complete 'The City: The Eyes of Nauriel'","The crew separates and prepares to enter the city by different paths.","Enter Umbar Baharbêl by the Beacon Gate, which leads to the Sail-haven","Caebar said he would meet you at one of the markets in the Sail-haven when you have learned what your crew discovered.","Talk to Caebar at a market in the Sail-haven","Chapter 6.5: The City of the Corsairs","Your crew has split up to search Umbar Baharbêl for information that will aid in the rescue of Thorongil and the completion of your mission.","'I hope the rest of the crew learned something valuable, ${PLAYER}, for I have had a hard time of it. I leaned out over one of the railings and studied the Citadel of Winds from afar, but that place seems to be a fortress, and impregnable. I cannot think of any way we will get inside, if that is where the Kindred of the Coins is holding the prisoners.\
\
'I am sorry, I am feeling rather out of sorts. Someone bumped into me right before you arrived, and I almost fell. Folk should watch where they are going!'","Your mission nears its end. Thorongil and Corudan are sure to be held somewhere within Umbar Baharbêl, just down the coast road.","Complete 'The City: The Short Straw'","Complete 'The City: Elves, Dwarves, and Trouble'","Complete 'The City: Sirgon's Wound'","'The rest of the crew will be somewhere within the city now, searching for information that will aid us in the rescuing of Thorongil and your Elf-friend. You will need to search the several districts of the city if you are to find them, I think: the Fleet-fast, the Upper and Lower Wards, and the Sail-haven, at least! I will see you at one of the markets in the Sail-haven when you have learned what there is to be learned!'","Caebar has entered Umbar Baharbêl by the Beacon Gate on the north-western side of the city.","You will enter the city by the Beacon Gate, which provides entrance to the north-western area of the city.","'I am no strategist, ${PLAYER}, but even I know we are likely to attract unwelcome attention if we approach the city as a group. What do you think?'\
\
You advise your crew to split up and enter the City of the Corsairs by separate gates.\
\
'That is a good idea! We will all meet up after we have learned what we can inside the city. Until then, farewell! And be careful!'","Wait for your crew to disperse","Complete 'The City: Sigileth's Curiosity'"},
[3219]={"Caebar is in the Sail-haven.","Find the lamp nearest the crocodiles, on the rocks to the west","Examine another toppled lamp to the west along the rocks","Cruel Dancer waves you over to her","Cruel Dancer spoke of crocodiles outside the city, and Caebar believes she means the ones that can be found to the south-east.","'I am glad you received my message. I wondered after I left it if perhaps I was too subtle for the scribe to realize it had been given to him.\
\
'Our shared purpose is almost complete, ${PLAYER}. The line of lamps indicates the way to a secret harbour used by certain members of the Kindred of the Coins. I have reason to believe your prisoners are held within, and several of the bounties upon the Kindred are ripe for me to claim.'","The toppled lamp to the west of the crocodiles merits some examination.","A lamp lies overturned here upon the rocks","Talk to Caebar in the Sail-haven","Cruel Dancer spoke of lamps in the night, somewhere near the crocodiles.","Another lamp lies to the west.","Find the camp of crocodiles to the south-east of the city","Before this lamp was overturned, it may have guided ships along the river","Caebar has had a close encounter with Cruel Dancer, but did not realize it at the time. What has the dangerous bounty-hunter discovered that may be of use to you?","You feel eyes upon you. Someone watches from the west","'Do you think it means she's found a way to the prisoners? Lamps in the night? Crocodiles?'\
\
Caebar thinks it over.\
\
'I heard the crocodiles to the south-east of the city have been a problem for merchants trying to go that way. Maybe that is where we should start? But it sounds like only one of us should go? That must be you, right? Tell me that you think she means you!'\
\
You assure Caebar that you will investigate the crocodiles outside the city by yourself, and he should continue his efforts in the Sail-haven. He breathes a sigh of relief and wishes you well.","Caebar handed you the note he discovered in his pocket, and you should read it.","'I gave you the note! What do you think it means?'","Cruel Dancer is west of the line of lamps, standing upon the rocks overlooking the river.","Confront the person watching you to the west of the line of lamps","Someone watches you from the rocks to the west of the line of lamps.","Now where are these broken lamps?","Talk to Cruel Dancer by the coil of rope","Read the note Caebar discovered on his person","Examine the toppled lamp","Chapter 6.6: Lamps In the Night","'Why are you staring at me like that?'\
\
You encourage Caebar to check his belongings, concerned that he might have fallen victim to a pickpocket. He frantically searches his clothes for his money-purse.\
\
'Here it is, thank goodness; but as light as it ever is, I am sorry to say. But what is this?'\
\
He retrieves an unfamiliar scrap of parchment from one of his pockets, and his eyes go wide as he reads the message written on it.\
\
'It is a message from Cruel Dancer!' he whispers, handing it to you.","'I heard the crocodiles to the south-east of the city have been a problem for merchants trying to go that way. Maybe that is where you should start?"},
[3220]={"Your search proves fruitless, revealing no sign of Eskil's contract","Habla con Fastrith Halcomida en Zarkul-sulûn","Talk to Eskil Bloodthumb in Zarkul-sulûn","This chest contains many papers, but none bearing Eskil's name","'Yes, yes. Remember that I am doing all of you a favour.'","You find no sign of Eskil's contract","Section the Third: Ending the Agreement\
==========================\
This agreement shall be binding for each of the listed parties, Apprentice and Sculptor alike, and it shall continue in effect until such time as Sculptor delivers to Dáin II, King Under the Mountain, a signed parchment containing the desire of both parties to terminate it. Without such a delivery, this agreement will continue in perpetuity.\
\
May it be a fruitful and satisfactory apprenticeship for both parties!\
\
Witnessed on this day the Third of October,\
in the Year 3018,\
with seals affixed,\
in the Hall Under the Mountain,\
by Dáin II Ironfoot,\
King Under the Mountain","Fastrith coughs politely","'Stáli has not fully moved into Gundabad yet, and his luggage remains in Zarkul-sulûn. What do you say to searching his baggage for my brother's contract, and studying it for some loophole that will free Eskil from his service? If you go at once, we can do our best to keep Stáli from learning of this regrettable, but necessary, intrusion!'","Stáli the Hewer arrives, a shrewd look on his face. Fastrith and Eskil follow at a distance","'I thought I saw you here, friend. I returned to Zarkul-sulûn to bring more dwarves and supplies back with me to Gundabad. We can walk back together.'","Examine Eskil's contract","Talk to Stáli the Hewer upstairs in Zarkul-sulûn","Bueno...","'I suppose...'","<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Zarkul-sulûn when you accept this quest.</rgb>\
\
'Aye, that's the spirit! There must be some way to free my brother from this dangerous apprenticeship. Who could have anticipated that working for a sculptor would send him among such Orc-infested dangers? Mere months ago, when he agreed to work for Stáli, I thought the worst of his worries would be living up to his epithet of Bloodthumb!\
\
'By hitting his thumb with a chisel, ${PLAYER}, that's what I mean. You get it? Lovely.\
\
'Anyway, Stáli has not fully moved into Gundabad yet, and his luggage remains in Zarkul-sulûn. What do you say to searching his baggage for my brother's contract, and studying it for some loophole that will free Eskil from his service? If you go at once, we can do our best to keep Stáli from learning of this regrettable, but necessary, intrusion!'","Chapter 6.6: The Fine Print","Section the First: Duties of the Apprentice\
===========================\
The duties of the Apprentice shall not be limited in any way by the omission of any particular duty in this section, but shall be deemed to include any such reasonable responsibilities that shall be suggested by the Sculptor. The meaning of \\qreasonable\\q for this section, and for any following section, shall be interpreted as \\qthe course most likely to be favoured by the will of Dáin II, King Under the Mountain.\\q\
\
The duties of the Apprentice shall include, but be not limited to, the following responsibilities:\
\
One (1): Acquisition of materials for the creation of any works of art required by the Sculptor, purchased with supplied coin. Any excess coinage is to be returned promptly and without fail. Upon discovery of such a failure, the excess will be tallied and deducted from the Apprentice's weekly stipend (see Section the Second).\
\
Two (2): Thorough weekly cleaning of workshop space in order to foster creative work on the part of the Sculptor. Any spots missed in the cleaning shall be tallied and a percentage deducted from the Apprentice's weekly stipend (see Section the Second).\
\
Three (3): Timely preparation of meals for the Sculptor, no earlier than eight in the morning for breakfast and no later than six of the clock for dinner; drinks to be made upon request. The Sculptor does not like berries of any kind on his plate, but he is partial to honey and any products made from it, such as mead. The appearance of berries anywhere near the Sculptor's table will be noted, and a deduction made from the Apprentice's weekly stipend (see Section the Second).\
\
Four (4): Praise to be made for the Sculptor's work (when appropriate). Private criticism of such work will be noted, and a deduction made from the Apprentice's weekly stipend (see Section the Second). Public criticism will be noted twice, and count double.\
\
Five (5): In the event of illness or maiming that causes the Apprentice to be unable to carry out his duties, be they daily or weekly in nature, he is to provide a substitute for the day or week in question. If the substitute is found lacking, such deficiency will be noted and a deduction made from the Apprentice's weekly stipend (see Section the Second). Similarly, if the Apprentice is deemed to be contagious and refuses to nominate a substitute, that will also be grounds for a deduction from his weekly stipend.\
\
Six (6): Greeting guests of the Sculptor and assessing who is to be admitted and who is deemed unwelcome. The Sculptor's time is valuable and not to be wasted! Special consideration is to be given to those who bring gifts for the Sculptor, especially mead. The discovery that mead might have been given as a gift should the guest have been informed beforehand by the Apprentice will be met with disappointment, which is worse than anger. Disappointment in this case will take the form of a deduction from the Apprentice's weekly stipend (see Section the Second).","'What do you think, ${PLAYER}? I believe we could argue that despite the specific references to King Dáin, it was always intended that his part in the agreement should transfer to any King Under the Mountain that should follow him. After all, this agreement was created with war already visible upon the horizon, and King Dáin was not one to shy away from conflict! Perhaps if we petition King Thorin Stonehelm...'\
\
Fastrith shakes her head.\
\
'No, it is too long a journey back to Erebor, and I know Stáli would not agree to make it. I would need to take the journey, and my brother would remain endangered by his master's whims while I made the trip. We need a more immediate remedy, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Wait. What about that section there, where Eskil is obligated to nominate a substitute to carry out his duties in the event that he becomes ill or... maimed...? He still has all his limbs, praise Durin, but I would say he is indeed sick... sick of carrying out such dangerous errands for his master! But who can replace my brother in his apprenticeship until we can petition King Thorin to cancel the agreement? I know just the person!'\
\
Fastrith stares at you, challenge lighting a fire in her eyes.\
\
'Me, ${PLAYER}, I speak of myself! I will do it! I am not afraid of a few Orcs, and I have always been more courageous than my brother, dear though he is to me. And I would not mind learning what I might about sculpting, either. What does Stáli have to say about this?'","Hmmm....","Stáli brandishes the contract with a flourish","Hmmm?","Stáli the Hewer has returned to Zarkul-sulûn.","'I suppose....'","Eskil Bloodthumb stands on the upper level of Zarkul-sulûn, looking resigned to his fate.","'It sounds bad, ${PLAYER}, doesn't it?\
\
'I'm thinking, but I see no way out of it! Does it really say that the only way to get out of the contract is to deliver a signed paper to King Dáin? But he is dead! He died at the gates of the Lonely Mountain during the siege that ended the war before this one!\
\
'I suppose there is nothing to be done. I will be bound to this apprenticeship until my dying day... and that could very well be THIS day, or at the very latest on the morrow!'","Talk to Durin on the lower level of Zarkul-sulûn","Fastrith Hawkfeast stands on the upper level of Zarkul-sulûn, seeking to gain your attention.","You hear footsteps approaching.","'A substitute apprentice? I don't know about this... I have become quite fond of the lad, after all. But now that you mention it, the meals he made were always undercooked, and he never cleaned the corners of my workshop as thoroughly as he should have....\
\
'Fine! I accept Eskil's sister Fastrith as my apprentice in his stead, but I will deduct a portion of her weekly stipend to cover my inconvenience! I am doing you all a favour! Don't expect another!\
\
'And this is what I expect: for Fastrith to find me the Zabad'ibîn wherever they have been taken! Only then will I be happy about this!'","Section the Second: Duties of the Sculptor\
===========================\
The duties of the Sculptor shall only include responsibilities here listed. This is their full extent:\
\
One (1): The Sculptor shall provide a weekly stipend of coin to the Apprentice, modified as described above in Section the First.\
\
Two (2): The Sculptor shall provide instruction in the art of sculpting and the preparation of fine artwork (as time allows and at the Sculptor's inclination, informed by whether the Apprentice displays a natural propensity for the subject. This propensity is to be assessed by the Sculptor and by no other, save the King Under the Mountain, should the Apprentice choose to frivolously spend the king's time in this manner).","Stáli the Hewer is on the upper level of Zarkul-sulûn.","Stáli the Hewer has returned to Zarkul-sulûn, and he holds Eskil's contract out for your study.","Fastrith Hawkfeast is interested in finding some way to free her brother Eskil Bloodthumb from his apprenticeship to Stáli the Hewer.","Well...?","Talk to Stáli the Hewer in Zarkul-sulûn","Prince Durin is on the lower level of Zarkul-sulûn.","Search Stáli's luggage for Eskil Bloodthumb's contract","'I know why you're here, ${PLAYER}, and if you think I have to release my apprentice from his obligations, you are gravely mistaken!\
\
'Study the contract if you like! I have it right here, for I keep such things on my person at all times... you never know when someone might try to make such a binding agreement \\qmysteriously\\q vanish!'","With that settled, you should speak with Durin downstairs before returning to Gundabad","Stáli the Hewer's luggage can be found upstairs in Zarkul-sulûn.","You hear footsteps approaching","'It is a perfect solution!'","Preamble and Naming of the Parties\
========================\
Let it be known to all in the Lonely Mountain and its environs, and to every inhabitant of dwarfdom throughout this Middle-earth, that on this the third day of October, Dáin II Ironfoot, King Under the Mountain, did recognize and witness this agreement between two parties come before him.\
\
The parties are named as follows, with due identification presented and accepted in the sight of King Dáin. Party the first: Stáli the Hewer, noted sculptor and artist of great renown, resident of Tumnu-dûm, the dwelling-halls, known herein as the Sculptor. Party the second: Eskil Bloodthumb, noteworthy accomplishments asked for by the first party but none were offered by the second and are therefore omitted; also a resident of Tumnu-dûm, the dwelling-halls, known herein as the Apprentice.\
\
As a matter of course, the King Under The Mountain expressed his opinion that the parties enter into this agreement of apprenticeship of their own free wills, and that no undue influence was exercised upon either party."},
[3221]={"'These are my cousins, come from afar. Dwalin is the Steward of Thorin's Hall, in the Blue Mountains, and Glóin acts as emissary for the King Under the Mountain.\
\
'The conversation has left me parched. If I am to entertain visitors, I will need more water to refresh me.'\
\
Dís gives you a meaningful look, and you volunteer to bring up some water from the well at the base of the hill.","Cleared brush from the path (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You volunteered to bring water from the well at the base of Raven-hill to Dís.","'Yes?'\
\
Dís stares at you, but says nothing more. Hesitantly, you begin to ask about the Arkenstone, but before you can properly word the request she interrupts you.\
\
'The Heart of the Mountain? It lies with my brother Thorin beneath the Mountain. I have not visited him in some time.'\
\
She looks at you slyly.\
\
'The path down the hill is choked with brush and stones. Someone should do something.'\
\
You offer to clear the path, and Dís grunts noncommittally.","'You wish to open the tomb of Thorin Oakenshield and ensure the Arkenstone remains within? None could have breached the tomb without our knowledge, ${PLAYER}. And yet, even as I speak these words, I am gripped with uncertainty. If the Heart of the Mountain has been taken, it might explain the diminishment of our craft-skill....'\
\
The King Under the Mountain strokes his beard thoughtfully.\
\
'Yes, ${PLAYER}, we should learn if the Arkenstone still lies within the tomb or if some enemy has taken it. I alone cannot give you leave to open the tomb of Thorin Oakenshield, though I am King Under the Mountain and possess lordship of all that lies within. It would not be proper to open Mazal Akrâz without the permission of Thorin's sister, Dís. Her children also lie in that place, and I would not have their rest or that of her brother disturbed without her leave.\
\
'She is the Keeper of Raven-hill, ${PLAYER}, and that is where you will find her. Speak to her and learn if she will allow the tomb to be opened.'","'The conversation has left me parched. If I am to entertain visitors, I will need more water to refresh me.'","Clear brush from the path up Raven-hill (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'More friends have arrived, and a Wizard too. As friends I count Dori, the High Hoard-seeker, and Nori, the Keeper of Coffers. They are my distant kin. Of the Wizard Gandalf I have fewer kind words to speak.'\
\
Dís looks around her, and you brace yourself for another task.\
\
'Ah, there is nothing else that needs doing right now, but do not think I am unaware of this plan of yours! I have so few visitors on most days that this slow trickle of friends and kin must mean something. You might as well tell me. What do the surviving members of my brother's adventuring band ask of his sister?'\
\
Gandalf opens his mouth to speak, and Dís silences him with a look.\
\
'I don't want to hear it from you, Wizard. I want this ${RACE} to tell me. Well? Spit it out, ${RACE}!'","You offered to clear the brush and stones from the path up Raven-hill for Dís.","Cleared stones from the path (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Gandalf by the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain","Pick up the bucket of water at the base of Raven-hill","The King Under the Mountain has agreed to your request to open the tomb of Thorin Oakenshield and ensure the Arkenstone remains within, but he wants you to first obtain permission from Thorin's sister Dís.","Defeat foes near Dale for Dís (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Bombur's progress up the hill was slow, and he told me he spied a number of foes in the vicinity of Dale during the ascent. I cannot think about the Heart of the Mountain while my neighbours are endangered!'","'The path down the hill is choked with brush and stones. Someone should do something.'","Dís is at Raven-hill, south-west of the Lonely Mountain.","'Now listen here, ${PLAYER}, and listen close. Thorin Oakenshield's sister Dís is very old, and she is unlikely at first to be very accommodating to our request. She will look more favourably upon it, I expect, if she were to see the familiar faces of Thorin's old friends and companions. But not all at once! Such a crowd will set her ill at ease, and she will not allow the intrusion.\
\
'I think there may be a way. I am reminded of an old trick that was of use to me during the Quest of Erebor, when Smaug still lived, his stolen hoard unrecovered. I will let the remaining dwarves of Thorin's Company know my plan. For your part, speak to Dís and be as friendly and as helpful as you may.'","'This is a day for visitors! Bifur, the Keeper of Hammers, and Bofur, the Master of Chisels, have come to Raven-hill. Even Bombur, the Warden of the Larders, has paid me a visit. Most unexpected. These dwarves accompanied my brother and my sons on the Quest of Erebor.'\
\
This seems as good an opening as any, and you ask again about the Arkenstone. As before, Dís interrupts you.\
\
'Bombur's progress up the hill was slow, and he told me he spied a number of foes in the vicinity of Dale during the ascent. I cannot think about the Heart of the Mountain while my neighbours are endangered!'\
\
Dís raises her eyes to you in challenge, and you volunteer to deal with the foes that lurk around Dale.","'It would not be proper to open Mazal Akrâz without the permission of Thorin's sister, Dís. Her children also lie in that place, and I would not have their rest or that of her brother disturbed without her leave.\
\
'She is the Keeper of Raven-hill, ${PLAYER}, and that is where you will find her. Speak to her and learn if she will allow the tomb to be opened.'","Gandalf wishes to speak with you by the throne of King Thorin III, in the Hall Under the Mountain.","Find Dís, the sister of Thorin Oakenshield, at Raven-hill","Chapter 6.6: The Keeper of Raven-hill","Dís, the sister of Thorin Oakenshield, is at Raven-hill.","You volunteered to defeat foes in the vicinity of Dale for Dís.","'I think there may be a way by which Dís can be made most amenable to our plan. I am reminded of an old trick that was of use to me during the Quest of Erebor, when Smaug still lived, his stolen hoard unrecovered. I will let the remaining dwarves of Thorin's Company know my plan. For your part, speak to Dís and be as friendly and as helpful as you may.'","Clear stones from the path up Raven-hill (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated foes for Dís (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Dís at Raven-hill","You set down the bucket of water as more dwarves come up the hill","This must be Dís, the elderly sister of Thorin Oakenshield"},
[3222]={"Use the coil of rope and climb down to the secret grotto","Despite your misgivings, you know that this may be your best chance to reach the Kindred's prisoners undetected. You resolve to remain alert in case Cruel Dancer attempts any treacherous action.","You rescued one prisoner from the Kindred of the Coins, and your friends now recover at the amphitheatre east of the city.","'Here is what I know of this secret harbour. It has been the berth of the ship belonging to Tatháta the Sea-beast, but ever since Nakási Wave-reaper's husband perished in Gondor, she has used it for her own ship as well. I do not know for what reason she chooses not to dock in the city proper, but I believe we will find both vessels in the harbour when we descend.\
\
'The way is treacherous, but we can use this rope to descend to the ledge we must take. It is narrow, with only room for one of us to pass at a time. Once you reach the far side of the ledge, there is a ladder that descends to the hidden harbour where our two targets keep their ships. You can go first down the rope... I will be right behind you.'","Chapter 6.7: Lair of the Beast","'The way is treacherous, but we can use this rope to descend to the ledge we must take. It is narrow, with only room for one of us to pass at a time. Once you reach the far side of the ledge, there is a ladder that descends to the hidden harbour where our two targets keep their ships. You can go first down the rope... I will be right behind you.'","The coil of rope by Cruel Dancer will allow you to reach the lair Cruel Dancer discovered.","'I still cannot believe it, ${PLAYER}! I never believed I would see you again... and yet here you are, such a great distance from where we parted! It is truly remarkable, and I delight that our reunion has come to pass!'","Talk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the city","Cruel Dancer has located the grotto where two members of the Kindred of the Coins seem to harbour their ships: Tatháta the Sea-beast and Nakási Wave-reaper."},
[3223]={"Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain","Talk to Gandalf by the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain","'This feels right to me, ${PLAYER}. The Gúrzyul gained their continuing lives through the powers of Sauron, and now that he is gone, perhaps that power fades. Can it be their strength declines even now, just as the craft-skill of the dwarves lessens with the absence of the Dwarf-ring? Do the Gúrzyul seek some means of survival, some power to counteract this decay? It would explain Ugrukhôr's desperation, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'If it is not a Bugdatish he seeks, not an artifact, but a Bugdash, a birth-name, perhaps he believes this information will stave off his decline. We must remain vigilant and keep the Gúrzyul from attaining the knowledge that will save them. This journey was valuable, my friend, though we defeated no Gúrzyul and found neither artifacts nor weapons. The wisdom we found is treasure enough.\
\
'I will ask the king to grant me a room within the Mountain and will retire there to consider our next course of action. Then we will face the Gúrzyul, and bring them to an end.'","'My brother Thorin was entombed in Mazal Akrâz with the Arkenstone, and with an Elven-sword beside. You think the Heart of the Mountain has been stolen? What thief would dare disturb the Oakenshield's rest or risk the guards of his tomb? No, do not try to convince me of this. There is no need.\
\
'It has been too long since I visited my brother and my sons where they lie beneath the Mountain. I will allow you to ensure the Arkenstone remains with Thorin while I pay my respects to my brother and to Fíli and Kíli. I am old, ${RACE}. It will be good for Durin's Folk to know the fate of the Heart of the Mountain, and it will benefit my own heart to see my lost kin at least one more time before I join them.\
\
'Tell the Wizard he has permission, but not to go alone. We will all go together.'","Chapter 6.7: Wood, Lake, Mountain, and Stone","Gandalf is by the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.","Gandalf is at Raven-hill, waiting to travel with you and the surviving members of Thorin's Company to ensure the Arkenstone remains entombed with the Oakenshield.","King Thorin III is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.","'It is good that Dís has given her permission to open the tomb of Thorin. We must know if Karazgar or his agents have worked some evil involving the Arkenstone.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Dís has given her permission to the dwarves of Thorin's Company to investigate his tomb and learn if the Arkenstone remains within.","'I am satisfied by your report, ${PLAYER}, and put at ease by the knowledge that the Arkenstone is still kept safe by Thorin Oakenshield beneath the Mountain. There is no end to the mischief Karazgar and others of his ilk seek to work upon my lands and my people, but the Heart of the Mountain remains beyond his reach.\
\
'I am less pleased by Gandalf's supposition that the loss of the dwarf-ring Handórm has caused the diminishment of our craft-skill, for such a loss cannot be reversed. That ring is gone, along with the others to which we held a claim, and none of them are coming back. It is not our way to give up hope, and our artisans will continue to strive, but I mourn the great works that once were made and will now have no rivals.\
\
'Thank you all the same, ${PLAYER}.'","'I will allow you to ensure the Arkenstone remains with Thorin while I pay my respects to my brother and to Fíli and Kíli. I am old, ${RACE}. It will be good for Durin's Folk to know the fate of the Heart of the Mountain, and it will benefit my own heart to see my lost kin at least one more time before I join them.\
\
'Tell the Wizard he has permission, but not to go alone. We will all go together.'","Talk to Gandalf at Raven-hill and travel to Mazal Akrâz"},
[3224]={"'I see... I am sorry.'\
\
Corudan stares at you carefully, and you try to tell him with your eyes that Nona is alive but her feelings toward Horn have cooled in recent months. The silence is finally broken by Sigileth.","Driftwood greets Corudan warmly.","Driftwood steps forward, a smile upon his face","You have rescued a friend from the Kindred of the Coins. Has the experience changed him, or have those he left behind changed in his stead?","'Horn, my friend! It is good to see you! I see you have shared in ${PLAYER}'s recent adventures, and I wish only that I could have done so as well!\
\
'But where is Nona? Surely she is here too? I cannot imagine she would be content to sit out such a fight as we all have now before us?'","Sigileth is at the amphitheatre east of the city.","The silence extends, awkwardly and overlong","Corudan looks at you carefully.","Corudan laughs. 'I am ready for more, my sister. The Kindred is not ready for us.'","Corudan looks around eagerly.","'I am saddened to have missed your recent adventures, my friends, but I am pleased we are now reunited.'","Talk to Driftwood at the amphitheatre east of the city","Chapter 6.8: One Prisoner Rescued","'Our mission is not yet over,' she says","Talk to Sigileth at the amphitheatre east of the city","'Horn, my friend! It is good to see you!'","Talk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the city","'You must have had many adventures since we parted, my friend! What brings you all the way to the land of Umbar? Many months and more miles have passed since I saw you last at Helm's Deep, in Rohan!'\
\
You tell Corudan, briefly, about some of the experiences you have had since his departure. He asks if you know how Leafshade fared after he went away, and you say as far as you know the Ent remains in good health and spirits. He smiles fondly.\
\
'I am glad. I do not doubt that he could have survived any attack by Nakási or Tatháta if he was roused to battle, but I feared for the creatures of his grove and the trees for which he cared. I know the Ents are fearsome when enraged... but I cannot help but think something is lost when they are called to fight. Something in them is wounded. It is true for Men and Elves, in my experience, and I think it may be so for the Ents as well. They are meant for peace, for the care and tending of things that grow.\
\
'I went with the Corsairs so they would not force Leafshade into battle. I sought to exert my influence upon them, and while I was not wholly successful I think it was for the best. Save for my words I fear the boy Thorongil would not have lived to reach Umbar.'","An awkward silence fills the air","'It is about time Corudan joined us again, wouldn't you say?'","'I see you found our wayward Elf, ${PLAYER}! It is about time Corudan joined us again, wouldn't you say?'","Driftwood remains silent.","Wait for Driftwood to arrive","'My purpose for joining this adventure has now been satisfied, but I will not have it said that I abandoned the mission when it was half-done. My brother has been rescued from the Kindred of the Coins, as I knew he would be, but they still hold the young heir of Pinnath Gelin captive.'","Corudan is pleased to see his friends again."},
[3225]={"Corudan laughs. 'I am ready for more, my sister. The Kindred is not ready for us.'","Corudan waits for you to speak.","Think about what to tell Corudan","You have rescued a friend from the Kindred of the Coins. Has the experience changed him, or have those he left behind changed in his stead?","'I am saddened to have missed your recent adventures, my friend, but I am pleased we are now reunited.'","'Our mission is not yet over,' she says","Chapter 6.8: One Prisoner Rescued","How should you tell Corudan about some of the mournful events that transpired?","'Why do you hesitate, my friend? What has happened?'\
\
Sadly you tell Corudan of Horn's death before the walls of Minas Tirith during the Battle of Pelennor Fields. The Elf remains silent for a long moment. When at last he speaks, his voice is choked with emotion and he does not sound like himself.\
\
'Horn always possessed more courage than he believed himself to have, ${PLAYER}. I hope that Nona holds his memory dear. Know that I will. I know this too: Gléowine must record the name of our friend in song, for he fought for Rohan, and though I was not there I know he fought with courage on behalf of his friends and for his kingdom.'\
\
You tell Corudan that Gléowine did intend to include Horn in the song he composed of the battle, and the Elf smiles. After a moment Sigileth speaks up.","'My purpose for joining this adventure has now been satisfied, but I will not have it said that I abandoned the mission when it was half-done. My brother has been rescued from the Kindred of the Coins, as I knew he would be, but they still hold the young heir of Pinnath Gelin captive.'","Sigileth is at the amphitheatre east of the city.","'You must have had many adventures since we parted, my friend! What brings you all the way to the land of Umbar? Many months and more miles have passed since I saw you last at Helm's Deep, in Rohan!'\
\
You tell Corudan, briefly, about some of the experiences you have had since his departure. He asks if you know how Leafshade fared after he went away, and you say as far as you know the Ent remains in good health and spirits. He smiles fondly.\
\
'I am glad. I do not doubt that he could have survived any attack by Nakási or Tatháta if he was roused to battle, but I feared for the creatures of his grove and the trees for which he cared. I know the Ents are fearsome when enraged... but I cannot help but think something is lost when they are called to fight. Something in them is wounded. It is true for Men and Elves, in my experience, and I think it may be so for the Ents as well. They are meant for peace, for the care and tending of things that grow.\
\
'I went with the Corsairs so they would not force Leafshade into battle. I sought to exert my influence upon them, and while I was not wholly successful I think it was for the best. Save for my words I fear the boy Thorongil would not have lived to reach Umbar.\
\
'But where are our other friends, ${PLAYER}? Do you not still adventure with Horn, Nona, and Gléowine?'","Corudan is eager to hear what befell his friends... but you do not know how to tell him some of the mournful things that transpired.","Talk to Sigileth at the amphitheatre east of the city","Talk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the city"},
[3226]={"'To the bridge up ahead. Come, friend.'","'A gift for Lady Arwen awaits you in the Court of Lothlórien. It is Glorfindel's betrothal gift to her, but the honour is yours to deliver it.'","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Talk to Arwen by the statue.","'Come, let us go on through the narrow pass ahead.'","Arwen meets your eyes as you approach her, and you present her with the gift directly. She opens the silken box and you explain the flowers are from Glorfindel.\
\
'I know then what these are and what is their meaning. It is a good and a beautiful thought Glorfindel has given me in this gift. Come, ${PLAYER}. Walk with me a spell.'","A distant look comes across Arwen's face","'An age is ending, ${PLAYER}. It is not ended quite yet, and in the counting of Men and dwarves, it will not be over for some modest span to come. But for me, to have known centuries... centuries before my heart was given, moving freely from Imladris to Lorien, from Lorien to Imladris, like a carefree minnow between pond and stream. Then to know that nothing shall be as it was.\
\
'Do you know what these flowers are, ${PLAYER}? They are lovers' tokens, and they are wrought with uncommon skill so that a sympathy exists between them, as if they were tied by an unseen thread no matter the distance. If anything should befall the owner of one flower - should they grow ill or die - then the other's flower will wilt, wither, and crumble. Thus may my Aragorn always know that I am well and whole, and I may know the same of him.\
\
'It is at once a great comfort and a constant reminder of our doom and of endings-to-be.'","Deliver the gift to Arwen in Imlad Gelair","The world opens out before you, a breeze rustling the leaves of the trees","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Talk to Arwen upon the second bridge.","The air is sweet and clear, this Elven retreat fine to behold","You should ask Lady Galadriel in the Court of Lothlórien for Arwen's gift.","Ask Galadriel for the gift","Walk with Arwen to the left statue","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Go with Arwen onto the second bridge.","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Go with Arwen to the left past the bridge, where the statue stands.","Gift in hand, it is time to visit Arwen in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell, once more.","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Talk to Arwen under the trees before the second bridge.","Talk to Arwen","Chapter 6: A Mortal Gift","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Talk to Arwen upon the bridge.","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Go with Arwen to the bridge ahead.","'Indeed, I have tarried in Rivendell many years now, though it is not counted overlong in the reckoning of my people. These last tens of years, I have lived here in anticipation of a promise, waiting to learn if fortune should decree it held or broken. That brief time has been both as an eternity and a single breath to me.\
\
'Shortly, we shall set forth for Gondor, as you know, and shortly thereafter, when we reach that land, I shall become one with the treasure of my heart. He will be king and I queen. Like Lúthien, whose likeness is here before us, and Beren. Elf-maid and Man. Much gained, yes, and much lost.\
\
'Come, let us go farther down the path.'","'A true gift is one which sings of the receiver in the voice of the giver, it is said. By that mark, Glorfindel has chosen the truest of gifts.'\
\
Lady Galadriel produces two exquisite flowers, and only after a moment do you perceive that they are brooches, wrought of silver filament, green and violet silk, and finest cloth-of-gold, and not real flowers at all. She returns them to a silken box, which she hands to you.\
\
'Take these to Arwen, ${PLAYER}. She will tell you something of what they mean to her, if she wishes.'","'Much will come to pass, ${PLAYER}. It will come soon, swift as a diving hawk. Swift as the sun's last descent into night. Much will be gained, and much, too, lost.'\
\
Arwen laughs, softly, sweetly, and a little sadly.\
\
'You are thinking, I am sure, that much has already happened since first your journey began. Nor are you mistaken! You have seen much, but soon all Middle-earth shall see more. And while you have been through many lands and among many peoples, I have been here and among only my own.\
\
'To the left now, where that statue stands.'","Walk with Arwen a little further","'The gift for Lady Arwen has been found, ${PLAYER}. Lady Galadriel herself holds it and awaits your arrival. Though it is Glorfindel's betrothal gift, the honour is yours to deliver it.'","Walk with Arwen some more","Walk with Arwen to the bridge","'Let us go there, where the statue stands by the water.'","Arwen looks up at the statue and you are struck by a strong resemblance","Arwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell.\
\
Go with Arwen farther down the path, through the narrow pass.","Accept the honour of delivering Glorfindel's betrothal gift to Arwen.","'I am going off to dwell in the lands of Men, and I shall become as they who dwell there, ${PLAYER}. I will gain my heart's desire and I will be Queen of the heirs of Númenor, at the dawn of a new age. But I will lose the home I have known. I will lose so many faces dearest to me, who I leave behind and who themselves will make even greater journeys, soon enough. I will lose the roots-deep certainty of days unending. Where I go, days will be numbered, and so also lives.'\
\
Arwen stops and meets your gaze with level eyes that are filled with many things.\
\
'I thank you for walking with me, ${PLAYER}. I thank you for listening kindly and without judgment. Sadness and joy are like two streams joined into a river, and the finest of Elven weavers could not part them now. But I have a journey to prepare for, and time will not tarry.\
\
'I will see you in Gondor, friend? I hope that I do. I should like that very much!'"},
[3227]={"'Busca por todo Zelem-melek y las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo armaduras abolladas, hojas rotas y escudos agrietados que pueda usar para la ejecución de mi plan.'","'Estos serán perfectos, ${PLAYER}; justo el tipo de cosas que necesito para equipar a los dos equipos que estamos reuniendo. Algunas de estas piezas pueden ser reparadas, y el resto se fundirá para hacer nuevo equipo.'","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has reunido muchas piezas del equipo que te ha pedido Bori, y ahora deberías llevárselas.","Bori quiere que recolectes armaduras, armas y escudos que puedan ser reparados o fundidos para equipar a los enanos que ejecutan su audaz plan.","'Incluso si mi plan sale bien, ambos grupos de enanos estarán en peligro. Los orcos de la Mano Blanca son mortales, y seguro que habrá peleas. Sin embargo, estamos bajos de equipo, y ciertamente carecemos de la armadura y las armas que mis dos equipos requerirán.\
\
'Si puedes encontrar armaduras abolladas, hojas rotas y escudos agrietados en los orcos por todo Zelem-melek, las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo y dentro de sus campamentos, este equipo podría ser reparado; si están demasiado dañados, podríamos fundirlos y usarlos para hacer nuevas armas y armaduras.\
\
'En cualquier caso, podré equipar a mis equipos con las armas y armaduras que la victoria requerirá.'","Armaduras abolladas, hojas rotas y escudos agrietados se pueden encontrar en los orcos y dentro de sus campamentos por todo Zelem-melek y las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Bori necesita equipar a los dos equipos que ejecutarán su ataque a Stazgnâkh, y quiere que reúnas los materiales que le permitirán hacer esto.","'¡Aún no me has traído el equipo que necesito!'","Lleva armaduras, armas y escudos a Bori","Capítulo 6: Armas de la Mordedura Más Afilada"},
[3228]={"Capítulo 6: Las sospechas de Bori","'Es probable que las Obras Hidráulicas estén llenas de criaturas peligrosas. Derrota a esas criaturas y memoriza la ubicación de las habitaciones, y podría ser capaz de discernir la ubicación de las armerías que Óin estaba buscando.'","Derrota a las criaturas de las Obras Hidráulicas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Te doy la bienvenida de nuevo, ${PLAYER}! Cuéntame sobre las salas que has descubierto. A partir de las placas de las habitaciones que has visto, podría ser capaz de discernir cuál es la que se menciona en el Libro de Mazarbul, el armario que Óin buscaba.\
\
'¡La Sala del Mithril, sí... creo que debe ser esa, ${PLAYER}! ¡Bien hecho!'","Bori sospecha que ha dado con algo que permitirá a los enanos darle la vuelta a los amenazantes orcos de Moria.","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has explorado las Obras Hidráulicas para encontrar las armerías que buscaba el enano Óin, como se explica en el Libro de Mazarbul. Deberías volver ahora con Bori.","Has memorizado la placa de la habitación (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","En las Obras Hidráulicas se pueden encontrar criaturas acuáticas peligrosas.\
\
Bori te ha pedido que derrotes a las criaturas que se encuentran entre las ruinas de las Obras Hidráulicas.","Las placas de las habitaciones se pueden encontrar por todas las Obras Hidráulicas, al igual que criaturas acuáticas peligrosas.\
\
Bori te ha pedido que memorices la ubicación de las placas en varias habitaciones diferentes de las Obras Hidráulicas.","Has derrotado a las criaturas de las Obras Hidráulicas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Brogur te ha dicho que su sobrino Bori quiere hablar contigo sobre algo.","Memoriza las placas de las habitaciones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Bori quiere hablar contigo sobre algo, pero no sé de qué se trata.'","'Estoy tan contento de que hayas dado un golpe tan duro a los Ghâsh-haï que casi se me olvida: Bori, mi sobrino, quiere hablar contigo sobre algo. No quiso decirme qué es lo que le tiene tan emocionado, pero me alegra ver que no se deja vencer por la tristeza. De hecho, no creo haberlo visto tan alegre desde que mi hijo fue asesinado por el Guardián del Agua.\
\
'Es una gran lección saber convertir el dolor en fuerza interior. ¡Pregúntale a Ashpar sobre la fuerza de los enanos!'","Bori te saluda calurosamente y luego mira a su alrededor de forma conspiratoria.\
\
'Creo que podría haber dado con algo, ${PLAYER}. Ayer, mientras visitaba a mi padre, eché un vistazo al Libro de Mazarbul y vi algo interesante: una línea cerca del final que decía que el enano Óin buscaba \\qlas armerías superiores de las Terceras Profundidades,\\q y alguna mención de una poderosa hacha. ¿Crees que Óin podría haber ido a buscar Zigilburk?\
\
'Si encontráramos el hacha de mithril Zigilburk, creo que podría cambiar el rumbo de la tormenta que se avecina. Óin no debe haberla encontrado, pero si lo hizo, ¿crees que la expedición de Balin podría haber sobrevivido? Nunca lo sabremos.\
\
'Viaja a las Obras Hidráulicas y busca placas de habitación; memorízalas y vuelve a mí con sus ubicaciones, ¡y podríamos encontrar el armario por el que Óin buscaba! Mata también a cualquiera de las criaturas mortales que haya allí; si tengo razón, puede que haya otro viaje allí en nuestro futuro.'"},
[3229]={"'Bori es un buen chico, y se convertirá en un gran enano. Sin embargo, creo que su preferencia por contar historias en lugar de trabajar duro pasará con el tiempo. Mi primo Brogur y yo no éramos diferentes a su edad.\
\
'Tomará algo de tiempo fabricar los picos con los materiales que has entregado. Mientras mis enanos trabajan en eso, te pido que prestes tu ayuda a Brogur. Si realmente deseas ayudar a los enanos, ¡no se debe perder ni un momento!\
\
'Encontrarás a mi primo al norte de aquí, en algún lugar a lo largo del camino que sube a la Puerta de Acebeda. Es gruñón, incluso para su linaje, pero agradecerá tu ayuda.'","'Brogur es severo, al igual que su padre, pero respeta la fuerza y la amistad. Agradecerá tu ayuda.\
\
'Búscalo al norte de aquí, a lo largo del camino que sube a la Puerta de Acebeda.'","Capítulo 6: El primo Brogur","Bósi te agradeció tu parte en la recolección de materiales para la fabricación de nuevas piochas, y te envió a Brogur para que puedas prestar tu ayuda a su primo.","El primo de Bósi, Brogur, se encuentra en algún lugar a lo largo del camino que sube a la Puerta de Acebeda, al norte de la posición de Bósi.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que prestes tu ayuda a su primo Brogur mientras se fabrican las piochas.","'¿Cómo dijiste que te llamabas? ${PLAYER}?\
\
'¿Es siquiera un nombre de verdad? ¡Vas a tener que trabajar especialmente duro para compensar eso!'"},
[3230]={"'No pongas en duda mi valor, ${CLASS}, pero no seguiré al joven Bori hasta la muerte. El señor Brogur ya ha perdido a su hijo en este empeño; a menos que alguien más sabio que Bori lidere este asalto a Stazgnâkh, temo que el señor Bósi también pierda al suyo.'","Proponer el plan de Bori a los enanos de la Sala Vigesimoprimera (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Bori necesita que reclutes a algunos enanos para llenar las filas de los dos grupos necesarios para su plan: el grupo de distracción y el grupo de ataque.","La Sala Vigesimoprimera en Zelem-melek está llena de enanos que Bori quiere reclutar para su audaz misión contra la Mano Blanca.\
\
Bori necesita reclutar enanos para completar los dos grupos necesarios: una fuerza de distracción y un grupo de ataque principal.","Capítulo 6: Enanos de gran valor","'Tengo un gran respeto por Bori, por supuesto, pero tengo suficiente trabajo que hacer sin tener que lanzar piedras a un nido de avispones. ¡Este plan está mal concebido, y a menos que los señores Bósi o Brogur lo ordenen ellos mismos no tendré nada que ver con él!'","'¡Necesitaré la ayuda de los enanos más valientes de esta compañía si mi plan va a tener éxito, ${PLAYER}! Un grupo hará una finta contra el cruce vigilado en el Camino Oriental, y yo lideraré al otro contra Stazgnâkh, el campamento de la Mano Blanca.\
\
'¡Habla con los enanos en la Sala Vigesimoprimera y recluta a tantos como puedas para mi misión! ¡Haz que piensen en honor y valor, porque ambos serán necesarios!\
\
'¡Una vez que la Mano Blanca sea expulsada de Moria, tendremos paz bajo las montañas!'","'Ya tengo tareas que cumplir, ${PLAYER}. Lo siento por no poder ayudar a Bori en su misión, pero lo respeto por haber emprendido esta tarea!'","'¿Qué es este plan de Bori? ¿Un ataque de distracción? Soy un poco anticuado, y no aprecio ese tipo de tácticas; los enemigos deben ser desafiados de frente.\
\
Incluso si esto fuera más de mi agrado, tengo demasiadas tareas que hacer y no suficiente tiempo para completarlas todas. Es una pena que no pueda luchar junto al joven maestro.'","'¡Seguiré al hijo de mi señor Bosi a la batalla, y con gusto! ¡El tiempo de la Mano Blanca en Moria pronto llegará a su fin!'","Propuesto el plan de Bori a los enanos de la Sala Vigesimoprimera (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'¡Maravilloso! ¿Has encontrado enanos valientes para ejecutar mi plan?'\
\
Bori escucha mientras le cuentas sobre Stilling y Wíli, los voluntarios que reclutaste. Espera expectante por más, y luego su rostro se cae.\
\
'¿Eso es todo? ¿Solo dos enanos? ¿Cómo puede ser esto, ${PLAYER}? ¡Eso apenas es suficiente para un grupo! Bueno, estoy seguro de que hiciste lo mejor que pudiste. De alguna manera me las arreglaré.'","'Me ofrezco voluntariamente para la misión del joven Bori. ¡Cuanto antes se expulse a la Mano Blanca de Moria, más seguros estaremos todos! ¡Que nadie llame a Stilling un cobarde!'","'Habla con los guerreros de la Sala Vigesimoprimera y reclútalos para los dos grupos detallados en mis planes, ${PLAYER}.'","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has intentado reclutar a algunos enanos para el audaz plan de Bori contra la Mano Blanca, pero muy pocos se han ofrecido como voluntarios."},
[3231]={"Lenglammel se encuentra en el campamento de Gwathrendath, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Has hecho lo que has podido para contrarrestar la amenaza de las criaturas Sinnombre que acechan entre los Fundaciones de piedra.","Se pueden encontrar grietas en el abismo por todas partes en las Fundaciones de Piedra, no muy lejos de Gwathrendath. \
\
Lenglammel te ha pedido que coloques Piedras élficas frente a las grietas del abismo cerca del campamento para disuadir a las criaturas Sinnombre de acercarse.","Lenglammel está preocupada de que las criaturas Sinnombre buscadas por Mazog se estén acercando demasiado a su campamento.","Piedras élficas colocadas en las grietas del abismo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Las criaturas Sinnombre a veces se arrastran por las grietas en las paredes del abismo; coloca estas Piedras élficas cerca de ellas para disuadirlas de hacerlo. También deberías derrotar a las bestias Sinnombre dondequiera que las veas, porque son muy peligrosas, y se están volviendo más feroces y numerosas por hora.'","Capítulo 6: Maldades bajo el mundo","'Las criaturas Sinnombre que viven en las profundidades de la tierra son extremadamente peligrosas, pero eso no impide que Mazog quiera esclavizarlas. Es víctima de Dol Guldur, eso es seguro, pero no siento ninguna lástima por él. Estas criaturas son mortales, y se acercan a Gwathrendath cada vez más con cada hora que pasa.\
\
'¡Y aún así Magor no regresa! ¡Esto no es típico de él para ser tan tardío! Si no fuera tan fuerte, estaría preocupado, pero Magor entrenó con Celeborn en los Días Antiguos y puede cuidarse a sí mismo.\
\
'Hay grietas en las paredes no muy lejos de Gwathrendath. Coloca estos berilos frente a las grietas para disuadir a los Sinnombre de acercarse a las grietas.'","Coloca piedras élficas en las grietas del abismo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Has hecho lo que has podido, ${PLAYER}, pero en lo que respecta a los Sinnombre, espero que sea suficiente.'"},
[3232]={"Talk to Calenglad at Tinnudir","Daervunn has sent you to bring word of the Grey Company's mission to Calenglad and the Rangers of Evendim.","'You say that Aragorn has need of the Dúnedain? I wondered if this day would come. We have safe-guarded Annúminas and the lands around Lake Evendim for so long now that it seemed we would do so forever. To be told, thus, that it comes to an end, and we must travel into distant lands to the south....'\
\
Calenglad gazes for a moment out at the clear waters of Lake Evendim.\
\
'I will go with the Grey Company. That is my duty, and I will not shy away from it. But first I want to save some of the relics of Annúminas from being plundered. Angmarim still haunt the city, leaderless though they be, and in the past few weeks they have allied themselves with numerous tomb-robbers to strip the city of any relics they can find. Let us recover such relics from one of the wards while still we can. Speak with me when you are ready to go.'","Calenglad is at Tinnudir, the Ranger-camp on the shores of Lake Evendim.\
\
Calenglad is waiting to speak with you about taking one more journey into Annúminas to rescue some relics from the Angmarim and tomb-robbers that seek to plunder them.","'I will go with the Grey Company, but first I want to clear one of the wards of Annúminas of relics that would be plundered by the Angmarim and their tomb-robber allies if we must leave.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'I do not know whether he will wish to join the ranks of the Grey Company on their southward journey, but Calenglad should be told of the mission all the same. He feels a very strong bond to the lands around Lake Evendim, and to the ruins of Annúminas, and may not be able to bring himself to leave.\
\
'Bring him the message, in the event I misjudge his temperament. You will find him at Tinnudir, the Ranger-camp on the shores of Lake Evendim. If he does join the company, he will be a valuable ally on the southern road.'","Chapter 6: Farewell to Evendim","'You will find Calenglad at Tinnudir, the Ranger-camp on the shores of Lake Evendim. I do not know if he will decide to join the Grey Company on their southern road, but if he does he will be a valuable ally.'","Calenglad is at Tinnudir, the Ranger-camp on the shores of Lake Evendim.\
\
You have done as Calenglad asked, and in his own way, he has bade farewell to the lands of Evendim. He is ready now to travel with the Grey Company, and you should speak with him.","'That is the way of it, ${PLAYER}. Some part of my heart will remain always within the walls of Annúminas, though duty carry me far away. It will be up to others, now, to safe-guard the places... and the people... that I hold dear.\
\
'I will ride to Aragorn, and let the future hold what it may... I will face it unblinking.'","Talk to Calenglad and travel with him to the Flooded Ward","Calenglad is at Tinnudir, the Ranger-camp on the shores of Lake Evendim.\
\
Daervunn has sent you to enlist the aid of Calenglad and the Rangers of Evendim for the Grey Company."},
[3233]={"'You have work to do! I will slay more warriors of hostile clans than you can, and I will do it for my son.'","Radanir is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees to the east of the Uch-lûth village of Lhanuch.\
\
Suvulch told you that Radanir was looking for you about an urgent matter.","Suvulch is by Wadu's favourite tree, on a rise by ox-pens west of Lhanuch, and hostile Dunlendings can be found throughout Enedwaith.\
\
Suvulch has challenged you to a competition to slay hostile Dunlendings in memory of Wadu.","Hostile Dunlendings can be found throughout Enedwaith.\
\
Suvulch has challenged you to a competition to see who can defeat the most Dunlendings of enemy clans in honour of Wadu.","'There you are! I have been looking everywhere for you! We have received another letter from Ergothorn.\
\
'I left it on that crate there. If he speaks the truth, we have little time to waste!'","'If we can believe the words of Ergothorn, a party of uruks marches toward Zudrugund. If they seize Nár, he could tell them of our errand!\
\
'Or he could tell them nonsense. But I think we have no choice, ${PLAYER}. We have to do something in case Ergothorn is right.'","Find Suvulch somewhere near Lhanuch","You last saw Suvulch at Wadu's favourite tree, on a rise by the ox-pens, west of Lhanuch.\
\
Nona is angry at her father Suvulch for his cruel treatment of Wadu while Wadu was still alive, and she wants you to tell Suvulch so.","'All men are fools! Your leader Halbarad is a fool for refusing my request, the Brehur are fools for delaying so long in action against our enemies, and my father Suvulch is a fool as well!\
\
'He has been avoiding me since Wadu died. Do you know what I think? I think he is ashamed to show his face for his cruel treatment of Wadu while he still lived. He should feel that shame! It is his alone!\
\
'He should have been kinder to his son while Wadu lived. You find him and tell him so!'","Defeat hostile Dunlendings throughout Enedwaith, and return to Suvulch when you are satisfied","Talk to Suvulch","Nona is not pleased that Halbarad has refused her request to travel south with the Grey Company and is also angry with her father Suvulch.","Read the letter on the crate by Radanir","'I have left the letter on that crate there. Read what Ergothorn has to say, but read quickly! If what he says is true, we may not have much time.'","A second letter from Ergothorn is on the crate near Radanir, at the camp-site of the Grey Company in the grove of trees east of Lhanuch.\
\
Radanir has found a second letter from Ergothorn and wants you to read it and give your opinion on what the mysterious correspondent has to say.","'How many hostile Dunlendings have you slain?'\
\
Suvulch listens to your count and nods.\
\
'My count is higher! Yet it does not matter, for we have done this for the memory of my son. Let his enemies rue the day they slew him from ambush and caused us to notice the stink of them.\
\
'Shortly after I returned from battle, one of your Rangers spoke with me. He said his name was Radanir, and he wanted to speak with you. You should find him and see what he wants of you. He said he would be at the duvodiad camp among the trees to the east of my village.\
\
'Thank you for the competition, ${PLAYER}. It is not enough to answer for my son's life, maybe, but it is something.'","'What do you have to say to me, duvodiad?'\
\
Suvulch listens impatiently as you recount Nona's words to him about Wadu.\
\
'You cannot speak to me of this matter, and neither can my daughter! Only one language will we speak: the language of battle.\
\
'You and I will fight hostile Dunlendings of other clans, duvodiad, and we will measure which of us has the authority to judge the other. Do not return until you have slain many of our enemies!'","Talk to Radanir at the grove of trees east of Lhanuch","'You have fought many Dunlendings of other clans. They were the enemies of Wadu, and they are my enemies. I am pleased you have done this.'","Defeat hostile Dunlendings throughout Enedwaith","'It was a good competition, and the foes of Wadu surely regret their treachery. The Ranger named Radanir is looking for you. You should go see him. He said he would be at the duvodiad camp among the trees to the east of my village.'","To the Rangers:\
\
I do not have much time to write this; I beg you to move with all possible haste. A group of uruks have come out of Dunland, but instead of passing further north as others have done, these have begun the climb into Thrór's Coomb. I fear they have orders involving the dwarves that still live there, especially the one called Nár.\
\
You must defend this dwarf from the uruks! He knows much that, told to the wrong person, could be hurtful to your errand.\
\
Ergothorn","'My father Suvulch should feel great shame for the way he treated Wadu while he was alive. Find him, wherever he is, and tell him so!'","'Suvulch has challenged you to a competition to slay the foes of the Uch-lûth? He does this for Wadu?\
\
'It is not enough. He should have done this when my brother was alive.'","Chapter 6: For Wadu","Defeated a hostile Dunlending warrior","Find Radanir at the grove of trees east of Lhanuch","'My father can do what he likes in memory of Wadu, but it will never be enough for me. He is simply too late.'","Radanir is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in the grove of trees east of Lhanuch.\
\
You have read Ergothorn's second letter, which calls for you to go to the defence of Zudrugund."},
[3234]={"'Your eyes may play tricks on you within these ruins.'","Chapter 6: Fúni Gem-cutter","Fúni Gem-cutter has been taken to the abandoned ruins of Minas Elendúr by the Ninkoth uruks.","'This dwarf for whom you are looking is somewhere in Minas Elendúr? Well, you will have your hands full looking for him. These ruins are a bewildering maze crawling with uruks of the Ninkoth tribe and other dangers. It is enough to drive a man mad!'","'My father is somewhere in the ruins of Minas Elendúr? You need to rescue him, ${PLAYER}! The Elves say that Minas Elendúr is far to the east of here!'","Fúni Gem-cutter is being held somewhere within the depths of Minas Elendúr, far to the east of Echad Eregion.\
\
You have learned the location of Fúni Gem-cutter and should now attempt his rescue.","'I have been asking the Elves here for information about Minas Elendúr, but there is not much to tell. The ruins were the site of a terrible battle, long ago, and have remained empty ever since. They can be found far to the east of here.'","'I have been told there was a great battle here, long ago.'","The floor is stained with blood. Will this lead to Fúni Gem-cutter?","'The Elves at Gwingris would not tell me much of these ruins, but they told me enough to whet my curiosity: that this was the site of a battle, long ago, and none of the people who lived here were spared the sword. But the goal of the enemy was not treasure, for the coffers were left untouched. Untouched!\
\
'But there is something strange about the rooms and corridors of Minas Elendúr, and the cellars of Delotham, which run beneath it. You see things, sometimes, disturbing things. It is as if the horrors that fell upon that place scarred it in some way, some way that the stones have not forgotten. It would be a brave ${RACE} indeed to explore the place from top to bottom!\
\
'Some rooms in Minas Elendúr can only be reached by stairs within Delotham, and the opposite seems also to be so! I do not know why the Ninkoth uruks have come to this place, but I feel it must be as bewildering to them as it is to me! Wherever they are keeping this dwarf for whom you are looking, it will not be easy to find!'","Find Fúni Gem-cutter somewhere within Minas Elendúr","'I have had an idea, ${PLAYER}, and we cannot leave until Fúni Gem-cutter is rescued.'","'By Durin, a friendly face! I had all but given up hope of rescue, and here you appear as if from nowhere! Hurry, there is not much time!'","'Something is not right within these ruins, friend.'"},
[3235]={"Derrota a los trasgos a lo largo de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva los mapas rudimentarios a Bósi","Capítulo 6: Trasgos en las galerías occidentales","'Los trasgos han hecho de este lugar su hogar en la oscuridad durante mucho tiempo. Estos mapas podrían tener secretos que mostrarnos, por desagradables que parezcan.'\
\
Bósi examina los mapas durante un buen rato, y luego su rostro se ilumina con una amplia sonrisa.\
\
'¡Puede que haya resuelto nuestro enigma, ${PLAYER}! ¡Creo que podemos discernir la ubicación del Corazón de Fuego a partir de estos mapas!'","Lleva los mapas rudimentarios a Brogur","Brogur se encuentra en la Cámara de Mando, subiendo las escaleras del este en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, ubicada en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has matado a muchos trasgos y recogido sus mapas mientras buscabas el Corazón de Fuego.","'No puedo quejarme de esta misión tuya, ${PLAYER}: has matado a muchos trasgos a pesar de tu búsqueda de una forja que probablemente nunca existió.\
\
'Estos mapas rudimentarios de los trasgos no me dicen nada que ya no supiera: que los trasgos son criaturas sucias y repugnantes, y que sus mapas no valen nada.\
\
'Muéstraselos a mi primo Bósi, sin embargo. Quizás él tenga más paciencia que yo y te diga algo útil.'","'No creo que el Corazón de Fuego exista, ${PLAYER}. Habríamos oído hablar de esta legendaria forja si existiera. Mientras la buscas, bien podrías matar trasgos en las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata. Son muchos, y quizás quieras llevar uno o dos aliados contigo.\
\
'Si quieres, echa un vistazo a sus mapas; quizás hayan encontrado esta forja imaginaria tuya.'","'No me has traído nada de interés.'","'Siempre tendrás mi respeto por lo que hiciste frente a las Puertas de Durin, vengando a mi pobre hijo con tu excelente arma, pero debo ser honesto contigo: creo que estás perdiendo el tiempo. Mientras deambules por la oscuridad buscando esta forja de fantasía, bien podrías hacer algo que valga la pena, ${PLAYER}.\
\
Parece haber una gran presencia de trasgos en las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata, al sur y debajo de la Gran Excavación. Mientras buscas este legendario Corazón de Fuego, bien podrías matar trasgos mientras lo haces, especialmente los que se han mudado a Gamil Filik, la Mina Mayor. Los trasgos son muchos, y llevar uno o dos aliados podría ser una buena idea.\
\
De hecho, ¿por qué no robar algunos de sus mapas? Han vivido aquí en la oscuridad durante mucho tiempo, y sus mapas rudimentarios podrían mostrar el camino hacia esta mítica forja tuya, además de ser útiles para aquellos de nosotros que buscamos caminos que realmente existen.'","'Bósi siempre ha sido mejor que yo para este tipo de trabajo mental. Muéstrale los mapas y tal vez tenga más que decirte. Para mí, parecen garabatos crudos e horribles. Los trasgos son criaturas miserables, ¿no es así?'","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, justo afuera de la Cámara de Mando.\
\
Brogur no ha visto nada útil en los mapas rudimentarios de los trasgos que encontraste, pero su primo Bósi podría tener más suerte interpretándolos.","Trasgos derrotados en las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿No me has traído nada? Qué curioso.'","Brogur duda de que el Corazón de Fuego exista, y quiere que al menos hagas algo con el problema de los trasgos mientras lo buscas.","Se pueden encontrar trasgos en las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata, al sur y debajo de la Gran Excavación, y sus mapas se pueden encontrar dentro de Gamil Filik, la mina que han ocupado.\
\
Brogur te pidió que mataras trasgos mientras buscas el Corazón de Fuego, y que estuvieras atento a sus mapas; es posible que hayan descubierto la forja y la hayan incluido en sus mapas rudimentarios."},
[3236]={"Las Cámaras de Sabiduría, Conocimiento y Reflexión Profunda se encuentran en toda la Gran Excavación, al igual que Katûb-zahar. Cualquiera de estos lugares puede tener los registros mineros que Bróin debía encontrar.\
\
Bróin está insatisfecho con las tareas sin sentido que su padre Brogur le ha asignado, y está extremadamente frustrado de que los enanos hagan este tipo de trabajo mientras Bori sigue prisionero de las fuerzas de Mazog.","'No has regresado con los registros mineros, ${PLAYER}, y no puedo culparte. ¡Qué pérdida de tiempo!'","'¿Has regresado con los registros mineros? Mi padre estará complacido, aunque yo no lo esté. ¿Por qué debemos perder tanto tiempo en tareas sin sentido como esta cuando mi primo sigue siendo prisionero de Mazog?'\
\
Bróin toma los registros mineros de tus manos con un suspiro, pero al leerlos, sus ojos se abren y su rostro se ilumina.\
\
'¿Entiendes lo que has encontrado, ${PLAYER}? ¡Ja ja! ¡No son simples registros mineros! ¡Estas páginas pueden contener la clave para rescatar a mi primo Bori! Escucha esto:\
\
'\\qMelkólf Tallapiedra encargado de trabajos de detalle en la pared trasera de Rushdurinul durante la noche para la finalización de Zurr-thurkh; instrucciones especiales retenidas por orden de Durin.\\q\
\
La palabra Rushdurinul llamó mi atención, ${PLAYER}, pues es el nombre del trono de Durin, el mismo trono que Mazog ha reclamado para sí. Y luego ver el nombre Zurr-thurkh, o \\qcamino secreto...\\q ¿podría ser que este enano, Melkólf Tallapiedra, fue encargado de crear un pasaje secreto fuera de la sala del trono de Durin para que el rey lo usara en caso de peligro? ¡Si este pasaje fue completado, podría usarse para acceder a Mazog! ¡Podría usarse para rescatar a mi primo Bori!'","'El mensajero enviado por Bróin fue muy claro en que primero debíamos ocuparnos de la corrupción dentro de Buzun-ghâr. Una vez hecho esto, su maestro deseaba que lo visitaras de nuevo en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada en la Sala de Reunión Militar, al este de Sulnul-dûm y al oeste del Salón de Piedra, aquí en el Camino de Durin. La entrada a la Senda Pacífica está al noreste de Buzun-ghâr.'","Estas estanterías no contienen ningún registro minero.","Bróin está descansando en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada en la Sala de Reunión Militar, al este de Sulnul-dûm y al oeste del Salón de Piedra, en el Camino de Durin. La entrada a la Senda Pacífica está al noreste de Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Bróin ha enviado aviso de que desea hablar contigo de nuevo. Orvar te dijo que trataras a Bróin con amabilidad, creyendo que sus pruebas en la guarida acuática del Vigilante y la pérdida de su primo ante las fuerzas de Mazog pueden haberlo afectado profundamente.","Bróin está en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada en la Sala de Reunión Militar, al este de Sulnul-dûm y al oeste del Salón de Piedra, en el Camino de Durin. La entrada a la Senda Pacífica está al noreste de Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Has recuperado algunos de los registros mineros que el padre de Bróin quería que encontrara, pero incluyen detalles curiosos que interesarán mucho a Bróin.","Capítulo 6: Talladores de piedra","Lleva los registros mineros a Bróin","'¿De qué sirven los registros mineros cuando mi primo Bori sigue siendo prisionero de los orcos? ¡Esto es exasperante, ${PLAYER}!\
\
Mi padre quería que buscara registros de nodos minados en Khazad-dûm, pero me niego a hacerlo mientras Bori siga cautivo. Si lo haces por mí, yo me quedaré e intentaré encontrar alguna forma de rescatar a Bori de las mazmorras de Mazog.\
\
Los registros mineros pueden encontrarse en los distintos archivos de la Gran Excavación: las Cámaras de Sabiduría, Conocimiento o Reflexión Profunda, y en Katûb-zahar. Un conjunto de registros mineros debería bastar para mi padre. Tráelos aquí cuando encuentres alguno. ¡Qué pérdida de tiempo!'","'El mensajero enviado por Bróin fue muy claro en que primero debíamos ocuparnos de la corrupción dentro de Buzun-ghâr. Pero una vez hecho esto, su maestro deseaba mucho que lo visitaras de nuevo en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada en la Sala de Reunión Militar, al este de Sulnul-dûm y al oeste del Salón de Piedra, aquí en el Camino de Durin. La entrada a la Senda Pacífica está al noreste de Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Si me permites esto, ${PLAYER}, debo decirte que Bróin no ha sido el mismo desde que lo devolviste con nosotros; no es culpa suya, pues soportó mucho en la guarida acuática del Vigilante, maldito sea su nombre, pero el hijo de Brogur puede estar ahora algo afectado. ¡Y luego perder a su primo Bori ante las fuerzas de Mazog! Eso no puede haber ayudado.\
\
Trátalo con amabilidad y paciencia, ${PLAYER}, pero si las peticiones que te haga parecen un poco peculiares, al menos sabrás la causa.'","Has encontrado registros mineros, pero contienen información curiosa.","Este cofre no contiene ningún registro minero.","Bróin no está seguro de qué hacer y quiere que le ayudes a encontrar alguna forma de ayudar a Bori, capturado por las fuerzas de Mazog.","Busca registros mineros para Bróin","'Hola de nuevo, ${PLAYER}. Mi mensajero regresó de Buzun-ghâr con la noticia de que estabas en las profundidades intentando acabar con la corrupción que se encontraba en ese pasaje; veo que tuviste éxito.'\
\
Bróin parece a punto de decir algo más, pero decide no hacerlo. Tras una pausa incómoda, comienza de nuevo, y esta vez las palabras salen en torrente.\
\
'¡No entiendo por qué desperdiciamos tanto esfuerzo en tareas tan insignificantes mientras mi primo Bori languidece en las mazmorras de Mazog! ¿Por qué los enanos de mi padre siguen minando mientras Bori está cautivo? Puede que ya no viva, pero si lo hace, así como yo sobreviví en la guarida acuática del Vigilante, ¿no será que cada hora que perdemos lo acerca más a la muerte a manos de los orcos? ¡Y aun así nadie hace nada!'\
\
Bróin respira hondo, esforzándose por calmarse.\
\
'Mi padre me ha pedido que busque registros de nodos minados en Khazad-dûm, pero no puedo dedicarme a un trabajo tan inútil. Si lo haces por mí, podré seguir pensando en alguna forma de ayudar a Bori. Busca estos registros en cualquiera de los viejos archivos en la Gran Excavación: las Cámaras de Sabiduría, Conocimiento o Reflexión Profunda, o en Katûb-zahar.'"},
[3237]={"Brogur te ha dicho que su sobrino Bori ha propuesto un plan audaz, que podría acelerar la reconquista de Khazad-dûm por los enanos.","'Gracias por ayudarme con los preparativos, ${PLAYER}. Estoy casi listo, pero... no, no es nada. Estoy listo.'","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has ayudado a Bori a prepararse para su audaz ataque contra la Mano Blanca, y ahora deberías informarle.","Ayuda a Bori con sus preparativos (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Mi sobrino Bori ha ideado un plan audaz, ${PLAYER}. Ha concebido un ataque de distracción contra una determinada sala de las Profundidades para atraer a los Orcos de la Mano Blanca fuera de su campamento; de esta manera, un segundo grupo podría entrar en el campamento y derrotar a su líder.\
\
'Será peligroso, para ambos grupos, pero es un buen plan. Imagínalo: con un solo golpe de hacha, ¡cortaremos la cabeza de la presencia de la Mano Blanca en Moria! Las preocupaciones de Bósi se calmarán ante tal victoria.\
\
'¿Ayudarás a mi sobrino Bori con los preparativos para este ataque? Aún llora por Bróin y siente que debe ganar honor por partida doble: por él mismo y por mi hijo caído. Si este ataque tiene éxito, lo habrá hecho.'","Capítulo 6: Honor suficiente para ambos","Bori se encuentra con Brogur en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Brogur te ha dicho que su sobrino Bori ha ideado un plan audaz para dar un golpe a los Orcos de la Mano Blanca en Moria, y quiere que le ayudes con sus preparativos.","Ayudaste a Bori con sus preparativos (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Habla con mi sobrino Bori aquí y ayúdale con los preparativos para su ataque contra los Orcos de la Mano Blanca, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[3238]={"Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has evaluado la fuerza de la fuerza en el cruce vigilado a lo largo de la Carretera Oriental y has encontrado dos entradas a Stazgnâkh, el campamento de la Mano Blanca entre las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.","'Un equipo de enanos liderará un ataque de distracción en un puesto avanzado en la Carretera Oriental para atraer a la fuerza principal de los Orcos de la Mano Blanca fuera de su campamento, Stazgnâkh. En ese momento, un segundo grupo entrará sigilosamente en Stazgnâkh y derrotará al líder de la Mano Blanca.\
\
'Necesito información sobre estos lugares, ${PLAYER}: examina la fuerza de la fuerza a lo largo de la Carretera Oriental y familiarízate con el diseño de Stazgnâkh. Quiero que recolectes barriles de pólvora negra dentro de Stazgnâkh y me los devuelvas; ¡debemos privarlos de esta arma peligrosa donde podamos! Investiga estos lugares y vuelve a mí con cualquier información que descubras.\
\
'Mi padre siempre me dice que la información es una de las armas más poderosas de un enano. ¡Cómo manejemos la información que traigas determinará el éxito de mi plan!'","Encuentra el cruce vigilado en la Carretera Oriental","El cruce vigilado en la Carretera Oriental se encuentra en Nud-melek, y el campamento de la Mano Blanca de Stazgnâkh está ubicado entre las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Bori te ha pedido que investigues el cruce vigilado a lo largo de la Carretera Oriental, y que recolectes barriles de pólvora negra del campamento de la Mano Blanca de Stazgnâkh para que te familiarices con él.","'No me has traído suficientes barriles de pólvora negra, ${PLAYER}.'","Capítulo 6: Planificando el ataque más sabio","El plan de Bori llama a un ataque de distracción en la Carretera Oriental para atraer a la fuerza principal de los Orcos de la Mano Blanca fuera de Stazgnâkh para que otro grupo de enanos pueda eliminar al líder.","Lleva los barriles de pólvora negra a Bori","Has evaluado la fuerza de la fuerza en el cruce vigilado","'Has hecho muy bien, ${PLAYER} -- la información que has traído será de gran valor mientras llevamos a cabo mi plan. ¡Gracias, mi ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}!'","'Stazgnâkh se encuentra entre las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo. Búscalo para encontrar barriles de pólvora negra, y espía también el cruce vigilado en la Carretera Oriental.'"},
[3239]={"Talk to Prince Ingór","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should place the crystals that you mined in the crystal planters scattered throughout Vérnozal.","Chapter 6: Return of the Noble Hall","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
You should decorate Vérnozal with Zhélruka runners for Prince Ingór.","'Aye, this hall is very welcoming now. Look around you, ${PLAYER}. You can almost see Gundabad as it once was, filled with life and beauty, as it soon will be again.\
\
'I believe that we have accomplished much on this day.'","Decorate Vérnozal with Zhélruka runners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to the Zhélruka and to fight on their behalf in Gundabad.","'The hall of Vérnozal does look more lived in, does it not? Still, the hall has yet to truly brighten. It needs to be a shining beacon of hope to all those who venture to Gundabad. Perhaps the hall needs to feel more like the homes from which we have all come.\
\
'${PLAYER}, you must help us give the hall of Vérnozal a more comforting touch, so it will remind us all of hearth and home. Here, take these floor runners and lay them throughout the hall.'","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.","'Good work! The hall feels more like a home already! Now what else is missing? Ah yes, crystals! Upon reflection, I have decided this hall does not have enough crystal in it.'\
\
Ingór smirks at you.\
\
'I have heard of a plentiful crystal mine in Gundabad where we can harvest some crystals for the hall. Go and mine some crystals for the hall of Vérnozal. The Zhélruka Clan is counting on you!'","Plant crystals in crystal planters throughout Vérnozal (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Planted crystals in crystal planters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[3240]={"'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para ir? Magor ha viajado por delante y te encontrará en Azanarukâr.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: La inspiración te ayudará si decides emprender este desafío. Esta instancia solo puede completarse en solitario o en grupo de dos personas.</rgb>","'Has enviado a Gwathnor y Grawulun sin forma a las profundidades, ${PLAYER}, ¡y no un momento demasiado pronto! No puedo decir si esta es la última de las reliquias dejadas por Gorothúl en Moria, pero al menos hemos ganado algo de tiempo.\
\
'Mientras Gorothúl siga vivo, también lo hace el peligro de que pueda crear más balizas como esta, una vez más atrayendo a Gwathnor o Grawulun... y la próxima vez puede que no los encontremos antes de que alcancen su nivel máximo de poder.\
\
'Debes ir ahora a Haldir en el flet justo fuera del Bosque de Oro. Dile que los enanos de la Guarnición de Hierro han acordado llevar a Mazog al Bosque Negro por una ruta indirecta que no pasará por Lothlórien, como se solicitó. Dile también que la expedición de la Hueste Dorada debe ocurrir con la mayor rapidez posible. ¡Demasiado retraso, y podríamos encontrarnos atrapados entre Dol Guldur por un lado y Gwathnor y Grawulun renacidos por el otro!'","Habla con Lenglammel para viajar a Azanarukâr","Lenglammel se encuentra en Gwathrendath, el campamento élfico entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Has destruido la reliquia de Gorothúl y enviado a Gwathnor y Grawulun sin forma a las profundidades, por un tiempo. Ahora deberías informar a Lenglammel.","'Nos estamos preparando para partir tan rápido como nos sea posible, , pero los preparativos de la Hueste Dorada no pueden apresurarse demasiado, no sea que condenemos su misión al fracaso. Tomará algún tiempo para que los enanos lleven a Mazog al borde del Bosque Negro, y eso permitirá que se realicen todos los preparativos necesarios.\
\
'Espero que estés ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]} cuando llegue ese momento, ${PLAYER}. Tanto los enanos de la Guarnición de Hierro como los elfos de Lothlórien confiarán en tu valor y habilidad. También espero que esta expedición no sea un error. Ha pasado mucho tiempo desde que el bosque llevaba el nombre del Gran Bosque Verde.\
\
'Te veré de nuevo, , cuando llegue el momento.'","Habla con Lenglammel en Gwathrendath","'Magor se aventura en las profundidades desde que lo rescataste, ${PLAYER}, diciendo solo que considera que es su deber personal evitar que los peligros sin nombre de Azanarukâr salgan de allí.\
\
'En su viaje más reciente a través de los fuegos de esas cavernas, vio a un número de Regmyl transportando lo que parecía ser un ídolo de alguna importancia maligna. Los siguió por un tiempo, pero en un momento dado parecieron darse cuenta de su presencia, y encontró necesario retirarse.\
\
'Reúne tus fuerzas y háblame, ${PLAYER}. Te llevaré hasta Magor. Juntos, deben regresar a Azanarukâr, averiguar si el ídolo de los Regmyl es una reliquia de Gorothúl y destruirlo.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: la inspiración te ayudará si decides emprender este desafío. Esta instancia solo puede ser completada por un grupo de uno o dos jugadores.</rgb>","Habla con Haldir en Talan Haldir","Lenglammel se encuentra en Gwathrendath, el campamento élfico entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Lenglammel está esperando para hablar contigo y llevarte a Magor para un asalto a Azanarukâr.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: La inspiración te ayudará si decides emprender este desafío. Esta instancia solo puede ser completada por un grupo de uno o dos jugadores.</rgb>","Lenglammel te dijo que otra de las reliquias de Gorothúl ha sido encontrada en las profundidades de Azanarukâr y debe ser destruida.","'Apresúrate a Talan Haldir, ${PLAYER}, con el mensaje de que la Hueste Dorada debe partir tan pronto como sea posible.'","Haldir se encuentra en Talan Haldir, justo fuera de la frontera del Bosque de Oro.\
\
Lenglammel te ha enviado a Haldir para transmitirle un mensaje importante: la expedición de la Hueste Dorada debe llevarse a cabo lo antes posible.","Capítulo 6: Regreso a Azanarukâr"},
[3241]={"'Has llegado a Ost Galadh, ${PLAYER}, donde la Hueste Dorada se prepara para la siguiente etapa de su viaje. ¿Es el camino de los Malledhrim también el camino de la Guardia Oculta? No sé si debería serlo, pero si debe serlo, al menos aprenderemos qué peligros hay a lo largo de él.\
\
Viaja al este de Ost Galadh y mantén los ojos abiertos por los enemigos en el camino. A medida que el camino sube hacia Minas Gîl, hay piedras erguida a un lado del camino. Quizás puedas esconderte detrás de estas piedras y aprender cuál es la presencia orca en Emyn Lûm.'","'No puedo recomendar el camino recto a través de Emyn Lûm para la Guardia Oculta.'","Habla con Enedhel en Ost Galadh","Enedhel está en Ost Galadh, en Emyn Lûm.\
\
Te has escondido detrás de las piedras erguidas en el camino hacia Minas Gîl, al este de Ost Galadh, y ahora deberías regresar a Enedhel con lo que has aprendido.","El camino al este de Ost Galadh es la ruta más directa hacia la fortaleza de Dol Guldur.","'Está claro que el Enemigo está vigilando el camino recto a través de Emyn Lûm.'","Se pueden encontrar piedras erguidas a lo largo del camino inclinado hacia Minas Gîl, al este de Ost Galadh.\
\
Enedhel te ha pedido que te escondas detrás de las piedras erguidas en el camino hacia Minas Gîl para aprender qué tan de cerca los Orcos están vigilando el camino oriental hacia Dol Guldur.","Escóndete detrás de las piedras erguidas en el camino hacia Minas Gîl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Te escondes detrás de la piedra erguida","'El camino al este de Dol Guldur puede estar vigilado por los Orcos, ${PLAYER}. Viaja al este de Ost Galadh y escóndete detrás de las piedras erguidas que bordean el camino hacia Minas Gîl. Puede que aprendas algo sobre la presencia orca en Emyn Lûm.'","Capítulo 6: Reconocimiento de Emyn Lûm","'Veo, ${PLAYER}. Parece que los Orcos están vigilando muy de cerca el camino a través de Emyn Lûm. Lo que es seguro para la Hueste Dorada no es seguro para la misión de la Guardia Oculta.\
\
'No puedo recomendar este camino a Cúcheron. La Guardia Oculta debe encontrar otro camino hacia Dol Guldur... un camino secreto. El paso por Emyn Lûm está demasiado vigilado.'"},
[3242]={"Tomas nota de la presencia de orcos en Krul Lugu","Encuentra a Malendol dentro o alrededor de Krul Lugu","Erymbes se encuentra en el Santuario Verde, al norte de los campamentos orcos de Krul Lugu, en Taur Morvith.\
\
Has explorado los campamentos orcos de Krul Lugu y defendido a Malendol, y ahora deberías regresar con Erymbes para informarle de lo que has aprendido.","Malendol puede estar en algún lugar dentro o alrededor de las fortificaciones orcas de Krul Lugu, en Taur Morvith.\
\
Has evaluado la presencia de orcos en Krul Lugu y ahora deberías buscar a Malendol, que podría estar en problemas.","Capítulo 6: Reconocimiento de Taur Morvith","Has defendido con éxito a Malendol","'${PLAYER}, ¿vienes de Krul Lugu? Fui a explorar esos campamentos orcos, pero más orcos salieron marchando desde el este, desde Dol Guldur, y no pude reunirme con Erymbes en el norte. He estado descansando para recuperar mis fuerzas antes de intentar llegar allí.\
\
'Aún no estoy a mi plena fuerza, y más orcos vienen del sur. ¡Debes ayudarme!'","'Hay un gran número de campamentos orcos en Taur Morvith, ${PLAYER}. No sé si la ruta del sur es el camino ideal que la Guardia Oculta deba tomar para llegar a Dol Guldur. Mi amigo Malendol se dirigió hacia el sur para investigar, pero no ha regresado.\
\
'Si vas hacia el sur y exploras los dos fuertes orcos que hay allí, podrías encontrar alguna señal de mi amigo. Si la presencia de orcos es tan grande como para causarle problemas, ciertamente es demasiado peligroso para la Guardia Oculta llevar a Mazog por ese camino.\
\
'Esperemos que Malendol no esté en Krul Lugu mismo, pero deberías comenzar tu búsqueda allí, por si lo peor ha ocurrido.'","Krul Lugu es el nombre orco de un par de fortificaciones orcas en el centro de Taur Morvith, al sur del Santuario Verde.\
\
Erymbes te ha pedido que investigues la presencia de orcos en Krul Lugu y que luego busques a su amigo Malendol.","Evalúa la presencia de orcos en Krul Lugu","Habla con Erymbes en el Santuario Verde","'Quiero que evalúes la presencia de orcos en Krul Lugu, las fortificaciones orcas situadas al sur, en el centro de Taur Morvith, y que luego busques a mi amigo Malendol.'","'Debes buscar a mi amigo Malendol dentro o alrededor de las fortificaciones orcas de Krul Lugu, al sur, en el centro de Taur Morvith. ¡Podría estar en peligro!'","Los orcos tienen una fuerte presencia en Taur Morvith.","'Gracias por explorar los campamentos orcos de Krul Lugu y por ayudar a Malendol, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Con lo que tienes que decir sobre la presencia de orcos en Taur Morvith, debo recomendar a la Guardia Oculta que la ruta del sur hacia Dol Guldur no es segura. Llevar al orco Mazog por este camino sería realmente imprudente.\
\
'Deben encontrar otro camino hacia la fortaleza, un camino que preserve el secreto de su misión.'"},
[3243]={"Lleva el paño con las muestras de veneno a Gladiel junto al Santuario del Antiguo","Las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas representan un peligro para todos los que pasan por allí, pero aún queda por determinar cuán grande es la amenaza para la Guardia Oculta.","'Una sola araña no tiene suficiente veneno para ser un peligro real. ¡Evita los grupos!'","'Las fuerzas del Enemigo no parecen estar vigilando las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.'","'Todavía estoy esperando que recojas muestras de veneno de las arañas en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, ${PLAYER}.'","'Usa el paño que te di para recolectar muestras de veneno de las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, y determinaré cuán peligrosa puede ser esta ruta para la Guardia Oculta.'","Habla con Gladiel junto al Santuario del Antiguo","'Las Hondonadas Enmarañadas son intrincadas y salvajes, y sus arañas son mortales.'","'¡Salve, ${CLASS}, te doy la bienvenida, camarada, porque no he visto nada más que arañas y perros negros durante tres días, y es bueno hablar finalmente con alguien considerado aliado. Una gran oscuridad se cierne sobre este rincón del bosque, probablemente emanando de los túmulos justo al norte de aquí; nadie ha cuidado esos túmulos durante una era, y ahora son hogar solo de males... ¡y las arañas están por todas partes!\
\
'No puedo recomendar que la Guardia Oculta pase por aquí hasta que sepamos con certeza cuán mortal puede ser el veneno de estas arañas. Parece que los ojos de Dol Guldur no están vigilando las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, pero eso no será un alivio para ninguno de los miembros de nuestra compañía que caigan ante las arañas en nombre del secreto!\
\
'Toma este paño y úsalo para recoger el veneno de las arañas muertas aquí en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas; veré cuán peligroso puede ser.'","Recolecta muestras de veneno de las arañas en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se pueden encontrar arañas en todas las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.\
\
Gladiel te ha pedido que recojas veneno de las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas usando el paño que te dio.","Capítulo 6: Reconocimiento de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas","'Muéstrame las muestras de veneno que has recolectado usando el paño que te di, ${PLAYER}.\
\
En cantidades tan pequeñas como las que encontrarías con una sola araña, este veneno te hará sentir mal, pero no debería tener efectos duraderos. Dosis grandes del veneno serían más serias, por supuesto, pero puedo recomendar el paso a través de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas a los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta, siempre y cuando puedan limitar la exposición a grandes números de estas arañas mientras pasan.'","Gladiel está junto al Santuario del Antiguo, en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.\
\
Has recolectado varias muestras de veneno de las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas y deberías devolverlas a Gladiel para que las examine.","Muestras de veneno recolectadas de arañas en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[3244]={"'Esto es lo que esperaba, ${PLAYER}: pregunta a tres Elfos qué camino es mejor tomar y recibirás tres respuestas, cada una diferente.\
\
'Nos queda poco tiempo para perder. Quiero que explores estas rutas propuestas, mi complaciente ${CLASS}, y evalúes los peligros de cada una.\
\
'Quizás eso nos ayude a tomar una decisión. Busca a los exploradores que enviamos a las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, Emyn Lûm y Taur Morvith y pregúntales sobre los peligros que han encontrado.'","'Estos Elfos deben llegar a un acuerdo sobre lo que hay que hacer a continuación, ${PLAYER}, ¡o perderemos aún más tiempo en la inactividad!'","Ayuda a Enedhel en Ost Galadh, en Emyn Lûm","'He decidido lo que debemos hacer, ${PLAYER}. El camino a través de Taur Morvith nos acercaría demasiado a los campamentos de orcos en ese valle, y estamos seguros de que el camino directo a través de Emyn Lûm, por el que marchará la Hueste Dorada|, ya está siendo vigilado. No, nuestro camino pasa por las Hondonadas Enmarañadas. Será peligroso, pero eso mismo servirá como un manto para los ojos espías.\
\
'Habla con Issuriel en la bodega de esta posada y dile que he elegido el camino que ella sugirió.'","Cúcheron se encuentra fuera de la Posada Embrujada, ubicada entre los Troncosombríos.\
\
Has obtenido las opiniones de los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta sobre qué ruta tomar hacia Dol Guldur y has recibido tres propuestas diferentes.","Cúcheron está fuera de la Posada Embrujada, en los Troncosombríos.\
\
Has hecho lo que Cúcheron te pidió al reunir información sobre las posibles rutas hacia Dol Guldur y ahora deberías regresar con él.","'Issuriel se encuentra en la bodega de esta posada. Dile que he decidido que el camino de la Guardia Oculta debe pasar por las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, aunque sea peligroso.'","Capítulo 6: La elección de los caminos","Ayuda a Gladiel en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas","Los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta se han encontrado con una dificultad: con la muerte de Raddir, ninguno de ellos sabe con certeza qué ruta había planeado para llevarlos a Dol Guldur en secreto.","'La muerte del Elfo Raddir ha hecho incierto el destino de este viaje, ${PLAYER}, ya que ninguno de los Elfos sabe por qué camino planeaba llevarnos en secreto a Dol Guldur.\
\
'Habla con los Elfos aquí en la bodega y trata de decidir el curso adecuado. Alguien debe dar un paso adelante y tomar el mando, o será el próximo invierno antes de que avancemos siquiera un solo paso... ¿y quién sabe qué le sucederá a Bori mientras tanto?'","Habla con Cúcheron en la Posada Embrujada","'Raddir nos llevó al Bosque Ahogado a pesar del peligro por una razón, ${PLAYER}. Debe haber planeado que tomáramos el camino más al sur hacia Dol Guldur y que nos llevara en secreto hasta la base sur del pináculo rocoso sobre el que se encuentra la fortaleza.\
\
'Por lo tanto, deberíamos dirigirnos hacia el sur a través de las zonas rocosas de Taur Morvith. Estoy seguro de que ese es el camino que Raddir quería que tomáramos.\
\
'Los otros miembros de la compañía pueden no estar de acuerdo, pero al menos debemos salir, o su muerte habrá sido en vano.'","'Hemos enviado exploradores por delante, ${PLAYER}, como solemos hacer; búscalos en los lugares salvajes y pregúntales qué peligros han descubierto. Encuéntralos en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, Emyn Lûm y Taur Morvith.'","Los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta se encuentran en la bodega de la Posada Embrujada.\
\
Bróin te ha pedido que vayas a hablar con los Elfos de la Guardia secreta sobre lo que debe hacerse a continuación.","Ayuda a Erymbes en Taur Morvith","'Terminemos con los caminos secretos. El curso más directo, como una flecha rápida, es el que deberíamos tomar ahora si queremos evitar un destino similar.'","'Veo, ${PLAYER}. No sé si debo alegrarme de que nuestro camino nos lleve a las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, pero mi corazón me dice que este es el camino que debemos seguir.\
\
'Hay una cosa más, ${PLAYER}. Dudo en mencionarlo, pero algo me ha estado preocupando durante un tiempo...'","Issuriel se encuentra en la bodega de la Posada Embrujada, situada entre los Troncosombríos.\
\
Basándose en la información que has proporcionado, Cúcheron ha decidido que la ruta propuesta por Issuriel hacia Dol Guldur tiene la mayor probabilidad de éxito. Quiere que le informes que este es el camino que tomará la Guardia Oculta.","'El Enemigo nunca esperaría que tomáramos el camino a través de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, ya que ese lugar tiene una reputación peligrosa. Ese es el camino de mayor secreto, y solo a través de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas llegaremos a Dol Guldur con nuestro prisionero y nuestra presencia sin ser anunciados.'","'No podemos esperar aquí una revelación que puede que no llegue, ${PLAYER}: nunca sabremos qué camino Raddir tenía pensado para nosotros.\
\
'No, debemos decidir y decidir rápido. El camino rápido será el camino más seguro. Movámonos directamente hacia el este a Dol Guldur por el camino más directo; Raddir creía que nuestra mayor fortaleza estaba en el secreto, pero el peligroso camino a través del Bosque Ahogado le costó la vida.\
\
'Terminemos con los caminos secretos. El curso más directo, como una flecha rápida, es el que ahora deberíamos tomar si queremos evitar un destino similar.'","Tres exploradores han sido enviados a las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, Emyn Lûm y Taur Morvith.\
\
Cúcheron te ha pedido que hables con los Elfos que envió a investigar las áreas a lo largo de las rutas propuestas por la Guardia Oculta. Gladiel está en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, al oeste del Santuario del Antiguo, cerca de la frontera de Gathbúrz. Erymbes está en Taur Morvith, junto al Santuario Verde, al sur de la Ruina Salvaje. Enedhel está en Ost Galadh.","'No sé qué hacer, ${PLAYER}. Creo que Raddir pensaba acercarse a Dol Guldur por los caminos menos propensos a ser vigilados por las fuerzas del Enemigo, pero nuestra incursión en el Bosque Ahogado...\
\
'Tengo que creer que Raddir sabía lo que estaba haciendo, ${PLAYER}, y que conocía los riesgos. Pero aún así nos llevó al Bosque Ahogado; debe haber tenido una buena razón para hacerlo.\
\
'El Enemigo nunca esperaría que tomáramos el camino a través de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, porque ese lugar tiene una reputación peligrosa. Ese es el camino del mayor secreto, y solo a través de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas llegaremos a Dol Guldur con nuestro prisionero y nuestra presencia sin ser anunciados.'","'Como esperaba, los Elfos no pueden ponerse de acuerdo sobre esto, y ningún miembro de esta compañía tiene el poder de simplemente decir qué ruta tomarán.\
\
'Sal de la Posada Embrujada y dile a Cúcheron las opiniones de los Elfos... y dile también que no podemos perder más tiempo en la inactividad!'","'Deberíamos dirigirnos al sur a través de las profundidades rocosas de Taur Morvith. Estoy seguro de que ese es el camino que Raddir quería que tomáramos.'","Habla con los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta","Habla con Issuriel en la Posada Embrujada"},
[3246]={"'To begin with, they shan't be in Udûn any longer. I have looked at the maps, and they were nearly to Dor Amarth when we found them. If the wretches still think there is someone in Barad-dûr to buy their miserable tidings, then that is where they have gone.\
\
'That, then, is where you should begin your search for them.'","'You again? I should have guessed. Didn't bring your two little friends along, did you? Too dangerous, eh? Well, no matter.'\
\
The half-orc is seized by a painful coughing fit.\
\
'Not going to strike me? You've only come to mock me, then. Laugh at how there's no Red Eye in that tumble-down tower out yonder. Nothing worth selling and no one a-buying. Nothing but malice *cough* *cough* and death and illusions out here in this cursed place. I have half a mind that you're an illusion, yourself. Ptah!\
\
'I suppose you'd love to know all about your precious *cough* *hack* - precious Shire and the rest of that rot. The Wizard's got his designs on it, he does, and he's been in and out of there for some years. Oh, don't let that sour look spoil your pretty face. He's got plenty of improvements planned, he and that Lotho do. Plenty underway, even now. Why, there's even a gate on the Brandywine Bridge, now.\
\
'Ah ha! Ha ha *cough* *cough* *hack*...ugh. Oh. Leave me, wretched ${RACE}. Leave me to die in peace.'","Habla con Merry","Habla con el Semiorco","You should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion to hear what, exactly, they are thinking about with regard to Mordor.","There can be no mistaking it: this was one of the two remaining half-orcs, come to a bitter end","Habla con Gandalf","Return to Bâr Thorenion","Habla con Pippin","Pippin and Merry have asked you to go in search of the two half-orcs who fled the last encounter. You have found one of them, come to a bitter end, on the path to Barad-dûr, and should examine the corpse.","'There you are! What a grave face. Tell us what you have learned. Please, I cannot take the suspense a moment more.'\
\
Choosing your words carefully, you confirm what the two hobbits believed they knew - that the Wizard must have been Saruman and that he had designs on the Shire. You suggest more generally that the Shire they return to might not quite be the Shire as they left it, but, with the words of Gandalf ringing in your ears, can bring yourself to tell them no more.\
\
After a long pause, Merry finally speaks.\
\
'I see then. Those fellows worked for Saruman, then, and fled him hoping to profit from a new master. Rotten luck for rotten apples, I say! And so all those barrels of pipe-weed were for more than his own smoking habits, I take it. Still, I don't see how much harm that can do. There is only so much Hornblower farmed each season, and if too much goes missing it is sure to be noticed.\
\
'Pippin, ${PLAYER}, can we make a pact not to burden Frodo or Sam with this? They have been through enough, and if there is trouble of some kind in the Shire, I had far rather they learn that when we get there, and not have it spoil these golden days of celebration. It shall weigh on my own heart enough, I know, though I think I shall work hard to forget about it awhile.\
\
'And yet, I know I cannot forget about going home any longer. That I shall remember every moment from this time forward, I am afraid.'","You should talk to Merry in Bâr Thorenion to hear his thoughts on where the two remaining half-orcs might be.","Pippin and Merry have asked you to go in search of the two half-orcs who fled the last encounter. Tracks leading from the corpse of the first have led at last to the second, who lives still. You should talk to him and learn what you can.","Chapter 6:  The Last Word","'How glad I am you are here, ${PLAYER}. If you wish to know the truth, we were just talking about you.\
\
'You see, we could not stop thinking about the two of those fellows who fled, and what they might know, and how they are still out there in Mordor. And we thought to ourselves, we made a promise to Frodo and not for all the world would we break it. But ${PLAYER} made no such vow! Oh, but you see where this is going, don't you? You are clever enough for a ${RACE}, and no doubt about it!\
\
'And anyway, we have heard some of the adventures you have had out there, and know you will be going back out there, anyway. While you are there, why not track down those two fellows? Oh, say you will, ${PLAYER}, won't you? \
\
'Merry, you say the bit about where they might be.'","On returning to Bâr Thorenion, Gandalf has appeared and beckoned you over to speak with him.","'Hold a moment, ${PLAYER}. I know where you have been and guess what you have learned, for I have known the truth of it myself for some little while, though through somewhat different means.\
\
'You cannot, of course, withhold the truth from Pippin and Merry in any broad sense, but allow me to counsel you that they need not hear every painful detail you have learned.\
\
'Think for a moment, of the many days of happiness that lie ahead, and the bitter challenge that lies in wait for them after the long road home. Does that foreknowledge bear any good? I do not think it does. Prepare them for the hard truth when they can see it with their own eyes, for that is an honest kindness, but perhaps, no more.\
\
'Weigh my words and act on your own judgment. That is all I ask.'","A look of abject misery and fear is etched across the half-orc's lifeless face. Signs of a struggle on the ground about him clearly show marks of both pursuer and pursued, bearing roughly east.","Although they promised Frodo they would not return to that land, Pippin and Merry find their thoughts turning back towards Mordor once again.","'I have word that Masters Peregrin and Meriadoc wish to speak with you, ${PLAYER}. It has something to do with Mordor, though I know nothing more of the matter. They will, of course, be found in Bâr Thorenion.'","Found the final half-orc","Pippin and Merry have asked you to go in search of the two half-orcs who fled the last encounter. Merry believes they will be found somewhere in Dor Amarth, on the path to Barad-dûr.","Search for the half-orcs","Sigue el rastro","Examine the dead half-orc","Return to Merry and Pippin in Bâr Thorenion with news of what you learned from the dying half-orc.","You should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion, telling them at least some of the whole truth, as Gandalf counselled you.","'Pippin, you explain.'","Gandalf is here and beckons you over","Pippin and Merry have asked you to go in search of the two half-orcs who fled the last encounter. You should follow the trail leading from the one half-orc, in hopes of finding the other.","The tracks of the final half-orc lead onward","'${PLAYER}! There you are. Do you have a moment? We have been discussing Mordor.'"},
[3247]={"'At last it is time. Come now, ${PLAYER}, and tell no one where we go.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'King Elessar will be glad to hear of our conquests in Mordor, ${PLAYER}. Give him my regards too, and my wish that he will one day join us as we sojourn!'","Talk to Mithrandir in the throne room and stand guard","'King Elessar waits for you in the throne room with Mithrandir. Perhaps you should learn what brings the Wizard here, for he is not often seen in the city these days.'","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Elessar and the Kingdom of Gondor, and to fight on their behalf in Mordor.","Mithrandir has come to the throne room of King Elessar, atop Minas Tirith.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, I expected you before this. Well, it is good that you are here now!\
\
'There are words I must speak to Aragorn, but I do not wish to be interrupted. This room will not do; there are too many guards about! Enough safety for a king, but too many listening ears.\
\
'I have a place in mind where Aragorn and I may speak away from his guards. Fear not! His person will be safe, for I would have you attend us and stand guard. You will prevent any interruptions, especially by members of the Withered Tree that might seek to harm the king. Speak to me when you are ready to go, and we will wait for nightfall.'","Talk to King Elessar in his throne room","King Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.","Talk to Mithrandir in King Elessar's throne room","'It was from an abundance of caution that I asked you to attend us, ${PLAYER}, for I feared interruption by those calling themselves the Withered Tree. I am pleased that no such marauder sought to do harm to Aragorn or to the scion of Nimloth. Indeed, I think now that no man of Gondor could bring himself to damage the young sapling, if he knew what it portended: a sign of growing goodness in the years to come.'","'For how long did the fruit of the last tree lie hidden above the city, ${PLAYER}? Long years indeed, though the sapling has yet to reach seven years of growth! I will take Mithrandir's advice to heart, and when ever the fruit ripens it shall be planted, so the line of the tree will not vanish from the world. The Wizard's lesson was not subtle; it is not lost on me that the line of kings is much the same. There is time yet, and my heart is lightened by this discovery!\
\
'Thank you for your part in this, my friend. The sapling should be planted in the Court of the Fountain, and let the folk of the city draw hope from the sight!'","Chapter 6: The Wizard and the King"},
[3248]={"'I and my brother will stand with you to rescue Thorongil, ${PLAYER}. Will we not, Corudan? Or have you had your fill of this place already?'","You have found the Hungry Deep Tavern, a popular eating and drinking establishment","'I am not one for gossip, friend, but I have heard a thing or two about the Kindred of the Coins that you might find interesting! For the right price, that is....'\
\
As you consider how you might get this man to tell you what he knows without having to part with too much coin, his eyes suddenly widen.\
\
'I... I have to be going. I know nothing! Nothing!'","Chapter 7.1: Asking Questions","Find the Hungry Deep Tavern that overlooks the Sail-haven","'We will stand with them, will we not, Corudan?'","Daxamat is at the amphitheatre outside the city.","'I will stand with you, ${PLAYER}, not only because of your rescue, and not only because of the adventures we shared in the Kingdom of Rohan. I will stand with you because it is right.\
\
'I was not mistreated by the Kindred of the Coins, despite Nakási's words and her frequent promises to exact revenge upon any who aid Gondor. At sea I was given permission to walk freely about the ship, and I followed her commands quickly and well. Did my captivity chafe? I cannot say it did not, but I felt it was in service of a noble purpose, and that was enough. Tatháta suggested I be allowed to walk freely about the ships and the harbour when we docked, but the Wave-reaper feared my servility was an act, and commanded her kinswoman to keep me tied to the mast while Nakási was away. I cannot tell you with complete certainty if she was right, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'But I can tell you this. The Kindred of the Coins value their captives only for so long as they retain value. Had I proven a burden or unmanageable, I think I would not have survived the voyage to Umbar. It may be the same with the young heir of Pinnath Gelin. If he loses his value as a hostage, I believe he will not long survive in the Kindred's company.\
\
'Nakási brought him to Azagath Sea-shadow in the Citadel of Winds, from where the Kindred rule this city. I will help you as I can... but how do you intend to enter the most well-guarded district of Umbar Baharbêl?'","'When my brother and I returned to Umbar, his plan had been for us to visit some of the taverns and inns of the city so we could learn what had happened while we were gone, recruit a larger crew, and Jajax could acquire a more suitable ship. That plan ran into some trouble! But I think at its heart it was still a good idea, because at taverns people speak more freely. If there is any way into the Citadel of Winds, someone at one of the taverns may unknowingly speak of it.\
\
'I hope I am not being too forward with this suggestion! But it makes sense to me, ${PLAYER}. If everyone splits up and checks different taverns in the city, we may more quickly learn of a means of rescuing Thorongil from Azagath.'","The Whelk and Cockle Tavern is not as busy as the Hungry Deep","The folk here seem to be studiously avoiding your gaze.","Talk to patrons of the Hungry Deep Tavern (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The Whelk and Cockle Tavern is not as popular as the last one you visited, but patrons here may still know something.","Rothog the Storm is at the Whelk and Cockle Tavern in the Sail-haven.","Talk to Corudan at the amphitheatre","Rothog the Storm has come to the Sail-haven","Part of your mission has been completed... but half of it remains, for Thorongil is still a prisoner of the Kindred of the Coins.","'You. ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Rothog stares down at you impassively, his face a mask.\
\
'Hármelak wants to see you,' he says.","Talked to patrons of the Hungry Deep Tavern (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The Hungry Deep Tavern is located up a set of stairs in the Upper Ward, from where it overlooks the Sail-haven.","'If everyone splits up and checks different taverns in the city, we may more quickly learn of a means of rescuing Thorongil from Azagath.'","Patrons of the Hungry Deep Tavern may have information of use to you.","'I am worried for our rulers. I heard a rumour that the widow of Balakhôr the Scourge has offered bounties on the leaders of the Kindred of the Coins, and even now her trained killers are loose in the city! They say no one has seen Tumúldo Fierce-water in weeks, and even Tatháta the Beast is missing. She often walked the streets of the Lower Ward, her fighting-hounds by her side, but I cannot remember the last time she did.\
\
'We owe the Kindred much for dealing with the Heirs of Castamir and releasing us from the shackles of Ordâkh. I hope they are all right.'","Daxamat suggests you speak with patrons at two taverns in the Sail-haven and Upper Ward","Talk to Rothog the Storm outside the Whelk and Cockle Tavern","Talk to patrons of the Whelk and Cockle Tavern (${NUMBER}/2)","The Whelk and Cockle Tavern is located to the west of the Hungry Deep, in the Sail-haven.","Find the Whelk and Cockle Tavern to the west, in the Sail-haven","Talk to Daxamat at the amphitheatre","A hush falls over the people nearby","What has caused this sudden stillness?","'How do you intend to enter the most well-guarded district of Umbar Baharbêl?'","Daxamat clears his throat, seeking your attention","'The Hungry Deep Tavern is the finest in the city, if you ask me. Every time I come here I eat too much.\
\
'The Kindred of the Coins? They mean well, and if you ask me they have done right by us, but I think they keep secrets from us all the same. Seven of them there are, you know that, but there has been turnover among their ranks since the uprising. Some say Guild-master Imilka was in league with the Heirs of Castamir and Tatháta was right to replace her in the Kindred... but I don't know. And there was another, a scholar whose name I misremember... whatever happened to him? He ruled in the Tor-gardens, but now he is gone and that half-troll, Rothog, has his place in the Kindred! He frightens me.\
\
'Oh, when I eat too much I also speak too much! Favour me and tell no one of these things I have said.'","Corudan is at the amphitheatre outside the city."},
[3249]={"This is the entrance to the recently-delved New-lodes of Narathâk","Chapter 7.1: Inside the Lonely Mountain","'Welcome to Mesem-azhâr. If you are a friend of my son, you may come and go as you like. All I ask is that you follow the Gem-cutter family rules: when you come to the Jewelstead you never complain, you keep in good cheer, and you help us with our work.'","Gandalf was given a residence within the Lonely Mountain and plans to retire there to study while you help the Gem-cutters with their day-to-day work.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, I hoped you would find time to visit! This is Mesem-azhâr, the Jewelstead, home to my family for many years. It is a humble place, but the hearth is warm and you are welcome to stave off the chill of the heights whenever you have need!\
\
'My father Fúni and my brother Fúsi have not yet returned from their excursion on the other side of the Misty Mountains, but I will be pleased to introduce you to my mother, and to another of my brothers who remains in Erebor.\
\
'Mother Amma! This is ${PLAYER}, the ${RACE} I mentioned to you!'","Mother Amma has asked you to pick up the finely-crafted necklace and deliver it to Erfith, the customer who requested it. Erfith can be found on the west side of the Dwelling-halls of Erebor, on one of the lower levels.","The entrance to the New-lodes of Narathâk is located east of the Dwelling-halls, beyond the passage that runs from the entryway to the Hall Under the Mountain.","Authi's brother Gráfar Splitstone has asked you to carry a crate of precious stones back to Mother Amma in the Jewelstead. The Gem-cutter family home is located in the south-west corner of the Dwelling-halls.","You have found the entrance to the Jewelstead, home of the Gem-cutter family","'I had expected the delivery to come from one of the Gem-cutters themselves, but so long as I have the piece I requested I suppose it is worth no complaint. There is something about the personal touch that turns an ordinary customer into a repeat customer, if you ask me, but apparently that is not something everyone believes. Unless...'\
\
Erfith trails off, and looks at you conspiratorially.\
\
'I heard a rumour that the Gem-cutters might have fallen on hard times and they plan to leave Erebor in disgrace. I am not saying it is true, just that I heard of it from the tale-spinner Khîl, and if the Gem-cutters have chosen to delegate their responsibilities to others then perhaps there is some truth in it.\
\
'Thank you for the delivery, even so. I will miss the Gem-cutters when they depart Erebor, even if their service has lost the touch of the personal that first made me interested in their pieces. Do you think this has something to do with Fúni's long departure? He brought one of the sons with him, but left the others with his wife. I heard from Khîl that they might rejoin him and start a new life away across the Misty Mountains, but I don't know that I believe that part of it.'","Talk to Mother Amma in the Jewelstead","Pick up the finely-crafted necklace and deliver it to Erfith on the west side of the Dwelling-halls","Defeated vermin in the New-lodes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The New-lodes of Narathâk have been recently delved, and can be found east of here, beyond the passage that runs from the entryway to the Hall Under the Mountain. My brother spends most of his waking hours mining for the precious gems we need to further our craft. There has always been great demand for the jewellery my family fashions, and Gráfar works hard to ensure we have what we need to meet it!'","Authi Gem-cutter's brother Gráfar is in the New-lodes of Narathâk.","Someone named Khîl has been spreading rumours about the Gem-cutters","The home of Authi Gem-cutter and his family can be found in the south-western corner of the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","The New-lodes of Narathâk are crawling with cave-claws and other pests, and Authi's brother Gráfar asked you to help make the mine safe for the miners by thinning out some of the vermin.","'You should familiarize yourself with Erebor and its people. Perhaps you can lend some assistance to Authi Gem-cutter and his family? I am certain they would welcome your company, and will not mind showing you around.\
\
'I believe you will find Authi's home in the Dwelling-halls, located south of the Hall Under the Mountain and to the west.'","'You will deliver the necklace to Erfith? Better you than me, ${PLAYER}. We all call him Erfith the Quarrelsome, and it is a well-deserved moniker, I assure you. You'll usually find him on the west side of the Dwelling-halls, down on one of the lower levels. I saw him not long ago to the east and down the stairs, but he might have moved on since then.'","Defeat vermin in the New-lodes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I heard a rumour that the Gem-cutters might have fallen on hard times and they plan to leave Erebor in disgrace. I am not saying it is true, just that I heard of it from the tale-spinner Khîl, and if the Gem-cutters have chosen to delegate their responsibilities to others then perhaps there is some truth in it.'","Find the home of Authi Gem-cutter in the Dwelling-halls","'Ah, you must be ${PLAYER}! Authi speaks highly of you, and tells me you can hold your own in a good old-fashioned tavern brawl. Are you also adept at clearing mines of vermin? Every new delve we dig seems to unearth all manner of unpleasant pests, and these New-lodes are no exception.\
\
'I have a crate of precious stones ready to return to Mother Amma and I could use someone to carry it, but if you could first thin the ranks of the cave-claws and other irritations in Narathâk I would be ever at your service.'","'How did it go, ${PLAYER}? Did Erfith the Quarrelsome find something about which to complain?'\
\
You reluctantly recount the rumour that Erfith mentioned to you, about the Gem-cutters leaving Erebor in disgrace, and Authi's cheerful face twists angrily.\
\
'Leave the Lonely Mountain? And in disgrace? What rubbish! Where did Erfith hear this nonsense? Who is spreading these lies about my family?'","'Erfith requested a fine necklace some weeks ago, and it is now ready to deliver to him. He paid us a tidy sum for it, but it took quite a long time to make and he had better appreciate it. Do not say this to his face, but his neighbours call him \\qErfith the Quarrelsome,\\q so I would not put it past him to find some defect or flaw with the work.\
\
'You should be able to find Erfith on the west side of the Dwelling-halls, on one of the lower levels. Look to the east and down the stairs.'","Mother Amma nods at you, and indicates she has a necklace that needs delivering","Talk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead","Talk to Gráfar Splitstone in the New-lodes of Narathâk","'King Thorin has given to me a room in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor, and I will retire there to think upon what we have discovered. The efforts of the Gúrzyul to increase their power in the wake of Sauron's passing are of interest to me, particularly those of Karazgar here in the north. Durin's Folk have provided me with several leads to study, and I shall follow each of them as far as I am able.\
\
'Such courses of study are lonely pastimes, but they are rarely fruitless. I will see you when I have learned what I may, but while I am so engaged I suggest you familiarize yourself with Erebor and its people. Perhaps you can lend some assistance to Authi Gem-cutter and his family? I am certain they would welcome your company, and will not mind showing you around.\
\
'I believe you will find Authi's home in the Dwelling-halls, located south of the Hall Under the Mountain and to the west.'","'Welcome to Mesem-azhâr, ${PLAYER}. If you are a friend of my son, you may come and go as you like. All I ask is that you follow the Gem-cutter family rules: when you come to the Jewelstead you never complain, you keep in good cheer, and you help us with our work. These rules are more important than ever with my husband Fúni still away, for he did not take all of the work away with him; indeed, he took almost none!\
\
'When he returns he will have an earful from Mother Amma about the longer than expected duration of his journey, I promise you that! But for now I will follow the Gem-cutter rules: never complain, keep in good cheer, and make sure my sons and their friends do their share of the work!'","Pick up the crate of precious stones by Gráfar Splitstone","Talk to Erfith on the west side of the Dwelling-halls","Mother Amma is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","'I have a crate of precious stones ready to return to Mother Amma and I could use someone to carry it, but if you could first thin the ranks of the cave-claws and other irritations in Narathâk I would be ever at your service.'","Mother Amma strokes her beard and considers you carefully","Authi Gem-cutter is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","'You have heard the rules, ${PLAYER}. Let us visit my brother Gráfar at Narathâk and see if he needs any assistance with his work in the New-lodes. That should satisfy Mother Amma, and I intended for you to meet my brother anyway.\
\
'The New-lodes of Narathâk have been recently delved, and can be found east of here, beyond the passage that runs from the entryway to the Hall Under the Mountain. My brother spends most of his waking hours mining for the precious gems we need to further our craft. There has always been great demand for the jewellery my family fashions, and Gráfar works hard to ensure we have what we need to meet it!'","Find the entrance to the New-lodes of Narathâk east of the entryway within the Lonely Mountain","Erfith accepts the necklace and admires its fine craftsmanship","'My father Fúni and my brother Fúsi have not yet returned from their excursion on the other side of the Misty Mountains, but I will be pleased to introduce you to my mother, and to another of my brothers who remains in Erebor.'","Erfith the Quarrelsome is on the west side of the Dwelling-halls of Erebor, east of the Jewelstead and down the stairs.","'You did very well to clear out some of the vermin! My brother was right to praise your skills and your helpfulness. This crate of precious stones is ready to deliver to Mother Amma back home, if you are still willing to prove my brother a good judge of character.'"},
[3250]={"'Bori went north-west, and will be pleased for you to join him. Beware of the insects that have made their homes here, and destroy any that threaten your safe passage!'","Defeated creatures in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Prince Durin has ordered the Gabil'akkâ to push further into Gundabad in opposition to the hostile Orc-defenders.","Bori has agreed to meet you by the upper crypts, further north in the Pit of Stonejaws.","'Hail, friend!'","'Hail, friend! Are you here to study the tombs in the Houses of Rest? Well, it is not truly a scholarly mission that brought me hither; my father expects me to learn if the Orcs have defaced the tombs here during their long residence. But I am also interested in learning the names of the dwarf-families that lie here entombed, and thought I could accomplish both errands at once!\
\
'Let us climb a little higher, ${PLAYER}. The path west of here eventually slopes upward to the north, near more of the crypts.'","Find Bósi at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws, north of Máttugard","A cruel sword of Orc-make is embedded here in the wall","You have found Bósi at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws","Durin ordered Bósi of the Iron Garrison to scout the further reaches of the Mountain-home, and has asked you to meet up with them at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws, north of Máttugard.","Find and talk to Bori further north in the Pit of Stonejaws","Talk to Bósi at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws","Prince Durin has returned with you to Máttugard.","Bósi is at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws.","Defeat creatures in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Let us climb a little higher, ${PLAYER}. The path slopes upward to the north, near more of the crypts.'","Chapter 7.1: The Houses of Rest","You have caught up to Bori by the upper crypts","'Threats remain here and there within Máttugard, but for the most part we have secured these halls and I do not fear they will be retaken. The time has come to push deeper into Gundabad. To that end I have ordered scouts to survey the further reaches: beyond Deepscrave to the west and north from Máttugard into the Pit of Stonejaws. Perhaps you can work to accomplish the second of these?\
\
'You proved a good friend to Bósi of the Iron Garrison, so I ask you to meet up with him at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws. Help him to survey that cavern and the tombs housed within, the better to expand the foothold of the Gabil'akkâ in Gundabad. I will await report of your success, ${PLAYER}!'","Bósi's son Bori has gone to search the crypts in the Pit of Stonejaws, and could use your assistance to the north-west.","Bori asked you to search more of the crypts along the westward path, which eventually turns north and slopes upward.","Bori calls you over to him","Find Bori to the north-west in the Pit of Stonejaws","You try to remove the sword but it is held fast by the rock","Talk to Durin in Máttugard","Search more of the crypts along the north-western path for evidence of the Orcs","'Welcome, my friend! Are you here to lend us your aid? I must give my thanks to the prince when next we return to Máttugard, for you have always been a great help to us in each of our endeavours.\
\
'My son Bori went on ahead to seek for the Houses of Rest, the tombs of our people. They are said to line the walls of the Pit of Stonejaws, and I am interested to see them as well, but something else has drawn my attention: a great city in the pit, home not to the bones of our ancestors but to more recent, and unwelcome, arrivals. I will take a small party of Longbeards to appraise this city. Perhaps you can bring my son to join us after he learns if the Houses of Rest are free of Orcs?\
\
'Bori went to the north-west, and will be pleased for you to join him. Beware of the creatures that have made their homes here, and destroy any that threaten your safe passage!'","'I find that Orc-sword quite curious. Did they fight among themselves for the privilege of ransacking the Houses of Rest?'\
\
'As I climbed past the crypt-entrances, I tried to read the names of the families entombed within. It was not an easy task, for most of them have faded with the passage of the years, and I could not make many of them out.\
\
'I saw markers for the Line of Arnvíth... the Line of Félag... Yngvi's Line...'\
\
Bori stands up straight and rubs his chin.\
\
'Perhaps the faded letters prevented the Orcs from disturbing the timeless sleep of the dwarves that lie within. For that let us be grateful. If the Orcs believed these dwarves had names of importance, they might have cracked open their tombs in search of wealth.\
\
'I see signs that much else in the Pit of Stonejaws, and throughout the Mountain-home, was plundered and defaced. But how can this be so? Legend tells us that such villainy should have been prevented!'","Talk to Bori in the Pit of Stonejaws","<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Máttugard when you accept this quest.</rgb>\
\
'Then let us return! The conquest of the Mountain-home will wait no longer!'","'You proved a good friend to Bósi of the Iron Garrison, so I ask you to meet up with him at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws, north of Máttugard. Help him to survey that cavern and the tombs housed within, the better to expand the foothold of the Gabil'akkâ in Gundabad. I will await report of your success, ${PLAYER}!'"},
[3251]={"'Khîl is one of the Zhélruka, a clan of dwarves from the east, but he has lived here in Erebor for many years and caused no serious trouble... until now! He is a spinner of tales, and in my experience he has never had a truthful thing to say; I have found his untrue tales to be harmless, for the most part. He has never spoken ill of my family before. Why has he now begun to spread these lies about the Gem-cutters?\
\
'Go ask him why he has chosen this course, ${PLAYER}. He tends to loiter outside, by the entrance to the Lonely Mountain, but I have not seen him today.'","How can Khîl believe this tale? Thafar-gathol never existed","'The promise of finding lost Thafar-gathol has long moved the hearts of Longbeards and Zhélruka to adventure among the dangerous mountains, disturbing worm and Orc alike, but none have returned from such journeys with news of its whereabouts. It has attained an air of mystery and of dread, and some dwarves have chosen less daring pursuits, if less rewarding.\
\
'That is the case with the Gem-cutters, a Longbeard family whose jewellery has achieved some renown among the folk of the Lonely Mountain. In recent months, their craft has fallen somewhat and Fúni Gem-cutter has had to leave his wife and two of his sons behind while he seeks some means of recovering their fortunes. I heard he travelled beyond the Misty Mountains and is over-long in returning, which causes his wife to worry. If he does not return soon, and with good tidings of new fortune, she will be forced to abandon their home and set out from the Lonely Mountain in disgrace. It is a shame, but such things have been happening more and more often in these difficult days.'\
\
You tell Khîl that you have heard these rumours concerning the Gem-cutters are untrue, and he snorts.\
\
'I only know what I have heard, friend. It is not so hard to believe, is it? I speak only the truth, and I bristle at the suggestion that my stories are anything but honest!'","This machine sounds very implausible","'It is as I said, is it not? Khîl Tale-spinner always speaks such nonsense. What stories did he spin for you today?'\
\
You briefly recount Khîl's words, and Authi laughs aloud.\
\
'Utter rubbish and nonsense! Everyone knows that King Brand and Dáin Ironfoot fought side by side before the gates of the Lonely Mountain, and when the King of Dale fell, the King Under the Mountain fought to protect his ally's body from the ravages of their foes, ceasing only when he too was slain. And a machine powered by a fire grim? How could the Jangovar have ever constructed such a device, or tamed such a spirit? It is an absurdity.\
\
'But none of these are as unbelievable as the tale of Thafar-gathol! Bah! If such a city ever existed, it would have been found by now. Preposterous drivel!'","Talk to Khîl and hear his tale","A dwarf named Khîl has been spreading lies about the Gem-cutter family, and Authi wants you to find him and get him to stop.","'Ah, another listener! If you would like to hear grand tales about the history of the dwarves and other peoples of the North, you have come to the right spot!'","Thafar-gathol sounds as it always has: a fanciful story with little basis in reality","Valves and pipes? No one else has mentioned such a machine at the battle","What nonsense! There was no such machine at the battle!","This disrespect cannot stand! King Brand and Dáin Ironfoot died before the gates of Erebor!","This must be Khîl. He seems to have attracted an audience","If Thafar-gathol existed, would it not have been found by now?","This story beggars belief. No such machine existed at the battle","'It was in March that an army of Jangovar came out of the east and crossed the Ironfold, led by their fearsome chieftains and emboldened by the power of Sauron. They threatened the people of the Dale-lands, and King Brand stood between his people and their terrible foes.\
\
'While the Men of Dale fled before the approaching army, hoping to make for the safety of the Lonely Mountain and the protection of their dwarf-allies, King Brand stood alone in the water of the river-crossing. He was felled by arrows in the stream, and King Dáin escaped to the safety of Erebor. Should he have stood with his ally, and risked death thereby? Who can say? The dwarves had need of their king, and after the flight to the Lonely Mountain he fought against the Jangovar and died before the very gates. The Mountain was besieged, and both Dale and Erebor were saved only by the sudden defeat of Sauron in the lands far to the south.\
\
'Had it only come sooner, both King Brand and Dáin Ironfoot might still live to lead their people.'","Actually, King Brand and Dáin Ironfoot died before the gates of Erebor. Khîl's account is wrong","'Khîl is one of the Zhélruka, a clan of dwarves from the east, but he has lived here in Erebor for many years and caused no serious trouble... until now! He is a spinner of tales, and in my experience he has never had a truthful thing to say, but I have found his untrue tales to be harmless, for the most part. He has never spoken ill of my family before. Why has he now begun to spread these lies about the Gem-cutters?\
\
'Go ask him why he has chosen this course, ${PLAYER}. He tends to loiter outside, by the entrance to the Lonely Mountain, but I have not seen him today.'","Demonstrate to Khîl that you are ready to <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to his tales","It is good the machine was destroyed before the Jangovar plot could be successful","Is that truly how events unfolded?","That is how you remember the last moments of King Brand and Dáin Ironfoot","'You say Erfith mentioned the name Khîl? That does not surprise me. He is one of the Zhélruka, a clan of dwarves from the east, but he has lived here in Erebor for many years and caused no serious trouble... until now! He is a spinner of tales, and in my experience he has never had a truthful thing to say; I have found his untrue tales to be harmless, for the most part. He has never spoken ill of my family before. Why has he now begun to spread these lies about the Gem-cutters?\
\
'Go ask him why he has chosen this course, ${PLAYER}. He tends to loiter outside, by the entrance to the Lonely Mountain, but I have not seen him today.'","How can Khîl believe this tale? Lost Thafar-gathol is a tale for children","This dwarf does not know what really happened. King Brand did not die at the river-crossing","Khîl might be found outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain.","'These stories are of recent vintage, it is true. Harken now to a tale of the distant past, a tale that grows in mystery and allure with every passing decade. More than six thousand years ago, the land shook with great calamity and the home of my people was riven with great cracks and torn asunder. The beautiful Hall of Torrents in the distant east collapsed, and thousands of my people were slain. The Zhélruka became a wandering people, and were turned away by all their neighbours.\
\
'But King Durin II, who ruled in Khazad-dûm, heard of their plight and showed mercy to the wanderers. He bade them travel to the Grey Mountains, and promised a place would be made for them in Gundabad. King Túruz of the Zhélruka began a great march across the northern lands, and stayed for a time helping the Longbeards of the Iron Hills repair their own damaged halls. When the Zhélruka again departed for Gundabad, they parted as friends, and promised a healthy trade partnership when they came to their new home.'\
\
Khîl pauses dramatically.\
\
'But they never arrived at Gundabad. King Túruz and the Zhélruka disappeared in the Grey Mountains, and no trace of them was ever found. King Durin and his son Borin sent several companies of dwarves to search for them, but to no avail. After seven-times-seven years, the Longbeards gave up the search.\
\
'And yet one of the Zhélruka survived. His name was Gúrek, and he appeared without warning at the gates of Gundabad, half-starved and raving mad. He told a confused tale of what had befallen his people: that they came across a stream that flowed out of the high mountains and gleamed like silver. The shine of the water came from tiny fragments of mithril, and when the Zhélruka followed it to its source they discovered a grand cavern full of gold, wondrous gemstones, and mithril to rival Khazad-dûm.\
\
'They abandoned their journey at once and carved a great hall they named Thafar-gathol, the Grey Citadel, and they used all their craft and spells to hide the entrance. What became of Thafar-gathol no tale tells, and neither does history record how Gúrek alone came to Gundabad. But Zhélruka and Longbeard alike still lust for the riches of lost Thafar-gathol, and despite numerous attempts at searching the Grey Mountains, none have ever had the good fortune to find it since it vanished. But it is still out there, my friends, waiting to be found.'","Chapter 7.2: A Damaging Song","'I heard Fúni Gem-cutter travelled beyond the Misty Mountains and is over-long in returning, which causes his wife to worry. If he does not return soon, and with good tidings of new fortune, she will be forced to abandon their home and set out from the Lonely Mountain in disgrace. It is a shame, but such things have been happening more and more often in these difficult days.'","Khîl refuses to take back his story about the Gem-cutters","Talk to Khîl outside the Lonely Mountain","That isn't right, is it? King Brand and Dáin Ironfoot died before the gates of Erebor, didn't they?","Find Khîl outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain","Khîl is wrong. King Brand and Dáin Ironfoot died before the gates of Erebor","Respond to the truthfulness of Khîl's account: <rgb=#00FF00>agree</rgb>, <rgb=#00FF00>yes</rgb>, <rgb=#00FF00>ahem</rgb>, <rgb=#00FF00>angry</rgb>, <rgb=#00FF00>confused</rgb>, <rgb=#00FF00>grumble</rgb>, or <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>","The story of lost Thafar-gathol excites your imagination. Can it be found?","The Jangovar machine was truly a complex and forbidding construct","'There is no shortage of tales from the Battle of Dale and the Siege of the Lonely Mountain, my friends. Have you heard tell of the great furnace the Jangovar built by Raven Hill? A frightening construction of pipes and valves it was, with wings of red leather extending above in mimicry of the dragon Smaug.\
\
'None can say for certain what powered the terrible device, but I heard from some who saw it that the furnace contained a fire grim of unsurpassed heat. Metal pipes carried noxious fumes from the device to channels in the stone. The Jangovar believed they could fill the Lonely Mountain with smoke and force the dwarves to flee from their well-protected fastness.\
\
'You may scoff, but friends of mine saw this device with their own eyes! It was destroyed by a small group of canny dwarves, who manipulated the valves and prevented too much smoke from entering the Mountain. They shut down the machine and defeated the fire grim, if such it was. Truly there was enough bravery to go around on that day, even if some do not believe this tale. I assure you it is true!'","Talk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead","You have heard much of the battle, but have seen no evidence of such a machine","Khîl the Tale-spinner is outside the entrance to Erebor, regaling onlookers with his stories.","Did the Jangovar truly assemble such a machine as Khîl describes?","Authi Gem-cutter is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Imagine the treasures that must await within lost Thafar-gathol, if it could be found","Such nonsense! Thafar-gathol never existed, and tales of it cannot be believed"},
[3252]={"Find the courtyard in Hármelak's manor","Talk to Hármelak in the office of her manor","Find the garden of Hármelak's manor","'The Kindred of the Coins was my idea, ${PLAYER}, inspired by the Corsair councils that once governed Umbar between the reigns of tyrants. A King or a Queen or a Steward can begin with the best of intentions, but they can be corrupted. They can make the wrong choice, but a group can guard against such wrong choices. A group can see all the sides of a problem. In a city such as Umbar Baharbêl, only a council can lead effectively for the good of all. That was my idea, ${PLAYER}: a council of leaders that would not be subservient to any outside force; not Gondor, not the Empire of Ordâkh, not the Dark Lord Sauron or his servants.\
\
'During the rule of the Heirs of Castamir and the Church of the All Seeing, I asked Khôltekh to fashion seven medallions in the form of large coins that could be worn as necklaces. Each was made of a different material, signifying our disparate backgrounds and influences, but each had something in common. Khôltekh embedded a shard of Abâshal, the valuable sea-opal treasured by his people, into each coin.\
\
'Only days after Balakhôr perished in Gondor, a tremendous quake rocked the city. The temple of Sauron crumbled and fell into the earth, and I knew it was the time to act. I sent the medallions fashioned by Khôltekh to my chief allies, and the uprising began. The Sea-stone Mutiny would spell the end of outside authority over Umbar: that of Ordâkh, that of Gondor, that of Sauron. The Kindred of the Coins would make Umbar Baharbêl a Free City again.\
\
'Let us speak further in my office.'","Talk to Hármelak by the courtyard","Hármelak arrives in the courtyard","Hármelak arrives in the garden of her manor","Hármelak asked you to wait for her in the garden to the north.","Wait for Hármelak in the garden to the north","Hármelak has arrived in her office.","'Thank you, Rothog.'\
\
Hármelak studies you silently for a moment. When she speaks again, her lips turn upwards in a faint smile.\
\
'Welcome to Umbar Baharbêl, ${PLAYER}. I could have invited the others of your group, but I prefer to speak to you alone about this matter. You understand. It is not often that I have the opportunity to speak to such as you. It is the matter of our hostage that brings you here, I understand?'\
\
You keep your expression guarded, but Hármelak's smile becomes more pronounced.\
\
'Khôltekh prides himself upon knowing everything that transpires in this city, but he does not share everything with us. I have eyes of my own, and they see a great deal at a variety of interesting places: outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast, by the home of Belondor and Mêshka in my very own Upper Ward, among the alleys of the Sail-haven. Your group has not remained hidden to my eyes, ${PLAYER}, and I know why you have come to my city.\
\
'Let us continue our discussion by the fountain of my courtyard.'","Chapter 7.2: An Audience With The Golden Queen","Talk to Hármelak in the garden of her manor","Hármelak asked you to wait for her in the office to the north.","'Let us continue our discussion by the fountain in my courtyard.'","'You stand in the presence of one of the wealthiest people in all of Umbar, ${PLAYER}, but know this: wealth does not grant complete power. How many of my rivals had riches but lacked the will to maintain their control? Now their wealth is mine. The folk of the city whisper that my fortune rivals that of many dwarf-lords, but their whispers are untrue: my fortune exceeds that of even the dwarf-kings! I am the matron of the most powerful merchant clan in Umbar, and we trade in all manner of expensive goods from across the Haradwaith: spices, jewels, silks, artwork, even relics of ancient days.\
\
'I was widowed when I was young, and my husband's brothers sought to gain control of the business. They failed. It takes an iron will to prosper as I have. Did I not witness Mût Tadaul, the Death of Light, when I was but a young girl? I knew the evils of the Church of the All Seeing from a young age, but I saw too the value of maintaining the appearance of cooperation. In public I allied with the Ordâkhai occupiers and then with the Heirs of Castamir, but always I worked secretly against them. Quietly I set up a network of those opposed to the interlopers endangering my city. It brought me into contact with some who shared my goal of making Umbar Baharbêl a Free City: Azagath and Belondor, Khôltekh of the Temámir, the smugglers Tumúldo and Nakási.\
\
'When Balakhôr perished in the war and the power of the Heirs of Castamir was broken, I knew the time had come to act. We will speak of it further in the garden to the north.'","Wait for Hármelak in the courtyard of her manor","Find the office to the north in Hármelak's manor","Wait for Hármelak in the office to the north","'Azagath is a Black Númenórean, a blood-ally of Balakhôr during the Scourge's rise to power. Their friendship soured when Balakhôr sought to claim rulership over all of Umbar in the name of the Heirs of Castamir. Azagath opposed his bid, a duel was fought, and Azagath suffered defeat; he received a scar upon his face and pled for mercy. It was granted, and he was banished. We did not see him for many years, and during that time Azagath's warnings were proven true. I called for his aid during the Sea-stone Mutiny, and when he returned to the city he did so as a beloved hero. \\qHadôru,\\q they called him, \\qHe Who Returned.\\q\
\
'There was no celebration for me, ${PLAYER}. I never fled the city, so I had no need to return a hero! I was here always: steadfast! Unyielding! The Kindred was my idea, but when the seven of us cast our lots for who would lead us, it was Azagath who prevailed. He is charming, any can see that, and the others believed he could more easily inspire the Umbari people than I could. I have been patient through all these troubles. Is that not inspiring?'\
\
Hármelak stares at you with eyes of ice, and despite her words you can tell that being passed over for leadership of the Kindred bothers her more than she is willing to say.\
\
'Do not misunderstand me. I would be content for any to lead us if he or she held dear the interests of the city, ${PLAYER}. But I think it is not so for Azagath. He has some plan of his own, a secret he keeps from the rest of us: The Song of Waves and Wind. I know not what it is, but it cannot be in the interest of my city.'","Hármelak arrives in the office and takes her seat","Rothog the Storm has brought you to speak with Hármelak, the Golden Queen.","'I take you to see her,' Rothog continues. Some of the people nearby stare at you and the half-troll member of the Kindred of the Coins, many of them backing away or preparing to run if his attention turns to them.\
\
'Now, ${PLAYER}. Hármelak does not like to be kept waiting.'","Hármelak asked you to wait for her in the courtyard of her manor.","Hármelak asked you to wait for her in the garden to the north of the courtyard.","Hármelak has arrived in the courtyard.","'When Balakhôr perished in the war and the power of the Heirs of Castamir was broken, I knew the time had come to act. We will speak of it further in the garden.'","Hármelak has arrived in the garden of her manor.","Talk to Hármelak in her manor","Hármelak is in the main hall of her manor.","'Let us speak further in my office, to the north.'"},
[3253]={"'The rubble that blocked the way into this room must be of fairly recent vintage, for it did not prevent someone from looting the stones from the mosaic on the opposite wall. Orcs or goblins, no doubt; they have no love for fine dwarf-art, and would seize any opportunity to despoil such a thing as that. It is a pity we cannot tell what it might once have shown.\
\
'It does remind me of a mosaic that once stood in the throne room of the Hall Under the Mountain, and which Stáli the Hewer had begun to restore. I wonder if this is similar to that one? He will be interested to see this, even as incomplete as it is. Curse the Orcs for their damage! This mosaic might once have been a great work of art, but like so much else in Gundabad it has been ruined by their hateful efforts.\
\
'But we can do nothing about it for now. Let us return to my father, far below in the Pit of Stonejaws.'","Bori needs your help to clear the rubble and debris away from the entrance to the south-west.","'Here, friend, and keep quiet.'","Together, you and Bori have cleared the rubble away from the room to the south-west, and can now gain entrance.","Bori is in Zul-mazal.","Examine the broken mosaic in Zul-mazal","Bori has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over the Pit of Stonejaws, which contains the crypts of the many dwarf-families that were laid to rest over the years.","Bori needs your help to clear the rubble and debris away from the entrance.","'What awaits us within? I will follow after you, friend!'","'¡Mira eso!'","Explore the room you have unearthed from the rubble","Even from this great height, the presence of the Orcs is unmistakeable","Bósi is outside Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws.","'Here, friend. Let us keep our voices quiet while we make our plans.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> out over the Pit of Stonejaws","Talk to Bósi outside Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws","Chapter 7.2: So Say The Legends","A broken mosaic decorates one wall of this chamber.","Talk to Bori by the upper crypts in the Pit of Stonejaws","'<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> out over the Pit of Stonejaws, ${PLAYER}, and tell me what you see.'","Bósi is outside the fortress of Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws.","'Perhaps it is just a legend, after all. How could the dead lords of Gundabad stand by and watch for so many years, and do nothing?'\
\
Bori sighs and turns his attention to the rubble-choked passage behind you.\
\
'Can you help me shift some of those rocks aside? I would like to take a look inside that room. It may be a tomb or memorial of some kind, and perhaps the debris kept the Orcs out even as it blocks our own passage.'","Find Bósi outside Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws","Bori is by the upper crypts in the Pit of Stonejaws.","'We can do nothing about the damage to this room for now. Let us return to my father, far below in the Pit of Stonejaws.'","Bori is interested in the legends and history of Gundabad, and wants your help to learn as much of them as he can.","'Many are the great stories that have come down through the ages to us, ${PLAYER}. They stir our passions and fill us with dwarf-pride. One of these tales concerns these very tombs: according to legend, the lords of Gundabad will one day rise from their crypts and walk once again among the living. When they see the evils perpetrated by the Orcs in Gundabad, they will unleash their wrath upon those who despoil the great dwarf-halls, slaying their enemies from sunrise to sunset. Then, when their day of reckoning is done, the great lords will return to the Houses of Rest and slumber again for eternity, the Mountain-home made free of their foes.\
\
'<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> out over the Pit of Stonejaws, ${PLAYER}, and tell me what you see.'","Clear rubble from the entrance to the south-west","Talk to Bori in Zul-mazal","Many of the stones in this mosaic have been lost to looters and time"},
[3254]={"'Prove to me you can carry that bowl of sea-water without spilling a single drop, and perhaps you can accompany us into the Citadel. Bring it to the courtyard of the Teeming Net Tavern, to the south-east, and we will see if you are steady enough to join us.'","'Be gone now.'\
\
Before you turn to leave, you quietly ask Rothog why he is helping you. The half-troll stares impassively down at you and says nothing.","Talk to Ushu on the dock beside the Harbour Warden's tower","'We should not say anything.'","Hármelak has given you some information that may help you get past the guards into the Citadel of Winds.","You have accomplished the task set before you by Ushu and Enât","The women eye you suspiciously as you approach","Hármelak told you that every day Azagath's servants can be found on the docks by the Harbour Warden's tower, filling bowls with water to carry to the Citadel of Winds.","'I would not seek to supplant any member of the Kindred of the Coins, for ours is a necessary council and Umbar is made better by our efforts. But this too is its strength: the Kindred itself is more important than any individual member. Were Azagath to fall during your rescue of the Gondorian hostage, that would be a most unfortunate turn, but the Kindred itself would survive... and that is everything.'\
\
Hármelak holds your gaze but lowers her voice.\
\
'Azagath returned to the city in the grip of a curious superstition. Every morning he instructs some among his servants to carry empty bowls down to the docks beside the Harbour Warden's tower. They fill these bowls with saltwater from the bay. Once this is done, they then carry these bowls of saltwater through the streets of the city until they reach the bridge beyond the Fleet-fast. The guards let them pass, without fail, and once inside they fill the fountains within the Citadel with the saltwater they carry. At midnight, the fountains are emptied... and at dawn the process begins again.\
\
'No one pays attention to the servants who carry the water, ${PLAYER}, not the folk of the city, not the guards of the Fleet-fast, and not Azagath Sea-shadow. Among these servants you could gain access to the Citadel of Winds, and whatever might befall then... well, it would be for the benefit of the city, would it not?\
\
'I trust this discussion has been as illuminating for you as it has been for me. Rothog will see you out.'","'We have our own tasks to complete, stranger, and have no time to speak with such as you.'\
\
You apologize for interrupting, and ask if they could use any help with their task. The servant stares at you suspiciously.\
\
'Why?' she asks.","Azagath's water-bearers are on the dock beside the Harbour Warden's tower.","Azagath's water-bearers are on a dock by the Harbour Warden's tower.","Pick up the bowl of water on the dock","Rothog the Storm has escorted you from Hármelak's manor. He clearly believes his task is finished.","Talk to water-bearer Ushu on the dock","Talk to water-bearer Enât on the dock","'¿Si?'","Chapter 7.3: Beneath His Notice","Rothog looks down at you but says nothing.","The water-bearers will only allow you to accompany them into the Citadel if you can prove up to their task.","You should find some of the water-carriers mentioned by Hármelak","Find Azagath's water-carriers on a dock near the Harbour Warden's tower","'Forgive Enât her distrust, stranger, but we have reason to be wary. Our master is very particular about the means by which we carry out his commands. We bring sea-water through the city to the fountains inside Sûr Birix, the Citadel of Winds, every morning, and every night those fountains are emptied to await our return the next morning. It is hard, heavy work, and there are fewer of us now than there used to be. Azagath has dismissed some of our fellows before now, but... no one seems to know where Sadûkh has gone.'\
\
Enât hisses at Ushu to not say anything more, and the woman nods.\
\
'He may be fine, and he may not. But without Sadûkh our work will be more difficult. Azagath smiles with his mouth, but his eyes are unmoved, and if we do not find some way to replace Sadûkh's burden we may be the next ones to disappear.\
\
'Prove to me you can carry this bowl of sea-water without spilling a single drop, and perhaps you can accompany us into the Citadel. Bring it to the courtyard of the Teeming Net Tavern, to the south-east, and we will see if you are steady enough to join us.'","The servant's companion calls for your attention","Ushu nods at the bowl, challenging you to carry it without spilling any of the water","Talk to Rothog the Storm outside Hármelak's manor","'You did well-enough, stranger. You may accompany us when next we perform our duties, and I will ask no questions of you. Your reasons for wanting to gain access to Sûr Birix are your own, but you must endanger none of my friends. If such treachery seems possible, I will alert the guards at once.\
\
'Let this last warning guide your steps. Neither Enât nor I know what happened to Sadûkh, but of this I am certain: he saw something he was not supposed to see, some secret of the Sea-shadow, and now he has paid for it.\
\
'Azagath is dangerous. We water-bearers may be beneath his notice... but it may not be possible to always remain so.'"},
[3255]={"'Are you ready to go? Surely King Thorin will hear my plea and command Khîl to cease speaking falsehoods about my family!'","Talk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead and go with him to petition the king","Authi Gem-cutter is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","'I am pleased that King Thorin ruled in my favour, but I cannot help but feel that in some respect I am being punished for bringing the matter to him! Now we have to escort Khîl to his father's home in Járnfast? Bah! Let him travel by himself!\
\
'I suppose I should gather my belongings for the journey. At least Khîl's gossip has been stopped, and he will no longer trouble my family in Erebor. That is surely worth the trip to the Ironfold, ${PLAYER}.'","Authi Gem-cutter is very angry about the gossip Khîl has been spreading about his family, and he wishes to petition King Thorin about the matter.","Chapter 7.3: Grievances","Talk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead","'And yet, none of these tales are as personally offensive to me as the gossip he spreads about my family. It seems he will not stop until he is forced to stop, ${PLAYER}. I must take this matter before King Thorin. Only the King Under the Mountain can prevail upon Khîl to cease his rumourmongering.\
\
'Will you speak on my behalf before the King? I trust you and no others to help me with this, my friend. Tell me if you are willing, and we will petition King Thorin together.'"},
[3256]={"'I will see you in the courtyard to the south when you are done here, friend.'","Strakhbuk roars a challenge and rushes to battle!","Talk to the dwarf-woman Bróin saw within Shakhajât","Bósi has asked Imák and Bróin to draw the defenders of Shakhajât out into the open.","'Stáli may one day teach me the ways of sculpture, but until then I think I will adopt axe-handling as my trade!'","The Dwarves of the Iron Garrison plan to combat the denizens of Shakhajât in the Pit of Stonejaws.","'Our fellowship is not the only one to have infiltrated Shakhajât, ${PLAYER}. Other dwarves have arrived, including a dwarf-woman of no small ferocity! I watched her engage in combat with a hobgoblin and as I beheld her prowess my own fears evaporated! Will you make sure she fares well enough in the courtyard ahead?'\
\
You assure Bróin you will find her, but if she is as fierce as he says, you are certain she will be fine.\
\
'Aye, she was most striking... and struck her foes with abandon, too! Impress her by slaying the hobgoblins, our shared foes, and making the Pit of Stonejaws safer for all of us!'","'If we are to advance from Máttugard, we will need to do something about the city the Orcs have established here. Shakhajât, it is called, and long has it stood among the broken teeth of the Pit of Stonejaws. It was here that Bolg mustered the force that met its end before the gates of the Lonely Mountain in the Battle of Five Armies, but I do not know what it is like within its walls today.\
\
'We need to draw the attention of its defenders so some of us can get inside and cause some trouble! Who volunteers? Imák? Bróin? Will the two of you blast a great signal upon horns of battle, drawing forth the hobgoblins that reside within the city?'","Defeated hobgoblins in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bori is waiting to meet up with you outside Shakhajât.","Bósi has agreed that you can carry out Bróin's part of the plan: climbing either the left or right slope around the fortress and using a discarded horn of battle to draw forth some of the hobgoblins from Shakhajât.","Bróin gives you a relieved smile","'I suppose I can cause a distraction... if I must. Yes, I can... I can do it.'","Meet up with Bróin inside Shakhajât","You have caused a sufficient distraction for the dwarves to enter Shakhajât","Bróin greets you warmly","Now that you have carried out your part of the plan, you should join the dwarves inside Shakhajât.","Use a horn of battle on one of the slopes to either side of the fortress to draw forth and defeat hobgoblin defenders of Shakhajât","Defeat hobgoblins in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Hearty greetings to you, ${PLAYER}! Can you imagine my brother Eskil in such a place? I can... but not for long. It is better that I am here!'\
\
You tell Fastrith that she has an admirer in Shakhajât, and he sent you to check on her.\
\
'An admirer? Well now! I trust that he's no Orc or hobgoblin? A fine dwarf, you say? Better and better! But this is no place for such idle talk. I will meet you outside the city once your business here is concluded, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Bróin outside Shakhajât","'You and Imák will fashion a suitable distraction, and the rest of us will sneak into Shakhajât as a group.'","'If you need a distraction, I am your dwarf. I can make enough noise the defenders of Shakhajât will think five armies approach, and all of them dwarves!'","Imák is pleased with the plan, and will do his part","Talk to Bróin inside Shakhajât","'What's that, ${PLAYER}? You wish to draw the eyes of the defenders away on your own? We do not need three teams to do this.\
\
'Very well, you and Imák will fashion a suitable distraction, and the rest of us will sneak into Shakhajât as a group. Climb either the left or right slope that extends around the fortress and find one of the discarded horns of battle with which to draw hobgoblin attention.'","Bróin is inside Shakhajât and desires to speak with you.","Talk to Bósi outside Shakhajât","Talk to Bori outside Shakhajât","Chapter 7.3: Skulls of Shakhajât","Bróin has seen a dwarf-woman fighting in the fortress and wants you to check on her while you combat the forces inside Shakhajât.","Bori laughs abruptly, drawing your attention","'We need to draw the attention of its defenders so some of us can get inside and cause some trouble! Who volunteers? Imák? Bróin? Will the two of you blast a great signal upon horns of battle, drawing forth the hobgoblins that reside within the city?'","'Will you find her and make sure she fares well enough within the walls of the city?'","The dwarves have made their presence known to Bósi's satisfaction and are now ready to meet up outside Shakhajât.","'Did I hear her correctly? She is apprenticed to Stáli the Hewer, the sculptor from Erebor?\
\
'That is a curious coincidence, is it not?'","'I am glad to see you made it back outside, ${PLAYER}, as did these others!'\
\
You ask Fastrith why she ventured inside Shakhajât, and whether she needs your help escaping the contract with Stáli, as did her brother. She laughs in response.\
\
'No, my droll friend! My master Stáli did not send me here. His instructions were simple: \\qFind me the Zabad'ibîn,\\q he said. I reckoned they would be more likely found in dangerous places than in peaceful ones. A search of the chief-stead seemed in order. I found no gemstones, but there were plenty of Orc-skulls against which I tested the sharpness of my axe. Would that I had replaced my brother in his apprenticeship before this! Such fighting really gets the blood flowing, doesn't it?\
\
'Perhaps Stáli will eventually teach me the ways of sculpture, but until then I think I will adopt axe-handling as my trade!'","You can tell that Bróin is uncomfortable with the plan","Talk to Fastrith outside Shakhajât","Bósi is outside Shakhajât. Given Bróin's discomfort with the plan, perhaps you should volunteer in his stead?","Talk to Imák outside Shakhajât"},
[3257]={"Talk to Fastrith and travel with her to Zul-mazal","'How odd that we should discover a broken mosaic on the same day we encounter an apprentice to one renowned for the study and restoration of such works of art?\
\
'Stáli the Hewer will surely be interested in examining our discovery, ${PLAYER}. Does his apprentice care to see it, and confirm if I am right?'","'Lead on, my friend!'","'Stáli the Hewer will surely be interested in examining our discovery, ${PLAYER}. Does his apprentice care to see it, and confirm if I am right?'","Chapter 7.4: A Broken Mosaic","Bori believes that Stáli the Hewer would be interested in the mosaic you found in Zul-mazal, and suggested that his apprentice Fastrith Hawkfeast take a look on behalf of her master.","'A broken mosaic? I can certainly take a look. With Shakhajât apparently free of any of the Zabad'ibîn, I have the rest of the day free.\
\
'Let me know where to go, ${PLAYER}.'","'Hmm. There's something about this chamber, ${PLAYER}, and it's not the hobgoblins. Well, it's not just the hobgoblins.'\
\
Imák sniffs the air.\
\
'Yes, there is something peculiar about the air in here. You know my sense of smell is highly refined, do you not? Well, something here is a bother to it, and I don't like it.'","Talk to Fastrith outside Shakhajât","Imák is standing in Zul-mazal, waiting to speak with you.","Talk to Imák in Zul-mazal","Fastrith is outside Shakhajât, waiting for you and Bori to bring her to Zul-mazal to examine the interesting mosaic.","Fastrith Halcomida se encuentra a las afueras de Shakhajât."},
[3259]={"Visit Arin, a friend of the Gem-cutters who lives in Járnfast but is likely fishing in the Redwater","'King Thorin believes it is time for his son to learn the ways of the king, does he? That is new. Thorin is stubborn, as are most of his family, and I thought his decision to keep Durin from harm or difficulty would last longer than this. Why the change, I wonder?\
\
'Safe travels to you, ${PLAYER}. Keep one eye open for Karazgar or his agents while you travel in the Ironfold. I will see you when you return.'","King Thorin has given you a task to complete in the Ironfold, and you will accompany Authi Gem-cutter with his own.","Gandalf is in the Wizard-home, east of the Jewelstead and up several stairs","Talk to Khîl at the entrance to Járnfast","'You may do as you like, ${PLAYER}, but I shall not be visiting Khîl... not unless my king commands me to do so!'","'It has been many years since last I was here, before my father Bránit and I fell out of friendship. He died some time after that, before we were ever reconciled, and I saw no reason to return.\
\
'I suppose now I should put his house in order. You and Authi are welcome to visit me there at any time; I would appreciate the company! My father's house is up a ramp opposite the entrance.'","Authi is at the entrance to Járnfast.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, there you are. I have been studying several historical accounts concerning the struggles of Durin's Folk. Many are the hardships they have faced, more than a few of their own making, but these accounts do not agree on all the particulars. Dragons feature prominently, as you might expect, and I see the hand of Karazgar at work in some of the events that befell the dwarves in this area.'\
\
You tell Gandalf that King Thorin has requested you travel to Járnfast, in the Ironfold, and return to the Lonely Mountain with his son. Gandalf strokes his beard.\
\
'He believes it is time for Durin to learn the ways of the king, does he? That is new. Thorin is stubborn, as are most of his family, and I thought his decision to keep Durin from harm or difficulty would last longer than this. Why the change, I wonder?\
\
'Safe travels to you, ${PLAYER}. Keep one eye open for Karazgar or his agents while you travel in the Ironfold. I will see you when you return.'","'Well, I am here, despite my wish to be elsewhere. Surely Khîl could find his own way back to his father's old home, but you will not hear me speak crosswise to King Thorin's commands. We are to escort Khîl to Járnfast, and that we will do. I will only grumble about it a little, and beneath my beard.\
\
'Mother Amma suggested that we make the most of the journey into the Ironfold, since the Gem-cutters do not often travel out that way. She has made a list of suggested activities for us to pursue on our way. \\qA Gem-cutter always seeks to make things better for those he meets!\\q she says, and I could not possibly argue with that. So her list consists of a few tasks she recommended we complete to keep the land and its people safe, as well as a number of family friends in the Ironfold I have not seen in some time that we might visit. I do not feel particularly strongly about which of these tasks we complete, so I leave the decision-making up to you, ${PLAYER}. Why not choose four of these errands to carry out on our way to Járnfast?\
\
'No, Khîl, you do not get a say in the matter! This is your fault, and you're lucky we let you speak on this journey at all. You leave the decisions to me and to ${PLAYER}.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Complete any four of the objectives Authi has suggested as you travel through the Ironfold to Járnfast.</rgb>","'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}, for coming with me to Járnfast. It has been many years since last I was here, before my father Bránit and I fell out of friendship. He died some time after that, before we were ever reconciled, and I saw no reason to return.\
\
'I suppose now I should put his house in order. You and Authi are welcome to visit me there at any time; I would appreciate the company! My father's house is up a ramp opposite the entrance.'","Meet up with Authi and Khîl outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain","Visit Méthur, a friend of the Gem-cutters who lives in Hammerstead","Chapter 7.4: Iron Road","Authi and Khîl are waiting for you, but neither seems eager to depart","Find an entrance to the town of Utterby","Defeat Easterlings throughout the Ironfold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'If you have any preparations to make before we set out for the Ironfold, I suggest that you make them! You might want to check in with Gandalf before we leave. I do not know him very well, but I know enough about Wizards to tell you they do not like surprises! Tell him we will be away for a few days, so if he has need of you he will know where you might be found.\
\
'King Thorin ordered that a room be set aside for the Wizard somewhere in the Dwelling-halls. I believe you will find it east of here and up several stairs. I expect it was chosen to satisfy the well-known predilection of Wizards for tall towers, and will be quite high up! I will meet you outside once you have spoken with Gandalf.'","Defeat beasts throughout the Ironfold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have not been back to my father's home in Járnfast for many years. Were it not for the command of King Thorin, I would not return now! But I cannot remain here if the King Under the Mountain orders me to leave. Zhélruka do not answer to Longbeards, but I will not gainsay the word of a king.\
\
'So we will be travelling companions for a short while, ${PLAYER}. I suppose I welcome the company, even if the son of Fúni Gem-cutter does not.'","Talk to Khîl outside the Lonely Mountain","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> from the cliff's edge at Skald's Drop to survey the lands below","Talk to Authi at the entrance to Járnfast","From the high cliff you can see the fair fields of the Bardings, far below","Authi has suggested you help the people of the Ironfold as you travel to Járnfast.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Complete any four of the objectives Authi has suggested as you travel through the Ironfold to Járnfast.</rgb>","'Mother Amma suggested that we make the most of the journey into the Ironfold, since the Gem-cutters do not often travel out that way. She has made a list of suggested activities for us to pursue on our way. \\qA Gem-cutter always seeks to make things better for those he meets!\\q she says, and I could not possibly argue with that. So her list consists of a few tasks she recommended we complete to keep the land and its people safe, as well as a number of family friends in the Ironfold I have not seen in some time that we might visit. I do not feel particularly strongly about which of these tasks we complete, so I leave the decision-making up to you, ${PLAYER}. Why not choose four of these errands to carry out on our way to Járnfast?'","Defeated beasts throughout the Ironfold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Authi outside the Lonely Mountain","From here you could <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over the lands below","Authi planned to meet you outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain after you prepared for the journey and said good-bye to Gandalf.","'It has been a long time since I have seen Authi! Why, it has been five years at the very least since I ventured to the Lonely Mountain. How fares your mother? When last I visited, she put me to work sifting through buckets of rock, separating tiny flakes of copper from the stones. \\qGem-cutter house-guest rules!\\q she said. Perhaps that is why I have not visited since then!\
\
'Ah, but it is good to catch up with friends. We have had a fair amount of trouble here in the Ironfold, but I understand the fighting was thickest in Dale and at the foot of the Mountain. The Easterling armies passed by Járnfast just after the gates were shut, but the Men of Utterby had no such sturdy door to close; the Jangovar sacked the town and some of them remain there, as far as I have heard.\
\
'You keep Authi out of trouble, my friend. The worst of the fighting may be over, but nowhere is really safe, not these days.'","The entrance to Járnfast is in the north-east corner of the Ironfold.","Khîl Tale-spinner is at the entrance to the Lonely Mountain.","Defeat insects throughout the Ironfold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You are fortunate you caught me, Authi! I was about to head back to the city, empty-handed I'm afraid. The fishing has been poor for a fortnight. I suspect the Easterlings are to blame in some measure, for a portion of the Jangovar came by here on their way west. I understand they joined more of their number who were coming up the Drop, but my work does not take me out by Utterby so I didn't see that with my own eyes.\
\
'What brings you to the Ironfold, Authi? Your family is well, I hope!'\
\
Authi and Arin spend a few minutes regaling each other with news of their families, and Arin promises his friend the pick of his next catch.\
\
'I am sure I will have something for you too, ${PLAYER}, if the fish ever resume biting. Until next we meet, friends!'","'I will meet you outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain after I have gathered the things I will need for the journey and said good-bye to my mother and my brother. It will not be long; we Gem-cutters are not especially sentimental.\
\
'If you have any preparations to make before we set out for the Ironfold, I suggest that you make them! You might want to check in with Gandalf before we leave. I do not know him very well, but I know enough about Wizards to tell you they do not like surprises! Tell him we will be away for a few days, so if he has need of you he will know where you might be found.\
\
'King Thorin ordered that a room be set aside for the Wizard somewhere in the Dwelling-halls. I believe you will find it east of here and up several stairs. I expect it was chosen to satisfy the well-known predilection of Wizards for tall towers, and will be quite high up!'","You have come to Járnfast, the Ironfort of the dwarves","Gandalf is in the room that was given to him in the Dwelling-halls, east of the Jewelstead and up several sets of stairs.","Defeated Easterlings throughout the Ironfold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Authi Gem-cutter is at the entrance to the Lonely Mountain.","You have successfully escorted Khîl to Járnfast and should now speak to him.","Defeated insects throughout the Ironfold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The town of Utterby was occupied by the Jangovar, who now call it Er Shamol","Travel to the entrance of Járnfast, in the Ironfold"},
[3260]={"Talk to Náin the Slakeless in Járnfast","Find Náin the Slakeless, Lord of the Ironfort, at his throne","'You come from the Lonely Mountain, and from my brother? I bid you welcome, but I do not know why he sent you to me. I saw him short weeks ago, when the siege was lifted. Aye, I did my part in lifting it! I cannot imagine there have been events of import enough to send a messenger so soon.\
\
'My older brother Thorin did little in the way of fighting during the war. We have always been different, and ladies of our mutual acquaintance will happily tell you that my blood runs hotter than his, and my temper too! It is not a slight, do not take it as such! He is the King Under the Mountain and I am the Lord of the Ironfort and Iron Hills, both stations of importance, but I am sworn to serve him. I would serve him regardless, for he is my elder and dear to me, but he is also my king, and that alone merits respect.\
\
'You are here for his son? When the Easterlings brought their war through the Ironfold, Thorin sent word to me that Durin was to remain within the Ironfort, and I saw it done. Afterward I marched to the Lonely Mountain and there engaged in such battle as you would hardly believe! Stranded atop one of the spurs of the Mountain I was, wielding the Black Mattock with unheralded ferocity. Well, I have heralded it aplenty now to my minstrels, so in time folk from all about will hear the tale, or my minstrels will have an earful to match this golden one I earned following the battle!\
\
'If it had been up to me, Durin would have come with me to the fighting. Alas it was not. His father has always been a cautious sort. The boy was not happy about staying behind, and he spends most of his days deep in his cups, drowning his resentment and his boredom. Go to the Quenching Trough, his preferred tavern, and give him the news that his father seeks him. He will surely be pleased.'","'I am going to find a tavern and spend some coin and some time while you go about the second part of our errand, ${PLAYER}. I have heard the Quenching Trough is quite good; look for me there if you need me.\
\
'King Thorin's younger brother Náin is Lord of the Ironfort, and you should find him at his throne, atop the northern ramps. They call him Náin the Slakeless now, for his appetite for battle cannot be quenched! I heard his deeds during the Siege of Erebor were quite extraordinary; no doubt he will tell you of them. Once that is done, it is to be hoped he will consent to his nephew Durin travelling with us back through the Ironfold.\
\
'Come find me when you have Durin in your company and are ready to return to the Lonely Mountain.'","'What d'you want? Leave m'alone, stranger. Don't want to talk to you. M'busy.'\
\
Durin takes a long pull from his beer, spilling quite a lot of it, and wipes his beard with the back of his hand. He peers at you woozily, apparently trying to decide why you haven't left yet. You introduce yourself as ${PLAYER}, an emissary from King Thorin, and describe your charge. Durin's eyes widen and he sets his mug down on the table too heavily.","With his steel teeth, a false eye, and a golden ear, Náin is an impressive figure","'Let us go now to my uncle Náin and tell him we leave at once, ${PLAYER}. I am ready to prove myself worthy, and let none doubt my resolve!'","The Quenching Trough is a low-ceilinged tavern opposite the entrance to Járnfast.","Find Durin in the Quenching Trough opposite the entrance to Járnfast","You have completed the first part of your commitment to King Thorin, and now it is time to undertake the second portion of your responsibility: bringing word to his son Durin that it is time to return to the Lonely Mountain.","Náin the Slakeless, Lord of the Ironfort, can be found at his throne atop the northern ramps.","Durin is in the Quenching Trough, a low-ceiling tavern opposite the entrance to Járnfast.","Durin is in the Quenching Trough, a low-ceilinged tavern opposite the entrance to Járnfast.","'You are here for Thorin's son? When the Easterlings brought their war through the Ironfold, my brother sent word to me that Durin was to remain within the Ironfort, and I saw it done. Afterward I marched to the Lonely Mountain and there engaged in such battle as you would hardly believe! Stranded atop one of the spurs of the Mountain I was, wielding the Black Mattock with unheralded ferocity. Well, I have heralded it aplenty now to my minstrels, so in time folk from all about will hear the tale, or my minstrels will have an earful to match this golden one I earned following the battle!\
\
'If it had been up to me, Durin would have come with me to the fighting. Alas it was not. His father has always been a cautious sort. The boy was not happy about staying behind, and he spends most of his days deep in his cups, drowning his resentment and his boredom. Go to the Quenching Trough, his preferred tavern, and give him the news that his father seeks him. He will surely be pleased.'","Chapter 7.5: Errands at the Ironfort","'King Thorin's younger brother Náin is Lord of the Ironfort, and you should find him at his throne, atop the northern ramps. They call him Náin the Slakeless now, for his appetite for battle cannot be quenched! I heard his deeds during the Siege of Erebor were quite extraordinary; no doubt he will tell you of them. Once that is done, it is to be hoped he will consent to his nephew Durin travelling with us back through the Ironfold.\
\
'Come find me when you have Durin in your company and are ready to return to the Lonely Mountain.'","Talk to Durin in the Quenching Trough","Durin sits up straight, and the change is striking: he stares at you alertly","'My father wants me to return to Erebor? These are joyous tidings indeed! I thought I would never be permitted to leave the Ironfort ever again, neither in peace or in war. More the pity that the war is ended, and I never had the chance to prove myself in it!'\
\
His drink-bred surliness is gone, but now it is replaced with a sudden flash of uncertainty.\
\
'Am I ready to prove myself? My father did not think me strong enough to fight, commanding me to remain behind the sealed doors of the Ironfort. How can I know I will make him proud now, untested as I am?\
\
'What did you say your name was again? ${PLAYER}? Let us go now to my uncle Náin and tell him we leave at once. I... I am ready to prove myself worthy, and let none doubt my resolve!'","Talk to Durin (again) in the Quenching Trough","You have found Durin, but he seems unprepared for your tidings","'I see you found my nephew, ${PLAYER}. Very good! I had a task in mind for him to complete, but now that he is needed at the Lonely Mountain I shall find someone else to take care of it.\
\
'What is that, Durin? Speak up, boy, my recent exploits have done something to my hearing, I can't imagine what. You want to handle this task before you set out for the Mountain? Ah, I am proud of you! Truly you will be a great king someday. Why, dare I say it...\
\
'Nay, I will not say it. You will grow into your name, of that I have no doubt. Let me tell you the details about this task I have for you and for ${PLAYER}. I am sure ${PLAYER} does not wish to be left out? No, of course not!'"},
[3261]={"Your mission to Umbar has reached its successful conclusion, but a number of unresolved questions leave the situation in the city and surrounding lands in some doubt.","'During the sea-voyage that brought young Thorongil and me to Umbar, I did what I could to keep the boy out of trouble. It was not always an easy task, and I tell you truly that it was a thankless one... but I am relieved that both he and I survived the passage. That he has also been brought safely from the Citadel of Winds... it is a sign of your prowess and my memory of our shared adventures that I am less surprised by that!\
\
'I look forward to hearing of my sister's adventures and to telling her my own. I still cannot believe that she is alive, but of course she was always... stubborn. She might say the same of me, but I believe Sigileth has always been more headstrong than I am. Since you have spent time with each of us, only you can tell us for certain.'\
\
Corudan smiles.\
\
'No, you can keep your answer. I know what it is.'","Chapter 7.5: Every River Leads To The Sea","'I have spoken with the others, and I still do not understand one thing. If the Corsair Jajax arranged with Khôltekh to gain access to the Citadel with his prisoner... why did the Temámir not accompany Jajax inside? If he believed Jajax's prisoner was truly Queen Arwen, would he not want to be present at the Kindred's triumph?'\
\
Gimli strokes his beard.\
\
'Unless... unless Khôltekh knew that Jajax had not actually captured Queen Arwen. But why would he help us rescue Thorongil? Is he secretly working against Azagath's aims?'\
\
You tell Gimli that your audience with Hármelak has shown you the Kindred of the Coins may not be as united in their purposes as it seems from the outside.\
\
'That is why the King Under The Mountain is so important, ${PLAYER}. I will keep thinking about it. Khôltekh's place in all this makes my head hurt!'","The successful completion of your mission to Umbar is the result of those who helped you, and many of them are now by the Harbour Warden's tower and want to speak with you.","Talk to Jajax by the Harbour Warden's tower","Talk to Nimrodel by the Harbour Warden's tower","Nimrodel is by the Harbour Warden's tower.","'Has it been so long that you have forgotten the most important rule of all, ${PLAYER}? Never count Jajax out of a fight, for he will return and surprise you! It is a lesson the Prince of Dol Amroth has now learned. You should have seen his face when it became apparent that only Jajax could turn defeat into victory!\
\
'Aye, it seemed defeat was certain. He has spies in this land, a band of whisperers and movers-in-secret that go by the name \\qCircle of the Eagle,\\q and when they reported to him that your ship never arrived, he despaired. A plan was conceived, a desperate plan, but it was considered the only option left to save the captive boy. The Prince could not achieve it, nor could the King. Only a Corsair would do. Only THE Corsair would do, and that means Jajax!\
\
'It is good to be owed favours by Kings and Princes, ${PLAYER}, and I shall be well-rewarded for my part in this deception. I admit I believed the water carried by Nimrodel was in some way enchanted and would prove more effective that it turned out... but all is well now. It must be the good fortune of Jajax coming through in the end once again.\
\
'How did my brother fare on your voyage? I hope he did not make too great a mess of things without me there to set him right!'","Talk to Caebar by the Harbour Warden's tower","'I have listened to the account of what transpired within the Citadel, ${PLAYER}, and my mind is clear. Belondor has no love for Gondor, and who could blame him for that, but he is not a monster. Whatever evil lies at the heart of the Kindred of the Coins, my old friend is not the cause of it. He would have prevented Nakási from slaying their young hostage... I am sure of it.\
\
'Azagath and the web he has woven has my friend caught, just as I was enmeshed by the commands of the Steward Denethor. Belondor is not beyond saving. Of this I am certain.'","'Our mission to Umbar is completed, ${PLAYER}, for both captives held by the Kindred of the Coins have been rescued. I will return with Thorongil to Anfalas as soon as it can be arranged. His father Carandolion will be very pleased, but not surprised, to learn that we have triumphed!\
\
'There will still be work to be done here in Umbar. I know it.'","'My brother always has a plan or a scheme in mind, ${PLAYER}! Do you think he had this planned all along? Is this why he refused to join your crew? It must be, surely!'\
\
You consider whether to dispel Daxamat's notion of his brother, and decide not to do so. You suspect that it would take a ship's hold full of evidence to lessen Daxamat's opinion of his brother, and even then it might not be possible.\
\
'My brother is really something, isn't he?' Daxamat asks you, and you have no choice but to nod in agreement.","Talk to your friends by the Harbour Warden's tower about the successful conclusion of your mission","'I have listened to the account of what transpired within the Citadel of Winds, ${PLAYER}, and it seems to me that Azagath Sea-shadow is no mere man. Nimrodel says she felt the mark of Sauron upon him... do you think he may be one of the Gúrzyul? If so, he has kept his nature hidden from the others of the Kindred and from the Umbari people. Nakási Wave-reaper spoke to you of the Song of Waves and Wind before she left Gondor, and I understand Hármelak mentioned it when you met with her, but she knew little more than its name.\
\
'Can it be that the Song of Waves and Wind has as its foundation some evil of Mordor? If that is so, we cannot leave Azagath to make use of it... whatever it may be. The adventure that brought us to Umbar is over... but our work here is not finished.'","'For long years I believed I was no longer a part of the world, ${PLAYER}, and I sheltered with the Avorrim and stood at a remove from all others. The kindness of Arwen, and the good heart of Roamingstar, have taught me I was wrong. In gratitude I offered to play a role in their drama... was it very different than the role I played for so long, the role of Dorthaneth?\
\
'I have set aside my veil of mourning, ${PLAYER}. It is good to be of help to my friends, no matter the dangers. Their kindness is like the warm sun upon my skin, and I welcome it.\
\
'But do not mistake me! The danger of Azagath remains. I judge that he is no ordinary man; I felt Sauron's mark upon him.'","'It is done, for now, is it not? We have carried out the commands of King Elessar, though they have brought us far from our homes.'\
\
Caebar looks out over the water, and shrugs his shoulders.\
\
'I suppose I don't really have a home any longer, do I? My mother and my uncle Carlong would not welcome me back to Ethring, not even if they knew the part I played on this grand adventure. Especially not if they knew. It wasn't that large a part, but I'd like to think I was some help along the way.\
\
'It is up to me to make a new home for myself now, somewhere out here in the world. I was so afraid of... I cannot say what I was afraid of, exactly... I think it was the \\qbigness\\q of the world, that sense of vast, open spaces, far beyond the land in which I grew up. It is so different here, but perhaps that is a good thing for me. I could not find a place in which to belong in the land of my birth. Maybe I will find a place here.\
\
'Thank you for bringing me along on your voyage! I will do whatever I can to help King Elessar bring peace to Gondor, and if that causes further conflict with the Kindred of the Coins, well... I will do what I can to help. All you need do is ask, ${PLAYER}. I will follow wherever you lead!\
\
'Just... maybe not aboard a ship next time,' he says, with laughter in his eyes.","Caebar is by the Harbour Warden's tower, a long way from his home.","'I have not had time yet to rest and to speak with my brother, for we have gone from one danger to another. I look forward to hearing of Corudan's adventures and telling him of my own. Perhaps that time has come.\
\
'It may not last, for while the Kindred of the Coins has claimed to make this a Free City, it would seem an evil has taken root within the membership of that council. I do not think your business in this land is yet finished, ${PLAYER}. Azagath remains a danger... and my heart tells me he is not the only member of the Kindred who is not as they appear.'","Jajax is by the Harbour Warden's tower."},
[3262]={"'What say you others? Will you come with us and hinder the workings of these Angmarim? If they have conducted some evil in this chamber we will make them tell us!'","Talk to Imák at the Witch-gate","'We have arrived. This is the Witch-gate.\
\
'Scouts report that the vale beyond is crawling with Angmarim cultists. I do not know much of this people, but I understand you have adventured in their realm? What can you say of them?'\
\
You briefly describe your adventures in Angmar, and Imák nods sagely.\
\
'Aye, it sounds dreadful. Guard against such bewitchment as they seek to bring against us, and we will stand strong, ${PLAYER}. They are servants without a master now, and we will scatter them like dried leaves. You fear them not, and neither shall I!'","Imák has asked if Fastrith and Bróin wish to investigate the dealings of the Angmarim cultists in Câr Bronach.","Imák stands at the Witch-gate between the Pit of Stonejaws and Câr Bronach.","'It is the unpleasant stench of ritual that I smell, ${PLAYER}, the distinctive odour of magic: the smell of a spell lingers about this chamber. I suspect it is the doing of Angmarim cultists such as those the scouts have spied lurking about the vale of Câr Bronach.\
\
'What say you others? Will you come with us and hinder the workings of these Angmarim? If they have conducted some evil in this chamber we will make them tell us!'","Meet up with Imák at the Witch-gate between the Pit of Stonejaws and Câr Bronach","Imák insists that he can smell the odour of magic about the chamber of Zul-mazal, and believes it may be the doing of Angmarim cultists.","Talk to Bróin in Zul-mazal","'We have arrived. This is the Witch-gate.'","'Bah! Let them stay if they want. If they could smell the distinct aura of magic that hangs upon this chamber they would not wish to stay, but few noses can boast of such perception as mine possesses!'","Strange runes carved into the Witch-gate lend the passage a foreboding air","'I believe I will remain here, ${PLAYER}, if that is all right with you. There is still much to be learned about this mosaic, though it lacks so many of its stones.\
\
'Perhaps Bróin will keep me company?'","'I would go with you, ${PLAYER}, but someone should really stay with Fastrith and keep her company while she studies the mosaic. Wouldn't you say? It would be a lonely business otherwise!'","Chapter 7.5: The Smell of a Spell","Imák has suggested that you meet up at the Witch-gate, which can be found at the connexion between the Pit of Stonejaws and Câr Bronach.","Talk to Fastrith in Zul-mazal"},
[3263]={"Talk to Náin the Slakeless in Járnfast","Durin is at his uncle's throne in Járnfast.","Defeated look-outs near Utterby (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated reinforcements near Skald's Drop (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Biraisbij tharâkh: Jangovar tents on the eastern side of Utterby","'There lies the town of Utterby, surrounded by the tents of the Jangovar. I do not think all who remain within are warriors, ${PLAYER}. We have no quarrel with the refugees, but those of the Jangovar who bear weapons wish us ill, and I mark them our enemies.\
\
'My uncle spoke true when he said I have little combat experience, but I have studied the art of war and am no novice in battlefield understanding! I was taught that the efficient commander finds the victory, and that is what I want to become. Let us use the words of my people to communicate on the battlefield, ${PLAYER}. The Jangovar will not understand us if we speak in this way, and that will give us the advantage.\
\
'First comes biraisbêj tharâkh, \\qscouting the approaches.\\q If I shout \\qbiraisbij tharâkh!\\q you will know we need to scout the locations to which our efforts turn. Next comes bini'zêg utrâd, \\qblinding the watchers.\\q Your objective in that case will be to defeat any look-outs that threaten to raise the alarm. Our next aim will be mahinsês mamahkhafdân, \\qrescuing the prisoners,\\q if any Dale-folk have been taken captive. By that point we should see about isgêr narakakâ, \\qdefeating the reinforcements\\q that are likely to come from Skald's Drop. I am still working out the kernel of a plan, but it may involve ensêkh, \\qsetting a trap,\\q if all goes well.\
\
'Do you understand all this, ${PLAYER}? Good! We cannot fail!'","'There lies Utterby. It was once the home of Dale-folk, but now it is occupied by the Jangovar.'","Isgir narakakâ (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have been ensêkh, ${PLAYER}! Weaken the cliff-face and we may be able to stall the Jangovar passage up the Drop!'","'Durin told me of the work you two did near Utterby and Skald's Drop, and I must commend you for it. I do not think the Jangovar will long remain in the Ironfold to trouble us!\
\
'Part of me wishes my nephew would remain here to assist me with finishing the job. As Lord of the Iron Hills, I command much respect and bear a great deal of responsibility for maintaining their peace, but my brother Thorin outranks me in age and in authority. He calls for his son, and I will not stand in the way!\
\
'It is time for my nephew to learn what it takes to lead, and to grow into the greatness of his name. Was it not for that very purpose that his father named him Durin?'","Ensikh to waylay the Jangovar at the cliff-face near Skald's Drop (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Chapter 7.6: Danger at the Drop","Bini'zig utrâd (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Let us go at once to Utterby and assess the situation. I know it is foolish to rush into battle without a plan, so meet me outside the city and we will gather the information we need to attain victory!'","The prisoner is grateful for your help, and makes his escape!","'Mahinsis mamahkhafdân, ${PLAYER}! And then isgir narakakâ!'","'First comes biraisbêj tharâkh, \\qscouting the approaches.\\q If I shout \\qbiraisbij tharâkh!\\q you will know we need to scout the locations to which our efforts turn. Next comes bini'zêg utrâd, \\qblinding the watchers.\\q Your objective in that case will be to defeat any look-outs that threaten to raise the alarm. Our next aim will be mahinsês mamahkhafdân, \\qrescuing the prisoners,\\q if any Dale-folk have been taken captive. By that point we should see about isgêr narakakâ, \\qdefeating the reinforcements\\q that are likely to come from Skald's Drop. I am still working out the kernel of a plan, but it may involve ensêkh, \\qsetting a trap,\\q if all goes well.'","Biraisbij tharâkh: Jangovar tents on the southern side of Utterby","'Part of me wishes my nephew would remain here to assist me with finishing the job. As Lord of the Iron Hills I command much respect and bear a great deal of responsibility for maintaining their peace, but my brother Thorin outranks me in age and in authority. He calls for his son, and I will not stand in the way!\
\
'It is time for my nephew to learn what it takes to lead, and to grow into the greatness of his name. Was it not for that very purpose that his father named him Durin?'","Durin suggested using dwarf-phrases that will be unfamiliar to the Jangovar in order to confuse your foes and to attain strategic advantage when you move against them:\
\
Biraisbêj tharâkh, \\qscouting the approaches.\\q \
Bini'zêg utrâd, \\qblinding the watchers.\\q \
Mahinsês mamahkhafdân, \\qrescuing the prisoners.\\q \
Isgêr narakakâ, \\qdefeating the reinforcements.\\q \
Ensêkh, \\qsetting a trap.\\q","You study the arrangement of the tents on the eastern side of Utterby","'Durin has a fine mind for military tactics and strategy, but he has little in the way of true experience, ${PLAYER}. Once he returns to his father in the Lonely Mountain, it will be more difficult for him to attain such valuable seasoning. I must impart to him what I can before he sets forth, and goes beyond the reach of my training.\
\
'As it happens, the state of affairs in the Ironfold could use some adjustment. My nephew may be just the one to do it, all while getting some good experience of his own. The town of Utterby was occupied by the Jangovar on their way to the Lonely Mountain, and I hear reports that Easterling reinforcements climb Skald's Drop every day. Many of them gather in tents around the city, and they ravage the lands thereabout.\
\
'Durin, I ask that you go to Utterby with ${PLAYER} and do what you can to combat our foes. It will be a good opportunity for you to accomplish two goals at once: to show what you have learned and to aid the people of the Ironfold. Do you agree to this plan?'","Meet up with Durin east of Utterby, in the Ironfold","Náin the Slakeless hopes that you and his nephew Durin will be able to combat some of the Easterling threat that remains within the Ironfold.","'We have done a great deal to hinder the efforts of the Jangovar Easterlings in the Ironfold, Uncle Náin.'","'I am ready for the challenge if you are, ${PLAYER}! Let us go at once to Utterby and assess the situation. I know it is foolish to rush into battle without a plan, so meet me outside the city and we will gather the information we need to attain victory!\
\
'You will not be disappointed, Uncle Náin! Let us go, my friend. Utterby awaits!'","Durin can be found by his uncle's throne in Járnfast.","'I think we have done very well, ${PLAYER}! My uncle is sure to be impressed by the work we have done to combat the Jangovar here in the Ironfold. And better: by weakening the cliff-face we have made it possible to hinder the flow of the Jangovar reinforcements climbing Skald's Drop. We will not collapse the path now, but dwarves will be able to do so at my uncle's command, should he deem it necessary.\
\
'Let us return to him in Járnfast with these good tidings!'","Talk to Durin at Skald's Drop","'The state of affairs in the Ironfold could use some adjustment, and my nephew may be just the one to do it! The town of Utterby was occupied by the Jangovar on their way to the Lonely Mountain, and I hear reports that Easterling reinforcements climb Skald's Drop every day. Many of them gather in tents around the city, and they ravage the lands thereabout.\
\
'Durin, I ask that you go to Utterby with ${PLAYER} and do what you can to combat our foes. It will be a good opportunity for you to accomplish two goals at once: to show what you have learned and to aid the people of the Ironfold. Do you agree to this plan?'","Weakened the cliff-face (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Durin eagerly watches the town of Utterby, threatened by the Jangovar","Durin is beneath the rising cliff-face at Skald's Drop.","'Ah, I hate when he talks like this, ${PLAYER}. I love my uncle, but not a day goes by without him telling me that I must be Durin the Deathless come again. Can you imagine it? It is quite frustrating.\
\
'It is not an uncommon name among my people, and no one forbade my father from naming me thus! It is not fair to compare me to such a measure... it would not be fair to anyone!'","Talk to Durin in Járnfast","The prisoner thanks you and makes his escape!","You study the arrangement of the tents on the southern side of Utterby","Durin is east of Utterby, in the Ironfold.","Talk to Durin east of Utterby","Mahinsis mamahkhafdân (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Náin the Slakeless, Lord of the Ironfort, can be found at his throne atop the ramps."},
[3264]={"Having scouted the Iron Pass, Imák thinks you should now do the same for the Narrow Way, the southern pass into Elderslade. He also wants you to continue your efforts to make the mountain paths safe for the Gabil'akkâ.","Venko has asked you to show the crumpled parchment to Imák.","Talk to Imák at the Narrow Way","You have met up with Imák at the Narrow Way only to discover that a former companion also shows an interest in the situation at Câr Bronach.","'Read the report I took from the Angmarim who thought to capture me, ${PLAYER}, and show it to Imák. I would know what both of you make of it.'","'I do not know these lands, but I studied the maps of the Gabil'akkâ and learned enough of them to plan our next steps. We should head north through Câr Bronach and see the state of the Iron Pass; no doubt it has been well-travelled in the months since the fall of Angmar Reborn.\
\
'It is not just the Angmarim that haunt these slopes. Let us slay the beasts that threaten our passage as we make for the Iron Pass.'","'Let us go back the way we came, and study the southernmost pass for similar signs. Any beasts that dare to threaten us will regret it, and serve as a warning to the Angmarim that fled to Câr Bronach!'","Scout the Narrow Way between Câr Bronach and Elderslade","'Ah-ha! I knew it! Did I not tell you so, ${PLAYER}? The Angmarim that fled to Câr Bronach brought an artifact of evil with them!'","Imák believes the mountain passes of Câr Bronach have been overrun by Angmarim cultists that threaten the mission of the Gabil'akkâ in Gundabad.","Read the crumpled parchment given to you by Venko","Talk to Venko at the Narrow Way","'¡Aquí!'","'Hail, friends! It is good to see you again. I trust you are here on the orders of Prince Durin? I myself was sent here by command of Prince Ingór, but I see no reason we should not join forces, as we did in the Wells of the Langflood, if our goals align and we work not at cross-purposes.\
\
'I was set upon by cultists of Angmar when I first came to Câr Bronach, but after a bit of sword-work I freed myself. From the body of my captor I took this!'","Chapter 7.6: Iron Pass and Narrow Way","Angmarim cultists fled through the Iron Pass to Gundabad when their kingdom fell","Your former companion Venko has also come to investigate the Narrow Way between Câr Bronach and Elderslade.","'What news does the old Zhélruka have for us?'","Venko is waiting to hear your thoughts at the Narrow Way between Câr Bronach and Elderslade.","Defeat beasts in Câr Bronach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Scout the Iron Pass in the north-western reaches of Câr Bronach","Venko hands you a crumpled piece of parchment","'We are in agreement, then? The cultists brought something out of Angmar, and we need to keep them from using it for some evil purpose!\
\
'I am sure both princes would agree on this, ${PLAYER}. Let us work together to end the danger this poses for the Gabil'akkâ!'","'Look who it is, ${PLAYER}! Our old friend Venko!'\
\
Imák lowers his voice.\
\
'The three of us did not always get along, it is true. But I confess that the several days since we adventured together have made me miss this old Zhélruka. What tidings does he have for us?'","'We should head north-west to the Iron Pass and slay the beasts that block our way.'","Defeated beasts in Câr Bronach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Iron Pass is located in the north-western reaches of Câr Bronach, and Imák wants you to make the road there as safe as you can while investigating the enemy presence on that route to Angmar.","You and Imák are not the only adventurers with an interest in the Narrow Way","Give the crumpled parchment to Imák at the Narrow Way","Venko gave you a crumpled piece of parchment that he wrestled from one of the Angmarim, and is waiting for you to read it.","'It is just as I said! This road may once have been little-travelled, but since their kingdom fell, the Angmarim have passed this way in great numbers.\
\
'Cultists fled this way, but I do not think they came alone. If the Men of Angmar are like those I knew in Mordor, I am sure they filled their pockets with as much wealth as they could carry. I do not begrudge them that, though such riches are surely tainted by evil, and woe to those who seek to spend them! No, what worries me, and should worry you, is what else these cultists might have brought out of Angmar when their kingdom fell. Did they bring with them artifacts of fell power, relics of the Witch-king's rule? They might have brought anything from their defeated kingdom, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Let us go back the way we came, and study the southernmost pass for similar signs. Any beasts that dare to threaten us will regret it, and serve as a warning to the Angmarim that fled to Câr Bronach!'","'The Angmarim that fled to Câr Bronach brought an artifact of evil with them!'","Talk to Imák at the Iron Pass"},
[3265]={"Talk to Náin in the hidden chamber","Talk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Quenching Trough","Authi Gem-cutter is in the Quenching Trough.","'I have been cleaning out my father's house, ${PLAYER}, and I... well, I found something unusual. I have no friends here in Járnfast save for you, so there is nowhere else for me to turn!\
\
'Will you come help me make sense of this? Please tell me you will!'","Náin is in the hidden chamber in Khîl's home in Járnfast.","Satisfied with his efforts against the Jangovar in the Ironfold, Durin is now ready to return to the Lonely Mountain with you, but first you need to find Authi Gem-cutter and make sure he is ready to go home.","'Khîl has come here and will not stop bothering me! Will you help him with whatever nonsense he is chattering about?'","Talk to Khîl and travel to his father's home","'You'll come see? Good, good! I really appreciate this, my friend!'","'I am ready to return to the Lonely Mountain with you, ${PLAYER}. I understand there is to be another dwarf travelling with us? Yes, Authi Gem-cutter. Where is he to be found?\
\
'The Quenching Trough? You are welcome to go there and retrieve him, friend. I have spent more than enough time within those walls, and do not desire to spend any more. Now my thirst can only be quenched by battle and glory, and that lies beyond Járnfast!\
\
'I will meet up with you after you have found Authi.'","Talk to Khîl in the Quenching Trough","'Oh! ${PLAYER}! My friend! I have discovered something most unusual!'","Chapter 7.7: The Hidden Chamber","'You are welcome to go to the Quenching Trough and retrieve Authi Gem-cutter, friend. I have spent more than enough time within those walls, and do not desire to spend any more. Now my thirst can only be quenched by battle and glory, and that lies beyond Járnfast!\
\
'I will meet up with you after you have found Authi.'","'Have you come to save me, ${PLAYER}? I simply wanted to drink in peace, but Khîl has come here and will not stop bothering me! Will you help him with whatever nonsense he is chattering about?'","'You might as well go with him, ${PLAYER}. After you see whatever has him so worked up we can set out for our return to the Lonely Mountain.'","Khîl is in the Quenching Trough, quite distraught.","'What does this mean? For how long has this chamber remained hidden right beneath our very noses? I do not like secrets in my city, ${PLAYER}, especially when those secrets come from the land of Mordor.'"},
[3266]={"Venko shivers nervously","Bring the orders from Magith to Venko outside Tâg Fógarrach","'Do not be fooled by such sentimental apparitions, Venko! I feel in my heart this has something to do with the rituals of the Angmarim being conducted in their vile tower. This has the stench of foul magic upon it, and I wager they are somehow to blame. We must not fall for their tricks!'","'Dúsek could not be here, and yet he was, in appearance just as I remember him. What can it mean, my friends?'","'The Angmarim are up to something in Câr Bronach, that much is clear. Defeat as many of the cultists as you can find, and I will do the same. Some of them are bound to carry reports from which we can learn more of their plans, and with good fortune we may learn where they brought this artifact!'","You retrieved a set of orders from one of the cultists you faced in Câr Bronach, and should read it to learn what you can of their movements and plans for the mountain passes.","'Defeat as many of the cultists or their Trév Duvárdain allies as you can find, and I will do the same. Some of them are bound to carry reports from which we can learn more of their plans, and with good fortune we may learn where they brought this artifact!'","Defeated Angmarim cultists or Trév Duvárdain in Câr Bronach (${NUMBER}/8)","Venko saw something disturbing to the south-east, just behind Tâg Fógarrach, and he has asked you to investigate. Whatever he saw, the vision seems to have shaken the Zhélruka's composure.","Talk to Imák south-west of Tûr Fúar","Someone watches","Chapter 7.7: The Valley of Ghosts","Defeat Angmarim cultists or Trév Duvárdain in Câr Bronach (${NUMBER}/8)","Venko saw something disturbing by the mountainside to the south-east, behind Tâg Fógarrach, and he has asked you to investigate. Whatever he saw, the vision seems to have shaken the Zhélruka's composure.","'Did you... did you see anything, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Venko that you felt eyes upon you, but the watchful presence did not show itself to you. His brow creases with worry and with thought.\
\
'I thought I saw my younger brother Dúsek. He stood there, just by the mountainside, and watched me in silence. I called out to him, but he did not answer. I called again, though I knew it was for naught, for Dúsek is dead and will never see Gundabad. Did we not honour him at the Reikfoss, ${PLAYER}, both he and my eldest brother Lékhun, slain by the Frost-horde?\
\
'Dúsek could not be here, and yet he was, in appearance just as I remember him. What can it mean, my friends?'","Talk to Venko outside Tâg Fógarrach","Venko believes there is more to learn from the messages carried hither and yon by Angmarim cultists within Câr Bronach. He wants you to wrest from them any such missives.","Read the orders from Magith","Imák is south-west of Tûr Fúar, stroking his beard thoughtfully.","Defeat Angmarim cultists or Trév Duvárdain in Câr Bronach (7/8)","You find a set of orders on this Angmarim","Venko is outside Tâg Fógarrach. No doubt the Zhélruka will be pleased to see the set of orders you recovered from the Angmarim cultist you defeated.","Ordered by Prince Ingór to learn more about the Angmarim presence in Câr Bronach, Venko is pleased to adventure with you and Imák once again.","'I thought I saw... well, someone that couldn't be there. Can you... can you go to the south-east, just behind Tâg Fógarrach, and see if there is anything to see?'","'Hmmm? What?'\
\
Venko appears quite distracted, his attention distant. At last he notices your presence and turns confused eyes on you.\
\
'Oh, I am sorry, ${PLAYER}. I thought I saw... well, someone that couldn't be there. Can you... can you go to the south-east, just behind Tâg Fógarrach, and see if there is anything to see?'","The watchful presence departs. You are once again alone","You feel watchful eyes upon you, but otherwise no sign of anyone","Venko is outside Tâg Fógarrach, disturbed by whatever it was he saw.","Investigate the mountainside to the south-east, behind Tâg Fógarrach, and learn what could have shaken Venko's composure"},
[3267]={"'We need to bring word of the Angmarim intention to break the wards on the Gloomingtarn. Let us climb the path to the Witch-gate itself and then we will bring this urgent message together!'","Approaching the gate, you see a figure that cannot be","'If the vision that so troubled Venko is the result of some Angmarim ritual, I think I know just where we will find the source of it. What do they call their tower? Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire? If those orders you recovered are to be believed, it may be that the complement of guards promised by Magith the Scather has not yet been dispatched to fortify the tower.\
\
'Let us sneak inside and put an end to whatever magic these cultists think to unleash. We will all be the better for it, and Venko not least of all!'","Talk to Venko north of the Witch-gate","Talk to Imák at the Witch-gate","'We need to bring word of the Angmarim intention to break the wards on the Gloomingtarn. Let us meet up at the Witch-gate and then we will bring this urgent message together!'","Someone watches","'What is wrong, ${PLAYER}? What did you see?'\
\
You tell Imák you recognized a figure from your past, who could not possibly be there.\
\
'I believe you, for I also saw someone impossible. I saw a dwarf-woman named Anorta, who I knew during my captivity in Mordor. I escaped from the Black Land, but Anorta did not. She is dead. She could not be here... and yet I saw her standing just ahead, just as I remembered her.'","'The Drearspire awaits us. Are you ready?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Once again, the watchful presence departs and you are alone","Chapter 7.8: A Silent Presence","Return to the Witch-gate with Imák and Venko","'This time I saw my eldest brother, Lékhun, and he seemed just the same to me as he did in life. What did the watchful presence show to you, ${PLAYER}? Who did you see?'\
\
You tell Venko that you beheld a Ranger named Amdir, who suffered a grievous, corrupting injury from a Nazgûl's blade when you adventured in Bree-land. He nods solemnly.\
\
'He is dead, or worse than dead? Then he cannot be here... and yet you saw him. There is some strange force at work in these mountains, but it is not the work of the Angmarim. It is something else.'","Venko is at the Witch-gate, waiting to speak with you about what you saw.","Imák stands at the Witch-gate, a haunted expression on his face.","Imák believes that the troubling presence that so disturbed Venko might be the result of a ritual being conducted by the Angmarim in Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire. The Stout-axe thinks the three of you should investigate, despite the danger.","Talk to Venko at the Witch-gate","Talk to Imák and sneak into the Drearspire of Tûr Fúar","Imák and Venko are prepared to depart Câr Bronach, and want to travel with you to the Witch-gate.","You once again feel the watchful presence.","Venko is north of the Witch-gate.","Imák believes that the troubling presence that so disturbed Venko might be the result of a ritual being conducted by the Angmarim in Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire, and he wants you to investigate."},
[3268]={"Chapter 7: A True Friend of Durin's Folk","Thorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.","'Have you returned to see the king? It is good that you have done so, but you should also speak to Bósi. The loss of Khazad-dûm will be treating him badly.'","'When first you were made known to me, I did not expect to see such depth of service, ${PLAYER}. You have exceeded my expectations in every respect, and are a true friend of Durin's Folk.\
\
'But more than that, you are a true friend to me: Thorin III, King under the Mountain. I adopt the name \\qStonehelm\\q with pride, and will wear it as a symbol of my steadfastness and strength, and that of Durin's Folk. It will be a reminder to me that not all deeds come easily, and those for which we struggle may be the most worthy of all.\
\
'It is with that spirit that I will not inflict a harsh punishment upon Bósi and the Iron Garrison for fleeing from the disaster of Khazad-dûm. There will come a day when the hammers of the dwarves ring again in the depths of that mighty city. It will be my duty to prepare Durin's Folk for that day, and I will undertake it as best I may.\
\
'You are always welcome in these halls, ${PLAYER}! Go forth and seek glory and treasure worthy of your name and your tale!'","Bósi is in the Hall under the Mountain.","'Welcome back to the Lonely Mountain, ${PLAYER}. When last I saw you, I planned to speak with the King under the Mountain and accept his judgment in the matter of the Iron Garrison, but the appearance of Lachagar quite interrupted the matter. I have since spoken with the king, and he has ruled mercifully. I still have my freedom, and my neck!\
\
'Were there some who might see cowardice in this ruling of King Thorin? Perhaps at one time, but his bravery in the battle with Lachagar has proven to many that he is made of the same strong material as his father. His mercy is seen as wise and just by most of the dwarves here. I am grateful for his leniency, if not convinced I am deserving of it. I will grieve for my cousin Brogur and the many others who fell in Khazad-dûm, early and late, Miners and Guards, and will never forget them.\
\
'King Thorin believes that only Durin could retake Khazad-dûm now. Perhaps he is right, but for now I cannot think so. I have been instructed to bring you to the king. Speak to me when you are ready.'","'Welcome back to Erebor, ${PLAYER}. Bósi wished to speak with you, and then you should attend King Thorin, who has further words for you.'","Talk to Bósi in the Hall under the Mountain","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to Durin's Folk and fight on their behalf in Mordor.","'The King under the Mountain waits to see you. Come with me, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Bósi and go with him to see the king","Talk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain","Bósi has been instructed to bring you before the King under the Mountain.","'It has been some time since you returned to the Lonely Mountain, has it not? You should present yourself to King Thorin and see what taxing errand he has for you now! Perhaps you can speak to Bósi when you go, and learn how he fares.'"},
[3270]={"Talk to Radanir and travel with him to Zudrugund","'Are you ready, ${PLAYER}? We will travel to Zudrugund together, and at once!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo, you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","Radanir is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in the grove of trees to the east of Lhanuch.\
\
Radanir is waiting to speak with you, and together you will travel to Zudrugund with all haste to try and defend it from the uruks of which Ergothorn wrote.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo, you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","Corunir is in Zudrugund.\
\
You have managed to stave off an attack on Zudrugund by the Grishgúk Uruks led by Núrzumgrat, and should speak now to Corunir.","Chapter 7: Attack on Zudrugund","'We have to leave at once if we are to have any hope of arriving in time to face the uruks, ${PLAYER}. We may already be too late. Let me know if you are ready!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","Talk to Corunir in Zudrugund","'I am pleased that you came to the defence of Zudrugund, ${PLAYER}! Once again, Ergothorn has saved us a great deal of trouble. Why do I not feel more relieved by this?'","Ergothorn has left the Rangers a second letter: a band of uruks has come out of Dunland and is marching towards Zudrugund!","'We were able to defend Zudrugund from attack, but we are still no closer to solving the mystery of Nár. And now we know that Saruman has some interest in the dwarf as well! You should return to Zudrugund and speak with Corunir.'"},
[3271]={"Collect treasure coffers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I am still waiting for you to do what you said you would do!'","'Excellent, excellent! We will bring these treasures out into the sunlight with us. Let us go, ${PLAYER}! I will meet you back at, what was the name? Echad Eregion? Tell my son I am on my way.'","'My father is back, ${PLAYER}, and he was very pleased at your performance within the ruins. He's been deep in conversation with one of the Rangers here.\
\
'I think they want him to make something, but what it is I have no idea! That Ranger, Radanir, might be able to tell you more.'","'The dwarf's father has returned from the ruins, ${PLAYER}. He has been deep in conversation with Halbarad for a while now.'","'I will leave shortly for Echad Eregion! Tell my son I will be there soon!'","'There is treasure all over these ruins, ${PLAYER}. We cannot leave it in the hands of these uruks!'","Collected treasure coffers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'These uruks call themselves \\qNinkoth\\q, but I care not; they are as miserable a creature as any I have seen. It seems they have come north on the heels of another breed, but these have designs of settling down in these lands. What an idea! Better up here than down near Zigil-jabâl, my home in the White Mountains, but still too close for comfort. We have had troubles there enough.\
\
'The Ninkoth uruks kept me alive for a purpose, friend. They've been bringing golden trinkets to me from throughout the cellars of this place, with the idea that I could somehow fashion them into items of worth. Which of course I can, but would never do for these creatures!\
\
'I cannot bear the thought of these treasures being left here for the Ninkoth. Explore these ruins, gather up the treasure, and bring it back to me! I would not mind a bit if you took some time to slay some uruks, either! Oh! You may want to make a map!'","Treasure and Ninkoth uruks can be found throughout the ruins of Minas Elendúr and the Delotham under-cellars.\
\
Fúni Gem-cutter is waiting for you to retrieve as much treasure from the ruins as you can.","Talk to Radanir at Echad Eregion","Fúni Gem-cutter is in Minas Elendúr.\
\
You have done what Fúni asked, and should return to him with the treasures you have gathered.","'You found Fúni Gem-cutter, but he will not leave until you recover treasure from the ruins of Minas Elendúr? How long will this delay last?'","Bring treasures to Fúni Gem-cutter in Minas Elendúr","Chapter 7: Bewildering Ruins","'I have just been talking with Halbarad, ${PLAYER}, and now this whole affair with the Gem-cutters makes sense to me. I now know why Halbarad thought this delay to be necessary, and I agree with him.\
\
'He has a commission for Fúni Gem-cutter, a task for which Fúni is well-suited. He wants Fúni to make an imitation of the Ring of Barahir.'","'My father has not yet returned! You must go to Minas Elendúr and show him the way!'","You have found Fúni Gem-cutter, but he is not content merely to be rescued: he wants you to rescue as much gold from the Ninkoth uruks in Minas Elendúr as you can.","'You have gathered treasure from Minas Elendúr? At least you have deprived the Ninkoth uruks of it. But where is Fúni Gem-cutter?'","Fúsi Gem-cutter is at Echad Eregion.\
\
You have rescued his father and should bring the news to Fúsi.","Talk to Fúsi Gem-cutter at Echad Eregion","Radanir is at Echad Eregion.\
\
The Rangers have been discussing something with Fúni Gem-cutter, now that he has been rescued, and Radanir may know more about it.","'My father is still within Minas Elendúr? What is taking so long?'","'I do not yet know what the Rangers want my father to make. That Radanir might know!'"},
[3272]={"'Cuando llegamos aquí, a las Fundaciones de Piedra, lo hicimos por petición de la Dama Galadriel, y teníamos un objetivo principal: averiguar qué destino le había deparado a Mithrandir, el Peregrino Gris, en estas profundidades.\
\
Sí, hablo de Gandalf. Pasó a la sombra del abismo, y la esperanza de la Dama era que pudiera ser encontrado, y que esté sano y salvo. El Elfo Magor lo buscó durante muchos días, pero no encontró ningún rastro. \
\
Magor todavía no ha regresado, ${PLAYER}, y estoy empezando a preocuparme. Hay dos lugares que me gustaría que buscaras para encontrar alguna señal de Mithrandir o Magor: la parte superior de la sección inferior de la Escalera Interminable y el Lago negro. Cuando hayas buscado en ambos lugares, espero que tengas alguna señal del Mago o de Magor.'","'No me has traído nada útil.'","Lenglammel se encuentra en su campamento de Gwathrendath, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Has buscado en ambos lugares y has encontrado el sombrero quemado de Gandalf en el medio del Lago Negro. La Escalera Interminable está bloqueada por escombros quemados y ennegrecidos. Parece que Gandalf sobrevivió lo suficiente para enfrentarse al Balrog, pero lo que pasó después es desconocido para ti. Ahora deberías hablar con Lenglammel.","Capítulo 7: Más allá de la luz y el conocimiento","Describes tu hallazgo del sombrero quemado de Gandalf en medio del Lago Negro y de los escombros que obstruyen la Escalera Interminable. Lenglammel suspira.\
\
'Tus noticias sobre Mithrandir y la falta de noticias sobre mi amigo Magor me llenan de inquietud, pues aún desconocemos cuál ha sido su suerte. Te lo agradezco, pero podría ser que, al menos, Magor vuelva pronto con nosotros.\
\
'Dithaliwenn encontró algo mientras estabas fuera'.","Busca encima de la sección inferior de la Escalera Interminable","'Quedan varios lugares por buscar, ${PLAYER}, y en particular el pie de la Escalera Interminable y el Lago Negro. Quizás encuentres alguna señal de Mithrandir o del Elfo Magor en esos lugares. Al menos eso espero.'","El Lago Negro y el pie de la Escalera Interminable se encuentran entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Lenglammel te ha pedido que busques en varios lugares alguna señal de Mithrandir o del Elfo Magor.","Lenglammel no ha tenido éxito hasta ahora en su misión principal en Moria: localizar y rescatar a Mithrandir, si es que se puede rescatar a un Mago.","Busca el Lago Negro","Estos escombros están quemados y rotos, y bloquean el paso por la escalera","Lleva el sombrero quemado a Lenglammel","Este sombrero está quemado y cubierto de cenizas, pero sin duda perteneció a Gandalf el Gris"},
[3273]={"'The Lossoth rely in large part upon the skill of their hunters. Forochel is an inhospitable land, and though they are accomplished hunters and know every hill and plain around the Ice-bay, there can still be lean times.\
\
'In recent days, after some of the hunters have brought down game animals, a screaming apparition has descended upon their prey from out of the darkness and borne it away amid the Lossoth's confusion and terror. I do not know what manner of beast this may be, but I have tracked it to what must be its lair.\
\
'Come with me and let us finish this screaming shadow, that the Lossoth may bring in enough food to feed their people, and I will be satisfied. I will bring my knowledge of the south-lands with me as we ride to Aragorn.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Chapter 7: Lothrandir of the Frozen Wastes","Calenglad has sent you to speak with Lothrandir, a Ranger sent to Forochel, to bring him word of the Grey Company's mission.","'Lothrandir is a good man, and a fine Ranger. You will find him at Sûri-kylä, the major Lossoth village in Forochel.'","'Gun Ain's life is her own, now. Whether it will be long or short will depend upon the choices she makes. If she spurns our help and continues to harass the Lossoth, it will be short indeed. Perhaps she will find a way to leave her troubled past behind. It is to be hoped she will do so, for otherwise she will perish, alone and without the name for which she grieves.\
\
'You have done as I asked, and now the Lossoth will be able to bring in their rightful prey without interference. I will do my duty, as I said I would. I will join the Grey Company on the south road.'","'You say it is time for the Dúnedain to ride out of the north, ${PLAYER}? It is a long way to Rohan, and even if that be where Aragorn has need of us, none know the perilous roads like I do.\
\
'Yes, I have travelled in the southern lands. I have walked the hills and valleys of Enedwaith, been stalked by savage creatures in the mysterious wood-lands, and climbed among the rocky heights of Thror's Coomb. There are dangers on that road that must not be dismissed. There is no guarantee that even a dozen Rangers will come to Aragorn at his time of need...or at all.\
\
'The blood of the Dúnedain flows through my veins, and they will always be my people, but I have another people now as well, and I want them to be safe. I speak of the Lossoth. Will you help me protect them from the mysterious foe that strikes from the heart of storms and under the cover of black night?'","Lothrandir is at Sûri-kylä, the major village of the Lossoth in Forochel.\
\
Calenglad has sent you to bring your message to Lothrandir, in Forochel, with the warning that he has lived among the Lossoth for so long that he may have taken on something of their customs and personalities.","Talk to Lothrandir and help him find the screaming shadow","Lothrandir is at Sûri-kylä, in Forochel.\
\
You have found the cause of the Lossoth's hunting troubles and have hopefully ended it. Lothrandir, at least, seems satisfied.","'I will speak with some others of the Dúnedain here in Evendim about joining with the Grey Company on its journey south, but you should travel now north to Forochel. I sent the Ranger Lothrandir to meet with the Lossoth some time ago about the growing danger of Angmar, but once his task was completed, he loved the land and its people so much that he decided to remain.\
\
'He would be disappointed to learn the Grey Company was called without his participation. Travel north to Sûri-kylä to speak with Lothrandir, but keep this in mind: he has lived among the Lossoth for quite a while now and has surely adopted some of their customs and taken on something of their personalities.'","Lothrandir is at Sûri-kylä, in Forochel.\
\
You have given Lothrandir the message, but he seems unsure of the Grey Company's ability to reach Aragorn in time and wants your help with a Lossoth issue.","Talk to Lothrandir at Sûri-kylä"},
[3274]={"Tranquiliza a los nerviosos Malledhrim a lo largo de Audaghaim (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Issuriel está preocupada por el sentimiento de terror que se cierne sobre el pueblo abandonado de Audaghaim y por las cosas extrañas que los Elfos han visto allí.","'Estoy listo para salir de este lugar, ${PLAYER}. He visto formas fantasmales en la penumbra, imágenes vagas en las esquinas y entre los árboles aquí en Audaghaim.'\
\
Ofreces palabras reconfortantes al nervioso Elfo, y él te agradece por tomarte el tiempo. De repente, sus ojos se abren de alarma.","Capítulo 7: Al borde","'¡Todos mis amigos están nerviosos, reportando extrañas visiones justo al borde de la vista. No podemos salir de Audaghaim lo suficientemente rápido para mí!'\
\
La tranquilizas con palabras amables, y ella te agradece por tomarte el tiempo para consolarla.","'Habla con algunos de los Elfos por todo Audaghaim sobre las cosas perturbadoras que han visto y tranquilízalos diciéndoles que todo estará bien. No podemos quedarnos aquí mucho más tiempo, pero quiero que los nerviosos Malledhrim entre nosotros sepan que estamos seguros mientras debemos quedarnos.'","Los nerviosos Malledhrim se encuentran por todo Audaghaim.\
\
Issuriel te ha pedido que tranquilices a los nerviosos Malledhrim por todo Audaghaim diciéndoles que todo estará bien, a pesar de las cosas perturbadoras que han visto en este pueblo abandonado.","'¿Lo sientes, ${PLAYER}? No puedo quitarme la sensación de que algo muy malo está sucediendo en las ruinas de este pueblo. Estaba mirando por encima de la cascada, y una gran ola de terror me invadió. No sé qué fue, pero no me quedé mucho tiempo.'\
\
Lo tranquilizas con palabras reconfortantes, y él parece sentirse mejor.","'Esta ciudad abandonada también me pone nervioso, ${PLAYER}, así que puedo entender por qué nuestros amigos están nerviosos. Hay algo en Audaghaim que me hace sentir incómodo.'","Nerviosos Malledhrim tranquilizados a lo largo de Audaghaim (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Seguramente has notado el sentimiento de terror que se cierne sobre partes de Audaghaim, ${PLAYER}. No pensé mucho en ello cuando llegamos, pero mi inquietud ha crecido, y ahora otros están reportando haber visto extraños espectros por toda la ciudad.\
\
¿Puedes tranquilizarme, camarada? Te pediría que hables con algunos de los Elfos por todo Audaghaim sobre las cosas perturbadoras que han visto y les asegures que todo estará bien. No podemos quedarnos aquí mucho más tiempo, pero quiero que los nerviosos Malledhrim entre nosotros sepan que estamos seguros mientras debemos quedarnos.'","Habla con Issuriel en la Posada Embrujada","Issuriel está en el sótano de la Posada Embrujada, en Audaghaim.\
\
Has tranquilizado a un gran número de nerviosos Malledhrim y deberías volver a ver a Issuriel."},
[3276]={"Talk to Lady Galadriel to be released, finally, from your service.","Glorfindel is come to the Council of War in the Court of Lothlórien.","Chapter 7: The Bow is Drawn","Habla con Galadriel","'Come with me, ${PLAYER}. There are things the council would discuss. But there is more, for you have been of great help to our cause and the Lord and Lady wish to offer thanks to you for your service.'","'You have done so much for us, ${PLAYER} and our gratitude is near immeasurable. By the fair stars above and the sign of the golden leaves, I free and release you from your troth of service.\
\
'Go now and serve whom and how you please. I have every faith you will bring light and goodness wherever your journeys take you.'","Habla con Orophin","You should talk to Orophin and join the War Council.","'Urgent and wondrous tidings, ${PLAYER}! Glorfindel is arrived in the Court of Lothlórien. They await your arrival. Go. Go now!'","'I hardly believed your account, ${PLAYER}, but now I must hold my eyes for liars, for there is Glorfindel himself, among the Council of War. I beg of you, speak to Orophin, who shall present you, for this is an occasion of joyous ceremony.'"},
[3277]={"'¡Imagínate lo imparables que seríamos si pudiéramos recuperar Zigilburk de las tinieblas del pasado! ¡No temería ningún ataque de los orcos, eso es seguro!\
\
'Tengo un buen presentimiento sobre esto: la Sala del Mithril debe ser sin duda las armerías que Óin buscaba. ¡Si tan solo las hubiera encontrado a tiempo, ¡los enanos de la expedición de Balin podrían haber sobrevivido!\
\
'Es demasiado tarde para ellos, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, pero no para nosotros. Viajaremos a la Sala del Mithril en busca de estas armerías. Habla conmigo cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Se sugiere completar esta misión mientras estás en una comunidad. La inspiración te ayudará si decides emprender este desafío solo o con un grupo más pequeño.</rgb>","'¡Esta aventura puede no ser fácil, pero si podemos encontrar Zigilburk en las profundidades de Ghân-gharâf, todo habrá valido la pena!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Se sugiere completar esta misión mientras estás en una comunidad. La inspiración te ayudará si decides emprender este desafío solo o con un grupo más pequeño.</rgb>'","Habla con Bori","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bori y tú descubrieron a Bróin, todavía vivo a pesar de las grandes dificultades, y lo trajeron sano y salvo del tesoro sumergido donde encontró el hacha de mithril Zigilburk.","'¡${PLAYER}, somos héroes! Bróin sigue vivo, y el hacha de mithril Zigilburk ha salido de las tinieblas justo en nuestro momento de mayor necesidad!\
\
'¿Puedes creer nuestra buena fortuna? ¡A este ritmo, en una semana seguramente habremos expulsado al último orco aullando como un perro de Moria!'","Capítulo 7: El tesoro sumergido","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bori está esperando para hablar contigo y viajar a la Sala del Mithril, donde cree que encontrarás el hacha de mithril Zigilburk. Te pidió que trajeras aliados.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Se sugiere completar esta misión mientras estás en una comunidad. La inspiración te ayudará si decides emprender este desafío solo o con un grupo más pequeño.</rgb>","Bori cree que has descubierto la ubicación de las armerías que el condenado enano Óin buscaba hace muchos años, y que podrían contener el hacha de mithril Zigilburk.","Habla con Bori y viaja a la Sala del Mithril"},
[3278]={"'Has luchado valientemente y bien, ${PLAYER}, como esperaba, pero lo más importante es esto: ¡las forjas secretas del Corazón de Fuego están ahora al servicio de mi pueblo!\
\
'Es una lástima que no hayamos encontrado a Zigilburk en el Corazón de Fuego, pero me equivoqué al esperarlo: rara vez las armas permanecen en el lugar de su fabricación, ¿no es su propósito salir al mundo y encontrar gloria en el campo de batalla? Aun así, esto sigue siendo una gran victoria para mi expedición.\
\
'Si tienes la habilidad, las forjas de Nâr-khelab están, por supuesto, a tu servicio.'","Bósi cree que ha descubierto la ubicación de Nâr-khelab, la forja donde se fabricó el hacha de mithril Zigilburk.","'Are you ready, ${PLAYER}? If my guess is near the mark, we will soon find the Heart of Fire, and I will set the dwarves of my company to its mighty forges!\
\
'And perhaps Zigilburk itself still remains within! Imagine: an axe made entirely of mithril. What a wonder!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'Mira aquí, ${PLAYER}. ¡El lugar de Nâr-khelab, el Corazón de Fuego, está en este mapa rudimentario de los trasgos! ¿No lo ves?'\
\
Bósi se ríe, claramente disfrutando de la atención.\
\
'Déjame decirlo así, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}: sabemos que la puerta del Corazón de Fuego está sellada; de hecho, tú descubriste el truco para abrirla en la Cámara de las Palabras de Durin. Pero los trasgos no pueden conocer ese truco: las páginas que contenían el secreto fueron perturbadas solo por los rascabismos; si los trasgos hubieran encontrado esas páginas y comprendido su significado, ciertamente las habrían tomado.\
\
'No estamos buscando una habitación en este mapa, ; estamos buscando un tramo de pared sin perturbar detrás del cual podría estar oculta tal habitación, ¡y he encontrado justo ese lugar! ¡Avísame cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} y juntos viajaremos a ese lugar!'","Habla con Bósi y viaja con él para encontrar Nâr-khelab","Bósi está en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación de Moria.\
\
Con la ayuda de Bósi, has descubierto la entrada oculta a Nâr-khelab, el Corazón de Fuego, y ahora deberías hablar con él.","Bósi está en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, cerca de la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación de Moria.\
\
Bósi cree que ha intuido la entrada oculta a Nâr-khelab, el Corazón de Fuego, y está esperando para viajar allí contigo.","'¡Qué increíble que Nâr-khelab exista realmente!'","'¡Los enanos de mi compañía han ido a trabajar en las forjas de Nâr-khelab, y es un trabajo alegre!'","Capítulo 7: El Pasaje Vacío"},
[3279]={"Derrota a los huargos de las sombras (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Bróin","'Has regresado, ${PLAYER}, ¡y ${PLAYER:victorioso[m]|victoriosa[f]} sobre los huargos de las sombras! Realmente eres ${PLAYER:un aventurero[m]|una aventurera[f]} de gran valía, ¿no es así?\
\
'Para decir la verdad, mi batalla contra ese huargo de las sombras no fue exactamente digna de una canción; estaba demasiado asustado para hacer algo más que sobrevivir. Supongo que no soy un gran héroe. ¿Está en mí hacer grandes hazañas? ¿Alguna vez se cantará una canción sobre mí, o mi nombre será olvidado?\
\
'Eres muy amable, . Espero tener pronto la oportunidad de demostrar mi valía como tú lo has hecho.'","'Eres ${PLAYER:el viajero[m]|la viajera[f]} que ayudó a Bori a recoger esas piedras, ¿verdad? Eso pensé, tengo buen ojo para los rostros y nunca olvido un nombre, ¡especialmente uno que pertenece a ${PLAYER:un aventurero[m]|una aventurera[f]}! Por supuesto, cuanto más peligrosas sean las hazañas que logres, más memorable serás, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Eso es lo que espero hacer, ya sabes. Una vez que entremos en Khazad-dûm, Bori y yo nos convertiremos en grandes héroes, y las historias de nuestras aventuras se contarán por toda la tierra. Dentro de unos años, 'La historia gloriosa de Bróin el Poderoso' podría inspirar a los jóvenes enanos tal como las canciones de Durin y de Thorin Escudo de Roble inspiran a Bori y a mí hoy en día.\
\
'Si quieres ayudarme con la tarea que me dio mi padre, sin embargo, no lo rechazaría. Hay huargos de las sombras al sur, al otro lado del lecho del Sirannon seco. Derrota a algunas de las bestias por mí, si quieres; ya he matado a uno de ellos, pero eso no es realmente suficiente. ¡Que la buena fortuna te acompañe, ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}!'","Capítulo 7: La historia gloriosa de Bróin el Poderoso","'Realmente aprecio esto, ${PLAYER}. Tus combates con los peligrosos huargos de las sombras seguramente serán una parte importante de tu historia.\
\
'Los encontrarás al sur de aquí, del otro lado del lecho seco del Sirannon.'","Huargos de las sombras derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El hijo de Brogur, Bróin, ha pedido tu ayuda para combatir a los peligrosos huargos de las sombras que merodean más allá de las orillas del Sirannon.","Bróin se encuentra al pie de las escaleras que suben al lago fétido frente a la Puerta de Acebeda, al este de donde viste a Bosi.\
\
Has derrotado a un gran número de huargos de las sombras y ahora deberías volver a ver a Bróin.","Los huargos de las sombras se encuentran al sur de las escaleras que suben al lago frente a la Puerta de Acebeda, del otro lado del lecho seco del Sirannon.\
\
Bróin ha encontrado la manera de endosarte esta tarea, y ahora tienes que enfrentarte a los huargos de las sombras en su lugar."},
[3280]={"Capítulo 7: El Taller Perdido","'¡Lo lograste, ${PLAYER}! Mira estos dibujos: esto es claramente Zabadgathol, lo que significa que estos pasillos aquí conectan con Rushdurinul, y...'\
\
Bróin se ríe de alegría.\
\
'¿Ves este túnel aquí? Apostaría todos los tesoros de Khazad-dûm a que este pasaje no aparece en ningún mapa salvo en este.'\
\
'Ahora, ¿dónde podemos acceder a este pasaje, Zurr-thurkh, el \\qcamino secreto?\\q Si lo seguimos por aquí... nosotros...'\
\
La sonrisa de Bróin se convierte en una máscara de confusión.\
\
'A menos que esté leyendo mal, ${PLAYER}, parece que Zurr-thurkh conecta con... ¿Buzun-ghâr? ¿Puede ser esto realmente?'","Encuentra el taller de Melkólf Tallapiedra y búscalo en busca de menciones de Zurr-thurkh","El pasaje al taller de Melkólf Tallapiedra se encuentra en la ladera de Zirakzigil; toma la salida oeste de la Senda Pacífica, y luego gira al oeste y sube una corta pendiente hasta la entrada.\
\
Bróin te ha pedido que encuentres el taller de Melkólf Tallapiedra y lo busques en busca de cualquier mención de Zurr-thurkh, el camino secreto hacia la sala del trono de Durin que podría haberse construido hace mucho tiempo. Ha decidido no acompañarte al taller.","'El pasaje al taller de Melkólf Tallapiedra se encuentra en la ladera de Zirakzigil. Toma la salida oeste de la Senda Pacífica. Una vez fuera, gira al oeste y sube una corta pendiente hasta la entrada de la cueva. Debes entrar y buscar cualquier mención de Zurr-thurkh.\
\
Me quedaré atrás en esta ocasión. ¡Te acompañaré en la próxima aventura, lo prometo! Hay mucho por hacer aquí, como seguro comprendes.'","Bróin cree que has descubierto la mención de un pasaje secreto hacia Rushdurinul, donde Mazog ha establecido su trono, y podría usarlo para rescatar a su primo Bori.","'Melkólf Tallapiedra fue famoso por gran parte de su trabajo, aunque nunca he oído hablar de este \\qcamino secreto.\\q Su inclusión en estos registros puede haber sido un descuido de un escriba de la época de Durin, ¡pero puede que nos haya dado lo que necesitamos para liberar a mi primo de las garras de las fuerzas de Mazog!\
\
Mazog se ha atrincherado en la gran fortaleza de Zabadgathol, rodeado de guerreros orcos. Pero si se construyó un pasaje secreto de escape en la pared trasera de Rushdurinul, ¡podríamos colarnos en la fortaleza sin ser vistos!\
\
El taller de Melkólf Tallapiedra fue descubierto recientemente, pero no quedaron enanos para custodiarlo; ¿quién podría haber sospechado lo importante que sería? Toma la salida oeste de la Senda Pacífica, y una vez que salgas a la ladera de la montaña, gira al oeste y sube la corta pendiente hasta la boca de la cueva. Entra en el pasaje y busca información sobre el camino secreto hacia Rushdurinul.'\
\
Bróin palidece ante tu petición de que te acompañe allí.\
\
'Oh, no -- necesito quedarme aquí. Hay mucho por hacer aquí. Te acompañaré en la próxima aventura, ¡lo prometo! Deberías viajar al taller solo, para mantener el secreto.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse en grupo.</rgb>","Bróin está en la Senda Pacífica, ubicada en la Sala de Reunión Militar, al este de Sulnul-dûm y al oeste de la Sala de Piedra, a lo largo del Camino de Durin.\
\
Has recuperado unos planos del taller de Melkólf Tallapiedra que revelan un camino secreto hacia Rushdurinul, la sala del trono de Durin, que ahora está ocupada por Mazog y sus orcos."},
[3281]={"'Cuando dé la orden, Stilling y Wíli se dirigirán a la encrucijada vigilada en el Camino Oriental. Dos horas después, atacarán el puesto avanzado e intentarán convencer a los defensores de que su fuerza es de un tamaño mucho mayor.\
\
'Mientras tanto, tú y yo nos acercaremos sigilosamente a Stazgnâkh. Si estoy en lo cierto, la fuerza principal de Orcos de la Mano Blanca saldrá del campamento para defender la encrucijada vigilada en el Camino Oriental. Luego entraremos al campamento y encontraremos al líder de los Orcos de la Mano Blanca en Moria. Una vez que esté muerto, estarán sin líder y desorganizados, ¡y serán una amenaza menor para nosotros!\
\
'Habla conmigo cuando estés ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]}, ${PLAYER}. ¡Si tan solo Bróin pudiera ver nuestro momento de triunfo!'","'Mi sobrino no tiene por qué preocuparse: Ashpar estaba obviamente haciendo amenazas vacías en un intento de salvar su propia vida; estoy orgulloso de Bori por no ceder a la coerción del Orco.'","'Somos victoriosos, y mi corazón se llena de orgullo. La Mano Blanca está ahora sin líder y en el mayor desorden, ¡tal como esperaba!\
\
'Además, Stilling y Wíli regresaron ilesos de su peligrosa misión. ¡Estos Orcos han subestimado la ingeniosidad de los enanos!\
\
'Aún así, me pregunto qué quiso decir Ashpar cuando habló del \\qverdadero poder en Moria\\q. Tal vez mi tío tenga algunas sugerencias que darnos al respecto...'","Capítulo 7: La Mano Blanca en la oscuridad","Ha llegado el momento para que Bori ponga en marcha su audaz plan para expulsar a la Mano Blanca de Moria.","Habla con Bori y pon en marcha su audaz plan para combatir a la Mano Blanca","'¿Estás ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]}, ${PLAYER}? Partiremos para Stazgnâkh, y le daré la orden a Stilling y Wíli de que se dirijan al puesto avanzado vigilado en la carretera este.\
\
'¡Vamos a expulsar a la Mano Blanca de Moria, ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}; ya verás!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario, y no se puede completar con una comunidad.</rgb>","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
El plan de Bori ha sido un éxito, y ahora deberías hablar con él al respecto.","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bori te espera para dar la orden, y luego pondrá su plan en marcha.","'Habla con mi tío Brogur sobre las últimas palabras de Ashpar. Hoy hemos obtenido una gran victoria, pero todavía me preocupa un poco la fanfarronería de Ashpar.'","Brogur se encuentra con Bori en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bori está preocupado por las últimas palabras de Ashpar, y quiere que le preguntes a Brogur por consejo."},
[3282]={"Has ayudado a Bróin con su tarea","Brogur está preocupado por el comportamiento inusualmente agresivo de los lobos de la región y quiere que se ocupen de ellos.","Capítulo 7: Voces de lobos en el viento","Encuentra la causa de la locura de los lobos","Bosi se encuentra al sur de donde viste a Brogur, a la vista de las escaleras que suben al lago que se extiende frente a la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Has aprendido algo sobre la locura de los huargos de las sombras ayudando a Bróin con su tarea, y ahora debes ir a ver a Bosi.","'Mi hijo Bróin probablemente esté perdiendo el tiempo cerca de las escaleras, perdiendo el tiempo en interminables charlas. La fuente de la locura de los lobos de las sombras probablemente se encuentre al sur de aquí, al otro lado del lecho seco del Sirannon. Tal vez encuentres alguna pista en la cueva de Filgogân, en el suroeste de esta región'","Ayuda a Bróin con la tarea que le dio Brogur","'¿Dices que encontraste el cuerpo quemado de un lobo al otro lado del Sirannon? No tengo la respuesta a este misterio, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Mientras ayudabas a mi primo, las nuevas picas se terminaron. Son de muy alta calidad y seguramente serán de gran ayuda en la Puerta de Acebeda.'","El cuerpo de este lobo está quemado, su pelaje carbonizado.","'Alguna locura se ha apoderado de los lobos de la región, lo que los ha llevado a una furia ciega. Son mucho más agresivos de lo habitual y temo que puedan atacar nuestra expedición pronto.\
\
¿Puedes escuchar sus estremecedores aullidos en el viento? Envié a mi hijo Bróin a desafiar a estas bestias de las Sombras, pero no ha regresado. Probablemente esté perdiendo el tiempo con el hijo de mi primo, charlando cerca de las escaleras que están por allá.\
\
Regresa al lecho seco del Sirannon y sube por la orilla opuesta de donde proviene el terrible clamor. Hay una cueva, Filgogân, en el extremo suroeste de la región. Podría ser que encuentres alguna explicación para la ira de estas criaturas dentro de esa cueva. ¡Temo que debas ayudar a mi hijo con su tarea, porque aún no me ha hablado sobre su exitosa finalización! Habla con mi primo Bosi cuando hayas terminado.'","La causa del comportamiento temible de los lobos puede encontrarse entre sus guaridas, al sur de donde viste a Brogur y al otro lado del lecho seco del Sirannon. Brogur cree que la cueva de Filgogân podría contener alguna pista sobre la locura de los lobos, en el extremo suroeste de la región. Bróin se puede ver hablando con Bori en la base de las escaleras que suben al lago frente a la Puerta de Acebeda.\
\
Brogur te ha pedido que busques la causa de la creciente locura de los huargos de las sombras, y que ayudes a su hijo Bróin con una tarea. Cuando hayas hecho cada una de estas cosas, te dijo que hablaras con su primo Bosi."},
[3283]={"You should talk to Pippin in Bâr Thorenion, and learn what sort of 'formal invitation' he and Merry are talking about.","'You're too early, ${PLAYER}! You did get our formal invitation, didn't you? No? Well, you're here all the same and that is always a good thing.'","'You have helped us out a great deal, ${PLAYER}, and we shall never forget it. I know you are going off to help others now, but I have a curious feeling we will see each other again -- here, or elsewhere, perhaps back in the Shire when the time comes! Until then, good speed and glad tidings.'","'Look, Pippin. ${PLAYER} has come early!'","'We wanted to have everyone here. You know, Aragorn, Gandalf, Gimli - the Fellowship and everyone else who has really mattered on this whole adventure. And that certainly includes you, ${PLAYER}. Since you are here early, why don't you stay around and help out?\
\
'Well, there is no real work to be done. All these helpful Gondorian Men see to that. But you can keep me and Merry in good company until the others arrive.'","The Ranger seems somewhat perplexed.\
\
'I have a -- well, I suppose it is some manner of formal invitation for you, ${PLAYER}. You are requested to join Masters Meriadoc and Peregrin and select other personages -- that is what they said -- at Bâr Thorenion. I think you should go.'","Chapter 7: World Behind and Home Ahead","Habla con Merry","The hobbits have issued you a 'formal invitation' to Bâr Thorenion.","You should talk to Pippin and Merry in  Bâr Thorenion.","'Oh, how I am stuffed! It rarely happens, but I must confess I have somewhat over-eaten. No matter! I shall sleep it off and rise to a new day, tomorrow.\
\
'I realize that you have adventures yet before you, ${PLAYER}, and that what Frodo said about turning our gaze homeward was meant for us and not for you. Still, I wanted you to know how much we have benefitted your company, not to mention your bravery, these days. I hope we shall still see you again from time to time. Farewell, friend!'","Habla con Pippin"},
[3285]={"'These foes will not escape us. We will pursue them into their very stronghold, and no hiding-place will remain unsearched. I will thrust my sword into every closet and cabinet within which one of these villains might hide!'","'Azagath has not escaped my Justice... he has only delayed it. Even as the water builds in power behind the dam that blocks the river, so will the strength of my vengeance increase for every day he remains unpunished. He will regret his flight.\
\
'But what evils might he find buried beneath the Mâkhda Khorbo?'","Talk to Nauriel and help her pursue the fleeing members of the Kindred","Nauriel stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower, preparing to pursue the escaping members of the Kindred deeper into the Citadel of Winds.","'The people of the city believe the Mâkhda Khorbo was destroyed in the great earthquake that accompanied Sauron's fall, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'But you know, as I do, that such destruction is not always complete. Sometimes... something remains.'","'The boy Thorongil has been saved, but I still see a loose thread in the tapestry of evil that brought him, and all of us, to Umbar! One look at his mother's face reveals it, ${PLAYER}. No sum of gold or silver could make me dare to cross her, but the Kindred of the Coins has done so, and she has not forgotten!\
\
'What does Lady Nauriel plan to do next?'","Nauriel stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower.","'But what evils might he find buried beneath the Mâkhda Khorbo?'","'What does Lady Nauriel plan to do next?'","Thorongil has been rescued, but questions remain about the members of the Kindred of the Coin who fled from the Five Sisters.","Sigileth stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower.","Talk to Sigileth outside the Harbour-warden's Tower","'Half of the job is done, my friend, but the other half remains, and its name is Justice.\
\
'Three members of the Kindred of the Coins fled deeper into the Citadel of Winds when my son was rescued. They will not escape us. We must return to the Citadel and pursue them. Azagath, Belondor, and Nakási will pay for endangering my son.\
\
'Speak to me when you are ready to return to that place.'","Sigileth hums a tuneless melody, attracting your notice","Talk to Nauriel outside the Harbour-warden's Tower","Chapter 8.1: Azagath Pursued"},
[3286]={"Gandalf is at his chambers on the upper level of the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","'These Zhélruka are getting impatient, and I fear what might happen if they seek to force their way across the Dale-lands. If it comes to violence...\
\
'I will remain here with Authi, ${PLAYER}, and we will do our best to calm them. You hurry on to the Lonely Mountain and tell my father that Bótuz Frostblood and his band grow tired of waiting. Perhaps the king had a good reason for keeping the Zhélruka messenger from returning?\
\
'Go, ${PLAYER}, and with haste! I fear the Zhélruka will not wait much longer, and the situation here will get worse if it is not resolved quickly.'","Talk to Durin among the large Zhélruka force","'This book cannot remain in Járnfast! I will not allow it! It must be taken from the Iron Hills! It remained hidden near my people for too long, and now that I know of its presence I will no longer tolerate it! Take it to your Wizard friend, ${PLAYER}. Take it to Gandalf, and let him decide what to do about the evil thing!'","'These dwarves are liars, ${PLAYER}. I have seen no messenger, and even if I had I would not listen to any request of his! I am not convinced the Zhélruka have a claim to land in the Grey Mountains, and at any rate I have no obligation to allow them to pass by the foot of the Lonely Mountain. Let them go around, if they must, and take the long road that passes well north of here. They shall not pass through my lands and trouble the folk of Dale.\
\
'I will dispatch some warriors to reinforce my son, and they will ensure the Zhélruka stay put. ${PLAYER}, go find Gandalf at his chambers in the Dwelling-halls. Perhaps the threat of Wizard-magic will encourage these Zhélruka to remain peaceable!'","'Did you see? The Jangovar surrounding Utterby remain in disarray, like as not a result of our efforts there.\
\
'But that is not what has drawn my attention, ${PLAYER}. A large party has taken this road westward; I spy dust on the horizon, kicked up from the road as they passed. Could it be the Easterlings attempt another attack on the Lonely Mountain? Let us follow them and ensure they do not!'","'For this chamber to remain undiscovered for so long fills me with amazement, ${PLAYER}, but I do not fear the room or its contents. The black-bound book has some connexion to Sauron? What is that to me? Sauron is defeated and can trouble us no more. Any dread I would feel at the mention of his name or his works has gone and cannot stir my heart to worry.\
\
'Long did I nurse the resentment of being left behind while my uncle fought in the war, but now we are to return to the Lonely Mountain and I find a spring in my step that was not there before. I aim to prove myself to my people and to the world, and the memory of Sauron cannot diminish my eagerness!\
\
'Let us set forth, ${PLAYER}. Let us go to Utterby and admire our handiwork there before we continue on to the Lonely Mountain and King Thorin. You can deliver the black book to Gandalf while I speak with my father.'","Pick up the Black Book of Mordor from the table where it lies","'What is this you bring to me, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
Gandalf takes the black book, warily eyeing the sigil on the cover. You describe the hidden chamber in which the book was found, and the Wizard strokes his beard thoughtfully. He carefully opens the book and turns several of its leaves.\
\
'Some of these pages contain words written in the Black Speech, but there are also dwarf-runes of several varieties, and many blank pages. I suspect these gaps are not truly empty, but contain words written in the hidden fashion used by dwarves to keep secrets. Most interesting! This book clearly has its origin in Mordor, but the Mordor of a thousand years ago is not the same as it is today. Truly, even in a month's time Mordor has greatly changed!\
\
'I will study this book with interest, but I see from your expression that more than one purpose has drawn you hither.'","The party Durin witnessed from afar reveals itself to be a large band of Zhélruka","Talk to Khîl in the hidden chamber","'A large party has taken this road westward; I spy dust on the horizon, kicked up from the road as they passed. Could it be the Easterlings attempt another attack on the Lonely Mountain? Let us follow them and ensure they do not!'","Meet up with Durin on the road west of Utterby, in the Ironfold","Talk to Durin in the hidden chamber","'I will remain here with Authi, ${PLAYER}, and we will do our best to calm them. You hurry on to the Lonely Mountain and tell my father that Bótuz Frostblood and his band grow tired of waiting. Perhaps the king had a good reason for keeping the Zhélruka messenger from returning?\
\
'Go, ${PLAYER}, and with haste! I fear the Zhélruka will not wait much longer, and the situation here will get worse if it is not resolved quickly.'","King Thorin looks at you curiously as you approach without the son he sent you to retrieve","'Where is Durin? Did I not send you to bring my son back from Járnfast? How can it be you have not fulfilled this request, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'What? He came with you as far as the edge of the Dale-lands, but has stopped to treat with a band of Zhélruka? I have heard nothing of this, ${PLAYER}! Explain this business!'\
\
You quickly describe your encounter with Bótuz Frostblood and the Zhélruka he leads, and recount Durin's decision to remain behind to keep the situation from worsening.\
\
'These dwarves are liars, ${PLAYER}. I have seen no messenger, and even if I had I would not listen to any request of his! I am not convinced the Zhélruka have a claim to land in the Grey Mountains, and at any rate I have no obligation to allow them to pass by the foot of the Lonely Mountain. Let them go around, if they must, and take the long road that passes well north of here. They shall not pass through my lands and trouble the folk of Dale.\
\
'I will dispatch some warriors to reinforce my son, and they will ensure the Zhélruka stay put. ${PLAYER}, go find Gandalf at his chambers in the Dwelling-halls. Perhaps the threat of Wizard-magic will encourage these Zhélruka to remain peaceable!'","'What brings this Zhélruka force here? Who leads this band, and for what purpose?'","Durin stands among the group of Zhélruka that intends to cross the Dale-lands.","Khîl Tale-spinner is in the hidden chamber in his father's house where you discovered the Black Book of Mordor.","Durin has spied a large party heading west on the road to the Lonely Mountain, and he wants to investigate.","'I do not like the tone of this Zhélruka! He should show more respect to King Thorin and to the Longbeards!'","'Do you think my father knew of this room? He cannot have! Certainly my mother Zéma would not have permitted such an artifact as that tome of Mordor to remain within her walls, so near to her child! It is preposterous, ${PLAYER}. And what of these runes? I have not studied the language of my people in many years, and the words are quite difficult for me to read. I think this one might speak of Thafar-gathol, the lost Grey Citadel sought by both Zhélruka and Longbeard alike, but I cannot say for certain. That is not an evil place, though it be shrouded in mystery. The book, however, I cannot explain. What would Vóin have to do with artifacts of Mordor?\
\
'I like it no more than Lord Náin, ${PLAYER}. Pick up the book and carry it to Gandalf with my approval. Present it to him for study, and if he determines that it poses no danger, I ask that you return it to me. Unpleasant as it seems, this tome is an artifact of my house and I would not have it lost, unless the Wizard confirms that it be wholly evil. Even so, I would want to have some form of compensation in that case. The book is more than a thousand years old and of great historical interest for my people and for me personally.'","Talk to Gandalf at his chambers in the Dwelling-halls and give him the Black Book of Mordor","Durin wanted to meet up on the road west of Utterby to admire his handiwork.","The black leather binding feels cool to the touch","Durin is in the hidden chamber in Khîl's family home in Járnfast.","Catch up to the large party heading west","'My people have the right to cross to our lands in the Grey Mountains, no matter what King Thorin says about it! I sent my messenger to be polite, but now I begin to think the king did not deserve even that measure of courtesy!'","Chapter 8.1: The Black Book of Mordor","The Black Book of Mordor is on the table in the hidden chamber in Khîl's family home in Járnfast.","Talk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain","'Lord Náin may not believe me, but you must, ${PLAYER}! Don't you? I swear to you I had no knowledge of either chamber or tome! My thrice-great grandfather Vóin lived more than a thousand years ago, and of his line I knew only my father Bránit; each of the others were names only, names in a family tree I did not see the need to study!\
\
'Do you think my father knew of this room? He cannot have! Certainly my mother Zéma would not have permitted such an artifact as that tome of Mordor to remain within her walls, so near to her child! It is preposterous, ${PLAYER}. And what of these runes? I have not studied the language of my people in many years, and the words are quite difficult for me to read. I think they might speak of Thafar-gathol, the lost Grey Citadel sought by both Zhélruka and Longbeard alike, but I cannot say for certain. That is not an evil place, though it be shrouded in mystery. The book, however, I cannot explain. What would Vóin have to do with artifacts of Mordor?\
\
'I like it no more than Lord Náin, ${PLAYER}. Pick up the book and carry it to Gandalf with my approval. Present it to him for study, and if he determines that it poses no danger, I ask that you return it to me. Unpleasant as it seems, this tome is an artifact of my house and I would not have it lost, unless the Wizard confirms that it be wholly evil. Even so, I would want to have some form of compensation in that case. The book is more than a thousand years old and of great historical interest for my people and for me personally.'","Talk to Bótuz Frostblood among the large Zhélruka force","Within the rune-covered walls of the secret chamber in the home of Khîl Tale-spinner you found a black-bound book written by his thrice-great grandfather Vóin and hidden long ago.","'Long did I nurse the resentment of being left behind while my uncle fought in the war, but now we are to return to the Lonely Mountain and I find a spring in my step that was not there before. I aim to prove myself to my people and to the world, and the memory of Sauron cannot diminish my eagerness!\
\
'Let us set forth, ${PLAYER}. Let us go to Utterby and admire our handiwork there before we continue on to the Lonely Mountain and King Thorin. You can deliver the black book to Gandalf while I speak with my father.'","'Why are these Zhélruka here?'","Hurry to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain","Bótuz Frostblood leads a group of Zhélruka toward the Dale-lands.","King Thorin III is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.","'You are with these Longbeards, ${RACE}? I am Bótuz Frostblood, leader of this Zhélruka band. I hope you have answers for me, for my patience is nearly spent. It has been days since my axe has drawn blood, and she is thirsty! Tell me what transpires in Erebor, and tell me quickly!\
\
'You came from the east and not the west? Bah! We have been waiting here for our messenger to return, a dwarf of good speed and loyal temperament, but he is hours overdue. He was to speak with the King Under the Mountain and obtain permission for us to cross the Dale-lands on our way to the Grey Mountains. Why has he not returned? Why has he not sent word? I smell treachery, ${RACE}! Has King Thorin imprisoned him? This insult cannot stand!\
\
'We will wait for a little while longer, but my Zhélruka will not wait long! We sent word to the king as a matter of courtesy, but I begin to question whether such courtesy was deserved! No one, not even a king, can get away with insulting Bótuz Frostblood! Perhaps I and my Zhélruka will force our way through the Dale-lands to our promised lands among the Grey Mountains, and spit upon Thorin's permission!'","'My people have had a friendly relationship with the Zhélruka for thousands of years, ${PLAYER}. When our halls were cracked and damaged in the devastation that followed the fall of Thangorodrim, it is recorded that the Zhélruka stayed for a time in the Iron Hills and participated in the Great Mending. Most of that people went on to Gundabad, though they never arrived and their fate is shrouded in mystery. Over the centuries since, small families of Zhélruka came to live in the Ironfold and here in Járnfast, and rarely caused trouble.\
\
'But look at this chamber, ${PLAYER}! What evils might have been worked within its walls? What foul sorcery was recorded within that book? The sigil on its cover is known to me, indeed it is known to all of Durin's Folk: the Eye of Sauron, feared and despised! Did Khîl's forebears worship Sauron at the height of his powers? Do the Zhélruka worship him still, even following his defeat? Were you privy to this knowledge, Khîl? What have you to say for yourself, villain?\
\
'This book cannot remain in Járnfast! I will not allow it! It must be taken from the Iron Hills! It remained hidden near my people for too long, and now that I know of its presence I will no longer tolerate it! Take it to your Wizard friend, ${PLAYER}. Take it to Gandalf, and let him decide what to do about the evil thing!'","Durin wears a thoughtful expression as he gazes off to the west"},
[3287]={"He scowls and accepts the salve. 'I suppose I need this,' he grumbles","'Take these salves and bandages and bring them to any dwarves who need them. So many dead, so many wounded... I hope this will be enough, but I fear it will not be.'","Durin nods solemnly","Slagvi thanks you for the bandage, wincing at the pain in his leg","Prince Ingór refuses the bandage.\
\
'I need it not,' he insists.","Treat as many wounded dwarves at Maergrind as you can","'Aye, Slagvi. Do this in memory of Stóthkell, and honour him. I will send Bósi to assist the two of you later.\
\
'The Angmarim cannot be allowed to despoil the ground where my ancestor Durin first awoke. Keep them from staining Gloomingtarn with their steps or their foul magic, ${PLAYER}.'","Stóthkell has no further need of your help. The forge-master is dead","Talk to Slagvi at Maergrind","Búkk is at Maergrind.\
\
You have treated the dwarves you could, and should now return the remaining supplies to Búkk.","Bósi refuses the bandage. 'I am merely winded,' he says","Búkk is at Maergrind.\
\
Durin asked you to collect salves and bandages from Búkk with which to heal the hurts of those dwarves who are not already beyond help.","Chapter 8.2: Broken Bones, Broken Hearts","'Where is Búkk? We have need of your salves and poultices, your slings and bandages! ${PLAYER}, find Búkk! Fire and flames, pox and bother! Where is Búkk?'","It is too late for any of your supplies to help him. He is dead","'Thank you, my prince.\
\
'${PLAYER}! The reason I must ask to accompany you brings me no joy, but I am grateful that you and the prince allow it. It should be Forge-master Stóthkell who safe-guards the Gloomingtarn, but he cannot, and I must do it in his stead.'","Slagvi is at Maergrind.","He smiles weakly and gratefully accepts the bandage","Durin is at Maergrind.","Slagvi limps over and begs the prince's pardon","'Vengeance will have to wait, though it pains me to say so! We must do something about our dead and wounded.\
\
'Where is Búkk? We have need of your salves and poultices, your slings and bandages! ${PLAYER}, find Búkk! Fire and flames, pox and bother! Where is Búkk?'","Durin is at Maergrind, furious at Gorgar's attack and grieving for the slain.","'Yes, Slagvi, what is it?'","Gorgar's attack has left many dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ dead or wounded. If the conquest of Gundabad is to be successful, Prince Durin and those loyal to him must recover from this defeat, and resist despair.","Talk to Búkk at Maergrind","This Zhélruka warrior is beyond help. He is dead","'Thank you for your quick action, friend. This haste may yet save some of our wounded from succumbing to their injuries and joining the list of the slain.'","Longbeards and Zhélruka were wounded during Gorgar's attack, and many of them require treatment for their wounds.","'My prince, I hope you will forgive this interruption and grant me this boon: may I accompany ${PLAYER} on this task? I mourn for Stóthkell who perished at Gorgar's hands, and I wish to see to the safety of Gloomingtarn and the Wakening Stone that lies within. It is what the forge-master would want, and I desire to do right by his memory.'","'Will you grant me this boon, my prince?'","Talk to Durin at Maergrind","'I am here, I am here!\
\
'Gorgar will not escape retribution for this attack, but I fear we have sustained such losses that we may lack the fighters to hold the son of Bolg responsible! No, that cannot be. It must not be!\
\
'Take these salves and bandages and bring them to any dwarves who need them. So many dead, so many wounded... I hope this will be enough, but I fear it will not be.'","Return the remaining supplies to Búkk at Maergrind","'Thank you for your quick action, friend. This haste may yet save some of our wounded from succumbing to their injuries and joining the list of the slain.\
\
'Líkmund... Stóthkell... Thettmárr... too many dead at Gorgar's command.'","Búkk hands you a bundle of salves and bandages","He accepts the bandage with a grateful smile","'Stand strong against Orc and cultist alike, and avenge Forge-master Stóthkell.'","Glóin thanks you for the bandage","'I am still angry, ${PLAYER}, do not mistake me! But my rage, once white-hot, has cooled to a slow-burning ember. I will not allow it to push me into recklessness. Gorgar will pay for this, if not today then on the morrow. But you have a report for me from the vale of Câr Bronach? Tell me what you learned there; I will not let Gorgar's attack divert or delay our plans, and I would know what you discovered.'\
\
You tell Durin that Angmarim cultists intend to use an artifact they rescued from Barad Gúlaran during the fall of Angmar Reborn to break the wards on Gloomingtarn.\
\
'That cannot be allowed! That place is sacred, and must be protected from the cultists and Gorgar both! If you are willing, I ask you to go with Bósi of the Iron Garrison and put an end to that Angmarim mission.'"},
[3288]={"Collected gemstones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Mâkhda Khorbo is to the north-west of the city.'","Corudan has asked you to speak with a distant onlooker down the hill to the east.","Talk to Corudan by his sister east of the Mâkhda Khorbo","Collected rusty weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sigileth is beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.","Corudan stands by the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.","'An Umbari woman has been watching us from down the hill to the east. Perhaps you should find out what she wants?'","Collect gemstones from spectres or darkwaters near the Mâkhda Khorbo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Corudan catches your eye","Sigileth stands by the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.","'An Umbari woman has been watching us from down the hill to the east, ${PLAYER}. I do not think she intends to do us any harm, but whenever I face in her direction she quickly busies herself with some unobtrusive task.\
\
'Perhaps you should see if she has any information for us, or at least determine that she does not mean ill?'","Sigileth is waiting for you to return to her east of the Mâkhda Khorbo with the strange objects for which she asked.","Collect finger-bones from wights near the Mâkhda Khorbo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the strange items she requested to Sigileth east of the Mâkhda Khorbo","Talk to Corudan beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo","Collected finger-bones from wights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We should travel by land to the outskirts of the temple and learn if the fleeing members of the Kindred have disturbed the ruin. It may be they seek only escape... but if evils of Sauron do remain beneath that structure, we cannot risk Azagath coming into possession of them.\
\
'My brother and I will accompany you, ${PLAYER}. He would not say this to you directly, but privately he mourned to me that you ventured into the Citadel to rescue Thorongil without him.\
\
'The Mâkhda Khorbo is to the north-west of the city.'","Talk to Sigileth beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo","Collect rusty weapons from outside the Mâkhda Khorbo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I saw you speaking with those Elves near the ruined temple up on the hill. What purpose brought the three of you to that place? I have seen Elves of the Oasis from time to time, when I have gone to the markets of the city to sell my wares, but your companions do not seem to hail from across the desert. I judge they came from across the bay, perhaps from Gondor?'\
\
You remain silent, and Rukân chuckles to herself.\
\
'Worry not, stranger! I am no follower of the Church of the All-Seeing, and I steer clear from that temple, as should all goodly folk! Not long ago I witnessed Azagath Sea-shadow and some of his people disembark their ship in the cove beneath the hill, and I wondered what madness might have drawn them inside. Nothing good, I imagine. Pestilence and plague have troubled Khûtra in recent days, and something spoils the fish. After you have halted whatever evil drew you and Azagath to the Mâkhda Khorbo, you should return to me and I will tell you more about those ills.\
\
'But for now let your companions know where Azagath and his allies debarked their ship. They possessed an evil intent... I am certain of it.'","Meet up with Sigileth and Corudan beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo","'What is it, Corudan?'","'What said our distant onlooker, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Sigileth that Azagath and his allies made use of a sheltered cove beneath the hill on which rests the Mâkhda Khorbo, and they have now gone inside the lower tunnels for some unknown purpose.\
\
'Then that is where your road leads, is it not? Corudan and I will guard the path and ensure none think to flee this way, while you muster your allies and face Azagath beneath the temple.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>If you wish to participate in the raid, this is when 'The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo' raid takes place during the story.</rgb>","'When the Golden Host of Lothlórien waged the Battle of the Tower in the forest of Mirkwood, I did not know of its success until many weeks passed... and every week felt as long as an age in the darkness beneath Dol Guldur. It was only when you delved deeply into those forgotten passages that I ceased to be She Who Remains and became once again Sigileth, ${PLAYER}, and learned that the Golden Host had achieved victory.\
\
'But there was evil beneath Dol Guldur, and even today each of my senses are attuned to it. I feel the presence of Sauron's works here at the Mâkhda Khorbo, even as I did in those dark dungeons. It is not as strong here as it was in the Room of Voices, but still my senses are troubled by the feel of it.\
\
'Bring me some relics from the Dead that walk near the temple, for they may allow me to learn the... I do not know the precise word to describe it, but this will have to serve... they may allow me to learn the flavour of the evil that remains here. Bring me rusty weapons from the steps of the temple, gemstones from spectres and spirits, and finger-bones from the wights that lurk nearby. Why finger-bones?'\
\
Sigileth raises one eyebrow and you are surprised to hear mirth in her voice when she responds.\
\
'I did not think you would want to drag a bunch of wights over here for my investigation, ${PLAYER}. Just their finger-bones will do.'","'Azagath must think to acquire some evil beneath the Mâkhda Khorbo. He must be prevented from finding whatever it is he seeks, unless that be death.'","'I have never seen this place before, ${PLAYER}. When Nakási and Tatháta sailed their ships back to Umbar with me and Thorongil aboard, they docked at their hidden harbour south of the city. I had only heard talk of the Mâkhda Khorbo and not seen it until today.\
\
'The structure itself is not as damaged as I had thought it to be. It is not difficult to believe the levels below-ground may also have survived the great quake that followed Sauron's fall, and remain somewhat intact.'","'I had forgotten how poor my sister is at keeping secrets, ${PLAYER}. I did not begrudge you your decision to go alone into the Citadel, no matter what Sigileth says!\
\
'I would have gone with you, had you asked. But of course you know that!'","'Did you recover the items I requested?'\
\
Sigileth examines the strange items you acquired from the vicinity of the Mâkhda Khorbo. After a few moments of study, she looks up at you.\
\
'These blades are rusty from the salt of the sea breeze, and unsuitable for use. Only the Dead would wield these; no living servant of Sauron or of the Kindred would think to use such a weapon, unless there was no other choice.\
\
'The gemstones are interesting. When such stones as these are found within the earth, they are usually quite clear, but the gems around which these spirits and spectres form are cloudy instead. See the shapes that seem to swirl within their foggy depths? They are most peculiar.\
\
'I cannot read very much from the finger-bones you have brought to me. No, I do not need you to drag an entire wight here to me, as I threatened before! I have learned this, and it may be enough: these wights were given motion by spirits of evil. There must be a great number of such creatures still within the Mâkhda Khorbo, though Sauron himself be gone.'","Talk to Rukân down the hill to the east","'My sister's thoughts dwell upon the evils that might lie within the Mâkhda Khorbo, but I need not see them to know that a corruption lies within the very heart of the Kindred of the Coins.\
\
'But Azagath is well-loved by his people. Do the folk of Umbar Baharbêl know that he has betrayed them?'","Sigileth is no stranger to the works of Sauron, and she believes that Azagath should be prevented from delving beneath the Mâkhda Khorbo for anything of that sort that may remain there.","The ruins of the Mâkhda Khorbo stand to the north-west of Umbar Baharbêl. Sigileth and Corudan asked to meet up with you there.","'Bring me some relics from the Dead that walk near the temple, for they may allow me to learn the flavour of the evil that remains here. Bring me rusty weapons from the steps of the temple, gemstones from spectres and spirits, and finger-bones from the wights that lurk nearby.'","Sigileth asked you to retrieve a number of curious objects near the Mâkhda Khorbo so she may examine them.","Corudan is beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.","Chapter 8.2: Something Remains","'For now let your companions know where Azagath and his allies debarked their ship. They possessed an evil intent... I am certain of it.'","'The structure itself is not as damaged as I had thought it to be.'","Sigileth and her brother Corudan greet you as you approach"},
[3289]={"'With the devastation that heralded the end of the First Age, much of Middle-earth was shaken and sundered. In their land far to the east, the stronghold of the Zhélruka was destroyed and they became a wandering people. Their neighbours turned them aside and wished them ill, but King Durin II of Khazad-dûm took pity upon them and bade his folk make a home for the displaced people at Mount Gundabad. They disappeared in the mountains and never arrived, but a single survivor emerged centuries later. He spoke of the vanished Zhélruka and Thafar-gathol, a citadel he claimed they delved in the mountains. He insisted too that its riches could match those of mighty Khazad-dûm. Mad ravings, surely. None of the many to seek it over the years, Longbeard and Zhélruka alike, have ever found it. I do not believe it ever existed.\
\
'Dwarves from Khazad-dûm did uncover the remains of an ancient delving in the Grey Mountains, and although they found a great deal of iron ore they found no mithril; this could not be Thafar-gathol. They called it Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep, and soon their iron production threatened to rival that of the Iron Hills. Scholars whisper that this threat to their prosperity caused the Dwarves of Járnfast to send word of the Steel Keep to the Zhélruka, who demanded it was theirs by right. If the Dwarves of the Iron Hills did take part in this none have proven it, but it seems likely to me. Ever since, the Zhélruka have jealously guarded their claim to holdings in the Grey Mountains, and that resentment has coloured their dealings with all other people. If Bótuz Frostblood and others of the Zhélruka believe their property is being kept from them they will not hesitate to spill blood to regain it.\
\
'I will not involve myself in this matter. Return to King Thorin and warn him not to trifle with the Zhélruka. They will become a dangerous foe if they feel they are being treated unfairly, and the Dwarves of the Lonely Mountain need more friends, not new enemies.'","Durin stands among the wind-swept grasses of the heights","You have found Durin on the road that climbs into the Grey Mountains.","'My father must have sent you to find me.'","King Thorin is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.","Durin has followed the Zhélruka into the Grey Mountains, and at King Thorin's request you should look for him on the road that climbs into Ered Mithrin.","'These Zhélruka have proven themselves to be impolite and no friend to me or to my people. I am insulted, and demand satisfaction! I do not say my son should have stood alone against dozens of these traitors, but I wish the Zhélruka had been made to pay for this slight in some fashion! Had they waited for my warriors to arrive, they would not have dared to cross, or they would have paid a good sum in blood and in pain! They are brazen enough to disregard my commands, but too cowardly to engage in outright battle for it!\
\
'Go to the Grey Mountains and tell my son to return. These Zhélruka will pay for this outrage, but it will not be for Durin to exact the price. He belongs here with me, and will learn the responsibilities of kingship at my feet.'","Return to King Thorin with Gandalf's warning about the Zhélruka","'Authi Gem-cutter has come from the edge of the Dale-lands with urgent news, ${PLAYER}! He says that Bótuz Frostblood and his band of Zhélruka forced their way into the Dale-lands against my wishes and have marched for the Grey Mountains! At first my son Durin barred their way, but he refused to spill dwarf-blood and allowed them to pass! It seems he followed them, intending to watch them and prevent the Zhélruka from doing any harm to the people of Dale or the lands around the Lonely Mountain. He sent Authi back to bring me word of their movements.\
\
'This is an outrage, ${PLAYER}! These Zhélruka have proven themselves to be impolite and no friend to me or to my people. I am insulted, and demand satisfaction! I do not say my son should have stood alone against dozens of these traitors, but I wish the Zhélruka had been made to pay for this slight in some fashion! Had they waited for my warriors to arrive, they would not have dared to cross, or they would have paid a good sum in blood and in pain! They are brazen enough to disregard my commands, but too cowardly to engage in outright battle for it!\
\
'Go to the Grey Mountains and tell my son to return. These Zhélruka will pay for this outrage, but it will not be for Durin to exact the price. He belongs here with me, and will learn the responsibilities of kingship at my feet.'","Talk to Durin on the road that climbs into the Grey Mountains","Find Durin on the road that climbs into the Grey Mountains","'Ah, I see. The relationship of the Zhélruka and the Longbeards has been tumultuous during the years of their interaction, changing from peace to outright war and then to uneasy truce. The passage of the years and the waning of memory finally caused friendship to once again emerge between them... and now this happens to cast that renewal into doubt.\
\
'With the devastation that heralded the end of the First Age, much of Middle-earth was shaken and sundered. In their land far to the east, the stronghold of the Zhélruka was destroyed and they became a wandering people. Their neighbours turned them aside and wished them ill, but King Durin II of Khazad-dûm took pity upon them and bade his folk make a home for the displaced people at Mount Gundabad. They disappeared in the mountains and never arrived, but a single survivor emerged centuries later. He spoke of the vanished Zhélruka and Thafar-gathol, a citadel he claimed they delved in the mountains. He insisted too that its riches could match those of mighty Khazad-dûm. Mad ravings, surely. None of the many to seek it over the years, Longbeard and Zhélruka alike, have ever found it. I do not believe it ever existed.\
\
'Dwarves from Khazad-dûm did uncover the remains of an ancient delving in the Grey Mountains, and although they found a great deal of iron ore they found no mithril; this could not be Thafar-gathol. They called it Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep, and soon their iron production threatened to rival that of the Iron Hills. Scholars whisper that this threat to their prosperity caused the Dwarves of Járnfast to send word of the Steel Keep to the Zhélruka, who demanded it was theirs by right. If the Dwarves of the Iron Hills did take part in this none have proven it, but it seems likely to me. Ever since, the Zhélruka have jealously guarded their claim to holdings in the Grey Mountains, and that resentment has coloured their dealings with all other people. If Bótuz Frostblood and others of the Zhélruka believe their property is being kept from them they will not hesitate to spill blood to regain it.\
\
'I will not involve myself in this matter. Return to King Thorin and warn him not to trifle with the Zhélruka. They will become a dangerous foe if they feel they are being treated unfairly, and the Dwarves of the Lonely Mountain need more friends, not new enemies.'","'This is bad, ${PLAYER}! Durin followed those traitors all by himself, and he might be in danger!'","'This is bad, ${PLAYER}! This is very bad!'","Talk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain","A band of Zhélruka desires to travel to the Grey Mountains, but its presence near the Lonely Mountain has threatened to spark an incident between the Zhélruka and the Longbeards.","'Did my father send you to bring me back to the Lonely Mountain, ${PLAYER}? Bótuz Frostblood and his band of Zhélruka have gone on ahead, but now that I behold this place with my own eyes I see some of what has driven them to come here, against my father's command.'\
\
Durin looks around at the rocky highlands and the towering peaks of the Grey Mountains.\
\
'Do you see it too? The vast mountains, the untouched valleys, the hidden recesses beneath them... each holds the promise of adventure! My father's throne-room is no place for me. I should not waste my years there in study and in idleness, as he did. No, I belong here in the unexplored wilderness! I should seek its lost treasures, just as my people have done for thousands of years! Only then will I find the glory that is to be mine! Uncle Náin would understand, even if my father does not.\
\
'I am not going back until I have proven I am worthy of my name, ${PLAYER}. Remember our deeds in the Ironfold? You were a good companion and a reliable friend to me. I ask you to adventure with me here, and together we will achieve great things!'","Chapter 8.2: The Zhélruka","Authi Gem-cutter stands before the king. What is he doing here?"},
[3290]={"Collected hatchling-wings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We have found them.'","'Now that I look upon the Anvil for myself, I find its beauty impossible to describe, but that beauty is matched by a terrible feeling of watchfulness. Let us not forget the horrors that slept behind its shimmering surface, ${PLAYER}, and take care not to disturb them! Instead let us put the Anvil to our backs and collect a number of trophies from the drakes and worms that stalk among the steaming geysers of the Withered Heath and throughout Ered Mithrin. I have a plan that requires them, but let us also collect them in memory of the dwarves that perished in sight of the Anvil.'","'What a sight! The Anvil is even larger and more magnificent than I imagined it to be!'","'This would be the straight way to Stormwall, but I see that the stairs have collapsed. To reach the old fortress we would need to brave the canyons, and if I remember my maps aright the cliffs and gullies on the approach to the stronghold are certain to be quite confusing. Perhaps we will return here when we are better supplied. Let us leave this canyon and find the Zhélruka; they intended to establish a camp in the old stronghold of Skarháld, south of here and to the west.'","Collect hatchling-wings in Ered Mithrin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Durin stands by the Anvil on the Withered Heath.","'We found the Zhélruka, ${PLAYER}, and it also seems some Longbeards from the Lonely Mountain have made their way to Skarháld! I wonder if they attained permission from my father to come here, or if they too dismissed his command? A small part of me regrets that it was necessary for me to do so, but I believe it truly was. He will understand when I return in glory.\
\
'I will take the various trophies we obtained from the dragon-kind in the vales and present them to the Zhélruka as proof of our intentions here. They will see that their goals are ours, and we should work together if we are all to thrive in this land.\
\
'It is a good plan, is it not? It is.'","'Ah, those teeth and hides will serve my purposes quite well. Thank you, my friend!\
\
'We should depart now, for I find the more I gaze upon the smooth ice of the Anvil the more reluctant I am to leave it behind, as if it carries upon its surface some strange power of bewitchment! Do you feel it too?\
\
'Let us go, ${PLAYER}. If we travel south back through the Wyrmgap and a little ways to the west, we should find another canyon that leads north to Stormwall. I wish to survey the path to Stormwall before we seek the Zhélruka, and while we explore the Vales of Mithrin we should collect some further trophies from the creatures there: drake-hatchling wings and burning scales, if you please.'","Durin stares up at the Anvil, preoccupied with his own thoughts","Defeated enemies in the Wyrmgap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat enemies in the Wyrmgap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Durin has asked you to defeat some of the worms and drakes that stalk the Withered Heath and Ered Mithrin, and collect their teeth and hides.","Collected drake-teeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Durin beckons you to his side, signaling for quiet","Travel with Durin to the canyons south of Stormwall","Collect worm-hides throughout Ered Mithrin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We should exercise caution, for I sense the presence of dragon-kind very near to us. They may have roosted within Stormwall and increased in number. I am still waiting for hatchling-wings and burning scales, but these canyons seem to have more than enough of each for our purposes.'","Talk to Durin in the canyons south of Stormwall","'If we travel south back through the Wyrmgap and a little ways to the west, we should find another canyon that leads north to Stormwall. I wish to survey the path to Stormwall before we seek the Zhélruka, and while we explore the Vales of Mithrin we should collect some further trophies from the creatures there: drake-hatchling wings and burning scales, if you please.'","'Behold the Anvil of Winterstith, ${PLAYER}! How many dwarves have looked upon its smooth surface and questioned the reflections that gazed back, asking of themselves what their futures were to be? Did they believe the answers in their hearts? Longbeards have come here in search of treasure or knowledge, and it is said that more than one Zhélruka king perished on the Heath while seeking the Citadel. Dóbruz? Ilkún? I cannot remember their names. My teachers would be shamed and disappointed!\
\
'But whatever their names may have been, I do remember their fates. How could a young dwarf forget their stories? For one of these kings sought the remains of his lost forebear and the way to Thafar-gathol, and while digging beneath the Anvil his dwarves accidentally caused a great collapse. The glacier was split in twain, and hundreds of cold-drakes awoke within and boiled from the crack in the ice. The few Zhélruka that survived the initial attack fled back to the Steel Keep, but the rest of the dwarves were slain. My teachers say it was dwarf-made fire that eventually melted the ice, sealing most of the cold-drakes within again, but I heard from somewhere that it was one or another of the Wizards that closed the crack and mended the Anvil. I wonder which is the truth?\
\
'Now that I look upon the Anvil for myself, I find its beauty impossible to describe, but that beauty is matched by a terrible feeling of watchfulness. Let us not forget the horrors that slept behind its shimmering surface, ${PLAYER}, and take care not to disturb them! Instead let us put the Anvil to our backs and collect a number of trophies from the drakes and worms that stalk among the steaming geysers of the Withered Heath and elsewhere throughout Ered Mithrin. I have a plan that requires them, but let us also collect them in memory of the dwarves that perished in sight of the Anvil.'","Collected worm-hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The old fortress of Skarháld is south and west of the path to Stormwall. Durin is at the eastern entrance of the city, waiting to speak with you.","Durin is in the canyons south of Stormwall.","'The fortress of Stormwall has been abandoned for an age, but at its height it was known for its riches. The dwarves who dwelt here made fine work in gold and silver, but it was that very reputation that brought about their downfall; rumour of their treasure drew the attention of dragons, and the dwarves were driven out.\
\
'This would be the straight way to Stormwall, but I see that the stairs have collapsed. To reach the old fortress we would need to brave the canyons, and if I remember my maps aright the cliffs and gullies on the approach to the stronghold are certain to be quite confusing. Perhaps we will return here when we are better supplied. Let us leave this canyon and find the Zhélruka; they intended to establish a camp in the old stronghold of Skarháld, south of here and to the west.'","Collect burning scales in Ered Mithrin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'There should be a narrow passage to the north-west of here, the Wyrmgap, bored through the very stone by the dragon-kind that came down from the north. Let us see if any of their kin still inhabit the gap, and bring battle to them if they do! I would like to pass through the Wyrmgap to the Withered Heath beyond and see the great Anvil for myself. Many tales tell of the Anvil, and dreams of it have fired my imagination since I was small!'","Collect drake-teeth on the Withered Heath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Zhélruka stare suspiciously at you and Durin as the two of you approach","Durin asked you to defeat enemies in the Wyrmgap on your way to the Anvil on the Withered Heath.","Now that Durin has seen the Grey Mountains for himself, he has decided he wants to adventure among them for glory and for treasure, rather than remaining at the Lonely Mountain with his father.","Talk to Durin by the Anvil on the Withered Heath","Talk to Durin at the eastern entrance of Skarháld","Durin asked you to defeat enemies in the Vales of Mithrin.","'There will be adventures enough for both of us, ${PLAYER}, I am certain of that! I will not look back fondly upon the time I spent in Járnfast, kept from honour and glory, but something at least came from the captivity of my youth. Many were the tales I heard, and many were the maps I studied, and now that we are here among the Grey Mountains I will see these subjects with my own eyes, and thereby make them real!\
\
'There should be a narrow passage to the north-west of here, the Wyrmgap, bored through the very stone by the dragon-kind that came down from the north. Let us see if any of their kin still inhabit the gap, and bring battle to them if they do! I would like to pass through the Wyrmgap to the Withered Heath beyond and see the great Anvil for myself. Many tales tell of the Anvil, and dreams of it have fired my imagination since I was small!'","The old fortress of Skarháld is south and west of the path to Stormwall.","Collected burning scales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Travel to the old fortress of Skarháld, where the Zhélruka planned to encamp","Chapter 8.3: An Inhospitable Land","Travel with Durin to the Anvil on the Withered Heath"},
[3291]={"Slagvi wants to honour the memory of Stóthkell by protecting the sacred lake of Gloomingtarn from the Angmarim, and has volunteered to accompany you there.","Examine the White Stone Forge on the island in the lake","'It is as I feared: they have somehow modified the runes, sapping them of their power. They are now only ordinary stones, and Gloomingtarn lies open to the cultists, that they may walk where they will, and spoil what they wish.\
\
'We must follow them inside, and teach them they are not welcome! Let us enact the vengeance of Stóthkell, and of all the dwarves who revere this place, upon the intruders!'","Talk to Slagvi on the Stone of Wakening","Cross to the island and find the White Stone Forge and the Black Stone Anvil","Slagvi stands beside the rune-stone wards at the entrance to Gloomingtarn.","'We will find the entrance to Gloomingtarn beyond the Orc-infested cavern of Deepscrave, to the west. Let us journey there and see if the warding-runes have kept the cultists from gaining entrance to that sacred site.'","The rune's power has been drained by specific lines, carefully etched","Slagvi stands at the entrance to Gloomingtarn, beside the broken wards.","Defeated Angmarim cultists within Gloomingtarn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Slagvi beside the lake in Gloomingtarn","Slagvi stands beside you in silence as you contemplate the distant rocks","Slagvi has come to the Stone of Wakening, and he is not happy.","Talk to Slagvi by the lakeshore","Slagvi grimly observes the rune-stone wards at the entrance to Gloomingtarn","Defeat Angmarim cultists within Gloomingtarn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Let us cross to the Wakening Stone and see the black anvil and the white forge on his behalf.'","Talk to Slagvi at the entrance to Gloomingtarn","Meet up with Slagvi at the entrance to Gloomingtarn from Deepscrave","'I cannot believe this! The White Stone Forge is here, as it should be, but the Black Stone Anvil has been taken away by unknown villains! This is a grievous insult!\
\
'Stóthkell would die of a broken heart had he lived to see it!'","'I fear we may be too late.'","The Wakening Stone stands in the middle of the lake in Gloomingtarn.","The White Stone Forge gleams even in the dim light, unaffected by time's passage","Slagvi has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> toward the Stone of Wakening, the island that stands in the lake.","Studying the stones on either side of the entrance may reveal what happened to the wards that once blocked passage to Gloomingtarn.","'This is the cavern where Durin the Deathless awoke, ${PLAYER}, first of all the dwarves. Do you see the island in the lake? <rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> across the water, and tell me what you see.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> toward the island that stands in the lake","Chapter 8.3: In Memory of the Forge-master","Slagvi asked you to defeat any Angmarim cultists you find lurking within the cavern of Gloomingtarn.","The White Stone Forge is as Slagvi described, but of the anvil there is no sign","Someone etched further lines upon this rune. Now it feels inert, robbed of power","'We must follow the cultists inside, and teach them they are not welcome! Let us enact the vengeance of Stóthkell, and of all the dwarves who revere this place, upon the intruders!'","Slagvi asked to meet with you at the entrance to Gloomingtarn from Deepscrave, where he fears the rune-stones warding passage to that sacred cavern may be threatened.","It is said that Durin himself constructed the White Stone Forge and the Black Stone Anvil in the days after he first awoke.","Slagvi stands beside the lakeshore in the vast cavern, deep in thought.","Examine the rune-stone wards (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Do you see the island in the lake? <rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> across the water, and tell me what you see.'","'I fear we may be too late, ${PLAYER}. Examine the warding runes and tell me what you see.'","'I fear we may be too late. Examine the warding runes and tell me what you see.'","'The island in the lake is called the Stone of Wakening, for it is said that Durin awoke there, first of all the dwarves. He built an anvil of black stone and a forge of white brick, and the sound of his hammer echoing over the water called forth the ancient fathers of the dwarves. They stood on the shore of the lake, observing his work.\
\
'Stóthkell would have loved to stand here, ${PLAYER}. He spoke of it often, and my heart is aggrieved to know now that he never will.\
\
'Let us cross to the Wakening Stone and see the black anvil and the white forge on his behalf. The bridge is just to the south.'"},
[3292]={"Gather information from residents in the Lower Ward (2/3)","'Will you return to the Upper and Lower Wards of the city and learn what people are saying about Azagath, Belondor, and Nakási?'","He falls silent and says nothing further","Gather information from residents in the Lower Ward (${CURRENT}/3)","'Keep your voice down, stranger! There are unfriendly ears about!\
\
'Well, I do not know if there are, but it is better to stay on the side of caution, is it not? People say Azagath Sea-shadow was driven from the Citadel by a great beast, and only the swords of Nakási Wave-reaper and Belondor of the Fleet-fast saved his life! I have remained on guard for any sign of the sorcerers who unleashed the beast upon the Kindred, but so far I have not seen anything. They could be anywhere.\
\
'You should come back to me when you have finished your own errands for the day. I may have learned something by then!'","'I saw you in the Citadel, stranger. You were there. Were you also in the Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo?'\
\
Belondor shakes his head sadly.\
\
'The writing was there, but I did not see it until it was too late. There was cruelty in the Sea-shadow, as there was cruelty in all of us... but I believed it was needed against the evils arrayed against us. The Church of the All-Seeing, the Empire of Ordakh... these were foes against which we could show no mercy. The hatred I bore for Gondor...\
\
'Aye, I would not show mercy to any warriors of Gondor who opposed us. But not children. The boy Thorongil was not yet a man, and Azagath would have drenched the stones of the Citadel with his blood. Nakási would have obeyed the command, and done whatever the Sea-shadow ordered. The writing was there, but even then I followed the two of them as they fled. In the Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo my crew paid for my inaction, my indecision. Azagath slew them with dark, unnatural magic, and their sacrifice meant nothing.\
\
'Do you have a crew of your own, stranger? Do you know what it means to lose them all, and for nothing?'","'Sometimes word travels slowly, and on other occasions it can spread faster than wildfire.'","The rumour was true: Belondor has returned to the Sail-haven","Gathered information from residents in the Lower Ward (${CURRENT}/3)","Belondor stands atop one of the piers extending out into the waters of the Sail-haven.","Gather information from residents in the Upper Ward (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Have I heard anything of late concerning the Kindred of the Coins? I confess to you I have not paid very much attention to their dealings in recent days, for I have been much occupied with caring for my new friend Rûmina. She is asleep right now, but when she wakes she is like to cause quite a commotion, chasing either her tail or the rodents that infest the Lower Ward and the Sail-haven!\
\
'She was the loyal companion of a Corsair captain and sailed from port to port with him, but now that he has retired from that trade he has given his ship-cat to me. She seems quite happy with her new circumstance, but she keeps me very busy!\
\
'If you check back in with me perhaps you can help the two of us with something? That would be very good of you.'","'Pssst... stranger.'\
\
The man stares at you with piercing eyes. After a moment you realize he is speaking to you nearly without moving his mouth.\
\
'I saw a well-dressed man in blue and silver making for one of the north-south piers extending out into the waters of the Sail-haven,' he says. 'You might go see this man.'","Find the man wearing blue and silver on one of the north-south piers of the the Sail-haven","Belondor says nothing.","Chapter 8.3: The Words in the Wards","Talk to Belondor in the Sail-haven","'I do not know which it will be. Sometimes word travels slowly, and on other occasions it can spread faster than wildfire. Will you return to the Upper and Lower Wards of the city and learn what people are saying about Azagath, Belondor, and Nakási?\
\
'If tongues wag as I think they will, rumour that these leaders of the Kindred fled beneath the Mâkhda Khorbo in search of some evil will not be gladly received. At least... I hope it will not. Begin your search in the Upper Ward, for it is nearer.'","A man in the Lower Ward told you he saw a well-dressed man in blue and silver walking along one of the north-south piers extending out into the waters of the Sail-haven, north-west of the Lower Ward.","Corudan has asked you to speak with residents of the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl about Azagath and the other leaders of the Kindred that fled with him.","The man says nothing further to you.","Gathered information from residents in the Upper Ward (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Azagath was well-loved by the people of Umbar Baharbêl, and Corudan wants to know if they have learned of his escape from the city.","'Yes? You have caught me at a good time, my friend, for I have just come into a large sum of money! Or rather, I will have just as soon as I collect upon a daring wager I made at Dahâl Huliz, the grand arena within the Tor-gardens. What a glorious day it is today!\
\
'How do I feel about the Kindred of the Coins? Oh, I think they are doing a very good job of things. They saved us from the rule of the Empire of Ordakh and the Church of the All-Seeing, after all. Let me just say this, friend. If the Kindred was not in power, I would not feel comfortable telling you about my winnings at Dahâl Huliz, for fear that the Church would take my winnings for their own. I do not think any of the Kindred would do so... unless the Golden Queen is made jealous by my newfound wealth!'\
\
Mokhlêsh falls silent, considering this uncomfortable new thought.\
\
'Hmm. If you return to me when you have a moment, I might have some work for you. I cannot be too careful when such a large sum is at stake.'","Corudan has asked you to speak with residents of the Lower Ward of Umbar Baharbêl about Azagath and the other leaders of the Kindred that fled with him.","'What do I think of the Kindred of the Coins? I think they have ruled us well and fairly since the war's ending, and neither the Heirs of Castamir nor the Empire of Ordakh could have done better. I have heard some troubling rumours that there was fighting in the Citadel not long ago, and I hope the ones responsible will soon be apprehended. May justice come swiftly for the ones responsible!\
\
'I heard there was fell magic involved. It is said a great beast with five heads emerged from a column of water and shook the Citadel to its very foundation, but that is not the most surprising thing I have heard! I heard each of the five heads bore a woman's countenance, and the beauty of each was matched only by her ferocity.\
\
'Yes, it is preposterous, but this is a land where surprising things can happen! I was not there, and neither were you. I believe this beast lives, unless Azagath has already slain it. If you were a resident of this city you would know he is capable of great martial feats. Return to me when you have a moment and we will see who knows the city of Umbar Baharbêl, and who does not!'","'What do I think of the Kindred of the Coins? This is a difficult question for me to answer, friend.\
\
'It is true they have promised a return to peace and an increase in prosperity since they came to power and cast out the Empire of Ordakh, and it seems this will be made so. But they also promised to heed the will of the people and hear their concerns, but the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja remains shut. Where once I saw Azagath and the other leaders of the Kindred walking through the city, that has happened less and less often of late. Where are Tatháta and her mighty hounds? Where are Tumúldo and his wife Nakási? The only leader of the Kindred I see with any regularity is the dwarf Khôltekh, and I do not like the look in his eye. He is plotting something within the Shoreward Stone, you mark my words.\
\
'But for my part I believe the Kindred has our best interests in mind. Truthfully I would feel more at ease if they reopened Dâr Laja and kept their promise!'"},
[3293]={"'I have decided... reluctantly... that such slaughter will not prove a salve for the hurt done my people, though the villains who stole the Black Stone Anvil deserve such dealings. Let us instead learn where they have taken it, that we may recover it and restore it to this sacred ground. Many more than one hundred and one cultists may fall before we accomplish this, and I will not weep for them.\
\
'But I see that Bósi and his kin have arrived on the lakeshore. Let them know the Black Stone Anvil has been stolen, but tell them gently; they suffered a great deal in Moria, and this insult will grieve them no less than it does me.'","Bósi greets you warmly","'I see that Bósi and his kin have arrived on the lakeshore. Let them know the Black Stone Anvil has been stolen, but tell them gently; they suffered a great deal in Moria, and this insult will grieve them no less than it does me.'","Defeat Angmarim in Gloomingtarn (${NUMBER}/101)","You hear Slagvi calling for you from the Stone of Wakening","Chapter 8.4: An Insult Never To Be Forgotten","Meet up with Bósi and the other Longbeards on the lakeshore","'It must have been the cultists from Angmar! Did I say they would pay for their intrusion into Gloomingtarn? That was nothing compared to this insult! The villains who hauled away the Black Stone Anvil will suffer the wrath of the dwarves and all who call them friend! I will not sleep until those responsible are slain!\
\
'You will aid me in this, yes? I ask that you slay one hundred and one Angmarim cultists in Gloomingtarn! That will show them the reach of our anger, and still it will only be the start!'","Slagvi has sworn vengeance upon the Angmarim cultists that removed the Black Stone Anvil from the island of Durin's awakening.","Bósi is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.","'The villains who hauled away the Black Stone Anvil will suffer the wrath of the dwarves and all who call them friend! I will not sleep until those responsible are slain!\
\
'You will aid me in this, yes? I ask that you slay one hundred and one Angmarim cultists in Gloomingtarn! That will show them how serious we are!'","Bósi and some other Longbeards have come to the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.","Defeat Angmarim in Gloomingtarn (6/101)","'I am saddened by the theft of the Black Stone Anvil, but I think we can recover it. Mark my words: forging-hammers will once again ring against it, echoing throughout the caverns of Gundabad. We will make certain of it, not only to honour Durin the Deathless who built it, but also for the memory of Stóthkell the Forge-master, who fell in Máttugard.\
\
'My son thinks he knows where the Black Stone Anvil was taken.'","Defeated Angmarim in Gloomingtarn (${NUMBER}/101)","Slagvi has demanded that you slay one hundred and one Angmarim as payment for their theft of the Black Stone Anvil.","Talk to Slagvi on the island in the lake","Slagvi is standing on the Stone of Wakening, the island in the middle of the Gloomingtarn lake.","'We stand upon sacred ground, my friend.'","Talk to Bósi on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn"},
[3294]={"Talk to Sirgon outside the Harbour-warden's Tower, in the Sail-haven","Chapter 8.4: Gondor and Umbar","'What brings you to this city, stranger? I deem you have sought me out. Why?'\
\
You tell Belondor that you have come to Umbar in the company of his old friend Sirgon. Belondor remains silent for a long time before speaking.\
\
'It has been many years since I named Sirgon a friend, and it must be the same with he who is the Lord of Lebennin. Was he rewarded for his blood-red service by the Steward of Gondor? Did chasing me into the rocks of Shedax Khîn win him glory and fortune? He slew friends of mine in that pursuit... did he tell you? Has he come to Umbar Baharbêl to finish the job he began those many years ago? He would be wise to steer clear from my manor, for the wrath of Mêshka my wife will be more deadly to him than all the spines of the desert, or the pointed rocks of the Shield Isles.'\
\
You tell Belondor that Sirgon has already spoken with Mêshka, and she made her opinion of him very clear. Belondor looks at you with surprise.\
\
'And he did not clap her in irons? He is not here to drag us back to Gondor in chains? Has the King not sent you and he here to inflict his will upon us? If not... then why has Sirgon come here?'\
\
You consider what you might tell Belondor, but decide upon the truth: that Sirgon feels the burden of his past with Belondor and Mêshka, and he hopes to reconcile with them, if such a thing might be possible.\
\
'If what you say is true, let him speak these words to me himself. I will await him at The Hungry Deep Tavern. Now begone. I would be alone with my thoughts, as I was before. I have friends to mourn.'","Talk to Sirgon outside the Harbour-warden's Tower and go with him to meet with Belondor","'And so you stand before me once again, ${PLAYER}. I am touched to hear of the reconciliation between Belondor and the man of Gondor who has so disturbed his heart for these many years. I trust this thaw will not make him weak? Without Azagath and Nakási, the Kindred of the Coins must appear strong now, stronger than ever before.\
\
'The people must be reassured that the Kindred is here for them, despite the betrayal of the Sea-shadow. I have come to a decision, and I would like to ask you for help in seeing it done.'","'Then it is time. To the Hungry Deep we go.'","Belondor has asked to speak with his one-time friend and long-time foe, if it is true that Sirgon has come to Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Hármelak inside her manor","Sirgon stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower, in the Sail-haven.","Sirgon stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower, in the Sail-haven, waiting to go with you to meet with Belondor.","Hármelak is inside her manor, waiting to speak with you about the Kindred of the Coins.","'You have seen Belondor? What did he say to you, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You relay Belondor's message, and Sirgon thinks it over. At last he steeples his fingers in front of his face and closes his eyes. When he reopens them again, he has come to a decision.\
\
'The Hungry Deep Tavern overlooks the Sail-haven, but it is located in the Upper Ward. Belondor's wife Mêshka commanded her guards to slay me should I return to that place.\
\
'But I would speak again with Belondor and tell him what I have come to believe. I am not afraid of Mêshka's headsmen. I would bare my neck before them if it meant I could ease this burden from my back, ${PLAYER}. I have carried it for too long.\
\
'Will you accompany me, my friend? Let me know when you are ready to leave.'","'Tell Sirgon to meet me at The Hungry Deep tavern. Now begone, for I have friends to mourn.'"},
[3295]={"'It has been many hundreds of years since any dwarves lived in this place, but the signs of each previous habitation are there if you know where to look. To the Longbeards this was Tharrazhâr, and they stocked the keep with the metals they prized and the equipment they needed to defend it. When my people first dwelt here they gave it the name Brúgrad, but they had their eye set upon larger and more wealthy cities, and did not intend to remain long.\
\
'It was a useful foothold, but it proved a tenuous one. Many Zhélruka set out from Brúgrad in search of fabled Thafar-gathol, but those who returned did so only with disappointment. And at last there came a day when the returners came back to a fallen fortress. None can say how long the dwarves fought against the dragons, but in the end none called it Brúgrad any longer. Now the ruins are named only in the Westron Speech, and the heart of every true Zhélruka scholar mourns, knowing what was lost when the name became Skarháld.'","'Bótuz Frostblood will be near the top of the stronghold, ${PLAYER}. Present yourself to him and say that we are at his service here in Skarháld. Longbeard and Zhélruka alike have much to gain as friends and allies, and the mountains can only be conquered if we work together, despite the differences we may have had in the past.'","Leave the keep of Skarháld and learn what transpired outside","Bótuz Frostblood is near the top of the fortress of Skarháld.","Talk to Dóbrokh","Inek eyes the siege defences with disapproval","Talk to Inek the Brash","'I delivered the trophies we collected to Bótuz Frostblood, and he seemed quite impressed by our valour, ${PLAYER}. He has charged me with cataloguing the supplies here in the keep, and I have agreed. This work is not well-suited to one of my lineage, but I understand the need for it and want to encourage cooperation between the Longbeards and the Zhélruka here in Skarháld. This work will bear fruit in the long run, I am sure.\
\
'Wait. Did you hear that? There is a commotion of some sort outside. We should go see what is happening!'","Dóbrokh stands at the edge, unconcerned by the long drop","Find Inek the Brash at the siege defences","A crowd of dwarves surround a wounded Zhélruka warrior","Kópat assists his brethren with establishing crafting facilities in the keep","'I thought I was not observed... but he must have seen me. The blades flew faster than I... could have expected....'\
\
The scout clutches his side, where a sharp weapon has cut through his armour. One of the nearby dwarves asks who it was that did this to him, and he grimaces in pain.","'Are you here for sight-seeing or for helping us, ${RACE}? Yes, I remember you and your companion speaking with Bótuz before we crossed to the Grey Mountains. What can you tell me of this Durin? He tried to stop us from entering the Dale-lands, but when Bótuz refused to heed his warning he did nothing. That is a sign of weakness. His father must be very disappointed in him.\
\
'I am proud to count myself among the Zhélruka, for we reinforce our position with actions... not with empty words! Let other dwarves waggle their beards in discussion, and while they speak the Zhélruka will take what they want!\
\
'I will tell you no false-hoods: sometimes this creed causes others to resent the Zhélruka. Bótuz knows this, and he commanded me to inspect the defences of this fortress. Sadly, I must report that this equipment is not satisfactory, and will require some work if it is to be made war-worthy.'","Talk to Bótuz Frostblood at Skarháld","'I heard raised voices! Let us see what has happened outside! The cataloguing of the supplies can wait!'","Talk to Vútro the West-wind and learn how he was injured","Talk to Durin inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld","You and Durin have come to the old fortress of Skarháld, where Longbeards and Zhélruka both attempt to survive in the dangerous Grey Mountains.","'Like Stormwall, this fortress was abandoned for centuries. Once it climbed proudly up the mountain's side, but time and the repeated onslaughts of dragon-kind have worn away some of its majesty. Much like my people, however, it perseveres, no matter the hardship it endures!\
\
'Bótuz Frostblood will be near the top of the stronghold, ${PLAYER}. Present yourself to him and say that we are at his service here in Skarháld. Longbeard and Zhélruka alike have much to gain as friends and allies, and the mountains can only be conquered if we work together, despite the differences we may have had in the past.'","You heard raised voices outside the keep. What is happening?","Find Kópat inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld","Durin is inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld.","Talk to Kópat","A crowd of dwarves surround a wounded Zhélruka warrior on the upper level of Skarháld.","'I welcome you to Skarháld, ${PLAYER}. Make yourself at home here, and meet with my chieftains. Look for Inek, Kópat, and Dóbrokh on the upper levels of Skarháld and in the keep.'","'Oh, it's you. I heard that the son of Thorin had come to Skarháld bearing drake-teeth and burning scales, hatchling-wings and worm-hides, as if that proves anything to me. Did he slay these creatures or did you, ${PLAYER}? He is young and brash, and I know his sort: a king's son, dreaming of glory but unable to attain it. He is soft! The lands of my people are harsh and cruel, and he would not long have lasted in the hard lands.'\
\
Bótuz snorts, delivering his taunts with relish.\
\
'Durin! I see the arrogance of the Longbeards in that name. Thorin is a fool to aim so high!\
\
'But you are different, ${PLAYER}, and I welcome you to Skarháld without reservation. Make yourself at home here, and meet with my chieftains. Look for Inek, Kópat, and Dóbrokh on the upper levels of Skarháld and in the keep.'","Chapter 8.4: The Stones of Skarháld","'Watch your footing, ${RACE}. It is a long way to the valley floor below, and if you are not careful you might find yourself taking the fast way down. Most are not as surefooted as Dóbrokh!\
\
'Far away to the east are the lands from which my people came, past the mountains and to others beyond. Many were the hardships we endured there, and the sum of them made the Zhélruka slow to smile and wary of strangers, but it also made us hardy and tough, and protective of the things we hold dear.\
\
'I say we came from the East, and that is true, but that is not the home for which we have spent so many lifetimes searching. How many kings of the Zhélruka have sought for such a home in these very mountains? How many more will follow us in that purpose? Dóbrokh cannot say.'","Find Dóbrokh at the view from the high eastern arch","Bótuz Frostblood told you to look for his chieftains Inek, Kópat, and Dóbrokh on the upper levels of Skarháld and in the keep."},
[3296]={"'I think I will come along. After all, if I do not keep Bróin from stumbling into the dangers that wait for him in that direction, who will do so? There is also the matter of my apprenticeship: I have not yet searched Clovengap for the Zabad'ibîn sought by my master, and it is only a matter of time before he gets it into his head that they must surely lie within.\
\
'Lead on, I say!'","Bori is waiting by the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn for you to agree to his plan.","Bori of the Iron Garrison thinks the Angmarim may have hauled the Black Stone Anvil out of Gloomingtarn, and if you hurry you may be able to find and retrieve the ancient artifact before they do it some harm.","'It is no easy matter to move such a thing, ${PLAYER}, and legend says of the Black Stone Anvil that it was heavier than other such tools. That solidity imbued weapons hammered upon it with similar qualities, and it is said that no weapon Durin ever crafted upon the Black Stone Anvil and in the White Stone Forge could be turned away, unless it be by armour forged from the same.\
\
'If the Angmarim have taken it, they must have taken it across the lake by boat, and hauled it north on ropes into Clovengap. We would have seen signs of its passage had they dared take it south or east, and we did not. I suggest we investigate Clovengap, and perhaps we will learn for what purpose the cultists sought to steal such a relic of our history.\
\
'Is my cousin with us? Will Bróin consent to leave Fastrith behind? This expedition will be dangerous.'","'I have said my say.'","Talk to Bori by the lakeshore and travel with him in search of the Black Stone Anvil","Bósi is in Clovengap, north-east of the tunnel to Gloomingtarn.","'I hear you, cousin, and I insist that I meant no disrespect.'","Fastrith is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.","Talk to Bróin on the lakeshore","'Bori believes it must have been hauled on ropes north to Clovengap, although the purpose for which the cultists would put it remains a mystery to him, and to me.\
\
'Hear him and see if you agree.'","Chapter 8.5: Assault on Clovengap","Bori is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.","'I see no reason to leave Fastrith behind if she is willing to risk the dangers. If Bori were to look around him, he would see no sign of hearth or home nearby... we are far from the Lonely Mountain, and I say Fastrith has already proven herself more than his equal in courage!'\
\
Bróin's eyes flash dangerously, and you wonder for how long this declaration has been brewing.","Talk to Bósi in Clovengap, north-east of the tunnel to Gloomingtarn","Talk to Bori on the lakeshore","'The wargs will return, and in greater numbers. We must remain cautious while we set up camp, and be ready for anything.'","'I did not mean to offend, and I hope I have not. Let us all remain friends as we venture into Clovengap!'\
\
Bori lowers his voice and speaks only to you.\
\
'They cannot be helped, ${PLAYER}. He is smitten beyond aid, and she is reckless to a fault. I do not know which is more hopeless! We will have to keep our eyes on them as we adventure, for their safety, and ours! Anyway... onward!'","'Hear what Bori has to say and see if you agree, friend. I think he is right on this.'","Fastrith laughs merrily","'How can I fear to adventure in Clovengap when I have not yet seen it? It could be lovely!'","'Bori should not speak of what he does not understand. It is a fault of his!'","'Clovengap is bound to be dangerous, and each member of this expedition would do well to heed it.'","Talk to Fastrith on the lakeshore","Bróin is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn."},
[3297]={"'What did you say? You recovered the keys from the Heirsworn, and a new lock is being made for Dâr Laja? I confess to you I did not think you would do it! But it warms my heart to know that Lady Hármelak's wishes are being carried out. The Meeting-hall will open and the Kindred will once again hear the voice of the people!\
\
'It will take some time for everything to be ready, but I hope when all is prepared you will return to us, my new friend. It will be a new dawn for Umbar, and let none doubt the days of sunshine that lie before us!'","Yamin is located just to the north of the Grand Market in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.","Jaith guards the entrance to Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall, in the centre of the Upper Ward.","Defeated an Heirsworn Corsair in the Sail-haven","Chapter 8.5: Hármelak's Resolve","At last! You have found the keys to Dâr Laja!","Talk to Jaith outside Dâr Laja about opening the Meeting-hall","Bring the keys you recovered to Yamin just north of the Grand Market in the Upper Ward","Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall, is located in the centre of the Upper Ward.","Hármelak has decided that, in the wake of Azagath's betrayal, the people of Umbar Baharbêl need to be reassured that the Kindred of the Coins are working to ensure their safety and prosperity.","Talk to Jaith outside Dâr Laja in the centre of the Upper Ward","'What are these? The keys to the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja? The last I heard, these were in the hands of Heirsworn down at the Sail-haven. It seemed to me the Kindred of the Coins were willing to let them keep them. Being already in power, they were in no hurry to reopen the Meeting-hall and hear from the people again.\
\
'But I am to fashion a new lock and keys for Dâr Laja so it can be reopened? Those are very surprising tidings, both welcome and unwelcome, if you understand me. I recently lost an apprentice, you see, but there is just as much work as ever. If you return here when you have a moment, I might have some work for you.\
\
'But for now I shall begin on this new task. It will be some time before everything will be ready.'","Defeat Heirsworn in the Sail-haven until you find the keys to Dâr Laja","Jaith told you that Heirsworn in the Sail-haven might have absconded with the keys to Dâr Laja, and they must be recovered before the hall can safely be opened to the people.","'Speak with Jaith, who guards Dâr Laja here in the Upper Ward of the city. He will tell you what must be done to reopen the Meeting-hall. It may take some time, but with this decision I hope we take the first steady steps toward a brighter future for Umbar and its people.'","'For now I shall begin on this new task. It will be some time before everything will be ready.'","'If you are able to wrest the keys from the Heirsworn in the Sail-haven, we might be able to do something... but not until then. Once you retrieve the keys, if such a thing is possible, you should bring them to Yamin just north of the Grand Market to see about making a new set of keys and a better, more secure lock for the Meeting-hall.'","'Hármelak wants the Meeting-hall opened? Oh, I do not think we can do that.\
\
'No, no, no, do not misunderstand me! I would leap at once to carry out the Lady Hármelak's command! It is just that the keys to Dâr Laja were stolen by the Heirsworn, and ever since those villains ran off with the keys, we have not been able to get inside. A new lock might be fashioned, given enough time, but it is not safe for us to proceed for as long as the Heirsworn hold onto the keys.\
\
'If you are able to wrest the keys from them, we might be able to do something... but not until then. The Heirsworn can be found all over the Sail-haven, if you are ready for a fight. Once you retrieve the keys, if such a thing is possible, you should bring them to Yamin just north of the Grand Market to see about making a new set of keys and a better, more secure lock for the Meeting-hall. If you are able to do all that, come let me know! But I will not hold my breath until then. You understand: it is just that folk are always making big claims at sunset, and by dawn nothing has come of it.'","'We will reassure the folk of Umbar Baharbêl that the peace will continue, and prosperity will be theirs. The Kindred of the Coins will hear their concerns and act upon them. The Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja must be reopened. Its doors have remained shut for too long, and the voice of the people has grown distant.'\
\
Hármelak's eyes shimmer in the light of her richly-decorated chamber.\
\
'When you were last here, ${PLAYER}, I spoke some words concerning the Sea-shadow. You have now seen what I then believed, and still do: he was not trustworthy, and owed his allegiance to some other. I think now that he drew his powers and his strength from forces unnatural, from He-Who-Sees-All... from Sauron. For your part in deposing him, in driving him from Umbar, you have my gratitude. I know you are not from this land, but I believe you have a giving heart, a charitable will, and an understanding mind. Will you help me set right what Azagath and Nakási have disturbed?\
\
'If so, speak with Jaith, who guards Dâr Laja here in the Upper Ward of the city. He will tell you what must be done to reopen the Meeting-hall. It may take some time, but with this decision I hope we take the first steady steps toward a brighter future for Umbar and its people.'"},
[3298]={"Talk to Bótuz Frostblood and join the search for Karazgar","'Karazgar wants to speak... with Bótuz....'","Talk to Bótuz Frostblood on the upper level of Skarháld","'Before today, Vútro was one of our finest scouts, able to outrun even the West Wind. Alas for Vútro! This wound will keep him from the wild lands. A scout that cannot walk the wilderness is of no use to me or to my people.\
\
'The Weeping Warrior is known to us, ${PLAYER}, even in the distant lands from which we came. His reputation for cruelty is unmatched; he has long had designs on the North, and has troubled both Longbeards and Zhélruka in pursuit of it. Even so, I do not fear him. I will bring a small force of my finest warriors for two purposes: as a wise exercise of caution, and also as a demonstration of our power. Perhaps Karazgar will decide he does not wish to oppose the Zhélruka in these mountains, and will leave us in peace.\
\
'I would have you come with us, ${PLAYER}, but your friend Durin must remain behind. I gave him a task suited to his abilities, and at any rate this meeting will be too dangerous for an unproven king's son.'","'Vútro will tell us where he encountered Karazgar, and we will find the Weeping Warrior. Let us hear what he has to say, and if it is not to my liking he will regret it!'","Chapter 8.5: The Warrior Found","'Karazgar thinks to frighten us with words, but he overestimates their power. Have I not told you that words mean little to me, and only actions earn my respect? Let Karazgar speak. We will blunt his words with hammers, and cut his intentions with our axes!\
\
'The Zhélruka will prevail!'","'It was... he of the terrible mask... the Weeping Warrior!\
\
'He held a knife to my throat... and gave me a message...'\
\
Vútro closes his eyes, overcome with the pain of his wound.\
\
'Karazgar wants to speak... with Bótuz....'","Bótuz Frostblood is on the upper level of Skarháld, and he plans to lead a party of dwarves in search of the Weeping Warrior.","Bótuz Frostblood is on the upper level of Skarháld.","Vútro the West-wind ran afoul of the Weeping Warrior and barely escaped with his life."},
[3299]={"The Angmarim are here in great numbers, but of the Black Stone Anvil there is no sign","Bósi has asked you to search a number of locations within Clovengap for the missing Black Stone Anvil, and to defeat the wargs charged with protecting the area from intruders.","'While we work, perhaps you can quiet some of the warg-voices that trouble the stillness, ${PLAYER}. Ránulur's brothers and sisters will not abandon their efforts to avenge him upon us; would we, in their position? You know we would not.\
\
'I ask that you also keep your eyes open for the missing Black Stone Anvil, or some sign of its passage. Be not blinded by the beauty of the once-verdant ladder-gardens! We are here for a purpose, and should see it done.'\
\
Bósi chuckles.\
\
'I know you would not be distracted so, ${PLAYER}. I was speaking more to myself than to you. Not since Khazad-dûm have I seen such beautiful terraces, and... ah, it does not matter. Good fortune go with you, my friend. When you return perhaps we will know where next to search.'","'You are back, and sooner than I expected! What did your explorations teach you of this place? Was there any sign of the object of our search?'","Investigate the Angmarim presence at Garanashmar","All is silent in the old vineyard, any fruitful pursuit there long abandoned","Investigate the sounds coming from Dashat-zahar","Chapter 8.6: The Beauty of Akrakír","Talk to Bósi in Clovengap","Defeat wargs in Clovengap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Investigate the old vineyard of Maranazhâr","Defeated wargs in Clovengap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hornets have occupied Dashat-zahar. The Angmarim will not trouble to come here","'Quiet some of the warg-voices that trouble the stillness, and also keep your eyes open for the missing Black Stone Anvil, or some sign of its passage.'","The Longbeards of the Iron Garrison comb the gardens of Akrakír for the missing Black Stone Anvil, hoping to find the ancient artifact before it is put to some terrible purpose by their enemies.","Bósi is at his camp not far from the south-western entrance to Clovengap."},
[3300]={"Send Zhélruka craftsmen to repair the siege defences (${NUMBER}/4)","Tally the weapons stored inside the keep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Speak to some of the craftsmen here in the keep and see if they can repair the ballistae or produce a greater supply of heavy arrows to be set with them.'","Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, has promised to bring war to Skarháld, and Bótuz Frostblood wants you to ready the defences.","The mountains shake again!","'Karazgar will attack Skarháld as he promised, and we will need to repel him. Go to your friend Durin inside the keep and help him assess our equipment. I want to ensure we have weapons and armour enough for my Zhélruka when Karazgar does attack.'","'The mountains shake as if caught in a great gale! Has the Weeping Warrior worked some sorcery upon us?'","The mountains shake!","'What is happening? The very mountains shake beneath my feet!'","Durin asked you to count the weapons and armour currently stored inside the keep of Skarháld, as well as to assess the quality of the siege defences on the upper level outside the keep.","The mountains shake! What is happening?","Sent craftsmen to repair the siege defences (${NUMBER}/4)","'I feared it was so, for the siege defences seemed in a poor state, even to my casual eye. Speak to some of the craftsmen here in the keep and see if they can repair the ballistae or produce a greater supply of heavy arrows to be set with them.\
\
'I hold no authority over these dwarves, but I hope they will understand the importance of these suggestions! My teachers impressed upon me the need for suitable preparations; it is much better to mourn the lost time after a victory than it is to mourn a lost battle!'","Made a tally of the armour (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Bótuz Frostblood inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld","There is a distant rumbling as the keep shakes beneath your feet","Talk to Durin inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld","'Even so, I do not think Karazgar's words are without meaning. He will attack Skarháld as he promised, and we will need to repel him. Go to your friend Durin inside the keep and help him assess our equipment. I want to ensure we have weapons and armour enough for my Zhélruka when Karazgar does attack.'","'Did you feel that? What is happening?'","Assessed the defences and found them wanting (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Durin is inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld.","This time the rumbling is more pronounced, as the keep shakes again","Chapter 8.6: Tremors in the Foundation","'I would appreciate it if you could tally the weapons and armour contained in the side rooms, and to inspect the siege defences outside the keep. We will need to know what deserves the most attention if we are to prepare in time for Karazgar's return.'","'I heard some of the Zhélruka talking, ${PLAYER}. Is it true that Karazgar has promised three assaults upon Skarháld? This inventory of the supplies has become much more important than it was mere hours ago! Have you come to assist me?\
\
'I would appreciate it if you could tally the weapons and armour contained in the side rooms, and to inspect the siege defences outside the keep. We will need to know what deserves the most attention if we are to prepare in time for Karazgar's return.'","Tally the armour stored inside the keep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Durin is inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld, which has been shaken to its foundations.","Bótuz Frostblood is inside the keep of Skarháld.","Durin has requested that you send Zhélruka craftsmen inside the keep to repair the siege defences.","Made a tally of the weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Assess the quality of the siege defences outside the keep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[3301]={"Bótuz Frostblood wants you to keep an eye on Durin during the defence of Skarháld.","Durin is outside the keep on the upper level of Skarháld.","'Are you ready, ${PLAYER}? Tell Durin that even he must fight! If Karazgar is behind this, we will make him regret it!'","'Will you work with me to make this stronghold safe, and to take revenge upon the Weeping Warrior? If you will vouch for the Longbeard prince, he is welcome to join hands with the Zhélruka in these two purposes.'","'To battle! We will find Karazgar's weaknesses and exploit them! Imkhih sabkyûd, ${PLAYER}!'","The death of Bótuz Frostblood threatens to leave the Zhélruka at Skarháld in disarray. One of his lieutenants must rise to lead his fellows.","Chapter 8.7: The First Promise","Talk to Durin inside the keep and defend Skarháld","'The first of Karazgar's promises has been fulfilled, and claimed the life of Bótuz Frostblood. With one deadly strike, he has left the Zhélruka here without their leader. Who now will lead them? Who now will organize the defences?'","Find a lieutenant of Bótuz Frostblood to lead the Zhélruka","While surveying the damage, Inek catches your eye","'If I once believed the ill fortune of the Zhélruka had been exaggerated by the bards, I do no longer! The loss of Bótuz Frostblood must be a grievous injury to them, and I confess that it pains me also. Would Bótuz and the others who died during Karazgar's attack still be alive if I had not lowered my weapon in the Ironfold? Would they still live if I had kept them from crossing the Dale-lands? Ah, I will not dwell upon it. What was done is done, and might have been worse.\
\
'It is good to hear that Inek will take up the mantle of leadership and ready his people for another attack. Karazgar promised to come to Skarháld three times? How much worse will be the following assaults, if this was merely the first? It bodes ill, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I know the Zhélruka do not care for me. Nay, do not seek to deny it! It is true. I am unproven. Did I count myself ready when we battled the Easterlings outside Utterby back in the Ironfold? That counted for naught, or less than naught! To do battle against Karazgar, in defence not only of my people but of another... that is where my true glory lies. We will stand with Inek and his Zhélruka to repel whatever Karazgar sends against us, and perhaps afterward I will feel my name deserved. It will be my honour to stand with them and with you, ${PLAYER}. There is much we must do if we are to be ready. The first promise is fulfilled. When the next comes, we must be ready. We have no choice.'","'Karazgar toys with us, ${PLAYER}, as a cat does with a mouse! He had the advantage, but he did not press it. The first of his promises has been fulfilled, and claimed the life of Bótuz Frostblood. With one deadly strike, Karazgar has left the Zhélruka here without their leader. Who now will lead them? Who now will organize the defences?'","'Bótuz was supposed to lead us here in the Grey Mountains! What are the Zhélruka going to do now? Who will lead us on this venture now that the Frostblood is dead?'\
\
Inek the Brash clenches his fists and lives up to his name.\
\
'It has to be me! No others of his lieutenants are suited to the task! Kópat is a scholar, much good may it do us here, and Dóbrokh may be a fine warrior but he does not command respect the way Bótuz did. It falls to me to manage the defences. It can be no one else!\
\
'Bótuz thought you a worthy ally, ${PLAYER}. Will you work with me to make this stronghold safe, and to take revenge upon the Weeping Warrior? If you will vouch for the Longbeard prince, he is welcome to join hands with the Zhélruka in these two purposes.'","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld","'Keep an eye on your friend and ensure he does not embarrass himself!'","Karazgar has not given the Dwarves of Skarháld enough time to prepare. He launches the first of his promised attacks, seeking to attain his goals with a single throw."},
[3302]={"Bróin has called for your attention in Clovengap.","Investigate the frozen reaches of Clovengap, to the north-west","Crushed into the snow and ice of one booted footprint you find a single red pebble","Bróin has asked to see the red pebble you found.","Bróin calls over to you, seeking your attention","Bróin asked to meet with you atop the terrace to the west, a short distance away from the others.","'It seems the northern reaches of Clovengap have been iced over and frozen, a sure sign Hrímil Frost-heart has chosen that place for her lair, or that she has spent time there for another reason. What that might be I cannot guess, but I deem it important we learn what we can of it!\
\
'Investigate that frozen place and keep a close eye for any clues that might shed light upon her intentions in Clovengap! Did the Angmarim bring the Black Stone Anvil there, hoping to present it to the dragon? I cannot see what use she might have for it, but the minds of dragons have always been impenetrable to the dwarves, and to me in particular!\
\
'To reach the frozen river-bed in the northern reaches of Clovengap, make your way through Frósthel on the left side of the Ladder-gardens.'","'Investigate that frozen place and keep a close eye for any clues that might shed light upon the dragon's intentions in Clovengap.\
\
'To reach the frozen river-bed in the northern reaches of Clovengap, make your way through Frósthel on the left side of the Ladder-gardens.'","Bróin looks around nervously, and asks to see the red pebble you found","'Thank you for agreeing to speak with me.'","A disorganized array of Orkish footprints has drawn your attention.","Bósi is in the south-west portion of Clovengap, waiting to hear what you learned during your investigation of the frozen reaches.","Chapter 8.7: The Rimed Passage","'Can we talk, ${PLAYER}? No, not here. Let us meet... over there, atop the terrace to the west.'","Talk to Bósi in the south-western portion of Clovengap","Talk to Bróin and show him the pebble you found in the boot-print","Examine the booted footprints in the icy channel","The northern reaches of Clovengap may have become home to Hrímil Frost-heart, and Bósi wants you to investigate... carefully. He suggested you make your way through Frósthel on the left side of the Ladder-gardens to reach the frozen river-bed.","'Investigate that frozen place and keep a close eye for any clues that might shed light upon the dragon's intentions in Clovengap.'","Talk to Bróin atop the terrace to the west, in Clovengap","'Hmm. Why should the Orcs meet with the dragon? Do they hatch some plan to push the Gabil'akkâ back out of Gundabad?'","A disorganized array of booted footprints in the icy channel draws your attention","Bósi is concerned about the frozen northern reaches of Clovengap, and believes you should investigate to learn if it has become a lair for Hrímil Frost-heart.","Talk to Bróin in Clovengap","'You found the prints of Orkish boots in the snow outside the rimed passage? That tells me that Gorgar's Orcs may speak with Hrímil Frost-heart from time to time... and that is not good for the Gabil'akkâ.\
\
'But I cannot say I know the significance of this red pebble you found. It was crushed beneath an Orkish heel? Perhaps that means it is of no significance to our enemies either, and will at least pose us no danger.\
\
'I will need to think about this. And still no sign of the Black Stone Anvil!'","'Yes, my friend, this is perfect!'\
\
He catches himself abruptly and lowers his voice, looking nervously toward the rest of your party.\
\
'Thank you for agreeing to speak with me, ${PLAYER}. I do not know if you noticed, but I have become quite fond of Fastrith, and I have been trying to put together a present for her, a sign of my affection.'\
\
You assure Bróin that you had noticed, and so had everyone else, except perhaps Fastrith herself. He grumbles something that you don't quite make out.\
\
'I thought I might find one or all of the Zabad'ibîn for her, but the more we adventured in Gundabad the less likely that began to seem to me. Instead I have been trying to collect enough colourful stones with which she could finish the mosaic in Zul-mazal. Do you think she would like that? I have been picking up likely pebbles wherever I find them, and this one appears just right.'"},
[3303]={"'You have come back at just the right time, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'While you were away... my guards caught a prisoner.'","'Could you collect for me such of these pebbles as you can find, ${PLAYER}? Do not go out of your way for them, but as you complete tasks for Prince Durin and defeat the foes of the Gabil'akkâ, search their bodies for suitable colourful stones and add them to the pouch in which I collect them. It will be easy, and you will be helping not only the Gabil'akkâ but also your good friend Bróin! It is not just one excellent purpose... but two!\
\
'Thank you, my friend. I will owe you a favour for each pebble you find! Is that not worth something? I will meet you in Máttugard when you have filled the pouch with stones.'","Found a yellow stone!","Talk to Durin at Maergrind in Máttugard","'Perfect! I can tell from the heft of this pouch that you found many of the stones I sought, and indeed you have found more than any of the others who gathered pebbles for me!\
\
'Aye, I asked some others to gather colourful stones, ${PLAYER}. Did you think you were the only one? It is such a large mosaic, and so many stones are missing! But you are my favourite, and have done the best, good ${RACE}.\
\
'Perhaps you should check in with Prince Durin? There was quite a commotion a short time ago. I think something has happened.'","Durin is at Maergrind in Máttugard.","Collect black stones from enemies in Câr Bronach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect white stones from enemies in Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect red stones from enemies in Clovengap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Found a blue stone!","Collect green stones from enemies in Deepscrave (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I am not the only one who has found these pebbles to be of interest! Many of the enemies we have faced in Gundabad also seem attracted to the colourful stones, and I have noticed that some of them carry such pebbles on their persons as they travel on their various errands through every region of the caves.\
\
'Could you collect for me such of these pebbles as you can find, ${PLAYER}? Do not go out of your way for them, but as you complete tasks for Prince Durin and defeat the foes of the Gabil'akkâ, search their bodies for suitable colourful stones and add them to the pouch in which I collect them. It will be easy, and you will be helping not only the Gabil'akkâ but also your good friend Bróin! It is not just one excellent purpose... but two!\
\
'Thank you, my friend. I will owe you a favour for each pebble you find! Is that not worth something? I will meet you in Máttugard when you have filled the pouch with stones.'","Found a red stone!","Collect blue stones from enemies in Gloomingtarn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Found a green stone!","Bróin has asked you to collect any colourful stones you find from the enemies you face on behalf of the Gabil'akkâ throughout Gundabad.","Collect yellow stones from enemies in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the pouch of stones to Bróin at Maergrind in Máttugard","Found a black stone!","Chapter 8.8: A Pouch of Stones","Bróin is at Maergrind in Máttugard, eager to see how many stones you were able to find.","Found a white stone!","Bróin has noticed that the foes of the Gabil'akkâ often pick up these coloured stones scattered throughout Gundabad, and he thinks you might help him with his own goal while still helping the overall effort of his people."},
[3304]={"'Talk to Halbarad here at Echad Eregion. He can tell you more about his plan.'","'Think of this, ${PLAYER}: the line of Isildur is recognized by the heirlooms of that house: the shards of Narsil, now reforged; the Sceptre of Annúminas, long kept in Rivendell; and the Ring of Barahir, almost lost in Forochel but regained. I believe you have heard the story.\
\
'And now, this Grey Company rides to the defence of Aragorn in the southern lands, lands increasingly under the sway of the uruk. Danger crowds around us upon every side, but our own safety must be secondary to that of Aragorn. Imagine, therefore, if a member of our company is slain or taken captive by the Enemy. If that man bore a ring of the same description as the Ring of Barahir, would that not give his captor pause?\
\
'I have therefore made this proposal to Fúni Gem-cutter: to craft rings so like to the ring of Barahir, based on Candaith's description, that should any of this Company fall into the hands of the Enemy, it may sow confusion into his mind. This confusion may buy the true Heir precious time. Tell me when you are ready, and we will go with Fúni to the forges he will use.'","Talk to Halbarad in Echad Eregion","'Halbarad can tell you more, but as he said to the rest of us, \\qWhat chance is it that puts a wandering jewel-crafter right in our path at this moment?\\q He is right. It is a small chance, surely, but a happy one.\
\
'Talk to Halbarad, here at Echad Eregion, to learn more about his plan.'","Halbarad has had an idea: to equip each Ranger of the Grey Company with an imitation of the ring of Barahir, in order to confuse any servants of the Enemy in the event a Ranger is captured.","'It is done, ${PLAYER}. I hope that this was just a momentary delay that we will never have needed; but in the sad event that one of our friends is slain or captured by the Enemy, perhaps his Bebarahir will buy our chieftain Aragorn some precious seconds.\
\
'All of our struggles are for him, for the return of the heir of Isildur, the return of the king of Gondor.\
\
'We must soon be off again. Our destiny awaits us in the wide southern lands.'","Halbarad is at Echad Eregion.\
\
Halbarad is waiting to travel with you to the forges Fúni will use to craft imitation Rings of Barahir for the Grey Company.","Halbarad is at Echad Eregion, waiting to speak with you.\
\
Fúni Gem-cutter has crafted imitation rings for the Grey Company, and you should speak now with Halbarad.","Chapter 8: As Near As May Be","Talk to Halbarad at Echad Eregion","'It is time, ${PLAYER}. Fúni Gem-cutter will craft rings for every Ranger in the Company, and we will need to be on guard for any possible danger.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>","'Look at this, ${PLAYER}. Truly this is Bebarahir, so like as may be to the ring of Barahir that only very few might tell the difference.'","'Halbarad is waiting to speak with you about the plan.'","Talk to Halbarad at Echad Eregion and travel to the forges","Halbarad is at Echad Eregion.\
\
Radanir has told you of Halbarad's plan to have Fúni Gem-cutter craft an imitation ring of Barahir."},
[3305]={"'Estamos en plena retirada, ${PLAYER} -- ¡la bestia del lago es demasiado para nuestras magras armas!\
\
'Si tan solo tuviéramos alguna reliquia de los viejos tiempos, podríamos tener una oportunidad contra la criatura. Las armas de nuestros Padres eran de una fabricación más fuerte y más afilada, su arte olvidado; la habilidad de los herreros de hoy es menor.\
\
'Una caja de armas fue descubierta en una de las cuevas cerca de aquí poco después de que llegamos. Tal vez una de esas armas sea digna de ser un azote para este monstruo.'","Bósi te espera en su pequeño campamento para acompañarte a las Puertas de Durin.\
\
Los enanos de Bósi han reparado los picos, y ahora quiere que los lleves con él a los trabajadores.","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir? Dime cuándo lo estés, y caminaremos juntos a las Puertas de Durin.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ADVERTENCIA: Una vez que completes este capítulo, la Expedición se moverá a Moria, y cualquier misión de Expedición que quede en tu registro de misiones será cancelada. Si tienes alguna misión de Expedición en curso, deberías completarla ahora, ya que esas misiones ya no estarán disponibles después de completar este capítulo.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario, y no puede ser completada con una comunidad.</rgb>","Capítulo 8: Frente a las Puertas de Durin","Los enanos de la expedición de Bósi y Brogur esperan la apertura de las Puertas de Durin.","'Hazme saber cuando estés ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]}, ${PLAYER}, y caminaremos juntos a las Puertas de Durin. Con estos picos recién reparados, nuestros enanos pronto despejarán el camino hacia Moria.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ADVERTENCIA: Una vez que completes este capítulo, la Expedición se moverá a Moria, y cualquier misión de Expedición que quede en tu registro de misiones será cancelada. Si tienes alguna misión de Expedición en curso, deberías completarla ahora, ya que esas misiones ya no estarán disponibles después de completar este capítulo.</rgb>","Ráthwald se encuentra fuera del arco, cerca del campamento de Echad Dúnan, en Eregion.\
\
Los enanos se han retirado en desbandada de las Puertas de Durin, y ahora deben planear para un futuro incierto.","Habla con Bósi y viaja a las Puertas de Durin"},
[3306]={"'Deberías ir a ver a Bróin. Estoy seguro de que estará deseando contarte sus aventuras.\
\
'En este momento se está recuperando en la Senda Pacífica, un campamento que mi padre ha establecido para aquellos que deben descansar para recuperarse de las heridas recibidas en la lucha contra los orcos y otras criaturas hostiles de las minas.\
\
'La entrada a la Senda Pacífica se encuentra a lo largo del Camino de Durin, al noreste de los jardines. Allí encontrarás a Bróin recuperándose de sus pruebas.'","Bróin está vivo y se está recuperando de sus pruebas en la Senda Pacífica.","'${PLAYERNAME:Amigo[m]|Amiga[f]} , yo... gracias por haberme rescatado. Te confieso que esta no es el tipo de aventura que tenía en mente cuando llegamos a Acebeda.\
\
'Cuando la criatura del lago me atrapó frente a las Puertas de Durin, pensé que era mi última hora. Pero debe haber tenido la intención de guardar parte de sus presas para más tarde, porque me dejó dentro del tesoro acuático en las profundidades de Moria, como Oin, hace tantos años.\
\
'Encontró Zigilburk, . ¿Quién sabe cuánto tiempo lo empuñó para defenderse de la monstruosa criatura en las profundidades? Y sin embargo, al final, incluso con el hacha de mithril, no pudo escapar. Ese habría sido mi destino también, si no hubieras encontrado tu camino hacia las profundidades acuáticas y ahuyentado a la bestia.\
\
'No deseo más aventuras. No quiero canciones ni cuentos; ya he tenido suficiente.'","Bróin se está recuperando en la Senda Pacífica, un campamento que se ha establecido a lo largo del Camino de Durin, al noreste de los jardines.\
\
Bori está seguro de que Bróin querrá hablar contigo sobre sus aventuras.","Capítulo 8: La historia de Bróin","'La Senda Pacífica se encuentra a lo largo del Camino de Durin, al noreste de los jardines. Estoy seguro de que Bróin querrá hablar contigo sobre sus aventuras.'"},
[3307]={"Searched book-shelves on the upper level of Zudrugund (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'I do not know what interest Nár could have in this variety of topics, ${PLAYER}. A list of repairs at a dwarf-hold in the White Mountains, a page from Frithgeir's journal, and the story of some beast, likely more tale than true? I can think of no common thread to tie these together, just as I could not the last time we tried to make sense of the dwarf's curious behaviour.\
\
'Return to Halbarad and tell him that, for now, Zudrugund is safe from the Uruks. You should be able to find him among the huts on the western side of Lhanuch.'","Nár is in Zudrugund.\
\
You have searched the book-shelves pointed out to you by Corunir, and should speak to Nár to see if he can shed any light at all on what you found there.","Search book-shelves on the upper level of Zudrugund (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'That was quite a battle, was it not? Ah, it has been a long time since uruks dared to show their faces here! I must tell Thrór when he comes back.'","'I confess that I cannot piece together any solution to this riddle, ${PLAYER}. I see no reason for what you found on those shelves to drive Nár to distraction so. Perhaps he can shed some light, though I do not expect it.'","'I can tell you where the book-shelves that Nár spent time at before the attack are located. They are on the upper level, on the north side of the library here in Zudrugund.'","'We have had both successes and failures at Zudrugund, ${PLAYER}. We protected Nár, but he keeps his secrets safe from us! Go tell this to Halbarad, among the huts on the western side of Lhanuch.'","'I have bad news, ${PLAYER}. We have found Ergothorn. He is dead.'","Chapter 8: Further Secrets","(You found a book, of which the cover is missing, as are many of the pages, but it has been recently read and was clearly put back carelessly.)\
\
...but the beast returned that night, and the walls all around shook with the sound of its fury. The doors were barred, but the bars bent with each mighty crash of the creature's bulk, and cracks began to appear along their lengths. \\qWe must return its youngling!\\q cried Selur over the din, and he leapt forward, knocking aside the warriors that braced the door with their bodies. The first bar gone, and then the second! \\qNo, Selur!\\q they shouted, but it was too late: the third bar fell to the floor, and Selur threw open the door.\
\
Old Stonetooth was through the doorway in seconds. Selur was trampled underfoot, along with many good dwarves that spoke against the capture of Pebblewart; it availed them nothing in the end. Stonetooth thundered down the length of the hall, braying for her young. And then, an answering bleat! It drew her down side passages and steep stairways, the flagstones cracking beneath her great weight.\
\
The dwarves freed Pebblewart from his cage, and many of them ran; those that witnessed the reunion of mother and child did not survive to tell of it. But the next day, when the dwarves ventured back to those broken halls, all was empty. Old Stonetooth and Pebblewart were never seen in those caves again, and none know where they went. But it is still said today, when the earth shakes, that Pebblewart is running beneath the mountains, expressing joy at his freedom, carving great channels in the walls of the deepest caves with his golden horn.","(You have found some pages, which have been hastily torn from a larger volume -- perhaps a diary or record of events -- and seem to be only a few years old.)\
\
...surprisingly cold for March. Our friend the Ranger came by again today, and we spoke for a time about the situation in the north. His chief is on some errand to Mirkwood, but it seems to me that Túgonn knows little of it as well.\
\
Nár has been in high spirits lately; I think he likes receiving visitors, though he does not always recognize them for who they are. Still, it seems to me he enjoys the company. He does spend a great deal of time in the mine; I only accompany him occasionally, but there are only so many times I can see Thrór's Stone-house standing empty before the melancholy is too much. Nár sees it as it was, I think, so I am content to let him visit it by himself.\
\
These periods give me time to write in my book, which is fine by this dwarf. I think tomorrow I will walk down to the Coomb and see about picking more of the herbs I have read about. Perhaps I will make that brew after all. It will be nice to have Nár to talk to again.","Talk to Nár in Zudrugund","Corunir is in Zudrugund.\
\
You have spoken with Nár, but yet again he has provided very little with which you can piece together a solution.","(You found a stack of loose papers, yellowed with age, which seem to have been placed back onto the shelf randomly, with no regard for keeping them in order.)\
\
...and in the last month, a great number of the supports have fallen, giving rise to much concern among the dwarves who have stalls in Zigil-jabâl. A dozen of our stone-masons were directed to repair the supports, and trade should resume shortly.\
\
With these stone-masons went several waggons of material, chiefly unearthed stone, but also a number of fine gems: a gift to the dwarves at Kechel. We will see how hotly burn their forges, and if they can work the gem-stones into their craft as well as we are able.\
\
(Judging from the state of the next page, it is even older, and only a few words can still be read.)\
\
...time we lost one of our own to the Forbidden Halls. They should seal it away and forget it was ever delved.","'What is it? You are speaking nonsense. You should speak more clearly if you want to be understood!'","You have repelled an attack on Zudrugund by the Grishgúk uruks, but Nár's curious behaviour before the attack causes Corunir concern.","Talk to Halbarad in Lhanuch","Halbarad is among the huts on the western side of Lhanuch.\
\
You have defended Zudrugund from the uruks, and Corunir now wants you to report of your success to Halbarad.","The book-shelves that so agitated Nár are on the upper level, on the north side of the library in Zudrugund.\
\
Corunir has noted the book-shelves that Nár spent so much time at in the moments before the attack and wants you to search them for information that might be of use.","Talk to Corunir in Zudrugund","'Before the attack, Nár became very excited, and no amount of calming words from Frithgeir could settle him. He moved from shelf to shelf in a certain section of the library, and in his agitated state, I could not even get his attention!\
\
'I will point out to you the shelves. Perhaps, this time, you will find some relevant information that will help us get to the bottom of our mysterious dwarf!\
\
'The shelves are on the upper level, on the north side of the library.'"},
[3308]={"Issuriel está en Gadorgar, una sala de almacenamiento dentro de las ruinas de Ost Galadh.\
\
Debilitado por los efectos del gwigael, Issuriel tiene algo que decir sobre la misión de la Guardia Oculta.","Issuriel y los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta están ahora listos para llevar a Mazog en la siguiente etapa del viaje a Dol Guldur: una ruta peligrosa a través de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.","Capítulo 8: Mazog en la red","Habla con Achardor en Ost Galadh","Issuriel está dentro de la bodega de la Posada Embrujada, en los Troncosombríos.\
\
Ha llegado el momento de que la Guardia Oculta viaje a través de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas con Mazog. Issuriel espera tu palabra de que estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para comenzar.","'¡Siempre nos topamos con el peligro!'","Habla con Bróin en Ost Galadh","Habla con Issuriel en Ost Galadh","'¡La mayoría de estas arañas son pequeñas... No conocía a Saebereth!'","'¡Quizás deberíamos haber tomado el camino a través de Emyn Lûm! Me culpo por esto.'","'¡No puedo creer que Issuriel esté muriendo! ¡No puedo creerlo!'","Habla con Issuriel y viaja por Râd Iorist con la Guardia Oculta","'¡Si hubiera sabido de Saebereth, nunca habría recomendado este camino!'","'¡Esto no podría haber salido peor, ${PLAYER}! Esta terrible aventura habrá cobrado otra vida para el amanecer, y no estamos más cerca de lograrlo y terminar con esta misión tonta.\
\
'No me importa Mazog -- que el gwigael destroce su cuerpo hasta el final, y todos estaremos mejor -- pero la herida de Issuriel no puedo tolerarla y no lo haré.\
\
'Mataría a mil arañas si eso significara salvar a la pobre Issuriel, pero mataré a un solo orco si ella muere en este viaje de mal agüero!'","'Si tuviera la oportunidad de vivir esta misión de nuevo, no lo intentaría, ${PLAYER}. Demasiados han muerto, elfos y enanos por igual, y ese conocimiento pesa mucho sobre mis hombros.'","'Ahora que se ha tomado la decisión, mi mente está más tranquila, ${PLAYER}: nuestro camino hacia Dol Guldur pasará por las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, peligrosas aunque sean, porque solo por ese camino nuestra misión puede permanecer en secreto; y el secreto es nuestra mayor arma.\
\
'Házmelo saber cuando estés ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]} para emprender el viaje, y partiremos hacia Râd Iorist, la ruta que hemos elegido.'","'¡Tus palabras no son un bálsamo para mi ira! ¡No puedes decir nada que me haga cambiar de opinión!'","'¿Puede algo salir bien para los Malledhrim?'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir? Las Hondonadas Enmarañadas están llenas de peligros, y no será cosa fácil atravesarlas hasta el otro lado con seguridad.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse con una comunidad.</rgb>","Issuriel tose débilmente y lucha por hablar.\
\
'Yo... no... quiero que la Guardia Oculta... falle. Mazog... Mazog no puede morir.'","Bróin está en Gadorgar, una sala de almacenamiento dentro de las ruinas de Ost Galadh.\
\
Achardor está al límite de su temperamento, y se necesitará mucho para evitar que mate a Mazog en su frustración. Bróin desea razonar con él.","'¡Cuántos de mis amigos deben morir antes de que abandonemos este ridículo viaje! ¡Una plaga sobre la Guarnición de Hierro y sus cuellos rígidos!'","Achardor está en Gadorgar, una sala de almacenamiento dentro de las ruinas de Ost Galadh.\
\
El viaje a través de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas resultó desastroso: tanto Mazog como Issuriel han sido envenenados por el letal veneno gwigael. Achardor está furioso y debe ser calmado.","'No importa, ${PLAYER}. La misión ha fracasado. Incluso si ahora llegáramos a las puertas de Dol Guldur, solo tendríamos un cadáver para intercambiar. Mazog no sobrevivirá al viaje.\
\
'Nuestra oportunidad de salvar a Bori muere con Mazog. ¿La Garde secrète? ¡Ni siquiera pueden protegerse a sí mismos!'"},
[3309]={"Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Brogur te ha pedido que le lleves a Bósi noticias de la victoria de su hijo sobre Ashpar y los orcos de la Mano Blanca en Moria.","'¡Bósi se alegrará de escuchar la victoria de su hijo sobre la Mano Blanca! Regresa a la Cámara de la Encrucijada en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación, y cuéntale la gran aventura de Bori.'","Capítulo 8: El alcance de Mazog","Brogur te ha pedido que le cuentes a Bósi la victoria de su hijo sobre la Mano Blanca en Moria.","Bósi escucha atentamente mientras le cuentas la historia de la victoria de su hijo sobre Ashpar y la Mano Blanca, pero sus ojos se llenan de lágrimas cuando escucha las últimas palabras del orco. Se recompone antes de hablar, y su rostro vuelve a ser severo.\
\
'Pensaste que me traerías alegría con esta noticia de mi hijo, , y siento que no sea así. Conozco a este \\qMazog\\q del que hablas, porque es un nombre que he oído, y recientemente.\
\
'La Mano Blanca no es la mayor amenaza para los enanos dentro de Moria, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Ashpar le estaba diciendo la verdad a mi hijo. Estamos en grave peligro.'","Habla con Bósi en la Cámara de la Encrucijada","'No te preocupes por las últimas palabras de Ashpar. El orco estaba tratando de salvarse, pero era demasiado tarde para que las palabras hicieran efecto.\
\
'Desearía que mi propio hijo hubiera vivido para acompañar a Bori en esta aventura. Había honor suficiente para todos, y le habría hecho bien a Bróin ser parte de una victoria así.\
\
'Deberías llevarle a mi primo Bósi noticias de los valientes éxitos de su hijo contra la Mano Blanca. ¡Quizás eso lo anime un poco!'"},
[3310]={"'Magor nos contó todo, ${PLAYER}, y se ha puesto en camino de regreso a Lothlórien para informar a la Dama Galadriel de lo que ha sucedido.\
\
'¡Tus hazañas son realmente increíbles, amigo mío! No solo has rescatado a Magor, sino que también has frustrado los planes no solo de los orcos, sino, lo que es más importante, de Gorothúl de Dol Guldur también.\
\
'Eres completamente extraordinario. Tienes el mayor elogio de Magor, y el mío propio.'","'Dithaliwenn encontró una piedra élfica, muy parecida a las que te di antes, cerca de la boca de la cueva de Azanarukâr, de la que emanaba un hedor vil. No fuiste tú quien colocó esta piedra, ${PLAYER}. ¡Debe haber sido Magor! Pero ¿por qué habría dejado la piedra en lugar de regresar al campamento él mismo?\
\
'Creo que la cueva que encontró Magor debe ser la fuente del gran mal que la Dama Galadriel percibió bajo Moria, ${PLAYER}. Si puedes rescatar a Magor de sus garras, puede que nos pueda contar algo sobre su poder.\
\
'Reúne tu coraje, camarada. Sea lo que sea esta nueva maldad, si pudo vencer a un gran elfo como Magor en combate, debe ser realmente peligrosa.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: La inspiración te ayudará si decides emprender este desafío. Esta instancia solo se puede completar en solitario o en grupo de dos personas.</rgb>","Dithaliwenn ha encontrado una pista sobre el paradero del elfo perdido Magor cerca de Azanarukâr, y Lenglammel quiere que lo encuentres.","Habla con Lenglammel y ve a Azanarukâr","Lenglammel se encuentra en su campamento de Gwathrendath, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Has ganado una gran victoria en las profundidades bajo Moria, y deberías hablar ahora con Lenglammel.","Capítulo 8: Nueva Diablería","Lenglammel se encuentra en su campamento de Gwathrendath, entre las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Lenglammel quiere que hables con ella sobre tu viaje a Azanarukâr en busca de Magor y el misterioso mal que habita allí.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: La inspiración te ayudará si decides emprender este desafío. Esta instancia solo se puede completar en solitario o en grupo de dos personas.</rgb>","'Ve con coraje, ${PLAYER}, a las profundidades en busca de Magor. Él puede ser capaz de contarnos algo sobre el gran mal que la Dama Galadriel ha sentido en las profundidades.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: La inspiración te ayudará si decides emprender este desafío. Esta instancia solo se puede completar en solitario o en grupo de dos personas.</rgb>"},
[3311]={"Corunir is at Aughaire, the settlement of the Trev Gallorg, in Angmar.\
\
You have rescued Golodir from the depths of Nûrz Ghâshu and should speak now with Corunir, your ally on that journey.","'You should travel now into Angmar to tell the Rangers Corunir and Golodir of the Grey Company's journey.'\
\
Lothrandir listens as you briefly tell him the reasons Elrond felt Golodir should not be troubled with the errand.\
\
'I see. I do not agree, but if that is the will of Elrond, there is little enough I could say to dispute it. Corunir, then, should be told of the Grey Company's mission. You will find him at Aughaire, the settlement of the Trev Gallorg in Angmar.'","'We must travel into the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu if we are to rescue Golodir!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Duo, Small Fellowship, or Fellowship group sizes by using the Skirmish Join Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 65.\
\
If this is your first Skirmish, you should visit one of the Skirmish Camps found throughout Middle-earth and speak with a Skirmish Captain to properly train. Skirmish Camps can be found in the following regions: Ered Luin, Bree-land, the Shire, the Lone-lands, the North Downs, the Trollshaws, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria, and Lothlórien.</rgb>","Capítulo 8: Las profundidades del deber","'You will find Corunir at Aughaire, the settlement of the Trev Gallorg in Angmar.'","Completa la escaramuza: Rescate en Nûrz Ghâshu","Habla con Corunir en Aughaire","The Ranger Corunir is at Aughaire, the settlement of the Trev Gallorg in Angmar.\
\
You must go with Corunir into danger if Golodir is to be rescued.","'${PLAYER}! You have come just in time, for I do not know what I would do if you had not arrived! Golodir, my captain...he is in grave peril!\
\
'The death of his daughter, Lorniel, brought him to the very brink of despair, but I thought his triumph over the False King would bring him the peace he sought. For a time it seemed it did, but lately he has lapsed into such a pit of grief that he seems not to know even we his friends. His sorrow fuels his anger at the remnants of Angmar, and he goes alone into even the most dangerous strongholds of evil. The False King is gone, but not even Golodir can long stand against the servants that still remain in many of those places!\
\
'But he has gone too far this time, ${PLAYER}, and I do not know what to do. I need your help, for in his grief and rage I fear that Golodir is blinded to the danger, and where he goes there can be no return. He travels alone into the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu, ${PLAYER}! We must rescue him!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Duo, Small Fellowship, or Fellowship group sizes by using the Skirmish Join Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 60.\
\
If this is your first Skirmish, you should visit one of the Skirmish Camps found throughout Middle-earth and speak with a Skirmish Captain to properly train. Skirmish Camps can be found in the following regions: Ered Luin, Bree-land, the Shire, the Lone-lands, the North Downs, the Trollshaws, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria, and Lothlórien.</rgb>","The Ranger Corunir is at Aughaire, the settlement of the Trev Gallorg in Angmar.\
\
Lothrandir has told you where you might find Corunir, that he may be called to the muster of the Grey Company.","'You have my deepest thanks, ${PLAYER}, for aiding me in the rescue of Golodir from the very depths of Nûrz Ghâshu. He must have drawn the notice of Erebún during one of his excursions into the cities of Angmar following the defeat of the False King. Who knows what would have happened if the rogmul had maintained his dominance?\
\
'We can be glad that did not happen, ${PLAYER}. I think it is best for Golodir to come with us as part of the Grey Company. It is not healthy for him to remain in this land, as marked with grief as it must be for him. The wide southern lands will do him good, I am sure of it.\
\
'He will be kept busy, as we all will be, and I believe that to be the best means of rising above grief, as he must and will. Thank you again, my friend.'","Lothrandir has sent you to speak with Corunir, a Ranger who has lived for many years in the settlement of Aughaire, in Angmar."},
[3312]={"Chapter 8: The Dreadful Dourhands","Talk to Prince Ingór","You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to the Zhélruka and to fight on their behalf in Gundabad.","'Remember to be friendly with those Dourhands. I do not want any unpleasant incidents in this hall, ${PLAYER}. Be careful.'","'${PLAYER}, a group of Dourhands has come to Vérnozal. We could not send them elsewhere, as it is now the way of the Zhélruka to be kind to all dwarves in Gundabad. I ask you to cater to them, as much as is advisable, but also to keep an eye upon them. I do not entirely trust these newcomers.'","Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.\
\
Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.","'Good riddance to those Dourhands. They certainly overstayed their welcome! I believe everyone was glad to see them off. The Hall of Vérnozal is not a filthy inn, suitable only for drunken revelry, but a great beacon of Gundabad reclaimed!'"},
[3313]={"La entrada a Zurr-thurkh, el camino secreto, se encuentra en las profundidades de Buzun-ghâr, donde luchaste contra Grawulun el Caerog.\
\
Orvar ha aceptado encontrarse contigo dentro de Zurr-thurkh, si puedes encontrar la entrada, para montar el rescate de Bori de las garras de Mazog.","'¿Ves el bien que se puede lograr cuando elfos y enanos trabajan juntos, ${PLAYER}? ¡Mazog tenía razón en temer la alianza y esperar que nunca ocurriera!\
\
El enano Bróin llegó a Lossathrod, jadeando tras una larga carrera, y pidió que lo acompañáramos en su búsqueda de ti. Dijo que cometió un error al dejarte intentar el rescate de su pariente solo con Orvar, y su arrepentimiento lo impulsó a seguir adelante. ¡Tuviste suerte de que recuperara el valor cuando lo hizo, ${PLAYER}, tú y Orvar!'","Corunothiel está en Lossathrod, el campamento en Buzun-ghâr.\
\
Has salido de Rushdurinul victorioso sobre Mazog, pero has recibido la desafortunada noticia de que Bori y los otros cautivos han sido enviados a Dol Guldur con Gorothúl. Corunothiel espera para hablar contigo.","'Si puedes encontrar la entrada a Zurr-thurkh en las profundidades de Buzun-ghâr, cerca de donde luchaste contra Grawulun el Caerog, te esperaré al otro lado. ¡Entonces veremos si podemos rescatar a Bori de las garras de Mazog!'","Encuentra la entrada a Zurr-thurkh y úsala para llegar detrás de los muros de Zabadgathol","Capítulo 8: El Camino Secreto","'¿Dices que hay un camino detrás de los muros de Zabadgathol, hacia Rushdurinul, donde Mazog ha puesto su trono? No lo sé, ${PLAYER} -- me parece poco probable.'\
\
Con una ceja levantada, Orvar escucha tu explicación sobre la idea de Bróin de que podría ser posible rescatar a Bori.\
\
'Todo esto está muy bien, pero ¿por qué Bróin no viene contigo en esta tarea, ${PLAYER}? Si me preguntas, aún no supera su experiencia en la guarida acuática del Vigilante. Me parece que el señor Brogur ha intentado darle tareas triviales a su hijo para sacarlo de su melancolía, pero aún no ha funcionado. Bróin no será él mismo hasta que logre vencer el miedo que lo atenaza.\
\
No importa. Si desciendes una vez más a las profundidades de Buzun-ghâr, donde enfrentaste a Grawulun el Caerog, y puedes encontrar la entrada a Zurr-thurkh, te acompañaré al otro lado.''","Has encontrado los planos de un túnel secreto de escape desde la sala del trono de Durin. Si alguna vez fue construido, podría usarse para entrar en secreto a Zabadgathol y rescatar a Bori.","¿Cuántos destinos debieron entrelazarse para que la Guarnición de Hierro abriera la entrada a Buzun-ghâr justo cuando la necesitamos, ${PLAYER}? Si el \\qcamino secreto\\q fue construido, ¡encontrarás la entrada en lo profundo de Buzun-ghâr! ¡Debe ser una señal que haya ocurrido hoy, de todos los días!\
\
Bróin de repente no puede mirarte a los ojos.\
\
'Ojalá pudiera acompañarte por el \\qcamino secreto\\q y rescatar a Bori, ${PLAYER}, pero aún hay mucho por hacer y... bueno, me necesitan aquí. Lucharemos juntos en la próxima aventura, lo juro.\
\
Regresa a Buzun-ghâr, al suroeste de aquí, en la esquina sureste de Tharâkh Bazân, y habla con Orvar Martillo de Campana. Él te acompañará por Zurr-thurkh, si existe, aunque debe ser tu único compañero, por motivos de secreto.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse en grupo.</rgb>","Orvar Martillo de Campana está en Buzun-ghâr, al suroeste de la Senda Pacífica, en la esquina más al sureste de Tharâkh Bazân, por el Camino de Durin.\
\
Bróin te ha pedido que hables con el enano Orvar para que te acompañe por el camino secreto hacia Rushdurinul.","'Me necesitan aquí, ${PLAYER}... hay mucho por hacer. Juro que te acompañaré en la próxima aventura.\
\
Regresa con Orvar a Buzun-ghâr, en la esquina sureste de Tharâkh Bazân, al suroeste de aquí por el Camino de Durin, y pídele que te acompañe por el \\qcamino secreto.\\q ¡Aún puedes rescatar a mi primo Bori de las garras de Mazog!'"},
[3314]={"Animados por su éxito en las minas, muchos de los enanos han seguido a Brogur más al este, hacia la Sala Vigesimoprimera.","Brogur está en la Cámara de Liderazgo, una pequeña sala junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera en Zelem-melek.\
\
Brogur ha llevado a una compañía de enanos más al este en Moria, y ha establecido una nueva base de operaciones en la Cámara de Liderazgo, junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera.","'¡Bienvenido a la Cámara de Liderazgo, ${PLAYER}! Desde aquí guiaré a mi pueblo hacia una gloria aún mayor en Moria!'","Capítulo 8: La Sala Vigesimoprimera","'Brogur estará en la Cámara de Liderazgo, una pequeña sala junto a la Sala Vigesimoprimera en Zelem-melek.'","'Ya hemos tenido grandes éxitos aquí en Moria, ${PLAYER}, y Brogur se ha ido hacia el este con muchos de los nuestros buscando la sala Vigesimoprimera y las casas reales de Durin.\
\
'Me preocupa esta prisa. Sí, hemos logrado una gran victoria con el descubrimiento del Corazón de Fuego, pero temo que Brogur avance demasiado y se meta en problemas.\
\
'Viaja a la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la sala vigesimoprimera en Zelem-melek y advierte a mi primo contra este movimiento.'"},
[3315]={"Act naturally!","Daxamat stands within the entryway of Dâr Laja.","Enter the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja in the Upper Ward","Jajax is keeping an eye on the coffer containing suggestions for those who might join the leadership of the Kindred of the Coins, and he would like you to do the same.","Daxamat told you his brother Jajax has gone to speak with the Kindred in the main hall of Dâr Laja.","Examine the suggestions coffer at the foot of Hármelak's dais in Dâr Laja","'Take a closer look at that coffer, my good and subtle friend. Tell me if you notice any weaknesses I might exploit... for the good of the city, of course. My heart weeps that the folk of Umbar Baharbêl have been deprived of my presence for so long, and I aim to make up for those lost years!'","Daxamat nods to you in greeting","'Welcome to the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, where the Kindred of the Coins hear the voice of the people and act upon their concerns! Keep your weapons sheathed, speak with a civil tongue, and there will be no cause for trouble.'\
\
Jaith smiles broadly as he notices you for the first time.\
\
'${PLAYER}! It is good to see you! So many folk have passed through these doors that I confess I did not recognize you immediately, but that is now rectified. The Golden Queen has proven true to her word, and I see she made her choice of helper with wisdom! I did not think Dâr Laja would ever be opened again, and it would be my lot to guard a locked door for all the years of my life. But no! Even now the sound of agreeable conversation drifts from within!\
\
'You may pass inside, ${PLAYER}. I will not forget how you helped Lady Hármelak reopen the Meeting-hall, my friend. What a fine day this has become!'","Vigilant guards keep a watchful eye on the suggestions coffer inside Dâr Laja.","'I am pleased for you to see your handiwork, ${PLAYER}. Yes, it was my resolve to open the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, but it was you who recovered the keys from the Heirsworn and made my decision both safe and possible. I am grateful for it, and will not forget what you have done. You will come to see that we of Umbar Baharbêl have very long memories, if you have not learned it already.'\
\
Hármelak smiles sweetly.\
\
'Yes, ${PLAYER}, it is good that you have come, for there is a small matter about which we must speak. We have begun taking suggestions from the folk of the city to learn who they would have replace Azagath and Nakási in our ranks, but there is one other about whom we must speak. We must speak of Tatháta, ${PLAYER}. She remains Kinswoman of the Lower Ward, unless you have something to tell me that concerns her?'","Hármelak has called for you to speak with her in the main hall of Dâr Laja.","'It is good to see you, ${PLAYER}. My brother has gone ahead to the main hall, but I wanted to wait for you. It has been a strange morning.\
\
'Heralds sent by the Kindred travelled through the city, announcing that Dâr Laja would once again be opened. During the rule of the Heirs or the domination of Ordakh such a thing was considered impossible, and when the Kindred came to power the folk of the city believed it to remain so. And yet here we stand, within the great Meeting-hall of Umbar Baharbêl, and the Kindred of the Coins has come to listen to the wants and needs of their people. Rothog the Storm walked not three strides from me when he came inside, but his khopeshes remained strapped to his back, and he gave no indication that he might eat anybody! That is progress, is it not?\
\
'I cannot help but think that it was your arrival on these shores that set the city upon this course, ${PLAYER}. I thank you again, as I have before, for making me a part of your crew.\
\
'My brother is in the main hall of Dâr Laja, to the north-east. He will be pleased to see you as well, though he may not say so. You know how he is, of course.'","Talk to Jajax in the main hall of Dâr Laja","Talk to Hármelak in the main hall of Dâr Laja","The Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl has now been opened to the people of the city so they may bring their concerns before the Kindred of the Coins.","'This may not be easy, ${PLAYER}... but do they not say it is the hard thing that brings the greatest wealth and power?\
\
'Folk have come from all over the city to bring their concerns before the leaders of the Kindred, but that is of no account to me. I am more interested in the guarded coffer that stands at the foot of Hármelak's dais, for that is where folk are bringing their suggestions as to what worthy persons should succeed the members of the Kindred who fled the city. The guards are vigilant, yes, but if I can put my name into the coffer many times, it may be that Jajax will become Kinsman of the Citadel, or of the Sail-haven! Azagath and Nakási are not likely to return, after all, and their districts cannot remain leaderless for long. Imagine how much wealth and power I might wield as a member of the Kindred of the Coins, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Take a closer look at that coffer, my good and subtle friend. Tell me if you notice any weaknesses I might exploit... for the good of the city, of course. My heart weeps that the folk of Umbar Baharbêl have been deprived of my presence for so long, and I aim to make up for those lost years!'","The Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja has been opened at the command of the Kindred of the Coins, and a new dawn rises in Umbar.","Talk to Daxamat in the entryway of Dâr Laja","Hármelak, the Golden Queen, calls for you to attend her","'You may pass inside, ${PLAYER}. I will not forget how you helped Lady Hármelak reopen the Meeting-hall, my friend. What a fine day this has become!'","Vigilant guards stand by the coffer, ensuring the rules are followed","'My brother is in the main hall of Dâr Laja, to the north-east. He will be pleased to see you as well, though he may not say so. You know how he is, of course.'","Chapter 9.1: A New Dawn for Umbar"},
[3316]={"Trausti stands south-east of the fortress of Shakhajât, pleased to have retrieved his axe.","Talk to Durin north of Maergrind in Máttugard","'Our captive is a goblin of Gundabad. The guards caught him creeping in the shadows near the Steepset, no doubt on an errand of evil for Gorgar. He would have been slain out of hand if he had not been recognized, but that recognition will only stay the executioner's axe for a short while.\
\
'They have him in a cage north of Maergrind, down one level. Speak to those who watch him, and perhaps he will tell us something of use. We have no need for goblins, but our need is even less if they can tell us nothing.'","'I know this goblin, ${PLAYER}. Do you remember when Stáli the Hewer sent me into Deepscrave in search of the Zabad'ibîn, and I was captured by the Orcs? This goblin was my jailor! He it was that kept the hobgoblins from killing me! And then you and Trausti freed me from that place.\
\
'The guards were not happy, but I convinced them he seemed a figure of importance. They have jailed him, for now, but they are not happy about it! In truth I am not sure myself. Is this some trick?'","'They have our goblin prisoner in a cage north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard. Speak to those who watch him, and perhaps he will tell us something of use. We have no need for goblins, but our need is even less if they can tell us nothing.'","The goblin Glúrkub has given you information concerning the hobgoblin who took Trausti's axe, but can he be trusted? According to Glúrkub, the hobgoblin can be found living in a dwelling south-east of the fortress of Shakhajât.","'What was wrong has been set right, though it took a goblin's help! What would Lofrík say to that, I wonder? He would say that a bad deed is not entirely undone by a good one! Let us bear that in mind when we return to the prisoner.'","'Hobgoblin who took the axe very mean, very nasty, bad sort. But Glúrkub knows where he lives! In Shakhajât, that's the place. Knock on his door south-east of the fortress, and when he answers, take the axe right from him!'","'Shakhajât, he said? Let us go knock on the doors, ${PLAYER}, and woe to the hobgoblin that answers!'","'That was no ordinary axe, ${PLAYER}, and this goblin is responsible for its theft! He should die for its loss.'","'Eskil prevailed upon the guards to spare this goblin's life, for now, but I am less forgiving. One of his friends made off with my favourite axe, the one bearing Lofrík's golden tooth, and the loss of that precious memento has me inclined to take this goblin's head in payment!'","Shoshraf emerges from the house, ready to fight!","Eskil and Trausti are keeping watch over the captive goblin north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.","Talk to the goblin Glúrkub north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard","'This goblin kept me captive in Vatug-ronk, but he also kept his friends from visiting death upon me. Why would he creep so near to the Gabil'akkâ?'","Talk to Trausti north of Maergrind","Summon and defeat the hobgoblin Shoshraf in Shakhajât","Shoshraf has barely hit the ground before Trausti wrests the axe from his hand","'It was just as I said, wasn't it? Yes, it was, I can tell! Glúrkub will be so very helpful to you, as long as you keep him safe.\
\
'Yes, safe! Safe from both dwarves and Orcs! Do you agree? Think about it? Think about it. And then I will tell you my tale.'","Talk to Glúrkub, the captive goblin north of Maergrind","'Our prisoner may mix truths in with falsehoods to mislead us.'","Trausti is keeping watch over the captive goblin north of Maergrind.","The goblin Glúrkub is encaged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.","Talk to the dwarves who watch the goblin-prisoner (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Do you suspect a trap, as I do? Good ${RACE}! We will see about this hobgoblin, but if the captive has lied to us, we will come back at once and separate his head from his shoulders!\
\
'Shakhajât, he said? Let us go knock on the doors, ${PLAYER}, and woe to the hobgoblin that answers!'","Talk to Trausti in Shakhajât","Durin is keeping an eye on the captive goblin north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.","'By Durin's Beard, he was telling the truth! It feels good to have my axe back in hand, ${PLAYER}, for once again I feel that Lofrík is with me, though he died outside Moria. What was wrong has been set right, though it took a goblin's help! What would Lofrík say to that, I wonder?\
\
'He would say that a bad deed is not entirely undone by a good one, ${PLAYER}. Let us bear that in mind when we return to the prisoner.'","'Trausti has his axe again? That is good, ${PLAYER}, but I caution you and any others who speak to the prisoner not to trust everything he says. He may mix truths in with falsehoods in order to mislead us... indeed, I would expect nothing else.\
\
'And yet, if we bear that in mind he may provide the Gabil'akkâ with useful information. Ask him where he came from, and why he was creeping around near the Steepset.'","The Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ have caught a goblin sneaking around Máttugard, and now he is their prisoner.","'The axe! The axe! I knew it was important, I did! Something special about it? Glúrkub knows where it is! Maybe let him free if you find it?\
\
'Hobgoblin who took the axe very mean, very nasty, bad sort. But Glúrkub knows where he lives! In Shakhajât, that's the place. Knock on his door south-east of the fortress proper! And when Shoshraf answers, take the axe right from him!\
\
'Then you'll know Glúrkub is a very helpful goblin, and you'll set him free? Ah, we'll talk when you get back, yes we will. Think about it? You'll think about it.'","Chapter 9.1: The Jailor Jailed","The goblin Glúrkub has been imprisoned by the Gabil'akkâ."},
[3318]={"'I will stay here and rest my injured leg. But my thirst for vengeance will not sleep!'","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I know how difficult it is to sit out a battle, for it has happened to me! I know this too: Vútro has made the right decision. Once his leg has healed, he will once again be the swiftest scout in the Grey Mountains, I do not doubt it!\
\
'If you wish to join Hórin's raiding party, now is the time, my friend. I will await your return from the Anvil of Winterstith, and may it be in victory!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>If you wish to participate in the raid, this is when the 'Anvil of Winterstith' raid takes place during the story. If you do not wish to complete the Anvil raid, you will be told what happened there when Hórin's band returns to Skarháld.</rgb>","Inek has commanded that Hórin lead an expedition to the Anvil of Winterstith in pursuit of Karazgar, and he invited you to join the raiding party.","Talk to Vútro the West-wind in Skarháld","'Vútro the West-wind, who ran afoul of Karazgar not so long ago, desires to accompany Hórin's band on this raid. Hórin refused on account of his injury, but rumour has it that Vútro plans to follow them in secret. His leg is injured, and at best he will slow down the group. At worst he will endanger not only himself but the entire band! Convince him not to follow them to the Anvil, ${PLAYER}. I know he wants vengeance on Karazgar, but with this injury he will be more hindrance than help. He is to the south-east and down two levels, among the tents of the Zhélruka.'","Chapter 9.2: An Expedition to the Anvil","Durin is on the upper level of Skarháld.","Vútro has reluctantly agreed to stay behind","Vútro the West-wind is south-east of Durin and down two levels, among the tents of the Zhélruka in Skarháld.","'Now, on to other matters. At Inek's command, Hórin has assembled a raiding band to hunt for Karazgar at the Anvil of Winterstith. I will not attempt to stop you, for I know you are a ${CLASS} of great skill and do not fear such a challenge, but not everyone is as capable as you! I have learned that Vútro the West-wind, the scout that ran afoul of Karazgar not so long ago, desires to accompany Hórin's band on this raid. Hórin refused on account of his injury, but rumour has it that Vútro plans to follow them in secret.\
\
'His leg is injured, and at best he will slow down the group. At worst he will endanger not only himself but the entire band! Convince him not to follow them to the Anvil, ${PLAYER}. I know he wants vengeance on Karazgar, but with this injury he will be more hindrance than help. He is to the south-west of here, down two levels, among the tents of the Zhélruka.'","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld","'I know why you're here, ${PLAYER}, and I will save you the effort of telling me not to follow Hórin's band to the Anvil. I know what the others are saying: they think my injury will make me a burden. To them I say this:\
\
'Karazgar did this to me! I was a scout, the swiftest Zhélruka in all these mountains, and with one slice of his cruel blades he robbed me of my greatest ability! For that I desire vengeance! I will stay behind when the others go to the Anvil in pursuit of Karazgar, ${PLAYER}, but I want you to promise me something. If Hórin's band is not able to slay Karazgar, if the Weeping Warrior manages to outsmart them at the Anvil of Winterstith, I want you to help me achieve my vengeance.\
\
'So I will stay here and rest my injured leg. But my thirst for vengeance will not sleep!'"},
[3319]={"'Khôltekh delayed in relating this information to me, for reasons of his own. Learn what they may be, keep me informed of them, and tell me too of Tatháta's fate. We are allies now, ${PLAYER}, if perhaps not friends, and this matter concerns us both.'","Chapter 9.2: Tatháta Unaccounted","The Temámir guard asks you for the password","Talk to Birûk in Mekab-kuphâr","'I thought you might come to speak to me, friend. I have heard you were among the last to see Kinswoman Tatháta in life, and the others of my order are most interested to learn where she has gone in the days since. Did she follow Nakási and Azagath when the two of them fled? No one seems to know.\
\
'I can see you have an interest in this question as well! If so, then my resources are yours to command. Tatháta was last seen in Umbar-môkh, the tunnels beneath the city, and it happens that my people control a guarded entrance to those passages. With my password they will welcome you, and lend you the aid you might require.\
\
'Speak these words to the dwarves inside the southern entrance to Khabârkhad, and they will let you pass: Ijebad-nê!\
\
'You will need to leave Dâr Laja and travel south into the Fleet-fast to reach the entrance to Umbar-môkh where my people stand sentry. Pick up Tatháta's trail and you will be aiding both the Kindred of the Coins and yourself, ${PLAYER}. After all, you were among the last to see her alive.'","Mûluget is waiting for you to speak the phrase Khôltekh gave to you.","Khôltekh told you to go inside the southern entrance to Khabârkhad, where his folk guard an entrance to Umbar-môkh, the caverns and passages beneath Umbar Baharbêl.","'Word has begun to spread among the people that Azagath fled from the city, and while the details vary, in most of these stories both Tumúldo Fierce-water and Nakási Wave-reaper followed him. You and I know the truth of that, but it is best that the people not yet know. Of Tatháta no tales tell, but she has not been seen in some time.\
\
'Did I say \\qno tale?\\q This is not the truth complete, ${PLAYER}. Kinsman Khôltekh has spies everywhere, and this morning he related to me that some days ago one of these spies observed Tatháta engaged in combat with an Umbari woman he did not recognize. There was another who stood by, ${PLAYER}, and that other was you.'\
\
Hármelak raises her hand to silence you as you begin speaking.\
\
'I know the circumstances that brought you to our city... and I know too that Khôltekh delayed in relating this information to me, for reasons of his own. Learn what these reasons may be, keep me informed of them, and discover what you can of Tatháta's fate. We are allies now, ${PLAYER}, if perhaps not friends, and this matter concerns us both.'","Khôltekh will wish to speak with you in Dâr Laja.","Although the leaders of the Kindred of the Coins possess renewed optimism for the future of their city, questions remain about their missing kinswoman Tatháta.","Speak the password to Ayâl through the doors and down the corridor to the north-west","Find the entrance to Umbar-môkh that Khôltekh suggested","'Yes, yes, you gave me the password already. I am satisfied.\
\
'Continue on to Mekab-kuphâr to the north-west and you will find an able helper there. His name is Birûk, and he drew the dull stone for the day; that means it will be his duty to provide any of the help you will require. This is the command of Khôltekh, and therefore it is a command to follow.'","Tekûl stares impassively at you but grunts that you may pass his door","Mûluget nods and permits you to pass","Birûk has been assigned the task of helping you while you are within Umbar-môkh. You will find him to the north-west in Mekab-kuphâr.","Speak the password to Tekûl down the stairs","Tekûl is further ahead and down the stairs, waiting for you to speak the phrase Khôltekh gave to you.","'Speak these words to my dwarves inside the southern entrance to Khabârkhad, and they will let you pass: Ijebad-nê!\
\
'You will need to leave Dâr Laja and travel south into the Fleet-fast to reach the entrance to Umbar-môkh where my people stand sentry. Pick up Tatháta's trail and you will be aiding both the Kindred of the Coins and yourself, ${PLAYER}. After all, you were among the last to see her alive.'","Speak the password to Mûluget","Talk to Khôltekh in the main hall of Dâr Laja","'Is that so? Well, I am not one to speak against Khôltekh. If he has allowed you to use this entrance, I will not risk my neck to stop you!\
\
'There are other entrances to Umbar-môkh from the city above, but this one was given to the Temámir to guard, and we take this duty most seriously. Continue north-west to Mekab-kuphâr and you will find an able helper there. His name is Birûk, and he drew the dull stone for the day; that means it will be his obligation to provide any of the help you will require. This is the command of Khôltekh, and therefore it is a command to follow.'","Ayâl is beyond the doors and down the hall to the north-west, waiting for you to speak the phrase Khôltekh gave to you.","'Ah, you are newly-arrived to this guard-post of the Temámir? And at Khôltekh's command, no less?'\
\
Birûk sighs heavily.\
\
'I should have inspected the other stones and proven to myself they were truly shinier than the one I drew... but it cannot be helped for today. It is my duty to aid you. What brings you to Umbar-môkh?'"},
[3320]={"Prince Durin is furious, enraged with Glúrkub's story.","Chapter 9.2: The Divided Loyalties of Glúrkub the Goblin","Talk to the prisoner and experience 'The Divided Loyalties of Glúrkub the Goblin'","The goblin Glúrkub has a tale to tell, but whether or not he can be trusted is up to you and to the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ.","'I swear it is all true!'","The goblin Glúrkub wants to tell you his side of the story. He is caged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.","'That is my tale, and every word of it is true. Every word! Now you trust Glúrkub? Now you let him go?'","Durin seethes with anger","Glúrkub is caged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.","Talk to Durin by the cage","'The lies of this goblin cannot be believed!'\
\
Durin's face is a thundercloud. He is angrier than you have ever seen him.\
\
'I have not been controlled by the voice of Hrímil Frost-heart! I am no dragon's puppet!'","Talk to Glúrkub","'My story begins before your army came to Urbhármok, before this war of the dwarves. Hear it now, and know Glúrkub not to blame. Glúrkub just doing his best.'","'My tale is a long one, yes, long and sad. But you will hear it, yes? You will see it? Put yourself in my shoes, walk around and see from my side?\
\
'Maybe then you will know Glúrkub tells the truth, and Glúrkub can be trusted?\
\
'Maybe then you let me go?'"},
[3321]={"Collect old jewellery from the fingers of wights at Sektakhâb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find the axe that was misplaced somewhere at Sektakhâb","Collected old jewellery from Sektakhâb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Temámir dwarf Birûk has been volunteered to help you discover what happened to Tatháta.","Defeated wights at Sektakhâb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Corudan at Mekab-kuphâr","Because the axe does not fit inside the collection box, you should just lean it against the wall by the notice board.","Defeat decayed arms at Sektakhâb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","This must be the axe you learned about from the notice board","'I will ask around. But I should warn you. One thing is true beneath the city as it is in the streets above: there is a price for every question answered. If the Temámir of Mekab-kuphâr are to help you locate your missing woman, you should do what you can to help them in return: consult the notice board to the south-west to see what we need done, and perhaps you will accomplish some of those tasks for us while I ask your questions for you. It is only fair, is it not? In Umbar-môkh it is very important for things to be fair.'","Chapter 9.3: A Price for Every Answer","Deliver the old jewellery and the axe to the collection box at Mekab-kuphâr","Defeat wights at Sektakhâb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You will help us with some of the tasks posted on the notice board? Very good! While you are away at Sektakhâb, I will ask around and see what there is to learn of Tatháta's whereabouts.'","Birûk told you to examine the notice board to the south-west in Mekab-kuphâr to see how you can busy yourself while he seeks information concerning Tatháta's whereabouts.","Wights stalk the halls of Sektakhâb. Facing them may impress the Temámir","Corudan and Sigileth have arrived at Mekab-kuphâr.","Examine the notice board to the south-west in Mekab-kuphâr","'You should finish these tasks before we speak. It is only right.'","You deposit the old jewellery into the box, but the axe does not fit","Lean the axe against the wall by the notice board","Dealing with the wights at Sektakhâb, located to the west of Mekab-kuphâr, may encourage the Temámir to help you.","'You seek to learn where Tatháta the Sea-beast has gone? I have not seen her for quite some time. Are you certain she remains somewhere within Umbar-môkh? She is the Kinswoman of the Lower Ward, and you will usually see her striding through the streets, her two great hounds by her side.'\
\
You tell Birûk that Tatháta was last seen within a hidden harbour beneath the city, and none have marked her passage in the days since.\
\
'Well, I will ask around. But I should warn you. One thing is true beneath the city as it is in the streets above: there is a price for every question answered. If the Temámir of Mekab-kuphâr are to help you locate your missing woman, you should do what you can to help them in return: consult the notice board across the way to the south-west to see what we need done, and perhaps you will accomplish some of those tasks for us while I ask your questions for you. It is only fair, is it not? In Umbar-môkh it is very important for things to be fair.'","The notice board directed you to leave the things you recovered from Sektakhâb in the box back at Mekab-kuphâr.","<rgb=#FFFF00>The Dead That Walk</rgb>\
The bodies of the slain and interred remain not at rest, but are animated by spirits of evil and must be made still. Many can be found at Sektakhâb to the west.\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Arms Loosed From Their Bodies</rgb>\
Of great danger to the unwary, grasping arms crawl along by their fingertips and are not to be underestimated. Look for them among the crypts at Sektakhâb to the west.\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00>My Misplaced Axe</rgb>\
I lost my axe at Sektakhâb! Its edge has been dulled due to much use, but it is still of great sentimental value to me and I would have it returned. Leave it in the collection box if you bring it back, because I have business outside the city for several weeks and will not be back for some time.\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Valuable Trinkets and Jewelleries</rgb>\
It may be distasteful to some, but the valuables worn by the Dead at Sektakhâb are of no use to them, and might be of great use for the Temámir. Any concerns may be brought directly to Khôltekh, but the valuables should be left in the collection box.","Defeated decayed arms at Sektakhâb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You did not think we would leave you to search these caves by yourself, did you, ${PLAYER}?'","As you lean the axe against the wall, you feel eyes upon you"},
[3322]={"Durin has ordered you to kill the goblin prisoner.","'It cannot be true. It cannot.'\
\
Durin breathes heavily, studying the faces of the dwarves nearby, his brow creased in thought.\
\
'Gorgar asked \\qare you the same as I am?\\q What did he mean by that? What did he see? Did he recognize some compulsion in me, a compulsion he shares? Have we both been ensnared by the Dragon's voice?'","After a brief moment, Glúrkub speaks up: a thoughtful squeak","'It is true: when Hrímil says \\qtime to jump,\\q Gorgar says \\qhow high you want?\\q But maybe she not trust her power over him. She summons Gorgar not to her lair, but to another place, called Lugroz by the Orcs.\
\
'When he go see her, she make him leave fancy hammer behind. She scared of it, for some reason. Glúrkub not know why: hammer small, but Dragon very big! But she not like it. He leave it on weapon-rack near path to the summit, and when he done meeting with her he come down mountain and take it back. Any who dare touch it would die by Gorgar's hand, but none have because none risk it!'","Chapter 9.3: A Question of Trust","Glúrkub is encaged in Máttugard.","'You will obey my order! Slay him where he stands!'","Durin falls silent at last, his face a mask","Glóin is by the cage in Máttugard.","'My prince, I am sorry. If you deem my words worthy of punishment, I will accept it without objection. You are my prince, and if I live to see it you will be my king when your father no longer rules in Erebor.\
\
'You are Durin the Seventh, and no Dragon-trick can change that. I will follow wherever you lead.'","Glóin is standing by the cage, eyeing Durin warily.","Talk to Glúrkub","'Lies, all of them lies! This goblin claims that I am under Hrímil Frost-heart's control, obeying her command to reclaim Gundabad? Impossible! Unthinkable!\
\
'${PLAYER}! I command you to slay this goblin where he stands!'","Durin has calmed himself somewhat, but the prince still disbelieves the goblin's story.","Durin's breath still comes in ragged hitches, but he has for the moment mastered the fury that so seized him. He glowers at the encaged goblin with undisguised hatred, but now his expression contains something else: curiosity.\
\
'If Hrímil has the power to command Gorgar, why would she not allow him to wield the mithril hammer in her presence? She cannot fear he would use it against her, not unless she doubted her hold upon him. Does she fear the mithril hammer itself? That is very interesting, ${PLAYER}, and I see in it an opportunity.\
\
'Let this guide our next move. It will be dangerous, but it may yield treasure commensurate with the risk.'","Durin is by the cage holding Glúrkub.","Durin is furious at the words of Glúrkub and at Glóin's betrayal of his commands.","Talk to Glóin by the cage","'A cage can be arranged for you as well, Glóin, and for all who speak against me! Your age will not save you from captivity, or from cruel treatment! I am your prince!\
\
'Do you question that I am Durin the Seventh? For no Durin could ever be subject to Dragon-compulsion! If you believe the lies of this goblin, you deny the very foundation upon which this conquest is based!\
\
'Speak now, Glóin! Speak, and seal your fate!'","Kill Glúrkub","Durin is beside himself with rage at Glúrkub's story, and refuses to believe that he has been made a dragon's puppet.","Talk to Durin by the cage","'The goblin is our prisoner, my prince. He is helpless, and cannot be killed in this fashion.\
\
'It is beneath you to command ${PLAYER} to do this, Durin.'","Glóin catches your arm. 'Do not do this!' he warns you","The prince breathes heavily. Some of his rage departs"},
[3323]={"Climb the ladder inside the keep of Skarháld","'If you find foes within the keep or that threatening tunnel, do what you can to best them! Whatever lies within will be no friend to any of us, whether we be Longbeard or Zhélruka or something else entirely!'","Rocks fall and seal the exit of the escape tunnel","Defeat foes within Tharrazhâr or the crystal tunnels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A tunnel winds into the mountains behind Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld, and Kozun went inside to investigate. Kámat has asked you to find his friend and ensure his safety.","Find the entrance to the tunnel in the back of Tharrazhâr","'There are some things we need to do to ensure that Skarháld is ready if Karazgar makes good on his promise to return, ${PLAYER}. I will see to the repair of our siege defences and the replacement of the arrows and bolts we will need against further attack from the air.\
\
'But I have something else in mind for you, my friend. You helped me assess the supplies inside the keep before Karazgar's attack, but I noted more than just the inventory of armour and weapons held within. Do you know what else I saw? The upper levels of the keep were inaccessible, for the stairs had been damaged long ago by the passage of time. Who knows what those rooms and chambers might hold?\
\
'I asked Kámat and Kozun to find a ladder so they might search the rear of Tharrazhâr, the keep here at Skarháld. Go to them inside the keep and lend them what aid you can.'","The cave-mouth has been successfully sealed by rocks","While Inek focuses on taking the fight to Karazgar at the Anvil, Durin wishes to ensure that Skarháld is made ready for his possible return.","Kámat waves to you and calls you over","Gandalf has come to Skarháld with a small party of dwarves!","'You were sent here by the Longbeard prince? Very well, very well, but I will not be responsible for your safety if something were to befall you in these chambers! The vacant rooms of the keep do not seem to hold much danger, but Kozun and I found a tunnel in one of the walls, and strange sounds echo up from the depths.\
\
'If you do find foes within the keep or that threatening tunnel, do what you can to best them! Whatever lies within will be no friend to any of us, whether we be Longbeard or Zhélruka or something else entirely!'","Chapter 9.3: Another Way In","'The upper levels of the keep were inaccessible, for the stairs had been damaged long ago by the passage of time. Who knows what those rooms and chambers might hold? Well, I asked Kámat and Kozun to find a ladder so they might search the rear of Tharrazhâr, the keep here at Skarháld. Go to them inside the keep and lend them what aid you can.'","'We should collapse this cave-mouth, ${PLAYER}. Here, lend me a hand with this.'","Durin asked you to investigate the upper levels of Tharrazhâr, the formerly-inaccessible keep of Skarháld.","Defeated foes behind or within Tharrazhâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Kozun at the bottom of the tunnel","Return to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld","'Look who it is, ${PLAYER}! Are you acquainted with Gandalf the Wizard?'","Collapse the cave-mouth at the bottom of the escape tunnel","Talk to Kámat on the upper level of Tharrazhâr","Find the bottom of the winding tunnel behind Tharrazhâr","Durin stands on the upper level of Skarháld among a group of new arrivals, including a familiar Wizard.","Kozun has asked for your help in collapsing the cave-mouth at the bottom of the escape tunnel behind Tharrazhâr.","You have successfully collapsed the exit of the escape tunnel, and should now return to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld.","Talk to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld","'If you find foes within the keep or that threatening tunnel, do what you can to best them! Whatever lies within will be no friend to any of us, whether we be Longbeard or Zhélruka or something else entirely!\
\
'Kozun disappeared into the tunnel, and I have not heard from him since! I would appreciate it if you could find him and ensure he is safe. Who knows what dangers might lie within that tunnel? I know I have heard strange sounds echoing up from its depths!'","'Kámat sent you? He did not wish to follow me down here, but I do not begrudge him that. His is the path of learning and of books, whereas mine is that of the hammer and the axe.'\
\
Kozun peers through the cave-mouth.\
\
'Kámat may know more about this than I do, but I think this tunnel served as an escape tunnel for the Dwarves of Skarháld. See how it exits among the mountains? I do not know whether ancient dwarves ever made use of it for this purpose, but it does not take much learning to see that an escape tunnel might cut both ways. Dwarves could use it to escape, true... but Karazgar could use it to invade, were he ever to find the entrance! We should collapse this cave-mouth, ${PLAYER}. Here, lend me a hand with this.'","Strange sounds echo up from the depths of the winding tunnel","You found the bottom of the tunnel, where it empties onto a sloping path north-west of Skarháld","'Very good. With the cave-mouth collapsed, we need not worry that Karazgar might use this tunnel as a secret entrance to Tharrazhâr!\
\
'Let us hope we do not wish for an escape tunnel in the days to come! Ah, I jest. The Zhélruka run toward danger, not away from it. That has always been our way.'","Kámat and Kozun explored the upper level of Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld, and found a tunnel winding deep into the mountain. Kámat asked you to defeat any enemies you find within the chambers of the keep or in the tunnel."},
[3324]={"Orcs prowl the Welkin-lofts, and Durin has asked you to defeat those you find there.","Talk to Durin by the cage north of Maergrind, in Máttugard","'The Orcs may call it Lugroz, but to us those high places are known as the Welkin-lofts. Climb up there, slaying any of the Orcs you encounter, and see if the path to the summit is as Glúrkub described.\
\
'If there is no such weapon-rack, we will know his story for what it is: full of lies. But if he does tell the truth, and there is such a place for Gorgar to leave the mithril hammer when he is summoned by the Dragon... well, in that case, see if there is a hiding place nearby. I may have the beginning of a plan.'","'Climb to the Welkin-lofts, slaying any Orcs you encounter, and see if the path to the summit is as Glúrkub described. If there is a place for Gorgar to leave the mithril hammer when he is summoned by the Dragon... well, in that case, see if there is a hiding place nearby. I may have the beginning of a plan.'","Durin thinks you should investigate the Welkin-lofts and see what you can learn about the relationship between Gorgar the Ruthless and Hrímil Frost-heart.","Find a hiding place nearby, perhaps in the stand of trees to the north-west","Talk to Glúrkub in Máttugard","A number of weapons rest in the rack, but the mithril hammer is missing","Find the path to the summit in the south-east heights of the Welkin-lofts","'This is the plan. When next Gorgar goes to meet with the Dragon, you and Glúrkub will steal the mithril hammer from the weapon rack when Gorgar leaves it behind. If the goblin carries out his part in the plan, I will release him. In this way he will earn his freedom, and we will deprive Gorgar of his most deadly weapon, the hammer with which he slew Stóthkell and so many others.'","You need to find a hiding place nearby! Perhaps one could be found in the stand of trees to the north-west.","Chapter 9.4: A Look at Lugroz","Examine the weapon rack by the path to the summit","This place might serve to hide you when Gorgar goes to meet with the dragon","The path to the summit can be found atop a snow-covered terrace in the south-eastern heights of the Welkin-lofts.","Durin is north of Maergrind and down one level, by the cage holding Glúrkub in Máttugard.","A weapon rack stands by the path to the summit, as Glúrkub described.","'So it is as Glúrkub said? Then we will proceed with the plan.\
\
'It is this: when next Gorgar goes to meet with the Dragon, you and Glúrkub will steal the mithril hammer from the weapon rack when Gorgar leaves it behind. If the goblin carries out his part in the plan, I will release him. In this way he will earn his freedom, and we will deprive Gorgar of his most deadly weapon, the hammer with which he slew Stóthkell and so many others.\
\
'Can you accomplish this, ${PLAYER}? I trust no other with this important task.'","Defeat Orcs in the Welkin-lofts (${NUMBER}/6)","'I already told the important dwarf I agree to the bargain. What else would I do? Think about it? No one likes a cage, goblin or dwarf. And I know, because I used to close the cages and not open them! But that's not important now, no it isn't. I have been so helpful, haven't I?\
\
'Glúrkub can command Gorgar's Orcs to leave the fancy hammer undefended. It will be easy, you will see. And then freedom for Glúrkub!'","Defeat Orcs in the Welkin-lofts (5/6)","Defeated Orcs in the Welkin-lofts (${NUMBER}/6)","A weapon rack stands by the path to the summit","Glúrkub is encaged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.","You find a pouch of colourful stones on the Orc; Bróin will want to see this"},
[3325]={"Talk to Gandalf on the upper level of Skarháld","'Yes, I am here, ${PLAYER}. I have made some progress deciphering further pages in the Black Book, and I wish to share my discoveries with you. I deemed it wise to request a number of strong warriors to accompany me, and while King Thorin at first refused, in time he came around to my position. He needed a reminder of his people's history, and of the great deeds his forebears accomplished when their resolve was tested.'\
\
You ask Gandalf if it was the Wizard's idea that the Red Axe be sent to Durin.\
\
'I am sure I do not know where you might have gotten that idea, ${PLAYER}. King Thorin is welcome to do as he likes! I merely suggested a number of beneficial outcomes that might be reached by such a course, and if the King Under the Mountain agreed with my proposals certainly he has demonstrated wisdom befitting a king.\
\
'But that is behind us, and we should turn to more pressing matters. What is this I have heard about an expedition to the Anvil of Winterstith?'","Chapter 9.4: An Unexpected Delivery","Gandalf has come to Skarháld with a small party of dwarves including Hrostyr, the personal guard of King Thorin.","'I will wield the Red Axe on behalf of both my own people and the Zhélruka!'","Gandalf has come to Skarháld and stands on the upper level of the fortress.","'Gandalf has come to Skarháld with a small band of Longbeards from the Lonely Mountain. Even Hrostyr has come! He is the personal guard of my father the king, and it is most unusual to see him so far from the royal seat.\
\
'Why have they come here, you ask? They told me of the two purposes that brought them hither. First, to stand with us against the dangers of the Ered Mithrin, no matter how fearsome. And second, to deliver this!'\
\
Durin brandishes the weapon in his hand, and his voice is heavy with emotion.\
\
'This is the Red Axe, passed down from ancient days and wielded by my grandsire Dáin Ironfoot in many battles. When I came here against my father's command, I thought it would never be mine to wield. But Hrostyr says it is not so, and he relayed to me my father's words. \\qDurin,\\q I am told he said, \\qWhen you disobeyed my command on the edge of the Dale-lands, I was moved to anger and spoke words I am shamed to remember. My counsellors told me there was honour in your actions, but I did not see it.\\q\
\
'\\qDurin,\\q the message continued, \\qWhen I consider the history of the Longbeards, I see that no one can choose the times that will test him. I sought to shield you from a dangerous world, my son, but that was a father's ambition, and not the way of a king. Wield this Red Axe on behalf of our people, and when you return to the Lonely Mountain on the other side of many victories, all shall know you are fit to be King Under the Mountain after me. Go, my son! The Red Axe is yours!\\q\
\
'My heart swells to hear of my father's confidence, ${PLAYER}! I will wield the Red Axe on behalf of both my own people and the Zhélruka!'"},
[3326]={"Chapter 9.4: Trail of the Sea-beast","Sigileth holds her unnamed blade at the ready, eager to keep the Corsairs busy while her brother searches Tatháta's ship.","You have located another entrance to the hidden harbour","Wait for Corudan to depart","'Yes? Let us return to Mekab-kuphâr and show this map to your Temámir friend.'","Sigileth stands by the entrance to the hidden harbour, staring out at the docked ships.","Corudan stands by the entrance to the hidden harbour.","Corudan listens to your report with growing unease.\
\
'He is gone?'","Talk to Corudan by the entrance of the hidden harbour","Corudan will rely on you to keep the Corsairs busy while he searches the ship","That is peculiar. Birûk is missing","Sigileth surveys the harbour briefly before repeating her original assessment.\
\
'This will make discovering Tatháta's trail more difficult,' she says.","Talk to Sigileth in the hidden harbour","Corudan and Sigileth will want to hear what you learned. They are still at at Mekab-kuphâr, but both of the Elves are eager to depart.","Talk to Corudan at Mekab-kuphâr","Corudan and Sigileth have descended into Umbar-môkh to help you find Tatháta's trail.","'Let us move forward with care, for the entrance to the hidden harbour lies in the south-eastern corner of Dil-irmíz!'","Birûk has returned to Mekab-kuphâr and may have learned something that will help you learn what happened to Tatháta.","'What does my sister think? We cannot allow these Corsairs to prevent us from searching for Tatháta.\
\
'What do you think of this suggestion, ${PLAYER}? If you keep the Corsairs occupied out here, I can slip aboard Tatháta's ship and search her cabin for some clue that may lead us to her home in Umbar-môkh, if the Temámir is right and she does possess such a place.\
\
'I spent some time on that ship, as you know, and I should be able to search it more quickly than you or my sister. Keep the Corsairs and their Heirsworn Captains busy while I search, and I will meet you back here when I have finished!'","Corudan and Sigileth suggested that you return to Mekab-kuphâr and ask Birûk what he thinks of the circled areas on the map Corudan retrieved from Tatháta's ship.","'Yes! Our time was not wasted!\
\
'I found a map of Umbar-môkh in Tatháta's cabin, and certain locations on the map are circled in charcoal. It could be that one of these marked spots indicates a place of safety to which she may have escaped after fleeing from Cruel Dancer.\
\
'Let us return to Mekab-kuphâr and show this map to your Temámir friend.'","Devious Corsairs and their Heirsworn Captains have taken over the hidden harbour in Nakási's absence, and you should keep them busy while Corudan searches Tatháta's ship for some clue to her whereabouts.","Defeated devious Corsairs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Birûk at Mekab-kuphâr","'I spoke to some of my fellows about the missing Kinswoman Tatháta, and none of them have seen her of late. Most agree that she must have possessed a home of some kind within Umbar-môkh, for she did spend time in the tunnels when not at sea, but no one knows where it might be located. This is a place of secrets, after all. Even men and women of means and power may require a hiding-place from time to time. Them most of all!\
\
'But you said she was last seen at the harbour where her ship is docked? The entrance to that place is not far from here. Elves are known for their skill at observation, I understand? It may be your friends will pick up her trail, or notice something you have missed, if you return to this harbour and search for sign of her.'","Defeat devious Corsairs in the hidden harbour (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Corudan and Sigileth have arrived at Mekab-kuphâr.","Return to Mekab-kuphâr and ask Birûk about the map Corudan recovered","Corudan has returned to the entrance of the hidden harbour, but whether he found anything of use remains in doubt.","'It was a good deed, my friend, and one of the dwarves here agreed to ask his fellows about Tatháta? What has he learned?'","'If luck is with you, your friends may pick up Tatháta's trail within the hidden harbour. The entrance is to the south, in the south-eastern corner of Dil-irmíz. How did you go there before and not know its location, if you do not mind my asking?'","Corudan hurries away, his feet making little sound on either wood or rock.","Defeat Heirsworn captains in the hidden harbour (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Heirsworn captains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Corudan in the hidden harbour","An entrance to the hidden harbour can be found in the south-eastern corner of Dil-irmíz.","'Let us do what we can to help. If we aid the Temámir here with the tasks they have posted on that notice board...'\
\
Corudan falls silent.\
\
'You have already done that, I see! You are a step ahead of us, ${PLAYER}, but I am pleased to see that these past few months have not changed your way of thinking: you still desire to provide help where you can. I did not doubt it, but it is nice to see it demonstrated, all the same.\
\
'One of the dwarves here agreed to ask his fellows about Tatháta? What has he learned?'","'Yes? It is a good plan, but we must be careful. The ships belonging to Nakási and Tatháta surely remain within that hidden harbour, even if their captains do not. Still, the Temámir is correct that there may be signs within that point to Tatháta's destination. We were all rather occupied with our own situations when last we were there, ${PLAYER}, were we not?'\
\
Corudan laughs, a sudden and surprising sound in the damp and the dark of Umbar-môkh.\
\
'I had a very good view of your battle with Tatháta's lions, it is true, but I would have preferred to be free to help you with them... and you have told me of the dangerous climb that brought you to that harbour the first time. It is good to hear no such climb will be required today, for the main entrance lies in the south-eastern corner of Dil-irmíz!'","Find an entrance to the hidden harbour in the south-eastern corner of Dil-irmíz","Sigileth turns to you with a raised eyebrow. When she speaks, there is clear satisfaction in her voice.\
\
'I believed this might happen, ${PLAYER}. Now that word of Nakási's departure has begun to spread through the city, Corsairs have come to search her ship for any treasure she might have left behind. It would appear the harbour she chose is not as hidden as she may have believed it to be.\
\
'This will make discovering Tatháta's trail more difficult.'"},
[3328]={"You located Birûk, but he needs your help!","Find someone at Mekab-kuphâr who might know what happened to Birûk","'Very good, my friend. Which location would you like to choose? Nishabêt and its spiders to the north, or Lôkhalel and its grave-robbers to the north-west?'","<rgb=#FFFF00>Spiders of Nishabêt</rgb>\
Someone should do something about the spiders that have infested the chamber to the north of Mekab-kuphâr in Khabârkhad. They are contained within Nishabêt for now, but who can say how long they will remain there?\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Grave-robbers at Lôkhalel</rgb>\
Brigands and grave-robbers are plundering the chambers at Lôkhalel, north-west of Mekab-kuphâr, stealing valuables that belong to us. Someone needs to tell them that this is our territory!","'I thought I would try my hand at the adventuring life you have chosen, ${PLAYER}, but it proved more difficult than I expected. How do you do it, day after day?\
\
'No, it is not for me. I will remain in the service of Khôltekh, drawing stones to learn what my duties for the day will be. The shiny stones never take me from the safety of the camp, and the dull stones do so only rarely.'\
\
You tell Birûk that Corudan has acquired a map of Umbar-môkh with markings on it that may indicate potential hiding-spots for Tatháta, but the Elf has not yet arrived.\
\
'I will see him when I see him, I suppose. But until he gets here, I have had another idea that may help you track down your missing Kinswoman. I have not seen her, and the others I spoke with have not either... but there are more eyes in Umbar-môkh than yours or mine.'","Wait for Birûk to escape","'When last I noticed Birûk he was studying the notice board. Perhaps something there caught his eye?'","Birûk said he would meet you at Itekh-kên, in the northern reaches of Khabârkhad.","'Birûk? I have not seen him for a few hours. When last I noticed him he was studying the notice board. Perhaps something there caught his eye?'","Corudan suggested that you ask dwarves at Mekab-kuphâr if any of them saw where Birûk might have gone.","'Yes? You say the Temámir Birûk was seen studying the notice board, and the axe you left there is now missing? He may have taken the axe and gone to complete one of the posted tasks, ${PLAYER}. If he is to help us make sense of the map of Umbar-môkh I recovered, we need to find where he went. He may have gotten into trouble.\
\
'You should search one of the locations mentioned on the notice board, and Sigileth and I will search the other. After we have each scoured our chosen destination, let us meet at the northern camp... what is it called? Itekh-kên in Khabârkhad?\
\
'Which location would you like to choose, ${PLAYER}? Nishabêt and its spiders to the north, or Lôkhalel and its grave-robbers to the north-west?'","You have found Birûk, and he is in trouble!","Gêzheg does not know where Birûk has gone, but he did notice the dwarf studying the notice board at some point in the last few hours.","Talk to Corudan at Mekab-kuphâr","Talk to Birûk at Itekh-kên in the northern reaches of Khabârkhad","Examine the notice board at Mekab-kuphâr","Talk to Birûk and help him escape from danger","Search for Birûk at Nishabêt or Lôkhalel","'I thought these grave-robbers would be poorly-armed and untrained, ${PLAYER}, but they proved more deadly than I expected, and I only just escaped with my life! I am grateful for your help, and will meet up with you at Itekh-kên to the north-east!'","'I did not know the spiders had come to Nishabêt in such numbers, ${PLAYER}! I thank you for your help... and now I must make good my escape! I will meet up with you at Itekh-kên to the north-west!'","You believe Birûk has gone to complete one of the two tasks posted on the notice board, either to combat the spiders of Nishabêt to the north, or to face the grave-robbers of Lôkhalel to the north-west. Whichever of the locations you do not search will be visited by Corudan and Sigileth.","As you go to leave, you notice the axe you left here is now missing","Birûk has escaped from danger. You should meet up with him at Itekh-kên","'We need to know what has happened. Someone here may know where the Temámir Birûk has gone.'","'We need to know what has happened. It may be that your Temámir friend has left this place for a perfectly good reason... but he works for Khôltekh. The Kindred of the Coins has promised a new dawn for the people of Umbar, but let us not forget that should our interests diverge from theirs they would not hesitate to do us harm. We should give him only as much trust as caution warrants... and little more than that.\
\
'Perhaps I am overreacting. Someone here may know where the Temámir Birûk has gone.'","Decide between Nishabêt or Lôkhalel, and the Elves will search where you do not","Corudan will want to hear what you think might have happened to Birûk. The Elf has returned to Mekab-kuphâr with Sigileth.","Chapter 9.5: How Do You Do It?","Your Temámir contact Birûk has gone missing from Mekab-kuphâr while you investigated the hidden harbour.","Birûk flees for safety!"},
[3329]={"Talk to Dolek on the upper level of Skarháld","Mudro is to the north-east of Gandalf, on the upper level of Skarháld.","'Karazgar? So the whispers are true, then? The Weeping Warrior is still alive?\
\
'I heard that a couple of the Stout-axes that went with the expedition saw a trail of blood and rust leading away from the dragon's chamber, but I hoped they were mistaken. It seems they were not.\
\
'I will keep an eye from the heights for any sign of him, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps he will succumb to his injuries and trouble us no more. If he has not, Ibor might have seen him. Find him to the north-west and ask him for me, will you?'","'Karazgar? Alive? Bah!\
\
'I will watch for him. When he fulfilled the first of his promises, he flew his terrible drake to Skarháld. Now that the drake is slain, he will need to ascend to the fortress on foot, and I'd like to see him try!\
\
'I do not mean that, ${PLAYER}. Let us hope Karazgar accepts his defeat in the jaws of the dragon and skulks away, never to return to Skarháld. But I will remain alert, all the same.'","'The scouts have seen no sign of Karazgar? That may not be troubling news, but neither does it reassure. Perhaps we will learn more in the days ahead.\
\
'But let us turn now to the matter that brought me hither, ${PLAYER}. I wish to speak with you concerning the Black Book of Mordor.'","'I do not believe Karazgar was truly slain. It may be that the Herald of Winter has given the Weeping Warrior his fill of battle, for now, but I have heard whispers from the dwarves of this place that a trail of blood and rust led away from Hrímil's chamber. I am certain Karazgar lives.\
\
'Scouts here at Skarháld might have seen some sign of him. Mudro is to the north-east, and may know of Karazgar's escape.'","Talk to Gandalf inside the chamber that was given to him in the north-east corner of the upper level of Skarháld","'You went with the dwarves on their expedition to the Anvil? I suppose I should not be surprised, ${PLAYER}! That place has been both blessing and curse to the dwarves that seek their fortune in the Ered Mithrin. It was a blessing for the years it remained sealed, trapping many dangers behind its frozen surface, and that was the case for most of its history. I say it was a curse for the periods when it thawed, setting loose those evils upon the mountains. What did you encounter within?'\
\
You describe the events of Hórin's expedition to Winterstith and the great perils you faced there. When you have finished Gandalf strokes his beard, deep in thought.\
\
'It may have been merely good fortune that caused the Herald of Winter to seal herself once more within the glacier, ${PLAYER}, but I see another power at work. At any rate, the Dwarves of the Ered Mithrin have proven fortunate, for once; they need not worry about Hrímil Frost-heart on this day, although a day may come when they must.\
\
'I do not believe Karazgar was truly slain, however. It may be that the Herald of Winter has given the Weeping Warrior his fill of battle, for now, but I have heard whispers from the dwarves of this place that a trail of blood and rust led away from Hrímil's chamber. I am certain Karazgar lives.\
\
'Scouts here at Skarháld might have seen some sign of him. Mudro is to the north-east, on the upper level, and may know of Karazgar's escape. Durin has given to me a chamber in the north-east corner for my use while I stay at Skarháld. I will meet you there after you have learned what you can of Karazgar's location.'","'I will keep searching for any sign of the Weeping Warrior. I really hoped that dragon had been the end of him, ${PLAYER}. Dolek is to the south-west and may have seen something I did not, if you would like to ask him.'","Gandalf has come to Skarháld, but before he will share what he has learned from the Black Book of Mordor, he wishes to hear what happened to the dwarf-expedition to the Anvil of Winterstith.","Talk to Ibor on the upper level of Skarháld","'Karazgar? Why do you ask me about him, ${PLAYER}? I thought he was dead, slain by the terrible dragon that lurked within the Anvil! If he is not, that means Skarháld is still in danger!\
\
'I will keep searching for any sign of the Weeping Warrior. I really hoped that dragon had been the end of him, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Dolek is to the south-west, and may have seen something I did not, if you would like to ask him.'","Ibor is to the north-west of Dolek, on the upper level of Skarháld.","Talk to Mudro on the upper level of Skarháld","Gandalf is in the chamber that was prepared for him in the north-east corner of the upper level of Skarháld.","'Let us hope Karazgar accepts his defeat in the jaws of the dragon and skulks away, never to return to Skarháld. But I will remain alert, all the same.'","'Meet me inside the chamber Durin gave to me here at Skarháld. It is in the north-east corner of the upper level.'","'I will keep an eye from the heights for any sign of Karazgar. Perhaps he will succumb to his injuries and trouble us no more. If he has not, Ibor might have seen him. Find him to the north-west, on the upper level of Skarháld, and ask him for me, will you?'","Chapter 9.5: Report from Winterstith","Dolek is to the south-west of Mudro, on the upper level of Skarháld."},
[3330]={"Talk to Dolek on the upper level of Skarháld","Mudro is to the north-east of Gandalf, on the upper level of Skarháld.","'Our expedition to the Anvil must be deemed a success, for it brought about the ends of Karazgar and Vethúg Wintermind. I mourn for my fallen brothers, but I know they would be satisfied with that result!'","'I am fatigued, friend. Perhaps Dolek will continue the story of our expedition for you. He is to the south-west, on the upper level of Skarháld.'","'What did you learn of the expedition to the Anvil, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You relay what Mudro, Dolek, and Ibor told you about the events at Winterstith, and Gandalf listens to the account with interest. When you have finished, he strokes his beard, deep in thought.\
\
'It may have been merely good fortune that caused the Herald of Winter to seal herself once more within the glacier, ${PLAYER}, but I see another power at work. At any rate, the Dwarves of the Ered Mithrin have proven fortunate, for once; they need not worry about Hrímil Frost-heart on this day, although a day may come when they must.\
\
'I do not believe Karazgar was truly slain, however. It may be that the Herald of Winter has given the Weeping Warrior his fill of battle, for now, but I have heard whispers from the dwarves of this place that a trail of blood and rust led away from Hrímil's chamber. I am certain Karazgar lives.\
\
'But let us turn to the matter that brought me hither, ${PLAYER}. I wish to speak with you concerning the Black Book of Mordor.'","'I understand that a raiding-party of dwarves recently sought to oppose the efforts of Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, at the Anvil of Winterstith. Will you find some of these dwarves and hear their report? I wish to know what befell them at the Anvil, for it concerns us now most directly!\
\
'It seems one of these dwarves, Mudro, is recovering from the ordeal north-east of here, on the upper level of Skarháld. Speak to him and ask what happened to his raiding-party.'","'I understand you seek to hear of Hórin's expedition to the Anvil? How much have the others told you? The illusions of the dead kings, you say? I am glad I need not speak of them, ${PLAYER}. That was cursed dragon-magic, I tell you, and unnatural.\
\
'In the frost-maze we at last encountered our prey: Karazgar, still astride Vethúg Wintermind. We engaged in battle, and this time no strange illusions could stay our assault. With all of our strength we leapt at the drake, seeking to carve the record of our battle onto his hide! It seemed beyond hope at first, but slowly, the battle began to turn in our favour! \\qGive me your power, Karazgar!\\q the drake cried, \\qor we will both perish!\\q\
\
'But the Weeping Warrior bears no love for anyone but himself. As the drake at last succumbed to his injuries, with his final breath Vethúg cursed Karazgar. His words echoed against ice and stone, chasing Karazgar deeper into the tunnels of the Anvil. If I close my eyes I swear to you I can still hear his terrible voice. \\qMother!\\q he cried, \\qAvenge me!\\q\
\
'Should we have turned back? No dwarf of our company then wished to retreat, but now it is easy for those of us who made it back to Skarháld to say we should have. But instead we followed Karazgar, and so it was that we beheld his confrontation with Hrímil Frost-heart, brood-mother of the Frost-horde and Herald of Winter.'\
\
Ibor smirks.\
\
'I say \\qconfrontation,\\q but it was a one-sided affair. Hrímil seized him in her jaws and flung him around like a child's toy. She fell upon us then, and that is where many of our company perished. She leapt into the air and landed upon us with such force that the very ground beneath us crumbled! We fell a long way, and those of us that survived ran for our lives along the lower tunnel while Hrímil pursued us. As we tumbled down the final slope to safety, Hrímil sent one frigid blast after us, and the crack in the Anvil was sealed! She had trapped herself within, and let us thank whatever power caused her to do it, or she might have followed us all the way back to Skarháld!\
\
'Twenty-four of us went to the Anvil that day, ${PLAYER}, but only fourteen dwarves survived. At least Karazgar and Vethúg died and will no longer trouble us. That at least is a happy result, and Hórin's expedition must be deemed a success, despite the lives it cost us.'","Talk to Gandalf inside the chamber that was given to him in the north-east corner of the upper level of Skarháld","Gandalf has come to Skarháld, but before he will share what he has learned from the Black Book of Mordor, he wishes to hear what happened to the dwarf-expedition to the Anvil of Winterstith.","'Meet me inside the chamber Durin gave to me here at Skarháld. It is to the north-east of here.'","'We pressed on, leaving the unpleasant sight of our fallen kings behind us. Into the frozen maze we stepped, thinking the worst lay behind us. We were wrong.\
\
'Ibor will tell you more. He is to the north-west.'","Talk to Ibor on the upper level of Skarháld","'Yes, I fought with Hórin at the Anvil of Winterstith. We stood among the corpses of frost-drakes and saw Isvítha the Gluttonous breathe her last. Together with my fellows, I strode past the jagged ice and into the great cavern within the Anvil itself, following the path taken by Karazgar and Vethúg Wintermind.\
\
'The frozen cavern was not empty, though it did not contain our prey. Frost-bound Hobgoblins and whelps of the Frost-horde stood against us, terrible foes, but of a sort I was unafraid to face. As the last of them fell, I brandished my axe and prepared for whatever evil dared show itself, knowing that I and my fellows were ready to defy it! I did not know... I did not know what awaited us!'\
\
Dolek looks at you with sadness in his eyes, his shoulders slumping at the memory of the frozen cavern. He grips his axe more tightly and resolves to finish his story.\
\
'We moved forward onto the smooth surface of a long-frozen lake, and that is when we saw them. They were arrayed on a ledge above us, ghostly figures of kings long-dead. I swear I recognized some of their number, though many had been dead for hundreds of years or more! Aye, these were kings who vanished seeking the Citadel, but instead of finding lost Thafar-gathol they perished in the unforgiving North. For many of them, Winterstith proved their undoing... and yet there they stood, and I beheld them with my own eyes!\
\
'Nay, it was not so. Dragon-magic lay heavily upon that cavern, moving illusions against us. It chills my heart to remember that desperate fight! But still we pressed on, leaving the unpleasant sight of our fallen kings behind us. Into the frozen maze we stepped, thinking the worst lay behind us. We were wrong.\
\
'Ibor will tell you more. He is to the north-west.'","Ibor is to the north-west of Dolek, on the upper level of Skarháld.","'You wish to hear about Hórin's expedition to the Anvil, ${PLAYER}? Would that you had asked someone else! The memory of it is painful, for though we achieved some success, many good friends gave their lives at that cursed place and will not return.\
\
'Twenty-four of us there were, armed with our finest weapons and our strongest armour. Our scouts spied Vethúg Wintermind flying north above the Withered Heath, making for the Anvil of Winterstith, and we knew Karazgar drove him thither. The drakes and worms of the Frost-horde seemed to sense some terrible presence behind the frozen surface; did Karazgar seek to claim this power for himself?\
\
'As we approached the great crack in the Anvil, Vethúg flew overhead, stirring the frozen wind into madness all about us. Karazgar taunted us, but Longbeard, Zhélruka, and Stout-axe alike laughed at him. \\qYour empty words do not frighten us!\\q we shouted at him.\
\
'But it is not Karazgar we should have attended at that moment, ${PLAYER}. For as Vethúg drew near to the crack in the Anvil, mighty drakes of the Frost-horde sensed the presence of their kin! They flew from the rent in the ice in terrible number, seeking to put an end to their foes of old. Little did they care for our lineage, or for the different families arrayed before them. No, they saw dwarves bedecked in plate and leather, dwarves wielding blade and axe, and that was enough! The fighting was fierce, and by the end of the melee the ice was speckled with blood, that of drake and dwarf alike, but only the warriors of our band remained alive.\
\
'We were not yet triumphant. Before we could so much as catch our breath, a great worm crawled from the crack in the ice! Isvítha the Gluttonous she was called, ancient and hungry, and even as we shouted our war-cries she thanked us for bringing her dinner so near. But she had not accounted for the sharpness of our dinner-knives, or for our own appetite for battle!\
\
'With the door-warden Isvítha slain, the way into the Anvil was no longer barred. Karazgar took advantage, and steered Vethúg Wintermind into the gap. We had no choice but to follow!\
\
'I am fatigued, friend. Perhaps Dolek will continue the story of our expedition for you. He is to the south-west, on the upper level of Skarháld.'","Talk to Mudro on the upper level of Skarháld","Gandalf is in the chamber that was prepared for him in the north-east corner of the upper level of Skarháld.","'The Anvil of Winterstith has long been both blessing and curse to the dwarves that seek their fortune in the Ered Mithrin. It was a blessing for the years it remained sealed, trapping many dangers behind its frozen surface, and that was the case for most of its history. I say it was a curse for the periods when it thawed, setting loose those evils upon the mountains.\
\
'I understand that a raiding-party of dwarves recently sought to oppose the efforts of Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, at the Anvil of Winterstith. Will you find some of these dwarves and hear their report? I wish to know what befell them at the Anvil, for it concerns us now most directly!\
\
'It seems one of these dwarves, Mudro, is recovering from the ordeal north-east of here on the upper level of Skarháld. Speak to him and ask what happened to his raiding-party, ${PLAYER}. Durin has given to me a chamber in the north-east corner for my use while I stay at Skarháld. I will meet you there after you have learned what befell the dwarves at Winterstith.'","Chapter 9.5: Report from Winterstith","Dolek is to the south-west of Mudro, on the upper level of Skarháld."},
[3331]={"'I will continue to study these pages, ${PLAYER}. It is clear that Khîl's thrice-great grandfather Vóin has much yet to tell us, if we can solve the mystery he left behind.'","'I have spent some time studying these pages, ${PLAYER}, and I am no nearer to learning how this book came to be hidden in the secret chamber located in Khîl's home in Járnfast. But that is not to say my study has been fruitless! No, there is much to be learned from this tome, and I have made some progress already.\
\
'Listen well to my words and I will share some of the knowledge it has imparted to me!'","Talk to Gandalf in his chamber at Skarháld and learn of his discoveries from the Black Book","'Much that is in these pages remains unknown to me, but if you listen well to my words you will hear what I have learned.'","Gandalf is in the chamber granted to him by Durin at Skarháld, studying the Black Book of Mordor.","Chapter 9.6: Painting the Picture","Gandalf is in the chamber of Skarháld given to him by Durin, waiting to discuss with you the contents of the Black Book of Mordor.","Talk to Gandalf in his chamber at Skarháld"},
[3332]={"Defeat crocodiles in Ilmabiri (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You set down the meal and wine and wait for Tephísa to return","Birûk suggested that you defeat rats and crocodiles within Ilmabiri.","The empty metal plate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri waits for the bread Birûk gave to you.","You hear a girl's voice from the darkness beyond the grate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri.","The Terâsi girl you encountered in Ilmabiri asked you to retrieve a meal of higher quality from the Upper Ward, as well as a bottle of fancy wine, or she will tell you nothing. The tables at the Baths of Ilmai Iforikh in the Upper Ward may have what you need.","The empty metal plate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri waits for the meal and wine you \\qretrieved\\q from the Upper Ward.","Find the metal plate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri","Makhíl agrees to let you go. \\qKindred business,\\q he says with a wink","'We are outsiders in Umbar-môkh. We patrol these caverns and keep them as safe as we can, but we do not live here. When my day is done, I return to the Shoreward Stone. When yours is ended, I presume you seek food and shelter at one of the taverns of the city. It is not so for all who walk these tunnels.\
\
'I speak of the unseen ones, those the Umbari call \\qMâtrikhai.\\q My people have another name for them; to us they are the \\qTerâsi,\\q the forgotten ones. They creep into places no others could, and move with such speed that should you catch a glimpse of them from the corner of your eye, by the time you turned to look they have gone. They are children of Umbar, I think, and move about Umbar-môkh by secret passageways unknown to any other. It is said the Terâsi prowl the markets of the Upper Ward and the Lower when they are most crowded, stealing goods and coin whenever they can, and then slipping back into the tunnels and caverns undetected.\
\
'Temámir hearts warm to the Terâsi, for we see their hardships and take pity upon them. It has been our custom to leave food for these forgotten ones throughout Umbar-môkh on occasion. I will give you this crusty bread so you can do this as well. There is a suitable metal plate where you can leave it in the far south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri, but you should clear the area of crocodiles and rats before you do. If one of the Terâsi claims our gift, you should ask them if they know where your missing Kinswoman has gone.'","You set the bread on the plate. If Birûk is right, now you just need to wait","'There is a suitable metal plate where you can leave the bread in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri, but you should clear the area of crocodiles and rats before you do. If one of the Terâsi claims our gift, you should ask them if they know where your missing Kinswoman has gone.'","Defeat rats in Ilmabiri (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Wait for the Terâsi girl Tephísa to return","Wait and see if you are contacted by one of the Terâsi","You hear someone moving quietly in the darkness beyond the grate","Birûk has given you a curious directive that he insists will help you track down Tatháta's location within Umbar-môkh.","Place the meal and wine on the metal plate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri","Place the crusty bread on the metal plate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri","You hear someone moving about in the darkness","Birûk told you to find a metal plate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri.","Chapter 9.6: Unseen Ones","Once again, Tephísa's voice floats from the darkness.\
\
'This is much better fare, stranger. You have my thanks.\
\
'Now tell me again what you wished to learn.'","Birûk told you that leaving food here should summon one of the Terâsi, the forgotten ones of Umbar-môkh. Now you must wait and see if he was right.","The Terâsi girl you encountered in Ilmabiri asked you to retrieve a meal of higher quality from the Upper Ward, as well as a bottle of fancy wine, or she will tell you nothing. The tables at the Baths of Ilmai Iforikh may have what you need.","'Temámir hearts warm to the Terâsi, for we see their hardships and take pity upon them. It has been our custom to leave food for these forgotten ones throughout Umbar-môkh on occasion. I will give you this crusty bread so you can do this as well. There is a suitable metal plate where you can leave it in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri, but you should clear the area of crocodiles and rats before you do. If one of the Terâsi claims our gift, you should ask them if they know where your missing Kinswoman has gone.'","Talk to the girl in the darkness beyond the grate in the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri","Steal an unattended bottle of wine from the Baths of Ilmai Iforikh in the Upper Ward","Talk to Tephísa, the Terâsi girl in the darkness at the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri","A girl's voice drifts out of the darkness.\
\
'When people leave food out for us, they do not wait. Maybe you did not know this.'\
\
You respond that you were hoping to speak to someone who might know what happened to Tatháta, Kinswoman of the Lower Ward. The silence stretches for so long that it seems possible the unseen speaker has slipped away, but your patience is rewarded at last.\
\
'I might know something, but this bread is not enough. I want a true meal, something fancy. And wine! Bring me a meal and wine from the Upper Ward, and I may tell you what I know.'\
\
A sudden scuffling sound in the darkness tells you the girl is about to leave. You call out, asking how she will know you have fulfilled your side of the bargain.\
\
'Tephísa will know,' she calls back, and then you are certain you are alone again.","Your great ability as a Burglar has allowed you to avoid detection","Steal an unattended meal from the Baths of Ilmai Iforikh in the Upper Ward","Have you been seen?","'What do you think you are doing? None can avoid my watchful gaze, and I can easily see the meal and the wine you have taken do not belong to you.'\
\
The guard squints at you.\
\
'${PLAYER}? Ah! You must be here on some business for the Kindred, then? Very well, do not allow me to hinder it! I must have made some mistake. Your name has become quite well-known throughout the city, and your many deeds have elevated it to quite a height! Go in peace, and fulfill your mission!'","Defeated crocodiles in Ilmabiri (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated rats in Ilmabiri (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You must wait once again for the Terâsi girl Tephísa to return.","Tephísa, the Terâsi girl, has returned to the south-eastern corner of Ilmabiri.","This location matches the description given to you by Birûk"},
[3333]={"Corudan and Sigileth have suggested a number of places for you to search throughout Kamrabezûr, and encouraged you to defeat any foes that stand in the way of your investigation.","You explain your intention to learn what befell Tatháta in the days since she was last seen fleeing from the hidden harbour. Silence falls upon Ilmabiri for long moments. At last Tephísa's voice floats back to you.\
\
'Many of us live in the tunnels, stranger: more than you might think. Our eyes see much that the Temámir do not, for we can reach places even they cannot go; perhaps they choose not to go there, but we have not that choice. All of Umbar-môkh is our domain, and while the city is big, Umbar-môkh has vastness of a different kind.\
\
'A friend of mine witnessed Tatháta's flight. By secret paths he followed her, unseen, but he was not her only pursuer. An Umbari warrior-woman chased at her heels, deadly daggers flashing in the torch-light. He pursued them both into Kamrabezûr, but among those vaults he lost their trail. Many abandoned temples to the Church of the All-Seeing can be found in that place; it may be Tatháta gained entrance to one of those, and stays there now in hiding. Of the other, I cannot say. My friend believes Tatháta must have given her the slip as well, leaving her no choice but to return to the city above. That seems most likely to me.\
\
'Good-bye, stranger. I thank you for the food and for the wine! I hope Tephísa has been a help to you.'\
\
There is a brief rustling sound, and you know the girl has disappeared once again into the deeper darkness of Umbar-môkh.","Corudan stands at Kên Taghlim in north-western Kamrabezûr.","Corudan stands beside Galatâni's grave outside the city.","Sigileth stands at Kên Taghlim in north-western Kamrabezûr, prepared to go with you in search of Tatháta's hiding-place.","Corudan and Sigileth have also arrived at Kên Taghlim","Defeat sand-sifters in Kamrabezûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Birûk waits for you at Itekh-kên in Khabârkhad, and may be able to guide your search of Kamrabezûr for Tatháta.","'${PLAYER}, there you are! Let us move forward with care. There are several locations within Kamrabezûr that Tatháta marked on her map with charcoal, and any of them could indicate the place where now she hides.'\
\
You ask Corudan if he or his sister have encountered any of the beasts rumoured to have escaped from the arena, and he shakes his head.\
\
'No, but the folk we have met with speak of little else. Whatever was being kept in the holding-pens of the arena must have been ferocious indeed to frighten them so; the sound of it roaring in the darkness is apparently enough to make your blood run cold.'\
\
Sigileth makes no sound, but you can tell she does not believe these reports. Her brother continues.\
\
'We may encounter this creature or creatures if we continue our search of Kamrabezûr. I just want us to be prepared. Let me mark the locations we still must investigate on your map, and encourage you to combat any of the other dangers that cross your path.'","Talk to Corudan by the grave","Search the centre of the cultist camp of Jâx Ugikh for Tatháta","Talk to Corudan at Kên Taghlim in north-western Kamrabezûr","Birûk suggested that you go to Kên Taghlim in the north-western reaches of Kamrabezûr, but that you should steer clear of the great beasts rumoured to have escaped from the arena.","Cultists mass in these halls, but there is no sign of Tatháta","The unruly Dead stalk these corridors, but there is no sign of Tatháta","Talk to Sigileth at Kên Taghlim and go with her in search of Tatháta","'This is the place. I know it.'","Defeated sand-sifters in Kamrabezûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat All-Seeing Eye cultists in Kamrabezûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We found something, ${PLAYER}. It was not marked on Tatháta's map, but Sigileth feels certain this is the location to which she fled. Should we investigate it now?\
\
'What says my sister to this?'","'I think we should use caution. There are several locations within Kamrabezûr that Tatháta marked on her map with charcoal, and any of them could indicate the place where now she hides.'","Hostile veterans of Dahâl Huliz encamp here, but there is no sign of Tatháta among them","Search the centre of Harkhaphâr for Tatháta","Talk to Corudan at Kên Taghlim","Defeated All-Seeing Eye cultists in Kamrabezûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Chapter 9.7: The Beast Below","The information you learned from Tephísa guides you to Kamrabezûr in the north-eastern reaches of Umbar-môkh.","Search the centre of Ghâr Mejet for Tatháta","'You have returned! Were you able to draw the notice of any among the Terâsi?'\
\
You tell Birûk about what you learned from Tephísa, and he chuckles quietly.\
\
'The net is closing about your prey, ${PLAYER}. Kamrabezûr? I have already sent your Elf friends into that place! Several of the circled areas on the map they showed to me indicated locations within those vaults, and the words of the Terâsi have confirmed that Tatháta's flight brought her to that place. You should look for your friends at Kên Taghlim in the north-western reaches of Kamrabezûr.'\
\
Birûk prepares to go, but then he turns back to you, a concerned expression on his face.\
\
'There is one more thing, ${PLAYER}. Reports from Kamrabezûr indicate that at least one terrible creature prowls the vaults and corridors of that place. Something must have escaped from the arena, and until Rothog's men can retrieve it that region of Umbar-môkh cannot truly be called safe. Be careful.'","'Reports from Kamrabezûr indicate that at least one terrible creature prowls the vaults and corridors of that place. Something must have escaped from the arena, and until Rothog's men can retrieve it that region of Umbar-môkh cannot truly be called safe. Be careful.'","Find Kên Taghlim in north-western Kamrabezûr","'Está hecho.'","Talk to Birûk at Itekh-kên in Khabârkhad"},
[3334]={"Find frost-drake tracks to the south along the road","Talk to Vútro the West-wind by the hidden path among the rocks","'I did not mean to cause offence! Everyone knows Wizards are quick to anger, but I did not expect the wick to catch so swiftly!\
\
'I have a message for you, ${PLAYER}, from a mutual friend. He asked me to send you to him on the road to the Glimmerdeep with as much haste as you can manage, \\qas fast as the wind,\\q he said to me. Well, now I have delivered the message and I will take my leave, and more importantly I will leave the Wizard to his books, and in peace!'","By following frost-drake tracks in the Ered Mithrin, you found a hidden path climbing into the mountains. Did drakes of the Frost-horde come this way in search of Karazgar?","Chapter 9.7: The Wind and the Warrior","'Hello, ${PLAYER}. It is time!'","Talk to Vútro the West-wind outside Skarháld.","Find frost-drake tracks further south along the road","'Our mutual friend asked me to send you to him on the road to the Glimmerdeep with as much haste as you can manage, \\qas fast as the wind,\\q he said to me. Well, now I have delivered the message and I will take my leave, and more importantly I will leave the Wizard to his books, and in peace!'","Someone wants to meet you on the road to the Glimmerdeep, and you should find out who it is.","'I did not follow Hórin to the Anvil, ${PLAYER}, as you and Durin requested, and when the expedition returned with word that Karazgar had been slain by the Herald of Winter, my friends told me I was avenged. But I knew it was not so. I knew in my bones that Karazgar still lived, but none of the scouts have seen any sign of him since the expedition returned.\
\
'We know he is a master of stealth. Did he not prove his ability to move silently when he first ambushed me, cutting my leg with his cruel blade and robbing me of my fleetness? If he does not wish to be found, even the most alert of our scouts will not find him.\
\
'I stood nearby and listened as Hórin gave his report to Inek, who succeeded Bótuz Frostblood as the leader of my people here at Skarháld, and I think they missed something important! Karazgar had control over much of the Frost-horde, yes; did he not use its drakes and worms to attack us here? But that power derived from his mastery over Vethúg Wintermind. According to Hórin's account, Karazgar began to lose control over Vethúg as the battle turned against him, and when Vethúg perished, the drake died cursing his former master. What if Karazgar's control over the Frost-horde perished with Vethúg, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'Instead of scouting from on high for Karazgar, I instead watched for strange behaviour on the part of frost-drakes in the mountains. And behold! I saw many of the creatures moving with single-minded purpose. Not on behalf of Karazgar, no. I think they are seeking for him, wounded as he is, for the same purpose as I. I think the drakes seek him for vengeance, ${PLAYER}. If we follow their tracks, they may lead us right to Karazgar!\
\
'I saw them south of here! Hurry there and I will follow behind, and catch up as I can!'","A steep path climbs north-east to a shadowy cave entrance","A dwarf has come to Gandalf's chamber in Skarháld, and he has a message for you.","'I think we found it, ${PLAYER}. This must be Karazgar's lair, from where he launched his attack on Skarháld. Can you smell it? The stench of evil is all over this cavern!'","'But I see we have a visitor! What do you want, newcomer?\
\
'You have a message for ${PLAYER}? Then deliver it! Are you not aware that a Wizard's time is valuable?'","Climb the steep hidden path you discovered","'This dwarf is not here for me, ${PLAYER}, but for you! Hear his message and be on your way, for my time is precious!'","Vútro the West-wind leans on his staff and nods in greeting","'This is where the tracks have led us, ${PLAYER}. Karazgar may be stealthy enough to hide from Longbeard and Zhélruka scouts, but it seems he has found it more difficult to escape the sight of the Frost-horde. Many drakes and worms came this way, and if I am right they seek to avenge the death of Vethúg Wintermind!\
\
'We should climb this path and see where it goes, but remain alert! If I am right, we may find Karazgar at the end of it, and perhaps at his end as well!'","A partially-hidden path leads up among the rocks to the north-west","Frost-drakes passed this way in great numbers, heading south","'Look at this, ${PLAYER}!'","You followed frost-drake tracks to a partially-hidden path that winds its way up the mountains. Vútro the West-wind stands at the start of the path, eager to speak with you.","Talk to the Zhélruka messenger in Gandalf's chamber at Skarháld","Vútro the West-wind saw frost-drake tracks to the south, and he thinks following them will lead you to the wounded Karazgar.","Search along the road to the Glimmerdeep to find the message's sender","Vútro the West-wind is on the road leading to the Glimmerdeep.","'If we follow the tracks of the frost-drakes, they may lead us right to Karazgar! I saw them south of here, along the road! Hurry there and I will follow behind, and catch up as I can!'","Vútro the West-wind is inside the shadowy cave you discovered high among the rocks in the Ered Mithrin.","Talk to Vútro the West-wind inside the cave","'We should climb this path and see where it goes, but remain alert! If I am right, we may find Karazgar at the end of it, and perhaps at his end as well!'","Gandalf has come to Skarháld with the Black Book of Mordor, but the situation in the Ered Mithrin will not wait for the Wizard to finish his research, and there are other demands on your time."},
[3335]={"These drakes of the Frost-horde were slain by some sharp instrument","'Go forward with caution, ${PLAYER}, and I will follow behind. Worms of the Frost-horde or Karazgar himself may lie in wait for us, further ahead. I think we have cornered the Weeping Warrior in his lair, and a cornered animal is made more dangerous.\
\
'Remain alert for any threat, no matter what it might be!'","'Go forward with caution, ${PLAYER}, and I will follow behind. Worms of the Frost-horde or Karazgar himself may lie in wait for us, further ahead. I think we have cornered the Weeping Warrior in his lair, and a cornered animal is made more dangerous.\
\
'Remain alert for any sign of danger!'","Judging from its injuries, this drake engaged in fierce battle before it was slain","'We need to learn what happened here. Go forward with caution, ${PLAYER}, and I will follow behind. Worms of the Frost-horde or Karazgar himself may lie in wait for us, further ahead. I think we have cornered the Weeping Warrior in his lair, and a cornered animal is made more dangerous.\
\
'Remain alert for any threat, no matter what it might be!'","Small piles of rust shine in the pale light of the cavern","Vútro the West-wind has entered the large chamber at the rear of Karazgar's lair.","Search the lair for some sign of Karazgar","Steam still rises from the blood, even in the cavern's cold air","You have come with Vútro the West-wind to a cavern in the Ered Mithrin that may have served as Karazgar's lair. But where is the Weeping Warrior now?","Vútro the West-wind has asked you to search Karazgar's lair for some sign of the Weeping Warrior.","Chapter 9.8: Karazgar Cornered","The drake-corpse is warm to the touch. The creature has not been dead for long","The tunnel opens into a large cavern filled with the corpses of worms and drakes","Talk to Vútro the West-wind in Karazgar's lair","'I don't understand, ${PLAYER}. Where is Karazgar? It is clear from the butchery here that he engaged in battle with the Frost-horde that tracked him to his lair, but if he was the victor, as he seems to have been, then where has he gone?'"},
[3336]={"Talk to Hármelak in the main hall of Dâr Laja","You should leave Galatâni's dagger on the grave.","Hármelak waits in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja to hear what you have learned about Tatháta from your time seeking her in Umbar-môkh.","'You have returned safely from Umbar-môkh? Did you discover the reason for Kinswoman Tatháta's disappearance?'\
\
You tell Hármelak what transpired in the hidden chambers within Kamrabezûr, but when you begin to describe the ferocity of the great bear, she raises a hand.\
\
'Not here, ${PLAYER}. Few alone know this secret of Tatháta's, and the Meeting-hall is not the place to speak of it. We have a... more pressing concern to discuss now. We have opened the coffer containing the names of those suggested to join the leadership of the Kindred, and one name has appeared more often than any other.'","'Yes? My sister is right. We should tell Hármelak what transpired beneath the city.'","Chapter 9.8: Last Dance","Hármelak waits in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja to hear what you have learned about Tatháta.","Sigileth stands by the grave, deep in thought.","Sigileth stands quietly, deep in thought. At last she meets your eye.\
\
'I am moved by Galatâni's story, ${PLAYER}, for in it I see something of myself reflected. Well do I know the price of obsession, the cost of single-mindedness. This Umbari woman knew nothing of Elves; would it surprise her to recognize that part of her in some of my people, or in Sigileth of Lórien herself?\
\
'I cannot forget this woman, and will not. She named herself \\qCruel Dancer,\\q and it was a name well-chosen, for hers was a dance with death, and such cannot last forever.'\
\
Sigileth draws her sword.\
\
'My blade has found its name, ${PLAYER}. It shall be \\qBaugliltir,\\q that is \\qCruel Dancer\\q in Sindarin, and it shall remind me of she who participated in the death-dance, and at last succumbed. She remains with me now.'\
\
Sigileth sheathes Baugliltir and nods once more at the grave. Then she turns to you.\
\
'Hármelak will want to know what we learned beneath the city. It is time to return to Dâr Laja.'","Talk to Sigileth by the grave","You have emerged from Umbar-môkh with tidings of Tatháta for the Kindred of the Coins, but your information may herald trouble on the horizon.","Return to Hármelak in the main hall of Dâr Laja","Leave Galatâni's dagger on the grave","'Hármelak will want to know what we learned beneath the city. It is time to return to Dâr Laja.'","Corudan remains silent for a long time. When he speaks again, his voice is quiet.\
\
'My heart is conflicted, ${PLAYER}. Galatâni chose a path of cruelty and greed, and the words she spoke to Tatháta will surely cause trouble for us in the days ahead... but still her end was a sad one.'\
\
Corudan hands you a small dagger.\
\
'I retrieved this from the floor where it had fallen during their struggle, ${PLAYER}. It is the blade with which Galatâni cut her path through this life, and it should accompany her in death. Do you agree?'","'The blade with which Galatâni cut her path through this life should accompany her in death, yes?'","Hármelak eyes you carefully as you approach the dais, her expression unreadable"},
[3337]={"Gandalf stands on the upper level of Skarháld following his confrontation with Karazgar.","Talk to Gandalf on the upper level of Skarháld","Explore the tunnel with Vútro the West-wind","Talk to Vútro the West-wind outside the cave mouth north-west of Skarháld","'Wait a moment! This was the exit of the escape tunnel the Zhélruka discovered in the rear of the Skarháld keep, but I thought it was collapsed. Why then has the rubble been removed, the cave-mouth cleared?\
\
'I do not like this, ${PLAYER}! Who opened this passage again, and for what purpose?'","Karazgar's lair is filled with dead drakes of the Frost-horde that followed him from Winterstith, but the Weeping Warrior is nowhere to be found. Where can he have gone?","'We will brave the tunnel and learn what has happened, ${PLAYER}. We have no choice!'","<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Skarháld when you accept this quest.</rgb>\
\
'I need to think. When Vethúg died, Karazgar's control over much of the Frost-horde died with him. His last chance to regain that control was to dominate the Herald of Winter, but she proved far too powerful for his tricks. Grievously wounded and bleeding, he cast aside his blade and fled from Winterstith. At Hrímil's command and fuelled by hate, drakes of the Frost-horde followed Karazgar back to his lair, where he rearmed himself and fought for his life.\
\
'Did he win this engagement? He must have survived, for his body does not lie among the corpses of his foes. Where could he have gone? What would he still wish to...'\
\
Vútro falls silent.\
\
'He cannot have returned to Skarháld, can he? Is his hatred for us such that he would seek to destroy my people rather than rest and recover from his injuries? We cannot stay here, ${PLAYER}! We must return to Skarháld at once!'","Vútro the West-wind has called for a halt north-west of Skarháld, near a cave entrance.","Chapter 9.9: A Promise Kept","'I will meet you north-west of Skarháld, ${PLAYER}! Now hurry!'","'Karazgar has been shamed, but that does not remove the danger he poses to the Dwarves of the Ered Mithrin. So great was his desire to possess the Black Book that he thought to release his claim upon this land in order to get it! Nothing I have deciphered to this point explains his yearning for Vóin's tome, but I have seen enough of this Gúrzyul to know we should hinder his plots whenever we can.\
\
'Karazgar may be a master of deception, but I think his desire for the Black Book of Mordor was truthful. Does he believe it could hold the secret to maintaining his power, or his life's essence? Can it be possible that the book records his birth-name, his Bugdash? If that is so, surely he will seek it unceasingly. Despite Karazgar's defeat, he will one day return and try to seize it; the book cannot stay here at Skarháld.'"},
[3338]={"Hármelak is in the main hall of Dâr Laja, waiting to speak with you again.","'I am better-suited for the post than you are, and we both know it!'","'I was surprised to hear your name read aloud so often when they opened the coffer, ${PLAYER}. The people of the city have taken notice of your efforts on their behalf. Take pride in it, but know that the responsibility can prove a heavy burden.'\
\
Belondor sighs wearily.\
\
'We will have many demands upon our time in the weeks ahead. How will we decide what can be done, and what must be done? I hope you will help me sort our way through these issues.'","'Speak to the others here in Dâr Laja, and they may well ask for your assistance. Prove you act for Umbar, and you may receive their blessings.'","Talk to Jaith outside Dâr Laja","Talk to Rothog in Dâr Laja","'You grow more impressive by the day, ${PLAYER}! Must I keep an eye upon you from now on?'\
\
Khôltekh chuckles to himself, apparently amused by a secret joke.\
\
'Such power must be wielded with care, my friend, or you risk losing it. Many others have learned this lesson too late; I encourage you to learn it early.'","'I am amused, honoured, and a little upset with you, ${PLAYER}! You should have told me you planned to plant your name many times in the suggestions coffer! I do not know how you accomplished this feat, but I am impressed you were able to do it. Still, it was my idea, and I should be the one who joins the Kindred of the Coins, not you! Imagine the power I might wield as part of that august body!\
\
'I am better-suited for the post than you are, and we both know it. Well. We will see if they allow you to join at all. I suspect they will not, for as much as the people of the city seem to like you, I have seen the way each member of the Kindred looks at you, and there is distrust behind every pair of eyes. Mark my words, ${PLAYER}: they may speak friendly words, but in their hearts they cannot see you truly as a friend. There is too much bloodshed between Umbar and Gondor for that, no matter what Sirgon or the others may believe.\
\
'Jajax has always seen and spoken the truth. Doubt him at your peril!'","'You have done well for us today, ${PLAYER}; of that there can be no doubt, but let us see how you fare in the weeks ahead before we think overmuch of the future.\
\
'But Tatháta, it seems, may have reason to wish you ill, and your continued work alongside the Kindred means she may wish to do us harm as well... and that cannot be permitted. Go now to the guard outside Dâr Laja and tell him that she is not to be allowed to pass.'\
\
Hármelak carefully adjusts her bracelets.\
\
'Few know of Tatháta's true strength, for she has kept it hidden from all but her dearest friends. Let us keep that knowledge to ourselves for now, ${PLAYER}, unless she gives us a reason not to do so. Yes, I count myself among Tatháta's friends. Does that surprise you?\
\
'But warn Jaith, outside the Meeting-hall, that Tatháta is not to be underestimated. The events of the past few days may have given her reason to suspect even her friends of betrayal, and if she tries to attack the Meeting-hall it will be his duty to stand before her.'","Talk to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja","Talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja","Jajax has some words for you in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja.","Chapter 9.9: The Name","Talk to Hármelak in Dâr Laja","The guardsman Jaith stands outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja. Hármelak has asked that you warn him to keep watch in case Tatháta assaults the entrance in search of you or the leaders of the Kindred.","'One name was suggested more than any other to replace the missing members of the Kindred... and that name was your own, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Hármelak appraises you carefully.\
\
'The folk of Umbar Baharbêl have noticed your efforts on their behalf, it seems. That is not enough, but it is more than nothing. I do not know if you are the right person to join us, ${PLAYER}. Know that there would be tests and trials to ensure you are worthy of such an honour, as there were for the rest of us. I promise you nothing.\
\
'The city will face many challenges in the weeks ahead. Speak to the other leaders of the Kindred of the Coins here in Dâr Laja, and they may well ask for your assistance. Prove you act for Umbar, and you may receive their blessings.'","'Your name grows in worth, ${PLAYER}. If the people of the city continue to speak of you with such praise, I may have to order you to the arena.'\
\
Rothog smiles: an unpleasant sight.\
\
'Invite. I may have to invite you to the arena.'","Hármelak suggested that you speak with the other leaders of the Kindred of the Coins in the main hall of Dâr Laja about the dangers their people will face in the days ahead.","'Few know of Tatháta's true strength, for she has kept it hidden from all but her dearest friends. Let us keep that knowledge to ourselves for now, ${PLAYER}, unless she gives us a reason not to do so.\
\
'But warn Jaith, outside the Meeting-hall, that Tatháta is not to be underestimated.'","'I should prevent Kinswoman Tatháta from entering Dâr Laja? Has she thrown in with the traitors, then? I cannot believe it!\
\
'I will do what I can if she makes a threatening appearance, but I must warn you that she has always had the fiercest countenance and possesses great strength to match! If she wants to get inside, there may be little we guardsmen could do to prevent it! But still we will do our best.'\
\
As you bid farewell to Jaith, you fear he is right: if Tatháta demands entrance, there are few in Umbar Baharbêl who could stand against her.","One name was placed in the suggestions coffer inside Dâr Laja more than any other.","Talk to Jajax in Dâr Laja"},
[3339]={"'No nos atrevemos a acercarnos a nuestro antiguo campamento hasta que encontremos una forma de derrotar a la criatura del Lago Negro, ${PLAYER}. No puedo dejarte pasar.\
\
'Un número de enanos de nuestra expedición están descansando en Echad Dúnann, justo al oeste. Habla con Hundi allí; fue fundamental para descubrir la caja de armas de la que hablé.'","'Ráthwald tiene razón, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Sin un arma verdaderamente magnífica forjada a la manera de los Antiguos, no podemos esperar ni siquiera arañar la carne de esa criatura milenaria.\
\
'Pero las leyendas del pasado a veces aparecen cuando menos se esperan. Mis amigos y yo encontramos una caja de armas antiguas no mucho después de que la Guarnición de Hierro llegara a este lugar. Selecciona una de estas armas, y puede que tu elección nos ayude a despejar el camino hacia Moria de esa terrible criatura.\
\
'Toma también esta filigrana para grabar en tu arma, porque conozco a alguien que puede ayudarte a entender los usos de estas reliquias antiguas.'","'Hundi está en Echad Dúnann, el campamento justo al oeste de aquí. Habla con él sobre la caja de armas que su equipo recuperó de una de las cuevas de Eregion.'","Los enanos están desesperados por encontrar algún medio de derrotar al Guardián que espera en el Lago Negro, frente a las Muros de Moria.","Capítulo 9: Un arma de los días antiguos","Hundi está en Echad Dúnann, no muy lejos al oeste de Rathwald, en Eregion.\
\
Rathwald te ha enviado a hablar con su amigo Hundi, quien ayudó en la recuperación de una la caja con armas que podrían ser provechosas."},
